// Words: Jonathan's canonical commentary txt. Structure: his Notion pages.
import type { V205BookData } from '../types';

export const DATA: V205BookData = {
  book: "Isaiah",
  display: "Isaiah",
  chapters: {
    "1": {"chapter":1,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"In scripture, there is a concept I refer to as “folding.” Much of scripture is historical, so I don’t want to overemphasize this point, but when read in its proper context, many events involving Israel throughout the Old Testament foreshadow what is to come for this world. God has repeatedly proven that Israel is His people and has given them specific commands to be an example to the world. However, the Israelites often drifted away from God, prompting Him to send prophets to capture their attention."},{"kind":"para","text":"There are many “scholars” and religious groups who believe that God, in His sovereign plan, uses trials to get the nations’ attention. While this is true, it overlooks a crucial aspect: God consistently sent prophets to warn them first. It was not as if God enacted His plan without any rhyme or reason. The Israelites were aware of what was to come because they were warned, and we are warned today by our preachers and pastors. If you are part of a Bible-preaching church, the preacher should be delivering biblical warnings of things to come."},{"kind":"para","text":"In this book, the prophet Isaiah delivers a challenging prophecy about the nation of Israel, much of which relates to events we will see in the end times (the Book of Revelation is full of wonders). The most significant message Isaiah conveys is the prophecy of a Savior. During this time, the Babylonians were rapidly gaining world dominance. God could have subdued this nation and maintained Israel’s supremacy (as He did with the Assyrians in Hezekiah’s time), but He chose to allow the Babylonians to rise to power and conquer Israel. Why? Isaiah explains this. I consider this to be a “fifth” gospel, if you will (first of five). Isaiah provides detailed insights into the coming of the Messiah of Israel."}],"previously":[],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":9,"title":"The Rebellious Israel","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Right from the start, Isaiah makes it clear that his vision was towards Judah and Jerusalem. He was seeing something that would be specifically geared towards their necessities and circumstances. Of course, we can use the examples set forth here to help us navigate our own lives."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"All scripture is given by inspiration of God, and is profitable for doctrine, for reproof, for correction, for instruction in righteousness:","ref":"2 Timothy 3:16"},{"kind":"para","text":"But we must remember that God’s Word is specific as well (this is what I made mention of in the introduction to this book). He also gives a specific timeframe for when he is seeing this (it was during the time of Uzziah, Jotham, Ahaz, and Hezekiah’s reign)."},{"kind":"para","text":"Uzziah was the tenth king of Israel, Jotham is his son, Ahaz is the grandson, and Hezekiah is the great-grandson of Uzziah. All of these kings were good except for Ahaz. Hezekiah also made some mistakes before his death, but he was still listed as a good king. Having a little background knowledge of these kings might be beneficial to setting the tone of this particular book."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"In those days was Hezekiah sick unto death. And the prophet Isaiah the son of Amoz came to him, and said unto him, Thus saith the LORD, Set thine house in order; for thou shalt die, and not live. Then he turned his face to the wall, and prayed unto the LORD, saying, I beseech thee, O LORD, remember now how I have walked before thee in truth and with a perfect heart, and have done that which is good in thy sight. And Hezekiah wept sore. And it came to pass, afore Isaiah was gone out into the middle court, that the word of the LORD came to him, saying, Turn again, and tell Hezekiah the captain of my people, Thus saith the LORD, the God of David thy father, I have heard thy prayer, I have seen thy tears: behold, I will heal thee: on the third day thou shalt go up unto the house of the LORD. And I will add unto thy days fifteen years; and I will deliver thee and this city out of the hand of the king of Assyria; and I will defend this city for mine own sake, and for my servant David's sake.","ref":"2 Kings 20:1-6"},{"kind":"para","text":"But having a longer life might have been a bad thing for Hezekiah, because he led his enemy (which he didn’t realize is his enemy) into his house to see what kind of treasure he had."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"At that time Berodachbaladan, the son of Baladan, king of Babylon, sent letters and a present unto Hezekiah: for he had heard that Hezekiah had been sick. And Hezekiah hearkened unto them, and shewed them all the house of his precious things, the silver, and the gold, and the spices, and the precious ointment, and all the house of his armour, and all that was found in his treasures: there was nothing in his house, nor in all his dominion, that Hezekiah shewed them not.\" 2 Kings 20:12-13 \"Behold, the days come, that all that is in thine house, and that which thy fathers have laid up in store unto this day, shall be carried into Babylon: nothing shall be left, saith the LORD. And of thy sons that shall issue from thee, which thou shalt beget, shall they take away; and they shall be eunuchs in the palace of the king of Babylon. Then said Hezekiah unto Isaiah, Good is the word of the LORD which thou hast spoken. And he said, Is it not good, if peace and truth be in my days?","ref":"2 Kings 20:17-19"},{"kind":"para","text":"Now Isaiah is going to give the account of the things to come in this book of scripture."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"At that time Berodachbaladan, the son of Baladan, king of Babylon, sent letters and a present unto Hezekiah: for he had heard that Hezekiah had been sick. And Hezekiah hearkened unto them, and shewed them all the house of his precious things, the silver, and the gold, and the spices, and the precious ointment, and all the house of his armour, and all that was found in his treasures: there was nothing in his house, nor in all his dominion, that Hezekiah shewed them not.","ref":"2 Kings 20:12-13"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Behold, the days come, that all that is in thine house, and that which thy fathers have laid up in store unto this day, shall be carried into Babylon: nothing shall be left, saith the LORD. And of thy sons that shall issue from thee, which thou shalt beget, shall they take away; and they shall be eunuchs in the palace of the king of Babylon. Then said Hezekiah unto Isaiah, Good is the word of the LORD which thou hast spoken. And he said, Is it not good, if peace and truth be in my days?","ref":"2 Kings 20:17-19"}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"It should not be a surprise to any of us reading at this point that the Israelites have rebelled against the Lord. When we read through Deuteronomy, we saw the rebellion of this people over and over again. In fact, the very name “Israel” (as we have pointed out before) literally means “Wrestles with God.” They kept to their name and the definition of it, and they still do today."},{"kind":"para","text":"Looking at Israel today, they are very specific about cursing the given Messiah and screaming that at the top of their lungs. If you make mention of Christ to them today, they become deathly enraged. They protest heavily against the name of Christ, even more than our atheist friends. They are a difficult people to share the gospel with, and it is interesting to me that these are the people to whom Christ came and witnessed while on Earth. If this is how they are today, I imagine they were even worse back then. Their rebellion is not lost on the Lord, and He is extremely displeased with it."},{"kind":"thought","text":"### Main Thought: Looking at Israel today, they are very specific about cursing the given Messiah and screaming that at the top of their lungs. If you make mention of Christ to them today, they become deathly enraged. They protest heavily against the name of Christ, even more than our atheist friends. They are a difficult people to share the gospel with, and it is interesting to me that these are the people to whom Christ came and witnessed while on Earth."}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Think about this for a second. The animals know who they belong to better than the Israelites do. We are more stubborn than donkeys! The human species has a complex mind, and we utilize it for all the wrong reasons. The animals have a less complex mind, but they do what they can with the best of their abilities. They lead a great example for us because they are simple creatures. We just overcomplicate everything."},{"kind":"thought","text":"### Main Thought: The animals know who they belong to better than the Israelites do."},{"kind":"highlight","text":"### Highlight: The human species has a complex mind, and we utilize it for all the wrong reasons. The animals have a less complex mind, but they do what they can with the best of their abilities. They lead a great example for us because they are simple creatures. We just overcomplicate everything."}]},{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"As a prophet, these words of Isaiah are not easy to speak. It is not as if Isaiah has a heart of anger or vengeance against his people. In fact, Isaiah was there with his people. He was experiencing their iniquity firsthand. He was preaching to them out of a fear and desire for change. He is seeing what is coming, and he wants to prevent it the best he can by warning these people about it! He wants them to turn to the Lord and follow Him, not follow themselves. They could live prosperous lives if they just turn, or they can be held in captivity if they don’t."},{"kind":"para","text":"The truth is, Isaiah saw what these people were doing, and he saw how the Lord was reacting toward it, and he was conflicted with the problem. His people (God’s people) were turning against the Lord and abusing their prosperity for personal gain and neglecting God’s people."},{"kind":"thought","text":"### Main Thought: He is seeing what is coming, and he wants to prevent it the best he can by warning these people about it! He wants them to turn to the Lord and follow him, not follow themselves. They could live prosperous lives if they just turn, or they can be held in captivity if they don’t."}]},{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God knows that they won't stop either. He knows that once they start to rebel, they will grow in their rebellion more and more."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"A little leaven leaveneth the whole lump.","ref":"Galatians 5:9"},{"kind":"para","text":"It's almost like a snowball effect. One little push and suddenly you have an avalanche."}]},{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"They are receiving their own punishment. They were given a specific symbol for such things. They sin against the Lord, and there was a sacrifice for it that they could make with repentance. Instead, they have neglected the true meaning of the sacrifice, doing it out of necessity rather than out of desire and compassion for the Lord, and they have started to take their own sins upon themselves. This is the life of a man without Christ. If there is someone who doesn’t know Christ today, they are walking around in their wounds, bruises, and putrefying sores out of their own free volition!"},{"kind":"para","text":"I knew a man who had a very large hernia sticking out of his stomach. It was obvious, protruding, and no one could deny what it was. We had explained to him that it needed surgical removal or it could pop and it would be even worse after that. Apparently, he had been walking around with that thing for most of his life. He was living on the edge and in pain because he didn’t want to go see a doctor about it. We are all like that without Christ. We walk around on the edge and in pain only because we won’t come to the great physician for our most important need, which is salvation. He can provide the healing, and Isaiah will make that clear later in this book."},{"kind":"para","text":"Isaiah preaches a message here that sounds dismal and useless. He preaches a message that sounds as if there is no solution. But God has granted a solution, and they must understand and tread carefully to find it."},{"kind":"highlight","text":"### Highlight: If there is someone who doesn’t know Christ today, they are walking around in their wounds, bruises, and putrefying sores out of their own free volition!"},{"kind":"conversation","text":"### Conversation: I knew a man who had a very large hernia sticking out of his stomach. It was obvious, protruding, and no one could deny what it was. We had explained to him that it needed surgical removal or it could pop and it would be even worse after that. Apparently, he had been walking around with that thing for most of his life. He was living on the edge and in pain because he didn’t want to go see a doctor about it."}]},{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is about Jerusalem in particular. It was proven in their land because they were not just rebellious towards the Lord, but also towards each other. They were destroying themselves, and it was becoming just like Sodom and Gomorrah. Sodom and Gomorrah are examples of what can happen to rebellious people if left unchecked."},{"kind":"para","text":"Today, we have most of America in an upheaval. Many protests and riots have begun due to every sort of small infraction that our citizens can revolt against. They just want to spread chaos more than help. They want to hurt others because they, themselves, are hurting and they don’t know what to do with that hurt. They don’t have the Lord, and so they don’t have peace in this world."},{"kind":"para","text":"There are “Christian” groups who help the protestors in their protesting, but they don’t add any living water to the rage. All they do is pour gasoline on the fire in the cities. That is what the Israelites were doing. They were burning up their own cities simply because they wanted to do things their own way and not have to listen to the Lord. They had become prosperous, and wealth like that goes to a person’s head."},{"kind":"thought","text":"### Main Thought: Sodom and Gomorrah are examples of what can happen to rebellious people if left unchecked."}]},{"start":8,"end":9,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There is a small group that is still worth saving this country over. I wonder if it was ten just people?"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And he said, Oh let not the Lord be angry, and I will speak yet but this once: Peradventure ten shall be found there. And he said, I will not destroy it for ten's sake.","ref":"Genesis 18:32"},{"kind":"para","text":"Either way, God’s wrath waits if there are righteous people. There are a lot of rebellious people living in the world today. I believe there are more rebellious people in this world today than there are Christians. We are in a very small minority, especially here in the high desert of California. Our state of California is probably one of the worst as far as rebellion goes."},{"kind":"para","text":"But there is a remnant. There is a small group of believers who are praying for our state, nation, and world. There are still just people who are desiring to see a turning back to the Lord. And I truly believe, because of that alone, God has not destroyed us. He has every right to destroy this state, but He is waiting."},{"kind":"thought","text":"### Main Thought: Either way, God’s wrath waits if there are righteous people."}]}]},{"start":10,"end":17,"title":"Fake Practices","entries":[{"start":10,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Ouch. He isn’t just saying they would be like Sodom and Gomorrah anymore. He is flat out calling them this. He’s insulting them in a way. But that is how they were acting, and there was no easy way to explain that than to use an event that all of them would know very well."}]},{"start":11,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Their sacrifices were meaningless. At this point, it seems they were just giving sacrifices to try and fill the Lord up, rather than atone for their mistakes. They were just trying to “satisfy” the Lord, rather than worship Him. If we are not careful, we fall under the same routine as they do. We pray to satisfy the Lord, we read to satisfy the Lord, we attend church gatherings, functions, and fellowships only to try and appease God’s appetite, and that is the wrong spirit and heart to go into God’s service with. We should want to do these things, not to try and earn favor with God, but because we have had a changed heart."},{"kind":"para","text":"Before I was saved, you wouldn’t find me in fellowship with a Christian community. What would be the point? I didn’t desire to be with them (nor did I desire to please God). When I became saved, these were the only people I actually wanted to be with. We were suddenly closer in family than my own flesh and blood. The people of Christ matter a great deal to me now, and I don’t go to church, or start ministries, or serve because I’m trying to fill God up. I do it because I love the Lord, and He has given me a desire to do it. That is how the nation of Israel was supposed to be. That was how they started in Joshua, but they fell far, fast."},{"kind":"para","text":"It’s been about four hundred and fifty something years since they have entered into this land, and they have seen a lot of highs and lows throughout their stay and growth. The truth is (and I believe this to be true even still today), when God prospers us, we always fall away from Him. It’s our fleshly nature to start thinking we are something because God has made us something. We become arrogant and prideful, and that always leads us to sin."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Pride goeth before destruction, and an haughty spirit before a fall.\" Proverbs 16:18 \"Thus saith the LORD, Let not the wise man glory in his wisdom, neither let the mighty man glory in his might, let not the rich man glory in his riches: But let him that glorieth glory in this, that he understandeth and knoweth me, that I am the LORD which exercise lovingkindness, judgment, and righteousness, in the earth: for in these things I delight, saith the LORD.","ref":"Jeremiah 9:23-24"},{"kind":"para","text":"It is wise for us, than, to keep from growing attached to anything this world has to offer, and instead grow attached to God and His provision."},{"kind":"thought","text":"### Main Thought: At this point, it seems they were just giving sacrifices to try and fill the Lord up, rather than atone for their mistakes. They were just trying to “satisfy” the Lord, rather than worship Him."},{"kind":"highlight","text":"### Highlight: We pray to satisfy the Lord, we read to satisfy the Lord, we attend church gatherings, functions, and fellowships only to try and appease God’s appetite, and that is the wrong spirit and heart to go into God’s service with. We should want to do these things, not to try and earn favor with God, but because we have had a changed heart."},{"kind":"conversation","text":"### Conversation: Before I was saved, you wouldn’t find me in fellowship with a Christian community. What would be the point? I didn’t desire to be with them (nor did I desire to please God). When I became saved, these were the only people I actually wanted to be with. We were suddenly closer in family than my own flesh and blood. The people of Christ matter a great deal to me now, and I don’t go to church, or start ministries, or serve because I’m trying to fill God up. I do it because I love the Lord, and He has given me a desire to do it."},{"kind":"highlight","text":"### Highlight: The truth is (and I believe this to be true even still today), when God prospers us, we always fall away from Him. It’s our fleshly nature to start thinking we are something because God has made us something. We become arrogant and prideful, and that always leads us to sin."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Pride goeth before destruction, and an haughty spirit before a fall.","ref":"Proverbs 16:18"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Thus saith the LORD, Let not the wise man glory in his wisdom, neither let the mighty man glory in his might, let not the rich man glory in his riches: But let him that glorieth glory in this, that he understandeth and knoweth me, that I am the LORD which exercise lovingkindness, judgment, and righteousness, in the earth: for in these things I delight, saith the LORD.","ref":"Jeremiah 9:23-24"}]},{"start":12,"end":13,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Obviously, these things are what God wants for His children. He has given specific commands to this nation to do these things. But the way in which they were doing it was wrong. They didn’t do it with heart or care. It’s important to realize this because we are the same vain creatures as the rest of the world. Israel is giving an example of what not to do, and God is specifically pointing out why it’s wrong. Even their “solemn meeting” was wrong in the eyes of the Lord. These are heavy words to ponder. God was not pleased with anything they were doing, and these were the best things that they could possibly do. They were doing it out of a passed-down tradition and out of a spirit of necessity, and many religions today teach this same kind of doctrine. “Confess, because you have to.” “Pray because you’re told to.” “Believe because we need to.” “Marry because it’s commanded.” “Abstain because it’s best to.” “Fear because you were taught to.” These commands of religion don’t breed a heart of gratitude and relationship with the Lord. These commands of religion breed a heart of rebellion, and that is proven and expounded over and over again in scripture."},{"kind":"para","text":"The crazy part is, we see a world of rebellion all around us and we have the tenacity to ask “how” or “why” when we are the ones breeding this culture through our vain and worthless “worship” of God. You want to have a better relationship with the Lord? “Confess” to Him out of a repentant heart. “Pray” to Him out of a desired closeness. “Believe” in Him out of an assured mind. “Marry” in Him with the promises to Him. “Abstain” from sin out of a passion for Him. “Fear” Him out of an awe of His provision. The Israelites had lost that connection with God because they started doing things out of a religious practice, rather than do things out of a relationship with Him. We can take our own relationships in this life as an example. If you are married today (or if you are not but you have close friends), do you do things for the person you love just to get it out of the way, or do you do them with the intent to draw closer to that person? If you have the desire to just get it out of the way, then why are you even around that person if you don’t want to spend any time with them? Why do you claim to love them if you don’t desire to show your love through your acts?"},{"kind":"para","text":"The Catholic Church uses James quite a bit to show the necessity for works-based faith. They quote;"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Even so faith, if it hath not works, is dead, being alone.","ref":"James 2:17"},{"kind":"para","text":"They aren't wrong if you single this verse out. The whole context is important, however, and that is where we need to be if we want to \"rightly divide\" the word of truth. James speaks a lot about how we are to showcase our works towards the Lord if we have a faith."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Even so faith, if it hath not works, is dead, being alone. Yea, a man may say, Thou hast faith, and I have works: shew me thy faith without thy works, and I will shew thee my faith by my works. Thou believest that there is one God; thou doest well: the devils also believe, and tremble.","ref":"James 2:17-19"},{"kind":"para","text":"James says, “We work from our faith, not to receive our faith.” In other words, the only reason we have any sort of work towards the Lord is because we already have a relationship with him. May I also conclude in James that the term “works” has nothing to do with the law of God. Our works of righteousness are not law-based. We work for the Lord out of compassion, not out of law. If it were out of law, the Israelites would be accepted here, for that is how they were working. But as Isaiah will point out later on…"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But we are all as an unclean thing, and all our righteousnesses are as filthy rags; and we all do fade as a leaf; and our iniquities, like the wind, have taken us away.","ref":"Isaiah 64:6"},{"kind":"para","text":"But I'm getting ahead of myself."},{"kind":"thought","text":"### Main Thought: God was not pleased with anything they were doing, and these were the best things that they could possibly do."},{"kind":"highlight","text":"### Highlight: They were doing it out of a passed-down tradition and out of a spirit of necessity, and many religions today teach this same kind of doctrine. “Confess, because you have to.” “Pray because you’re told to.” “Believe because we need to.” “Marry because it’s commanded.” “Abstain because it’s best to.” “Fear because you were taught to.” These commands of religion don’t breed a heart of gratitude and relationship with the Lord. These commands of religion breed a heart of rebellion, and that is proven and expounded over and over again in scripture."},{"kind":"highlight","text":"### Highlight: You want to have a better relationship with the Lord? “Confess” to Him out of a repentant heart. “Pray” to Him out of a desired closeness. “Believe” in Him out of an assured mind. “Marry” in Him with the promises to Him. “Abstain” from sin out of a passion for Him. “Fear” Him out of an awe of His provision."},{"kind":"highlight","text":"### Highlight: In other words, the only reason we have any sort of work towards the Lord is because we already have a relationship with him."},{"kind":"highlight","text":"### Highlight: We work for the Lord out of compassion, not out of law."},{"kind":"thought","text":"### Main Thought: If it were out of law, the Israelites would be accepted here, for that is how they were working."}]},{"start":14,"end":15,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"It's not that God CAN'T hear or look upon them. It's that God WON'T do it. Of course, it is far from Him to look upon sin as well, but what He is ultimately saying here is that the Israelites have turned God away from providing for them because of their vain and traditional works. He doesn't want them anymore. They are abusing His ordinances."},{"kind":"thought","text":"### Main Thought: It's not that God CAN'T hear or look upon them. It's that God WON'T do it."}]},{"start":16,"end":17,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"It’s interesting to note that many men and women today identify as “religious.” They often declare, “Oh, yes, I am a Catholic (or Mormon, or whatever denomination you want to insert). I pray my set prayers, confess my set sins, and go to church every Sunday. I believe in God, and I love my priest (or pastor, or laity). I am extremely religious!”"},{"kind":"para","text":"However, I have no doubt that their understanding of religion is not scriptural. This is the works of religion, and it’s clearly labeled before us in Isaiah."},{"kind":"para","text":"\"Doing well.”"},{"kind":"para","text":"This means we do what's right and giving our best effort at it."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But ye, brethren, be not weary in well doing.","ref":"2 Thessalonians 3:13 \"Seeking judgement.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"This means we are looking for God to help us make the right decisions (not seeking judgement from man or church leaders)."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Therefore thou art inexcusable, O man, whosoever thou art that judgest: for wherein thou judgest another, thou condemnest thyself; for thou that judgest doest the same things.","ref":"Romans 2:1 \"Relieving the Oppressed.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"This means we are trying to help those who are hurting and don't know the Lord personally (or maybe they do, but they feel afflicted)."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But whoso hath this world's good, and seeth his brother have need, and shutteth up his bowels of compassion from him, how dwelleth the love of God in him?","ref":"1 John 3:17 \"Judging the Fatherless.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"This means making proper judgements to help them come to know the Lord (their Heavenly Father). It could also mean literally helping those that don't have a father (those that are orphaned), but I will keep it within the soulwinning aspect."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Asshur shall not save us; we will not ride upon horses: neither will we say any more to the work of our hands, Ye are our gods: for in thee the fatherless findeth mercy.","ref":"Hosea 14:3 \"Pleading for the Widows.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"This means taking care of and nurturing those that have lost their loved ones (usually those who are up there in age, specifically because the religious (back then and still today) took advantage of these women (they were easy targets))."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Beware of the scribes, which desire to walk in long robes, and love greetings in the markets, and the highest seats in the synagogues, and the chief rooms at feasts; Which devour widows' houses, and for a shew make long prayers: the same shall receive greater damnation.","ref":"Luke 20:46-47"},{"kind":"para","text":"These are the works of true religion, and even James says it."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Pure religion and undefiled before God and the Father is this, To visit the fatherless and widows in their affliction, and to keep himself unspotted from the world.","ref":"James 1:27"},{"kind":"para","text":"Notice how none of that has to do with keeping the law. It’s because the law is not good for anything except to show us our need for Christ. It’s a list of our shortcomings. It proves that we are worthless without the Lord, and all of our “works” are meaningless. In fact, even our works after salvation are very little compared to what God can do in our midst."},{"kind":"para","text":"When I would preach in front of the church (and even in our teen church), I would always pray to the Lord something like, “…God please move me out of the way. Let it only be your Spirit that is shown today…” These were not just fluffy words of humility. I truly desired that it would not be me that made a difference in people, but that it would be God that did it. This is still my desire today."},{"kind":"para","text":"We should desire to get out of the way when God is doing a work and be a person willing to glorify God from the sidelines. Often we want to get in the middle of it, and all we do is mess it up…"},{"kind":"thought","text":"### Main Thought: This is the works of religion, and it’s clearly labeled before us in Isaiah:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But ye, brethren, be not weary in well doing.","ref":"2 Thessalonians 3:13"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Therefore thou art inexcusable, O man, whosoever thou art that judgest: for wherein thou judgest another, thou condemnest thyself; for thou that judgest doest the same things.","ref":"Romans 2:1"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But whoso hath this world's good, and seeth his brother have need, and shutteth up his bowels of compassion from him, how dwelleth the love of God in him?","ref":"1 John 3:17"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Asshur shall not save us; we will not ride upon horses: neither will we say any more to the work of our hands, Ye are our gods: for in thee the fatherless findeth mercy.","ref":"Hosea 14:3"},{"kind":"thought","text":"### Main Thought: Notice how none of that has to do with keeping the law. It’s because the law is not good for anything except to show us our need for Christ. It’s a list of our shortcomings."},{"kind":"conversation","text":"### Conversation: When I would preach in front of the church (and even in our teen church), I would always pray to the Lord something like, “…God please move me out of the way. Let it only be your Spirit that is shown today…” These were not just fluffy words of humility. I truly desired that it would not be me that made a difference in people, but that it would be God that did it. This is still my desire today."},{"kind":"highlight","text":"### Highlight: We should desire to get out of the way when God is doing a work and be a person willing to glorify God from the sidelines."}]}]},{"start":18,"end":20,"title":"A Choice","entries":[{"start":18,"end":18,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There is always hope for the sinner. There is always a God waiting and willing to forgive. He is giving them a chance to turn everything around. He is giving them the opportunity to come to Him and be completely cleansed of sin. He has given the whole world this chance. We are held captive by our sins if we don’t take this opportunity to be cleansed of them."},{"kind":"highlight","text":"### Highlight: There is always hope for the sinner. There is always God waiting and willing to forgive."},{"kind":"thought","text":"### Main Thought: We are held captive by our sins if we don’t take this opportunity to be cleansed of them."}]},{"start":19,"end":20,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"It’s not even because God wants His children to suffer. That is not His desire. He wants a good relationship with His children. But He will not force that relationship to happen. He will give you the choice. He will leave the decision up to your desire. If you don’t desire Him, it’s your own doing of death. If you do desire Him, He will feed you only with goodness."},{"kind":"para","text":"Our open rejection of the Lord is not punished by God in this world, but punished by our own doings. We only inflict pain on ourselves here. But in eternity, that is when God will punish our rejection. We had the choice today to turn to Him, and if we don’t, then we can’t stand before Him and say, “Well, I didn’t know.”"},{"kind":"highlight","text":"### Highlight: If you don’t desire Him, it’s your own doing of death. If you do desire Him, He will feed you only with goodness."},{"kind":"thought","text":"### Main Thought: Our open rejection of the Lord is not punished by God in this world, but punished by our own doings. We only inflict pain on ourselves here. But in eternity, that is when God will punish our rejection."}]}]},{"start":21,"end":23,"title":"Leaning on Riches","entries":[{"start":21,"end":21,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"They had a great plan and a great start! God had given this nation something foolproof, and they just had to keep pursuing and moving forward. However, they became lazy and selfish. Why are we hardwired like that?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Of course, I believe that God purposely allowed sin to take place in the beginning because it meant the salvation of His Son and a symbol of real love from the Lord. But what makes us cater more towards the shiny things of this world over the treasures we can store in eternity? Why do we want our rewards now? It just robs us of our relationship with the Lord…"}]},{"start":22,"end":22,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Even their most “valuable” possessions are tainted. They aren’t really valuable if they are not completely true. True silver is valuable, and people will spend a lot of money to achieve it. Real wine is valuable, and people will spend (far too much) money to receive it."},{"kind":"para","text":"I worked in a movie star’s house when I was in construction, and one of the things he wanted built in his basement was a temperature-controlled wine room. This room wasn’t anything massive, but it was big enough to hold about a hundred bottles of wine. After we completed the room, he started putting his wine in there right away. We were working on some other parts of the cellar when I saw he had already filled his shelves. I didn’t enter the room, but I could see all the wine through the window, and he had to have thousands of dollars worth of wine in that one room."},{"kind":"para","text":"Imagine the wine being mixed with water. That is far less valuable. If all of the bottles of wine in that cellar were mixed with water, his thousands of dollars would be reduced to a few hundred in seconds. The Israelites were doing this, thinking they had something valuable, and all they did was dilute their own precious materials and make them worthless."},{"kind":"thought","text":"### Main Thought: They aren’t really valuable if they are not completely true. True silver is valuable, and people will spend a lot of money to achieve it. Real wine is valuable, and people will spend (far too much) money to receive it."},{"kind":"conversation","text":"### Conversation: I worked in a movie star’s house when I was in construction, and one of the things he wanted built in his basement was a temperature-controlled wine room. This room wasn’t anything massive, but it was big enough to hold about a hundred bottles of wine. After we completed the room, he started putting his wine in there right away. We were working on some other parts of the cellar when I saw he had already filled his shelves. I didn’t enter the room, but I could see all the wine through the window, and he had to have thousands of dollars worth of wine in that one room. Imagine the wine being mixed with water. That is far less valuable. If all of the bottles of wine in that cellar were mixed with water, his thousands of dollars would be reduced to a few hundred in seconds."},{"kind":"thought","text":"### Main Thought: The Israelites were doing this, thinking they had something valuable, and all they did was dilute their own precious materials and make them worthless."}]},{"start":23,"end":23,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Material gain is a huge problem in our world. We often think we are something special based on what we can afford. For instance, if you shop at Walmart, then you must not be very rich. The truth is, most Christians aren’t very rich. Many can’t even afford a place to live. Consider the Apostles; they were constantly moving from place to place."},{"kind":"para","text":"A rich Christian might have done something very wrong. Does this mean we should reject money and abstain from achieving it? Of course not! However, that should not be our goal. We can only serve one master."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"No man can serve two masters: for either he will hate the one, and love the other; or else he will hold to the one, and despise the other. Ye cannot serve God and mammon.","ref":"Matthew 6:24"},{"kind":"para","text":"There is a reason the poor find it easier to trust in the Lord more than the rich."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Then said Jesus unto his disciples, Verily I say unto you, That a rich man shall hardly enter into the kingdom of heaven. And again I say unto you, It is easier for a camel to go through the eye of a needle, than for a rich man to enter into the kingdom of God.","ref":"Matthew 19:23-24"},{"kind":"para","text":"The reason for this is because they lean on their riches. That is what they believe provides them with value. Friend, God is where the real value is, and it's far wiser to depend on Him, than it is to depend on your personal wealth."},{"kind":"thought","text":"### Main Thought: Material gain is a huge problem in our world. We often think we are something special based on what we can afford."},{"kind":"thought","text":"### Main Thought: A rich Christian might have done something very wrong."},{"kind":"highlight","text":"### Highlight: Friend, God is where the real value is, and it's far wiser to depend on Him, than it is to depend on your personal wealth."}]}]},{"start":24,"end":31,"title":"Getting What They Want","entries":[{"start":24,"end":26,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"In the book of Judges, we see the Israelites continuously becoming captive to the big cities around them. Judges have to come in and rescue them over and over again. For a time, they turn to the Lord, but then they start to put their faith back into their possessions again, and it doesn’t last. It doesn’t seem like anything will last when the Lord gives this nation providence. So why doesn’t God just send His Son now?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Well, I believe it’s because God wanted to display proof that there is no other way to have a lasting relationship with Him except through His Son. God is showcasing that every other way possible will not work. You cannot say, “Well, why didn’t God try this or that? Wouldn’t that have straightened up this world?” He did. The Old Testament shows all the ways in which God proves His salvation for His people and the constant falling away of His people even though God has saved them. So there is only one choice, and that is through (what God has planned all along) a Savior."},{"kind":"thought","text":"### Main Thought: So why doesn’t God just send His Son now? Well, I believe it’s because God wanted to display proof that there is no other way to have a lasting relationship with Him except through His Son. God is showcasing that every other way possible will not work. You cannot say, “Well, why didn’t God try this or that? Wouldn’t that have straightened up this world?” He did. The Old Testament shows all the ways in which God proves His salvation for His people and the constant falling away of His people even though God has saved them. So there is only one choice, and that is through (what God has planned all along) a Savior."}]},{"start":27,"end":29,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God tells them not to plant any gardens in Deuteronomy when they get into this new land."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Thou shalt not plant thee a grove of any trees near unto the altar of the LORD thy God, which thou shalt make thee. Neither shalt thou set thee up any image; which the LORD thy God hateth.","ref":"Deuteronomy 16:21-22"},{"kind":"para","text":"Why? Because He knows they will use it for idolatry. That is what they end up doing, mind you, as soon as the gardens are planted. These are gardens to fake gods, and FOR fake gods. They are openly rejecting the commands of the Lord by making these gardens and serving these false images."}]},{"start":30,"end":31,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is not just harsh because God wants to make them suffer. It is harsh because this is what they have asked for by rejecting the Lord and His relationship with them. Again, they have the opportunity and choice to turn back. God has provided the warning, but He will not make them choose the right thing. He will leave the choice to them, and (spoiler alert) they choose wrong. Because of this, God doesn’t find a way of escape for them. They have chosen to reject the Lord, and so that is the reward they will receive. It was their own choices that brought them here, and God has no other option than to let them reap what they sow. Sometimes that is how it is."},{"kind":"para","text":"Instead of God keeping you from doing something because it’s bad for you, He will give you what you want because you don’t realize the consequences. We cannot complain after that and say, “God, why didn’t you keep me from this?” after we have spent year after year praying and begging and going against everything that the Lord has commanded."},{"kind":"thought","text":"### Main Thought: They have chosen to reject the Lord, and so that is the reward they will receive. It was their own choices that brought them here, and God has no other option than to let them reap what they sow."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":9},{"start":10,"end":10},{"start":11,"end":11},{"start":12,"end":13},{"start":14,"end":15},{"start":16,"end":17},{"start":18,"end":18},{"start":19,"end":20},{"start":21,"end":21},{"start":22,"end":22},{"start":23,"end":23},{"start":24,"end":26},{"start":27,"end":29},{"start":30,"end":31}],"verses":{"1":"The vision of Isaiah the son of Amoz, which he saw concerning Judah and Jerusalem in the days of Uzziah, Jotham, Ahaz, and Hezekiah, kings of Judah.","2":"Hear, O heavens, and give ear, O earth: for the Lord hath spoken, I have nourished and brought up children, and they have rebelled against me.","3":"The ox knoweth his owner, and the ass his master's crib: but Israel doth not know, my people doth not consider.","4":"Ah sinful nation, a people laden with iniquity, a seed of evildoers, children that are corrupters: they have forsaken the Lord, they have provoked the Holy One of Israel unto anger, they are gone away backward.","5":"Why should ye be stricken any more? ye will revolt more and more: the whole head is sick, and the whole heart faint.","6":"From the sole of the foot even unto the head there is no soundness in it; but wounds, and bruises, and putrifying sores: they have not been closed, neither bound up, neither mollified with ointment.","7":"Your country is desolate, your cities are burned with fire: your land, strangers devour it in your presence, and it is desolate, as overthrown by strangers.","8":"And the daughter of Zion is left as a cottage in a vineyard, as a lodge in a garden of cucumbers, as a besieged city.","9":"Except the Lord of hosts had left unto us a very small remnant, we should have been as Sodom, and we should have been like unto Gomorrah.","10":"Hear the word of the Lord, ye rulers of Sodom; give ear unto the law of our God, ye people of Gomorrah.","11":"To what purpose is the multitude of your sacrifices unto me? saith the Lord: I am full of the burnt offerings of rams, and the fat of fed beasts; and I delight not in the blood of bullocks, or of lambs, or of he goats.","12":"When ye come to appear before me, who hath required this at your hand, to tread my courts?","13":"Bring no more vain oblations; incense is an abomination unto me; the new moons and sabbaths, the calling of assemblies, I cannot away with; it is iniquity, even the solemn meeting.","14":"Your new moons and your appointed feasts my soul hateth: they are a trouble unto me; I am weary to bear them.","15":"And when ye spread forth your hands, I will hide mine eyes from you: yea, when ye make many prayers, I will not hear: your hands are full of blood.","16":"Wash you, make you clean; put away the evil of your doings from before mine eyes; cease to do evil;","17":"Learn to do well; seek judgment, relieve the oppressed, judge the fatherless, plead for the widow.","18":"Come now, and let us reason together, saith the Lord: though your sins be as scarlet, they shall be as white as snow; though they be red like crimson, they shall be as wool.","19":"If ye be willing and obedient, ye shall eat the good of the land:","20":"But if ye refuse and rebel, ye shall be devoured with the sword: for the mouth of the Lord hath spoken it.","21":"How is the faithful city become an harlot! it was full of judgment; righteousness lodged in it; but now murderers.","22":"Thy silver is become dross, thy wine mixed with water:","23":"Thy princes are rebellious, and companions of thieves: every one loveth gifts, and followeth after rewards: they judge not the fatherless, neither doth the cause of the widow come unto them.","24":"Therefore saith the Lord, the Lord of hosts, the mighty One of Israel, Ah, I will ease me of mine adversaries, and avenge me of mine enemies:","25":"And I will turn my hand upon thee, and purely purge away thy dross, and take away all thy tin:","26":"And I will restore thy judges as at the first, and thy counsellors as at the beginning: afterward thou shalt be called, The city of righteousness, the faithful city.","27":"Zion shall be redeemed with judgment, and her converts with righteousness.","28":"And the destruction of the transgressors and of the sinners shall be together, and they that forsake the Lord shall be consumed.","29":"For they shall be ashamed of the oaks which ye have desired, and ye shall be confounded for the gardens that ye have chosen.","30":"For ye shall be as an oak whose leaf fadeth, and as a garden that hath no water.","31":"And the strong shall be as tow, and the maker of it as a spark, and they shall both burn together, and none shall quench them."}},
    "2": {"chapter":2,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"That is how we want to view this book, and it's how Isaiah meant it to be viewed. In our first chapter of Isaiah, we get a look at the current state of Israel, their lifestyle, their falling away from their God, their fake practices, and Isaiah brings them a choice for their future. Of course, God already knows what they will choose, and it won't go well with them."},{"kind":"para","text":"In this chapter, we get a distant future look at Israel and what happens to them if they continue to fall into this path they are headed down. He warns them of a tribulation period to come where they will not be able to escape, and only the true worshipers will have a standing chance in that era."}],"previously":["I love this book of the Bible because it is filled with prophecy and a very strong gospel message. That is how we want to view this book, and it's how Isaiah meant it to be viewed. In our first chapter of Isaiah, we get a look at the current state of Israel, their lifestyle, their falling away from their God, their fake practices, and Isaiah brings them a choice for their future. Of course, God already knows what they will choose, and it won't go well with them. In this chapter, we get a distant future look at Israel and what happens to them if they continue to fall into this path they are headed down. He warns them of a tribulation period to come where they will not be able to escape, and only the true worshipers will have a standing chance in that era. Of course, most of Jerusalem believes that they ARE true worshippers, but Isaiah (and the Lord of course) knows that they are anything but genuine in their worship and following of God."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":1,"title":"Judah and Jerusalem","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Here we have the assurance that it is Isaiah who is receiving this vision of things to come, and it’s about Judah and Jerusalem. There are those who acclaim the idea that this is talking about the church, but I don’t see how. I believe this is specifically speaking about the children of Israel, and not the church at all, especially because the church isn’t something that is talked about in the Old Testament (but there are some very interesting parallels to the future church). However, I do keep an open mind on the matter, and so I will give the best details regarding which side takes what stance and why (as I will do in the book of Revelation)."},{"kind":"para","text":"Just as John will do in Revelation, Isaiah will make sure to mention if he is showing a “sign” or a symbol for things to come, and it’s not exactly literal. This is a prophecy about the very distant future of Israel, and the way in which Isaiah starts this out is very direct and obvious that this is about Judah and Jerusalem."},{"kind":"thought","text":"### Main Thought: There are those who acclaim to the idea that this is talking about the church, but I don't see how. I believe this is specifically speaking about the the children of Israel, and not the church at all, especially because the church isn't something that is talked about in the Old Testament. However, I do keep an open mind on the matter, and so I will give the best details regarding which side takes what stance and why (as I will do in the book of Revelation)."}]}]},{"start":2,"end":4,"title":"The King of All","entries":[{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I think in “the last days,” we will experience a portion of what Israel will go through. The church has a significant stance over Israel, mostly because they are considered apostates and anti-Christs. Most of Jerusalem still hates Christ today. There are many videos of protestors in Israel who picket the name of Christ and call for death to Jesus, even today. It’s quite sad. I am under the impression that “the last days” reference here is speaking about exactly that. It’s speaking about the great tribulation period. From chapter 2 to chapter 5, that is what Isaiah will mostly be focused on. I don’t believe it’s by any mistake that John quotes Isaiah quite a lot in his final book."},{"kind":"para","text":"“Mountain” here means “a kingdom” or “an authority.” So it seems that there will be one place for all the people to come out of, and it seems that this place will likely be in Jerusalem. This will be “God’s Kingdom,” in which He reigns and rules, and all the other kingdoms will be destroyed."},{"kind":"thought","text":"### Main Thought: I am under the impression that \"the last days\" reference here is speaking about exactly that. It's speaking about the great tribulation period. From chapter 2 to chapter 5, that is what Isaiah will mostly be focused on. I don't believe it's by any mistake that John quotes Isaiah quite a lot in his final book."}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"It should be our desire today. Of course, Isaiah is speaking about a future for the people of Jerusalem, but obviously, this is something that they should be desiring to hold in their possession today, and it’s something that they have openly rejected. Once again, we see a good majority of Israel today who completely and utterly hate the Lord and His acclamation of Christ. That will eventually change, but only after everything else has already fallen apart. At that point, they won’t have any other way to turn except to Christ."}]},{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Revelation makes it clear that Christ will eventually judge the nations and the people during that time. There will be a large remnant that He will judge, and there will be people who are living with Him, as well as people living around Him. Those that live around Him are people that will eventually try to make war with Him and (obviously) won't succeed."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"These shall make war with the Lamb, and the Lamb shall overcome them: for he is Lord of lords, and King of kings: and they that are with him are called, and chosen, and faithful.","ref":"Revelation 17:14"},{"kind":"thought","text":"### Main Thought: There will be a large remnant that he will judge, and there will be people who are living with Him, as well as people living around Him. Those that live around Him are people that will eventually try to make war with Him and (obviously) won't succeed."}]}]},{"start":5,"end":9,"title":"A Mix of the World","entries":[{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Another specificity that John harps on in his writings. He consistently references Christ being the light of the world and life. It was something that Jesus said, and it seems to have stuck to him quite deeply. Maybe he was really into studying Isaiah, and that is why he clung so tightly to Christ's light. We really SHOULD be walking in the light of the Lord, for that is the only way that we can escape darkness and tribulation."},{"kind":"highlight","text":"### Highlight: We really SHOULD be walking in the light of the Lord, for that is the only way that we can escape darkness and tribulation."}]},{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The Israelites, along with a significant portion of the world both then and now, were seeking comfort and light from anything except the Lord. Isaiah’s remark about them being like the Philistines serves as a prod, as the Philistines were extremely ungodly, hating the God of Jacob and attempting to kill the Israelites several times, succeeding on a few occasions. During the time of Isaiah’s writings, the Israelites were living like the rest of the world, and I believe Isaiah was very concerned about their future prospects, as they were meant to be a people separated from the world, not a people of the world."},{"kind":"para","text":"I feel just as baffled as Isaiah does here when I see self-proclaimed Christians doing all the wrong things against the Lord. They love their worldly things, and there is no sign of the light of the Lord in them. Are they serious about God, or are they just playing the part? Isaiah knows that these people aren’t serious about God because God has been telling them. This vision didn’t come because Isaiah can see how the people are (though, I’m sure Isaiah saw their wickedness and was in distress because of it). Rather, this vision comes because God is revealing what will happen to Israel by their own wills and desires. This will happen, and it’s simply because they keep turning away from the Lord and His leading over and over again."},{"kind":"thought","text":"### Main Thought: The Israelites were living like the rest of the world during the time of Isaiah's writings, and I think Isaiah was very concerned about their future prospects seeing as they were to be a people separated from the world, not a people OF the world."}]},{"start":7,"end":9,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The heathen men were living the exact same way as the Israelites did. They were living in their sin, rejecting the Lord’s law, and seeking after worldly lusts and desires. They were growing accustomed to the lifestyles of all the nations around them, rather than being an example to them of how to follow after the Lord. It is so easy for God’s children to fall for this trick."},{"kind":"para","text":"We must be bold enough to stand against our culture if it is calling us away from Godly things and Godly living. We must be strong enough to stand when the culture commands our fall. We must be willing to preach with unction when the people around us want us to be quiet. Does this mean we should constantly be battling the world? Probably not. This simply means we must be ready to stand up for the faith when the battle comes to your doorstep, rather than cower down and join the enemy."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Wherefore take unto you the whole armour of God, that ye may be able to withstand in the evil day, and having done all, to stand. Stand therefore, having your loins girt about with truth, and having on the breastplate of righteousness;","ref":"Ephesians 6:13-14"},{"kind":"highlight","text":"### Highlight: We must be strong enough to stand when the culture commands our fall. We must be willing to preach with unction when the people around us want us to be quiet."}]}]},{"start":10,"end":18,"title":"Everything Bows to God","entries":[{"start":10,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"It is interesting that Isaiah says this here, because John says this instead..."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And said to the mountains and rocks, Fall on us, and hide us from the face of him that sitteth on the throne, and from the wrath of the Lamb:","ref":"Revelation 6:16"},{"kind":"para","text":"Of course, John is speaking about literal rocks falling on them. Isaiah is speaking about the Lord being their rock. He is quoting David's view of the Lord."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"The LORD is my rock, and my fortress, and my deliverer; my God, my strength, in whom I will trust; my buckler, and the horn of my salvation, and my high tower.","ref":"Psalm 18:2"},{"kind":"para","text":"The strongest rock we can hide behind is the Lord. If we are going to be able to stand, it would be wise to stand behind a shield..."},{"kind":"highlight","text":"### Highlight: The strongest rock we can hide behind is the Lord."}]},{"start":11,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There is no way you can stand in the last days as someone who feels powerful. As I've said before, there will be a good portion of people who will try, and they will utterly fail because the Lord is GOD. It baffles me that they would know this and yet still try and overthrow the Lord. They will literally know that this is God, and they will still think they have the capability of defeating Him. The sad thing is, I believe it because people are like that today. God can show them physical and literal evidence of His existence and His providence (Lord knows He has), and they will still find reason to reject Him. Why would it be any different when He is physically sitting right in front of them?"},{"kind":"thought","text":"### Main Thought: They will literally know that this is God, and they will still think they have the capability of defeating Him."}]},{"start":12,"end":18,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This gives a prominent picture to this verse:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"That at the name of Jesus every knee should bow, of things in heaven, and things in earth, and things under the earth; And that every tongue should confess that Jesus Christ is Lord, to the glory of God the Father.","ref":"Philippians 2:10-11"},{"kind":"para","text":"Even the trees, mountains, towers, and ships will bow to the Lord in that day. What a great picture! There will be nothing that is able to stand in the presence of the Lord, and those things we think are so valuable to us right now will be things we wonder why we cared so much about before. It will only be Jesus, and we will have no other thoughts except \"God, be merciful of me and my life.\""},{"kind":"thought","text":"### Main Thought: Even the trees, mountains, towers, and ships will bow to the Lord in that day."}]}]},{"start":19,"end":22,"title":"No Place to Go","entries":[{"start":19,"end":19,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Again, I draw attention to John's writing. The people that will do this are those that don't desire to know the Lord. They will have no excuse not to worship at that point, yet they will still try and run from Him, thinking there is no way for Him to forgive them. The truth is, they might be right when He returns. They will no longer be saved by faith (which is how we are saved today according to Scripture)."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For by grace are ye saved through faith; and that not of yourselves: it is the gift of God: Not of works, lest any man should boast.","ref":"Ephesians 2:8-9"},{"kind":"para","text":"So if they see the Lord, it will no longer be faith that saves them, but sight."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Now faith is the substance of things hoped for, the evidence of things not seen.","ref":"Hebrews 11:1"},{"kind":"para","text":"That is not the way the Lord wants you to come to Him. Will He allow it? I don't know; we will see when we get there (though I wouldn't gamble on it). These people seem to know that God has rejected them, and so they look for any escape on this Earth that they can get so that they won't be utterly destroyed. Little do they know that ALL of Earth will be made new, and there is no place for them to hide. But we can talk about that at the end of this book."},{"kind":"thought","text":"### Main Thought: That is not the way the Lord wants you to come to Him. Will He allow it? I don't know, we will see when we get there (though I wouldn't gamble on it)."}]},{"start":20,"end":21,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Their idols will seem worthless at that moment of the Lord’s return. They will witness the tribulation, destruction, turmoil, death, and suffering, and they will look at all their material belongings and wonder, “Why did I ever care about these things?” It is something we should come to terms with today."},{"kind":"para","text":"Look at your money. Is it worth your trust? Look at your family. Are they worth losing for? Look at your title or position. Is it worth not becoming God’s child over? We can have these things; that is not something I am denying. However, they should not be our means. They should not exist in our lives for us to lean on. We should be utilizing those things to build a life that is headed for eternity with the Lord. That is why the Lord has granted those things in your life. He wants you to live in the direction of eternity. Use the resources He gives you, don’t depend on them. Don’t depend on anything but Him for eternity’s sake."},{"kind":"highlight","text":"### Highlight: Look at your money? Is it worth your trust in? Look at your family? Are they worth the losing for? Look at your title, or your position? Is it worth not becoming God's child over? We can have these things, that is not something I am denying, but they should not be for our means. They should not exist in our lives for us to lean on. We should be utilizing those things to build a life that is headed for eternity with the Lord."},{"kind":"highlight","text":"### Highlight: He wants you to live in the direction of eternity. USE the resources He gives you, don't depend on them. Don't depend on anything but Him for eternities sake."}]},{"start":22,"end":22,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Furthermore, don’t have confidence in man. I’m glad Isaiah finishes this chapter by saying this because there is a good portion of religionists today who trust in man more than they trust in God. They believe their priest, their pope, their pastor, their reverend, their father, or mother are more likely to deal with their faith problems and spiritual needs than God is. There is no help from them that can bring your faith closer to the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"Church, of course, is a community that believers can have so they can encourage and strengthen each other. However, at the end of the day, your faith is your own, and no other person can help you stand in it. In the end of our life, we will be face to face with the Lord."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"We are confident, I say, and willing rather to be absent from the body, and to be present with the Lord.","ref":"2 Corinthians 5:8"},{"kind":"para","text":"You, alone, will be face to face with God, and there will be no one there to stand up for you, or to coerce you, or to give you counsel, or to mediate for you. There will be no lawyer in your presence, unless you have Jesus Christ as your personal Savior alone. Your priest or pastor won’t be there to give your account for you. You won’t be able to use your priest or pastor as a reference for access to Heaven."},{"kind":"para","text":"Only Jesus Christ is your lifeline, and if you don’t have Him right now, you will not have Him in judgment. Choose who you want by your side when you enter the judgment room of the Lord, your priest, or the high priest (Jesus Christ)?"},{"kind":"thought","text":"### Main Thought: I'm glad Isaiah finishes this chapter up here by saying this, because there is a good portion of religionists today who trust in man more than they trust in God."},{"kind":"highlight","text":"### Highlight: Only Jesus Christ is your lifeline, and if you don't have Him right now, you will not have Him in judgement. Choose who you want by your side when you enter the judgement room of the Lord, your priest, or the high priest (Jesus Christ)?"}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":9},{"start":10,"end":10},{"start":11,"end":11},{"start":12,"end":18},{"start":19,"end":19},{"start":20,"end":21},{"start":22,"end":22}],"verses":{"1":"The word that Isaiah the son of Amoz saw concerning Judah and Jerusalem.","2":"And it shall come to pass in the last days, that the mountain of the Lord's house shall be established in the top of the mountains, and shall be exalted above the hills; and all nations shall flow unto it.","3":"And many people shall go and say, Come ye, and let us go up to the mountain of the Lord, to the house of the God of Jacob; and he will teach us of his ways, and we will walk in his paths: for out of Zion shall go forth the law, and the word of the Lord from Jerusalem.","4":"And he shall judge among the nations, and shall rebuke many people: and they shall beat their swords into plowshares, and their spears into pruninghooks: nation shall not lift up sword against nation, neither shall they learn war any more.","5":"O house of Jacob, come ye, and let us walk in the light of the Lord.","6":"Therefore thou hast forsaken thy people the house of Jacob, because they be replenished from the east, and are soothsayers like the Philistines, and they please themselves in the children of strangers.","7":"Their land also is full of silver and gold, neither is there any end of their treasures; their land is also full of horses, neither is there any end of their chariots:","8":"Their land also is full of idols; they worship the work of their own hands, that which their own fingers have made:","9":"And the mean man boweth down, and the great man humbleth himself: therefore forgive them not.","10":"Enter into the rock, and hide thee in the dust, for fear of the Lord, and for the glory of his majesty.","11":"The lofty looks of man shall be humbled, and the haughtiness of men shall be bowed down, and the Lord alone shall be exalted in that day.","12":"For the day of the Lord of hosts shall be upon every one that is proud and lofty, and upon every one that is lifted up; and he shall be brought low:","13":"And upon all the cedars of Lebanon, that are high and lifted up, and upon all the oaks of Bashan,","14":"And upon all the high mountains, and upon all the hills that are lifted up,","15":"And upon every high tower, and upon every fenced wall,","16":"And upon all the ships of Tarshish, and upon all pleasant pictures.","17":"And the loftiness of man shall be bowed down, and the haughtiness of men shall be made low: and the Lord alone shall be exalted in that day.","18":"And the idols he shall utterly abolish.","19":"And they shall go into the holes of the rocks, and into the caves of the earth, for fear of the Lord, and for the glory of his majesty, when he ariseth to shake terribly the earth.","20":"In that day a man shall cast his idols of silver, and his idols of gold, which they made each one for himself to worship, to the moles and to the bats;","21":"To go into the clefts of the rocks, and into the tops of the ragged rocks, for fear of the Lord, and for the glory of his majesty, when he ariseth to shake terribly the earth.","22":"Cease ye from man, whose breath is in his nostrils: for wherein is he to be accounted of?"}},
    "3": {"chapter":3,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: In our last chapter Isaiah made it clear that the Israelites must turn to the Lord. They need to stop following their own lusts and their own desires because that will just lead them astray, and it will ultimately get them into trouble. When trouble comes, they will have no way to escape it, no place to hide, and no way to stop it from happening."},{"kind":"para","text":"In this chapter, Isaiah gets into the details of the trouble they will face. They will have a time of prosperity before it all falls apart, but you can bet any money that a people who have turned from the Lord WILL see a very drastic fall when the time comes. Isaiah gives some pretty vivid detail to what that will be like if they don't turn to the Lord in the time that they have."}],"previously":["In our last chapter, Isaiah made it clear that the Israelites must turn to the Lord. They need to stop following their own lusts and desires because that will just lead them astray and ultimately get them into trouble. When trouble comes, they will have no way to escape it, no place to hide, and no way to stop it from happening. In this chapter, Isaiah delves into the details of the trouble they will face. They will experience a time of prosperity before it all falls apart, but you can bet any money that a people who have turned from the Lord will see a very drastic fall when the time comes. Isaiah provides some pretty vivid details of what that will be like if they don’t turn to the Lord in the time that they have."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":7,"title":"A Collapsed Economy","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"We will see over and over again that famines occur throughout the Bible to get God’s people back to Him. In this instance, we are told that God has taken the substance away from Jerusalem and Judah. He’s made it difficult for them to survive because they are doing some heinous and wicked things at this particular juncture of time. We get ideas of what things they were doing throughout some of the other prophets of scripture (Jeremiah and Ezekiel), but I don’t think we can ever really grasp the full scope of reality being pictured here."},{"kind":"para","text":"Passing their children through the fire is certainly heinous and should not be looked on lightly, but that wasn’t the only thing they were doing to earn God’s judgment and wrath. They were treating their neighbors unfairly, killing, raping, destroying, and stealing. It was not a good time for the Israelites at this moment."},{"kind":"thought","text":"### Main Thought: We get ideas of what things they were doing throughout some of the other prophets of scripture (Jeremiah, and Ezekiel), but I don't think we can ever really grasp the full scope of reality being pictured here."}]},{"start":2,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Their leadership will dwindle, and their rise to power will fall. God has taken care of them over and over again, and there should be no reason for them to turn away from Him, and yet that is exactly what they do every time He brings them into a high mountain."},{"kind":"para","text":"Think of it this way (because the idea of them being wayward seems like a strange thing to us): when you are experiencing a good time in your life, do you think about any of the bad things? If you are financially stable for this month or the other, do you think about or worry about affording to pay your bills? Probably not. After some time of being in that mode, you start to become used to it, comfortable even. So you start splurging and buying things you don’t really need or aren’t that important. Perhaps you start spending money on sinful things."},{"kind":"para","text":"After the first time, the Lord says and does nothing, and you feel more comfortable with it. Then, all of a sudden, you are in too deep into this sinful thing, and you start falling behind on your finances. The Lord has a way of turning you back and making you realize how foolish you were to turn away to begin with. Thankfully, when we turn back, He is always there and ready to forgive and move forward."},{"kind":"thought","text":"### Main Thought: Thankfully, when we turn back, He is always there and ready to forgive and move forward."}]},{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God is going to put under-qualified men as their leaders. They will be unlearned, arrogant, and ignorant. They won’t look out for the best interest of the people, and they won’t help the economy move forward. Honestly, this is a great picture of our day today under the Biden administration. Not to get too political here, but we live in an age where we have children as our princes and babies are ruling over us. We have come so far from God, and so we face recessions, inflation, and terrible leadership, because the Lord appoints His people."},{"kind":"para","text":"I find the topic of politics fascinating when you view it from a Biblical perspective. The Bible says that God is sovereign."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Thine, O LORD, is the greatness, and the power, and the glory, and the victory, and the majesty: for all that is in the heaven and in the earth is thine; thine is the kingdom, O LORD, and thou art exalted as head above all. Both riches and honour come of thee, and thou reignest over all; and in thine hand is power and might; and in thine hand it is to make great, and to give strength unto all.\" 1 Chronicles 29:11-12 \"But our God is in the heavens: he hath done whatsoever he hath pleased.\" Psalm 115:3 \"A man's heart deviseth his way: but the LORD directeth his steps.","ref":"Proverbs 16:9"},{"kind":"para","text":"This means that God has a WILL. But WE ALSO have a will."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Behold, I stand at the door, and knock: if any man hear my voice, and open the door, I will come in to him, and will sup with him, and he with me.\" Revelation 3:20 \"For God so loved the world, that he gave his only begotten Son, that whosoever believeth in him should not perish, but have everlasting life.\" John 3:16 \"But as many as received him, to them gave he power to become the sons of God, even to them that believe on his name: Which were born, not of blood, nor of the will of the flesh, nor of the will of man, but of God.","ref":"John 1:12-13"},{"kind":"para","text":"Yet, in it all, God is able to overthrow the will of man."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"The king's heart is in the hand of the LORD, as the rivers of water: he turneth it whithersoever he will. Every way of a man is right in his own eyes: but the LORD pondereth the hearts. To do justice and judgment is more acceptable to the LORD than sacrifice.","ref":"Proverbs 21:1-3"},{"kind":"para","text":"God doesn’t overthrow man’s will very often, and the reason He doesn’t is because He wants man to use his freewill to seek after God’s Sovereign Will. How does He do this if He’s not forcefully controlling man to do His bidding? Through trials. Most men pray when they are about to die from a person holding a gun to them (and perhaps that is the only time they have ever prayed in their entire lives). Most men will search for good when everything around them is nothing but bad (and there is none good but one). Most men will desire a better will when they have been doing nothing but making the wrong choices."},{"kind":"para","text":"My point is, when we have children and babies as our leaders, and we have inflation and recession in our economy, we will be far more likely to seek after a Savior in the Heavens than if everything is going well and we are thriving. So God sets up wicked people to change our wicked hearts back to Him."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Thine, O LORD, is the greatness, and the power, and the glory, and the victory, and the majesty: for all that is in the heaven and in the earth is thine; thine is the kingdom, O LORD, and thou art exalted as head above all. Both riches and honour come of thee, and thou reignest over all; and in thine hand is power and might; and in thine hand it is to make great, and to give strength unto all.","ref":"1 Chronicles 29:11-12"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But our God is in the heavens: he hath done whatsoever he hath pleased.","ref":"Psalm 115:3"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"A man's heart deviseth his way: but the LORD directeth his steps.","ref":"Proverbs 16:9"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Behold, I stand at the door, and knock: if any man hear my voice, and open the door, I will come in to him, and will sup with him, and he with me.","ref":"Revelation 3:20"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For God so loved the world, that he gave his only begotten Son, that whosoever believeth in him should not perish, but have everlasting life.","ref":"John 3:16"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But as many as received him, to them gave he power to become the sons of God, even to them that believe on his name: Which were born, not of blood, nor of the will of the flesh, nor of the will of man, but of God.","ref":"John 1:12-13"},{"kind":"highlight","text":"### Highlight: God doesn't overthrow man's Will very often, and the reason He doesn't is because He wants man to USE his freewill to seek after God's Sovereign Will."},{"kind":"highlight","text":"### Highlight: My point is, when we have children and babies as our leaders, and we have inflation and recession in our economy, we will be far more likely to seek after a Savior in the Heavens then if everything is going well and we are thriving. So God sets up wicked people to change our wicked hearts back to Him."}]},{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Kids today often express disdain for authority figures. They dislike being taught and ruled over, and they resent those who enforce rules or laws. Many schools and higher-ups have contributed to this attitude by teaching children to dislike these aspects of society. We are left wondering why they appear arrogant and disobedient, and why they don’t listen or behave appropriately."},{"kind":"para","text":"The truth is, these children are experiencing a form of oppression. They are being taught incorrect values and behaviors by the very people we have entrusted with their education. We bear the responsibility for potentially damaging their future hopes and goals. It is our duty to train up a child in the right way."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Train up a child in the way he should go: and when he is old, he will not depart from it.","ref":"Proverbs 22:6"},{"kind":"para","text":"It makes you wonder when you read things about Eli's children or Samuel's children and how misbehaved they were. What kind of father were these men? Perhaps they were great judges, or great priests, but they didn't seem to be very good at leading their families..."},{"kind":"thought","text":"### Main Thought: The truth is, they are in the middle of oppression, in the sense that they are being taught the wrong things and the wrong way to behave by the people WE have personally put them under. We are the responsible ones for ruining their future hopes and goals. It is our responsibility to train up a child..."}]},{"start":6,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There is no one willing to take charge of them because of how terrible things have gotten. They will be without rulership, and truthfully, they don’t need to be. They have had God as their ruler for so long in the beginnings, and yet they decided to find a king to rule them. They have gotten their kings, and they have turned from the Lord and depended upon the king. Kings have come in and turned the people from the Lord, and now they are at a point where they are no longer seeking after the rulership of the Lord, and they are only seeking out man’s leading. This is not good for any society, even still today. God IS King, and we must put Him in His rightful place if we are going to expect any sort of good leadership in our land."},{"kind":"highlight","text":"### Highlight: God IS King, and we must put Him in His rightful place if we are going to expect any sort of good leadership in our land."}]}]},{"start":8,"end":15,"title":"Rejecting the Prophets","entries":[{"start":8,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"It wasn’t as if they were just doing heinous things. They were literally doing the very things that God strictly commanded them NOT to do. Our sinful, fleshly nature is such today."},{"kind":"para","text":"It’s like if there was a red button that says, “Don’t push me.” We are enticed to push that button because our sinful nature likes to push the limits of what we can and can’t do just to see what happens. Ultimately it’s not for any particular reason. We just have a nature that tells us to rebel."},{"kind":"para","text":"Our sinful fleshly desires like to push red buttons all the time. We push God’s buttons when we use our free will. We always do the wrong things, and in doing such, we purposely provoke the Lord, and then have the tenacity to ask “Why?”"},{"kind":"thought","text":"### Main Thought: We push God's buttons when we use our freewill's. We always do the wrong things, and in doing such, we purposely provoke the Lord, and then have the tenacity to ask \"Why?\""}]},{"start":9,"end":9,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"They aren't even trying to hide the fact that they are sinning. They are enjoying their sin, and they do it in the open, and they want others to be a part of it too. The Sodomites were not a very good example to follow. They were the rapists in the days of Genesis. It was a city fully given over to sexual abuse. The Israelites are proud to be like the Sodomites."},{"kind":"thought","text":"### Main Thought: They aren't even trying to hide the fact that they are sinning. They are enjoying their sin, and they do it in the open, and they want others to be a part of it too."}]},{"start":10,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Even in the midst of a perverse people, God takes care of those that are seeking after Him. He takes care of His own. Those that know the Lord, love the Lord, and are serving the Lord, they might be few, but God will see them and protect them."},{"kind":"highlight","text":"### Highlight: Those that know the Lord, love the Lord, and are serving the Lord, might be few, but God will see them and protect them."}]},{"start":11,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Those that don't seek Him will not be taken care of by the Lord. Or, perhaps, we can say they will be \"taken care of\" just in the same way that the trash will be \"taken care of.\""},{"kind":"thought","text":"### Main Thought: Or, perhaps, we can say they will be \"taken care of\" just in the same way that the trash will be \"taken care of.\""}]},{"start":12,"end":14,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God has sent people to plead with these individuals, doing everything possible to encourage them to turn back. This situation exemplifies the ongoing conflict between God’s Will and man’s Will. God’s Will influences those who yield to it, enabling them to witness to others about His Will. In contrast, man’s Will is often driven by a hunger for lust and idolatry. When one person is willing to follow God’s Will, God typically places that person in a position of influence. However, there are few who are willing to be influenced by the Lord. Consequently, many people ignore or reject the words of God’s people."},{"kind":"para","text":"It is important to remember that the writer of this book, Isaiah, is a prophet. He is a man of God, commissioned by the Lord to witness to these people about their disgraceful acts and teach them to repent and turn back to the Lord. Yet, they refuse to listen. In fact, several individuals have approached them to point out their wrongdoings and offer guidance on how to correct them. Despite this, they remain unresponsive."},{"kind":"highlight","text":"### Highlight: God's Will will influence a man to whom is yielded to it so that he can witness to others about God's Will. Man's Will is only yielded to his hunger for lust and idolatry."}]},{"start":15,"end":15,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Why do they do this? It seems to even be lost on God. He knows that they are wicked because of the sin that entered into the world, but when God is trying to help them, all they do is hurt God in return. It’s a very sad reality to know that there are people (and they are in the masses) that are purposely desiring to hurt God. God can take it, of course, but it’s still a miserable thing to the Lord that there are so many that are willing to reject Him rather than listen to His plea for them."},{"kind":"para","text":"He doesn’t want to destroy them, but they are not giving Him a choice. He gives them chance after chance, but nothing will turn them away from their lusts. God is still in the business of giving chances, but people are still not willing to turn away today. The gospel message is more prominent and more open than it ever has been, and yet they still don’t want to hear it. How cruel and wicked of a person you have to be to reject the greatest truth about your souls ever given to man as a gift from the Lord."},{"kind":"highlight","text":"### Highlight: He knows that they are wicked because of the sin that entered into the world, but when God is trying to help them, all they do is hurt God in return."},{"kind":"highlight","text":"### Highlight: The gospel message is more prominent and more open than it ever has been, and yet they still don't want to hear it."}]}]},{"start":16,"end":26,"title":"Beauty to Ashes","entries":[{"start":16,"end":17,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Isaiah is pointing out that the women of his day are enticing men with their bodies rather than with their holiness. They are acting almost as a “prostitute” is maybe the tamest way of thinking about it. They are purposely trying to entice men with their looks and their clothing rather than trying to marry and encourage men."},{"kind":"para","text":"So the Lord sends in a disease that will be very uncomfortable for both the girls and the boys. That is the case still today. There are many young men and women who sleep around today, and all it takes is one mistake to ruin the rest of your life with a disease. This is yet another reason why it’s important to wait for marriage to entertain the idea of sex. Otherwise, you are playing with fire, and you WILL likely get burned."},{"kind":"para","text":"We live in a day where there are more diseases transmitted than ever before, and instead of our schools and leaders encouraging marriage, they are encouraging “safe” practices. There is no safe practice outside of marriage, you can be sure of that."},{"kind":"thought","text":"### Main Thought: Isaiah is pointing out that the women of his day are enticing men with their bodies, rather than with their holiness."},{"kind":"highlight","text":"### Highlight: We live in a day where there are more diseases transmitted than ever before, and instead of our schools and leaders encouraging marriage, they are encouraging \"safe\" practices. There is no safe practice outside of marriage, you can be sure of that."}]},{"start":18,"end":23,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Isaiah has observed some aspects of their attire and actions. In the 20 articles he references, he emphasizes that there is nothing inherently wrong with what they are wearing. Can you identify one item that is inappropriate to wear? Clearly, it is the reason and manner in which they wear it that makes it problematic. We should strive to dress our best, but we must avoid dressing immodestly in the process."},{"kind":"thought","text":"### Main Thought: Name one thing here that is not okay to wear... Obviously, it's the reason and way they are wearing it that makes it wrong."}]},{"start":24,"end":24,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The women’s beauty will deteriorate with their collapsing economy. Perhaps that is a decent enough sign to see how the economy is doing. Are the women dressing their best anymore? If not, can they afford to do so, or do they have the desire to do it? Why? And it’s likely because they can’t afford it, or because they just don’t have a desire to. A depressed and oppressed people will find it hard to get out of bed in the morning."},{"kind":"para","text":"Our nation today talks a lot about oppression from their mob pits and their fake news outlets. How can we tell if they are truly oppressed? Well, do they have the energy to scream and complain about their oppression in the streets and on TV? Yes? Then they aren’t oppressed. An oppressed person is so undone and so stuck that they can’t find a reason to even get out of bed in the morning, let alone to complain about their oppression. The only thing a truly oppressed person will do is plead with the Lord and pray for hope to come."},{"kind":"para","text":"The people that are screaming on TV are usually those that try and give a “voice” to the oppressed, but they themselves aren’t oppressed. In fact, if they want to help the oppressed, screaming about it in mobs and on television is the worst way to help them. Give your time, your spirit (that is if you have the Lord), and resources to them personally. That will help their oppression."},{"kind":"thought","text":"### Main Thought: Perhaps that is a decent enough sign to see how the economy is doing. Are the women dressing their best anymore? If not, can they afford to do so, or do they have the desire to do it? Why? And it's likely because they can't afford it, or because they just don't have a desire to. A depressed and oppressed people will find it hard to get out of bed in the morning."},{"kind":"highlight","text":"### Highlight: How can we tell if they are truly oppressed? Well do they have the energy to scream and complain about their oppression in the streets and on TV? Yes? Then they aren't oppressed. An oppressed person is so undone and so stuck that they can't find a reason to even get out of bed in the morning, let alone to complain about their oppression. The only thing a truly oppressed person will do is plead with the Lord and pray for hope to come. The people that are screaming on TV are usually those that try and give a \"voice\" to the oppressed, but they themselves aren't oppressed. In fact, if they want to help the oppressed, screaming about it in mobs and on television is the worst way to help them. Give your time, your spirit (that is if you have the Lord), and resources to them personally. That will help their oppression."}]},{"start":25,"end":26,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The strongest among them won’t even be a match for the enemy anymore. America has a strong military, but with such weak leadership and a mass exodus of the church, we have no actual strength to win anything. The Lord has been faithful to our country for generations. Our forefathers, being just and righteous men themselves, have set up a biblical structure for us to follow. However, when we are not following that structure biblically, we lose our strength in freedom and become a people of oppression. When we turn away from God, we can watch our society crumble and fall, and lament and mourn at the gates because of the desolation of it. We CANNOT, however, ask how we got here when the Lord has sent people by the DOZENS to preach His Word."},{"kind":"thought","text":"### Main Thought: America has a strong military, but with such week leadership, and a mass exodus of the church, we have no actual strength to win anything."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":9},{"start":10,"end":10},{"start":11,"end":11},{"start":12,"end":14},{"start":15,"end":15},{"start":16,"end":17},{"start":18,"end":23},{"start":24,"end":24},{"start":25,"end":26}],"verses":{"1":"For, behold, the Lord, the Lord of hosts, doth take away from Jerusalem and from Judah the stay and the staff, the whole stay of bread, and the whole stay of water.","2":"The mighty man, and the man of war, the judge, and the prophet, and the prudent, and the ancient,","3":"The captain of fifty, and the honourable man, and the counsellor, and the cunning artificer, and the eloquent orator.","4":"And I will give children to be their princes, and babes shall rule over them.","5":"And the people shall be oppressed, every one by another, and every one by his neighbour: the child shall behave himself proudly against the ancient, and the base against the honourable.","6":"When a man shall take hold of his brother of the house of his father, saying, Thou hast clothing, be thou our ruler, and let this ruin be under thy hand:","7":"In that day shall he swear, saying, I will not be an healer; for in my house is neither bread nor clothing: make me not a ruler of the people.","8":"For Jerusalem is ruined, and Judah is fallen: because their tongue and their doings are against the Lord, to provoke the eyes of his glory.","9":"The shew of their countenance doth witness against them; and they declare their sin as Sodom, they hide it not. Woe unto their soul! for they have rewarded evil unto themselves.","10":"Say ye to the righteous, that it shall be well with him: for they shall eat the fruit of their doings.","11":"Woe unto the wicked! it shall be ill with him: for the reward of his hands shall be given him.","12":"As for my people, children are their oppressors, and women rule over them. O my people, they which lead thee cause thee to err, and destroy the way of thy paths.","13":"The Lord standeth up to plead, and standeth to judge the people.","14":"The Lord will enter into judgment with the ancients of his people, and the princes thereof: for ye have eaten up the vineyard; the spoil of the poor is in your houses.","15":"What mean ye that ye beat my people to pieces, and grind the faces of the poor? saith the Lord God of hosts.","16":"Moreover the Lord saith, Because the daughters of Zion are haughty, and walk with stretched forth necks and wanton eyes, walking and mincing as they go, and making a tinkling with their feet:","17":"Therefore the Lord will smite with a scab the crown of the head of the daughters of Zion, and the Lord will discover their secret parts.","18":"In that day the Lord will take away the bravery of their tinkling ornaments about their feet, and their cauls, and their round tires like the moon,","19":"The chains, and the bracelets, and the mufflers,","20":"The bonnets, and the ornaments of the legs, and the headbands, and the tablets, and the earrings,","21":"The rings, and nose jewels,","22":"The changeable suits of apparel, and the mantles, and the wimples, and the crisping pins,","23":"The glasses, and the fine linen, and the hoods, and the vails.","24":"And it shall come to pass, that instead of sweet smell there shall be stink; and instead of a girdle a rent; and instead of well set hair baldness; and instead of a stomacher a girding of sackcloth; and burning instead of beauty.","25":"Thy men shall fall by the sword, and thy mighty in the war.","26":"And her gates shall lament and mourn; and she being desolate shall sit upon the ground."}},
    "4": {"chapter":4,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: In our last chapter, Isaiah warns the Israelites about their future collapse if they don't turn to the Lord quickly and repent. Sadly, they don't repent, and they continue to reject the prophets that God sends their way. Because of this, God will turn everything that they hold dear into nothing, and they will be given over to a life that is lacking and wanting because they have gone so far away from the Lord. It's not as though they have just done a few bad sins... No, they were purposely doing heinous things that were in exact opposition to the Lord's commands, and so God must do something about it to get His children back on track (which is what leads to their captivity to Babylon)."},{"kind":"para","text":"In this chapter, Isaiah reveals a few others things that will take place, and gives some hope and peace to those that are still for the Lord. Though a majority of the people in Israel are doing everything in their power to go against God and His commands, there is still a small remenant there that is living in obedience, and God will give protection."}],"previously":["In our last chapter, Isaiah warns the Israelites about their future collapse if they don’t turn to the Lord quickly and repent. Sadly, they don’t repent and continue to reject the prophets that God sends their way. Because of this, God will turn everything that they hold dear into nothing, and they will be given over to a life that is lacking and wanting because they have gone so far away from the Lord. It’s not as though they have just done a few bad sins; no, they were purposely doing heinous things that were in exact opposition to the Lord’s commands, and so God must do something about it to get His children back on track, which leads to their captivity to Babylon. In this chapter, Isaiah reveals a few other things that will take place and gives some hope and peace to those who are still for the Lord. Though a majority of the people in Israel are doing everything in their power to go against God and His commands, there is still a small remnant there that is living in obedience, and God will give them protection."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":1,"title":"Life During Wartime","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Now, much in the same way, the Babylonian captivity that the Israelites were captured in will mimic how the end of times will be. There's a reason that Babylon is mentioned quite a bit in Revelation."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And there followed another angel, saying, Babylon is fallen, is fallen, that great city, because she made all nations drink of the wine of the wrath of her fornication.\" Revelation 14:8 \"And the great city was divided into three parts, and the cities of the nations fell: and great Babylon came in remembrance before God, to give unto her the cup of the wine of the fierceness of his wrath.\" Revelation 16:19 \"And upon her forehead was a name written, MYSTERY, BABYLON THE GREAT, THE MOTHER OF HARLOTS AND ABOMINATIONS OF THE EARTH.\" Revelation 17:5 \"And he cried mightily with a strong voice, saying, Babylon the great is fallen, is fallen, and is become the habitation of devils, and the hold of every foul spirit, and a cage of every unclean and hateful bird...Standing afar off for the fear of her torment, saying, Alas, alas, that great city Babylon, that mighty city! for in one hour is thy judgment come...And a mighty angel took up a stone like a great millstone, and cast it into the sea, saying, Thus with violence shall that great city Babylon be thrown down, and shall be found no more at all.","ref":"Revelation 18:2;10;21"},{"kind":"para","text":"Who the new Babylon will be is hugely up for debate. I have my guesses, but I cannot say for sure. All I will say is that this captivity won’t be a pretty one, and the next captivity will not be pretty either. The men of war will be decimated, so much so that seven women will be married to one man. It will empower the women, and they will all have their own jobs and work to do, and they will be very desperate for change and help. It will be as if the roles are reversed in those days."},{"kind":"para","text":"The men that they marry will not be men of war. They will be men of submission. Perhaps the men will stay home and the women will work. I really don’t know. It’s likely that the women will not have very good or comfortable jobs, but jobs that require them to do some pretty heinous things for income’s sake. This actually happens quite a bit during wartime, and it leaves a lot of very sad women alone due to casualties."}]}]},{"start":2,"end":6,"title":"Safety Will Come","entries":[{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Again, it’s very obviously connected to both the Babylonian captivity and the end of days. God’s chosen, those who have accepted Christ and are living for Him, will dwell in safety. They will be satisfied in the Lord’s provision and not bogged down by the loss of materialism like the rest of the world."},{"kind":"para","text":"“The branch” can always be associated with the Lord when we read it. Jesus is the branch of the Lord. “Branch” here means “sprout.” He will sprout when things are desperate and in waste. Of course, His first coming was in love and salvation. His second coming will be a little different…"}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There will be stragglers both in the Babylonian captivity and in the Great Tribulation who will be of God’s children. They will be protected by the Lord to survive these periods for His future prosperity and Kingdom establishment. I have perhaps made a valuable connection that should be recognized (or at least thought of) as we dive deeper into scripture and into prophecies like this. Anytime the Bible (especially in the Old Testament) makes mention of future prophecies, they are likely small images of something greater to come. Prophecies of the Lord are build-ups."},{"kind":"para","text":"For instance, we see the tribes of Israel bowing to Joseph. That is a symbol of what Joseph went through, of course (as we know that they eventually do bow to Joseph because he was in charge of Pharaoh’s provision), but that is also a symbol of the Israelites’ main mission (which is to bow before the Lord Jesus Christ). That is a build-up prophecy. This could be treated in the same way, and perhaps there are some connections we can make to the last days. Maybe those that are killed in those days will be resurrected bodily? We see that those who have died in Christ were risen with Him physically."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Jesus, when he had cried again with a loud voice, yielded up the ghost. And, behold, the veil of the temple was rent in twain from the top to the bottom; and the earth did quake, and the rocks rent; And the graves were opened; and many bodies of the saints which slept arose, And came out of the graves after his resurrection, and went into the holy city, and appeared unto many.","ref":"Matthew 27:50-53"},{"kind":"para","text":"Maybe there will be a time of this during those days, as Jesus’ bodily resurrection symbolized more than just defeat over death. It was proof that He can raise the dead back to life. Perhaps I’m looking too deeply. I just find it fascinating that this bit of the Bible is here, right after Jesus dies and comes back to life. This is certainly more than just a coincidence, and it’s there for more than just a one-time purpose. God doesn’t work in one-time purposes. In fact, God spends most of His time throughout all of scripture repeating the same messages over and over again. Maybe, perhaps, in different ways, but the core of the message is the same. The whole Bible is a gospel message if we read it correctly. Isaiah is certainly a gospel account (as we will get to in the next few chapters)."},{"kind":"para","text":"The sad thing is, most people read it either for personal gain or they read it in the wrong context. They pick it apart rather than read it as a whole. Recently, we had a group of men go through the entire Bible in 30 days. One man put together this whole list of what order we can read the Bible in so it’s in a proper context and the story flows smoothly. After we were done, it seemed everyone had a different theme to hold onto, but every theme all related to Jesus in some way. It all led up to the gospel message. When we pick the Bible apart, we lose the theme of Christ. We must keep the Bible together in order to rightly divide the word of Truth."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Study to shew thyself approved unto God, a workman that needeth not to be ashamed, rightly dividing the word of truth.","ref":"2 Timothy 2:15"}]},{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There will be cleansing that takes place, and the evil of this world will be purged of their sin and destruction. Those who have killed and destroyed will be put in their rightful place. God will also prepare His people for His coming. Many of us are not prepared. If I can be quite frank with you, I feel underprepared as well. Perhaps I will never feel fully prepared, and I do want the Lord to have a proper work in me before He comes again. He is doing a work; this much I know, and so we are being more prepared every day. That is why we are currently here today. We are preparing ourselves for the Lord’s coming."},{"kind":"para","text":"While love and salvation were the anthem of His first coming, judgment and burning will be the theme of His second coming; we can be sure of that."}]},{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Another proper prophecy is expanded here, portraying the image of the Passover. Every house marked with the blood of the lamb was protected by the Lord. In the end, that is what God will do in Zion. He will protect those who live with Him there. It will not just be His temple that is protected; it will be our homes as well if we are dwelling with Him. This is a great promise, and it’s one that the Israelites were to remember every day and celebrate often."},{"kind":"para","text":"It seems, at least at this point in the Bible, that they have forgotten this and have cast it off completely. They don’t care about remembering their first captivity, and that is why they are being held captive again. It’s also why the world will fall into it in the end. Israel is just a small symbol of the church today. God has not just saved the land of Israel anymore; He has brought salvation to the whole world. Now, we all suffer together or prosper together, depending on the people’s directive to the Lord."}]},{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Inflation has been at an extreme high lately. Because of this, it has been difficult to afford basic essentials and necessities. One of those needs is electricity and gas. The other day, I was invited to the church, and I was a bit hesitant to go simply because it has been raining like crazy the last few days. I went anyway (people don’t know what they are doing when rain is coming from the sky. It’s like California drivers are freaked out by water), and after I got there, I basked in the dryness and warmth. I haven’t been warm for a bit (too expensive to run the heater). It was a bit of a relief!"},{"kind":"para","text":"In those times, God’s presence and house will be a refuge for those seeking protection and security. It will be a place where the heater can be run when it’s hot, and the AC can be run when it’s cold. You don’t have to search the world for peace and safety (especially in those days) because you will not find it. You must go to the house of God for it, and that is the only place you will dwell safely. It should be this even right now. We should be able to go to the house of God and feel at peace and in safety while we are there. If you do not, perhaps your place of worship is not the house of God? Or maybe some things need to change, and the Spirit needs to be refilled?"},{"kind":"para","text":"That is the real problem when we are in times of trial. It’s not about the war happening outside; it’s about the lack of Spirit happening in your own heart. “The heart of the problem is the problem of the heart.” That is the truth for both you and me."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":6}],"verses":{"1":"And in that day seven women shall take hold of one man, saying, We will eat our own bread, and wear our own apparel: only let us be called by thy name, to take away our reproach.","2":"In that day shall the branch of the Lord be beautiful and glorious, and the fruit of the earth shall be excellent and comely for them that are escaped of Israel.","3":"And it shall come to pass, that he that is left in Zion, and he that remaineth in Jerusalem, shall be called holy, even every one that is written among the living in Jerusalem:","4":"When the Lord shall have washed away the filth of the daughters of Zion, and shall have purged the blood of Jerusalem from the midst thereof by the spirit of judgment, and by the spirit of burning.","5":"And the Lord will create upon every dwelling place of mount Zion, and upon her assemblies, a cloud and smoke by day, and the shining of a flaming fire by night: for upon all the glory shall be a defence.","6":"And there shall be a tabernacle for a shadow in the day time from the heat, and for a place of refuge, and for a covert from storm and from rain."}},
    "5": {"chapter":5,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: In our last chapter, Isaiah warns the people about the coming difficulties they will face. He tells them that things will become exceedingly difficult for them, and desires that they would turn before it comes to pass. He also talks about safety for the people (the only true safety being in the Savior of course), and the necessity to take his words seriously."},{"kind":"para","text":"In this chapter, he explains why these things are going to come to pass, and he gives creedance to the Savior as his \"beloved\" and worth turning from our sins for."}],"previously":["In our last chapter, Isaiah warns the people about the coming difficulties they will face. He tells them that things will become exceedingly difficult for them and desires that they would turn before it comes to pass. He also talks about safety for the people, emphasizing that the only true safety is in the Savior, of course, and the necessity to take his words seriously. In this chapter, he explains why these things are going to come to pass and gives credence to the Savior as his “beloved” and worth turning from our sins for."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":2,"title":"A Song to the Beloved","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Isaiah is bringing out his inner Solomon with a song about his beloved. His beloved, of course, as in the Song of Solomon, is Jesus Christ. The vineyard will be explored more deeply in a moment, but we can recognize that Isaiah is speaking about Christ’s redemption of Israel based on these first few chapters. We get the picture that Isaiah is anticipating the coming of a Savior for God’s people, who are very heavily turned away from the Lord at this time."},{"kind":"para","text":"The thing is, as we’ve viewed the first few chapters, he is speaking about a multi-capture. Israel will be taken by Babylon and ruled by Romans, but in the future (that is, towards the end of humanity itself), it will be taken over and held captive by the whole Earth. This song is a quick song of love for the Savior (that is, Christ) who will protect His people and draw them out of their capture."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Here’s the Lord’s garden. He put in the best of the best. I don’t think any of us can argue that God did not present His best to the Israelites (or to humanity as a whole). God cannot send forth any better salvation to this Earth than His own Son."},{"kind":"para","text":"The problem with the garden is not with the seed planted. It’s not with the water produced, or the keeper keeping it. The problem with the garden is the branches from the vine. They were to be the best grapes to gather, and instead they were “wild grapes.” They were grapes, but they tried to act as if they didn’t know what garden they belonged in. “Wild grapes” means “worthless” or (my personal favorite) “stinkberries.” I don’t even know if they understood what they were. That is what Isaiah is getting at here. They were not acting like the fruit they were given."}]}]},{"start":3,"end":7,"title":"A False Prosperity","entries":[{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"If we look to the Lord and His providence, which one looks better? If we consider Isaiah and the rest of the land at that time, which one would we deem more righteous? Which one appears more attuned to the Lord? I think anyone with a basic knowledge of scripture would agree that Isaiah was set apart. He was doing well in his following of the Lord, and it would have been far wiser for the Israelites to take Isaiah seriously in his direction so they could turn from their evil, rather than ignoring him and rejecting his message altogether."},{"kind":"para","text":"The crazy thing is, they could judge Isaiah and the vineyard themselves. They could not say that the vineyard was proper. They couldn’t claim they were doing such a great job without the help of the Lord. They were living in luxury, sure, but it was the world’s definition of it. It was not a Heavenly luxury. They don’t even know what luxury looks like anymore… It’s still so today. The world (and even Israel) have forsaken Isaiah’s rule of judgment here. They have still forsaken the beloved. Yet, if they were to look at the world around them and see how far gone from the Lord we have all become, they could learn to love this Savior just as much as Isaiah speaks about here."}]},{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God has kept His vineyard perfect. He has done everything in His power and strength to get these men to turn to Him and turn away from their wickedness. He won’t just force the relationship on them. He won’t force them to turn to Him and love Him. Rather, He wants them to do that on their own, and you would think they would have by the simple fact that He continues to provide for them over and over again. But they don’t, and so God must show how foolish they are being."}]},{"start":5,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God is going to take away the protective wall He has placed for them and allow them to be uprooted from their comfort and wickedness. This refers to the capture they will face from the nations around them. They should have been taken over a long time ago, and they should have well understood that, yet they seem to continue to be prosperous. They will now learn that the only reason they have survived as long as they have is simply because the Lord gave them protection. He will stop the increase in the land, and it will become quite desolate. Even still today, it’s quite desolate. The Lord has strongly judged this nation, and the scars are still there to prove it. That’s why it’s so confusing and interesting to me that they have rejected the message of Isaiah even still to this day."}]},{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The vineyard, as mentioned earlier, is referred to as the house of Israel. The men of Judah were the vine intended to produce good grapes. However, they produced “stinkberries” and showed no desire to please the Lord in their actions. He desired that they judge righteously, but instead, they oppressed their own people. “Oppression” means “bloodshed.” They were not merely keeping people quiet or making them poor; they were literally killing their own people, whether through poverty or other physical means, as we can infer from their wickedness. The Lord wanted them to prosper in righteousness, but instead, all He heard was the cry of those being mistreated and murdered."},{"kind":"para","text":"This is just one particular issue with the land of that day. We have already discussed the issue of prostitution, unfair dealings, polygamy, rape, and infant sacrifice. These people were not well. They think they are, but they are far from prosperous."}]}]},{"start":8,"end":10,"title":"A Woe of Unity","entries":[{"start":8,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I like Isaiah because there is a lot of reference to Christ, and also to how Christ spoke. “Woe” is a term used to describe immense grief and horror. When scripture gives a woe, it is a very bad thing. Yes, we know that scripture is full of great things and happy thoughts, but we also have quite a few “woe’s” to address as well."},{"kind":"para","text":"Isaiah’s words are very similar to how Christ would present scripture. We start off with some woes here (six of them) just like Christ gave some woes as well (including in the book of Revelation)."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! for ye shut up the kingdom of heaven against men: for ye neither go in yourselves, neither suffer ye them that are entering to go in. Woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! for ye devour widows' houses, and for a pretence make long prayer: therefore ye shall receive the greater damnation. Woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! for ye compass sea and land to make one proselyte, and when he is made, ye make him twofold more the child of hell than yourselves. Woe unto you, ye blind guides, which say, Whosoever shall swear by the temple, it is nothing; but whosoever shall swear by the gold of the temple, he is a debtor! Ye fools and blind: for whether is greater, the gold, or the temple that sanctifieth the gold? And, Whosoever shall swear by the altar, it is nothing; but whosoever sweareth by the gift that is upon it, he is guilty. Ye fools and blind: for whether is greater, the gift, or the altar that sanctifieth the gift? Whoso therefore shall swear by the altar, sweareth by it, and by all things thereon. And whoso shall swear by the temple, sweareth by it, and by him that dwelleth therein. And he that shall swear by heaven, sweareth by the throne of God, and by him that sitteth thereon. Woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! for ye pay tithe of mint and anise and cummin, and have omitted the weightier matters of the law, judgment, mercy, and faith: these ought ye to have done, and not to leave the other undone. Ye blind guides, which strain at a gnat, and swallow a camel. Woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! for ye make clean the outside of the cup and of the platter, but within they are full of extortion and excess. Thou blind Pharisee, cleanse first that which is within the cup and platter, that the outside of them may be clean also. Woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! for ye are like unto whited sepulchres, which indeed appear beautiful outward, but are within full of dead men's bones, and of all uncleanness. Even so ye also outwardly appear righteous unto men, but within ye are full of hypocrisy and iniquity. Woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! because ye build the tombs of the prophets, and garnish the sepulchres of the righteous, And say, If we had been in the days of our fathers, we would not have been partakers with them in the blood of the prophets. Wherefore ye be witnesses unto yourselves, that ye are the children of them which killed the prophets. Fill ye up then the measure of your fathers. Ye serpents, ye generation of vipers, how can ye escape the damnation of hell? Wherefore, behold, I send unto you prophets, and wise men, and scribes: and some of them ye shall kill and crucify; and some of them shall ye scourge in your synagogues, and persecute them from city to city: That upon you may come all the righteous blood shed upon the earth, from the blood of righteous Abel unto the blood of Zacharias son of Barachias, whom ye slew between the temple and the altar. Verily I say unto you, All these things shall come upon this generation. O Jerusalem, Jerusalem, thou that killest the prophets, and stonest them which are sent unto thee, how often would I have gathered thy children together, even as a hen gathereth her chickens under her wings, and ye would not! Behold, your house is left unto you desolate. For I say unto you, Ye shall not see me henceforth, till ye shall say, Blessed is he that cometh in the name of the Lord.","ref":"Matthew 23:13-39"},{"kind":"para","text":"Think about that for a second. Nothing has changed from Isaiah to Christ. It’s likely that not much has changed from Christ’s death to His second coming either. The woes are just as brutal. Here, Isaiah gives the first of six woes and starts by saying that it will be disastrous for those who try to unite in this land “house to house, field to field” because it will all be destroyed and taken away."},{"kind":"para","text":"Uniting with the wicked is never a good idea, no matter what era or land you are living in. You might think you are making yourself stronger by uniting with those who seem strong, but if they are drawing you away from the Lord and His grace, you will only become more of an enemy to Him. No matter how many hands join together against the Lord, God always wins."}]},{"start":9,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God sends famines quite a bit through scripture. As a rule of thumb that I’ve learned while reading scripture, if famine is coming, it is because God is going to turn His people back to Him, and He will increase the land once again. Today, we can still take this into account. We are currently facing a bit of a famine. More prominently, we are facing inflation like we have never seen before. But things are starting to become difficult and hard to get. Gas is at an all-time high, eggs were about $10 a carton, milk had disappeared from the shelves (still difficult to get today in California), and toilet paper had vanished (to the point where people would wake up earlier just to get toilet paper when it was delivered to the store). Obviously, these are not easy or convenient times to be living in. We have been living on Ramen noodles for months now because we can’t afford to buy TV dinners or groceries to cook (perhaps I should start a farm?). I’m not saying all of this to receive pity (that does me no good anyway). I say this because I know that every time this happens throughout ALL of history, the Lord uses it and it produces amazing miracles for His glory. That is what I am anticipating. I know to look out for those signs now."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Israelites at this time will not understand why they are going through what they are going through until much later. When they are finally made free from their captivity (ish), they then become aware of what they had been missing all along. Nehemiah is a great book to represent this."}]}]},{"start":11,"end":17,"title":"A Woe of Crutches","entries":[{"start":11,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Woe unto them still today. There is nothing good in drinking to numb your pain. Even worse is they forget the Lord while they do this..."}]},{"start":12,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"They have leaned on their provision and their income as a means of their prosperity. The LORD needs to be the land’s prosperity if it is to flourish. I’ve noticed a shift in our government and culture today that pointedly makes it obvious that we are not a nation under God anymore. God is a background character in the lives of our nation."},{"kind":"para","text":"We have experienced a lot of this for a very long time now, and I think the emphasis behind playing politics this way is so that we can say (in the end) “Look what our hands did without God. God is not real nor important for a mighty nation.” Yet, when we look at our society today, we just see a nation in decline and collapse. We were better off with the Lord, and somehow we still want to try and trick ourselves into believing that if we just “hold strong” to our rejection of Him it will get better."},{"kind":"para","text":"How much longer do we wait before we turn back to Him? Do we wait for the whole nation to collapse to a point of no return? Do we wait until OUR captivity?"}]},{"start":13,"end":13,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Drinking often becomes a crutch for people. Many individuals abuse alcohol because it’s easier than actually dealing with their problems. If we can numb the pain and feel good about our circumstances, even for a short time, we will find a way to do it so we don’t have to worry or feel. However, pressure is God’s way of working on you, and when we try to block that with alcohol, we are ultimately saying, “I don’t want to learn or grow.” At that point, you become weak-minded and impossible."},{"kind":"para","text":"I think the growing process is painful for everyone, but there is a place today where you can go to get some help for the battle. It’s called the church. Now, I understand that not all churches are there for your best interest, and many of them won’t help you through your sins or addictions, but there are churches out there that will. I pray that I can be a voice of help and encouragement to everyone who is struggling in this world."}]},{"start":14,"end":14,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Death takes a hold on everyone, and the grave is satisfied with all of the souls of people. However, when we have the Savior, the grave does not receive our soul. There are different references to hell in scripture, but a good portion of the time (both in the Old and New Testament) it is speaking about the grave."},{"kind":"para","text":"These people are leading themselves to their own death. It was not by the Lord’s desire that they would live this way and reject His righteousness; that was the grave they dug for themselves."}]},{"start":15,"end":16,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"While the world falls apart around us, God still will get the glory in the end. That is the ultimate goal for all of this. They are falling away from the Lord and robbing God of the glory that He deserves. He has been a father to His people, but they have not been children in return to Him. He wants them to have a close relationship, and instead, they have rejected every opportunity to get to know Him. But their captivity will turn them around and require them to search out God’s provision."}]},{"start":17,"end":17,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God wants to bring His lambs back to the fold, and so He will do what He must in order to get that to happen. His sheep are valuable to Him. It's something else that Jesus will be sure to make very well known to the people of His day."}]}]},{"start":18,"end":19,"title":"A Woe of Sin","entries":[{"start":18,"end":19,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"These people didn’t care that they were sinning. They didn’t care that they were doing evil and heinous things to their neighbors and to the people who were innocent. In fact, they seemed to enjoy mistreating people. They were going out of their way to literally provoke the Lord to anger."},{"kind":"para","text":"Our society is not much different today. We may not have fallen into the same level of disgrace, but we are certainly very close to it. Our world likes to inflict pain on the innocent and kind-hearted people. While it seems that they are getting away with it here on Earth in our own vision, God is taking note of it, and they won’t get away with it forever."}]}]},{"start":20,"end":20,"title":"A Woe of Lies","entries":[{"start":20,"end":20,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Much of our society today encourages people to “believe your own truth.” This mindset, possibly prevalent in the past as well, suggests that truth is relative to one’s feelings and not defined by any existing standard. Teachers, state leaders, and national leaders seem to embrace this view. Personally, I find it simpler when we could assert, “This is truth because it’s obvious and can be proven,” rather than “this is true if you want it to be true.”"},{"kind":"para","text":"When we label evil as “good” or lies as “truths” (and vice versa), we diminish the value of truth. In fact, we make truth cheap if it cannot be proven. Consider the story of a man who went to a jeweler with diamonds he had found. He confidently declared, “Now, I know what I got and I want a couple million dollars for these huge diamonds.” The clerk, skeptical, replied, “Well, I have to inspect them first and then we can negotiate a price.” The man insisted, “Go for it! You will see that it’s worth exactly that and you can’t convince me otherwise.” The clerk examined the bag and revealed massive diamonds, astonishing the onlookers. However, as soon as the clerk picked up a diamond, he declared, “Sir, I cannot buy these from you.” The man, angered, asked, “Why not?!” The clerk explained, “Because these are plastic…”"},{"kind":"para","text":"Perhaps today, that man would want to file a lawsuit, truly believing those are real diamonds. Our society might even support his claim. However, the truth is, the clerk recognized a diamond when he saw one, and it was obvious that these were not real. When we know the truth, we cannot call anything else what the truth really is. Only the truth is the truth. Dress up a lie however you want, but there can only be one truth."}]}]},{"start":21,"end":21,"title":"A Woe of Foolishness","entries":[{"start":21,"end":21,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Keeping the analogy of the man with the diamonds, he truly thought he had something valuable. He was not willing to let anyone convince him otherwise. He was “wise in his own eyes.” His truth just brought him into foolishness rather than into wealth. That is what happens when we think we are so clever in our own thoughts."},{"kind":"para","text":"Be very cautious about giving your own thoughts on a matter with the Biblical grace to back you up. Otherwise, you are in danger of living in a “Woe” from the Lord."}]}]},{"start":22,"end":24,"title":"A Woe of False Power","entries":[{"start":22,"end":23,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Drunk men often think they are more powerful than they actually are. They attempt to rob people who are weaker than them, and in doing so, they rob those who are truly innocent and godly. Frequently, it is the godly men that the drunkards hate the most because they feel as if the godliest among them have far more than they ever could."},{"kind":"para","text":"A drinker believes that his best in this life is found in a bottle. In contrast, the Christian knows that there is nothing worth this life except to seek the Lord with everything he has. What a Christian man wants to do is help those transfer their longing for the bottle to numb the pain to a longing for the Lord to suffice their needs."},{"kind":"para","text":"However, that is not how the drinkers take it. Instead, they do things to provoke the Lord to anger, and the next verse illustrates that end."}]},{"start":24,"end":24,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"They don't see any good endings to their cause when they reject the people of the Lord as well as the Lord's Word."}]}]},{"start":25,"end":30,"title":"A World of Darkness","entries":[{"start":25,"end":25,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God is angry with the people, and rightfully so when we read the types of things they were doing and attempting. Yet, God is still longing to reach out to them. I do believe this is why He hasn’t simply ended it all today. His hand is still stretched out to humanity, and He is still desirous that His creation turn to Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"But there will be a time when enough is enough, and there will be no one left on Earth willing to go to Him. His hand will still be there, but He will do what must be done in order to balance the scales of justice."}]},{"start":26,"end":29,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God will make His judgment obvious. He still makes His judgment obvious today, and He will make it obvious in the last days as well. It’s always baffled me to read in Revelation that there will be people cursing at the Lord for proving His judgment. Instead of it changing their minds about God or making them realize that there is a God in Heaven, they continue to curse God and reject Him. This world hates God, and God still loves them. That’s the crazy part. God’s love is far larger than their hate, but in the end, He will not force people to love Him in return. If it’s not a choice they want to make for Him, then it’s not a love that God wants from His creation. Because of this, there will be judgment mixed with His love—judgment for those who don’t love Him. He loves everyone, that is true, but He will also judge those who are against Him and are evil against His people. You can bet your money on it."}]},{"start":30,"end":30,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This whole world is in darkness still. The only light that this world will have is the light of the gospel which is Jesus Christ."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Then spake Jesus again unto them, saying, I am the light of the world: he that followeth me shall not walk in darkness, but shall have the light of life.","ref":"John 8:12"},{"kind":"para","text":"It is miserable to know that there are people who enjoy their dark world. They don't want to shine light in their land. They want it to be worse than it currently is. These are that spirit of anti-Christ."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Hereby know ye the Spirit of God: Every spirit that confesseth that Jesus Christ is come in the flesh is of God: And every spirit that confesseth not that Jesus Christ is come in the flesh is not of God: and this is that spirit of antichrist, whereof ye have heard that it should come; and even now already is it in the world. Ye are of God, little children, and have overcome them: because greater is he that is in you, than he that is in the world.","ref":"1 John 4:2-4"},{"kind":"para","text":"The sad news is that it will continuously get worse and worse. However, the good news is that Christ is greater than darkness, and we can live boldly in this dark world with light to guide the way."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Israelites were about to see darkness on their land. Although they have largely been redeemed from it, there is still darkness there and all over the rest of the world that has decided to reject the only light."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":10},{"start":11,"end":11},{"start":12,"end":12},{"start":13,"end":13},{"start":14,"end":14},{"start":15,"end":16},{"start":17,"end":17},{"start":18,"end":19},{"start":20,"end":20},{"start":21,"end":21},{"start":22,"end":23},{"start":24,"end":24},{"start":25,"end":25},{"start":26,"end":29},{"start":30,"end":30}],"verses":{"1":"Now will I sing to my wellbeloved a song of my beloved touching his vineyard. My wellbeloved hath a vineyard in a very fruitful hill:","2":"And he fenced it, and gathered out the stones thereof, and planted it with the choicest vine, and built a tower in the midst of it, and also made a winepress therein: and he looked that it should bring forth grapes, and it brought forth wild grapes.","3":"And now, O inhabitants of Jerusalem, and men of Judah, judge, I pray you, betwixt me and my vineyard.","4":"What could have been done more to my vineyard, that I have not done in it? wherefore, when I looked that it should bring forth grapes, brought it forth wild grapes?","5":"And now go to; I will tell you what I will do to my vineyard: I will take away the hedge thereof, and it shall be eaten up; and break down the wall thereof, and it shall be trodden down:","6":"And I will lay it waste: it shall not be pruned, nor digged; but there shall come up briers and thorns: I will also command the clouds that they rain no rain upon it.","7":"For the vineyard of the Lord of hosts is the house of Israel, and the men of Judah his pleasant plant: and he looked for judgment, but behold oppression; for righteousness, but behold a cry.","8":"Woe unto them that join house to house, that lay field to field, till there be no place, that they may be placed alone in the midst of the earth!","9":"In mine ears said the Lord of hosts, Of a truth many houses shall be desolate, even great and fair, without inhabitant.","10":"Yea, ten acres of vineyard shall yield one bath, and the seed of an homer shall yield an ephah.","11":"Woe unto them that rise up early in the morning, that they may follow strong drink; that continue until night, till wine inflame them!","12":"And the harp, and the viol, the tabret, and pipe, and wine, are in their feasts: but they regard not the work of the Lord, neither consider the operation of his hands.","13":"Therefore my people are gone into captivity, because they have no knowledge: and their honourable men are famished, and their multitude dried up with thirst.","14":"Therefore hell hath enlarged herself, and opened her mouth without measure: and their glory, and their multitude, and their pomp, and he that rejoiceth, shall descend into it.","15":"And the mean man shall be brought down, and the mighty man shall be humbled, and the eyes of the lofty shall be humbled:","16":"But the Lord of hosts shall be exalted in judgment, and God that is holy shall be sanctified in righteousness.","17":"Then shall the lambs feed after their manner, and the waste places of the fat ones shall strangers eat.","18":"Woe unto them that draw iniquity with cords of vanity, and sin as it were with a cart rope:","19":"That say, Let him make speed, and hasten his work, that we may see it: and let the counsel of the Holy One of Israel draw nigh and come, that we may know it!","20":"Woe unto them that call evil good, and good evil; that put darkness for light, and light for darkness; that put bitter for sweet, and sweet for bitter!","21":"Woe unto them that are wise in their own eyes, and prudent in their own sight!","22":"Woe unto them that are mighty to drink wine, and men of strength to mingle strong drink:","23":"Which justify the wicked for reward, and take away the righteousness of the righteous from him!","24":"Therefore as the fire devoureth the stubble, and the flame consumeth the chaff, so their root shall be as rottenness, and their blossom shall go up as dust: because they have cast away the law of the Lord of hosts, and despised the word of the Holy One of Israel.","25":"Therefore is the anger of the Lord kindled against his people, and he hath stretched forth his hand against them, and hath smitten them: and the hills did tremble, and their carcases were torn in the midst of the streets. For all this his anger is not turned away, but his hand is stretched out still.","26":"And he will lift up an ensign to the nations from far, and will hiss unto them from the end of the earth: and, behold, they shall come with speed swiftly:","27":"None shall be weary nor stumble among them; none shall slumber nor sleep; neither shall the girdle of their loins be loosed, nor the latchet of their shoes be broken:","28":"Whose arrows are sharp, and all their bows bent, their horses' hoofs shall be counted like flint, and their wheels like a whirlwind:","29":"Their roaring shall be like a lion, they shall roar like young lions: yea, they shall roar, and lay hold of the prey, and shall carry it away safe, and none shall deliver it.","30":"And in that day they shall roar against them like the roaring of the sea: and if one look unto the land, behold darkness and sorrow, and the light is darkened in the heavens thereof."}},
    "6": {"chapter":6,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: In our last chapter, Isaiah sang a short song about the Lord, and warned the people about their false way of living. The Israelites thought that what they had was the best they were ever going to get, but they didn't realize that our best without the Lord is miniscual. He spoke about being cautious with who you unite with, and what they lean on during the times of their destruction, as well as woes for their sin, their lying, their foolishness, and their false power. He ended the chapter off with a very bleak message of darkness and turmoil because of the people's rejection and rebellion."},{"kind":"para","text":"In this chapter, we get a look at how Isaiah found himself in this ministry to begin with, the type of message he was tasked to give to the people, and the Lord's future revelation for the people of Israel because of their wickedness."}],"previously":["In our last chapter, Isaiah sang a short song about the Lord and warned the people about their false way of living. The Israelites thought that what they had was the best they were ever going to get, but they didn’t realize that our best without the Lord is minuscule. He spoke about being cautious with who you unite with and what they lean on during the times of their destruction, as well as woes for their sin, their lying, their foolishness, and their false power. He ended the chapter with a very bleak message of darkness and turmoil because of the people’s rejection and rebellion. In this chapter, we get a look at how Isaiah found himself in this ministry to begin with, the type of message he was tasked to give to the people, and the Lord’s future revelation for the people of Israel because of their wickedness."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":4,"title":"The Seraphim's Cry","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"King Uzziah was Judah’s good king. As we read through the books of the Kings (or Chronicles), we might recognize that there are many terrible kings who take the throne, but Uzziah was not one of them. He provided a lot of help for the Israelites during his leadership, and Isaiah seemed to miss his king. Isaiah was obviously under the impression that things were not going to look very good for the Israelites’ future, as he had been told by the Lord that it would be quite bleak."},{"kind":"para","text":"When Uzziah dies, Isaiah seems to seek out the Lord in His temple and receives a very prominent vision of the Lord sitting on His throne, lifted up high, with His “train” filling the temple. “Train” means “skirt” or “robe.” It seems that either God had a very long robe, or His glory is revealed in this way. While Isaiah may have lost his king, he has not lost His King. God still sits on the throne of the universe today, and that is something we must all remember."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"“Seraphim” means “fiery serpent.” Obviously, these creatures are a little more than a serpent is. They have quite a lot of wings and are seemingly coherent in their existence; they aren’t like an animal that acts on instinct. They are using their wings to cover their face, their feet, and to fly all at the same time. I can’t imagine what these things looked like, and Isaiah (as well as a few others who have seen them) doesn’t know how to explain them either. This is the best description we are going to get from Isaiah."},{"kind":"para","text":"We get a bit more of an inclination to these things, which can be spoken about in another setting, but it seems they served only one purpose for existing, and that was to give glory to the Lord."}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is their function every time we see them. Isaiah is Old Testament. Isaiah wrote this about 700 years before the New Testament, and it seems that even at the end (in Revelation) these creatures will still be supporting their only task. God could have made us one of these creatures, but He has given us the bigger pleasure of free will and the eternal work of a higher degree. Giving glory to the Lord is a very high honor, don’t get me wrong. But we get to give glory to the Lord, and then worship the Lord, and lead others to the Lord, and walk with the Lord, and learn from the Lord, and grow from the Lord, and learn to love the Lord more and more every single day. These Seraphim don’t. They were created for this one purpose, and they were quite good at this one purpose."}]},{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The Seraphim’s cries were moving the place. This had to be quite a scene for Isaiah to experience. If it were me, I would be quite undone. I would huddle into a ball on the floor and wait for the crying to stop, hoping that it would eventually. I would then wonder if I was in the right place. Thankfully, we get to see Isaiah’s reaction to this in the next verse."}]}]},{"start":5,"end":8,"title":"Up For the Task","entries":[{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"He certainly doesn’t belong here, and he knows it. He is seeing and hearing some very loud and glorious things, and he lets it be known (out loud, mind you) that he is undone and has walked (perhaps) into the wrong place. He says, “There is a lot of holiness here, and I am muddying this place up with just my talking alone.”"},{"kind":"para","text":"His presence was enough to make the place unclean, but even if he didn’t step foot in that temple that day, if he spoke in the doorway, it would have the same effect. Even looking through the doorway at the presence of the Lord was causing this holy temple to be unclean. Perhaps Isaiah didn’t see the King entirely. He knows who it is, though, and he doesn’t want to look up much longer."}]},{"start":6,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The Seraphim speaks some new words that we have not heard quite yet. He says, “This live coal is able to make you holy because it was on the altar of the Lord.” I don’t know if you’ve ever touched coal before, but it’s certainly not the cleanest thing to deal with. Just having it in your hand for a moment will turn your hands black. I love a good coal BBQ, don’t get me wrong, but they are always such a mess to deal with, so I don’t use it very often because of the mess."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Seraphim lets it be known that this coal, because of the presence of God, is able to cleanse Isaiah with just a touch. I want to recognize that the coal was “live,” which means it was hot. It was a burning coal that this Seraphim rushes over to Isaiah’s mouth. So, to get the full scope of the picture here: Isaiah comes to the temple to pray about the future (he had just lost his king), finds the Lord sitting upon the throne (high and lifted up), the Seraphim shouting praises to the Lord with loud enough voices that it shakes the place; Isaiah feels like he entered into the wrong place and is too sinful to be in this presence of the king. The Seraphim rushes over with a live coal from the altar of the Lord and touches Isaiah’s lips, cleansing him and preparing him for this moment."},{"kind":"para","text":"What’s it all for? Obviously, God took special note of Isaiah, and Isaiah seems to be an important part of history at this moment. There aren’t many people in scripture who have had front-row seats to the Lord like this. In fact, this is what God says about His presence:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And he said, Thou canst not see my face: for there shall no man see me, and live.","ref":"Exodus 33:20"},{"kind":"para","text":"I have reason to believe that Isaiah couldn't see the face of the Lord. He could (perhaps) see everything else, but His face was likely blocked in some way (perhaps by the Lord's train)."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"No man hath seen God at any time; the only begotten Son, which is in the bosom of the Father, he hath declared him.","ref":"John 1:18"},{"kind":"para","text":"To Isaiah, it seems like a very strange thing that he would be allowed this access to the Lord’s presence. I find some interesting connections in Isaiah to the rest of scripture. I had mentioned before that Isaiah (to me) is another gospel (and we will see that open up later on), but there’s a lot more linkage to this book than just the gospel alone."},{"kind":"para","text":"Isaiah happens to be 66 chapters long, and there are 66 books of the Bible. The first half (39 chapters) happens to talk about the Old Testament, and the first 39 chapters of Isaiah talk about the law. The last half (27 chapters) talks about the New Testament, and Isaiah’s last 27 chapters talk about the sacrifice of the Lord (the coming future of Israel). The New Testament quotes the book of Isaiah 66 times, and it is quite evident to any Bible reader (no matter your study level) that Isaiah is a very important book to connect the dots of scripture."},{"kind":"para","text":"He was not in the wrong place at the wrong time, and the Lord will know his presence in a moment. It seems (in a second) that Isaiah is interrupting a meeting with the Lord and some of the host of Heaven because God is looking for someone."}]},{"start":8,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I feel there is some missing context here. I think Isaiah knows there is some missing context as well. God seems to be in the middle of a meeting conversation and says, “So with all of this said, who will I send for this work?” Instead of Isaiah saying, “What do you need?” he says, “I’m here! Send me!” That was a bit of a premature jump."},{"kind":"para","text":"I will be quite upfront with you and transparent. I hesitate quite often to ask the Lord for tasks. I want to serve the Lord (don’t get me wrong), but I want to use my strengths to do it. I don’t want to get out of my comfort zone and do things I don’t know how to do. But that is not walking by faith now, is it? Going out on a limb to do something that needs to be done for the Lord is a scary prospect. I’m not saying that I don’t get out of my comfort zone (don’t misconstrue this here). What I am saying is that God is good and faithful, and I am often rebellious to Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"Isaiah doesn’t seem to care about what the task is; he is just ready to do it. I think there are a lot of people with this mindset, but the sad part about this mindset is they are usually tasked with something that swallows them. They come out of the other end of the task overburdened. That is what will happen to Isaiah, no doubt. However, the greatness of working for the Lord in this way is that God rewards His servants for the work. The deeper the faith work you do, the bigger His reward is to us. Isaiah’s faith work will not just be left in his generation. As I’ve said, it is intertwined with the rest of scripture and connects the Old and New Testaments together. His work is still being used today, as we are currently reading it."}]}]},{"start":9,"end":13,"title":"A Rejected Message","entries":[{"start":9,"end":9,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"So here’s the task (and we will get into more of what God says in a moment). It seems simple enough. Perhaps an angel should be sent (they are the messengers of the Lord). Isaiah doesn’t leave it up to the angels, however, and deems himself worthy for the task."},{"kind":"para","text":"God says, “Go and tell the people that they are very confused. They don’t see my goodness, and they have rejected my provision and presence.” That is the age in which Isaiah was living in. Uzziah was a good king, and the people flourished because of it, but all it did was cause the people to forsake the Lord, and that was not what they were supposed to do."}]},{"start":10,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Isaiah’s task was to bring bad news to them in hopes that they would turn and repent. Isaiah needed to be the bearer of bad news. That is a sad reality for ministers today. I would love to go into church and ministry and tell everyone, “Hey, God loves you, and you are doing great!” but sadly there isn’t always time for that. More often than not, I run into problems that people are having, and I can’t just say, “You are fine, God still loves you, and you don’t need to worry about it.” No, they are things that people DO need to worry about, and they are things that the scriptures lay hold of in detail about changing and making right. Thankfully, I can give them the good news of a fix, but I also have to bear bad news that it NEEDS to be fixed to begin with."},{"kind":"para","text":"Isaiah had to go and tell them bad news, and the hope was that they would start paying attention to what they were doing. The frustrating part for Isaiah (as it is for all ministers, mind you) is that no one will take it seriously until it’s too late. People should want to take the news seriously so they can be healed, but they often don’t (especially if they are doing well off financially or provisionally) and they give themselves deeper cuts than is necessary."}]},{"start":11,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"GREAT question from Isaiah. Often, the Lord calls the minister to a task like this (bad news is not an easy burden to bear), and we will bear that burden for a long time. Isaiah gets the timeline established right off the bat. “How long am I going to have to preach this message to them? Will there be a sign or some sort of hint that they have finally listened?” Sadly, we could preach the same sermon every Sunday, and people won’t remember it. They will hear it, and they will forget it as soon as they leave. Eventually, it will sink in if it’s preached long enough. So, how long is Isaiah supposed to preach this message? God says, “Once everyone has lost everything, then you can stop preaching this message.” The message was meant to turn the people around, and it will have the opposite effect. The people will ignore the message and suffer the consequences. That is the theme of Israel. It’s the theme with the Christian today."},{"kind":"para","text":"I can’t count how many times we will speak on a message or study through a chapter of scripture, and immediately after, people will bring up an issue or a problem they are facing and don’t know how to deal with. I have to gently remind them that we literally just read about the solution to that problem in the chapter a few moments ago. It seems to never fail. It’s actually quite interesting to see that God’s Word is still very much relevant to our current problems today. The people just need to listen to it and apply what they’ve heard. Isaiah has a message to give to the people, and it’s up to the people to either accept it (which would be the wise decision here) or reject it (which will be the choice they seem to make). For the whole city to be desolate will take some time. So Isaiah has quite a bit of work to do for a while. At least he will be busy. The most frustrating part is that they have no idea what the Lord has done for them, and they are about to forsake it all (only because they don’t want to turn to the Lord)."},{"kind":"para","text":"The lesson here is that you can either forsake everything to follow the Lord willingly or have it taken from you to get your attention."}]},{"start":13,"end":13,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"As I’ve read scripture, I have noticed a theme of light throughout the pages. It seems that God has provided a glimmer of hope in every page. Even in the book of Revelation, where light is forsaken, it shows up towards the end. This passage has some light in it."},{"kind":"para","text":"It looks quite bleak when we read the circumstances that the Israelites have found themselves in, but we notice that God will have a small remnant that will return. He always has at least a remnant of men and women who will seek to do His good pleasure. He has His light in the picture somewhere. Sadly, it will take time before that light comes and dwells with them, but it will come eventually, and that is the important thing to note here."},{"kind":"para","text":"They have to lose it all first before the remnant realizes what needs to be done. They need to see the control that the Lord has before they start taking His Word seriously. It relates so heavily to us today…"}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":9},{"start":10,"end":10},{"start":11,"end":12},{"start":13,"end":13}],"verses":{"1":"In the year that king Uzziah died I saw also the Lord sitting upon a throne, high and lifted up, and his train filled the temple.","2":"Above it stood the seraphims: each one had six wings; with twain he covered his face, and with twain he covered his feet, and with twain he did fly.","3":"And one cried unto another, and said, Holy, holy, holy, is the Lord of hosts: the whole earth is full of his glory. \"And the four beasts had each of them six wings about him; and they were full of eyes within: and they rest not day and night, saying, Holy, holy, holy, Lord God Almighty, which was, and is, and is to come.\" Revelation 4:8","4":"And the posts of the door moved at the voice of him that cried, and the house was filled with smoke.","5":"Then said I, Woe is me! for I am undone; because I am a man of unclean lips, and I dwell in the midst of a people of unclean lips: for mine eyes have seen the King, the Lord of hosts.","6":"Then flew one of the seraphims unto me, having a live coal in his hand, which he had taken with the tongs from off the altar:","7":"And he laid it upon my mouth, and said, Lo, this hath touched thy lips; and thine iniquity is taken away, and thy sin purged.","8":"Also I heard the voice of the Lord, saying, Whom shall I send, and who will go for us? Then said I, Here am I; send me.","9":"And he said, Go, and tell this people, Hear ye indeed, but understand not; and see ye indeed, but perceive not.","10":"Make the heart of this people fat, and make their ears heavy, and shut their eyes; lest they see with their eyes, and hear with their ears, and understand with their heart, and convert, and be healed.","11":"Then said I, Lord, how long? And he answered, Until the cities be wasted without inhabitant, and the houses without man, and the land be utterly desolate,","12":"And the Lord have removed men far away, and there be a great forsaking in the midst of the land.","13":"But yet in it shall be a tenth, and it shall return, and shall be eaten: as a teil tree, and as an oak, whose substance is in them, when they cast their leaves: so the holy seed shall be the substance thereof."}},
    "7": {"chapter":7,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: In our last chapter, Isaiah finds himself in a bit of a predicament. He has entered the temple of the Lord on a day when the Lord is having a meeting there, and becomes speechless. A creature comes and places a burning coal on his lips to give him the ability to speak up in this meeting, and takes the task (seemingly out of a knee-jerk reaction) of speaking to the people on the Lord's behalf. It is not an easy task, and he is told that it will lead him into a lot of rejection."},{"kind":"para","text":"We see Isaiah take his first task seriously in this chapter by talking to his first person about the prophecy. The first person he is tasked with talking to is the king of Judah (who is not a great man). God is trying to get Judah on the right track, but Judah is not willing to listen. This chapter is filled with some really great insight to the future of Judah, as well as to the moving of Israel towards captivity."}],"previously":["In our last chapter, Isaiah finds himself in a bit of a predicament. He has entered the temple of the Lord on a day when the Lord is having a meeting there and becomes speechless. A creature comes and places a burning coal on his lips to give him the ability to speak up in this meeting and takes the task (seemingly out of a knee-jerk reaction) of speaking to the people on the Lord’s behalf. It is not an easy task, and he is told that it will lead him into a lot of rejection. We see Isaiah take his first task seriously in this chapter by talking to his first person about the prophecy. The first person he is tasked with talking to is the king of Judah (who is not a great man). God is trying to get Judah on the right track, but Judah is not willing to listen. This chapter is filled with some really great insight into the future of Judah, as well as to the moving of Israel towards captivity."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":2,"title":"Judah and Israel War","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"At this point in history, there seems to be a war between Judah and Israel. Ahaz was working against the people of Israel, and as a result, the people of Israel have teamed up with the Syrians to try and destroy Judah for the land of Jerusalem. It appears to be a pretty intense war, as it is stated that they “could not prevail against it.” There really are no winners in this war, even if one side or the other was able to prosper from the land. We are told in 2 Kings about the type of leader this Ahaz character was."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Twenty years old was Ahaz when he began to reign, and reigned sixteen years in Jerusalem, and did not that which was right in the sight of the LORD his God, like David his father.","ref":"2 Kings 16:2"},{"kind":"para","text":"The really sad part is, Jotham (Ahaz's father) was listed as a \"good king.” His son didn't want to follow the line of his family for some reason. Then we are told in 2 Kings how Pekah led."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"In the second year of Pekah the son of Remaliah king of Israel began Jotham the son of Uzziah king of Judah to reign. Five and twenty years old was he when he began to reign, and he reigned sixteen years in Jerusalem. And his mother's name was Jerusha, the daughter of Zadok. And he did that which was right in the sight of the LORD: he did according to all that his father Uzziah had done.","ref":"2 Kings 15:32-34"},{"kind":"para","text":"We are under the impression that there was a small remnant of the Lord still searching His ways, but at the moment, they were in turmoil against each other."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Ahaz has gone against the Lord in so many ways. He was guilty of doing some really terrible things and following the practices of the heathens of that day. It is said that he burned his own children alive (2 Kings 16:3-4)."},{"kind":"para","text":"God is still trying to turn these wicked people’s hearts to Him. We will find (in the future as we read) that Judah will be mostly protected by the Lord for a season, but there will be a time when they are taken captive by Babylon (spoiler alert)."}]}]},{"start":3,"end":9,"title":"God Protects Judah","entries":[{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I feel, at least if I were in the position of Isaiah, it would be far easier to have a conversation with the king of Israel than with Judah. However, as the prophet of the Lord, they have to talk to the more difficult people. That is their calling. That is the pastor’s calling today. We just wish the conversations would flow smoothly and orderly, and we don’t have to worry about a single thing. We wish it was as easy as saying, “Hi, how are you?” and then ending the conversation with a laugh or a smile. It hardly ever is, and it’s usually the people we don’t know that we have to talk to. Some people are just flat out scary to talk to."},{"kind":"para","text":"Isaiah will have to talk to Ahaz, who was already in a distressed state, thinking that he has lost the war because Israel has teamed up with Syria. Now Isaiah is coming with some words of the Lord. This is what Isaiah must tell Ahaz…"}]},{"start":4,"end":9,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Isaiah is bringing good news to Ahaz. If Ahaz doesn’t take Isaiah’s (or God’s rather) word for it, then that’s on his own head. He is told to just stand still, and these people will be taken care of. God really wants to protect His people. However, His people are extremely stubborn and fight against the Lord’s leading and protection. Actually (if I may), we don’t even fight against it. We just downright ignore it. We are under the impression that the Lord won’t do anything on our behalf anyway, and so we take the problem into our own hands, and it turns into a nightmare because we have decided that God is not going to provide. We will never have anything established with that mentality."},{"kind":"para","text":"The real reason that God protects Judah here (aside from the fact that He really wants them to turn) is because Syria is not looking out for the best interest of God’s children. Syria is looking out for their own best interest, and in the end, will completely destroy God’s children as well as God’s promises. Judah needs to stand (as we all know) because the lineage links to Jesus (as we will see in a moment)."}]}]},{"start":10,"end":19,"title":"The Sign of God's Favor","entries":[{"start":10,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is fascinating to me. God says, “I know you want to know more, tell me how I can prove myself to you. Ask me how you can know for sure that this will happen. I don’t want you to doubt what I have told you today, so ask me about what sign I can give you.”"},{"kind":"para","text":"Ahaz is a faithless man. God is trying to get him to come to faith through this, and that is the only way the Lord will work. If Ahaz doesn’t come to faith, God cannot do what He really desires. It must be by faith alone that this man would turn to the Lord and trust in Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"This is interesting to me because Jesus says this:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"A wicked and adulterous generation seeketh after a sign; and there shall no sign be given unto it, but the sign of the prophet Jonas. And he left them, and departed.","ref":"Matthew 16:4"},{"kind":"para","text":"Yet, the Lord is using this exercise to get the faith of Ahaz on course. If Ahaz doesn't listen, it will not be fun."}]},{"start":12,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"“Tempt the Lord…” please, like he’s doing God a favor. God wants to give him a sign, and he is playing the part like he doesn’t need it. There are a lot of people in the world like Ahaz today. They reject every proof of the Lord possible because they don’t want to accept that God is real and that He is watching. Ahaz thinks he can do it on his own and doesn’t need the help of the Lord. Isaiah is just giving a message, and Ahaz will either take it or kill himself…"}]},{"start":13,"end":13,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Ahaz has had no problem abusing the countenance and strength of his men, but he can’t seem to come to the Lord and ask a simple question. What he is ultimately doing here (as is the case for so many atheists today) is making God as small in his life as possible. It’s as if he is saying, “My problems are too big for your God to handle.” The Lord wants to prove Himself, and Ahaz is rejecting it."},{"kind":"para","text":"Christians today would love to hear the Lord’s Word on specific matters in their lives. We don’t have prophets today, but we have God’s complete Word in our hands. We should be opening our Bibles daily with the thought, “God, prove yourself. Show me what you would have me to do. Show me where I can be strengthened.” Alas, most of us just say, “I would hate to tempt the Lord…”"},{"kind":"para","text":"Ahaz rejects the sign, but Isaiah will go forth telling Ahaz what the sign is anyway."}]},{"start":14,"end":14,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is such a huge verse of scripture! It is quite a big sign. How do we know that the Lord will be successful in the lives and legacy of Judah? Well, there will be a virgin who has a child. That is impossible. “Virgin” means what you think it means. She will never sleep with a man, and yet she will have a son, and His name will be “Immanuel.” “Immanuel” means “God with us.”"},{"kind":"para","text":"This is a huge prophecy lost on a very sinful and terrible man. He didn’t want to hear the sign, and yet he is hearing it now and likely thinking, “Just leave me alone, Prophet! I don’t care about a virgin having children. How is this going to help me?” This is a sign that is still debated today in much of every circle that I can think of. The argument is either that “virgin” doesn’t mean what we think it means, or “Immanuel” doesn’t mean what we think it means. Yet there is no disputing Isaiah’s specificity here."},{"kind":"para","text":"Isaiah (maybe) didn’t know how deep his words were at this moment. The Lord certainly knew, and it will be those words that God proves Himself by. It’s still those words today that people are conflicted by."}]},{"start":15,"end":15,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is a poor man’s meal. God, with humanity, will be in the lowest state possible. He certainly will choose good, and there is no strand of evil found in Him anywhere at all. Jesus proves God’s goodness wholeheartedly."},{"kind":"para","text":"If you can’t trace God’s goodness throughout any other part of scripture (which would be impossible, even David could see God’s love through God’s continuous rearing), then you can certainly find God’s goodness in the gospels. If you can’t find God’s goodness in the gospels either, then you are as rejectful as Ahaz here."}]},{"start":16,"end":16,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There are certain events that must occur before Jesus is born, and one significant aspect is the handling of the kings. Ahaz likely thought, “Right, I’m sure the kings will be gone. Good for them. Now let me think of what to do.” We can observe the life of Christ and see that Isaiah’s prophecy is clearly true."}]},{"start":17,"end":17,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There is a future for Judah and a future for the people of Ephraim. They will be dealt with, and there will be things that must take place. This will all happen, and there is no stopping it, even if Ahaz does something foolish and tries to get all of his own people killed in battle."},{"kind":"para","text":"Isaiah says, “There will be proof of God’s provision, but there are some things that have to take place first. The kings will be taken down, and the house of David (just as the Lord promised) will move forward.”"}]},{"start":18,"end":19,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There will be signs of God’s moving even in the day in which the Lord will triumph over Judah’s enemies. So if Ahaz didn’t want to believe the sign of the virgin birth (he wouldn’t see it anyway), then he could certainly believe the sign of the valley’s desolation and their hidings throughout the caves and thorns."},{"kind":"para","text":"The important picture to note here is that these people will be treated like this simply because they refused to take the Lord’s salvation. It’s the same repetitive pattern throughout all of scripture. It’s the same mundane and terrible pattern the world faces today. It will be the same useless pattern that humanity will face in the end times as well. We don’t have to live this way, yet it’s the choice we continually make as human beings."}]}]},{"start":20,"end":25,"title":"The Land Desolate","entries":[{"start":20,"end":20,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"It will be humiliating to those that reject the Lord. This (from a man's perspective) would not be a fun get away at the spa. They will seem to lose all their hair, and they will look like fools (because they are fools)."}]},{"start":21,"end":22,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"If there are any left at that time, those that remain will be happy to have what the Lord will provide for them. The land, at this time, has largely rejected the Lord’s providence. God has given them above and beyond what they deserved, and they have taken it for granted. They will see how foolish they were being when it’s all taken away, and there are others who come in and are blessed by it."},{"kind":"para","text":"God gives us so much to be thankful for, and we still find reason to get upset and abuse what we have. God can easily just give it to someone else who will appreciate it."}]},{"start":23,"end":25,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The land will be nearly completely useless. It would take a miracle to repopulate and reproduce the land to flourishing again. I don’t believe the land ever really gets back to prosperity. Solomon gives a pretty decent picture of how flourished the land was in that day in the Song of Solomon (and even in Ecclesiastes). Now that land will all be eaten up and destroyed because of the people’s negligence and terrible stewardship. All those promises and hard work made by their ancestors from Genesis to Joshua are completely gone. God will have to teach them lessons the hard way because they aren’t willing to listen any other way. Even with all of this prophecy of victory, Ahaz still won’t turn, and we will see what he chooses to do in the coming chapters."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":9},{"start":10,"end":11},{"start":12,"end":12},{"start":13,"end":13},{"start":14,"end":14},{"start":15,"end":15},{"start":16,"end":16},{"start":17,"end":17},{"start":18,"end":19},{"start":20,"end":20},{"start":21,"end":22},{"start":23,"end":25}],"verses":{"1":"And it came to pass in the days of Ahaz the son of Jotham, the son of Uzziah, king of Judah, that Rezin the king of Syria, and Pekah the son of Remaliah, king of Israel, went up toward Jerusalem to war against it, but could not prevail against it.","2":"And it was told the house of David, saying, Syria is confederate with Ephraim. And his heart was moved, and the heart of his people, as the trees of the wood are moved with the wind.","3":"Then said the Lord unto Isaiah, Go forth now to meet Ahaz, thou, and Shearjashub thy son, at the end of the conduit of the upper pool in the highway of the fuller's field;","4":"And say unto him, Take heed, and be quiet; fear not, neither be fainthearted for the two tails of these smoking firebrands, for the fierce anger of Rezin with Syria, and of the son of Remaliah.","5":"Because Syria, Ephraim, and the son of Remaliah, have taken evil counsel against thee, saying,","6":"Let us go up against Judah, and vex it, and let us make a breach therein for us, and set a king in the midst of it, even the son of Tabeal:","7":"Thus saith the Lord God, It shall not stand, neither shall it come to pass.","8":"For the head of Syria is Damascus, and the head of Damascus is Rezin; and within threescore and five years shall Ephraim be broken, that it be not a people.","9":"And the head of Ephraim is Samaria, and the head of Samaria is Remaliah's son. If ye will not believe, surely ye shall not be established.","10":"Moreover the Lord spake again unto Ahaz, saying,","11":"Ask thee a sign of the Lord thy God; ask it either in the depth, or in the height above.","12":"But Ahaz said, I will not ask, neither will I tempt the Lord.","13":"And he said, Hear ye now, O house of David; Is it a small thing for you to weary men, but will ye weary my God also?","14":"Therefore the Lord himself shall give you a sign; Behold, a virgin shall conceive, and bear a son, and shall call his name Immanuel.","15":"Butter and honey shall he eat, that he may know to refuse the evil, and choose the good.","16":"For before the child shall know to refuse the evil, and choose the good, the land that thou abhorrest shall be forsaken of both her kings.","17":"The Lord shall bring upon thee, and upon thy people, and upon thy father's house, days that have not come, from the day that Ephraim departed from Judah; even the king of Assyria.","18":"And it shall come to pass in that day, that the Lord shall hiss for the fly that is in the uttermost part of the rivers of Egypt, and for the bee that is in the land of Assyria.","19":"And they shall come, and shall rest all of them in the desolate valleys, and in the holes of the rocks, and upon all thorns, and upon all bushes.","20":"In the same day shall the Lord shave with a razor that is hired, namely, by them beyond the river, by the king of Assyria, the head, and the hair of the feet: and it shall also consume the beard.","21":"And it shall come to pass in that day, that a man shall nourish a young cow, and two sheep;","22":"And it shall come to pass, for the abundance of milk that they shall give he shall eat butter: for butter and honey shall every one eat that is left in the land.","23":"And it shall come to pass in that day, that every place shall be, where there were a thousand vines at a thousand silverlings, it shall even be for briers and thorns.","24":"With arrows and with bows shall men come thither; because all the land shall become briers and thorns.","25":"And on all hills that shall be digged with the mattock, there shall not come thither the fear of briers and thorns: but it shall be for the sending forth of oxen, and for the treading of lesser cattle."}},
    "8": {"chapter":8,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: In our last chapter, Isaiah spoke about the Judah and Israel war, the protection of God's people in Judah, why God shows favor to them, showing why the land of Israel becomes desolate, leading to another impending war in the future (a few of them in fact)."},{"kind":"para","text":"In this chapter we see a more prominent picture of Israel as they go to face war with the Assyrians. God is giving them chances and choices to make things right and turn to Him before they follow through with any sort of plan, but He is not going to force their hand one way or another. Israel is God's chosen people, but they were not acting as His chosen (as God has pointed out in the previous few chapters), and so God cannot bless them like He wants to. The Israelites were forsaking the blessings that the Lord had already provided for them, and that was going to hurt them greatly in the future. God is going to give them a small taste of what it is like if they continue down this path, because eventually they will be taken over. It won't be by Assyria, but it will be by someone much worse."}],"previously":["In our last chapter, Isaiah spoke about the war between Judah and Israel, the protection of God’s people in Judah, and why God shows favor to them. He explained why the land of Israel becomes desolate, leading to another impending war in the future, and in fact, several more. In this chapter, we see a more prominent picture of Israel as they face war with the Assyrians. God is giving them chances and choices to make things right and turn to Him before they follow through with any plan. However, He is not going to force their hand one way or another. Israel is God’s chosen people, but they were not acting as His chosen, as God has pointed out in the previous few chapters. Therefore, God cannot bless them as He wants to. The Israelites were forsaking the blessings that the Lord had already provided for them, and that was going to hurt them greatly in the future. God is going to give them a small taste of what it is like if they continue down this path, because eventually, they will be taken over. It won’t be by Assyria, but it will be by someone much worse."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":4,"title":"Isaiah's Second Son","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Oh, good ol’ Mahershalalhashbaz. “Mahershalalhashbaz” means “swift is booty, speedy is prey.” Just rolls right off the tongue if you ask me. The message being written here is specifically for King Ahaz now. We had a message come to him about the future of Israel, and now Isaiah is giving him a message about the current situation they face. So this message is for him, more than anyone else, but it was to be about “swift in booty, speedy in prey.” We will learn that this is Isaiah’s son that is spoken about here, and perhaps that is specifically for this reason recorded. His name was to humble the people (specifically the king). It was to give clarity that God will take care of the enemies of His people."},{"kind":"para","text":"Isaiah had another son whose name was “Shearjashub,” which also just… rolls right off the tongue… We read about him in the last chapter, and Isaiah was told to take his son to meet with Ahaz."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Then said the LORD unto Isaiah, Go forth now to meet Ahaz, thou, and Shearjashub thy son, at the end of the conduit of the upper pool in the highway of the fuller's field;","ref":"Isaiah 7:3"},{"kind":"para","text":"\"Shearjashub\" means \"a remnant shall return.” Both names signify a point in time of the leading and life of Israel. They are \"prophetic\" names."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"“Uriah” means “Jehovah is my light.” “Zechariah” means “Jehovah remembers.” “Jeberechiah” means “Jehovah will bless.” There are so many names featured in this chapter memorializing the fact that God is paying attention and doing a work. God loves His children, even when they are not loving Him in return. The purpose for these names and the timing of it all was because the Israelites needed to be completely surrounded with reminders so they don’t lose focus."},{"kind":"para","text":"These people, associated with these names, have a lot to live up to in order to showcase the Lord and His faithfulness. They seemed to be living up to it, though, because they were known as “faithful witnesses.”"}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Isaiah has a wife, and she conceives another child here. This is how we know that Mahershalalhashbaz is Isaiah’s son, obviously. He was born just for a time like this. That is a great reminder to us as well. We may not have a prophet’s name, but we were certainly born for this era for a purpose far above just suffering with the world. Sadly, that is the legacy so many people leave behind…"}]},{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"We have already studied some of this battle commencing in our last chapter, but the Assyrians will not have a victory over the people this day. Before the child gets a chance to say his first words, the Assyrians will have lost, and this is God’s way of proving who the real victor was. He would provide the victory for His children, though they don’t deserve it. He provides the victory, and it would be wise of these men to turn and start following the Lord. Ahaz, however, will not be a man that follows God."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Twenty years old was Ahaz when he began to reign, and reigned sixteen years in Jerusalem, and did not that which was right in the sight of the LORD his God, like David his father. But he walked in the way of the kings of Israel, yea, and made his son to pass through the fire, according to the abominations of the heathen, whom the LORD cast out from before the children of Israel. And he sacrificed and burnt incense in the high places, and on the hills, and under every green tree.","ref":"2 Kings 16:2-4"},{"kind":"para","text":"Israel was on a very destructive path with it's leaders, and yet God continuously provided for them in deep desire that they would turn. 2 Kings 16 gives the account of this battle and how it turns out, but we get the overview understanding that it is by God's grace (alone) that they are not consumed."}]}]},{"start":5,"end":8,"title":"Peace or Violence?","entries":[{"start":5,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"\"Shiloah\" means “sent.\" We will actually learn that later on."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And said unto him, Go, wash in the pool of Siloam, (which is by interpretation, Sent.) He went his way therefore, and washed, and came seeing.","ref":"John 9:7"},{"kind":"para","text":"You have to appreciate the tie-in that Jesus provides to this book here (one of several as we will see). The people refused what God has sent. The people have a very consistent track record of doing this, don’t they? We (still today) have a desire to refuse what God has sent. He has sent peace to the land, and they refused it. He has sent prosperity to the land, and they refused it. He has sent direction to the land, and they refused it. He has sent His Son to the land, and they refused Him. Israel was not even “wrestling” with God at this point. They were flat-out just walking away from Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"And so, in God’s grace, He provides another warning and example. He uses the waters that were sent as a picture of His grace for them and says, “I’m sending a different water. The water I sent before was calm and peaceful; now you will have water of rivers that will be swift and powerful.” As we have been getting so much mention of Assyria, the waters that can be assumed to be a symbol here would be the Euphrates River (which was quick-flowing and powerful). The picture is that God’s judgment will now be the water that comes through, rather than God’s grace."},{"kind":"para","text":"But even in this picture, here, we can track God’s grace given. This was a warning to them, and all they must do is turn to Him. They must forsake the direction they are headed away from the Lord and turn back to Him in obedience and service, otherwise, they will be signing their death warrant. God is not going to force them to go against Him. He’s not going to force them into trial and trouble either. But He will certainly allow them to entertain their minds with their own heartaches because of their own desire to turn away from Him. That’s on them, not on Him."}]}]},{"start":9,"end":10,"title":"God Protects","entries":[{"start":9,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God is with the Israelites, and at this time, if there was any nation against them, God would keep the Israelites continually going. I said “at this time,” but honestly, it’s still the truth today. God still continues to protect the land of Israel, and He will keep them protected even until the end of the world because they are still His chosen people. We are grafted into the family of God through grace, and they are chosen of God through grace."},{"kind":"para","text":"If we look at that land, it is largely given over to religionism today, but there will be a small remnant that will survive in the end, and they will be people whom God protects. God will protect His people, even if they are dangerously away from Him. God will have to do some work, but He always makes it happen that His children are brought back to the fold."},{"kind":"para","text":"The point of this section is to represent the fact that it was not by the king’s might or “war strategies” that the Israelites achieved victory. It is only by the sovereign will of the Lord."}]}]},{"start":11,"end":15,"title":"Don't Unite With Enemies","entries":[{"start":11,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Ahaz makes a confederacy with the Assyrians, which is what keeps them in good terms with one another. However, the relationship was not based on mutual trust but on mutual assets and material gain. In the long run, this will cause some issues, and eventually, Samaria will turn and join forces with Egypt, which will bring even more problems to the Israelites."},{"kind":"para","text":"God tells Isaiah (and anyone under the voice of Isaiah) to keep from trusting any of them. They have someone to trust that is far more powerful and far greater than any confederacy on this Earth, and that is the Lord. Really, the reason they make a pact with these lands is out of fear more than out of faith, and God has something to say about that…"}]},{"start":13,"end":14,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord should be our main focus. If we are to fear anything, it should be neglecting the leading, power, and salvation of the Lord. That will not be the main focus of the land (obviously), and they will all turn to what they can see, rather than what could be. The Lord, ultimately, knows this, and He knows what they will end up doing and how they will end up failing. But, again, He doesn’t let them go without warning and options."},{"kind":"para","text":"Isaiah was to depend on the Lord because the future problems coming their way would look quite bleak and terrible, leaving even Isaiah to wonder how he would be protected. Of course, God is good at protecting His children (and we will see that come to fruition over and over again, even in the likes of Jeremiah, who was consistently mistreated for His faith)."}]},{"start":15,"end":15,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"So many will fail and fall, only because they chose to depend on themselves and on their enemies. There is nothing (and I mean absolutely nothing) in this world that can be trusted to lean on. Everything here will fall apart."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is why we must lean on the eternal and supernatural. The Lord cannot fall apart, and He will not forsake His own. That’s historically proven, but it’s also a promise."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Be strong and of a good courage, fear not, nor be afraid of them: for the LORD thy God, he it is that doth go with thee; he will not fail thee, nor forsake thee.\" Deuteronomy 31:6 \"Let your conversation be without covetousness; and be content with such things as ye have: for he hath said, I will never leave thee, nor forsake thee.","ref":"Hebrews 13:5"}]}]},{"start":16,"end":18,"title":"God Is Present","entries":[{"start":16,"end":16,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is a fantastic verse! “Disciples” means “a learner.” There are twelve who will ultimately follow Jesus, and they will be sealed by salvation. The law is completed on the cross of Calvary by the Lord, and that is what will seal salvation for the whole world. However, it’s only the disciples of Jesus who will receive that sealing. If we are not the Lord’s disciples, we will not be sealed and protected."},{"kind":"para","text":"God gives a promise to the disciples here, and that is certainly meant for the Israelites at this time, but it’s also meant for us today. We will see our own countries go through wars, famines, inflation, and all sorts of turmoil. But when we are following Christ (learning of Him), we will have the seal of the Lord upon us. The seal of the law would be (in today’s age of grace) the seal of the Spirit."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"In whom ye also trusted, after that ye heard the word of truth, the gospel of your salvation: in whom also after that ye believed, ye were sealed with that holy Spirit of promise,","ref":"Ephesians 1:13"}]},{"start":17,"end":17,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"In the middle of chaos in our culture, we should be searching for the Lord. Throughout all of scripture, in the darkest times in this world, we can always find a glimmer of light shining through from the Lord somewhere if we are searching hard enough. God's light is always here, even when everything seems to be at it's darkest. We should simply be looking for Him and waiting on Him. He always shows up."}]},{"start":18,"end":18,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Isaiah makes it clear that his own life, and the lives of his family are great signs of God's workings. God has given Isaiah and his family purpose for their lives on Earth. Again (I've said it already in this chapter), God has placed us here for such a time as this, and we should be taking that very seriously to the extent that we are seeking out the Lord and living up to our names given by Him."}]}]},{"start":19,"end":22,"title":"The Light of Scripture","entries":[{"start":19,"end":19,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"People have always been in the business of trying to entice believers away from their beliefs. They try so hard to find flaws in everything else everyone follows, rather than find the flaws in their own thoughts and beliefs. “Oh don’t follow the Lord,” they say, “He will lead you into trouble and trials of various sorts. Instead, follow after me; I have fun and can sin to my heart’s content. God is too restrictive, and I’ve found a better way.”"},{"kind":"para","text":"They don’t realize their own flaws, and their ways certainly sound better, but in the end, you will find that the trials that come with their style of living are far heavier than following after the Lord. Take that bit of information from a man who has lived both lives."}]},{"start":20,"end":20,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is how we can know that they are right and true. If they do not speak according to scripture (and God's absolute Word), they are liars."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"This then is the message which we have heard of him, and declare unto you, that God is light, and in him is no darkness at all.","ref":"1 John 1:5"},{"kind":"para","text":"John (and scripture in general) makes it clear that light is where the child of God should dwell. If we are surrounded by darkness, we should be looking for light. It is only through the light of scripture that we can see clearly."}]},{"start":21,"end":22,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Those who reject the Word of the Lord travel through darkness. They think they know where they are going and believe they can see what is ahead, but they are just blindly traveling in a world that leads them astray. They fall for every sort of vain and meaningless tradition just so they can escape the light."},{"kind":"para","text":"Jesus is that light that drives away the darkness. That is why people don’t like to follow or talk about Jesus. He is too bright for them."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And this is the condemnation, that light is come into the world, and men loved darkness rather than light, because their deeds were evil. For every one that doeth evil hateth the light, neither cometh to the light, lest his deeds should be reproved. But he that doeth truth cometh to the light, that his deeds may be made manifest, that they are wrought in God.","ref":"John 3:19-21"},{"kind":"para","text":"Light is the greatest sign of God's grace. It's where God starts in His creation, and it's where He leads in His salvation, and it's where He ends in His eternity."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And God said, Let there be light: and there was light.","ref":"Genesis 1:3"},{"kind":"para","text":"It's where He leads in His salvation:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Then spake Jesus again unto them, saying, I am the light of the world: he that followeth me shall not walk in darkness, but shall have the light of life.","ref":"John 8:12"},{"kind":"para","text":"And it's where He ends in His eternity."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And there shall be no night there; and they need no candle, neither light of the sun; for the Lord God giveth them light: and they shall reign for ever and ever.","ref":"Revelation 22:5"}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":10},{"start":11,"end":12},{"start":13,"end":14},{"start":15,"end":15},{"start":16,"end":16},{"start":17,"end":17},{"start":18,"end":18},{"start":19,"end":19},{"start":20,"end":20},{"start":21,"end":22}],"verses":{"1":"Moreover the Lord said unto me, Take thee a great roll, and write in it with a man's pen concerning Mahershalalhashbaz.","2":"And I took unto me faithful witnesses to record, Uriah the priest, and Zechariah the son of Jeberechiah.","3":"And I went unto the prophetess; and she conceived, and bare a son. Then said the Lord to me, Call his name Mahershalalhashbaz.","4":"For before the child shall have knowledge to cry, My father, and my mother, the riches of Damascus and the spoil of Samaria shall be taken away before the king of Assyria.","5":"The Lord spake also unto me again, saying,","6":"Forasmuch as this people refuseth the waters of Shiloah that go softly, and rejoice in Rezin and Remaliah's son;","7":"Now therefore, behold, the Lord bringeth up upon them the waters of the river, strong and many, even the king of Assyria, and all his glory: and he shall come up over all his channels, and go over all his banks:","8":"And he shall pass through Judah; he shall overflow and go over, he shall reach even to the neck; and the stretching out of his wings shall fill the breadth of thy land, O Immanuel.","9":"Associate yourselves, O ye people, and ye shall be broken in pieces; and give ear, all ye of far countries: gird yourselves, and ye shall be broken in pieces; gird yourselves, and ye shall be broken in pieces.","10":"Take counsel together, and it shall come to nought; speak the word, and it shall not stand: for God is with us.","11":"For the Lord spake thus to me with a strong hand, and instructed me that I should not walk in the way of this people, saying,","12":"Say ye not, A confederacy, to all them to whom this people shall say, A confederacy; neither fear ye their fear, nor be afraid.","13":"Sanctify the Lord of hosts himself; and let him be your fear, and let him be your dread.","14":"And he shall be for a sanctuary; but for a stone of stumbling and for a rock of offence to both the houses of Israel, for a gin and for a snare to the inhabitants of Jerusalem.","15":"And many among them shall stumble, and fall, and be broken, and be snared, and be taken.","16":"Bind up the testimony, seal the law among my disciples.","17":"And I will wait upon the Lord, that hideth his face from the house of Jacob, and I will look for him.","18":"Behold, I and the children whom the Lord hath given me are for signs and for wonders in Israel from the Lord of hosts, which dwelleth in mount Zion.","19":"And when they shall say unto you, Seek unto them that have familiar spirits, and unto wizards that peep, and that mutter: should not a people seek unto their God? for the living to the dead?","20":"To the law and to the testimony: if they speak not according to this word, it is because there is no light in them.","21":"And they shall pass through it, hardly bestead and hungry: and it shall come to pass, that when they shall be hungry, they shall fret themselves, and curse their king and their God, and look upward.","22":"And they shall look unto the earth; and behold trouble and darkness, dimness of anguish; and they shall be driven to darkness."}},
    "9": {"chapter":9,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: In our last chapter, Isaiah gave the Israelites a choice between peace or violence. He established (what the Israelites should have already known) that God protects those that belong to Him. He warns them about uniting with the enemy (because that is something they considered to prevent a war from taking place). He gives them hope in the presence of God (if they would just turn to Him in trust), and he tells them about the importance of following the light of the scripture."},{"kind":"para","text":"In this chapter, Isaiah continues to give warnings, but He also provides the Isrealites (and the readers today) hope through a coming Savior. There will me a Son who comes into this world, and will correct all the wrongs, lift all the burdens, and change the hearts of all His children."}],"previously":["In our last chapter, Isaiah gave the Israelites a choice between peace or violence. He established (what the Israelites should have already known) that God protects those that belong to Him. He warns them about uniting with the enemy (because that is something they considered to prevent a war from taking place). He gives them hope in the presence of God (if they would just turn to Him in trust), and he tells them about the importance of following the light of the scripture. In this chapter, Isaiah continues to give warnings, but He also provides the Isrealites (and the readers today) hope through a coming Savior. There will me a Son who comes into this world, and will correct all the wrongs, lift all the burdens, and change the hearts of all His children."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":7,"title":"Unto Us","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"If I can be honest, I have no idea what is being spoken about here. It is possible that Isaiah is speaking about a distant future prophecy, but I don’t think he is (based on the rest of this chapter, which we will look deeper into in a moment). So if he isn’t talking about a future prophecy, then he must be talking about something a little more recent, or even before what Isaiah is speaking about here. Maybe he’s talking about the captivity that the Israelites faced from the Assyrians?"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"In the days of Pekah king of Israel came Tiglathpileser king of Assyria, and took Ijon, and Abelbethmaachah, and Janoah, and Kedesh, and Hazor, and Gilead, and Galilee, all the land of Naphtali, and carried them captive to Assyria.","ref":"2 Kings 15:29"},{"kind":"para","text":"Or perhaps it is speaking about the time of Christ, which is highly likely. The “more grievously afflicted” mention here could very well be speaking about the coming Messiah. He is the one, after all, who stirred up the falsities of these places and caused great grief to the religionists of that day. I think, if I can be honest, a good portion of people during the time of Christ would have rather been in captivity instead of listening to this man preach about the Kingdom of Heaven. That’s still the case today. Not everyone views the message of Christ as lovely and necessary, so they would rather get a root canal than have to suffer through someone telling them the truth."},{"kind":"para","text":"The references to Zebulun and Naphtali could just refer to the stretch of the Sea of Galilee, where Christ does most of His ministry work. You hardly see Him go much further than these areas, up and down the shoreline. In fact, Nazareth was in Zebulun, and Capernaum was in Naphtali. Of course, don’t just take my word for it. Scripture doesn’t leave us in doubt."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Now when Jesus had heard that John was cast into prison, he departed into Galilee; And leaving Nazareth, he came and dwelt in Capernaum, which is upon the sea coast, in the borders of Zabulon and Nephthalim: That it might be fulfilled which was spoken by Esaias the prophet, saying, The land of Zabulon, and the land of Nephthalim, by the way of the sea, beyond Jordan, Galilee of the Gentiles; The people which sat in darkness saw great light; and to them which sat in the region and shadow of death light is sprung up.","ref":"Matthew 4:12-16"},{"kind":"para","text":"We will see, through the rest of this passage, that Isaiah is very much speaking about the coming Christ and there is no mistaking who He talks about."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Christ is the light!"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Then spake Jesus again unto them, saying, I am the light of the world: he that followeth me shall not walk in darkness, but shall have the light of life.\" John 8:12 \"And the light shineth in darkness; and the darkness comprehended it not.\" John 1:5 \"Then Jesus said unto them, Yet a little while is the light with you. Walk while ye have the light, lest darkness come upon you: for he that walketh in darkness knoweth not whither he goeth.","ref":"John 12:35"},{"kind":"para","text":"Of course, when Jesus comes on the scene, these people will be so used to walking in darkness that His light just irritates them. There are some, however, who are tired of walking in darkness. They need a way of escape. That is who Christ came for. See, that is the look of salvation. We are all walking in darkness, and so He shines His light upon all, but it’s only those who accept the light and walk towards Him that will receive that light. All others will hide and quarrel in their darkness, waiting for the light to pass by, grateful to hide in the shadows."},{"kind":"para","text":"When I was younger, we used to play hide and seek out in the desert. My cousins and I would wait until it was nighttime, and the seeker would be the only one with a flashlight. We would scatter on the ten acres of property we had and hide while the seeker counted down. Once he was done, we would hear him shout from a distance, “Ready or not, here I come.” Oh, the joy of staying in darkness. If the light was getting closer, our hearts would race, and we would worry about being found too quickly. When the light passed by, it was like a relief."},{"kind":"para","text":"I believe that is how much of the world views the light of Christ. They want to hide from it and wait for it to pass by rather than take His light while they have the chance. But He is still seeking, and He is still finding until the day He simply stops…"}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"That is what religion looks like, honestly. They have the works, but lack the joy. They should be rejoicing over the harvest (that is, sinners coming to repentance), but instead, it becomes a to-do list or a routine. We should be very weary and cautious to ever fall into this category (and it is quite easy for us to fall here)."},{"kind":"para","text":"Of course, during this time, there will be an established church setting where people can come, and the harvest can be reached. The multiplication factor is not just from the nation alone but extends to the “uttermost” parts of the Earth."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But ye shall receive power, after that the Holy Ghost is come upon you: and ye shall be witnesses unto me both in Jerusalem, and in all Judaea, and in Samaria, and unto the uttermost part of the earth.","ref":"Acts 1:8"},{"kind":"para","text":"Isaiah, of course, doesn’t know that yet. The prophets didn’t know about the church in their day. Paul establishes that in Romans 16:25-26. So Isaiah knows that there is more to come in the next 2,000 something years, but he doesn’t know all of the details. He just knows that serving the Lord will become mundane again, and (if I can be honest) a lot of people treat the Lord’s service as such. They don’t find it joyous; they find it mundane."}]},{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is what Christ will do, and there’s no doubt about that if you are a child of God today. You have had your burden lifted from the Lord. You certainly carry burdens, but you have a God who is willing to carry them for you. The burden of sin, specifically, has been lifted, and that is what Isaiah is speaking about here."},{"kind":"para","text":"The reason that the Israelites suffer from slavery and being taken captive is not because God likes to punish these people. God doesn’t want to punish these people. They have done that to themselves through their own sins. They can’t live a life seeking the Lord because they are far more attached to their sin. As long as you serve sin, you cannot serve God. So the Lord allows the consequences of that sin to take place because His children need to learn how terrible it is to live that lifestyle."},{"kind":"para","text":"Christ, however, gives God’s children an escape from sin. He takes the burden of sin off the shoulders of the sinner so that we can all have the ability to be free from sin. That is what Christ desires to do for all of mankind. That is what He does when He comes for Israel."}]},{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I’ve said this before, and I think it bears repeating. When a prophet speaks, he is not just speaking about the present culture. He speaks about the future, and the future’s future. He speaks about what is to come shortly, what is to come in the time of Christ, and what is to come in the second coming. Those are the three main events of history. So this will be about a coming battle, but also one to come, and about the second coming. There will be a lot of terrible circumstances that will befall the people in all three cases (we know of the two already), and the third one (which hasn’t come yet) will be just as grievous (if not worse)."},{"kind":"para","text":"So, trials are coming, people are being warned, and there is only one thing that can be done! Look for a Savior. Well, what will that Savior look like? Thankfully, Isaiah explains:"}]},{"start":6,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God will come personally, His throne will be established over David’s throne, and He will set in order all things in that time. That was a great promise for all of Israel to hear right here. It can give them hope and comfort in their current circumstances, hope and comfort when Christ comes, and hope and comfort when He comes again. The Lord will establish Christ’s coming through all seasons, whether this speaks about His first coming or second coming. I believe it is referring to both. Most hold to the idea that it refers to one or the other, but I believe all prophecies refer to parts of God’s history. These titles fit in both instances."},{"kind":"para","text":"He was given to us as a child born to us. He is a son, but now and then. He is Wonderful, even at His birth and at His second coming. He is a counselor to those who are with Him today and those who are with Him in the tribulation. He is the mighty God, always and forever. He is the Everlasting Father and the Son given to us. He is the Prince of Peace, both today (even though the world is terribly chaotic) and in the tribulation (when the world will be even more chaotic). His authority and power have no end; He still reigns on the throne and is still sovereign over His creation both today and in the end."}]}]},{"start":8,"end":12,"title":"The Promise Stands","entries":[{"start":8,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Since the beginning of time, God has been preparing and planning these events to unfold. He knew exactly where the Israelites would be before He even created the Earth and everything in it. None of this is lost on Him. The even crazier part is that He has told all of these people since the beginning of time His plans for them, and they have continuously forgotten them. But He doesn’t forget, and He will accomplish what He said He would. And (spoiler alert) He does accomplish it."},{"kind":"para","text":"We will notice that Isaiah has (in a way) separated Jacob and Israel. We know that Jacob and Israel are the same person. So when he references Jacob, he is speaking about the sinful nature of the people. These are the people of the old man. Israel will be the people of the new man. I think that is an important distinction we should make here. Israel changed his name from Jacob because the Lord changed His purpose. Now, even still, when Israel is being spoken of here, it speaks about their sin. Those that were the children of Jacob (at this time) were sinning without the Lord. Those that were the children of Israel (at this time) were sinning while with the Lord."}]},{"start":9,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Really, what Isaiah is trying to get across here is that they would not be able to deny his words. The Lord is sending judgment, and they will know it for sure by the way in which things will fall apart. They won’t turn to the Lord either once things are in shambles."},{"kind":"para","text":"They will try to rebuild and they will say, “WE will build…” and “WE will change,” and it will all be for their own selfish ambitions. They won’t change anything on the inside of the walls; they will only change how it looks, but they still won’t have a proper heart."}]},{"start":11,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"They have a group of Assyrians primed up for a battle against them, and it seems that the Syrians and the Philistines will join behind them in attacking Israel. Assyria was already making great headaches for the Israelites. Now, to have three large armies attacking was surely going to be painful."},{"kind":"para","text":"But even still, as Isaiah says, God is still there. He will only allow a portion of heartache to come. He will not allow the Israelites to be completely demolished. He is still keeping His promise, and that is all for the purpose of the coming Savior, the Prince of Peace that Isaiah has already described. God is a merciful God."},{"kind":"para","text":"With their current lifestyle, it would not be a shock to anyone in the world at that time if God just let them be completely demolished and forgotten about. But God has chosen them for a reason, and He will fulfill what He has said He would do."}]}]},{"start":13,"end":17,"title":"Seek the Lord","entries":[{"start":13,"end":13,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The attackers of Israel will never turn to the Lord. This is why God has chosen Israel. It might seem like a strange thing to us that God would choose these people, but they really were the only ones turning back to God in these days. There was a very small number of people (and they are mostly spoken about in scripture) who turned to the God of Israel who were not a part of these people, but everyone else had their own gods and their own ideas of the afterlife."},{"kind":"para","text":"However, the Israelites were constantly aware of God’s presence (or lack thereof). They seemed to keep turning back to Him. If God had done the same thing for any of the other nations that He did for the Israelites, the results would never be the same. In fact, I have reason to believe that the Philistines were some of those people who were looked out for by the Lord. We see in Genesis that the Philistines have a king who is a God-fearing man. He is not of the tribe of Israel, but he believes and trusts in the God of Israel (as we see him with Abraham and Isaac worshipping the Lord with them)."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Philistines seem to have the same amount of time granted to them for preparedness, but they don’t get closer to the Lord. They get further and further away from God, and we see them completely reject the Lord after Israel’s first king comes in. Now, we see them on the attack against Israel, and Isaiah specifically says, “Those that are attacking you now, they do not seek the Lord of hosts.” They don’t care about God. They aren’t concerned about whether He is the right God or not. They are only concerned about making Israel suffer."}]},{"start":14,"end":14,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The sad part is that the enemy will have a small victory. Worse still, Israel will not be humbled by this. They will view their loss as a means of arrogance and will try to fight harder for their materialism, rather than turning to God, as their ancestors have learned over and over again. This beginning battle will be the easiest of the bunch, quite frankly. They will suffer much loss, but it will be nothing compared to Babylon and the Roman invasion."},{"kind":"para","text":"It might sound weird that Isaiah references the Israelites as “head and tail” (almost like a snake), but there is a purpose for that, which he answers in the next verse."}]},{"start":15,"end":15,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Those that are important to their tribe will be cut off, and those that are least important will be cut off, leaving the middle section. Those in the middle have a choice to make. They can fulfill the place of the head or fulfill the place of the tail. I think snakes are a great representation of this at the time."},{"kind":"para","text":"Snakes (if you’ve never seen one) have a small head. They have a spot to bite and chew, and what is the rest of a snake? It’s all stomach. A snake’s tail is actually towards the end of the snake, and it’s usually pretty lengthy, longer than the head most times. But the stomach in the middle is the longest part."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Israelites (after this war) will be the stomach. They have to join the head or tail, and if they are like a snake, there won’t be many making up for the head (because the head of the snake is the smallest part). Or! They can become a new creature entirely!"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Therefore if any man be in Christ, he is a new creature: old things are passed away; behold, all things are become new.","ref":"2 Corinthians 5:17"},{"kind":"para","text":"But that obviously won't be the case for the Israelites."}]},{"start":16,"end":16,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"It’s a sad reality that we have leaders who are leading people into sin and error. It’s still very much a problem today, and I have reason to believe it’s a bigger problem now. In those days, there was one nation following after truth. No one else would even look to it or wanted to understand it. Today, the truth is widely available for all to peer into, and the leaders (most of them) are denying the truth and keeping others from viewing and accepting it."},{"kind":"para","text":"Leaders who keep their people from seeking the truth are not real leaders and should never be trusted. God (over and over again in His Word) warns people about following corrupt leaders that keep their people away from Him. He hates those leaders, and He will take care of them in their time. But those that follow those leaders will also be in great error, and God is not with them either."}]},{"start":17,"end":17,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Today, we have truth staring directly into our faces, and yet we still have the purpose and reason to reject it and pursue lies and deceit. Then, we have the audacity, after being hurt by the lies, to say, “Well, I was never warned about this.” God warns all of creation about their errors. I don’t think the Assyrians, the Syrians, the Philistines, the Babylonians, the Romans, or any other type of leadership in the world (the Egyptians) went without a warning from the Lord of their evil."},{"kind":"para","text":"We see the Lord speak to world powers and leaders all the time in scripture, and those who reject God’s warning are those who suffer great consequences. Even today, I believe the Lord speaks to world leaders, but most of them reject the leading of the Lord, and so they face the consequences. Sadly, those that they are leading face the consequences as well. But God is able to take care of those who are genuine followers of Him, and those who are just following the man that’s in charge."}]}]},{"start":18,"end":21,"title":"Terrible Circumstances","entries":[{"start":18,"end":18,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Wickedness, or sin and evil living, is painful. There is no part of it that you can touch without getting burned. Some people think the burning is worth it. I watched a commercial about Crest mouthwash. They had a new formula that came out that keeps your mouth from burning when you swish with it. There was an older man who was using the old style of mouthwash and said, “If it’s burning, it’s working!” The new mouthwash was supposed to work even better, without the burn."},{"kind":"para","text":"These people think that the burning is a good thing. They might have said (like many of the false pastors and preachers today), “If there is pushback, then I must be doing something right for the Lord.” Now, I know that there are times when pushback happens when you are pleasing the Lord. More times than not, I could argue. But that does not mean we should be searching for pushback. Those that say, “Well, I must be doing something right if people are upset with me” are usually purposely causing problems with people. They are not doing something right. They are just trying to justify their wrongdoing and calling it “holy.”"},{"kind":"para","text":"Holy things are not pain-inducing. Holy things are peace-inducing. Wickedness is painful, and that is what the Israelites will have to learn. They will learn this lesson through the trials of the Lord specifically."}]},{"start":19,"end":19,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God has to light that fire… Again, this sounds cruel and inhumane, but those that the Lord is doing this to were cruel and inhumane. They were doing worse than what the Lord is going to do. The Lord does it to rid the evil; they were doing it to promote the evil. That will also be the picture of the end times. The world will see God’s wrath and think, “Gee, the Lord seems quite angry, He must not be a very loving God,” while simultaneously selling their Christian slaves, killing Christian men (and their families), aborting children, and sacrificing them to their personal idea of god (or to Satan himself in those days). Forrest Gump was right to say, “Stupid is as stupid does.”"}]},{"start":20,"end":21,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There is a two-fold way we can look at this. One is to look at this as literal cannibalism (which I believe was a very real occurrence during the time of Israels captivity). God speaks about this problem coming to pass in Deuteronomy in fact."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And he shall besiege thee in all thy gates, until thy high and fenced walls come down, wherein thou trustedst, throughout all thy land: and he shall besiege thee in all thy gates throughout all thy land, which the LORD thy God hath given thee. And thou shalt eat the fruit of thine own body, the flesh of thy sons and of thy daughters, which the LORD thy God hath given thee, in the siege, and in the straitness, wherewith thine enemies shall distress thee: So that the man that is tender among you, and very delicate, his eye shall be evil toward his brother, and toward the wife of his bosom, and toward the remnant of his children which he shall leave: So that he will not give to any of them of the flesh of his children whom he shall eat: because he hath nothing left him in the siege, and in the straitness, wherewith thine enemies shall distress thee in all thy gates. The tender and delicate woman among you, which would not adventure to set the sole of her foot upon the ground for delicateness and tenderness, her eye shall be evil toward the husband of her bosom, and toward her son, and toward her daughter, And toward her young one that cometh out from between her feet, and toward her children which she shall bear: for she shall eat them for want of all things secretly in the siege and straitness, wherewith thine enemy shall distress thee in thy gates.","ref":"Deuteronomy 28:52-57"},{"kind":"para","text":"It speaks of men eating their own arms. This could also be a reference to their appetite for sin. Both cases are evidential, but the sin appetite is what Isaiah has focused on for some time now. Perhaps Isaiah means both, or the Lord uses it as a reference for both. Either way, it’s a cruel and terrible life to lead, and yet, through all of their continuous rebellion and rejection of the Lord, His hand is still stretched out. It’s a hand of help and supplication, a hand of salvation and protection. All they must do is reach out and grab it. His hand is stretched out for all of humanity still today. Those who don’t have Him must simply reach up and grab it. There will be a day when that hand is closed, but until then, we are commissioned and desirous that all of those around us would grab the hand of the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"My prayer is, though quite unlikely that anyone who picks up this book is unsaved, if God sees fit, and you don’t have Him today, that it would be the day that you reach up and grab Him. Take ahold of His outstretched hand. It is there, and He is willing anytime you are."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":10},{"start":11,"end":12},{"start":13,"end":13},{"start":14,"end":14},{"start":15,"end":15},{"start":16,"end":16},{"start":17,"end":17},{"start":18,"end":18},{"start":19,"end":19},{"start":20,"end":21}],"verses":{"1":"Nevertheless the dimness shall not be such as was in her vexation, when at the first he lightly afflicted the land of Zebulun and the land of Naphtali, and afterward did more grievously afflict her by the way of the sea, beyond Jordan, in Galilee of the nations.","2":"The people that walked in darkness have seen a great light: they that dwell in the land of the shadow of death, upon them hath the light shined.","3":"Thou hast multiplied the nation, and not increased the joy: they joy before thee according to the joy in harvest, and as men rejoice when they divide the spoil.","4":"For thou hast broken the yoke of his burden, and the staff of his shoulder, the rod of his oppressor, as in the day of Midian.","5":"For every battle of the warrior is with confused noise, and garments rolled in blood; but this shall be with burning and fuel of fire.","6":"For unto us a child is born, unto us a son is given: and the government shall be upon his shoulder: and his name shall be called Wonderful, Counsellor, The mighty God, The everlasting Father, The Prince of Peace.","7":"Of the increase of his government and peace there shall be no end, upon the throne of David, and upon his kingdom, to order it, and to establish it with judgment and with justice from henceforth even for ever. The zeal of the Lord of hosts will perform this.","8":"The Lord sent a word into Jacob, and it hath lighted upon Israel.","9":"And all the people shall know, even Ephraim and the inhabitant of Samaria, that say in the pride and stoutness of heart,","10":"The bricks are fallen down, but we will build with hewn stones: the sycomores are cut down, but we will change them into cedars.","11":"Therefore the Lord shall set up the adversaries of Rezin against him, and join his enemies together;","12":"The Syrians before, and the Philistines behind; and they shall devour Israel with open mouth. For all this his anger is not turned away, but his hand is stretched out still.","13":"For the people turneth not unto him that smiteth them, neither do they seek the Lord of hosts.","14":"Therefore the Lord will cut off from Israel head and tail, branch and rush, in one day.","15":"The ancient and honourable, he is the head; and the prophet that teacheth lies, he is the tail.","16":"For the leaders of this people cause them to err; and they that are led of them are destroyed.","17":"Therefore the Lord shall have no joy in their young men, neither shall have mercy on their fatherless and widows: for every one is an hypocrite and an evildoer, and every mouth speaketh folly. For all this his anger is not turned away, but his hand is stretched out still.","18":"For wickedness burneth as the fire: it shall devour the briers and thorns, and shall kindle in the thickets of the forest, and they shall mount up like the lifting up of smoke.","19":"Through the wrath of the Lord of hosts is the land darkened, and the people shall be as the fuel of the fire: no man shall spare his brother.","20":"And he shall snatch on the right hand, and be hungry; and he shall eat on the left hand, and they shall not be satisfied: they shall eat every man the flesh of his own arm:","21":"Manasseh, Ephraim; and Ephraim, Manasseh: and they together shall be against Judah. For all this his anger is not turned away, but his hand is stretched out still."}},
    "10": {"chapter":10,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: In our last chapter, Isaiah gave some promises that were... well... promising! He talks about a Savior that will rescue His people, and the way in which He will come to us. He talks about the promise of salvation, and how the king should take it seriously if he wants to see victory. He pleads with the people (specifically the king) to seek the Lord in the middle of this fight and battle, and then explains the terrible circumstances that will befall them if they are not willing to go after God in this moment of great tribulation."},{"kind":"para","text":"In this chapter, Isaiah digs deeper into the takeover of Israel. He explains that the Lord will do this to them because of their actions and their constant betrayal of the Lord, and how it will lead them into a lot of pain and anguish. Yet the Lord will not let them be utterly destroyed. There will be a remnant, and God will save His people."}],"previously":["In our last chapter, Isaiah gave some promises that were… well… promising! He talks about a Savior who will rescue His people and the way in which He will come to us. He discusses the promise of salvation and how the king should take it seriously if he wants to see victory. He pleads with the people, specifically the king, to seek the Lord in the middle of this fight and battle, and then explains the terrible circumstances that will befall them if they are not willing to pursue God in this moment of great tribulation. In this chapter, Isaiah digs deeper into the takeover of Israel. He explains that the Lord will do this to them because of their actions and their constant betrayal of the Lord, and how it will lead them into a lot of pain and anguish. Yet the Lord will not let them be utterly destroyed. There will be a remnant, and God will save His people."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":4,"title":"Repaying Deeds","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Now, we must look at these chapters as prophecies, for that is what they are for the future of Israel. However, we are certainly able to apply them to our current era and conduct today. Here is a message to our leaders: “Woe” to them. They have written grievance to their people and have done it through unrighteous means, even calling it “righteousness.” They are self-righteous people, but they do not have the stamp of approval by the Lord. The leadership in Israel was playing that same game, and if history continuously repeats itself, we will see what that kind of leadership gets God’s children into."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Jesus will bring this same thing back up to the religionists of His day."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! for ye devour widows' houses, and for a pretence make long prayer: therefore ye shall receive the greater damnation.","ref":"Matthew 23:14"},{"kind":"para","text":"That is what religion does by the way. It prey's on the widows and fatherless. James says what real religion is;"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Pure religion and undefiled before God and the Father is this, To visit the fatherless and widows in their affliction, and to keep himself unspotted from the world.","ref":"James 1:27"},{"kind":"para","text":"Yet, if you were to look at any self-proclaimed religious group today, they do the complete opposite of pure religion. They rob from widows and abuse the innocence of people. What a sad and twisted world we live in. I suppose this should be a fair warning to those who practice such religions today. This is what will become of you, likely more spiritually than physically."}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Israel’s leadership was intended to be God-honoring, and honestly, the United States leadership should be the same. That was the structure our forefathers fought to preserve, yet we have largely followed the Israelites in rejecting God as the sovereign above all. This question could still be asked today: Where will our national leaders run to in the day of visitation? Where will our world hide in the desolation? There is nowhere to run for help. Even atheists will cry to the Lord in their day of anguish."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Israelites faced an imminent takeover, and Isaiah warned them to take action now to prevent catastrophe. They didn’t listen, and it is a great representation of our world today. We can warn people until we are blue in the face about the second coming of the Lord, but they won’t listen. They won’t care about it. They will largely reject it and find any reason possible to deny it. Their own ignorance will lead them to their own demise."}]},{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"What a verse! God is our power and strength. He is our provider and sustainer. If we don’t have Him, we will become less than prisoners and lead ourselves to the grave. This is very evident in our lives today. Without Christ, we are a slave to sin. We are worse than prisoners. We are free from physical shackles, yet still in prison to our flesh. We are dead men walking."},{"kind":"para","text":"God, during this time, is giving them a warning and letting it be known that the things about to come their way will be difficult for them to go through. It will literally destroy them. And yet, Isaiah says, “…but his hand is stretched out still.” In other words, “All of these things are going to happen because of your rejection of the Lord, and yet He is still there with open arms ready to forgive and heal.”"},{"kind":"para","text":"God will be there for the Israelites; He will give them a way of escape. He will literally provide forgiveness to them, and they will reject Him, curse Him, and live their fleshly lives without Him. Yet, He is still there waiting and desiring that they would turn to Him. From an outsider’s perspective, we would think that God has every right to just reject them and forget them. He has every right to completely demolish this land (including in our own land). Yet God shows mercy even in the midst of wickedness and darkness. He still desires to provide sight to the blind and hearing to the deaf."}]}]},{"start":5,"end":11,"title":"Used For Correction","entries":[{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The Assyrians were being allowed to conquer and triumph in this war, specifically because the Lord is trying to correct His children. They will, perhaps, not see it like that, but eventually (once they lose everything) they will have no choice but to turn to the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"They will try leaning on everything else around them first (because they will provide temporary comfort), but eventually those things will fall away, and then where else can they go?"}]},{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God is speaking about His own people here, relaying the message that they are the hypocrites. They are “religious” people, but they are not righteous. They resemble a significant portion of the world today. They believe there is a God, but they do not follow Him. They know there is a truth, but they do not accept it. They cannot deny the resurrection of Christ, yet they do not want to believe in Him. God is going to use wicked people, in this instance, to prosper over His own people. If we apply this to the church today, we can safely assume that God would likely do the same. If the church is not standing where it is supposed to, why wouldn’t God do something about it? Why wouldn’t He allow wicked people to run rampant in the church to get rid of it? I would hope He would anyway. He needs His children’s eyes back on Him because when we are left to our own devices, we are just plain old hypocrites. We say one thing and do another. We will tell you what to do and how to do it, but we will never actually do it ourselves. We are like little children, making up the rules as we go along so we can come out on top."}]},{"start":7,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The Assyrians didn’t know that they were being used by the Lord. I’ve mentioned it before, but it bears repeating. God doesn’t use people like puppets. I know that doesn’t sit well with certain people, but it’s scriptural. Every person who did terrible things in the “name of the Lord” was allowed those things for a reason, but not forced to do them for a reason. This includes Baalam and his prophesying."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Assyrians had it in their mind that they were simply fighting against a country they did not like, and that alone was their goal. So if you asked them, “Did you know the Lord is using you to do this?” they would likely deny your God altogether and acclaim the victory on themselves. They didn’t know the God of Israel. They hated the God of Israel."},{"kind":"para","text":"Other nations will see the downfall of Israel and think, “Man, they must have truly messed up if their God made them this prosperous just to take it all away.” They will see God’s work far better than the Israelites or Assyrians can see it."}]},{"start":9,"end":9,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"To the king of Assyria, there was no difference between the Israelites (including their God) and any other nation. They would simply think they were taking over a land. The livelihoods of the people were none of his business or care. The Hebrew words of these places are nearly identical and all relate to the same definition, speaking about watchtowers and fortresses. This is the path that Assyria will take as they conquer, and they will do it as if all the cities (in their eyes) were the same. It won’t be much of a fight for them because God is literally going to just give it over to them."}]},{"start":10,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"You’d think that the Israelites have learned their lessons over the years. If you read through the books of the Kings (or Chronicles), you will see that the Israelites have had this same issue for quite some time now. They are all falling for the same traps they have fallen for before."},{"kind":"para","text":"God has had to deal with them in this area once, and He will have to deal with them again (except on a much grander and deeper scale). Their sin has gotten out of control, and they are not willing to even look at their own fleshly lusts as evil anymore. They are starting to call it normal."}]}]},{"start":12,"end":19,"title":"Fixing Other Problems","entries":[{"start":12,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Wickedness will not go unpunished, including with the Assyrians. Just because God is allowing them to do His work doesn’t mean He is allowing their evil to just casually slide by. They needed a turning to the Lord too, but the Assyrians are not going to do that. So when Assyria is done, and the Israelites are living in their regret, that is when God will turn to the Assyrians and bring His punishment upon them."},{"kind":"para","text":"But Israel needs to be in a specific place first. Perhaps that is often the case with us. We are not where we are supposed to be, and so we are faced with all sorts of trouble until we are in a spot of submission and realization that we are in need of repentance. Then God will relieve us. It’s just going to take some molding and twisting to get us there."}]},{"start":13,"end":14,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"That is the problem with all of these leaders, honestly. They try to rob God of the glory He deserves. God provides, and God allows prosperity, yet they take it upon themselves and say, “Look what my pride and strength have gotten me!”"},{"kind":"para","text":"You will meet people like this in life (if you haven’t already). You can bet any money that you will see them fall quite hard in little to no time. In the end, the Lord will get the glory, no matter how many people try to take it from Him."}]},{"start":15,"end":15,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Instruments cannot speak for themselves. You will not have an axe claim its own victory. You might say, “Well yeah, they don’t have a brain or the ability to think on their own, so of course they won’t do that.” However, you must see the picture in which God is giving to the Assyrians (or any arrogant and prideful leader for that matter). Those who boast of their own strength are just tools without brains. They are used and think they are something tough, but they really aren’t much of anything without the wielder using them."},{"kind":"para","text":"God could easily keep the Assyrians from taking over the Israelites, but He won’t stop them. The Assyrians will think they are something special, but the Lord won’t allow them to prosper in that thought forever. Eventually, they will have to be dealt with (and eventually they are)."}]},{"start":16,"end":16,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"“Leanness” means “scantness” or “wasting.” It is supposed that this will be some sort of illness that will come upon the kings of Assyria. That is how God will deal with the kings. They cannot say, “Well, I am sick because I have allowed myself to get sick.” No one just allows themselves sickness. That is something that will happen by its own free volition. You cannot control a sickness; you can only try to heal one. People who are sick have nothing to rely on. That is why Jesus masterfully uses that illustration to the religionists of His day."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But when Jesus heard that, he said unto them, They that be whole need not a physician, but they that are sick. But go ye and learn what that meaneth, I will have mercy, and not sacrifice: for I am not come to call the righteous, but sinners to repentance.","ref":"Matthew 9:12-13"},{"kind":"para","text":"The problem is, there are a lot of sick people in our world today who are not willing to come to the Lord for healing. The Assyrian kings will be one of those people set forth as an example. We still don't seem to learn our lesson today."}]},{"start":17,"end":18,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The kings are mighty, but they will fall due to some sort of miraculous disease that will be spread. When that happens, there will be no denying that the Lord is doing a work. The light of His work will be undeniable, yet there will be plenty who try to write it off as something else."},{"kind":"para","text":"During the COVID pandemic, many people lived in fear and questioned the world and eternity as we know it. Some began to see what the Lord was really capable of and started questioning their faith and belief in God. Others tried to write it off and continued to say that God is not real. How can you see the world stand still for two years and still reject a sovereign God over everything? People still did it, and we will see that the Assyrians will still reject the light of the Lord in their toughest time in their history."}]},{"start":19,"end":19,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"In the last couple of verses, God calls the Assyrians a “mighty forest.” It will be destroyed, and God will light them up. It will be flourishing one moment and burnt to a crisp the next. That’s how quickly God can take care of a problem. He doesn’t have to prolong it."},{"kind":"para","text":"If you have a prolonged trial, it is likely that God is trying to teach you something through it. The Assyrians’ trial will be prolonged, but it won’t be long enough because they are not willing to turn to the Lord."}]}]},{"start":20,"end":26,"title":"Judah's Comfort","entries":[{"start":20,"end":20,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God wants us to be placed firmly on the truth. He wants us to be secure in His presence. He is the firm foundation. He is the solid ground. He is our shelter and safe place. It's okay to run and hide in the Lord. He actually wants that."}]},{"start":21,"end":21,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There is a threefold process, as I’ve mentioned before. It speaks about their current circumstances, noting that there will be a remnant left after the Assyrians are dealt with, and they will return."},{"kind":"para","text":"Then, it discusses our current circumstances today, with a more spiritual application, as we are a remnant of the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"Finally, and most importantly, it addresses the future regathering of God’s people. There will be a remnant saved in the last days as well."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And the dragon was wroth with the woman, and went to make war with the remnant of her seed, which keep the commandments of God, and have the testimony of Jesus Christ.","ref":"Revelation 12:17"},{"kind":"para","text":"God will always have a remnant of His people throughout history, and they will be delivered by the Lord as an obvious sign of God's presence in this life and world. There will be no excuse for anyone to reject the Lord when the obvious protection of the remnant is a symbol of His work."}]},{"start":22,"end":22,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Israel started off as a very small nation. They grew into a very large nation through the prosperity of God’s gifting. They will not dwindle into a very small nation again. If you look at Israel today, they are not many. Supposedly, there are 9.558 million Israelites living in the land today. Compared to the 333.3 million in the US, that seems like a very small fraction of people. That is still more than they had during the end of their Babylonian captivity, and it’s likely to be more than they have in Christ’s second coming."},{"kind":"para","text":"However, God has thrown non-Israelites into the mix of the family. We have been adopted into the family of God, and so we are counted as God’s people today. So the number increases drastically compared to the 9 million (and I guarantee there is a much smaller fraction that are actually Christians in that number). God has a lot of people today, but it will be dwindled down to a small percentage in the end (144,000, though I don’t believe that number to be literal, but we can talk about that in Revelation). Either way, God will have a remnant, and it will be proof that He protects His own and is able to bring them through even during the most turbulent times in history."}]},{"start":23,"end":23,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"“Consumption” simply means “full end.” He will gather His people and take care of the problems. This is even more evident that Isaiah is talking about the end times because a full end (to the Lord) is to completely wipe out evil. Not just the Assyrians, but ALL evil and sin."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And the devil that deceived them was cast into the lake of fire and brimstone, where the beast and the false prophet are, and shall be tormented day and night for ever and ever. And I saw a great white throne, and him that sat on it, from whose face the earth and the heaven fled away; and there was found no place for them. And I saw the dead, small and great, stand before God; and the books were opened: and another book was opened, which is the book of life: and the dead were judged out of those things which were written in the books, according to their works. And the sea gave up the dead which were in it; and death and hell delivered up the dead which were in them: and they were judged every man according to their works. And death and hell were cast into the lake of fire. This is the second death. And whosoever was not found written in the book of life was cast into the lake of fire.","ref":"Revelation 20:10-15"}]},{"start":24,"end":24,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Judah will be okay at this time. Those that are dwelling in Zion will be left out of this captivity. They are in an okay standing with the Lord at this moment. They have not completely rejected Him (yet). But the rest of Israel will fall into captivity because they have wholeheartedly given themselves over to their sin."},{"kind":"para","text":"Isaiah brings back Egypt here. Egypt was a display of the captive lifestyle. The Lord allowed them their slavery during that time to prepare them for their wilderness trek. They were to be prepared to take their burdens off and follow after the Lord. However, they liked wearing their burdens, and it caused them to follow God in pain and anguish. That is what it will look like for the Israelites. That is what it looks like for us who cannot lay our burdens down and follow after Christ."}]},{"start":25,"end":26,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There are still people in Judah who will feel the suffering for the sins of the people, as Judah is not completely innocent. However, they will have comfort from the Lord through the pain. Judah is part of Israel, so if there is suffering in one part of Israel, all of Israel will suffer with it."},{"kind":"para","text":"This is the great picture of the church today. We are all one body, and we will all suffer as one body if there is pain anywhere in it."}]}]},{"start":27,"end":34,"title":"About Face","entries":[{"start":27,"end":27,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Eventually, the Lord will relieve the pressure from the Israelites, and that is not just a prophecy from Isaiah. It is a promise to the Israelites from the Lord Himself. He promises to eventually relieve them and get them back on track. However, in order to do that, they must feel some pressure and pain. Otherwise, they will continue to go in the wrong direction and drown themselves in more wickedness and sin until there is no return for His people."},{"kind":"para","text":"God needs His people to return. If they don’t, the Savior cannot come, and the world cannot be saved."}]},{"start":28,"end":29,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is how the Assyrians will come in and take them down. They will roll through this way, and it will be the way in which the Israelites will be conquered. Isaiah is giving warning upon warning about what will come to pass. When it ultimately happens this way, they should not be dumbfounded. They should not be confused about how it happened."},{"kind":"para","text":"They are given every possible cause to prepare and be aware, and yet they will reject it. They will reject it because it’s coming from the mouth of Isaiah. They have already rejected his message, and the Lord warned him already that they would."}]},{"start":30,"end":32,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Whether or not the Assyrians took this route is highly debated. Most scholars argue that this is not the route they took. Whether or not that is accurate, I don’t know. I believe they likely could have. Whatever route they took, the picture is still the same. Screaming and wailing due to the chaos and pain they are facing (or going to face) will still sound the same."},{"kind":"para","text":"Whatever path the Assyrians might have taken to capture Israel doesn’t matter at the end of the day, because Israel was still taken, and they were still held in captivity. They will still have to face the reality of their lifestyle and suffer the consequences of their ignorance and arrogance. Isaiah is giving them plenty of warning of what was going to take place, and they have plenty of time to turn things around, but none of them will listen."},{"kind":"para","text":"Don’t feel bad if your message goes unheard or rejected from your family and neighbors. It’s been happening for centuries now."}]},{"start":33,"end":34,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This college class would be titled “How the Lord Brings Low 101.” It is a continuous review of how God has been able to turn His people back around to face Him. When I was in ROTC, they were very strict about following orders. It was a serious matter to them. Most people look at cadets in the ROTC program as kids who are pretending to play military. I did not take it as pretend military play. I took it because it gave me PE credits (and I hated PE). Little did I know that PE was a big part of ROTC. Either way, one of the things they made sure was ingrained in us was their callouts. When they said right or left, your right or left foot better be in tune, otherwise they would make us stop, yell at us for being out of line, and then start us over. The same was true for standing at attention, saluting, and about face. I liked about face. When they would give me the opportunity to lead the march, I used that one up. I abused it honestly (I think that’s why the other cadets liked it when I led). We would be walking in time, and out of nowhere, I would just yell “ABOUT FACE,” and everyone would have to turn around and walk the opposite direction. After about three steps, I would yell out “ABOUT FACE” again, and we would continue on in the right direction. It was a fun little game to me. I never did it in front of the teachers, but when we would go to raise the flag at the front of the school, I would play that game. Some of the other cadets would take it seriously and get upset because I was just making them walk back and forth for no reason, but others thought it was funny and brought some relief to them."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is what the Lord is doing to His children here. He is calling them to an About Face, and they must turn at the command. They might not understand why they are turning, but they will be thankful they followed the Lord in the end. Sadly, there will be people who tread their own path away from the instructions of the Lord, and they end up getting lost and confused because they have no idea what they are doing. They end up on their own because the rest of the people are serious about following instructions. May we be serious about following God’s instructions and leading."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":9},{"start":10,"end":11},{"start":12,"end":12},{"start":13,"end":14},{"start":15,"end":15},{"start":16,"end":16},{"start":17,"end":18},{"start":19,"end":19},{"start":20,"end":20},{"start":21,"end":21},{"start":22,"end":22},{"start":23,"end":23},{"start":24,"end":24},{"start":25,"end":26},{"start":27,"end":27},{"start":28,"end":29},{"start":30,"end":32},{"start":33,"end":34}],"verses":{"1":"Woe unto them that decree unrighteous decrees, and that write grievousness which they have prescribed;","2":"To turn aside the needy from judgment, and to take away the right from the poor of my people, that widows may be their prey, and that they may rob the fatherless!","3":"And what will ye do in the day of visitation, and in the desolation which shall come from far? to whom will ye flee for help? and where will ye leave your glory?","4":"Without me they shall bow down under the prisoners, and they shall fall under the slain. For all this his anger is not turned away, but his hand is stretched out still.","5":"O Assyrian, the rod of mine anger, and the staff in their hand is mine indignation.","6":"I will send him against an hypocritical nation, and against the people of my wrath will I give him a charge, to take the spoil, and to take the prey, and to tread them down like the mire of the streets.","7":"Howbeit he meaneth not so, neither doth his heart think so; but it is in his heart to destroy and cut off nations not a few.","8":"For he saith, Are not my princes altogether kings?","9":"Is not Calno as Carchemish? is not Hamath as Arpad? is not Samaria as Damascus?","10":"As my hand hath found the kingdoms of the idols, and whose graven images did excel them of Jerusalem and of Samaria;","11":"Shall I not, as I have done unto Samaria and her idols, so do to Jerusalem and her idols?","12":"Wherefore it shall come to pass, that when the Lord hath performed his whole work upon mount Zion and on Jerusalem, I will punish the fruit of the stout heart of the king of Assyria, and the glory of his high looks.","13":"For he saith, By the strength of my hand I have done it, and by my wisdom; for I am prudent: and I have removed the bounds of the people, and have robbed their treasures, and I have put down the inhabitants like a valiant man:","14":"And my hand hath found as a nest the riches of the people: and as one gathereth eggs that are left, have I gathered all the earth; and there was none that moved the wing, or opened the mouth, or peeped.","15":"Shall the axe boast itself against him that heweth therewith? or shall the saw magnify itself against him that shaketh it? as if the rod should shake itself against them that lift it up, or as if the staff should lift up itself, as if it were no wood.","16":"Therefore shall the Lord, the Lord of hosts, send among his fat ones leanness; and under his glory he shall kindle a burning like the burning of a fire.","17":"And the light of Israel shall be for a fire, and his Holy One for a flame: and it shall burn and devour his thorns and his briers in one day;","18":"And shall consume the glory of his forest, and of his fruitful field, both soul and body: and they shall be as when a standard-bearer fainteth.","19":"And the rest of the trees of his forest shall be few, that a child may write them.","20":"And it shall come to pass in that day, that the remnant of Israel, and such as are escaped of the house of Jacob, shall no more again stay upon him that smote them; but shall stay upon the Lord, the Holy One of Israel, in truth.","21":"The remnant shall return, even the remnant of Jacob, unto the mighty God.","22":"For though thy people Israel be as the sand of the sea, yet a remnant of them shall return: the consumption decreed shall overflow with righteousness.","23":"For the Lord God of hosts shall make a consumption, even determined, in the midst of all the land.","24":"Therefore thus saith the Lord God of hosts, O my people that dwellest in Zion, be not afraid of the Assyrian: he shall smite thee with a rod, and shall lift up his staff against thee, after the manner of Egypt.","25":"For yet a very little while, and the indignation shall cease, and mine anger in their destruction.","26":"And the Lord of hosts shall stir up a scourge for him according to the slaughter of Midian at the rock of Oreb: and as his rod was upon the sea, so shall he lift it up after the manner of Egypt.","27":"And it shall come to pass in that day, that his burden shall be taken away from off thy shoulder, and his yoke from off thy neck, and the yoke shall be destroyed because of the anointing.","28":"He is come to Aiath, he is passed to Migron; at Michmash he hath laid up his carriages:","29":"They are gone over the passage: they have taken up their lodging at Geba; Ramah is afraid; Gibeah of Saul is fled.","30":"Lift up thy voice, O daughter of Gallim: cause it to be heard unto Laish, O poor Anathoth.","31":"Madmenah is removed; the inhabitants of Gebim gather themselves to flee.","32":"As yet shall he remain at Nob that day: he shall shake his hand against the mount of the daughter of Zion, the hill of Jerusalem.","33":"Behold, the Lord, the Lord of hosts, shall lop the bough with terror: and the high ones of stature shall be hewn down, and the haughty shall be humbled.","34":"And he shall cut down the thickets of the forest with iron, and Lebanon shall fall by a mighty one."}},
    "11": {"chapter":11,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: Isaiah continued to give warning and prophecy about the impending doom of Israel if they don't correct course and pursue the Lord. It's been a long while since they have followed after God and His Will, and so they are digging themselves into a very difficult position of capture and turmoil. Isaiah has been giving them signs and warnings about what is to come, speaking about repaying their evil deeds, using their enemies to correct them, how God will eventually fix the issues through His soverign plan and Will, why He is providing Judah comfort (at least for the time being), and the necessity to turn from their sins and seek the guidance and presence of the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"In this chapter, Isaiah gives a message of hope, and where it will stem from. Judah is the kingly tribe. Their kings come through that tribe, but we will get a look at Jesse as the foundational lineage of salvation. We will see what salvation will look like, and who the person of Jesus Christ ultimately will become. We get some indepth looks at the way in which Christ moved, thought, and communicated with the Lord. Everything in this chapter (and several others to come) points directly to Jesus Christ and His ministry here on Earth, as well as the second coming of the Lord."}],"previously":["Isaiah continued to give warning and prophecy about the impending doom of Israel if they do not correct their course and pursue the Lord. It has been a long while since they have followed after God and His Will, and so they are digging themselves into a very difficult position of capture and turmoil. Isaiah has been giving them signs and warnings about what is to come, speaking about repaying their evil deeds, using their enemies to correct them, how God will eventually fix the issues through His sovereign plan and Will, why He is providing Judah comfort (at least for the time being), and the necessity to turn from their sins and seek the guidance and presence of the Lord. In this chapter, Isaiah gives a message of hope and where it will stem from. Judah is the kingly tribe. Their kings come through that tribe, but we will get a look at Jesse as the foundational lineage of salvation. We will see what salvation will look like and who the person of Jesus Christ ultimately will become. We get some in-depth looks at the way in which Christ moved, thought, and communicated with the Lord. Everything in this chapter (and several others to come) points directly to Jesus Christ and His ministry here on Earth, as well as the second coming of the Lord."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":5,"title":"A Branch From Roots","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Now, if you don't remember, we had spoken about this term \"Branch\" before."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"In that day shall the branch of the LORD be beautiful and glorious, and the fruit of the earth shall be excellent and comely for them that are escaped of Israel.","ref":"Isaiah 4:2"},{"kind":"para","text":"“Branch” means “A living sprout.” This is speaking about Jesus Christ, of course. The part I find interesting in this verse, however, is the “stem of Jesse” reference. The promise of the Messiah’s coming was given to David."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Moreover I will appoint a place for my people Israel, and will plant them, that they may dwell in a place of their own, and move no more; neither shall the children of wickedness afflict them any more, as beforetime, And as since the time that I commanded judges to be over my people Israel, and have caused thee to rest from all thine enemies. Also the LORD telleth thee that he will make thee an house. And when thy days be fulfilled, and thou shalt sleep with thy fathers, I will set up thy seed after thee, which shall proceed out of thy bowels, and I will establish his kingdom. He shall build an house for my name, and I will stablish the throne of his kingdom for ever. I will be his father, and he shall be my son. If he commit iniquity, I will chasten him with the rod of men, and with the stripes of the children of men: But my mercy shall not depart away from him, as I took it from Saul, whom I put away before thee. And thine house and thy kingdom shall be established for ever before thee: thy throne shall be established for ever.","ref":"2 Samuel 7:10-16"},{"kind":"para","text":"Obviously, Jesse is David’s father, so the promise is still made through that line. However, Jesse was not the man who received the promise, so why is Isaiah mentioning him here? Let’s try cutting up this verse a little bit to grasp the greater context."},{"kind":"para","text":"In our last chapter, we know that God will allow a good portion of Israel to be captured and scattered. There will be a remnant that returns, however, but it won’t be until after the proverbial “tree” has been cut down. The Israelite tree will look like it will never grow back, but from the “roots,” a branch will grow out. The roots of David’s tree begin at Jesse."},{"kind":"para","text":"There have been far better scholars who have pointed out that David was the royal line, and Jesse was the sheepherder one. Because Israel was not acting in the royal way they should have, the title of the sheepherder was more appropriate for Isaiah to use. It will also be in this lowly state that our Lord comes. He will not be a royal king like Israel had seen before. A King for sure, but not to reign over Israel in a battle-ready garment. Rather, He comes as a carpenter and a shepherd."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Is not this the carpenter, the son of Mary, the brother of James, and Joses, and of Juda, and Simon? and are not his sisters here with us? And they were offended at him.\" Mark 6:3 \"I am the good shepherd: the good shepherd giveth his life for the sheep.","ref":"John 10:11"},{"kind":"para","text":"He comes as a light and strait gate."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Then spake Jesus again unto them, saying, I am the light of the world: he that followeth me shall not walk in darkness, but shall have the light of life.\" John 8:12 \"Enter ye in at the strait gate: for wide is the gate, and broad is the way, that leadeth to destruction, and many there be which go in thereat: Because strait is the gate, and narrow is the way, which leadeth unto life, and few there be that find it.","ref":"Matthew 7:13-14"},{"kind":"para","text":"He comes as the bread and vine."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And Jesus said unto them, I am the bread of life: he that cometh to me shall never hunger; and he that believeth on me shall never thirst.\" John 6:35 \"I am the vine, ye are the branches: He that abideth in me, and I in him, the same bringeth forth much fruit: for without me ye can do nothing.","ref":"John 15:5"},{"kind":"para","text":"He is the branch that grows from the roots of the cut-down tree, and He will keep the Israelite lineage alive. I don’t understand how people can see Israel today and assume that God is done with them. I think the Lord is obviously still judging them hard, but I don’t think He’s done with them. I think there’s still a purpose for them yet, and scripture is clear from beginning to end that these people are still wrestling with the Lord. They will continually wrestle with God until His second coming. At that point, there will be no hope for them because they must turn to Him before they see Him. Either way, we should certainly be paying attention to the small remnant that remains in Israel, because I truly believe it is a sign of God’s reign and rulership. He is as done with Israel as He is with the rest of the world, mind you. If He is done with humanity as a whole, we are all doomed more than Israel."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The people thought this would be Solomon. Wisdom certainly rested upon Solomon, but Jesus IS Wisdom. God’s Spirit and Jesus are one person. They belong together. So when we have the Holy Spirit in our lives, it is only because we have Jesus in our lives, and we have trusted the sacrifice of our Heavenly Father. We cannot have one without the other."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"God is a Spirit: and they that worship him must worship him in spirit and in truth.\" John 4:24 \"This I say then, Walk in the Spirit, and ye shall not fulfil the lust of the flesh.\" Galatians 5:16 \"It is the spirit that quickeneth; the flesh profiteth nothing: the words that I speak unto you, they are spirit, and they are life.","ref":"John 6:63"},{"kind":"para","text":"It is obvious that our Lord Jesus Christ did everything in the Spirit of God. He had wisdom and understanding in every direction He took. He had counsel and might from the Father before making any decisions. He had knowledge and fear to seek out the Lord before going into any land or preaching any sermon. He is the embodiment of these verses."},{"kind":"para","text":"The promise that Isaiah is making here is a promise that is evidently kept. We will see in the rest of Isaiah that he brings up this Savior over and over again, and everything connects to Jesus Christ. This is why I consider this book as the first of five gospel accounts. This is good news for the Israelites who were ignoring Isaiah (and still ignore Isaiah today), and good news for the rest of the world."},{"kind":"para","text":"God’s power wasn’t limited to just the Jews in captivity. It was extended to the entire world living in captivity under sin. When God completes a promise, He is one to make sure there are no loopholes or loose ends. The promise is complete, and you can bank on the fact that He made it absolutely sure."}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is fascinating to me. We get a deep look at the person of Jesus through the gospels, but we don’t really see His line of thinking. We understand what He’s doing and why He’s doing it, but Isaiah gives a little more depth to His moving here. When He was simply a young boy, He was teaching to teachers in the temple!"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And when he was twelve years old, they went up to Jerusalem after the custom of the feast. And when they had fulfilled the days, as they returned, the child Jesus tarried behind in Jerusalem; and Joseph and his mother knew not of it. But they, supposing him to have been in the company, went a day's journey; and they sought him among their kinsfolk and acquaintance. And when they found him not, they turned back again to Jerusalem, seeking him. And it came to pass, that after three days they found him in the temple, sitting in the midst of the doctors, both hearing them, and asking them questions. And all that heard him were astonished at his understanding and answers. And when they saw him, they were amazed: and his mother said unto him, Son, why hast thou thus dealt with us? behold, thy father and I have sought thee sorrowing. And he said unto them, How is it that ye sought me? wist ye not that I must be about my Father's business? And they understood not the saying which he spake unto them. And he went down with them, and came to Nazareth, and was subject unto them: but his mother kept all these sayings in her heart. And Jesus increased in wisdom and stature, and in favour with God and man.","ref":"Luke 2:42-52"},{"kind":"para","text":"Jesus had “quick understanding” about important things regarding life and eternity. The Lord granted Him that from birth, otherwise His ministry wouldn’t have started until He was much older in life."},{"kind":"para","text":"Not judging from His eyes or ears does not mean He didn’t judge. This simply means that His judgment wasn’t based on sight and hearing alone. He was Heavenly minded in His judgment. God judges your heart more than your actions."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"I the LORD search the heart, I try the reins, even to give every man according to his ways, and according to the fruit of his doings.","ref":"Jeremiah 17:10"},{"kind":"para","text":"We have mentioned this before, but it is evident that God is more concerned about the reason a man does something rather than what the man is doing. He judges the heart and is able to understand if your heart is based on God’s love and grace or if it has wicked intentions. We see this repeatedly throughout the gospels, but Mark, in particular, demonstrates that Jesus was paying attention to the heart of what people were murmuring."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And immediately when Jesus perceived in his spirit that they so reasoned within themselves, he said unto them, Why reason ye these things in your hearts?","ref":"Mark 2:8"},{"kind":"para","text":"He was attuned to His own Spirit, and the hearts of those around Him who were confused and ignorant."}]},{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I am thankful that the Lord has judged this poor soul righteously. I know what I deserve, and yet His righteousness has given me access away from what I deserve and into a Spirit of grace and truth."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Jews might throw a fit about it because they think salvation is something they should horde. The Catholics may not like the idea that salvation is open to everyone who would simply receive it. The reformed may not agree with my form of “easy beliefism,” as they would call it. The atheists may not be thrilled that I am still preaching and touting a Christ who has freely loved me and given me salvation."},{"kind":"para","text":"But my faith does not depend upon any of them. My faith depends on the Lord alone, and His finished work on the cross. That is something we must consider. He judges poor souls righteously. Guess what? He judges rich souls righteously too. He judges the religionists and the well-to-do’s. They have the greater judgment honestly…"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"He that believeth on him is not condemned: but he that believeth not is condemned already, because he hath not believed in the name of the only begotten Son of God.\" John 3:18 \"I said therefore unto you, that ye shall die in your sins: for if ye believe not that I am he, ye shall die in your sins.\" John 8:24 \"And he shall judge the world in righteousness, he shall minister judgment to the people in uprightness.\" Psalm 9:8 \"For we must all appear before the judgment seat of Christ; that every one may receive the things done in his body, according to that he hath done, whether it be good or bad.","ref":"2 Corinthians 5:10"},{"kind":"para","text":"Judgement begins with those who are claimed \"in the faith.” That should be an eye-opener for all of us reading today."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For the time is come that judgment must begin at the house of God: and if it first begin at us, what shall the end be of them that obey not the gospel of God?","ref":"1 Peter 4:17"},{"kind":"para","text":"How did Jesus judge though? Well He judged with the \"rod of his mouth\" and the \"breath of his lips.” He used the Word of God to make His judgements. That is how we should ALL make our judgements."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Judge not according to the appearance, but judge righteous judgment.","ref":"John 7:24"},{"kind":"para","text":"We should not judge solemnly based on what we feel and what we think. We should judge according to the what God's Word says. That is how Jesus does it, and that is the example that He set for us to do as well. In fact, it is a command that is given to us in John 7."}]},{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There are many things that people try to pin on Jesus Christ. They attempt to make the same accusations against the Lord of creation, but they really can’t. They can try all they want, but they can never say that Jesus was not righteous and that He was not faithful. Everything He did was soaked in righteousness. Give me one lie He spoke in the gospel accounts. Give me one lie that God ever spoke throughout scripture. If you can find a lie in scripture from the mouth of God, you are either doing one of two things: You are misunderstanding the context. Read the whole chapter (preferably the whole book) before you start dissecting one particular verse because context makes the whole thing make sense. You are purposely misusing scripture to try and wrap it around your tainted perception of personal truth. You don’t want to be convinced that you might be wrong, so you pick apart a verse and think that it’s the final authority, not willing to have an open mind and the ability to learn and grow."},{"kind":"para","text":"When we engage in these methods of studying scripture, we will fail the message of God’s Word every single time. I speak this with love for everyone reading today. You (as a saved, born-again child of God) are just as guilty for this stubborn act of closing your heart off to the other person’s perspective. If you want to have love and compassion for the person you are sharing scripture with, you must view scripture and the world from their viewpoint. They aren’t seeing any of this like you are. If you are able to switch places with them, what would you be thinking in their shoes? If you had to deal with their ailments and problems, how would you want it navigated from their perspective?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Jesus was able to give righteous examples and faithful continuance, not because He was good at following God. Of course, He was. I am not denying that. But the reason He had so many people following Him, and twelve faithful members alongside Him, was because He was compassionate towards their needs. He didn’t just tell them to shut up and focus on Him. Rather, He asked questions and prodded their viewpoints to get them to think deeper about their own situations. He wanted them to know that He could see from their viewpoint, and they needed to see from His viewpoint as well."}]}]},{"start":6,"end":9,"title":"Complete Safety","entries":[{"start":6,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"When the Lord has established His reign, which is during His second coming, there will be no need for death or a “food chain.” The lamb will dwell with a wolf. In Jesus’ first appearance, He does not have nice things to say about wolves."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Beware of false prophets, which come to you in sheep's clothing, but inwardly they are ravening wolves.\" Matthew 7:15 \"Go your ways: behold, I send you forth as lambs among wolves.\" Luke 10:3 \"But he that is an hireling, and not the shepherd, whose own the sheep are not, seeth the wolf coming, and leaveth the sheep, and fleeth: and the wolf catcheth them, and scattereth the sheep.","ref":"John 10:12"},{"kind":"para","text":"He refers to specific people as “wolves.” They are individuals who will likely try to blend in with the sheep. I don’t know if the sheep realize how dangerous wolves are. I don’t own any sheep, but I have read stories and seen videos about how innocent lambs are taken by wolves. They don’t seem to see wolves as a threat until it’s too late. Once a wolf gets a sheep, the rest of the sheep are suddenly in great fear and they all run for their lives, knowing that this wolf is bad news. Otherwise, I think they just kind of ignore the wolf, thinking that they are okay and have no reason to worry. How innocent and foolish we are as the sheep of the Lord. We don’t realize the wolf that is living among us."},{"kind":"para","text":"When I was a youth pastor, the teens introduced me to a game called werewolf. You would draw cards from a box, and there were usually two werewolves in the game. There was a narrator who would keep their eyes open the entire game and would direct which person would open their eyes and which persons would keep their eyes closed. When it came time for the wolves to open their eyes, they would look at each other and have to remain as quiet as possible, deciding which person to kill. The townspeople would open their eyes and see someone had died, and they would have to make a decision on who they thought the wolf was and have them killed. 90% of the time, they would make the wrong choice and kill an innocent townsperson, and they would dwindle themselves down until the only two remaining people were the wolves. It was pretty rare that the wolves would last the whole game and win, but it did happen from time to time."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is really how it looks in the church if I’m honest. Pastors and ministers paint this picture about ministry that is truly unrealistic. The ministry is full of innocent sheep who are pointing fingers at each other and calling each other wolves, while the genuine wolf gets away with taking another life. There will be a day when these things will not be so. The sheep and the wolf will be able to dwell together. “Dwell” means “live.” They can literally live right in the middle of each other’s homes, and there will be no harm to them. Leopards and goats will live together. Cows and lions will live together. Cows and bears will eat together. A little child will be able to literally lead these animals as if they are safe to play with and be around. I would not be letting my daughters play with lions and wolves today. I wouldn’t even let them play with cows in all honesty. But in those days, it will be perfectly safe (and seemingly normal). Lions will eat straw like oxen. I can’t even picture that without smirking. It seems like such a strange concept to me. They will be satisfied with that though. Jesus will bring absolute peace and safety to this world like has never been seen before."}]},{"start":8,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is interesting. We are certainly getting a picture of something that is far in the future, above and beyond the Lord’s first appearance. So this is either taking place at His second appearance, or after (which is far more likely) His judgment is complete. It says there will be “sucking children” playing with the hole (whether the place in which the snake lives, or the mouth of it) of an “asp” (which is a snake). They can literally put an infant’s hand into a snake’s mouth and won’t have to worry about it. A “weaned” child (that is one that can finally walk around, but probably can’t even speak yet) will be able to play in a cockatrice’s den. “Cockatrice” means “poisonous serpent.” The den can be full of them and there would be no enticements from the snakes to try and poison this child. Even if there was, the child would be resistant and safe."},{"kind":"para","text":"But I find it fascinating that there will be children in those days. Will there be further life and having children in eternity’s future? I don’t know. I would assume not. But there is no real solid evidence that the New Earth will not become populous. Whatever the Lord sees fit is what we are to expect and find joy in. This kind of insinuates there would be, but I couldn’t tell you one way or another. Maybe having children will look a little different in those days. Maybe it will be more spiritual than physical. I could not say. Whatever the case may be, now is a good time to have kids, and plenty of them! Get your children into church, growing in the faith, and prepare them for a long and joyous eternity with you."}]},{"start":9,"end":9,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This sounds like paradise. I can’t wait to know the Lord so well that I don’t have to question a single thing. God’s knowledge is impossible for us to grasp today in our finite mortal bodies. His knowledge will be expounded and evident once we are received into glory. What a great and exciting thought to rejoice over today."},{"kind":"para","text":"Someday, we will not have to ever question anything ever again. If we stay faithful and true to the Lord today (even in the midst of our thoughts and concerns), God will eventually give us all the answers we have ever asked or thought of."}]}]},{"start":10,"end":10,"title":"The Gentiles Perspective","entries":[{"start":10,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is an incredible prophecy here. You who are reading this are likely a Gentile. “Gentile” means “nation usually of non-Hebrew origins.” This gives further clarity and providence to the Lord saving the whole world, not just the Jews. The Jews were very prominent in believing that God’s grace and salvation were closed off specifically to them alone. Even the disciples thought this way for a time. They find out in the book of Acts that they are completely wrong. This small verse right here is proof of how wrong they were. They must have missed it honestly. I think it would have been wise for each disciple to go through the book of Isaiah as a training course before becoming leaders of ministry, but that was not up to me. Thankfully, we have the whole of scripture as our training course today to qualify us."},{"kind":"para","text":"I had a man ask me the other day, “So what is your degree in? Theology? Bible teaching? Scriptural analysis?” I just smiled at this poor man whom I was about to break the confidence of and say, “I never studied in college at all.” Take that with what you will. I don’t care how unlearned or ignorant people perceive me as, when I have scripture, I have a solid foundation. We can just study scripture alone. Some people don’t know how to do that, and so a Bible college course might be a necessity, but I’m glad that the Lord has given me the ability to study scripture for our more unlearned folk down here outside of the college debt department. I have nothing against college; I want to make that clear. But if college is what is teaching you how to study and teach scripture and not God’s Word, you are sorely mistaken about God’s commands."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But continue thou in the things which thou hast learned and hast been assured of, knowing of whom thou hast learned them; And that from a child thou hast known the holy scriptures, which are able to make thee wise unto salvation through faith which is in Christ Jesus. All scripture is given by inspiration of God, and is profitable for doctrine, for reproof, for correction, for instruction in righteousness: That the man of God may be perfect, throughly furnished unto all good works.\" 2 Timothy 3:14-17 \"Thy word have I hid in mine heart, that I might not sin against thee.\" Psalm 119:11 \"Study to shew thyself approved unto God, a workman that needeth not to be ashamed, rightly dividing the word of truth.\" 2 Timothy 2:15 \"These were more noble than those in Thessalonica, in that they received the word with all readiness of mind, and searched the scriptures daily, whether those things were so.\" Acts 17:11 \"For the word of God is quick, and powerful, and sharper than any twoedged sword, piercing even to the dividing asunder of soul and spirit, and of the joints and marrow, and is a discerner of the thoughts and intents of the heart.","ref":"Hebrews 4:12"},{"kind":"para","text":"I can go down a list of the importance of studying God’s Word. The New Testament scriptures repeatedly show church leaders who were not “scholarly” men getting into positions of “scholarly” service. Honestly, I’m glad I don’t have a Bible education to taint my studies of scripture."},{"kind":"para","text":"I think many people believe what they believe about scripture because someone taught it to them rather than aligning it with the rest of the Bible. We must all come to the ability to personally evaluate scripture and rightly divide it, giving ourselves the room to learn, grow, and make our own valuable connections."},{"kind":"para","text":"Some people might not agree with some of the ways in which I have taught scripture, or some of the ideas I have seen in scripture, but I have no formal teaching to taint my vision of what is right in front of me. All I can do (as an unlearned man) is simply line up scripture with more scripture. That is why I have other verses to give testimony to it."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Heaven and earth shall pass away, but my words shall not pass away.","ref":"Matthew 24:35"}]}]},{"start":11,"end":11,"title":"A Second Recovery","entries":[{"start":11,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"“…in that day…” in what day? Well, in the last days. That is what Isaiah means when he says it. He has mentioned it a few times already, and every time he talks about the last days. So, in the last days, God is going to restore Israel to their land. The first time was coming in from Egypt (Joshua gives the account). The second time will be after His Second Coming. He will be calling His people from all over the world, as Isaiah is getting at. Not just Assyria, Egypt, Pathros, Cush, Elam, Shinar, and Hamath… but from the islands of the sea. Everywhere that God’s children are, He will gather them back again in the last days, and it will be His second time recovering His remnant."}]}]},{"start":12,"end":16,"title":"Always a Way","entries":[{"start":12,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Jesus Christ being the “ensign.\" \"Ensign\" means \"Signal pole\" or \"banner\" or \"something lifted up.” Jesus clarifies it Himself (thankfully)."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And as Moses lifted up the serpent in the wilderness, even so must the Son of man be lifted up:","ref":"John 3:14"},{"kind":"para","text":"The whole world knows about Jesus. Even in communist countries where it is illegal to even speak about scripture and Christ, they know that Jesus was a person who died on a cross. They have heard stories about this man named Jesus. I did not grow up in a Christian home by any means, yet I knew about Jesus. I didn’t know Jesus personally, but I knew that name. We even used His name in blasphemy. My Jehovah’s Witness grandma knew about Jesus. There is no denying His ensign. He is the most famous name in the entire Earth, and equally the most rejected in it. That’s what is crazy to me."},{"kind":"para","text":"Before the street preacher ever speaks about the name of Jesus to someone, they have already heard the name. They have probably heard it in their own families. They have denied it from the teaching of their parents. Perhaps their parents were staunch and strict Christians who robbed the joy of following the Lord. I couldn’t say, but I know that everyone hears about Christ no matter what part of the Earth you may reside in. It’s impossible for people not to talk about Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"People are in distress by that name today. They will complain and moan about the guys who speak that name, and they will try to shut down anyone who desires to mention it. Yet it’s something they will have to deal with for the rest of time. Jesus will never stop being talked about, no matter how many people try to kill the preachers."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Consider what I say; and the Lord give thee understanding in all things. Remember that Jesus Christ of the seed of David was raised from the dead according to my gospel: Wherein I suffer trouble, as an evil doer, even unto bonds; but the word of God is not bound.","ref":"2 Timothy 2:7-9"}]},{"start":13,"end":13,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Ephraim was the northern nation of Israel, whereas Judah was the southern nation. Remember, there was a great separation that took place just before their captivity. Ephraim will try to work with the Syrians to attack Judah. But when Christ rules, Ephraim and Judah will be cohesive and united. They will work together for the cause of Christ. There’s a lot of spiritual application to this, of course, but this is also literal. The prophecies (all of them) are symbolic and literal. That is why I love God’s prophecies so much. People can look at the book of Revelation and get hung up on what is symbolic and what is literal. There are whole chasms built between people of the faith because they don’t want to agree on which is which and how to divide the book up, but I can argue both sides."},{"kind":"para","text":"Why? Well, going back to what I’ve said before, I am not tainted by a scholarly viewpoint. No one taught me what Revelation said, and so I have been tasked with viewing the answers from both perspectives and making the most coherent and obvious conclusion linking up with the rest of scripture. I could argue both sides because both sides have their truth to them. Both sides also have their faults. I could argue both sides of the post-tribulation and pre-tribulation rapture people. I could argue all three sides of the premillennial, amillennial, and postmillennial reign as well. I have my solidified understanding of what makes the most sense biblically speaking, but I am not tainted by someone telling me what they think. I’ve conducted my own conclusion solely based upon what lines up the most with the rest of scripture."},{"kind":"para","text":"So, my goal with this is not to cause division and say, “This is how it is, and you must agree with it or else you are a Devil.” Rather, my goal with this is to open conversation and explore all aspects, making the most logical conclusion possible. Not everyone will agree with that method, but I think it’s the smartest and most adventurous method we can have. We should not shy away from someone else’s viewpoint simply because we have our minds made up. We should think on specific things. In fact, Paul says this;"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Finally, brethren, whatsoever things are true, whatsoever things are honest, whatsoever things are just, whatsoever things are pure, whatsoever things are lovely, whatsoever things are of good report; if there be any virtue, and if there be any praise, think on these things.","ref":"Philippians 4:8"},{"kind":"para","text":"Look at what the other person is talking about. Is it true? Perhaps there is truth to it, but we don’t really know. Is it honest? They might be sincere in their approach and are being as honest as possible. Is it just? If it has to do with God’s character and Will, it is likely something that is just. Is it pure? The intentions might be pure, but the motives behind what they are saying might not be. Is it lovely? That’s a good place to draw a line. If what they are saying is all the others, but it is not very lovely, you might want to refrain from the conversation any further. Is it of good report? This could also mean “Is there a lot of people who would agree with this?” Is there virtue or praise? If it brings glory to the Lord, then think on these things. Tick these boxes. Some of the boxes may not receive a tick quite yet, but if there is one box that is literally marked off and can’t fit into the conversation, you are wasting your time thinking on it. These all should go together if we are evaluating scripture. These things must line up with what we are talking about."},{"kind":"para","text":"Quite recently, I threw out the idea and concept that the Lord constantly brings His people back together over and over again throughout scripture, and it’s why I believe He chooses the twelve disciples that He does. I believe each disciple is from a specific tribe. I have no way to firmly confirm that (other than if Christ flat out says it Himself straight to our faces), so I told them to take it with a grain of salt, and it’s not a hill I’m willing to die on, just an astute observation. One particular person disagreed with my thought process (which is completely fine, I like the challenge), but the rest of the people disagreed with him. He is under the conclusion that the Lord is completely done with Israel because the church exists now. But let’s draw back to my original point. I knew that it might throw a bit of a wrench in the road of their thoughts, and I’m hopeful that it doesn’t cause a stumbling block to anyone in there (again, this was nothing I was going to firmly stand on), but I want us to line up my method of thinking with this verse in Philippians. Was my thought true? Well, we can’t really affirm it to be true, but it’s true that God continually unites His people (this whole chapter has been about that by the way). Was it honest? I tried my best to give as much information as possible, including extending Bible verses to clarify the purpose behind why I think it to be true, so it’s honest as can be. Is it just? Well, the Lord is just to do what He wants with His children, and I think bringing His children together for the common cause of following God is a just thing to do. Is it pure? Unity is a pure thing, so I am under the impression that this was as pure as pure could be. I had no intentions of trying to trip someone up, so I believe I did it with purity and prayer. Was it lovely? I think God unifying His wayward children is the most lovely thing written in scripture. That is the theme of scripture. Is it of good report? Well, other than the proofs and the texts that I used to clarify through scripture, there were a lot of men who had thoughts on it as well that coincided with what I was trying to portray, so I’d say so. Was there virtue and praise? I believe it extended glory right back to the Lord, and also Jesus’ heart for the lost of this world, so yes. It ticks all the boxes then, and so it’s right for us to think on these things. Even if there is one person who is against it, I think it’s an appropriate thing to think on by the standards of Paul’s encouragement to the Philippian church."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is how we will see unity in every aspect of life. Unity doesn’t come because we have decided that we are done fighting. Unity comes because Christ unifies us. Period. If there is no unity, someone is missing Christ."}]},{"start":14,"end":14,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"These people, including the Philistines, Edom, Moab, and Ammon, were all enemies of Israel. We have done a quite extensive study of these enemies, particularly the Philistines and Ammon, in previous chapters of scripture."},{"kind":"para","text":"During the time of the Messiah’s reign, these people will never have the ability to rule or hurt Israel again. The enemies of the Lord’s children will be restrained, and they will be ruled over. There will be no enemies during that time."}]},{"start":15,"end":15,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The “Egyptian sea” is likely a reference to the Red Sea. It would be an obstacle for the Israelites to cross through to get back to the land, but God has already demonstrated that He can perform a miracle with this obstacle through Moses when he split the Red Sea for them to pass over into the wilderness."},{"kind":"para","text":"Whatever the “seven streams” are doesn’t really matter. I’m sure we could probably take our guesses. The point is, God will provide a path over any obstacle that might stand in their way, even if there are seven, or seven hundred. God always provides a way to go through His Will safely."}]},{"start":16,"end":16,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Imagine that. Every person from every nation who knows the Lord will have the ability to cross this Earth straight into the land in which the Lord will be. We will have a single road leading straight to the Savior. There’s a lot of spiritual applicability in this verse that I hope we don’t miss."},{"kind":"para","text":"Christ only provides one road to salvation. It is only through Him. He IS the road. He is the spiritual “highway” spoken about here. The same way that there was a way made for Israel to escape Egypt, there will be a way for God’s children to escape the captivity they are currently in. Jesus is the path."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Jesus saith unto him, I am the way, the truth, and the life: no man cometh unto the Father, but by me.","ref":"John 14:6"},{"kind":"para","text":"Praise the Lord for our highway to salvation (Jesus Christ). He is the only way to eternal acceptance in the Lord."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":9},{"start":10,"end":10},{"start":11,"end":11},{"start":12,"end":12},{"start":13,"end":13},{"start":14,"end":14},{"start":15,"end":15},{"start":16,"end":16}],"verses":{"1":"And there shall come forth a rod out of the stem of Jesse, and a Branch shall grow out of his roots:","2":"And the spirit of the Lord shall rest upon him, the spirit of wisdom and understanding, the spirit of counsel and might, the spirit of knowledge and of the fear of the Lord;","3":"And shall make him of quick understanding in the fear of the Lord: and he shall not judge after the sight of his eyes, neither reprove after the hearing of his ears:","4":"But with righteousness shall he judge the poor, and reprove with equity for the meek of the earth: and he shall smite the earth: with the rod of his mouth, and with the breath of his lips shall he slay the wicked.","5":"And righteousness shall be the girdle of his loins, and faithfulness the girdle of his reins.","6":"The wolf also shall dwell with the lamb, and the leopard shall lie down with the kid; and the calf and the young lion and the fatling together; and a little child shall lead them.","7":"And the cow and the bear shall feed; their young ones shall lie down together: and the lion shall eat straw like the ox.","8":"And the sucking child shall play on the hole of the asp, and the weaned child shall put his hand on the cockatrice' den.","9":"They shall not hurt nor destroy in all my holy mountain: for the earth shall be full of the knowledge of the Lord, as the waters cover the sea.","10":"And in that day there shall be a root of Jesse, which shall stand for an ensign of the people; to it shall the Gentiles seek: and his rest shall be glorious.","11":"And it shall come to pass in that day, that the Lord shall set his hand again the second time to recover the remnant of his people, which shall be left, from Assyria, and from Egypt, and from Pathros, and from Cush, and from Elam, and from Shinar, and from Hamath, and from the islands of the sea.","12":"And he shall set up an ensign for the nations, and shall assemble the outcasts of Israel, and gather together the dispersed of Judah from the four corners of the earth.","13":"The envy also of Ephraim shall depart, and the adversaries of Judah shall be cut off: Ephraim shall not envy Judah, and Judah shall not vex Ephraim.","14":"But they shall fly upon the shoulders of the Philistines toward the west; they shall spoil them of the east together: they shall lay their hand upon Edom and Moab; and the children of Ammon shall obey them.","15":"And the Lord shall utterly destroy the tongue of the Egyptian sea; and with his mighty wind shall he shake his hand over the river, and shall smite it in the seven streams, and make men go over dryshod.","16":"And there shall be an highway for the remnant of his people, which shall be left, from Assyria; like as it was to Israel in the day that he came up out of the land of Egypt."}},
    "12": {"chapter":12,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: In our last chapter, Isaiah made it clear that God will gather His people again. He gave the characteristics of the coming Messiah, and what ultimate redemption will look like. We might be redeemed today, but there will be a day when the redeemed will be gathered, and the pain of this world will be destroyed and held down. Eventually there will be no pain at all, and Christ will have thrown sin and suffering into Hell with Satan and his demons."},{"kind":"para","text":"In this chapter, we will get a song of rejoicing in our salvation. It's a short chapter, but it's such a sweet thing to remember even for our lives today. We will see that this will be the mindset of the people during the tribulation period, or likely during the reign of the Lord in His second coming. We will have reason to rejoice about His presence when He comes again."}],"previously":["In our last chapter, Isaiah made it clear that God will gather His people again. He described the characteristics of the coming Messiah and what ultimate redemption will look like. We might be redeemed today, but there will be a day when the redeemed will be gathered, and the pain of this world will be destroyed and held down. Eventually, there will be no pain at all, and Christ will have thrown sin and suffering into Hell with Satan and his demons. In this chapter, we will receive a song of rejoicing in our salvation. It’s a short chapter, but it’s such a sweet thing to remember even for our lives today. We will see that this will be the mindset of the people during the tribulation period, or likely during the reign of the Lord in His second coming. We will have reason to rejoice about His presence when He comes again."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":2,"title":"Our Salvation","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Obviously, if a sentence starts with the word “and,” then we must assume it’s a continuous thought. Chapter 11 and chapter 12 go together. I’m glad they are not together, though, because there is a great reason to spend a lot of time in this chapter (with or without the rest of these chapters) because it brings us back to the gospel again."},{"kind":"para","text":"We received an affirmative message in our last chapter that God is going to reunite His people. We are assured of that. But this chapter is a prayer. It’s kind of treated as a Psalm in a way. This is what our experience is like under the salvation of Jesus. It will be the world’s Spirit when Jesus returns again to rule and reign."},{"kind":"para","text":"God’s anger is turned away from you the moment you receive Christ as your Savior. Even if you fall into sin, He will not expend His wrath upon you. Your debt has been forgiven. He will deal with you like you are His child, not like you are His enemy. He will deal with those that do not turn to Him like His enemy, but those that trust in Christ are His children."},{"kind":"para","text":"We will have more than enough reason to praise the Lord “in that day.” This would indicate the last days. Honestly, we could view this as the “Great Tribulation” days. When we are reading through the tribulation, we will not see butterflies and rainbows. There is not much flourishing. Yet the children of God will be able to sing praises to His name and receive comfort from the Lord! God protects and gathers His children."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God IS salvation. Christ is the physical embodiment of God’s salvation for mankind. If we cannot accept the physical proof of God’s gift to mankind, we will never accept the spiritual salvation of the Lord either. We are a people who must see to believe, and Christ is our sight of belief. It starts with Him. He is our strength and song. He has literally BECOME our salvation."},{"kind":"para","text":"Furthermore, this verse alone puts to bed the notion that we must do any sort of work to get salvation. God alone IS our salvation. If you want to be saved, Isaiah says you must have the person of salvation, not the works of salvation. In fact, Isaiah has spent the last eleven chapters specifically speaking against the idea that we can somehow earn salvation. He talks about how far gone these people are, and yet God will provide salvation to them in the midst of their sin."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But God commendeth his love toward us, in that, while we were yet sinners, Christ died for us.","ref":"Romans 5:8"}]}]},{"start":3,"end":6,"title":"Burst In Praise","entries":[{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Salvation is a well that never ends. Every time we draw from the well of Salvation, we find joy in doing it because it continues for the rest of eternity. Once you are saved, you will never stop being saved. God knows how to preserve His people through His Word."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"The words of the LORD are pure words: as silver tried in a furnace of earth, purified seven times. Thou shalt keep them, O LORD, thou shalt preserve them from this generation for ever. The wicked walk on every side, when the vilest men are exalted.","ref":"Psalm 12:6-8"},{"kind":"para","text":"By the way, whenever we see the word “Well” in scripture, we can associate it with God’s Word. “Water” is the resource we get from it. Christ is the Living Water. We have mentioned this several times before, but it’s important to keep that in our memories."},{"kind":"para","text":"In this verse, Isaiah is literally saying that salvation comes from God’s Word, from which we can draw our faith. This water is assurance."}]},{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"That can be today! We don’t have to wait for His second coming to praise the Lord and call upon His name. We know what He has done, and the fact that we are benefactors of His goodness should be enough reason to tell others about His name."},{"kind":"para","text":"I want us to understand that we are going to exalt something. We will either exalt ourselves, exalt others, or exalt the Lord. May it be turned on its head. We should start by exalting the Lord, and that will lift others up, which will (in turn) allow the Lord to lift us up as well."},{"kind":"para","text":"If there are people left behind, it’s because they have gotten one of these things out of place. Likely, they are not exalting the Lord like they should be."}]},{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Sing what? That’s a great question. I think a lot of people are under the impression that we should only be singing Psalms to the Lord. Psalms are great, and we should be utilizing those in our worship (I have nothing against it). Paul demonstrates a little further how we should be singing."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Speaking to yourselves in psalms and hymns and spiritual songs, singing and making melody in your heart to the Lord; Giving thanks always for all things unto God and the Father in the name of our Lord Jesus Christ; Submitting yourselves one to another in the fear of God.","ref":"Ephesians 5:19-21"},{"kind":"para","text":"While this is a prophecy for the end times, it can still be a reality today. We should be singing to the Lord and lifting others up for Him right now. We should take our time to praise God and exalt His name. Why don’t we? Why are we waiting for the end times to do it? We are acting as if He is not currently in our presence while we wander on this Earth in our faith. If we have a perfect salvation from Him, why don’t we sing about it for Him? He is listening, and He finds great joy that we would be willing to worship Him with our voices and in our faiths."}]},{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"How can we sit so silent? There should be something inside of you that simply wants to burst with cries and shouts to the Lord. There should be a stir that makes it so you can’t sit still. When I preach, I tend to move around a bit. I can’t seem to really sit still. I need to walk and talk (it helps me think). I do the same thing when I’m on the phone. It’s so much easier for me to think when my feet are moving. I don’t know why, but I feel like if I’m sitting down and trying to hold a conversation that I’m going to burst. I get antsy and a little anxious. I don’t know what that means (perhaps it’s some sort of mental ailment that I have never had treated or determined), but I know that feeling translates rather well to the feeling of keeping your mouth shut about God’s great salvation."},{"kind":"para","text":"We should be bursting out in tears and acclamation! We should be praising God for His greatness and the fact that He has given us an eternal security with Him. What a great and glorious reason to sing to the Lord. Mind you, that is what all of eternity will be filled with. We will just be singing to the Lord about everything all the time. We should get used to that now."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":6}],"verses":{"1":"And in that day thou shalt say, O Lord, I will praise thee: though thou wast angry with me, thine anger is turned away, and thou comfortedst me.","2":"Behold, God is my salvation; I will trust, and not be afraid: for the Lord Jehovah is my strength and my song; he also is become my salvation.","3":"Therefore with joy shall ye draw water out of the wells of salvation.","4":"And in that day shall ye say, Praise the Lord, call upon his name, declare his doings among the people, make mention that his name is exalted.","5":"Sing unto the Lord; for he hath done excellent things: this is known in all the earth.","6":"Cry out and shout, thou inhabitant of Zion: for great is the Holy One of Israel in the midst of thee."}},
    "13": {"chapter":13,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: In our last chapter, Isaiah gives us a victory story in the last days. He describes how excited God's children will be to see the Lord triumph and save His children. It will be a day of rejoicing for everyone that survived the terrible pains of the tribulation, and those that have already passed on. We will rejoice when the Lord's Salvation (that is Jesus Christ) comes again and reigns over this Earth. It was an alleviating chapter after reading about so much destruction and pain for God's children."},{"kind":"para","text":"In this chapter, the pain doesn't seem to stop. We go right back into another captivity and this time it will be placed on the southern part of Israel. We will see about this Babylonian empire, and what will ultimately become of it, and the scars and evidence of these events taking place is still proven and evident today!"}],"previously":["In our last chapter, Isaiah presents a victory story in the last days. He describes how excited God’s children will be to see the Lord triumph and save His children. It will be a day of rejoicing for everyone who survived the terrible pains of the tribulation and those who have already passed on. We will rejoice when the Lord’s Salvation, that is Jesus Christ, comes again and reigns over this Earth. It was an alleviating chapter after reading about so much destruction and pain for God’s children. In this chapter, the pain doesn’t seem to stop. We go right back into another captivity, and this time it will be placed on the southern part of Israel. We will see about this Babylonian empire and what will ultimately become of it. The scars and evidence of these events taking place are still proven and evident today!"],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":1,"title":"The Burden of Babylon","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"We are suddenly in a very different mood entering into this chapter. We came off a high of praise towards the Lord for His salvation and His unity to His children to “The burden of Babylon…” Babylon is a very widely known place of reference in our modern world. No one can deny the historical evidence and power of Babylon in our world. People want to reject and deny a large portion of scripture in every way, but historically speaking, they can’t deny this nation and the judgment that the Lord is going to provide to them. Babylon will be the place in which the Israelites will be taken into captivity. We get a clearer picture of this place in the book of Daniel, which is another great study."},{"kind":"para","text":"While God is trying to unite His children, the world is uniting against God. They are still uniting against the Lord today. Babylon has fallen, but the spirit of Babylon will rise again before the Lord’s second coming. “Babylon” means “confusion.” They were a mixed group of people that certainly lived in confusion. Their origins stem from Babel in the book of Genesis. All the world was unified at that time against the Lord, and so God had to confuse them in their speech to keep them from making a grave mistake."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And the whole earth was of one language, and of one speech. And it came to pass, as they journeyed from the east, that they found a plain in the land of Shinar; and they dwelt there. And they said one to another, Go to, let us make brick, and burn them throughly. And they had brick for stone, and slime had they for morter. And they said, Go to, let us build us a city and a tower, whose top may reach unto heaven; and let us make us a name, lest we be scattered abroad upon the face of the whole earth. And the LORD came down to see the city and the tower, which the children of men builded. And the LORD said, Behold, the people is one, and they have all one language; and this they begin to do: and now nothing will be restrained from them, which they have imagined to do. Go to, let us go down, and there confound their language, that they may not understand one another's speech. So the LORD scattered them abroad from thence upon the face of all the earth: and they left off to build the city. Therefore is the name of it called Babel; because the LORD did there confound the language of all the earth: and from thence did the LORD scatter them abroad upon the face of all the earth.","ref":"Genesis 11:1-9"},{"kind":"para","text":"We will see this place come up over and over again in Revelation, and it has a two-fold purpose in this prophecy of Isaiah. First, it serves a physical and literal purpose. Second, it has a symbolic and future purpose. This is another proof that God’s prophecies are both symbolic and literal."}]}]},{"start":2,"end":5,"title":"Weapons of War","entries":[{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God is literally allowing this nation to be lifted up. In the end times, there will be a great city that will be raised, and the whole world will look to its power. That city will only be allowed to exist because the Lord gives it room. We know that to be true because God will tear it down after all its time of prosperity and growth."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Standing afar off for the fear of her torment, saying, Alas, alas, that great city Babylon, that mighty city! for in one hour is thy judgment come.","ref":"Revelation 18:10"},{"kind":"para","text":"We can study that better in Revelation. God is giving them prosperity instead of His own children. He even calls them His “sanctified ones” and “mighty ones” for His anger in the next verse."}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"“Sanctified” means “set apart.” They are purposely set apart for the Lord’s use in this regard. They will be used to hurt and change the hearts of the people of God by the fact that God is prospering them more than His own children."},{"kind":"para","text":"Isaiah is getting the vision of God’s use for them and how He will provide them with an ultimate victory. God has done this with Assyria, and we read that a few chapters back."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"O Assyrian, the rod of mine anger, and the staff in their hand is mine indignation.","ref":"Isaiah 10:5"},{"kind":"para","text":"God can use the evil in this world to get His children back on track. He can use anything at His disposal to make sure righteousness will reign. He will allow wickedness to proceed, but He will not allow it to ever win. That’s what makes Him so good."}]},{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Assyria went against the Israelites, but the people of Judah were protected. Now, Babylon will go against the people of Judah. Judah has run its course. They should have learned the lessons of Northern Israel, but they don’t, and it will become a problem for them now because they have rejected the obvious leading of the Lord. They will be great in number, and it will be as a “tumultuous noise” to those in the battle."}]},{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"They will be a mix of people, as I mentioned before. They will be mighty individuals from all different walks of life. America is touted for its acceptance of religious diversity. It is self-praised for its desires to allow all walks of life. However, all walks of life, except for the Christian faith, are truly accepted. That is what Babylon will look like. It is what it will look like as we read through these chapters, and it will be what they look like in the end times as well. Everything will be accepted except for the Biblical God, and if the Biblical God is accepted, it will only be so that they can profit off of Him. They will only accept certain parts of it that match up with what makes them feel good about their sins and selves. In the end, Babylon will just be used as a weapon by the Lord."}]}]},{"start":6,"end":8,"title":"The Day of the Lord","entries":[{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The New Testament church spoke a lot about the day of the Lord too."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But of the times and the seasons, brethren, ye have no need that I write unto you. For yourselves know perfectly that the day of the Lord so cometh as a thief in the night. For when they shall say, Peace and safety; then sudden destruction cometh upon them, as travail upon a woman with child; and they shall not escape. But ye, brethren, are not in darkness, that that day should overtake you as a thief.\" 1 Thessalonians 5:1-4 \"But the day of the Lord will come as a thief in the night; in the which the heavens shall pass away with a great noise, and the elements shall melt with fervent heat, the earth also and the works that are therein shall be burned up. Seeing then that all these things shall be dissolved, what manner of persons ought ye to be in all holy conversation and godliness, Looking for and hasting unto the coming of the day of God, wherein the heavens being on fire shall be dissolved, and the elements shall melt with fervent heat?\" 2 Peter 3:10-12 \"Behold, I come as a thief. Blessed is he that watcheth, and keepeth his garments, lest he walk naked, and they see his shame. And he gathered them together into a place called in the Hebrew tongue Armageddon.\" Revelation 16:15-16 \"The sun shall be turned into darkness, and the moon into blood, before that great and notable day of the Lord come:\" Acts 2:20 \"To deliver such an one unto Satan for the destruction of the flesh, that the spirit may be saved in the day of the Lord Jesus.","ref":"1 Corinthians 5:5"},{"kind":"para","text":"Again, it cannot be emphasized enough that prophecy comes in three waves. The first wave involves the symbolism of the Lord of the events taking place on a more spiritual plane. The second wave is the literal interpretation of the Lord, where it comes to pass on God’s children for God’s purpose. Finally, there is a worldwide event that will shake and shatter the nations. When a prophet speaks through the Lord, it is set in stone and will come to pass in that way, every single time. This includes the prophecy here."},{"kind":"para","text":"Isaiah begins this prophecy, which is then carried over literally and symbolically to the New Testament church. Ultimately, it will become a worldwide prophecy revealed in the end times. Right now, however, the Israelites must prepare themselves for a catastrophic takeover by Babylon. They will not take Isaiah seriously, and they will learn the hard way that you do not forsake the Word of the Lord, both literally and prophetically."}]},{"start":7,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Jesus gives this same kind of picture for the Great Tribulation."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For nation shall rise against nation, and kingdom against kingdom: and there shall be famines, and pestilences, and earthquakes, in divers places. All these are the beginning of sorrows. Then shall they deliver you up to be afflicted, and shall kill you: and ye shall be hated of all nations for my name's sake.","ref":"Matthew 24:7-9"},{"kind":"para","text":"The birth pains are obvious to the one giving birth. To everyone else, we cannot relate. There will be a lot of very terrible things that will happen in this world (and specifically to Christians for the sake of following Christ), and it will not look like a very prosperous world. To the world itself, it will seem prosperous. To the Christian, we know that it’s God’s judgment being poured out."},{"kind":"para","text":"To the Israelites, they will know it’s God’s judgment being poured out too when Babylon comes in and takes them captive. Their captivity will be because of their rejection of the Lord. The Christians’ “captivity” in this world will be because of our following of Him. It seems that no matter which side we choose, we will be held captive in this world."},{"kind":"para","text":"I praise the Lord that I am not owned by this world, though. They can do whatever they want to my mortal body; I have a spiritual one that is far more important reserved for me in eternity."}]}]},{"start":9,"end":16,"title":"Utter Destruction","entries":[{"start":9,"end":9,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"His day is coming. That is a reason we should be taking our walks of faith far more seriously. We should be reaching and teaching with more fervency because “the Day of the Lord cometh, cruel both with wrath and fierce anger.” Thankfully, His anger is not reserved for His children. This time around, His anger will be solemnly reserved for those who do not know Him. We will be saved from His wrath."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And to wait for his Son from heaven, whom he raised from the dead, even Jesus, which delivered us from the wrath to come.","ref":"1 Thessalonians 1:10"}]},{"start":10,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is also talked in Revelation, and Jesus talks about it as well!"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And the fourth angel sounded, and the third part of the sun was smitten, and the third part of the moon, and the third part of the stars; so as the third part of them was darkened, and the day shone not for a third part of it, and the night likewise.\" Revelation 8:12 \"Immediately after the tribulation of those days shall the sun be darkened, and the moon shall not give her light, and the stars shall fall from heaven, and the powers of the heavens shall be shaken:","ref":"Matthew 24:29"},{"kind":"para","text":"The Israelites will be held in captivity for such a length of time that being outdoors would likely be a treat to most of them. They won’t be treated like free people. They won’t be treated like the children of God. They will be treated like slaves and treated like objects. That is something else we will see in the end times as well."},{"kind":"para","text":"The world says, “If God is good, then why does He allow bad things to happen like rape and murder?” They must have missed the part where He allows that to His children and to the Israelites in scripture because of the wickedness of the world. He will punish wickedness, though. If there was no wickedness, we would find another reason to complain about the Lord. Furthermore, we would not seek the standard of good because we would think our own goodness is the standard. We already think that. How much more if God just ignored our wickedness?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Here’s the key thought: God is good. We are not. That is why there is wickedness in this world, and it’s why God will judge us. In fact, He makes that clear in the next verse."}]},{"start":11,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I have only been alive for thirty-one years, and I can honestly say that this world is not getting less evil. We are moving towards the judgment of God. We will see what that looks like on a small scale through the captivity of Israel, but we will experience it on a worldwide scale in the last days. It is obvious to anyone with a functioning brain that we are spiraling towards God’s wrath being poured out. Whoever sees good in this world without God is assuredly evil."}]},{"start":12,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"To the world, you are not worth much more than the change in your pockets. To the Lord, your heart and mind are valuable. He provides you with value by the way. Without Christ, you have nothing to place value in you. You are sitting in idleness without any use or functionality. That might seem cruel to you, but it’s the truth. Christ gives us all value when we place our trust in Him because He is valuable."},{"kind":"para","text":"Think of it this way. If we have a trashcan, we might think of it as a little thing. If it gets destroyed or lost, we probably won’t put up too much of a fit and just go buy another one. It’s just a trashcan. Now, what if I told you that I stashed gold in that trashcan? Suddenly, that trashcan becomes far more valuable. Not because the trashcan itself is made of gold, but only because it has something valuable stored within it."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is what we are without Christ. We are just a trashcan. With Christ, we are a trashcan filled with value. Better yet, we are made completely new, and our whole lives become useful tools of important value. That, in itself, is a good reason to trust Christ. The better reason to trust Him is because He has proven His love for you by dying for you! What a great and valuable gift!"}]},{"start":13,"end":13,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There will be great Earthquakes when God judges this Earth."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And great earthquakes shall be in divers places, and famines, and pestilences; and fearful sights and great signs shall there be from heaven.\" Luke 21:11 \"And there were voices, and thunders, and lightnings; and there was a great earthquake, such as was not since men were upon the earth, so mighty an earthquake, and so great.","ref":"Revelation 16:18"},{"kind":"para","text":"The Earth itself will fear and tremble at the wrath of God. No one alive will be left to stand in boldness and pride once God is done with it."}]},{"start":14,"end":14,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"They aren’t going to be able to run too far. God shows His power by shaking the Earth, and yet we somehow think we can run and hide from His wrath. That’s a silly thought."},{"kind":"para","text":"I know they will be blaspheming the Lord even while His judgment is obviously being poured out. It wouldn’t surprise me if they think they can somehow hide from His anger like a child hiding their mistakes."}]},{"start":15,"end":15,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Who will be found? Well all of everyone. There won't be a single person left alive that God cannot find. When God is through making all things new, there won't be a single drop of sin or wickedness left on this Earth. It will all be done away with and destroyed. That is a promise of the Lord."}]},{"start":16,"end":16,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"We are looking at this from the perspective of the Lord. We have had several conversations in the past about why this will be absolutely righteous and necessary. From Genesis to Deuteronomy, there are moments where we have discussed why God would allow this kind of killing to take place. Similarly, from Joshua to 2 Samuel, there are instances that illustrate this point. We will continue to see it throughout the books of the Kings, to Isaiah, Ezekiel, and through to Revelation."},{"kind":"para","text":"God cannot let evil reign. He cuts off the family lineages of the most disgusting and heinous people because they will only be evil forever. There will be no saving them. God CAN’T save them. It’s not that He won’t; He simply can’t because they won’t want Him to. He will only save those who are willing to accept His salvation."}]}]},{"start":17,"end":22,"title":"The Destruction of Babylon","entries":[{"start":17,"end":17,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"We have gained a clear understanding of the future destruction of Babylon, the symbolic Babylon. Now, we are witnessing the destruction of the current Babylon during the time of Isaiah. This is how it will unfold. God will stir up the “Medes” against them. The Medes won’t care about taking any provisions. They aren’t doing it to obtain any sort of material gain. They are doing it simply to destroy the Babylonians. They dislike the Babylonians and their prosperity, and God is setting up a people to ensure they are put in check as soon as deemed necessary."},{"kind":"para","text":"It will be a shock to the world that Babylon will be taken over, but it’s also a promise that God will keep. Isaiah is letting it be known right now that it WILL come to pass this way."}]},{"start":18,"end":18,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"These Medes people will not have mercy on anyone in Babylon. They will kill the children and women as they see necessary. They don’t care about their age; they just care about extinguishing this race. They seem to do quite a number on them, because the Babylonians are not a thing in our current generation. They aren’t even a thing at the first coming of the Lord. They are quickly forgotten about and gotten rid of for as large of a power as they were. They were so large, in fact, that we are still finding Babylonian artifacts today! That is quite a thing to behold!"}]},{"start":19,"end":19,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Sodom and Gomorrah were destroyed within a couple of minutes. They were much smaller cities in comparison to Babylon. Although they were prosperous, they were not nearly as well-to-do as Babylon. However, God will take care of them just as quickly. It won’t be much of an effort for the Lord to prove His judgment and power."},{"kind":"para","text":"There is physical and historical evidence of this taking place, yet we still have a whole world that rejects this all-powerful God. They can’t call this a fluke. Everyone agrees that Babylon was huge, even bigger than Egypt. Yet, they still deny the cold-hard evidence that some sort of all-powerful being completely demolished this prosperous city without much effort."},{"kind":"para","text":"They could write it off as the Medes being far more powerful than them, but they really weren’t. There was no reason the Medes should have destroyed them so easily. Yet, that’s what happened, and we can’t assume anything other than God allowed it to happen. That’s the only thing that makes any logical, historical, or scientific sense of all of this."}]},{"start":20,"end":20,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Babylon is still a pretty desolate place today. If you could even get there (it’s overrun by terrorist organizations for the most part), you would not find anything worth risking your life over. God does a number on this place, and it’s not really worth the time in exchange to visit today. There are some things there that are interesting, but not interesting enough to put your life on the line."}]},{"start":21,"end":22,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There are probably plenty of animals scouring that land today. I imagine that they are probably powerful and vicious, and another reason that it would not be worth your time going there. “Satyrs” means “he-goat.” Some claim a “demon-possessed goat.” Demons can possess animals, by the way."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And there was a good way off from them an herd of many swine feeding. So the devils besought him, saying, If thou cast us out, suffer us to go away into the herd of swine. And he said unto them, Go. And when they were come out, they went into the herd of swine: and, behold, the whole herd of swine ran violently down a steep place into the sea, and perished in the waters.","ref":"Matthew 8:30-32"},{"kind":"para","text":"It would be an interesting thing to behold, but another thing I would not want to see up close and in person. “Dragons” means “serpent or venomous snake.” Really, the thing to note here is the quickness of Babylon’s destruction and the obvious judgment placed on it. It’s just in ruins still today, and no one lives there. Actually, people avoid living there because they are afraid of what might happen if they do. They don’t take into consideration what God’s Word says about it and live in fear of a superstition rather than the fear of the Lord’s judgment."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is how it will be in the end times, though. It will be destroyed quickly. The pains won’t last forever. Supposedly, the Tribulation period will last for about seven years. That is not a very long time in the grand scheme of things, but it’s enough time, however, and it will feel like a lifetime for the people who have to face the judgment of the Lord."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":9},{"start":10,"end":10},{"start":11,"end":11},{"start":12,"end":12},{"start":13,"end":13},{"start":14,"end":14},{"start":15,"end":15},{"start":16,"end":16},{"start":17,"end":17},{"start":18,"end":18},{"start":19,"end":19},{"start":20,"end":20},{"start":21,"end":22}],"verses":{"1":"The burden of Babylon, which Isaiah the son of Amoz did see.","2":"Lift ye up a banner upon the high mountain, exalt the voice unto them, shake the hand, that they may go into the gates of the nobles.","3":"I have commanded my sanctified ones, I have also called my mighty ones for mine anger, even them that rejoice in my highness.","4":"The noise of a multitude in the mountains, like as of a great people; a tumultuous noise of the kingdoms of nations gathered together: the Lord of hosts mustereth the host of the battle.","5":"They come from a far country, from the end of heaven, even the Lord, and the weapons of his indignation, to destroy the whole land.","6":"Howl ye; for the day of the Lord is at hand; it shall come as a destruction from the Almighty.","7":"Therefore shall all hands be faint, and every man's heart shall melt:","8":"And they shall be afraid: pangs and sorrows shall take hold of them; they shall be in pain as a woman that travaileth: they shall be amazed one at another; their faces shall be as flames.","9":"Behold, the day of the Lord cometh, cruel both with wrath and fierce anger, to lay the land desolate: and he shall destroy the sinners thereof out of it.","10":"For the stars of heaven and the constellations thereof shall not give their light: the sun shall be darkened in his going forth, and the moon shall not cause her light to shine.","11":"And I will punish the world for their evil, and the wicked for their iniquity; and I will cause the arrogancy of the proud to cease, and will lay low the haughtiness of the terrible.","12":"I will make a man more precious than fine gold; even a man than the golden wedge of Ophir.","13":"Therefore I will shake the heavens, and the earth shall remove out of her place, in the wrath of the Lord of hosts, and in the day of his fierce anger.","14":"And it shall be as the chased roe, and as a sheep that no man taketh up: they shall every man turn to his own people, and flee every one into his own land.","15":"Every one that is found shall be thrust through; and every one that is joined unto them shall fall by the sword.","16":"Their children also shall be dashed to pieces before their eyes; their houses shall be spoiled, and their wives ravished.","17":"Behold, I will stir up the Medes against them, which shall not regard silver; and as for gold, they shall not delight in it.","18":"Their bows also shall dash the young men to pieces; and they shall have no pity on the fruit of the womb; their eyes shall not spare children.","19":"And Babylon, the glory of kingdoms, the beauty of the Chaldees' excellency, shall be as when God overthrew Sodom and Gomorrah.","20":"It shall never be inhabited, neither shall it be dwelt in from generation to generation: neither shall the Arabian pitch tent there; neither shall the shepherds make their fold there.","21":"But wild beasts of the desert shall lie there; and their houses shall be full of doleful creatures; and owls shall dwell there, and satyrs shall dance there.","22":"And the wild beasts of the islands shall cry in their desolate houses, and dragons in their pleasant palaces: and her time is near to come, and her days shall not be prolonged."}},
    "14": {"chapter":14,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: In our last chapter, Isaiah warns the children of Judah about the coming captivity in Babylon. He has been warning the northern tribes about the captivity of Assyria, but now he is tasked with warning the rest about Babylon. They probably thought they were fine and didn't need to worry about being captured. They were just as sinful and wayward as their northern brothers though, and it will become their downfall because they don't desire to check it and correct it. He does leave off with a great promise of returning however, but they will have to face some very difficult and dire circumstances before that comes to pass."},{"kind":"para","text":"In this chapter, Isaiah speaks about the renewel of Israel, and the promise of God's continued support for the nation. He will keep to His end of the deal, and bring His children back into this land renewing His covenant to them. He will continue to reach out to them, and draw them as best as possible, and they will continue to wrestle with God every step of the way."}],"previously":["In our last chapter, Isaiah warns the children of Judah about the coming captivity in Babylon. He has been warning the northern tribes about the captivity of Assyria, but now he is tasked with warning the rest about Babylon. They probably thought they were fine and didn’t need to worry about being captured. They were just as sinful and wayward as their northern brothers, though, and it will become their downfall because they don’t desire to check it and correct it. He does leave off with a great promise of returning, however, but they will have to face some very difficult and dire circumstances before that comes to pass. In this chapter, Isaiah speaks about the renewal of Israel and the promise of God’s continued support for the nation. He will keep to His end of the deal and bring His children back into this land, renewing His covenant to them. He will continue to reach out to them and draw them as best as possible, and they will continue to wrestle with God every step of the way."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":2,"title":"A House Renewal","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is a very interesting verse for a few reasons. There are a lot of Israel supporters in many church circles, and I have no quarrels with that. I support people, not nations. I think that is God’s ultimate agenda as well. He will gather His people, not His nation. He will have mercy on “Jacob” particularly, and He will “choose” Israel again. He is going to renew His promise with Israel in this land."},{"kind":"para","text":"The hang-up is with the last part of this, which says, “and the strangers shall be joined with them.” There are going to be people who were not originally a part of the promise who will have access to the promise. The land will be given back to them, and they will have strangers coming with them. You are a stranger to the promised land by the way. Yet God has accepted you in. Praise the Lord for that."},{"kind":"para","text":"God promises prosperity and renewal to the house of Jacob, and the strangers are going to need to cleave to it. There is a better promise coming."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But now hath he obtained a more excellent ministry, by how much also he is the mediator of a better covenant, which was established upon better promises.","ref":"Hebrews 8:6"}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Instead of the Israelites being captives to Babylon, the Babylonians will be captive to Israel. The Babylonians were not going to show mercy to the Israelites as their captives. Eventually, they do, but it took time for them to figure that out. We can read about that in Nehemiah. The Israelites, however, are to be masters of their captives in a Godly way. They were to show their captives grace rather than retaliation. Israel will mess it all up all over again though and be brought back into captivity."},{"kind":"para","text":"This prophecy (as I’ve mentioned before) will extend to something much bigger than just Israel. It will extend to the church, which will alleviate the whole world. All captives who trust in Jesus Christ will be set free."}]}]},{"start":3,"end":8,"title":"Singing Victories","entries":[{"start":3,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"They will be able to look at this and say, “Isaiah was right all along! I didn’t see it coming like this, but he was right! We can rejoice in the Lord now.” Isaiah gives them some words to say to help them glorify God for what He has done and how He has led them through. They will no longer be controlled by their bondage."},{"kind":"para","text":"They have gotten themselves into trials of bondage so many times at this point that you would think they would learn their lessons, but they don’t. That is the problem with modern Christianity, mind you. They are free from sin and free from the power of Satan, and yet they still keep themselves under the thumb of Satan. Of course, I don’t believe that they are not saved because they are not perfect Christians, but it does make me feel sorry for them because they have the power to reject that sin and they are not working to use it. It is a work, by the way. It is not as if you are suddenly a perfect Christian who has all things figured out the moment you get saved."},{"kind":"para","text":"God has “broken the staff of the wicked, and the sceptre of the rulers,” and that gives us freedom from bondage. It gives us a reason to rejoice and glorify the Lord for His love for us."}]},{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"“Hindereth” means “refrain” or “hold back.” In other words, there is no one that can stop it. The persecution of the wicked is something that the Lord will take care of. We are guaranteed that."},{"kind":"para","text":"We might look at our wicked leaders today and beg God to do something. We might say, “God, where are you? Why aren’t you helping us? Why aren’t you doing something about this?” God waits for a specific time for things. He waits until the “fullness” of something before He enacts."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But when the fulness of the time was come, God sent forth his Son, made of a woman, made under the law, To redeem them that were under the law, that we might receive the adoption of sons.\" Galatians 4:4-5 \"Till we all come in the unity of the faith, and of the knowledge of the Son of God, unto a perfect man, unto the measure of the stature of the fulness of Christ:\" Ephesians 4:13 \"For it pleased the Father that in him should all fulness dwell;","ref":"Colossians 1:19"},{"kind":"para","text":"There is a “fullness” that must take place before God is going to do something about it. He knows how long it is going to have to take, and He knows why it must take that length of time. But we also know that God will enact His fullness as well. When His wrath is poured down, it will be in fullness. It won’t be as if He is just going to suddenly stop in the middle of it and think, “Maybe they have had enough.” No, that will be full. He allowed the evil men their fullness, and He is going to enact His fullness when enough is enough. Only God can measure how much is enough."}]},{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Through thousands of generations there will be singing to the Lord. God will perform victories above measure, and they are times and purposes to sing. That should help us figure out a way to prepare our voices for it today so we are ready for when there is a need for rejoiceful singing."}]},{"start":8,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"If the trees are able to rejoice for the Lord, there is no reason for us not to sing to the Lord in rejoicing. Trees reach towards the Heavens, and we must be reaching for them as well. If God has given us a reason to sing, then we should take that chance to do it. You might think, “Well, right now, God has not given me much of a reason to sing.” Yes, He has. Are you alive? Yes? Then you should sing! Are you saved? Yes? Then you should sing! Do you love the Lord? Yes? Then you should sing! Are you grateful for His presence in your life? Yes? Then you should sing! I can go down a whole list of purposes to rejoice and sing to the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Israelites are going to sing their songs of rejoicing because the Lord has freed them from captivity. That is a great reason to sing! “Feller” means “cut.” They should have been cut down if I’m being honest. They should have been completely wiped out and gotten rid of because of their terrible acts against the Lord. But the Lord was not willing to break the promises made to them. He knew what was to come next. He knew that the Savior still had to rescue them. That is where the story of Israel is headed still, and God will do what it takes to make sure they are not completely cut down."}]}]},{"start":9,"end":11,"title":"The Same Outcome","entries":[{"start":9,"end":9,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There is no honor amongst the dead, only amongst the living. If you have abused your honor here, you will not have honor in the afterlife. The Babylonian king may be in Hell with the rest of the wicked kings, but they will not be rejoicing by any means."},{"kind":"para","text":"They will be in torment, continual thirst, and need. They might think they are living like kings in the afterlife, but they are not. They are kings, but they are treated like peasants (if not worse than). They may wear royal apparel in Hell, but they will have no power there."}]},{"start":10,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Oh, the defeat of not accepting Christ. Those who are not kings on this earth, or rulers of any sort, think of themselves as something special when they don’t have the Lord. They will be weaker than weak in eternity. They will see how small they are when they are with actual rulers in pain and suffering. I pray that is not the case. I pray that they come to the Lord before it’s too late. I pray that they would see that the theme of scripture is making giants fall. God deals with the giants, and the bigger we are (whether in stature or pride), the harder we will fall."}]},{"start":11,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Now the body in the grave doesn't really matter when you have an afterlife in Hell. It doesn't matter if you have an afterlife in Heaven either. The body will decay and the worms will cover you either way. \"Pomp\" means “majesty.\" They will not be very majestic in their graves. They will decay just like the rest of us."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"All go unto one place; all are of the dust, and all turn to dust again.","ref":"Ecclesiastes 3:20"},{"kind":"para","text":"All that time spent gaining high status here on Earth for what? To just rot in the grave and in eternity. You cannot take your status with you in death; you leave everything behind. The Lord, however, will provide you with new status. You will either be without Christ, which is the status of a sufferer, or you will be with Christ, which is the status of a brother."},{"kind":"para","text":"If you want to be brought high in eternity, you must be on your knees today for the temporary. If you are high-minded and standing today, you will be brought low for eternity. Isaiah has actually already made mention of this."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For the day of the LORD of hosts shall be upon every one that is proud and lofty, and upon every one that is lifted up; and he shall be brought low:","ref":"Isaiah 2:12"}]}]},{"start":12,"end":15,"title":"Lucifer's Fall","entries":[{"start":12,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Satan is a great representation of exactly what these wicked leaders will experience. It is Satan, after all, who brings these people into their positions of power by the way. God allows those positions, but Satan is the one pulling the strings. There’s an interesting connection made here to Lucifer. We read this and assume it is speaking about Satan. How do we get that assumption? Satan is not mentioned at all in these verses, so how do we know for sure that Lucifer means Satan? Well, that’s where context comes in handy."},{"kind":"para","text":"There is a plethora of information regarding angels falling from Heaven, but the name “Lucifer” specifically has a meaning. “Lucifer” means “Light-bringer.” That’s odd. That is certainly not the type of name I would associate with Satan. That is the name I would associate with Jesus!"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"We have also a more sure word of prophecy; whereunto ye do well that ye take heed, as unto a light that shineth in a dark place, until the day dawn, and the day star arise in your hearts:","ref":"2 Peter 1:19"},{"kind":"para","text":"It doesn’t seem fitting to call this “Lucifer” fellow Satan, but we are quite confident that it is not talking about Jesus. He did not “fall” from Heaven like a star. He was not “cut down to the ground.” He also (specifically) did not weaken the nations either. So we must make connections to other parts of scripture to see if this lines up with Satan’s characteristics."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And there was war in heaven: Michael and his angels fought against the dragon; and the dragon fought and his angels, And prevailed not; neither was their place found any more in heaven. And the great dragon was cast out, that old serpent, called the Devil, and Satan, which deceiveth the whole world: he was cast out into the earth, and his angels were cast out with him.\" Revelation 12:7-9 \"And he said unto them, I beheld Satan as lightning fall from heaven.\" Luke 10:18 \"And no marvel; for Satan himself is transformed into an angel of light.","ref":"2 Corinthians 11:14"},{"kind":"para","text":"Satan gives power to these kings and entices them into thinking that power on Earth means greater power for eternity if they just ignore the Hebrew God. They fall for it and become “weakened,” not strengthened. If they wanted strength, they would have been wise to follow the Lord and let go of their own power. That is what the great kings of Israel did. The good kings depended upon the Lord. The bad ones were not bad because they were not powerful; rather, the opposite was true. They were extremely powerful, abused that power, and went against the Lord. That is what made them bad."},{"kind":"para","text":"Satan had plenty of power, and he abused it and lost control of everything. So now he tries to get leaders to mimic him and pull as many as possible away from the power of the Lord. He cannot hurt God in any other way except to abuse the free will of people and get them to spend an eternity in pain away from the Lord. That certainly does break God’s heart. We have further clarity that this is Satan based on the next verses."}]},{"start":13,"end":14,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"He thought that he could somehow transcend God. He would be a god over God. He would try and make his own throne higher, and it didn't work. All it got him was cast out of eternal glory, and sent straight to Hell."}]},{"start":15,"end":15,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"He may not physically be living in Hell today, but Satan knows his future. He is living there in spirit until the day comes when he will be living there physically. That day has not come yet. It hasn’t come yet because God is waiting for a “full” time to be made. There is a fullness that needs to be met, and we haven’t reached it yet. Though our world seems to be quite full of wickedness today, I don’t see how we can become any more full than we already are. God sees that there is still room in the tank of wickedness, and He is waiting for that to be filled up. He is waiting for a specific course before He is going to throw Satan into Hell physically. He will be placed on the “sides of the pit,” which I believe means “the deepest depths” of it. I think there are levels of pain in Hell. I think there are certain people who are going to experience more pain than others. We can talk about that in a different setting (perhaps Revelation). Satan will have his part in the deepest and hottest part of Hell. He will feel the full brunt of pain in eternity for his relentless attacks on the innocent, the Christians, and his ability to sway people away from the Lord. I hope he feels that pain every moment he is in there."}]}]},{"start":16,"end":19,"title":"A Place of Prisoners","entries":[{"start":16,"end":17,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Both Satan and the king of Babylon will face this question. Satan abuses people, making them believe they are something special when they truly aren’t. He is able to deceive them because he himself believes he is something special. Satan has genuinely tricked himself. I know he is not stupid, but he certainly plays the role quite well. I suppose someone who doesn’t have Christ is oblivious to the obviousness of scripture, but you’d think that Satan, as an eternal being, would be much smarter than he actually is."},{"kind":"para","text":"Notice the amount of chaos and destruction that Satan has orchestrated in his time on Earth. We will be able to look at him behind the bars of eternity and say, “Is this it? This is all there is? He didn’t end up as anything more than an eternal prisoner.”"}]},{"start":18,"end":19,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Satan is not much to look at. It’s his pride and arrogance that make him seem so small. Prideful people may be loud, but it’s always the Lord that has the final say. Satan will not have a good time in the afterlife, and we will say, “Man, this guy has no power. He claimed such high status and he is brought lower than the poorest person on Earth.” We will not have pity on him, though. He will deserve his place of rest, and he knows it. He knows that he will only end up in one place, and he will not have control over much else. That is why he is trying to make as many problems as possible while he has the chance here on Earth."},{"kind":"para","text":"This is the same thought as the leader of Babylon who will take the Israelites captive. He will be looked at as nothing more than a prisoner by the time the Lord is through with him."}]}]},{"start":20,"end":21,"title":"Satan's Children","entries":[{"start":20,"end":21,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Satan’s children will not succeed. That is a promise you can be assured of. God will not allow Satan to have the final say. He will not permit sin to continue to flourish. He will not give the time of day to Satan’s offspring to somehow taint the Earth again. He will completely banish Satan and his people, and they will not have much power in the afterlife."},{"kind":"para","text":"They will feel completely powerless and will regret their decisions to turn away from God and follow the lusts of this life. That is what Satan will give you, by the way. He will give you the lusts of THIS life. You will not receive anything more after this life, though. Those are only given by God."}]}]},{"start":22,"end":23,"title":"A Desolate Place","entries":[{"start":22,"end":22,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Again, Babylon will be a prophecy for the end times as well. That is why we can relate it to the leadership of Satan. Isaiah already refers to him as “Lucifer.” He’s just a fallen star who thinks he has all the power when he doesn’t."},{"kind":"para","text":"Babylon will have a pretty high head when they take over Israel. They will think they are something special. But they aren’t. They will come to ruin eventually. It will take some time, but God will allow that time to come. Once it’s over, God will cut off their name. There is nothing left of Babylon today."}]},{"start":23,"end":23,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"“Bittern” means “porcupine.” Babylon will be nothing more than a place for the animals to live. It will belong to them. They will own that land."},{"kind":"para","text":"“Besom” means “broom.” The broom that God will use to bring Babylon into submission is the broom of “destruction.” He will completely destroy this place and the inhabitants there."},{"kind":"para","text":"These are all historically proven and factual things that Isaiah is saying here. You can see these proofs with your own eyes."}]}]},{"start":24,"end":27,"title":"God Will Work","entries":[{"start":24,"end":24,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God doesn’t think or purpose anything by accident. His thoughts are absolutes. Period. If He thinks it, it will happen. That is a crazy reality to us. If we think something, rarely is it acted upon. Usually, if it is, it is something that is sinful or faulty. We think of things, and we might act upon them just to see them go to nothing or develop into something else that doesn’t even really matter. When God thinks, it is completed right then and there, and it lasts forever."},{"kind":"para","text":"If God were like mortal man, we would have a very confused and difficult world to trek through. He would be thinking of things that don’t belong here. I like to joke with my family from time to time and tell them that I can read their thoughts. I’ll start off by saying, “Okay, I’m about to read your mind, okay?” They’ll say “Okay…” and I’ll say, “Just don’t think of a pink elephant.” Well, I have just planted a thought into their minds now. They were likely not already thinking of a pink elephant, but now that I’ve said it, that is what they are going to literally think about. You are likely thinking of a pink elephant right now because you just read it. I planted that thought in your mind."},{"kind":"para","text":"Imagine if God thought like that. We would see pink elephants everywhere. It would likely become normal to us, but it is not a normal thing to reality. God has some thoughts, obviously, that we are not sure about. Cherubims, and creatures with hundreds of wings and eyes, and faces that we aren’t sure how to even describe. He has some thoughts that are quite outlandish in the eyes of this world. Thankfully, He reserves those thoughts for Heaven, and it will be quite a scene to behold when we get there. Here, though, God thinks of things that belong here, and they are here. Period."}]},{"start":25,"end":25,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The Assyrians are a problem for North Israel at the moment (in case you don't remember). But God has purposed freedom for them as well. He has purposed this upon the whole Earth. How do I know that? Well He says it in the next verse!"}]},{"start":26,"end":26,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God’s hand is stretched out to release the captives and free them from their oppression. People talk about oppression all the time still. They think that our government is oppressive, or our leadership is oppressive, or a specific culture, or a specific gender, or a specific skin color is oppressive. No… SIN is oppressive. If you want to stop being oppressed, you must deal with the problem of sin. That is the only way to rid oppression in your life."},{"kind":"para","text":"It doesn’t matter what the rest of the world can do to you when the Lord has stretched out His hand upon you to free you. The only reason that people may live in spiritual oppression today is only because they have chosen it for themselves. They can live in freedom if they choose. I think people just want to complain is what it is. They probably know they can be free, but it’s so much easier to just complain about not being free rather than holding on to the freedom the Lord offers."}]},{"start":27,"end":27,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Great question! There are a lot of people who don’t believe in the Lord. They claim that God is not true and that the Bible is a lie. Whether they believe it or not, God is still going to do what He has promised to do."},{"kind":"para","text":"It must be tiring to live a life constantly battling the obvious nature and miracles of the Lord. It must be exhausting trying to excuse the proofs that God gives to this world. It would not be a life that is worth the time to live. I would feel defeated every day I wake up and see that people are still going, and God is still merciful."},{"kind":"para","text":"It would be a difficulty for me to live a life that is against a being I don’t believe in and see Him still continue to perform what He purposes. No one is going to stop God from moving, even if they choose not to believe in it."}]}]},{"start":28,"end":30,"title":"Warning to the Philistines","entries":[{"start":28,"end":28,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Isaiah is speaking about events occurring during the time of King Ahaz’s death. The “burden” refers to Palestina, which we will read about shortly. The “Palestina” are the same as the “Philistines.” “Palestina” means “Land of sojourners” and would refer to the west coast of Canaan or the entire country of Palestine. These people have fought against Israel for a long time and will have reason to rejoice about the death of one of their kings."}]},{"start":29,"end":29,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Israel had repeatedly put the Philistines in their place throughout scripture. They will think that the Israelites’ God is suddenly against them and will be happy to see them start to drown and suffer. They are looking to see Israel fall. The serpent’s root will be that of Satan. There will be a time when Satan will have the world’s power. He will be on the leadership throne, so to speak. The Philistines are under the impression that strength comes from political leadership. We fall for that same trap honestly. We think that whoever is in charge of our government is the one that will make the real change. We are then sorely disappointed to find out that it is not the case. We should not put our trust in a political leader. We should only trust the leadership of the Lord. His leadership is the only one we can trust. That is what God is reminding the Philistines about here."},{"kind":"para","text":"Israel will have a couple of good kings to follow Ahaz, and then the rest of the kings will be a complete downfall. When the Philistines see that, they will probably become high-minded about the destruction of Israel and think that they have one (even though they are not the ones that will have to do anything to get the victory here). They don’t care who takes the victory as long as the Israelites are gotten rid of and destroyed. That won’t last forever, though, and God will bring His people back to the land. Satan will have time to destroy, and they will be on the wrong side of the battle at that point."}]},{"start":30,"end":30,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Satan’s hold will bring people to the grave. They will be judged by the Lord, and they will not have a means of escape. Those that have nothing will reign as royalty, and those that are prospering will fall by the wayside of God’s wrath and judgment. The Philistines won’t be able to stand in those days."},{"kind":"para","text":"It’s funny that God is warning the enemy here. He is giving them (even) a chance to change their ways. They can take the warnings of God seriously and prosper with His children if they so choose. They don’t choose that though, and they will suffer the consequences because of it."}]}]},{"start":31,"end":32,"title":"Our Trust In God","entries":[{"start":31,"end":32,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The “poor” of God’s people will trust in God’s foundation! Christ is who we are to trust in. He is our Savior. I don’t need to see Christ save me spiritually. I don’t need physical healing. I need His spiritual presence, and then face to face in eternity. All I want to do is be present with the Lord! I cannot wait until I see Him personally. For now, though, I am so thankful that He has not left me alone in my faith. I walk with Him every day, and He has given me access to His presence by the Holy Spirit of promise!"},{"kind":"para","text":"I’m thankful that He still desires a relationship with me even though I disappoint Him every day. I am thankful that He has not given up on me even though I give Him plenty of reason to. Those that don’t know Him are lost and doomed already. They must turn to Him if they don’t want to be left in crying and wailing. Otherwise, smoke is in their future. Destruction and chaos are what’s coming. They will be left in nothing but complete ruin, feeling forsaken and completely distraught. What a terrible future they have set up for themselves."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":9},{"start":10,"end":10},{"start":11,"end":11},{"start":12,"end":12},{"start":13,"end":14},{"start":15,"end":15},{"start":16,"end":17},{"start":18,"end":19},{"start":20,"end":21},{"start":22,"end":22},{"start":23,"end":23},{"start":24,"end":24},{"start":25,"end":25},{"start":26,"end":26},{"start":27,"end":27},{"start":28,"end":28},{"start":29,"end":29},{"start":30,"end":30},{"start":31,"end":32}],"verses":{"1":"For the Lord will have mercy on Jacob, and will yet choose Israel, and set them in their own land: and the strangers shall be joined with them, and they shall cleave to the house of Jacob.","2":"And the people shall take them, and bring them to their place: and the house of Israel shall possess them in the land of the Lord for servants and handmaids: and they shall take them captives, whose captives they were; and they shall rule over their oppressors.","3":"And it shall come to pass in the day that the Lord shall give thee rest from thy sorrow, and from thy fear, and from the hard bondage wherein thou wast made to serve,","4":"That thou shalt take up this proverb against the king of Babylon, and say, How hath the oppressor ceased! the golden city ceased!","5":"The Lord hath broken the staff of the wicked, and the sceptre of the rulers.","6":"He who smote the people in wrath with a continual stroke, he that ruled the nations in anger, is persecuted, and none hindereth.","7":"The whole earth is at rest, and is quiet: they break forth into singing.","8":"Yea, the fir trees rejoice at thee, and the cedars of Lebanon, saying, Since thou art laid down, no feller is come up against us.","9":"Hell from beneath is moved for thee to meet thee at thy coming: it stirreth up the dead for thee, even all the chief ones of the earth; it hath raised up from their thrones all the kings of the nations.","10":"All they shall speak and say unto thee, Art thou also become weak as we? art thou become like unto us?","11":"Thy pomp is brought down to the grave, and the noise of thy viols: the worm is spread under thee, and the worms cover thee.","12":"How art thou fallen from heaven, O Lucifer, son of the morning! how art thou cut down to the ground, which didst weaken the nations!","13":"For thou hast said in thine heart, I will ascend into heaven, I will exalt my throne above the stars of God: I will sit also upon the mount of the congregation, in the sides of the north:","14":"I will ascend above the heights of the clouds; I will be like the most High.","15":"Yet thou shalt be brought down to hell, to the sides of the pit.","16":"They that see thee shall narrowly look upon thee, and consider thee, saying, Is this the man that made the earth to tremble, that did shake kingdoms;","17":"That made the world as a wilderness, and destroyed the cities thereof; that opened not the house of his prisoners?","18":"All the kings of the nations, even all of them, lie in glory, every one in his own house.","19":"But thou art cast out of thy grave like an abominable branch, and as the raiment of those that are slain, thrust through with a sword, that go down to the stones of the pit; as a carcase trodden under feet.","20":"Thou shalt not be joined with them in burial, because thou hast destroyed thy land, and slain thy people: the seed of evildoers shall never be renowned.","21":"Prepare slaughter for his children for the iniquity of their fathers; that they do not rise, nor possess the land, nor fill the face of the world with cities.","22":"For I will rise up against them, saith the Lord of hosts, and cut off from Babylon the name, and remnant, and son, and nephew, saith the Lord.","23":"I will also make it a possession for the bittern, and pools of water: and I will sweep it with the besom of destruction, saith the Lord of hosts.","24":"The Lord of hosts hath sworn, saying, Surely as I have thought, so shall it come to pass; and as I have purposed, so shall it stand:","25":"That I will break the Assyrian in my land, and upon my mountains tread him under foot: then shall his yoke depart from off them, and his burden depart from off their shoulders.","26":"This is the purpose that is purposed upon the whole earth: and this is the hand that is stretched out upon all the nations.","27":"For the Lord of hosts hath purposed, and who shall disannul it? and his hand is stretched out, and who shall turn it back?","28":"In the year that king Ahaz died was this burden.","29":"Rejoice not thou, whole Palestina, because the rod of him that smote thee is broken: for out of the serpent's root shall come forth a cockatrice, and his fruit shall be a fiery flying serpent.","30":"And the firstborn of the poor shall feed, and the needy shall lie down in safety: and I will kill thy root with famine, and he shall slay thy remnant.","31":"Howl, O gate; cry, O city; thou, whole Palestina, art dissolved: for there shall come from the north a smoke, and none shall be alone in his appointed times.","32":"What shall one then answer the messengers of the nation? That the Lord hath founded Zion, and the poor of his people shall trust in it."}},
    "15": {"chapter":15,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: In our last chapter, we got a bleak look at how Israel will be captured, but a strong encouragement about how it won't last forever. Satan will not win in the end even though it may seem he has the upperhand. Satan has never had the upperhand by the way. He might trick people into thinking that he does, but he is always kept on a short leash."},{"kind":"para","text":"In this chapter, we get the full account of what comes of the land of Moab. It is even worse than what takes place in the land of Israel. It is absolute chaos and cruelty in the highest degree, and it's likely because they are self-professed followers of God, without actually having a heart for God. We will see what the end is of a people who are just playing the part rather than being honest and truthful about their faith and lifestyle."}],"previously":["In our last chapter, we received a bleak look at how Israel will be captured, but also a strong encouragement about how it won’t last forever. Satan will not win in the end, even though it may seem he has the upper hand. Satan has never had the upper hand, by the way. He might trick people into thinking that he does, but he is always kept on a short leash. In this chapter, we get the full account of what comes of the land of Moab. It is even worse than what takes place in the land of Israel. It is absolute chaos and cruelty in the highest degree, and it’s likely because they are self-professed followers of God without actually having a heart for God. We will see what the end is of a people who are just playing the part rather than being honest and truthful about their faith and lifestyle."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":3,"title":"Moab's Desolation","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Moab is going to be in dire straits seemingly suddenly. That is what “in the night” is insinuating. Moab has been a bit of a mess throughout the history that we have studied them. The only good thing that seems to have come out of Moab is Ruth. If you don’t remember, Moab was a nation that was started by Lot and his daughter. I won’t go into much more detail than that, but it’s sufficient to say that Moab was not a part of God’s desire. What they did was distasteful, and these people lived distasteful lives ever since. Assyria will destroy these people almost entirely. They will show no mercy to them."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"“Bajith” means “House,” and “Dibon” means “Wasting.” These are “the high places,” where they performed their pagan practices, which will be destroyed as they should be. “Nebo” means “prophet,” and “Medeba” means “water of rest.” They have been very much away from honoring and pleasing the Lord. They may have known God, but they were not worshipping Him. It’s a lot like our modern churches today. We have many churches that claim to know the Lord, but they have practices that are not at all Godly, especially the leadership of the churches. They abuse their walks with God in all honesty. They say, “Well, as long as we get people to the Lord, that is all that matters. Even if we have to kill babies to do it, it should bring people to the Lord.” That is the wrong way of thinking. That is the thoughts of the Moabites. They were doing heinous things against the Lord, worshipping in pagan temples, and then proclaiming the God of Israel. It’s a very sad thing to proclaim Christ and reject every characteristic of Him. We may say we know Christ, and yet have no grace, compassion, or standards that we live by."},{"kind":"para","text":"Here’s what should be our mindset. If we want people to know Christ, and there must be a sacrifice made in order for them to come, we should be the sacrifice. We should not desire that anyone be killed to come to the Lord. We should desire that we would be killed for people to come to the Lord. It is not our job to sacrifice the lives of others out of “righteous desires.” We can only sacrifice ourselves for the hope of the gospel. That is what all the Apostles did. They never threw anyone else out there to be a sacrifice so they could lead people to Christ. They only ever sacrificed themselves (which is why they all became martyrs of the faith)."}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The misery they will face will make them completely undone and so burdened that they will just be crying and howling uncontrollably everywhere they are. They will be wearing “sackcloth” because they have nothing else to wear. They will be so undone and so pained that they will have no choice but to live as poor people. These people are rich, mind you. The Israelites are all rich too. They have been living the good life because of the providence of God, and so they were on a trajectory towards immense sin and displeasure for God."},{"kind":"para","text":"They lived high lives because God was giving them provision, but all it did was make them careless and callous to the obvious love and guidance of the Lord. The Moabites lose their truth. They lose their grace. They lose their prosperity and righteousness. They lose everything because they acknowledge God but don’t follow God."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Having a form of godliness, but denying the power thereof: from such turn away.","ref":"2 Timothy 3:5"},{"kind":"para","text":"That is the modern church, is it not? That is the biggest problem with modern-day Christianity. We don’t truly believe what we are reading in scripture. We don’t really trust what God’s Word is saying. We don’t trust that it was even translated correctly. We don’t trust that people actually know what they are talking about when they read it, study it, and teach it. We have a trust issue in the Lord and the preachers of God’s Word."},{"kind":"para","text":"It’s because we have a lot of Moabites preaching today. We have people who are not trustworthy trying to give the “Truth” of God’s Word and living in exact opposition to it. We should be living what we are preaching; otherwise, we shouldn’t be preaching it."}]}]},{"start":4,"end":6,"title":"Cries Heard All Around","entries":[{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"“Heshbon” means “Stronghold,” and the strongest among them are going to be in tears. “Elealeh” means “God is ascending,” and they are going to be crying because they had not paid attention to God’s power and ascension. That is their biggest problem. “Jahaz” means “Trodden down,” and ironically, that is exactly what they will be. I don’t know how far apart Heshbon and Jahaz are, but even if it’s a few miles, that is a lot of crying. Imagine your neighborhood (alone) all crying together. Now imagine three cities doing it in unison from the amount of pain they are feeling."},{"kind":"para","text":"It is likely they are feeling the most pain from the loss of loved ones more than anything else. They are likely to lose their children, and fathers and mothers are separated, and children have lost both parents. It would be a very depressing and terrible thing to experience in any land, whether they deserved it or not. It will be a difficult course for these people, but it’s also a course that they have chosen for themselves."}]},{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Isaiah expresses that his own heart is crying out for Moab because of the impending hardships they are about to face. It is important to remember that Moab did not have good ties with Israel. They were not like good friends and neighbors trying to support each other. In all honesty, Israel probably wouldn’t care about what happens to Moab. Yet, the pain of Moab will be so great that it will cause Israel to cry over it. “Zoar” means “insignificance,” and even the poor among them will be in tears. They will have nowhere else to go but into a state of nothingness. “Luhith” means “Tablets,” and “Horonaim” means “two caves.” Their cries will be heard from all around, and everyone will be distraught by their destruction."},{"kind":"para","text":"God still loves these people, but these people don’t seem to love God. That is the only reason that God is allowing this to take place. They have turned from God for far too long and have gotten away with riotous living and heinous actions for long enough. God must put a stop to it somewhere, otherwise (historically speaking) it just gets worse. Imagine, for a moment, if Hitler was still alive today. Imagine he continued his reign of terror for many more years to come. We would have a very different world; nearly all of the Jewish people would be wiped out of existence. God put a stop to it when the time was right. It should have gotten the attention of the Jewish people. It did to some Jewish people. It made them realize that God was judging them. It forced them to look for a Savior. There was a good portion that found the Savior, but there was not enough."},{"kind":"para","text":"Israel is a nation very far from the Lord today. The majority does not identify with Christ. Even after the sufferings that God has given to them, they still don’t seem to have a desire to look into the truths of God’s Word and Christ’s salvation. How much pain does God have to give you in order for you to finally just turn to Him and lean on Him? You won’t do it through times of ease, that’s for sure. We will not seek the Lord when things are going well; we only seek salvation when we are in need of it. When do we need salvation? Well, in times when our lives hang in the balance. That is far bigger of a reality than most of us know, I’m afraid."}]},{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"“Nimrim” means “limpid” or “pure.” In those days, these waters will no longer be pure. I assume these waters were a source of replenishment if they are mentioned here in this way. They were keeping their civilization alive, and they will just become useless when they are taken over."},{"kind":"para","text":"Their fields will dry up, and their produce will come to nothing. It will be obvious that God has done something to keep these people from increasing any further."}]}]},{"start":7,"end":9,"title":"Nobody Left","entries":[{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Everything that they have gotten and stored up will be taken and destroyed, or given away. Imagine all your possessions becoming someone else’s. Everything you worked so hard for. Honestly, that is what will happen to all of us when we die. Our possessions will be given to someone else who will likely squander what we have."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"One generation passeth away, and another generation cometh: but the earth abideth for ever. The sun also ariseth, and the sun goeth down, and hasteth to his place where he arose. The wind goeth toward the south, and turneth about unto the north; it whirleth about continually, and the wind returneth again according to his circuits. All the rivers run into the sea; yet the sea is not full; unto the place from whence the rivers come, thither they return again. All things are full of labour; man cannot utter it: the eye is not satisfied with seeing, nor the ear filled with hearing. The thing that hath been, it is that which shall be; and that which is done is that which shall be done: and there is no new thing under the sun. Is there any thing whereof it may be said, See, this is new? it hath been already of old time, which was before us. There is no remembrance of former things; neither shall there be any remembrance of things that are to come with those that shall come after.","ref":"Ecclesiastes 1:4-11"},{"kind":"para","text":"This is why our treasures should not be stored up here. They should not be our most prized possessions. Rather the Lord should be our prized possessions, and we should be storing up our gifts for eternity. That is where we are headed, and no one can break through and steal those treasures."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Lay not up for yourselves treasures upon earth, where moth and rust doth corrupt, and where thieves break through and steal: But lay up for yourselves treasures in heaven, where neither moth nor rust doth corrupt, and where thieves do not break through nor steal: For where your treasure is, there will your heart be also.","ref":"Matthew 6:19-21"}]},{"start":8,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"\"Eglaim\" means \"double reservoir.” \"Beerelim\" means \"well of God.” They had a lot going for them it seems. The crying doesn't seem to stop either. They are all in distress. What a painful thing to hear for miles around."}]},{"start":9,"end":9,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"\"Dimon\" means \"river bed.” Their destruction will be so severe that it will actually affect waters on the outskirts of the land. There will be bodies and death everywhere in the land, and they will be floating in the water, tainting their water supply. It says that \"lions\" will go after those that escape Moab. I don't know if it is speaking about literal lions or not in this section. I would assume so. They will not catch a break, and they will be completely destroyed because of their terrible lifestyles of sin. They have had plenty of time to turn and follow after the Lord wholeheartedly, but they never do, and time proves that they never will because they keep getting worse and worse."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":9}],"verses":{"1":"The burden of Moab. Because in the night Ar of Moab is laid waste, and brought to silence; because in the night Kir of Moab is laid waste, and brought to silence;","2":"He is gone up to Bajith, and to Dibon, the high places, to weep: Moab shall howl over Nebo, and over Medeba: on all their heads shall be baldness, and every beard cut off.","3":"In their streets they shall gird themselves with sackcloth: on the tops of their houses, and in their streets, every one shall howl, weeping abundantly.","4":"And Heshbon shall cry, and Elealeh: their voice shall be heard even unto Jahaz: therefore the armed soldiers of Moab shall cry out; his life shall be grievous unto him.","5":"My heart shall cry out for Moab; his fugitives shall flee unto Zoar, an heifer of three years old: for by the mounting up of Luhith with weeping shall they go it up; for in the way of Horonaim they shall raise up a cry of destruction.","6":"For the waters of Nimrim shall be desolate: for the hay is withered away, the grass faileth, there is no green thing.","7":"Therefore the abundance they have gotten, and that which they have laid up, shall they carry away to the brook of the willows.","8":"For the cry is gone round about the borders of Moab; the howling thereof unto Eglaim, and the howling thereof unto Beerelim.","9":"For the waters of Dimon shall be full of blood: for I will bring more upon Dimon, lions upon him that escapeth of Moab, and upon the remnant of the land."}},
    "16": {"chapter":16,"intro":[],"previously":["In our last chapter, we received a very bleak description of what happens to the land of Moab if they do not turn to the Lord. Actually, the way it is written, it seems that these things are finality. This IS what will happen to Moab. We will see that by the end of this chapter here. In this chapter, we get what COULD happen if Moab decides to turn to the Lord and repent of their wickedness. They could prosper and be protected. They could even become a safe place for those looking for a fresh start after the rest of the lands are captured by Assyria. Of course, this is not the path that Moab will take, and so the last chapter will become their reality."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":5,"title":"Mercy Is A Theme","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The lamb was used as a mercy sacrifice in the Old Testament. It was what Christ is referred to in the New Testament, both in John and Revelation. Christ is the lamb that was slayed for the mercy and salvation of the whole world."},{"kind":"para","text":"Moab needed mercy. They needed to turn and repent from their sins. They needed salvation from the Lord. We need a Lamb sent today. The Lord has already been sent for us, but our country needs to take that Lamb and trust it. They need the Lamb as their sacrifice. We are dying here without Him."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Moab is going to be taken from their land because they are not willing to turn to the Lord. We have already seen the kind of people the Moabites were. David comes from a Moabite line. We read in Ruth that the Moabites were not very Godly people; in fact, they rejected God. They did not want to live under the authority and control of the Lord. Yet, they (as well as the rest of the world) were offered salvation. They were offered a chance to escape the coming danger and judgment. Of course, they aren’t going to listen. Why would they? They think everything is well and fine in their sins, and they are sitting comfortably in that. That is a great picture of the world today."},{"kind":"para","text":"We are all being warned about what happens when the well of sin dries up, and we think that it never will. We think we have a whole lifetime to figure it out. It could be gone tomorrow for all we know. Most of us don’t believe that we will face judgment or God’s wrath. We don’t believe that there will be a day when God sends in other lands to take us over. It’s a very stark reality, but it’s a reality nonetheless, and we must face the trials of it. I pray that the Lord keeps His genuine children safe. I pray that if there is anyone left here when that day comes, the Lord sees fit to protect His own. I know He will, actually. I’ve seen Him do that over and over again throughout scripture. Why would He stop now?"}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This could be a place of safe haven if they got things in proper order. It is interesting because the rivers of Arnon are not much to stop the Assyrians. Imagine if Moab turned. Imagine if they took counsel from the Lord and pursued His righteousness. That small river Arnon would have kept the Assyrians out. It would have given a place for the genuine children of God. Moab would have been a place that the Lord could turn and use. The Assyrians would be destined to fail against them. We would be reading a very different account in the coming pages if they had just taken counsel."}]},{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Moab was the outcast, and they could be known for harboring the Lord’s outcasts. They could be known for the Lord’s prosperity and reviving the nation. They could be known as the land that turned around. They just had to get rid of the troublemakers and overturn the ruling of the wicked. They just had to turn their sins away and listen to the directives of the Lord. They just had to follow God. That is all we need to do to see a revival in our country today."},{"kind":"para","text":"If we had a people that was so undone and in despair enough to turn from their wicked ways and trust in the Lord alone, we would see this country turn to prosperity in a heartbeat. Moab didn’t believe it though. May we learn a thing or two from Moab."}]},{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Mercy is a theme in scripture. It might be good to underline it if that is your thing. We might recognize that God is constantly looking to provide mercy to His people. He has made every means possible to give wayward and untoward people mercy."},{"kind":"para","text":"People think that God is evil. They say, “If God is so good, why is there so much evil in the world?” Then we see God completely destroy Sodom and Gomorrah, or flood the whole Earth (because of how disgustingly evil humans are), or take over the land of Canaan, and we say, “How dare God do something like that, it’s disgusting!”"},{"kind":"para","text":"Well, which one do you want? Do you want God to do something about the evil, or do you want to complain because He DID do something about it? Through it all, God rids the world of what is genuinely and truly evil, and He does it in a way that PROVES His mercy. His mercy will always be one of the options on the table, by the way. The only reason we may not obtain mercy today would only be because WE have personally rejected it."}]}]},{"start":6,"end":8,"title":"The Pride of Moab","entries":[{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Pride is the killer of a nation. Our nation is falling apart today because we have too many prideful people, both in leadership and under. We think we are something special, when we really are not. We think we can take control of the situation, when we have proven time and time again that we just bring things to ruin. Moab will learn that lesson the hard way."}]},{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I think it would be a good thing for people to see America crumble a bit (if I could be honest). We need people to cry over this country again. We really have no idea how good we actually have it today."}]},{"start":8,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"“…the lords of the heathen…” could have a two-fold meaning. “Heathen” means “nation” or “people.” They are a people who worship false things. Some have tricked themselves into thinking they can have a dual citizenship—one of this world and one of the next. This could either mean their “kings (or rulers)” were responsible for giving them their downfall, or it could mean their “idols” are responsible. Either way, we will be led by what we follow."},{"kind":"para","text":"Some follow after idols (money, fame, comfort, familiarity, traditions, practices, works, etc.), while others follow after authority (politics, priests, popes, pastors, reverends, bishops, bosses, etc.). We should ONLY be following after the Lord. If we are going to be following another person, may it only be because they are a proven man of God. Otherwise, sidestep that person or idol, and pursue the Lord alone."}]}]},{"start":9,"end":12,"title":"The Tears of God","entries":[{"start":9,"end":9,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Imagine the Lord crying over a nation. Imagine how much we break the heart of the Lord. Our God cries."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Jesus wept.","ref":"John 11:35"},{"kind":"para","text":"He cries for the men, women, and children who suffer from their sins. He cries because He wants them to love Him back, and they don’t. He loves us immensely, so much so that He is broken to see us suffer from our rejection of Him. He cries because He loves you. If He didn’t love you, He would not be concerned about your future wellbeing. He would not warn you about what is to come."},{"kind":"para","text":"The soulwinner today is a calloused man. They preach with zeal, but not with heart. They are not actually concerned about you turning to the Lord; they just want the numbers. They will not be seen physically crying for your soul. Why? Well, it’s because they don’t actually love you. We should love people enough to cry for them."},{"kind":"para","text":"It breaks my heart to know that there are hundreds of thousands of people every day that I walk by whom are going to spend an eternity in Hell and torment because they have rejected the Lord. I know I will not be the only one that reaches them, but I might be the last one before eternity. What a painful thought…"}]},{"start":10,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Wine is a symbol of wealth, and it was in those days, and it still is today. I have worked on many rich people’s homes, and almost all of them have a wine cellar. They have a place to keep their wine from drying out, overheating, or molding over. They have wine that is worth more than my car."},{"kind":"para","text":"There are a lot of wine tasting and wine-making places here in California. We are pretty well known for our wine. If this state (and country) continues the downward momentum that we are going, we will come to a stop of producing wine. That will be a pretty fair sign that we are doomed for captivity."}]},{"start":11,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God’s crying is a joyful noise. A harp is a sad instrument, but it’s also a soothing one. It brings comfort. In the sense of the Lord, it brings the realization that God cares. He cares what happens to the nations. He cares about directing His people to victory and freedom. He will use even the worst nations, like Moab, to bring forth a victory if they are willing."}]},{"start":12,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"They will have had their chance and squandered it. Once it’s all too late, that is when they will come before the Lord for help, but there’s nothing the Lord can do at that point. They can take a hold of salvation now, or they can live away from the Lord and rely on themselves. God has a time frame for salvation. It will only be open to people as long as He has not returned. But the day is coming. We don’t know when, or what needs to happen before then, but we get a glimpse of things that are supposed to come, and the time is very ripe for the Lord’s return. Today is the day of salvation."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"(For he saith, I have heard thee in a time accepted, and in the day of salvation have I succoured thee: behold, now is the accepted time; behold, now is the day of salvation.)","ref":"2 Corinthians 6:2"},{"kind":"para","text":"Why? Well, because the offer is present for you now. It might not be tomorrow. The Lord may return tomorrow and that access will be closed off."}]}]},{"start":13,"end":14,"title":"The Fate of Moab","entries":[{"start":13,"end":14,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God gave them a choice. Now He says, \"In three years, their destruction will come. They have already made up their mind to reject me.” There will be a remnant, but there won't be much there. It will only be destruction and chaos for them because they have chosen their fate…"}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":9},{"start":10,"end":10},{"start":11,"end":11},{"start":12,"end":12},{"start":13,"end":14}],"verses":{"1":"Send ye the lamb to the ruler of the land from Sela to the wilderness, unto the mount of the daughter of Zion.","2":"For it shall be, that, as a wandering bird cast out of the nest, so the daughters of Moab shall be at the fords of Arnon.","3":"Take counsel, execute judgment; make thy shadow as the night in the midst of the noonday; hide the outcasts; bewray not him that wandereth.","4":"Let mine outcasts dwell with thee, Moab; be thou a covert to them from the face of the spoiler: for the extortioner is at an end, the spoiler ceaseth, the oppressors are consumed out of the land.","5":"And in mercy shall the throne be established: and he shall sit upon it in truth in the tabernacle of David, judging, and seeking judgment, and hasting righteousness.","6":"We have heard of the pride of Moab; he is very proud: even of his haughtiness, and his pride, and his wrath: but his lies shall not be so.","7":"Therefore shall Moab howl for Moab, every one shall howl: for the foundations of Kirhareseth shall ye mourn; surely they are stricken.","8":"For the fields of Heshbon languish, and the vine of Sibmah: the lords of the heathen have broken down the principal plants thereof, they are come even unto Jazer, they wandered through the wilderness: her branches are stretched out, they are gone over the sea.","9":"Therefore I will bewail with the weeping of Jazer the vine of Sibmah: I will water thee with my tears, O Heshbon, and Elealeh: for the shouting for thy summer fruits and for thy harvest is fallen.","10":"And gladness is taken away, and joy out of the plentiful field; and in the vineyards there shall be no singing, neither shall there be shouting: the treaders shall tread out no wine in their presses; I have made their vintage shouting to cease.","11":"Wherefore my bowels shall sound like an harp for Moab, and mine inward parts for Kirharesh.","12":"And it shall come to pass, when it is seen that Moab is weary on the high place, that he shall come to his sanctuary to pray; but he shall not prevail.","13":"This is the word that the Lord hath spoken concerning Moab since that time.","14":"But now the Lord hath spoken, saying, Within three years, as the years of an hireling, and the glory of Moab shall be contemned, with all that great multitude; and the remnant shall be very small and feeble."}},
    "17": {"chapter":17,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: In our last chapter, Isaiah spoke about what could happen if the nation of Moab turned to the Lord and how they could prosper from their repentance of their evil and wicked lifestyle. They could be a nation of safety for other nations as well. By the end of the chapter though, we realize that they are not ever going to do that."},{"kind":"para","text":"In this chapter, we change topics from Moab to Syria and Ephraim. Ephraim is God's country. Syria is anti-God. Ephraim should not be making friends with them, and we will see that God is not happy about their decision to do so. So the Lord is going to provide proof that this is a bad idea."}],"previously":["In our last chapter, Isaiah spoke about what could happen if the nation of Moab turned to the Lord and how they could prosper from their repentance of their evil and wicked lifestyle. They could be a nation of safety for other nations as well. By the end of the chapter, though, we realize that they are not ever going to do that. In this chapter, we change topics from Moab to Syria and Ephraim. Ephraim is God’s country, while Syria is anti-God. Ephraim should not be making friends with them, and we will see that God is not happy about their decision to do so. So the Lord is going to provide proof that this is a bad idea."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":3,"title":"The Burden of Syria","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Damascus will be the reference to “Syria.” It was (and still is) the main city of Syria. So when we read that name, we can lump them together with Syria. They are joined with Ephraim (who we will read about in a moment) to go against Judah and its inhabitants. This was a betrayal, and the Lord will not allow this to stand. That is why they are going to face a “burden.”"},{"kind":"para","text":"Just like we had read about in Moab and other leading nations, Syria and Ephraim will have their time in God’s judgment, and it won’t be pretty. Damascus (specifically) will become an ash heap. It did. They built it back up several times over. I do believe it will be destroyed again in the future as well. Neither here nor there."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There will be nothing there but animals to find a place to rest. The whole place will be destroyed."}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"“Ephraim” has been mentioned hundreds of times before in scripture. Obviously, Ephraim was a name of a man in Genesis. In this context, it will be referenced as the ten cities of Israel that will be overtaken soon. They are confederate with Syria, and so the sins of Syria are joined with the sins of Ephraim, and they will both be in the midst of God’s burden to the nations. Ephraim should not have made friends with the enemy. They should not have been enticed by these wicked rulers. They were not living correctly before the Lord (neither nation), and so they were prospering in worldly pleasures but falling apart in Godly lifestyles."},{"kind":"para","text":"We have already spoken about some of the things they were likely doing (to women, children, and slaves), and so I don’t think it’s necessary to go into more detail about it. I will say, though, that they probably learned most of this from countries like Syria, who have been very prominent in these false acts of worship for centuries. They still have some terrible acts of worship today."}]}]},{"start":4,"end":6,"title":"The Glory of Jacob","entries":[{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The glory of “Jacob” specifically refers to the worldly name of Israel. It is the name they bore before becoming followers of God. Jacob is the man who holds onto the heel of something, and at this time, they are holding onto the heels of Syria. Syria represents their power, protection, and lord. When Syria falls, Israel will fall with them."},{"kind":"para","text":"Jacob’s glory is a worldly one, characterized by plenty of animals and finances. However, this glory will be robbed from them due to their rejection of the Lord. This is the path they have chosen. They opted for worldly provision, and thus they will receive a worldly reward. Worldly rewards are always painful and never sufficient."}]},{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"In other words, “There will be nothing left.” It will be completely unharvestable and uninhabitable. They will be completely lacking in all the goodness of God. They think the goodness of sin is sufficient for them, but they will learn quickly that they won’t be led very far with it."},{"kind":"para","text":"They will be led into pain and hunger. They will be led into weakness and cowardice. They will have nothing to show for all of their own efforts, and they will regret ever trusting in man to begin with. All of their strength and energy will be given to the enemy. That is not a fun thought."}]},{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There won’t be much left there except a small remnant. Again, this draws us forward to the tribulation era. We will see that a small remnant always seems to remain of God’s children. God needs this to be the case because He wants people to turn to Him more than anything else. He wants to give mercy, not pain. He wants to give prosperity, not destruction. Yet, our sinful nature forces the hand of the Lord to provide us with the worst kinds of punishments."},{"kind":"para","text":"May we learn to fight against our sinful nature. We must fight against our flesh. We must fight against what we want and pursue after what the Lord wants. Search His heart, not our own. Mold ourselves to Him. We cannot do that, though, unless we take the Word of God seriously and trust in His salvation."}]}]},{"start":7,"end":9,"title":"At That Day","entries":[{"start":7,"end":9,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"In that day, they will finally see how far away they have gotten from the Lord. They will finally realize how disgusting they have let their lives become. They will notice that they had been wrong all along and need to turn back to the Lord before they are completely wiped out and taken over. They will be little, but they will come back. They will turn back to the Lord, and the Lord will grant them access back to His presence."},{"kind":"para","text":"“At that day…” What day? It’s the day when they have lost everything. Sometimes that is the only way we will finally realize what we have—only once everything has been taken away."}]}]},{"start":10,"end":11,"title":"Replant","entries":[{"start":10,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"All that work for little to no reward. They will put in the effort because they knew that the Lord will provide the increase. Somewhere along the line, however, they forget that it’s the Lord that grows it. And so, they put in the work to prepare the growth, and forget the Lord, and God will get their attention when the time of harvest comes. They will see that they had been negligent of the Lord, and they will have nothing to show for it."},{"kind":"para","text":"What can you do? Well, you can pull the crops and replant. That is the only way for it to work. That is what the Lord will do with Ephraim. He will pull out the bad crops (the wicked people), and replant (the repentant people). They will grow again, but they won’t be the ones in control of the growth this time. It will be a different nation. They have already started the process of giving themselves over, and they will be taken from the land by the Assyrians, and then placed back there by the Lord. It will be the Romans that come into the vineyard to harvest the growth of the Lord. The Romans will benefit from the replanted crops (so-to-speak). It will be the Lord (Jesus Christ) that shows them how to grow."}]}]},{"start":12,"end":14,"title":"Rushing of Nations","entries":[{"start":12,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I don’t know if you’ve ever been to the beach, but the waters while you are there can be extremely loud. When the tide rolls in and the waves crash down, it is not a quiet thing. It’s usually soothing in my opinion."},{"kind":"para","text":"But this noise of the multitude of people will not be a soothing thing. They will all be crying to the Lord. They will be in utter despair because of the path they chose. They will eventually realize the mistake they had made…"}]},{"start":13,"end":13,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord will provide protection, and they will continue on. They have continued on even still today. They are currently facing battle against a couple of nations now, but they are a well-known location still today. The battle is not pretty. It’s all made from a bout of pride, honestly. They are seeking after land. I don’t know how the Lord will work out that battle. I don’t know the future goals the Lord has for Israel. It is honestly not for me to say. I know the Lord has plans for them though, and over and over again throughout history, God gives protection. I think He is still protecting today. He is still protecting many nations. The nations that are not given over to wickedness (fully) are those that God is chastising and bringing to Him. I truly believe that. In fact, I SEE that. The more chastisement that many of us receive (however), the more we try and fight against it. “Woe to the multitude of many people…” Woe to them for turning away from the Lord. Woe to them because God is going to do something about it."}]},{"start":14,"end":14,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"It will all look bleak, but the Lord will deal with it in His own way. They will be captured, and there should be no doubt about it. There will be a small remnant, and we can read ahead to see how they end up. It is not as if the rest of the story has not already been written for us. We can see that the Lord was absolutely right in the promises and actualities made here."},{"kind":"para","text":"These people will face their destruction and their burden with Damascus. They will be afflicted just like their allies. But the Lord is not done with them yet. We may not have much confidence in the Lord today, but those who know God know that He will not let evil just slip by. We know that God will do something about every war and every battle. He will deal with the wicked in battle and with the righteous."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":9},{"start":10,"end":11},{"start":12,"end":12},{"start":13,"end":13},{"start":14,"end":14}],"verses":{"1":"The burden of Damascus. Behold, Damascus is taken away from being a city, and it shall be a ruinous heap.","2":"The cities of Aroer are forsaken: they shall be for flocks, which shall lie down, and none shall make them afraid.","3":"The fortress also shall cease from Ephraim, and the kingdom from Damascus, and the remnant of Syria: they shall be as the glory of the children of Israel, saith the Lord of hosts.","4":"And in that day it shall come to pass, that the glory of Jacob shall be made thin, and the fatness of his flesh shall wax lean.","5":"And it shall be as when the harvestman gathereth the corn, and reapeth the ears with his arm; and it shall be as he that gathereth ears in the valley of Rephaim.","6":"Yet gleaning grapes shall be left in it, as the shaking of an olive tree, two or three berries in the top of the uppermost bough, four or five in the outmost fruitful branches thereof, saith the Lord God of Israel.","7":"At that day shall a man look to his Maker, and his eyes shall have respect to the Holy One of Israel.","8":"And he shall not look to the altars, the work of his hands, neither shall respect that which his fingers have made, either the groves, or the images.","9":"In that day shall his strong cities be as a forsaken bough, and an uppermost branch, which they left because of the children of Israel: and there shall be desolation.","10":"Because thou hast forgotten the God of thy salvation, and hast not been mindful of the rock of thy strength, therefore shalt thou plant pleasant plants, and shalt set it with strange slips:","11":"In the day shalt thou make thy plant to grow, and in the morning shalt thou make thy seed to flourish: but the harvest shall be a heap in the day of grief and of desperate sorrow.","12":"Woe to the multitude of many people, which make a noise like the noise of the seas; and to the rushing of nations, that make a rushing like the rushing of mighty waters!","13":"The nations shall rush like the rushing of many waters: but God shall rebuke them, and they shall flee far off, and shall be chased as the chaff of the mountains before the wind, and like a rolling thing before the whirlwind.","14":"And behold at eveningtide trouble; and before the morning he is not. This is the portion of them that spoil us, and the lot of them that rob us."}},
    "18": {"chapter":18,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: In our last chapter, Isaiah spoke about the burden of Syria, the glory of Jacob, the coming day of \"The Holy One of Israel, the necessity to replant His people back into the land, and the chaos that is going to pursue because of their unbelief and disobedience to the Lord. Thankfully, God doesn't just leave His children in wanting. He is paying attention to His children and (not only so) paying attention to the nations and enemies of His children. He is going to move people, and places where they need to be moved for an ultimate purpose of proving His glory and strength to the world (even though the world will (and still do) largely reject it)."},{"kind":"para","text":"In this chapter, we get a look at this land of Ethiopia. It seems as if this is a bit off topic, but there is a lot of behind the scenes things taking place with Israel (specifically Judah) and the war they are facing against Assyria. These nations are going to be changed for the rest of time because of things they are about to face from the Lord in the coming chapters, and through the crazy captivity that Judah is going to face. May we not forget that it is Assyria who will eventually take Judah captive afterall. God will not let Ethiopia intervene, and there is a purpose for that."}],"previously":["In our last chapter, Isaiah spoke about the burden of Syria, the glory of Jacob, the coming day of “The Holy One of Israel,” the necessity to replant His people back into the land, and the chaos that is going to pursue because of their unbelief and disobedience to the Lord. Thankfully, God doesn’t just leave His children in wanting. He is paying attention to His children and, not only so, paying attention to the nations and enemies of His children. He is going to move people and places where they need to be moved for an ultimate purpose of proving His glory and strength to the world, even though the world will (and still does) largely reject it. In this chapter, we get a look at this land of Ethiopia. It seems as if this is a bit off topic, but there is a lot of behind-the-scenes activity taking place with Israel (specifically Judah) and the war they are facing against Assyria. These nations are going to be changed for the rest of time because of things they are about to face from the Lord in the coming chapters, and through the crazy captivity that Judah is going to face. May we not forget that it is Assyria who will eventually take Judah captive after all. God will not let Ethiopia intervene, and there is a purpose for that."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":3,"title":"Ethiopia's Power","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"It’s never a good thing when scripture brings up “woes.” To us reading today, a woe doesn’t mean much. If I had a stranger come to me (or even a well-known preacher) and he said, “Woe to you for being so proud,” I probably wouldn’t care all that much, honestly. But when a prophet says it, that is a serious problem."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! for ye shut up the kingdom of heaven against men: for ye neither go in yourselves, neither suffer ye them that are entering to go in. Woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! for ye devour widows' houses, and for a pretence make long prayer: therefore ye shall receive the greater damnation. Woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! for ye compass sea and land to make one proselyte, and when he is made, ye make him twofold more the child of hell than yourselves. Woe unto you, ye blind guides, which say, Whosoever shall swear by the temple, it is nothing; but whosoever shall swear by the gold of the temple, he is a debtor! Ye fools and blind: for whether is greater, the gold, or the temple that sanctifieth the gold? And, Whosoever shall swear by the altar, it is nothing; but whosoever sweareth by the gift that is upon it, he is guilty. Ye fools and blind: for whether is greater, the gift, or the altar that sanctifieth the gift? Whoso therefore shall swear by the altar, sweareth by it, and by all things thereon. And whoso shall swear by the temple, sweareth by it, and by him that dwelleth therein. And he that shall swear by heaven, sweareth by the throne of God, and by him that sitteth thereon. Woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! for ye pay tithe of mint and anise and cummin, and have omitted the weightier matters of the law, judgment, mercy, and faith: these ought ye to have done, and not to leave the other undone. Ye blind guides, which strain at a gnat, and swallow a camel. Woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! for ye make clean the outside of the cup and of the platter, but within they are full of extortion and excess. Thou blind Pharisee, cleanse first that which is within the cup and platter, that the outside of them may be clean also. Woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! for ye are like unto whited sepulchres, which indeed appear beautiful outward, but are within full of dead men's bones, and of all uncleanness. Even so ye also outwardly appear righteous unto men, but within ye are full of hypocrisy and iniquity. Woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! because ye build the tombs of the prophets, and garnish the sepulchres of the righteous, And say, If we had been in the days of our fathers, we would not have been partakers with them in the blood of the prophets. Wherefore ye be witnesses unto yourselves, that ye are the children of them which killed the prophets.\" Matthew 23:13-31 \"And I beheld, and heard an angel flying through the midst of heaven, saying with a loud voice, Woe, woe, woe, to the inhabiters of the earth by reason of the other voices of the trumpet of the three angels, which are yet to sound!","ref":"Revelation 8:13"},{"kind":"para","text":"Prophets hold a special kind of weight behind their woes because they are deep and serious. Some people might claim themselves as prophets today, but it would be imperative that we don’t accept their acclamations. They are not prophets. They may “profit,” but they cannot “prophet.” (If I said this in a sermon, people would be quite confused.) Prophets today are nothing more than “fortune tellers.” They don’t know anything about the future of God. The only thing that can be considered true from a prophet today is what Revelation says about the end of days."},{"kind":"para","text":"Isaiah was a prophet when Israel needed prophets. He is giving God’s Word here as a promise and as a warning. The nation of Israel will not heed that warning (as we will see come to pass). The woes are warnings as well, but they are mostly promises. The people will continue the way they always have, and the woes will be applied to their accounts in this life. Isaiah is addressing Ethiopia specifically. Ethiopia, during this time, was the head honcho. It was the place that ruled the other places. In fact, it was a rival to Assyria and a ruler over Egypt. Remember, Judah is at war with most of this land, and it’s not looking very pretty for any of the territories surrounding this war. It’s assumed that there were talks from Judah about allying with Ethiopia. If Assyria was against Judah, and Assyria was against Ethiopia, then Ethiopia and Judah would be wise to confederate with one another."},{"kind":"para","text":"The “shadowing with wings” term used here could mean a slew of things. I have read that this land is still filled with birds today, so it could be referencing this. One commentator says it is referencing the many insects that are found there. Never been there myself, but I’ll stick with the birds assumption."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"“Bulrushes” means “reed” or “papyrus,” and it’s a ship carrying paper. I don’t know what places they are sending these messages to, but I don’t see how it’s important to the context of their might. I suppose it’s because they have the power and ability to run whole teams just to send a message to far-away lands."},{"kind":"para","text":"Usually, back then, if you had a message, you would relate it to one city, and that city would deliver it to the next, and so on until it reaches the city it needs to get to. It’s a dangerous game of telephone. A nation might say, “Give them the message we will attack at dawn,” and then it goes through the chain leading to the nation they are going to attack saying, “They will be back at your lawn.” Obviously, the messengers giving the message have to be trusted."},{"kind":"para","text":"In this nation, Ethiopia, they had the power to personally deliver messages no matter how far away they might be. They controlled all the travels and power. They could easily cut off whomever they liked (or disliked rather)."}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Some sort of symbol is coming from Ethiopia. What that symbol is, I don’t know. Most scholars and commentators claim that it will be the Ark of God. There are people who have claimed that the ark was carried there by the Israelites during the captivity, but I couldn’t tell you how true that is. All I can do is take their word for it."},{"kind":"para","text":"It doesn’t really matter because there is no power in that ark anymore. We have the power of the Lord through Jesus Christ to claim as our own, and we don’t need the Ark of God for worship. We just need the Holy Spirit of the Lord to satisfy us."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Then verily the first covenant had also ordinances of divine service, and a worldly sanctuary. For there was a tabernacle made; the first, wherein was the candlestick, and the table, and the shewbread; which is called the sanctuary. And after the second veil, the tabernacle which is called the Holiest of all; Which had the golden censer, and the ark of the covenant overlaid round about with gold, wherein was the golden pot that had manna, and Aaron's rod that budded, and the tables of the covenant; And over it the cherubims of glory shadowing the mercyseat; of which we cannot now speak particularly. Now when these things were thus ordained, the priests went always into the first tabernacle, accomplishing the service of God. But into the second went the high priest alone once every year, not without blood, which he offered for himself, and for the errors of the people: The Holy Ghost this signifying, that the way into the holiest of all was not yet made manifest, while as the first tabernacle was yet standing: Which was a figure for the time then present, in which were offered both gifts and sacrifices, that could not make him that did the service perfect, as pertaining to the conscience; Which stood only in meats and drinks, and divers washings, and carnal ordinances, imposed on them until the time of reformation. But Christ being come an high priest of good things to come, by a greater and more perfect tabernacle, not made with hands, that is to say, not of this building; Neither by the blood of goats and calves, but by his own blood he entered in once into the holy place, having obtained eternal redemption for us.\" Hebrews 9:1-12 \"Jesus saith unto him, I am the way, the truth, and the life: no man cometh unto the Father, but by me.","ref":"John 14:6"}]}]},{"start":4,"end":7,"title":"Pruning Hearts","entries":[{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God is saying, through Isaiah, that He won’t allow the alliance between Judah and Ethiopia. He is able to deal with the enemy Himself without the help of human hands. In all honesty, the Lord can deal with anything (I think we understand that well), but there are certain things He chooses NOT to deal with Himself. Why? Well, it’s because He wants our trust and faith in Him to do it. Many times we don’t have faith, and that keeps God from working in your life. Or perhaps we have faith, and He still doesn’t take care of the problem. Perhaps your faith is being tested."},{"kind":"para","text":"The best way to know how genuine your faith is is to see where you are at when God doesn’t seem to show up. That’s a difficult sentence for me to write, but it’s true. I don’t like the feeling of floating in nothing, waiting for the Lord to answer prayers. I don’t like the thought of being alone without the help of the Lord as if I am left to my own devices. I think the Lord does it on purpose to see what I will do. Will I continue to have faith and wait patiently on Him, or will I eventually come to my wits’ end and take it into my own hands? Sadly, I fail the test more often than I succeed at it…"},{"kind":"para","text":"Israel will fail this test too, and the Lord is still going to work on their behalf. He even says He is going to help them, but they will eventually reject the Lord anyway, and all that help and prosperity will get them nowhere but into the hands of pride and self-pity."}]},{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Pruning to the enemy means that they are going to be afflicted. Truthfully, it means the same thing for the child of God too. God prunes everyone. We all feel the sharpness of His pruning. The difference between those that are His own and those that aren’t is not the amount of pain we will feel when being pruned. Rather, the difference is the purpose of the pruning."},{"kind":"para","text":"God prunes the enemy to inflict pain and bring them low. God prunes His children to humble them and build them up. He prunes and peels back our calloused hearts, our calloused thoughts, and works and widdles away at our calloused conscience until there’s nothing left but raw, open, and sensitive flesh for Him to work with. That is a painful thing for us to experience, but it’s a needful thing because it means growth and it means wisdom. I pray for more wisdom. He gives it to me, but only through pruning."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord is going to wait until the Assyrians are ripe for the pruning, and He is going to go in and cut them down."}]},{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"In the end, they will be nothing more than bird food. They will be left as desolate and useless. Assyria is still present today. It’s still quite an interesting nation. Obviously, the Lord has not completely destroyed all of it, but He has converted them. It is said that the majority of Assyria (today) is Christian. Syria is still mostly Islamic, but Assyria has turned over. The pruning seems to have led them to the Lord over time."}]},{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"It seems that the Ethiopians will turn to the Lord in time as well. Supposedly, as of this writing, 67.3% of the people in Ethiopia claim Christianity as their identity. The others consider themselves Protestant or Roman Catholic. How genuine their Christian stance is today, I don’t know. Seeing as the majority believe that the Ark of the Covenant is in their possession, they follow many Old Testament laws. They don’t seem to understand the complete faith that Jesus brings to them. Perhaps they will over time, but it seems they will be some of those present when Jesus comes to reign on Earth during the end times. God is doing a work on Ethiopia. It seems He has been doing a work for quite some time, as it’s written right here in Isaiah. Perhaps that is something that Christians should be paying close attention to and pushing for greater outreach there."},{"kind":"para","text":"However, we cannot miss the huge dilemma that Judah is going to face. God says, through Isaiah, that He is going to take care of Assyria, the enemy of Judah, without the help of Ethiopia. Yet, we find that Assyria takes Judah captive. How is that God helping them? By what means is living in captivity a blessing from the Lord? It’s not. It’s a “woe,” remember? It’s a woe to the nation of Israel, and it’s a woe to the nation of Ethiopia, and it’s a woe to the nation of Assyria. Everything about this is a woe. It’s a time of trouble. There is nothing good about what is going to come out of this, and there is no one to blame for these problems but themselves. God could easily intervene, but He won’t. He won’t because they have rejected Him for so long. He won’t because their leadership has led them into captivity. He has kept them safe for so long, and He has no choice but to let them learn their lessons. He has no choice, at this point, than to give them what they so desire. They desired a lifestyle of captivity. Honestly, they were already living in the lifestyle of captivity. They were captive to their sins. Now they will live in captivity to Assyria’s sins, and they will see what it’s like to live that life away from the blessing and closeness to God that they should have been paying attention to for so many generations."},{"kind":"para","text":"But it will lead them back. It will lead them back to the Lord, and the generations that follow will have to learn from the father’s mistakes. Or at least you would hope…"}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":7}],"verses":{"1":"Woe to the land shadowing with wings, which is beyond the rivers of Ethiopia:","2":"That sendeth ambassadors by the sea, even in vessels of bulrushes upon the waters, saying, Go, ye swift messengers, to a nation scattered and peeled, to a people terrible from their beginning hitherto; a nation meted out and trodden down, whose land the rivers have spoiled!","3":"All ye inhabitants of the world, and dwellers on the earth, see ye, when he lifteth up an ensign on the mountains; and when he bloweth a trumpet, hear ye.","4":"For so the Lord said unto me, I will take my rest, and I will consider in my dwelling place like a clear heat upon herbs, and like a cloud of dew in the heat of harvest.","5":"For afore the harvest, when the bud is perfect, and the sour grape is ripening in the flower, he shall both cut off the sprigs with pruning hooks, and take away and cut down the branches.","6":"They shall be left together unto the fowls of the mountains, and to the beasts of the earth: and the fowls shall summer upon them, and all the beasts of the earth shall winter upon them.","7":"In that time shall the present be brought unto the Lord of hosts of a people scattered and peeled, and from a people terrible from their beginning hitherto; a nation meted out and trodden under foot, whose land the rivers have spoiled, to the place of the name of the Lord of hosts, the mount Zion."}},
    "19": {"chapter":19,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: In our last chapter, we continued to get the terrible and final look at some of these cities who are connected to Israel. We looked at Ethiopia, and how the Lord is going to prune the hearts of the people there to get them where they need to be. There is a purpose for everything, even for the judgement of God. It's not a fun purpose, but it's ultimately for the good of humanity, and the hopeful salvation of the lost and evil in this world. God wants to turn the hearts of this world around."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is what this chapter focuses on. It focuses on God's goals for the people of Egypt and in turn for the people of the world. All of this is leading to God's ultimate conclusion of unity and singleness through His salvation acceptance. God is going to unify His children with those that have been shunned by His children. People from Assyria and Egypt will be included in the promise of salvation just as much as the Israelites (even if the Israelites don't like the idea)."}],"previously":["In our last chapter, we continued to get a terrible and final look at some of these cities connected to Israel. We examined Ethiopia and how the Lord is going to prune the hearts of the people there to get them where they need to be. There is a purpose for everything, even for God’s judgment. It’s not a fun purpose, but it’s ultimately for the good of humanity and the hopeful salvation of the lost and evil in this world. God wants to turn the hearts of this world around. That is what this chapter focuses on. It focuses on God’s goals for the people of Egypt and, in turn, for the people of the world. All of this is leading to God’s ultimate conclusion of unity and singleness through His salvation acceptance. God is going to unify His children with those that have been shunned by His children. People from Assyria and Egypt will be included in the promise of salvation just as much as the Israelites (even if the Israelites don’t like the idea)."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":4,"title":"Judgement For Egypt","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"You might be noticing, at this point hopefully, that the nations discussed in the last few chapters are not nations of Israel. They are the nations surrounding Israel, and it seems they are going to undergo a time of judgment as well. When God’s children are not where they are supposed to be for the Lord, you can be assured that everyone around them is going to feel it. There will be shockwaves felt by people around you, like a ripple effect. They won’t suffer for your sins, but they will certainly feel the impact from them. That’s key to remember when you fall victim to sin. There are many good-hearted, Godly people who fall into sin all the time. Something to keep you on track and in repentance is your love for those around you. Your sin, no matter how secret or small it may seem, will have an effect on those you love. Your children will feel it, your spouse will feel it, your neighbors will feel it, your family and friends will feel it, and people you are next to will feel it. That’s just the way it happens."},{"kind":"para","text":"Think of it like being arrested. There have been several times when we have been driving down the street and we see a cop pull someone over and put them in handcuffs. The people driving by likely don’t know the person being arrested, but they are all involved with it now because they can see it. They are affected by some random person’s arrest (even if it is small to you, or nonessential). You saw it, and now you are affected by it. The Israelites are going to be judged hard by the Lord, and the ripple effects of that are going to be felt by all the surrounding countries. This includes Egypt. It’s kind of a shock to me that they weren’t mentioned sooner. We knew their name had to be on this list at some point. Egypt is ripe for judgment as well. They have been on a downward spiral since the beginning of scripture. We don’t find many kind things written about Egypt, and it’s the oldest written country we get in scripture. The Lord is going to visit them, and even their idols (which are fake, by the way) are going to move to His presence. That, honestly, is likely the main reason that the Lord is going to visit with them. They are idolatrous people. They have been for generations. They need to be corrected. The Lord seems to wait a long time. Egypt is going to be put to the test, to say the least."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There will be a civil war in Egypt. Apparently, this comes to pass, and it was the people of Egypt against the authorities of Egypt. It was a civil war against their own government. This conflict will cause great divisions in the country that are still noticeable today. I would assume that Egypt, as a whole, was very unified for a very long time under the control of one Pharaoh. However, something gets out of hand at some point, causing the people to rebel and succeed in their rebellion. This, assuredly, will cause Egypt to crumble as the world’s power."},{"kind":"para","text":"Throughout the Old Testament, we see Egypt as the hub of power. We don’t look at Egypt that way today. It seems this is when they started to fall off. The power that comes next will be Assyria, but that won’t last forever."}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"They are going to grasp at anything they possibly can when the Lord comes to visit them. They will not like the presence of the Lord in their country. It will only bring chaos and torment to them because they are literally fighting against the Lord. They don’t know God. They could have had the Lord for so long. I believe they did at one point."},{"kind":"para","text":"We look at when Joseph was in charge of Pharaoh’s home, and we can pinpoint the Lord’s presence. Pharaoh even says some surprising things about the God of Joseph. Obviously, the Lord has visited them quite a bit through scripture, but they continuously (like all the other nations) reject Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"Now that His own children are rejecting Him, He is going to visit His children, which will result in judgment and trials for everyone around them as well. God needed His children in this position first before He took care of the rest of the nations."}]},{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Tyranny is often seen as God’s way of judging a nation, a concept that has been observed throughout history. As a nation drifts further away from the Lord, it accumulates more evil through cruel leadership, not merely incompetent leadership. Such leaders commit heinous acts against their own people that should never occur. The Egyptians, for instance, are destined to live in poverty and face even worse trials than the Israelites are currently enduring. It is important to remember that the Israelites are experiencing sad and dismal circumstances during the time Isaiah is writing. This is vividly depicted in 2 Kings, where a woman laments that her neighbor refuses to let her eat her baby. The situation is quite dire. However, the Egyptians will also face a challenging era due to their failure to turn to the Lord. Israel’s current predicament is a result of their idol worship, and other nations will be similarly judged for their idolatry."}]}]},{"start":5,"end":10,"title":"Becoming Meaningless","entries":[{"start":5,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I do believe, based on scripture alone, that the Nile and the rivers of Egypt were flourishing for a good portion of history. They were places of rich wealth and soil. However, when God’s judgment came, those places became barren and empty. Even if you visit the Nile today, you will see that they don’t grow vegetation well along those areas. It’s still quite dead compared to the rivers and places we can see anywhere else today. You’d think it would be a lot more lively now, but the judgment of the Lord proves itself for all of eternity. That is why you want to make your calling and election sure today."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Wherefore the rather, brethren, give diligence to make your calling and election sure: for if ye do these things, ye shall never fall:","ref":"2 Peter 1:10"},{"kind":"para","text":"Eternity is a long time to be wrong about God's judgement, and if we are on the wrong side of His judgement that is an eternal error."}]},{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Once again, you will not find any paper reeds along the Nile. God’s promise is sure here when He says they will “be no more.” We should notice, as well, that God is warning the Egyptians about this. When He says this, He is saying it as a warning and as a promise. It’s a warning not because they will listen and turn to the Lord before it comes. It’s a warning because He knows that they won’t take it seriously. They cannot say, “Oh, God is not gracious, look at all the evil that has befallen us.” No. That is what a good majority of our world tries to say today, but they are sorely mistaken."},{"kind":"para","text":"God has given us thousands of warnings through His Word and through generations of writing His Word, and we are too gullible to listen to them. We cannot curse God for not being loveable to our sin. We cannot accuse God of not being graceful after giving us plenty of time and plenty of warning about the consequences of our sin. He has given us a way out, and we have chosen to reject it and ignore it and then turn our fingers against God, assuming that it was He who caused us to be such evil people. No. We have done that to ourselves against the Lord’s grace and mercy."},{"kind":"para","text":"Egypt has the opportunity to turn to the Lord still. They can take the warnings and believe them and turn to Him. But they won’t. So the prophecy being written about here will come to pass, and it’s still evident today. It will be something the whole world faces as well because we will eventually all turn away from God."}]},{"start":8,"end":10,"blocks":[]}]},{"start":11,"end":15,"title":"Terrible Leadership","entries":[{"start":11,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I think it’s important to notice the people around the leaders. To bring it to a grand scale, if we looked at our president today, we might see a brutish man. He might seem ignorant and arrogant. He might actually be ignorant and arrogant. But who are the people he has put around himself for counsel? That is who you need to pay attention to. Those people are going to direct the president’s mind."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is the same problem that Egypt is going to face. That’s the problem that the kings of Israel faced. That’s the same problem that our church leadership today faces. Leaders of all shapes and sizes make poor decisions about who they are closest to, to receive counsel from."}]},{"start":12,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Leaders want to hear good things about their own decisions. They don’t want to hear what they are doing wrong or what they can change. Leaders shun correction so they can accept fulfillment. In the end, they are robbing themselves of substance. They are robbing themselves of genuine ministry. They are robbing themselves of the love of God in all honesty."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"The way of a fool is right in his own eyes: but he that hearkeneth unto counsel is wise.","ref":"Proverbs 12:15"},{"kind":"para","text":"The counsel a leader should be receiving is counsel of correction. Leaders need people around them who are willing to say, “I don’t think that’s a good idea. I think we should slow down and think through this differently.” Sadly, leaders often take the counsel of people who simply say yes to them and nothing more. That’s not counsel at all."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Where no counsel is, the people fall: but in the multitude of counsellors there is safety.\" Proverbs 11:14 \"Without counsel purposes are disappointed: but in the multitude of counsellors they are established.","ref":"Proverbs 15:22"},{"kind":"para","text":"They want to take counsel from their own ambitions and desires and forget about the rest of the people’s hurts and wants. They want to try and fulfill their own joys with their own needs, their own callings, and not pour into the needs and callings of those around them. That’s too much work for a leader to do."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"He that trusteth in his own heart is a fool: but whoso walketh wisely, he shall be delivered.","ref":"Proverbs 28:26"},{"kind":"para","text":"Bad leaders seek to direct people. Good leaders seek to be directed."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"The fear of the LORD is the beginning of knowledge: but fools despise wisdom and instruction.","ref":"Proverbs 1:7"},{"kind":"para","text":"Instruction and correction walk hand in hand, and if we are not going to be swayed by the obvious truth of instruction, we are going to fail our leadership, and our people."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Take fast hold of instruction; let her not go: keep her; for she is thy life.","ref":"Proverbs 4:13"},{"kind":"para","text":"Do I need to say anymore? While we are looking at the hurts and pains of Egypt, it is a direct reflection of every single one of us as well. We are all in danger of rejecting counsel and prioritizing our own wants over the Lord’s wants. Egypt will be a picture of that. We should take note and learn from their mistakes, not continue to follow their downfall."}]},{"start":13,"end":13,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Leaders will become foolish if they have foolish people giving them counsel. Do not (and I cannot stress this enough), I repeat, Do NOT surround yourself with yes people. Surround yourself with wise people. People who will think on the Lord. People who will say, “Okay, but what does that have to do with Christ?” People who will be honest and who are not afraid to question your motives and integrity. Otherwise, you will only be making decisions for yourself, and there is no wisdom."},{"kind":"para","text":"Surrounding yourself with “yes” people only leads you into seduction, not into instruction. Look to some of Egypt’s best Pharaohs for proof of that. Look to your own church leadership for proof of that. Look into your political leadership for proof of that. Look into your work leadership for proof of that."}]},{"start":14,"end":15,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Again, we don’t see many things come out of Egypt anymore. Egypt still has a rich heritage and culture, but it’s not the power of this world today. It wasn’t the power of the world during the time of Christ either. The power at that time was Rome."},{"kind":"para","text":"We can get into all the power changes in a different setting, but it’s obvious that God did a work in the land of Egypt and changed the course of history for that land, which is evident still in our day."}]}]},{"start":16,"end":17,"title":"Egypt's Weakness","entries":[{"start":16,"end":16,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Obviously, this can be taken in a three-fold way. We have spoken about how prophecy works in threes. In this case, it’s speaking about the future of Egypt, but Egypt is also (and has always been) a picture of the world. So the whole world will be shaken, and the whole world will live in fear."},{"kind":"para","text":"Why “like unto women?” Well, I don’t know. Women were looked at as fragile and innocent in those days. They were looked at as people who needed to be taken care of by a man. Honestly, they should still be looked at as this today, but they aren’t. They don’t want to be looked at like that. But women still shake today. It’s just the facts. They are still the weaker vessel whether they want to agree with that or not. It’s just biology. That’s not just opinion."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Likewise, ye husbands, dwell with them according to knowledge, giving honour unto the wife, as unto the weaker vessel, and as being heirs together of the grace of life; that your prayers be not hindered.","ref":"1 Peter 3:7"},{"kind":"para","text":"When a leader’s world is shaken, they feel like a weaker vessel. Whether they are a man or a woman, it doesn’t matter. They will feel insignificant and unable."},{"kind":"para","text":"If a leader feels the shaking of the Lord today, they are likely doing something wrong. They should not be living in fear in their leadership."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For God hath not given us the spirit of fear; but of power, and of love, and of a sound mind.","ref":"2 Timothy 1:7"},{"kind":"para","text":"That is how Egypt will look at that time, and it will be how the whole world will look in front of the Lord."}]},{"start":17,"end":17,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is an interesting verse. God is pointing Judah out specifically, not all of Israel, just the land of Judah. It was a small land, in no comparison to Egypt. The Christian, in the end times, will look like the least in the world, especially going up against the world, but the Lord has promised victory. Judah will have victory over Egypt. They will be a powerful country against Egypt. Egypt will not stand a chance. Even today, I don’t see how they would win against Egypt. But that’s the promise of the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"This verse also proves that God is not done with Israel today. This has not been fulfilled. Unless there is a piece of history that has been missing that I don’t know about where Judah has conquered Egypt or has become a “terror” to Egypt, I assume the Lord is going to keep this promise still in the future. I suppose it could be argued that the Lord will relieve Judah from the reign of Egypt, which is evident mostly today, but they have not become a “terror” to them."},{"kind":"para","text":"It could also be argued that the Lord is speaking about the confederacy of Judah and Egypt here. He is saying that it’s not going to bring prosperity to them. Being allies with Judah is going to bring terror to them rather than victory. Egypt is just going to become collateral damage. So the terror will not be FROM Judah, it will be BECAUSE of Judah. The fact is, Egypt is going to experience God’s judgment, whatever way you want to see fit."}]}]},{"start":18,"end":18,"title":"The Turn of Egypt","entries":[{"start":18,"end":18,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Yet again, a prophecy that still has not come to pass. We are waiting for this one still, and that will happen in the end. I have no doubt there will be a city in Egypt (literally) called the city of Destruction. And there will be five cities speaking the language of Canaan."},{"kind":"para","text":"It sounds as though Egypt will just accept their judgment from the Lord at that time. They will know what they deserve, and they will give honor to God’s decision on the matter. I assume it will be after a very long time of suffering and anguish."}]}]},{"start":19,"end":22,"title":"Turning To The Lord","entries":[{"start":19,"end":20,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The Savior has come. Egypt can be saved as well as anyone else in this world. They must turn to the Lord. I assume they will not be doing this until the final days, but it’s good to know they will finally call out to God in anticipation of His rescue. Sometimes that is where the Lord needs to lead His people in order for them to take Him seriously."}]},{"start":21,"end":22,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God afflicts His children."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For whom the Lord loveth he chasteneth, and scourgeth every son whom he receiveth.","ref":"Hebrews 12:6"},{"kind":"para","text":"He does it so He can correct us. That is the point of affliction by the Lord. He wants us to turn to Him in trust and repentance. He wants us to understand our errors and desire Him more than our sin. Sometimes we are so blinded by the fun of our sin that we don’t see how much it is hurting the Lord. So, in order for us to see, He allows affliction. He allows chastisement. He allows us to go through a season of pain and hurt so we understand how important it is to turn to the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"The world is going to face this, and they will miss it for a very long time until they have no choice but to turn to Him. Only a small portion will take Him, though. This is why I believe the rapture takes place before the great tribulation, by the way. I believe the “five cities” spoken about here is displaying a very small remnant of people in the world who will turn to the Lord during that time. They will finally see what they have been fighting so long against."}]}]},{"start":23,"end":23,"title":"The Road to Salvation","entries":[{"start":23,"end":23,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Again, there is a much deeper spiritual connection here. There will be an open connection for the outcast to come to the Lord, and they will have a road that leads them straight there. Jesus Christ is that road, by the way. He is THE way to salvation."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Jesus saith unto him, I am the way, the truth, and the life: no man cometh unto the Father, but by me.","ref":"John 14:6"},{"kind":"para","text":"It's a service road. They will be loving their neighbors and serving the Lord (as it's supposed to be)."}]}]},{"start":24,"end":25,"title":"His People, His Work, His Inheritance","entries":[{"start":24,"end":25,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"What an ending. It’s a hopeful ending. All of these other chapters (so far) have seen nothing but pain and destruction. They have seen torment and agony with no ease on the horizon. The Lord is setting up specific things for an ultimate purpose of bringing Him glory. He is proving His sovereignty over everything."},{"kind":"para","text":"Egypt is the world. Assyria is God’s Work. Israel is God’s inheritance. It’s a sign of how man comes to God. We are in the world, we are a part of the world, and then the Lord gets a hold of us and starts a work. That work takes a toll. It takes a while, and sometimes it can take our whole lives. But He works on us every day until the day of our death. That is the inheritance of the Lord. He inherits our souls."},{"kind":"para","text":"If we are willing to accept His Work, we get to be the Lord’s inheritance quickly, and the work will be easier. But if we reject it, we will not be inherited, and we will see the destruction of all the other lands who are fighting against the Lord."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":10},{"start":11,"end":11},{"start":12,"end":12},{"start":13,"end":13},{"start":14,"end":15},{"start":16,"end":16},{"start":17,"end":17},{"start":18,"end":18},{"start":19,"end":20},{"start":21,"end":22},{"start":23,"end":23},{"start":24,"end":25}],"verses":{"1":"The burden of Egypt. Behold, the Lord rideth upon a swift cloud, and shall come into Egypt: and the idols of Egypt shall be moved at his presence, and the heart of Egypt shall melt in the midst of it.","2":"And I will set the Egyptians against the Egyptians: and they shall fight every one against his brother, and every one against his neighbour; city against city, and kingdom against kingdom.","3":"And the spirit of Egypt shall fail in the midst thereof; and I will destroy the counsel thereof: and they shall seek to the idols, and to the charmers, and to them that have familiar spirits, and to the wizards.","4":"And the Egyptians will I give over into the hand of a cruel lord; and a fierce king shall rule over them, saith the Lord, the Lord of hosts.","5":"And the waters shall fail from the sea, and the river shall be wasted and dried up.","6":"And they shall turn the rivers far away; and the brooks of defence shall be emptied and dried up: the reeds and flags shall wither.","7":"The paper reeds by the brooks, by the mouth of the brooks, and every thing sown by the brooks, shall wither, be driven away, and be no more.","8":"The fishers also shall mourn, and all they that cast angle into the brooks shall lament, and they that spread nets upon the waters shall languish.","9":"Moreover they that work in fine flax, and they that weave networks, shall be confounded.","10":"And they shall be broken in the purposes thereof, all that make sluices and ponds for fish. I don’t know if you’ve ever gone fishing before, but when you leave to go fishing, you usually want to prepare yourself with the necessities: a rod, a reel, a net, hooks, bait, a bag (or cooler), a license, a knife, and so on. If you take your time to go fishing in the right area, at the right time, with the right hook and bait, you will likely catch quite a lot of fish. That’s good food. But there is nothing worse than spending all the time getting ready, driving to your nearest fishing spot, setting out the line and hook, waiting for hours to try and catch something, leaving just before dusk, and coming home with nothing to show for it. That is miserable and frustrating. It’s a wasted effort, and it’s usually not fun when you have nothing to bring home with you. That is what Egypt will look like. Everything they do and take their time in doing, everything they would prosper in before and would earn a wage from, will be useless and will not work. It’s like the fish have disappeared, and they no longer have the ability to perform the art they once could before. Those people who could easily make a nice net or worked with flax and made useful tools will suddenly forget how to do it. That would be miserable as well. I used to love writing music. I could express myself greatly by writing a song. I haven’t done it in years. I have lost that talent, and I wish I could do it again. It took a lot of time for me to stop playing before I forgot how to do it. These people will lose their craft seemingly overnight. They will just completely forget how they are supposed to work. They will become people who have no joy or fulfillment in the things they loved so much. That’s another pretty evident sign of God’s judgment. Joy will be lost if the Lord is judging people.","11":"Surely the princes of Zoan are fools, the counsel of the wise counsellors of Pharaoh is become brutish: how say ye unto Pharaoh, I am the son of the wise, the son of ancient kings?","12":"Where are they? where are thy wise men? and let them tell thee now, and let them know what the Lord of hosts hath purposed upon Egypt.","13":"The princes of Zoan are become fools, the princes of Noph are deceived; they have also seduced Egypt, even they that are the stay of the tribes thereof.","14":"The Lord hath mingled a perverse spirit in the midst thereof: and they have caused Egypt to err in every work thereof, as a drunken man staggereth in his vomit.","15":"Neither shall there be any work for Egypt, which the head or tail, branch or rush, may do.","16":"In that day shall Egypt be like unto women: and it shall be afraid and fear because of the shaking of the hand of the Lord of hosts, which he shaketh over it.","17":"And the land of Judah shall be a terror unto Egypt, every one that maketh mention thereof shall be afraid in himself, because of the counsel of the Lord of hosts, which he hath determined against it.","18":"In that day shall five cities in the land of Egypt speak the language of Canaan, and swear to the Lord of hosts; one shall be called, The city of destruction.","19":"In that day shall there be an altar to the Lord in the midst of the land of Egypt, and a pillar at the border thereof to the Lord.","20":"And it shall be for a sign and for a witness unto the Lord of hosts in the land of Egypt: for they shall cry unto the Lord because of the oppressors, and he shall send them a saviour, and a great one, and he shall deliver them.","21":"And the Lord shall be known to Egypt, and the Egyptians shall know the Lord in that day, and shall do sacrifice and oblation; yea, they shall vow a vow unto the Lord, and perform it.","22":"And the Lord shall smite Egypt: he shall smite and heal it: and they shall return even to the Lord, and he shall be intreated of them, and shall heal them.","23":"In that day shall there be a highway out of Egypt to Assyria, and the Assyrian shall come into Egypt, and the Egyptian into Assyria, and the Egyptians shall serve with the Assyrians.","24":"In that day shall Israel be the third with Egypt and with Assyria, even a blessing in the midst of the land:","25":"Whom the Lord of hosts shall bless, saying, Blessed be Egypt my people, and Assyria the work of my hands, and Israel mine inheritance."}},
    "20": {"chapter":20,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"### Previously: In the past few chapters, we have been studying about the fall of the nations bordering around Israel. Isaiah has done a pretty good job at showcasing how easy it will be to take these places down because the Lord is going to be the one that causes the affliction to take place to begin with. When the Lord is your enemy, you will not be standing for very long. It's wise for nations to not make God their enemy, and even wiser for Israel (the chosen nation) to obey and turn to the Lord. They won't however and it will cause destruction of their country as well."},{"kind":"para","text":"In this chapter, we get a short and simple look at how vulnerable the nations are without the Lord. If it's possible for Assyria to rule these nations, why would it not be possible for them to take over the whole world and keep going?"}],"previously":["In the past few chapters, we have been studying the fall of the nations bordering Israel. Isaiah has done a pretty good job of showcasing how easy it will be to take these places down because the Lord is going to be the one causing the affliction to begin with. When the Lord is your enemy, you will not be standing for very long. It’s wise for nations not to make God their enemy, and even wiser for Israel (the chosen nation) to obey and turn to the Lord. However, they will not, and it will cause the destruction of their country as well. In this chapter, we get a short and simple look at how vulnerable the nations are without the Lord. If it’s possible for Assyria to rule these nations, why would it not be possible for them to take over the whole world and keep going?"],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":6,"title":"Nowhere to Turn","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"We have taken a deeper look at this particular situation in 2 Kings. Obviously, Assyria will be responsible for taking over the northern kingdom of Israel, while Babylon will take over the southern kingdom, or Judah. This should be well rehearsed at this point, and if it’s not, I highly recommend studying 1 and 2 Kings. It’s a bit of an emotionally heavy read, but I think it’s important for context. We are starting to catch up to the fact that Assyria is a real threat to Israel at this time, and Isaiah had spent a good portion of the beginning of this letter warning them about their impending doom. The degradation of Israel has been known for quite a few years at this point, and it was heading this direction for quite some time."},{"kind":"para","text":"So while all of this is happening, God goes to speak to Isaiah. I’m sure the things that Isaiah was witnessing were discouraging to say the least. Isaiah doesn’t want to see his own people fail and fall. He wants to see them repent and prosper. Honestly, I think that is the only way to prosper in this life. The prosperity preacher will tell you to give this and that to have prosperity. They will say, “You must take action, you must try harder, you must be who you want to be.” God says, “You want prosperity? Repent of your sins, let go of your actions, stop trying so hard, humble yourself before me.” Israel doesn’t do this, and so things are coming to a close, and Isaiah is left dumbstruck by it. The Lord had already warned everyone, and they didn’t heed the warning. But God is going to put Isaiah at ease."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Now, it does not directly say it here, but I have no doubt in my mind that Isaiah is questioning the methods of action by the Lord. You are reading this right. He is told to walk around Israel without any clothes on. People already thought Isaiah was weird. This will make him out to be even weirder. Not only so, but the next verse tells us that he does this for three years!"}]},{"start":3,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"You might say, “God could have demonstrated this very differently. He could have just said it.” However, people don’t learn from words. Well, some people might, but not everyone. I like to demonstrate things if I can. I like to have object lessons. This was an interesting object lesson. No one could argue that Isaiah didn’t warn them. He walked around preaching to them for three years, and they still didn’t get it. The symbol was that they will be just like Isaiah. They will have nothing but their vulnerabilities revealed to the world."},{"kind":"para","text":"Specifically, at this time, Assyria is going to take control of Egypt and Ethiopia. Assyria has become quite the powerhouse. It will lead to the captivity of Israel as well. Ethiopia and Egypt are just the surrounding countries. There will be nothing left to protect Israel from invasion at that point."}]},{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Ethiopia was becoming quite the powerhouse as well. So when they are taken over, they will be extremely confused. They will see it, and their expectations will be shattered. Egypt will lose its glory, which had been growing for generations upon generations at this point. The rest of the world will see a place like Egypt be brought down and think, “What chance do we have? Assyria is too powerful! We are all doomed to serve Assyria forever.” They would be right. But they still have a chance to repent and turn to the Lord. God is still offering them a way of salvation if they would just turn."},{"kind":"para","text":"We will notice that Isaiah is a big part of the history of Israel at this moment, and Isaiah is doing everything in his own power to preach and teach them, but they are just not getting it. They don’t even get it after he had preached to them naked. If anything would get their attention, you would think it was this, but it seems to go right over their head. Today, most probably wouldn’t bat an eye at a naked person walking around the streets. It happens a lot more than you think out here in the desert. They are usually drunks or high off their minds and so they have no idea what they are doing when they are doing it. Isaiah had no reputation like this though."},{"kind":"para","text":"Imagine your pastor started walking around naked for three years to prove a point. Or maybe don’t imagine it, but just relate it to Isaiah here for a moment. Something should (in some way) click in your brain that there is something you are missing and should be paying attention to. Not for Israel though. Not for the surrounding countries…"}]},{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"If these powerful countries can be taken over so easily by Assyria, Israel will not stand a chance. The question will be asked, “How shall we escape?” By human vision, there is no chance of escape. That is why they must turn to the Lord. You would think that in a desperate last-minute attempt, they would turn to God and beg for strength and provision. Their ancestors have done it before, and the Lord had come through. Yet that is not what takes place. It won’t be until after they are taken that they learn and realize that they have been doing this all wrong for too long. They have ignored God and need His help. It will have to lose everything before they realize that, though. Sadly, that is the case with most leadership today, even in the church."},{"kind":"para","text":"They lead people astray, or they reject their calling to minister to people, and people are abandoned and hurt, and there is a lot of conflict in the church, and the leaders don’t repent. They don’t turn to the Lord and ask for guidance. Instead, they turn to the Lord and pray for the other person. You are responsible for the souls around you. God has given you the responsibility to take care of those souls."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"As every man hath received the gift, even so minister the same one to another, as good stewards of the manifold grace of God.\" 1 Peter 4:10 \"I have shewed you all things, how that so labouring ye ought to support the weak, and to remember the words of the Lord Jesus, how he said, It is more blessed to give than to receive.\" Acts 20:35 \"For, brethren, ye have been called unto liberty; only use not liberty for an occasion to the flesh, but by love serve one another.\" Galatians 5:13-14 \"Even as the Son of man came not to be ministered unto, but to minister, and to give his life a ransom for many.\" Matthew 20:28 \"And whosoever of you will be the chiefest, shall be servant of all.","ref":"Mark 10:44"},{"kind":"para","text":"Ministry is about following the Lord, yes, but then taking what God gives you to give to those around you. That is ministry. It is usually reserved only for church work or lost souls, but that is a fake minister. Saved souls need ministers too, and they are the most rejected in the church today. They are rejected in this time as well. No one is taking care of Isaiah. Isaiah probably felt like a lone wolf for most of his ministry. He would serve others, but no one ever supported him. Most of the people were against him, even his own king and leadership."},{"kind":"para","text":"If you feel like you have been neglected by your leadership, you stand in good company. Just know that they will eventually regret not standing behind you, and their faulty leadership will eventually lead themselves into turmoil and suffering. You may not ever see it, but we can take the example of every single king of the northern kingdom as proof of what God will do with evil leaders. The only direction a wayward people can turn is to the Lord. So how shall we escape? Well, it’s only by the help and grace of Almighty God!"}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":6}],"verses":{"1":"In the year that Tartan came unto Ashdod, (when Sargon the king of Assyria sent him,) and fought against Ashdod, and took it;","2":"At the same time spake the Lord by Isaiah the son of Amoz, saying, Go and loose the sackcloth from off thy loins, and put off thy shoe from thy foot. And he did so, walking naked and barefoot.","3":"And the Lord said, Like as my servant Isaiah hath walked naked and barefoot three years for a sign and wonder upon Egypt and upon Ethiopia;","4":"So shall the king of Assyria lead away the Egyptians prisoners, and the Ethiopians captives, young and old, naked and barefoot, even with their buttocks uncovered, to the shame of Egypt.","5":"And they shall be afraid and ashamed of Ethiopia their expectation, and of Egypt their glory.","6":"And the inhabitant of this isle shall say in that day, Behold, such is our expectation, whither we flee for help to be delivered from the king of Assyria: and how shall we escape?"}},
    "21": {"chapter":21,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: In the past few chapters, we have gotten a look at the judgements and trials some of the nations AROUND Israel are going to face. Most of them will face the punishments because they were a part of trying to destroy and dethrone Israel, while others are collateral damage because of the sins of Israel seeping into the cultures around them. They all had the chance and privilege to turn to the Lord and repent, and not a single nation will do that. There are few in Israel who are looking for the Lord. Isaiah is ONE of a very small remnant following after God, and he has had to do some embarrassing things (like preaching naked to the people for three years)."},{"kind":"para","text":"In this chapter, we continue to look at more surrounding nations. We are going to look at the future prospect of these nations and their demise and burdens. We will start off with the burden of Babylon, going into the burden of Edom, and ending with the burden of Arabia. This chapter folds into a lot of the future promises of the world during the end times, which gives further validity that a prophets words are eternal."}],"previously":["In the past few chapters, we have examined the judgments and trials that some of the nations around Israel are set to face. Most of these nations will endure punishments because they were involved in attempts to destroy and dethrone Israel, while others will suffer as collateral damage due to the sins of Israel seeping into their cultures. Despite having the opportunity and privilege to turn to the Lord and repent, not a single nation will do so. There are few in Israel who are seeking the Lord. Isaiah is one of a very small remnant following after God, and he has had to endure some embarrassing situations, such as preaching naked to the people for three years. In this chapter, we continue to explore more surrounding nations, focusing on their future prospects, demise, and burdens. We will begin with the burden of Babylon, proceed to the burden of Edom, and conclude with the burden of Arabia. This chapter intertwines with many of the future promises of the world during the end times, providing further validation that a prophet’s words are eternal."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":5,"title":"Babylon's Takeover","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"With an introduction like this, we are going to have to assume Isaiah is given some symbolism here. To be sure, symbolism in scripture doesn’t mean that we cannot look at this as literal. Again (and I can’t emphasize this enough), prophets speak in threefold settings. It’s about the current situation, the future Israel, and the end times prophecy. This chapter and these verses will not be looked at any differently."},{"kind":"para","text":"We learn (in verse 9) that this “desert of the sea” is referenced as “Babylon.” Of course, we can talk more about this in the coming verses, but the way this is set up leaves us to believe that the interpretation of this verse is a bit of an oxymoron. How can you have a “desert of the sea?” It’s either a desert or a body of water; it cannot be both. So again, it is a symbol of Babylon. It’s a multitude (as we will read in scripture) of people, likely an ARMY of people. Babylon was strong and forceful, like water, but they were also weak and dry like the desert. Strong in physical stature for sure, but weak in spiritual standings. The land of that day certainly was terrible, and the people of that land were looking to inflict some damage on the Israelites. The same types of symbols will be given once again to Babylon and the likes in Revelation."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is a bit of a proverb here. Solomon was a wise man. He knew what he was saying when he wrote the Proverbs, and it was up to the reader to figure out what he meant by them. It all had a spiritual application, and I hope that it isn’t missed through the reading of Proverbs. But you don’t have to be too wise to figure out that a treacherous dealer (that is, someone who deals without faith or deceitfully) is going to make faithless deals. And it shouldn’t be a surprise to anyone that a spoiler (or someone who deals in violence) is going to spoil. If that is a surprise to you, you are gullible, friend. It’s like being surprised that water is wet and fire is hot. These are not new things. These are things that people can determine with common sense. Yet, every single one of us (myself included) is shocked to find that sinners sin."},{"kind":"para","text":"God is going to use the obvious suspects to come and spoil the city of Babylon. Babylon is a very flagrant and powerful city, and there was no reason that they should have been taken down. But Isaiah is prophesying that Media-Persia will take this city down and spoil it. I don’t believe Persia would have been much stronger than Babylon, yet God is notorious for using weaker nations to prove His strength. I do believe that is why He chooses Israel to begin with."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For thou art an holy people unto the LORD thy God: the LORD thy God hath chosen thee to be a special people unto himself, above all people that are upon the face of the earth. The LORD did not set his love upon you, nor choose you, because ye were more in number than any people; for ye were the fewest of all people: But because the LORD loved you, and because he would keep the oath which he had sworn unto your fathers, hath the LORD brought you out with a mighty hand, and redeemed you out of the house of bondmen, from the hand of Pharaoh king of Egypt.","ref":"Deuteronomy 7:6-8"},{"kind":"para","text":"There was nothing much that this nation could offer the Lord except gratitude and worship. That is what God wants from His people. We get so high-strung and arrogant from God’s goodness that we miss the weakness we must have in order to properly worship Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"When the Lord makes us strong, we think we are something special. It’s in that moment that we must realize how lost we really are without God and humble ourselves before Him. Otherwise, like Israel, it wouldn’t take much for Him to use much weaker people than you to take it all away."}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I could argue that Isaiah feels the pain of the Lord as he gives the vision. The Lord doesn’t want to see this happen to His children. He doesn’t want to see this kind of turmoil and sin chaotically engulf His creation. Yet He is tasked with watching it from high above, willing that everyone would turn and know Him. The majority of this world will reject Him, though, and that is not a comforting thought. It’s like labor pains to the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"I wouldn’t know what that feels like, but I have watched my wife go through labor, twice. The second time was even worse. She started having contractions, and so we went to the nearest hospital to us instead of the hospital she wanted to go to. She was asked if she wanted an epidural to help with the pain, and she was quite hopeful to get it. Well, the labor went faster than expected, and they couldn’t give her the epidural in time. So she was tasked with giving birth to this six-pound child naturally without anything to soothe her. It was quite the experience. There was nothing she could do but give birth to our second child, and she certainly did it through screams, pains, yellings, blood, pushing, doctors, and a whole sort of confusion and unpreparedness from all of us."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord views this situation with His creation in the same light. He views the pains of the world as the pains of labor. Eventually, it will end, but until then, it’s nothing but chaos and a lot of pain."}]},{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Again, I believe these are also emotions of the Lord. Isaiah cannot experience the full extent of God’s pain for creation, but he is certainly feeling a portion of it (at least what his mortal body can take so as not to give him a heart attack). The Lord can feel the emotions of all creation at once. He can be pleased with the righteous and hurt by the evil at the same time. He can be both judge and father. However, He cannot be both for one child. For instance, if you are a child of God, you are not going to receive God’s judgment and God’s love at the same time. You will have one or the other. If you are suffering through sin, you will face God’s conviction first. If you are repentant, you will experience God’s love."},{"kind":"para","text":"We can view it in much the same way we might treat our own children. Are we a forgiving father? God is a forgiving father. Are we a vengeful father? God is a vengeful father. Are we an understanding father? God is an understanding father. Are we a damning father? God is a damning father. We must be very careful with what God has entrusted us to steward in this life because we will reap what we sow, and that includes in the leadership of our homes."},{"kind":"para","text":"God was pleased with the Israelites. If we read through 1 and 2 Kings or 1 and 2 Chronicles, we can see that God had compassion on these people and moved them. It has gotten to a point (now here in Isaiah) where they have turned away from trusting the Lord, and the Lord has no choice but to turn His pleasure into fear. Isaiah feels bad for his fellow man and their sins, but God feels utter hurt to see them give up on His goodness even though He is freely offering it to them with hopes that they will be separated from the pleasures of sin, which only last for a season."}]},{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God is preparing the people for a takeover, but it doesn’t happen for quite some time. We don’t really see it come to pass until the book of Daniel, which takes place about two hundred years later. Anyone in Babylon at this time might read the words of Isaiah and just laugh. They would think that Isaiah had gone mad. The Persians reading this later on would perhaps be inspired and conflicted by these words being so accurate and true."}]}]},{"start":6,"end":10,"title":"Babylon is Fallen","entries":[{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I think it’s important to note that God does not just do anything without there being proof of His work. Every time the Lord has done something throughout history, we can find His signature somewhere. That is why it baffles me that there are people today who fight so strongly against the proof and evidence of the Lord. I used to be one of those people, but I did it out of ignorance. I did it because I didn’t understand the proof, and (quite frankly) I didn’t WANT to understand it. I was too naive to accept the proof given to me, and I didn’t want anyone else to try and force their opinion or beliefs down my throat, no matter how promising the evidence was. Instead of having the mind of an intellectual, I had the mind of a Neanderthal, and it’s true for anyone who rejects the truth."},{"kind":"para","text":"Detectives could say the same thing. If detectives have cold hard evidence to back up what they are looking for in the killer, they can be assured that they have the right guy. But if everyone just rejects the evidence and makes up their own story and interpretation of the events, they will never know what is true and what is fictional. Recently, there was a man who was sentenced to life in prison because he shot a healthcare CEO. There’s been a lot of division as to whether or not his actions were good and right, but murder is murder. I’m sure there’s more to the story than we are being told, but we are only able to capture a small portion of the overarching narrative. Someone posted about it online and said, “So this means that the ‘pro-lifers’ are anti-death penalty right? RIGHT?” It’s a trap conversation to be sure. Reading through the comments, a lot of people thought this guy was funny, “Yeah, you can’t be anti-abortion and pro-death penalty. That’s hypocritical.” You certainly can. If an unborn baby was a murderer, we would have a very different problem to face. Justice MUST be served if we want a safe society. What is the justice for killing a baby in the womb? What is the justice for killing a man who murdered a CEO in cold blood? I think there is quite a stark difference between the two. Yet, we have a whole slew of people in this world who cannot figure out the difference between them."},{"kind":"para","text":"God will have people who know the truth, and He will establish His truth and make it very obvious and very real. It is up to the individual to accept the truth or be like these inhumane people of our society today who can’t differentiate between killing an unborn child and killing a murderer."}]},{"start":7,"end":9,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The watchmen were waiting for any sign or message from neighboring cities. A man came by and told them some terrible news that would likely make a watchman fall. Babylon, the great city of the world, with all of its luxuries, glory, power, and might, has fallen. How is it possible? It’s possible only by surprise. Apparently, the Persians will get into the city under a wall, kill their king, and take it over. It will be that easy for them. Babylon will not expect it. That is how simple it will be for the devils dwelling there to fall. He will build up a city mightier than Babylon, and everyone will look to it as a great source of power and beauty. This is what will be said when the Lord deals with it."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And he cried mightily with a strong voice, saying, Babylon the great is fallen, is fallen, and is become the habitation of devils, and the hold of every foul spirit, and a cage of every unclean and hateful bird.","ref":"Revelation 18:2"},{"kind":"para","text":"It will be like a pebble dropped into the ocean by the Lord. It won’t take much effort. That is a great representation of this situation and the future promise of God’s judgment. Babylon would never turn to the Lord, and so He will allow it to be completely taken down. He will also use this to completely dumbfound the rest of the world who trusted in it rather than Him. And dumbfounded they will be."}]},{"start":10,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The threshing floor seems like a scary word for a scary place. To be “threshed” is to be “cultivated and collected.” You don’t thresh a product unless it has fully grown or unless it has withered away. At the moment of Isaiah’s pleading, Israel has become a withered product. They have no fruit or substance. So has Babylon. Isaiah (once again) feels the pain of the Lord. God has taken great care to grow these grapes of His vineyard, remember? That is how God refers to them. But instead, they have turned into “wild” grapes—tainted and poisoned grapes."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And he fenced it, and gathered out the stones thereof, and planted it with the choicest vine, and built a tower in the midst of it, and also made a winepress therein: and he looked that it should bring forth grapes, and it brought forth wild grapes.","ref":"Isaiah 5:2"},{"kind":"para","text":"Yet, the Lord still loves them. Isaiah still feels hurt for their loss. Why? Well, the Lord has raised them. He has given them everything they have ever needed and has provided every step of the way. And instead of accepting it and thanking the Lord, they accept God’s good gift and reject the giver."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"I have shewed you all things, how that so labouring ye ought to support the weak, and to remember the words of the Lord Jesus, how he said, It is more blessed to give than to receive.","ref":"Acts 20:35"},{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord loves to give. He gives everything, including His own life, to this world. We, as mere human beings, take and take from the Lord, and then spit in His face. How cruel and evil a creation we are."},{"kind":"para","text":"God is blessed by giving to you, and you are blessed by receiving. It is backwards. We should be blessed to give as well…"}]}]},{"start":11,"end":12,"title":"Morning and Night","entries":[{"start":11,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"“Dumah” means “silence.” It is a “mystical name of Edom indicating death and ruin” (according to Strong’s Concordance). Dumah is Edom. Interestingly, this is close to the English word “dumb,” which also indicates “silence.” Perhaps that is what God is referring to them as? We can also know that Dumah is Edom because Edom is the only place with Seir in it. Esau was a hairy man, and Seir means hairy, therefore they are one in the same. Esau IS Edom. That should be seared into our brains at this point."},{"kind":"para","text":"We have seemingly shifted gears suddenly. We were just talking about Babylon, and now we are talking about Edom. Isaiah is done with Babylon. There are other countries that need to be concerned too. Edom will have a “burden” as well. This verse is asking about what has happened to Edom. How long is it going to take? It’s insinuating a single “night” that seems to last forever. When God’s judgment pours out, it might only be for a moment, but it will feel like a lifetime because of how terrible it is."}]},{"start":12,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"scripture","text":"Yea, the darkness hideth not from thee; but the night shineth as the day: the darkness and the light are both alike to thee.","ref":"Psalm 139:12"},{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord is the author of both. WE (that is the saved) are children of light."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Ye are all the children of light, and the children of the day: we are not of the night, nor of darkness. Therefore let us not sleep, as do others; but let us watch and be sober. For they that sleep sleep in the night; and they that be drunken are drunken in the night. But let us, who are of the day, be sober, putting on the breastplate of faith and love; and for an helmet, the hope of salvation.","ref":"1 Thessalonians 5:5-8"},{"kind":"para","text":"The light references in scripture are hope references to us, while the dark references are fear references to the world. We are not overcome by darkness, but rather we are overcome by light. We are able to live in the midst of darkness as if it were light because the Lord lives in us. The night might be present, but we are living in the morning."},{"kind":"para","text":"If you are a child of God who cannot do that, you must come to terms with God’s light, friend. He will wrap you in His light, and you will have no choice but to accept it if you are a true child of God. Once you are saved, you cannot give it back. It doesn’t work that way, and yet I’ve seen many men try. They only live in darkness and hide their light, which makes them feel miserable until they just let the light out."},{"kind":"para","text":"Edom (that is the world) will live in darkness, but the children of God can live there in the light. They can be hopeful for the coming of the sun, while the rest of the city is drowning in their sins in the dark."}]}]},{"start":13,"end":17,"title":"Arabia's Burden","entries":[{"start":13,"end":13,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Once again, we have a transition from Edom into Arabia. Isaiah is done with talking about Edom. Some sort of catastrophe will strike Edom. We have read about some of it already. They were supposed to be brothers with the Israelites, but instead, they threw the Israelites to the enemy and rejected helping them. In fact, they just laughed at their calamity. That is the only reason the Lord is going to deal with Edom in this way. They should have helped their brother land."},{"kind":"para","text":"Arabia is also going to face some trouble. They will have a burden for their role in this as well. Arabia was (arguably) founded by the Ishmaelites. We have studied quite a bit on that in our previous chapters and books, and everything in our modern history (and geographical studies) provides immense amounts of evidence that this is the case. Some people would argue with me on this point, but I just can’t see any other way that it isn’t true. Once again, these were to be people that helped the Israelites. They were loosely related to each other as well. If it’s true they came from the line of Abraham, they have some blessings as well. They don’t help the Israelites, but they constantly fight against them (even still today). The Arabs are a rowdy bunch throughout history. To be fair, Abraham set this line up for this by sleeping with his handmaid. The Lord knew what would become of this line, and He warned about it years ago. This is what has become of them, and now they will have a burden because of the sins of Israel at this time."}]},{"start":14,"end":15,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The Arabs are wandering without their necessities being met. They had witnessed the battles and wars of other countries. Edom was suffering, Babylon had fallen, and now Arabia is on the run, in need of food and water. They have nowhere to turn or go. Everything seems to be against these cities at this time, and a new power seems to be coming in and taking over. Nowhere was safe."}]},{"start":16,"end":16,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Arabia is going to fall to pieces in a year. They didn’t have a lot of time to get things together and prepare themselves. Arabia would be judged just as badly as the other nations that have fought against the Lord’s people. They should have stayed out of battle and out of the conflict."},{"kind":"para","text":"Israel is to blame, though. They made a lot of allegiances to countries they shouldn’t have. They should have just relied on the Lord. They had so many years and generations to turn this around. God gave them so much time, but they never turned. And so they turned to the people around them, and they only caused more burden and conflict on the people of Israel."},{"kind":"para","text":"God was not going to let that slide, though. God ALWAYS takes care of His children, even if they are wayward and rebellious. He will turn His people around one way or another and exact judgment on those that are evil and unrighteous."}]},{"start":17,"end":17,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"It will happen. God had spoken it, so therefore it will be done. There’s no fixing it or going back. There’s no changing it now. There’s no running to God. They have had their chance time and time again."},{"kind":"para","text":"The sad part is, they will never even think about turning to the Lord even if they know that God is true in what He is saying here. They won’t desire to turn to Him. They have no means of repenting and trusting in God’s grace and goodness. So God will have no other choice but to follow through on His judgment and burden this nation for their sins and evil deeds. The world is not too far behind today, honestly…"}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":9},{"start":10,"end":10},{"start":11,"end":11},{"start":12,"end":12},{"start":13,"end":13},{"start":14,"end":15},{"start":16,"end":16},{"start":17,"end":17}],"verses":{"1":"The burden of the desert of the sea. As whirlwinds in the south pass through; so it cometh from the desert, from a terrible land.","2":"A grievous vision is declared unto me; the treacherous dealer dealeth treacherously, and the spoiler spoileth. Go up, O Elam: besiege, O Media; all the sighing thereof have I made to cease.","3":"Therefore are my loins filled with pain: pangs have taken hold upon me, as the pangs of a woman that travaileth: I was bowed down at the hearing of it; I was dismayed at the seeing of it.","4":"My heart panted, fearfulness affrighted me: the night of my pleasure hath he turned into fear unto me.","5":"Prepare the table, watch in the watchtower, eat, drink: arise, ye princes, and anoint the shield.","6":"For thus hath the Lord said unto me, Go, set a watchman, let him declare what he seeth.","7":"And he saw a chariot with a couple of horsemen, a chariot of asses, and a chariot of camels; and he hearkened diligently with much heed:","8":"And he cried, A lion: My lord, I stand continually upon the watchtower in the daytime, and I am set in my ward whole nights:","9":"And, behold, here cometh a chariot of men, with a couple of horsemen. And he answered and said, Babylon is fallen, is fallen; and all the graven images of her gods he hath broken unto the ground.","10":"O my threshing, and the corn of my floor: that which I have heard of the Lord of hosts, the God of Israel, have I declared unto you.","11":"The burden of Dumah. He calleth to me out of Seir, Watchman, what of the night? Watchman, what of the night?","12":"The watchman said, The morning cometh, and also the night: if ye will enquire, enquire ye: return, come. The morning could reference Christ. It could reference His return. The Earth is dark, but Christ will bring light.","13":"The burden upon Arabia. In the forest in Arabia shall ye lodge, O ye travelling companies of Dedanim.","14":"The inhabitants of the land of Tema brought water to him that was thirsty, they prevented with their bread him that fled.","15":"For they fled from the swords, from the drawn sword, and from the bent bow, and from the grievousness of war.","16":"For thus hath the Lord said unto me, Within a year, according to the years of an hireling, and all the glory of Kedar shall fail:","17":"And the residue of the number of archers, the mighty men of the children of Kedar, shall be diminished: for the Lord God of Israel hath spoken it."}},
    "22": {"chapter":22,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: In our last few chapters, Isaiah has been speaking about the judgment and leading of the surrounding cities of Judah. He is preparing people for the actions of the Lord, while giving warning to his own people about what is coming their way. Sadly, no one really listens to him, and all these things come to pass without them even realizing it. By the time it happens, it's too late for them."},{"kind":"para","text":"In this chapter, Isaiah is going to talk about the coming captivity of Judah. He will use God's previous victories for them as a means to try and grasp their attention of the seriousness of this, and also give them courage about leaning on the Lord and trusting in His providence and strength. He also points out some issues among their people, and things that the Lord is going to clean up in this time to further illustrate where God is going with His people (as far as what evil is going to look like, and how the Lord plans to save His people)."}],"previously":["In our last few chapters, Isaiah has been speaking about the judgment and leading of the surrounding cities of Judah. He is preparing people for the actions of the Lord while giving warning to his own people about what is coming their way. Sadly, no one really listens to him, and all these things come to pass without them even realizing it. By the time it happens, it’s too late for them. In this chapter, Isaiah is going to talk about the coming captivity of Judah. He will use God’s previous victories for them as a means to try and grasp their attention to the seriousness of this, and also give them courage about leaning on the Lord and trusting in His providence and strength. He also points out some issues among their people and things that the Lord is going to clean up in this time to further illustrate where God is going with His people (as far as what evil is going to look like, and how the Lord plans to save His people)."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":5,"title":"The Valley of Vision","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"“The valley of vision” is a reference to Jerusalem. The next few verses will provide strong evidence of this as we read, though they won’t explicitly state that this is Jerusalem. It’s pretty obvious, though, and Isaiah was a prophet for his country. He was an Israelite who gave counsel to the people of Judah. He was well respected by them and trusted. Although there were many leaders and people who turned their backs on him, they would still come back and ask for direction because he had proven time and again that he knew what he was talking about. That’s something that baffles me, even today. People can hear a man of God preach a message straight from the Word of God, provide proof of what God has said to be true, give them every reason to turn from their sins, pursue the Lord, and share testimonies from (literally) millions of people who have already chosen that path. Yet, there are still many people who reject the Lord. They simply don’t want to believe."},{"kind":"para","text":"The prophets are giving warnings about coming judgment and trouble for the land, and instead of aligning the prophets’ past truths with their current lifestyle, people try to align their current lifestyle with whether or not they want to listen. If they feel like they are having a pretty good and easy life right now, then why listen to the prophet? Just because things are going well for you doesn’t make the truth any less true. People will still be ignorant, though, because they don’t want to believe the Lord would ever do something like that to them when they are so rich and prideful. Then the Lord does what He said He was going to do, and instead of turning to Him (like a normal person should), they turn away from Him even more and say, “Well, that’s not my God then if He is going to treat me like this.”"},{"kind":"para","text":"Isaiah is writing this warning before the coming disaster. It is up to the Israelites to take the message and believe it. Jerusalem was set more on a mountain, so the fact that Isaiah is calling it a “valley” here tells me that they are very far away from the joy and glory of the Lord. The things they are about to experience will be in a valley low, not on a mountaintop high."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"It’s pretty obvious that this city doesn’t know how to feel. They are seeing the coming danger and are wondering if they should run in fear or if they should be excited and joyous about the occasion. The fact that they aren’t killed in battle tells us that they will be killed in a different way. They are likely not even killed by the enemies at all. History tells us that a good portion of them just simply starved to death because of famine and being cut off by so many enemies around them."},{"kind":"para","text":"During the time of the Babylonian captivity of Jerusalem, we could look on a map at the surrounding cities and see that Judah was a lone ranger in the middle of chaos and world powers. They stood no chance without the Lord. They will completely turn from the Lord, and when they do, the Lord will not fight their battles for them, and that is why they are given over to a different country. The Lord is not going to provide blessings for a people who are openly fighting against Him and His leading. Why would He? Why would a father provide aid and security for his children who don’t love him, call him, talk to him, or even acknowledge his existence? Worse yet, his children will take what their father will give them and abuse it on something sinful and against his desire for them. That is what God’s children are doing at this moment, and He is not able to protect them because of it."},{"kind":"para","text":"It wasn’t just the leadership doing evil and heinous things. I know we might read in 1&2 Kings how evil or good these kings may be, but the people under the leadership were following suit. Honestly, I could argue that is why the leaders were evil. The people under their leadership had influence over their leaders. There are a few leaders who were just plain evil, but most of the time it was because they took advice from evil people, rather than look for the advice that the Lord could give. The whole nation will be given over to evil, and that is why God deals with them in that way."},{"kind":"para","text":"The reason that America has not fallen off the map today is not because we are prosperous and we have a lot of riches. Rather, there are good God-fearing people still present here, and so the Lord has not done away with us… yet…"}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"When the Babylonians come in, they will take the leadership and throw them into prison. It won’t take much effort, honestly. Babylon will have a pretty easy time taking them over. The only reason it doesn’t happen sooner is because God gives Judah a chance. There are still some people there that are looking out for the Lord (even if they are few)."}]},{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The people are spoiled. Our country today is extremely spoiled. The world looks at America as pious and comfortable. There’s not necessarily a problem with comfort, but there is a problem with pride. Because we are so comfortable, we believe ourselves to be untouchable. The more pride we have in ourselves, the further the Lord distances Himself from us. The more we humble ourselves, the closer God gets."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Humble yourselves in the sight of the Lord, and he shall lift you up.","ref":"James 4:10"},{"kind":"para","text":"Our country’s greatest weakness is our pride. We are proud about a great deal of things. A good portion of our generation is proud to be gay or transgender. We are proud to be Catholics, Baptists, or Mormons. We are proud to be Republicans or Democrats. We are proud atheists or agnostics. We are proud deniers of truths or proud motivational speakers. We are proud black people, white people, or brown people. We are proud coffee drinkers or energy drink drinkers. We find pride in the dumbest and most minute things possible. We are proud to even be called Americans."},{"kind":"para","text":"I think there are some things we should stand proud in, but they are very few. One is we should be proud to be known by the Lord. We should love the idea that God knows us and has given Himself for us. We should be proud of the talents that the Lord has provided for us, so that we can use them for Him. We should be proud of the desires the Lord gives us to serve Him. All our pride, however, should bring us to humility before the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"\"A man's pride shall bring him low: but honour shall uphold the humble in spirit.\" Proverbs 29:23 \"But he giveth more grace. Wherefore he saith, God resisteth the proud, but giveth grace unto the humble.\" James 4:6 \"Let another man praise thee, and not thine own mouth; a stranger, and not thine own lips.\" Proverbs 27:2 I heard of a preacher who said he never shows pride to his kids. They were really into sports when they were younger and played some football in school. Whenever they won a game, the father would simply say, “Don’t be high-minded, the Lord was the only one that provided you the victory today.” I honestly think this is a rue. I think this is a terrible way to honor and love your kids. You should be proud of them, but they should learn to humble themselves before it gets to their heads. Proud in heart, but humble in mind. Inwardly proud, but outwardly humble. They will enjoy their efforts for these games and these skills if they actually think they are good at it."},{"kind":"para","text":"Christians don’t know how to take a compliment. I’ve seen so many of them slip up and lose their spiritual balance when someone says, “Wow, that was a great sermon today,” or “You are a great teacher,” or “worship leader,” or whatever it is that the Lord has called you to do. I’ve even tripped up over it. People would tell me, “That was a great sermon today,” and instead of just taking the compliment and praising the Lord, I would say, “I plagiarized the whole thing.” Technically, I’m not lying because it’s God’s Word that I am literally referring to and using when I teach, but I also have my own thoughts and personal experiences being shared. But my goal was to keep myself from getting a hot head about it. I did not want to be high-minded about my own sermons. Since then, I’ve learned to take the compliments and just go with it. (Sometimes people will thank me now, and I just say, “I did it all for you.” That throws a lot of Christians off.)"},{"kind":"para","text":"Pride is the obvious issue in every country, and we are certainly going to see that issue bring a country completely down through Israel as we read about Isaiah’s perspective."}]},{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Their protection will be gone when the Lord is no longer their delight. The walls aren’t going to protect them. Isaiah says they will be “broken down.” Moreover, they will have nothing to turn to except to cry out to the mountains for help. Throughout scripture, that seems to be the common theme that the Israelites go to when all is lost. They keep going to the mountains to hide. In the end times, I think that is where a good majority of the world will be hiding again. They won’t be able to live openly in those days, so they will be hiding in the mountains to refrain from being killed and destroyed by their government rulers. In fact, they will call out to the mountains to crush them and kill them to be away from the Lord’s judgment and terror."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And said to the mountains and rocks, Fall on us, and hide us from the face of him that sitteth on the throne, and from the wrath of the Lamb: For the great day of his wrath is come; and who shall be able to stand?","ref":"Revelation 6:16-17"}]}]},{"start":6,"end":11,"title":"Proof of God's Protection","entries":[{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Elam will be a help to Babylon. They have already helped the Babylonians fight against Assyria, so they will be a quiver for the Babylonians. Kir will help break down their walls and provide shield and protection for Babylon."}]},{"start":7,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Verse 8 kind of declares that this “Valley of vision” is, in fact, Judah. They will be completely surrounded, and it sounds like, according to Isaiah, they will know exactly where to go and where their weakest points of entrance will be. This is all the fault of Hezekiah. We read about Hezekiah’s mistake in letting Babylon see where all his treasures are. His enemies took note and were ready to siege Jerusalem because of it. We can talk more about that in 2 Kings. The point is, Babylon will have a very easy time breaking into Judah because they had been shown where everything was and how easy it was to take it all. Without the Lord’s help, they are destined to lose everything."}]},{"start":9,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"We have a record of this (further detailing that this valley is Judah)."},{"kind":"para","text":"\"So there was gathered much people together, who stopped all the fountains, and the brook that ran through the midst of the land, saying, Why should the kings of Assyria come, and find much water? Also he strengthened himself, and built up all the wall that was broken, and raised it up to the towers, and another wall without, and repaired Millo in the city of David, and made darts and shields in abundance.\" 2 Chronicles 32:4-5 They have come into this “takeover” territory before by Assyria. Assyria tried to strongarm Judah and take it over (they had done it to the rest of Israel, so why not to Judah as well?). They just needed the southern kingdom to complete their collection. The Lord uses Hezekiah to prevent this from taking place, and Hezekiah builds a wall (apparently tearing down people’s homes to do it) around a single fountain of water (their last resort). This was all they had left to keep them going and thriving. The Lord does not give Assyria entrance, and Judah is safe for a little while longer. But when Babylon comes, they won’t be so blessed to succeed again."}]},{"start":11,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"If they had looked back at their histories past, they would see how they won the battles before. They would understand that they were taken care of by divine intervention. They would see that David was a man who was after God’s heart. That Saul sought after Samuel’s advice, and Samuel always pointed him to God. They would see the judges who rescued them, and Joshua who triumphed to get them this land. They would see Moses who led them to victory several times over, and Israel who was protected and taken care of into his old age. They would see the providence and continued faith increase from Abraham, as well as the preserved lineage of these people through Noah."},{"kind":"para","text":"They would be able to link all these figures back to one source of power and perseverance, and they would only be able to say, “The Lord did it. He must be the one that does it again, otherwise we fall!” However, they will not “look unto the maker thereof…” and it will be their fall because of it. Even by the fact that they were not taken over by Assyria (not that long ago) would be proof enough that God is the real reason they have victory. But they won’t see it like that…"}]}]},{"start":12,"end":14,"title":"A Downward Spiral","entries":[{"start":12,"end":13,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God calls them to humility, and instead, they live in luxury and pride. Again, we are mimicking this in our generation right here in America. We are seeing the fall of America quite rapidly because of our pride. The only thing keeping us afloat is the humble people in our country. Those who have listened to the call of weeping and mourning for this country are living in sackcloth and destitution."},{"kind":"para","text":"Sadly, there are a lot of people who are stepping all over the humble Christians today so they can keep their riches and honor for themselves. They like to be valued by society and could care less about what kind of value the Lord can give them. Even pastors have rejected the value from the Lord, sadly."}]},{"start":14,"end":14,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God sees that it won’t go away. It won’t go away because the Lord has been protecting them. They have everything they need (or so they think) and have turned completely against the Lord and His presence. So God sees that it will continue forever in this way."},{"kind":"para","text":"They will abuse themselves and their own people. They will continue to worship false gods. They will continue to kill their own children by sacrificing them to gods that don’t even exist. They will continue to rape and maim their own people and abuse women for things that shouldn’t be done. Murder and abortion will run rampant, and people will fall head over heels for the lifestyle and easiness of sin."},{"kind":"para","text":"It’s all quite textbook, honestly. We’ve seen this happen already throughout history (even before Isaiah), and now we are seeing it happen again during the time of Isaiah, and today (in America) we are seeing it happen again. History is just one big spiral going back on itself. It doesn’t stray off course. If we last another 2000 years as a planet, we will run into this same problem again. I have no doubt in my mind that history will always repeat its same mistakes. We (as sinful human beings) don’t even learn lessons from our elders."}]}]},{"start":15,"end":25,"title":"Salvation's Mark","entries":[{"start":15,"end":16,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Shebna was not a fun person. He was irresponsible (at least Isaiah will say he is later)."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And when they had called to the king, there came out to them Eliakim the son of Hilkiah, which was over the household, and Shebna the scribe, and Joah the son of Asaph the recorder...And he sent Eliakim, which was over the household, and Shebna the scribe, and the elders of the priests, covered with sackcloth, to Isaiah the prophet the son of Amoz.","ref":"2 Kings 18:18;19:2"},{"kind":"para","text":"He was trying to make a name for himself, it seems. He wanted to be looked at as prosperous. Honestly, he is a great image of all of Judah at the moment. They think they are something special. They think they can have a bigger name than their God."},{"kind":"para","text":"Shebna was trying to leave a legacy of his own excellency by preparing this extravagant tomb for himself, but he won’t even be buried in Judah. Captivity is coming to him:"}]},{"start":17,"end":18,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Shebna’s glory will be washed away and forgotten. There’s a reason that Shebna is not a very well-known name in our churches (or world for that matter) today. People outside the church may know the name of David and the name of Jesus, but they will certainly never know the name of Shebna."}]},{"start":19,"end":19,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"He is a lofty thinker, this Shebna fellow. He thinks quite highly of himself. While I recognize that this is the current problem with Israel as a collective, and indeed the downfall of any civilization, it is also the mindset of the coming world power through Satan. God will let Satan lift himself up quite high. His pride will bring him into prosperity, and he will be the leader of a very large nation with plenty to spare and trade to any other nation willing to bow before him."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is also disguised as a man who seems godly. He is seen with the order to fix up the temple, and it seems that he was using that money for himself and his own legacy. But the Lord will not allow that to prosper. He won’t allow Satan to prosper either. Evil will not win in the end. It will seem and feel like it did, but God always has the last say, and He will always be finality."}]},{"start":20,"end":21,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Apparently, Eliakim is very different from Shebna. He will do what is right and put things in order for the right reasons instead of pocketing the money or abusing his authority and position. Perhaps this conversation taking place here (in Isaiah) was right after Hezekiah was threatened by Rabshakeh of Assyria in 2 Kings 19:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And it came to pass, when king Hezekiah heard it, that he rent his clothes, and covered himself with sackcloth, and went into the house of the LORD. And he sent Eliakim, which was over the household, and Shebna the scribe, and the elders of the priests, covered with sackcloth, to Isaiah the prophet the son of Amoz. And they said unto him, Thus saith Hezekiah, This day is a day of trouble, and of rebuke, and blasphemy: for the children are come to the birth, and there is not strength to bring forth. It may be the LORD thy God will hear all the words of Rabshakeh, whom the king of Assyria his master hath sent to reproach the living God; and will reprove the words which the LORD thy God hath heard: wherefore lift up thy prayer for the remnant that are left.","ref":"2 Kings 19:1-4"},{"kind":"para","text":"If that is the case, which is probably the most likely, it means during the conflict with Assyria, Shebna was robbing from God’s temple. It’s a weird time to be doing things like that. This also means it was before Hezekiah became sick and asked for more years to live. That is ultimately what will bring about the captivity of Babylon. It will be the Babylonians who come to see Hezekiah while he is not feeling well. The captivity doesn’t even make sense to them as Isaiah is saying it right now. Hezekiah is a good king, and he is doing everything he can to follow the Lord’s guidance. Why would God still give them over to be captive?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Well, it will be because of the small-minded decisions that Hezekiah makes to give his enemy knowledge of his possessions during a time of great conflict with all the cities neighboring Judah. It won’t be in Hezekiah’s lifetime, but it will follow in the generations after him (sadly)."}]},{"start":22,"end":22,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"We should be able to read this and line this up pretty quickly with Christ."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And to the angel of the church in Philadelphia write; These things saith he that is holy, he that is true, he that hath the key of David, he that openeth, and no man shutteth; and shutteth, and no man openeth;","ref":"Revelation 3:7"},{"kind":"para","text":"We might think, “Boy, Isaiah’s ADHD is acting up here. He took a sharp right turn all of a sudden from all the terrible things he said they are going to face.” He went from captivity to authority pretty quickly. He is talking about two people here. He is talking about Eliakim (who is going to put things in proper order), but he is (obviously) talking about Christ. Again, he’s a prophet, so he is bringing this word from a temporal standpoint (this is what will happen shortly), and from an eternal standpoint (this is what will happen in the future). The words of the prophets are always folding into those categories."},{"kind":"para","text":"Again, the evil in this world will not prosper, and the Lord will have the final say. He will bring the victory in the end, and it will be through Christ (always) that the victory comes. If you want to stand in victory, you MUST stand with Christ."}]},{"start":23,"end":24,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"These verses are WILD! Think about how closely related this is to Jesus for a moment. \"I will fasten him as a nail in a sure place...\""},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For dogs have compassed me: the assembly of the wicked have inclosed me: they pierced my hands and my feet.\" Psalm 22:16 \"The other disciples therefore said unto him, We have seen the Lord. But he said unto them, Except I shall see in his hands the print of the nails, and put my finger into the print of the nails, and thrust my hand into his side, I will not believe.\" John 20:25 \"And you, being dead in your sins and the uncircumcision of your flesh, hath he quickened together with him, having forgiven you all trespasses; Blotting out the handwriting of ordinances that was against us, which was contrary to us, and took it out of the way, nailing it to his cross;","ref":"Colossians 2:13-14"},{"kind":"para","text":"Interestingly enough, the gospels do not directly state that Jesus was “nailed” to the cross; they simply say He was crucified. However, by the fact that He asks Thomas to put his hand in the holes of his hands and feet, as well as Paul mentioning that our sins were nailed to the cross, along with other information we can gather from how crucifixions were conducted back then and other biblical references to the crucifixion, we can conclude that He was assuredly nailed to the cross."},{"kind":"para","text":"David also provides us with a prophecy, and all prophecies are fulfilled, including what Isaiah is saying here. Jesus will also be a glorious throne for His Father’s house, and He still sits on that throne (deservedly). “They shall hang upon him all the glory of his father’s house” is an interesting way to state that as well."},{"kind":"para","text":"Most will view the crucifixion as cruel and sinful, seeing an innocent man being hung for a problem that wasn’t even a real problem, with sinful man getting away with sinful deeds. However, the salvation displayed on the cross is “the glory of his father’s house…” Without it, we would not have hope for eternity, as well as hope for our dismal and simple lifestyles."}]},{"start":25,"end":25,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Of course, we can look at this as the antichrist coming and being cut down. He will be. As we’ve already mentioned, the Lord has the final say, and just like Shebna, Satan’s rule and dominance will not last forever. It will be like a nail that is removed. But we can also look to the Lord for this as well (the fall and tribulation of mankind)."},{"kind":"para","text":"“In that day…” again we have a threefold prophecy. It’s always threefold. In that day can refer to the coming captivity. They will be taken captive, and the things they have stationed now (even through Eliakim) will all be lost and disappear. It will come to nothing for future generations because they didn’t take hold of God’s goodness while they had the chance."},{"kind":"para","text":"In that day, when Jesus comes and dies for us on the cross, we will see that there are a lot of people who will still reject Him, even after His proven resurrection. They still reject Him today, and the moment they die without the Lord, the sure place is removed. In that day, when Jesus returns, the world will not have a second chance to come to Him. It will be too late. Salvation only comes by faith, and if they see the Lord, it will be too late."},{"kind":"para","text":"Isaiah’s final thought in this chapter should be a wakeup call for our nation and for those that don’t know the Lord. “That day” is coming. When it does, it will be too late. We have today and today only to get things right with the Lord. “That day” could be a long time off, or “that day” could be tomorrow. It’s not a gamble that anyone should be willing to make."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":10},{"start":11,"end":11},{"start":12,"end":13},{"start":14,"end":14},{"start":15,"end":16},{"start":17,"end":18},{"start":19,"end":19},{"start":20,"end":21},{"start":22,"end":22},{"start":23,"end":24},{"start":25,"end":25}],"verses":{"1":"The burden of the valley of vision. What aileth thee now, that thou art wholly gone up to the housetops?","2":"Thou that art full of stirs, a tumultuous city, joyous city: thy slain men are not slain with the sword, nor dead in battle.","3":"All thy rulers are fled together, they are bound by the archers: all that are found in thee are bound together, which have fled from far.","4":"Therefore said I, Look away from me; I will weep bitterly, labour not to comfort me, because of the spoiling of the daughter of my people.","5":"For it is a day of trouble, and of treading down, and of perplexity by the Lord God of hosts in the valley of vision, breaking down the walls, and of crying to the mountains.","6":"And Elam bare the quiver with chariots of men and horsemen, and Kir uncovered the shield.","7":"And it shall come to pass, that thy choicest valleys shall be full of chariots, and the horsemen shall set themselves in array at the gate.","8":"And he discovered the covering of Judah, and thou didst look in that day to the armour of the house of the forest.","9":"Ye have seen also the breaches of the city of David, that they are many: and ye gathered together the waters of the lower pool.","10":"And ye have numbered the houses of Jerusalem, and the houses have ye broken down to fortify the wall.","11":"Ye made also a ditch between the two walls for the water of the old pool: but ye have not looked unto the maker thereof, neither had respect unto him that fashioned it long ago.","12":"And in that day did the Lord God of hosts call to weeping, and to mourning, and to baldness, and to girding with sackcloth:","13":"And behold joy and gladness, slaying oxen, and killing sheep, eating flesh, and drinking wine: let us eat and drink; for to morrow we shall die.","14":"And it was revealed in mine ears by the Lord of hosts, Surely this iniquity shall not be purged from you till ye die, saith the Lord God of hosts.","15":"Thus saith the Lord God of hosts, Go, get thee unto this treasurer, even unto Shebna, which is over the house, and say,","16":"What hast thou here? and whom hast thou here, that thou hast hewed thee out a sepulchre here, as he that heweth him out a sepulchre on high, and that graveth an habitation for himself in a rock?","17":"Behold, the Lord will carry thee away with a mighty captivity, and will surely cover thee.","18":"He will surely violently turn and toss thee like a ball into a large country: there shalt thou die, and there the chariots of thy glory shall be the shame of thy lord's house.","19":"And I will drive thee from thy station, and from thy state shall he pull thee down.","20":"And it shall come to pass in that day, that I will call my servant Eliakim the son of Hilkiah:","21":"And I will clothe him with thy robe, and strengthen him with thy girdle, and I will commit thy government into his hand: and he shall be a father to the inhabitants of Jerusalem, and to the house of Judah.","22":"And the key of the house of David will I lay upon his shoulder; so he shall open, and none shall shut; and he shall shut, and none shall open.","23":"And I will fasten him as a nail in a sure place; and he shall be for a glorious throne to his father's house.","24":"And they shall hang upon him all the glory of his father's house, the offspring and the issue, all vessels of small quantity, from the vessels of cups, even to all the vessels of flagons.","25":"In that day, saith the Lord of hosts, shall the nail that is fastened in the sure place be removed, and be cut down, and fall; and the burden that was upon it shall be cut off: for the Lord hath spoken it."}},
    "23": {"chapter":23,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: We've been getting destruction after destruction in quite a few of these chapters already, and it seems like it's a lost cause for the entire world as we read through it. It has not been a good time for anyone since Israel has been taken captive, and the coming captivity of Judah will lead to even more turmoil for Israel, as well as the neighboring cities to Judah. God has the final say-so."},{"kind":"para","text":"In fact, this chapter is a revelation of God's last word having the final authority, and how it is to be respected as well as expected. Tyre will be the land we look at next, and it seems that they are going to get the worst of it. All of these other cities are promised a comeback, but Tyre is promised a complete destruction with no possiblity to rebuild."}],"previously":["We’ve been experiencing destruction after destruction in quite a few of these chapters already, and it seems like it’s a lost cause for the entire world as we read through it. It has not been a good time for anyone since Israel has been taken captive, and the coming captivity of Judah will lead to even more turmoil for Israel, as well as the neighboring cities to Judah. God has the final say-so. In fact, this chapter is a revelation of God’s last word having the final authority, and how it is to be respected as well as expected. Tyre will be the land we look at next, and it seems that they are going to get the worst of it. All of these other cities are promised a comeback, but Tyre is promised a complete destruction with no possibility to rebuild."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":7,"title":"Judgement For Tyre","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"We might remember that Tyre and Israel were confederate during the time of David’s reign. Hiram was friends with David and helped in the building of the Lord’s temple during the kingship of Solomon. Now, it seems that there is a burden placed on Tyre as well, as they are starting to become quite rich in their territory. And wouldn’t you know it? Tyre doesn’t exist today. Though there have been multiple attempts to rebuild it, the Lord has not allowed it to prosper."},{"kind":"para","text":"It seems the people of Tarshish will be devastated too. I assume the people of Tarshish got a lot of supplies and material goods from Tyre, but now that they can’t, they are stuck with missing out on great financial gain. This all actually might sound familiar to you if you have already read the end of this book. Revelation has a similar situation happen to a great and prosperous city:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And the merchants of the earth shall weep and mourn over her; for no man buyeth their merchandise any more: The merchandise of gold, and silver, and precious stones, and of pearls, and fine linen, and purple, and silk, and scarlet, and all thyine wood, and all manner vessels of ivory, and all manner vessels of most precious wood, and of brass, and iron, and marble, And cinnamon, and odours, and ointments, and frankincense, and wine, and oil, and fine flour, and wheat, and beasts, and sheep, and horses, and chariots, and slaves, and souls of men. And the fruits that thy soul lusted after are departed from thee, and all things which were dainty and goodly are departed from thee, and thou shalt find them no more at all. The merchants of these things, which were made rich by her, shall stand afar off for the fear of her torment, weeping and wailing,","ref":"Revelation 18:11-15"},{"kind":"para","text":"The picture of this city is more like “Babylon” during the time of Revelation. However, Tyre was just as prosperous as Babylon during the time of Isaiah. This leads to confusion among people about how such prosperity could occur in both instances."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Sidon and Tyre were neighboring cities that worked together through everything. Now, Sidon will be at a standstill because of the destruction of Tyre. They will be completely devastated and dumbfounded when they see Tyre has been leveled."}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Sihor will seem to suffer as well. They were helpful in producing crops and wealth for the land of Egypt. That, in turn, helped produce wealth for Tyre and the surrounding nations. God will certainly make a lot of very rich people confused and unhappy by putting an end to this one city."}]},{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Perhaps Sidon was responsible for creating Tyre originally. I don’t really know, but a lot of scholars far smarter than me seem to think that this is the case based on this one verse alone. I don’t see why not? Sidon still exists today. It just isn’t as glorious as it once was during the time of Isaiah, and I believe it’s because of what will happen to Tyre."}]},{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Egypt seems to be getting it from all sides. We already encountered the burden and judgment of Egypt a few chapters back, and it wasn’t very pretty. They are going to go through a lot, and yet God will still call them together in the end somehow. Of course, we probably know that Egypt is still around today. It didn’t get completely demolished. Once again, though, they are not a world power like they used to be. They have some power, but they wouldn’t be looked at as the first pick in a battle against any other nation."},{"kind":"para","text":"I do believe that the reason Egypt is not gaining power again is simply because of problems with Tyre, which led to problems with Sihor, which led to problems with their economy and power to grow crops. They had some of the most fertile land at one point, but the Lord seems to put a stop to that here in the book of Isaiah. And honestly, it’s due to the fact that Israel simply didn’t listen to the Lord. They didn’t turn back to Him. If Israel had listened, I think a lot of this history would be very different. But, of course, the Lord already knew this would take place, so He had this planned from the beginning of time."}]},{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"It will be the Babylonians that take Tyre by the way. They will take Judah, and they will take Tyre with them. Some escape to Tarshish, and they will feel the pains of their land as it is completely decimated."}]},{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There are still ancient bits of Tyre that you can physically see today. There is a lot of broken-up pottery and clay mouldings that lie waste in that land. Supposedly, even Alexander the Great didn’t think it would be a good idea for Tyre to be rebuilt, as he is seen sieging it in 332 BC. Interestingly, Alexander received help from Sidon during the takeover, and there is still nothing left of it even though they tried to rebuild on an island (of all places)."},{"kind":"para","text":"God does not want this city to come back to life. I assume it wasn’t just about material possessions either. Most of these wealthy cities have more in them than fancy dishes and dry goods to export. There was likely drugs and lustful trading happening as well. That will be the main issue to the city in Revelation as well. It’s an issue that is deeply looked at in 1 & 2 Corinthians, because Corinth will become a city that is just like Tyre."}]}]},{"start":8,"end":9,"title":"The Mob","entries":[{"start":8,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"That is probably why Tyre was such a liked city. If you traded with them, you became an heir to them. You became included in their culture and family. It’s like the Mafia on a grander scale. The Mafia accepts you when you do a job for them. You are family after that. Once you start to question them, you become an enemy quite quickly. Tyre was likely the same way. There are still countries that are like this today. Rome will be like this in a roundabout way. Honestly, I think Rome is a big reason that the Mafia became so popular in America later. The Mafia still exists today; they just don’t tout themselves like they used to."}]},{"start":9,"end":9,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is not me being pessimistic or rash when I speak about this, but I honestly believe that the church has a big problem with material gain today. Their glory lies in money. They think they are something if they are gaining a paycheck. In the church (again, I’m just being honest), the goal is to get paid to take care of people. I think pastors (specifically) should get paid to minister. I think they should get paid to take care of people (specifically the saved). However, they should not get paid to preach. That is the job for the whole congregation. They should not get paid to teach. That is the job for the whole congregation. They should not get paid to soulwin. That is the job for the whole congregation. They should not get paid to study, or to pray, or to attend this meeting or that meeting. That is the job for the whole congregation. That is not how the church works though. Honestly, I think most pastors are under the impression that they SHOULD be paid to preach, teach, soulwin, study, pray, and go on campaigns. That is a shallow-minded pastor."},{"kind":"para","text":"I posted on social media recently that “the problem with pastors today is they pray for your name, not for your needs. Honestly, most pastors don’t even know what your needs are.” A church member commented, “Yeah, but God does!” And she is absolutely right. However, you can’t say that about a lawyer you are paying. You can’t say that about a tutor you are paying. A therapist can’t say that. You can’t say, “Listen, I need legal advice, can you help me here? I will pay you for this.” and the lawyer tells you, “No, I’ll take your money, but I will just keep your name on my file and never deal with your actual problem. God knows your needs, let Him take care of it.” What a useless lawyer that would be. Yet that is how pastors are today. They have been placed in a position by the Lord, and instead of using their position (that they get paid for, mind you) as a means to help the saints of God, they ABUSE their position to ignore them and do “church things.” Pastors should be using their God-given position to meet the needs of the flock, not abusing their position to rob them of their joys."},{"kind":"para","text":"Tyre was a wealthy nation, and it was God that set them up there in all honesty. Israel was a wealthy nation, too, and it was God that set them up there. Both of them will lose everything because of their turning away and trusting in their idols and wealth. Both of them will come back to their land sanctioned by the Lord. One will rebuild their land, the other will never be able to build it up again. That is the difference between a saved man and an unsaved man. May we not take for granted where God has us and what God has given to us. It is quite possible that we will not be able to go back to it if we are leading in unrighteousness. Or maybe we will be in it too long and steer far too many innocent people astray…"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For the leaders of this people cause them to err; and they that are led of them are destroyed.","ref":"Isaiah 9:16"},{"kind":"para","text":"Seriously, I think a good majority of churches today are more like Tyre than they are like the Lord."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For if a man think himself to be something, when he is nothing, he deceiveth himself.","ref":"Galatians 6:3"}]}]},{"start":10,"end":14,"title":"Wasting God's Goodness","entries":[{"start":10,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Nothing is holding Tarshish back from exploration and trade. They will have to travel further for it, but Tarshish will be completely free from any ties or bonds with Tyre. The Mafia of Tyre will be taken care of and gotten rid of."}]},{"start":11,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"What an interesting way to put the devastation of this time. God says He has “shook the kingdoms.” They will feel the shaking and moving of God. They won’t see it as God, specifically, doing it, but they will know that something mighty certainly has caused a course of change for everyone around them. There is no way they can deny that a higher power has done this. They are seeing something impossible take place to a very large and successful city. Their wealth and prosperity have saved them from so many other things; why can’t it save them now?"},{"kind":"para","text":"May that be a warning to the church today. If you are relying on your wealth and prosperity from the Lord for gain, you will eventually see a falling apart and chaotic end to what God has given you in love and time. God must always have the lead; otherwise, we will waste His good gifts to us."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But seek ye first the kingdom of God, and his righteousness; and all these things shall be added unto you.\" Matthew 6:33 \"Lay not up for yourselves treasures upon earth, where moth and rust doth corrupt, and where thieves break through and steal: But lay up for yourselves treasures in heaven, where neither moth nor rust doth corrupt, and where thieves do not break through nor steal: For where your treasure is, there will your heart be also.\" Matthew 6:19-21 \"For they that are after the flesh do mind the things of the flesh; but they that are after the Spirit the things of the Spirit.","ref":"Romans 8:5 12 And he said, Thou shalt no more rejoice, O thou oppressed virgin, daughter of Zidon: arise, pass over to Chittim; there also shalt thou have no rest."},{"kind":"para","text":"This verse suggests that Tyre was owned and created by Sidon. Perhaps Tyre became far more wicked and sinful than Sidon, which is why God is dealing with Tyre in this way. I would assume this to be the case. It makes you wonder why God would allow places like Las Vegas and other worldly and lustful cities to still exist today. They won’t exist forever, but it’s truly God’s grace and patience displayed that these places haven’t been demolished."},{"kind":"para","text":"Either way, Sidon will feel the pains of what is happening to Tyre anyway, because they worked strongly together in everything they did. It seems that God knows where they are going to try and go next. He says, “Go ahead, pass over to Chittim, no matter where you go you aren’t going to find any rest or comfort.” The main reason they won’t find comfort is not specifically because the Lord is going to make them uncomfortable. It’s because their comfort was in financial prosperity, and when their only comfort is gone and destroyed, where else are they going to turn?"},{"kind":"para","text":"13 Behold the land of the Chaldeans; this people was not, till the Assyrian founded it for them that dwell in the wilderness: they set up the towers thereof, they raised up the palaces thereof; and he brought it to ruin."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Chaldeans, obviously, are the Babylonians. Assyria helped them prosper, and now they were even bigger and greater than Assyria could be. They will be the reigning kings of the world for a time. God’s Spirit seems to move like that. He allows great prosperity in nations for a time until that nation starts to abuse God’s goodness for sinful gain. Then His Spirit moves to a different country, and His wrath abides with the sinful one."},{"kind":"para","text":"I do believe that is where we are currently at in America. We had God’s Spirit, and we abused it for personal gain, and now we are seeing an immense and uncontrollable downfall. Where His Spirit goes next? I don’t know."},{"kind":"para","text":"14 Howl, ye ships of Tarshish: for your strength is laid waste."},{"kind":"para","text":"Once again, God reiterates the great loss this world is going to experience when Tyre is destroyed. Honestly, it will have moved to Babylon. It will seem as if there is no stopping Babylon at this point. Yet, Babylon is just a part of history now. They no longer exist today, and you are hard-pressed to find much viable evidence that it ever actually did exist. We have found evidence, but it’s few and far between because of how destructive they became."}]}]},{"start":15,"end":16,"title":"No Hope","entries":[{"start":15,"end":15,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Judah will also be gone for seventy years. As I’ve mentioned, both of these places will experience the same losses, and they will both be taken by the same people. They will both return to their same lands, but only one will be successful at rebuilding, while the other one never stands a chance at a new life."},{"kind":"para","text":"Christians and atheists experience the same trials in life today. They both have to suffer through the same ailments, pains, and temptations. They both have to deal with the same world. Yet one has hope of eternal life, and the other has no chance of building a life at all. What a miserable place to be in physically, spiritually, or mentally without the Lord of hope."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Now the God of hope fill you with all joy and peace in believing, that ye may abound in hope, through the power of the Holy Ghost.\" Romans 15:13 \"Rejoicing in hope; patient in tribulation; continuing instant in prayer;\" Romans 12:12 \"For I know the thoughts that I think toward you, saith the LORD, thoughts of peace, and not of evil, to give you an expected end.","ref":"Jeremiah 29:11 16 Take an harp, go about the city, thou harlot that hast been forgotten; make sweet melody, sing many songs, that thou mayest be remembered."},{"kind":"para","text":"They are only remembered today because of scripture, honestly. We can see the ruins, but we probably wouldn’t think too much of it if we didn’t have a historical account given to us here. Thankfully, we do, and we can remember that God has devastated Tyre. It’s entirely possible that God can do the same thing to this entire planet."}]}]},{"start":17,"end":18,"title":"Real Value","entries":[{"start":17,"end":17,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"If Tyre returns, nothing will change. They will go right back to the way things were before they were taken captive, as if they didn’t learn a single lesson. That is why the Lord doesn’t allow it to be built again. Perhaps, if the Lord allowed it to continue, they would have become an uncontrollable force in the world and would have turned the hearts of all mankind to sin."},{"kind":"para","text":"God has promised not to flood the Earth to kill everyone again, so He will have to destroy the Earth a different way. That is how Babylon in Revelation will be. That is why He will send His judgments, and that is why He will destroy the Earth a different way."}]},{"start":18,"end":18,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Honestly, real merchandise and luxury only come through knowing the Lord anyway. You want real riches that the world can’t have or trade? Trust in Christ and follow God. He gives riches that are quite literally “out of this world.” He provides better riches than anything we can get here. If your riches are here on Earth, you will not have anything that lasts because everything here will pass away."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Heaven and earth shall pass away, but my words shall not pass away.","ref":"Matthew 24:35"},{"kind":"para","text":"Which one is more valuable in that light? Is anything in this world valuable if it just passes away anyway? Or is Christ’s Word more valuable because it doesn’t?"}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":9},{"start":10,"end":10},{"start":11,"end":11},{"start":15,"end":15},{"start":17,"end":17},{"start":18,"end":18}],"verses":{"1":"The burden of Tyre. Howl, ye ships of Tarshish; for it is laid waste, so that there is no house, no entering in: from the land of Chittim it is revealed to them.","2":"Be still, ye inhabitants of the isle; thou whom the merchants of Zidon, that pass over the sea, have replenished.","3":"And by great waters the seed of Sihor, the harvest of the river, is her revenue; and she is a mart of nations.","4":"Be thou ashamed, O Zidon: for the sea hath spoken, even the strength of the sea, saying, I travail not, nor bring forth children, neither do I nourish up young men, nor bring up virgins.","5":"As at the report concerning Egypt, so shall they be sorely pained at the report of Tyre.","6":"Pass ye over to Tarshish; howl, ye inhabitants of the isle.","7":"Is this your joyous city, whose antiquity is of ancient days? her own feet shall carry her afar off to sojourn.","8":"Who hath taken this counsel against Tyre, the crowning city, whose merchants are princes, whose traffickers are the honourable of the earth?","9":"The Lord of hosts hath purposed it, to stain the pride of all glory, and to bring into contempt all the honourable of the earth.","10":"Pass through thy land as a river, O daughter of Tarshish: there is no more strength.","11":"He stretched out his hand over the sea, he shook the kingdoms: the Lord hath given a commandment against the merchant city, to destroy the strong holds thereof.","15":"And it shall come to pass in that day, that Tyre shall be forgotten seventy years, according to the days of one king: after the end of seventy years shall Tyre sing as an harlot.","17":"And it shall come to pass after the end of seventy years, that the Lord will visit Tyre, and she shall turn to her hire, and shall commit fornication with all the kingdoms of the world upon the face of the earth.","18":"And her merchandise and her hire shall be holiness to the Lord: it shall not be treasured nor laid up; for her merchandise shall be for them that dwell before the Lord, to eat sufficiently, and for durable clothing."}},
    "24": {"chapter":24,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: We have looked at quite a few cities in our last few chapters and the destruction that is impeding onto them quite quickly. Nothing seems to be letting up, and it seems like everyone is doomed. Honestly, they really all are doomed from the Lord's wrath and judgement. It will not be a fun or pretty time to live in these cities."},{"kind":"para","text":"In this chapter, we get what the look of the people will be during God's reign of judgement. It will seem as if the whole world has been put at a standstill, and there is no escaping for ANYONE. However, this is just a section of the world facing it during the time of Isaiah. Eventually (when Christ returns) the whole world WILL actually feel it."}],"previously":["We have examined quite a few cities in our last few chapters and the destruction that is impeding upon them quite quickly. Nothing seems to be letting up, and it appears as though everyone is doomed. Honestly, they really all are doomed from the Lord’s wrath and judgment. It will not be a fun or pretty time to live in these cities. In this chapter, we get a glimpse of what the people will look like during God’s reign of judgment. It will seem as if the whole world has been put at a standstill, and there is no escaping for anyone. However, this is just a section of the world facing it during the time of Isaiah. Eventually, when Christ returns, the whole world will actually feel it."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":6,"title":"The Curse Fulfilled","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"When the Lord is involved, it’s like a whirlwind of emotions. Sometimes things are empty, and sometimes things are full. It feels like you have everything, and then it feels like you are missing something. Usually, if it feels like you are missing something, you are probably only missing Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"Sometimes it feels like the world is spinning correctly, and sometimes it feels like the world is upside down. The Lord is the only one who can turn this world upside down."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And when they found them not, they drew Jason and certain brethren unto the rulers of the city, crying, These that have turned the world upside down are come hither also;","ref":"Acts 17:6"},{"kind":"para","text":"They did it by preaching the truth of God’s Word. Honestly, that is the only reason the world feels so upside down during Isaiah’s time as well. The truth was revealed, and everything seemed out of place. And now everyone will be scattered. Everyone will feel homeless. God does that to us still sometimes. Sometimes we feel out of place in our own churches and in our skin. We feel like this is not where we are supposed to be."},{"kind":"para","text":"There are two possible reasons for this. Either you are experiencing displacement because of your sin (like the Israelites are experiencing), or you are feeling displacement because of the leadership’s sin. Honestly, you really don’t belong. Your home is in Heaven, and you are just passing through this life. The church is supposed to be a glimpse of Heaven, but you are hard-pressed to find one that actually represents that."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Dearly beloved, I beseech you as strangers and pilgrims, abstain from fleshly lusts, which war against the soul;","ref":"1 Peter 2:11"},{"kind":"para","text":"This is a strange place to say the least. If you don’t feel like you belong, it’s because the Lord has made you feel that way. This place is not your home. To be with Him is where you belong."},{"kind":"para","text":"To the world, these things are catastrophic. It will make people feel like they are dying, and there is no escape from this pain. To the child of God, however, we know that He is paying attention to how we move."},{"kind":"para","text":"We might get hurt, and we might die, and we might feel confused, but we trust that God knows what He is doing and that He is doing it for a far greater reason than ourselves."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"scripture","text":"For there is no respect of persons with God.","ref":"Romans 2:11"},{"kind":"para","text":"Everyone will feel the same thing. Again, however, the people of God will know that it’s the Lord doing it, and the rest of the world will just be grasping at whatever they can, confused about what is going on. I’m glad the Lord doesn’t do anything without a warning. Everyone knows what will take place, but most won’t believe it. Honestly, it couldn’t be any more obvious in this world, but they will still have blind eyes to it."},{"kind":"para","text":"The people (that’s those without the Lord) will feel the judgment of God, and the priests (people OF the Lord) will feel the judgment of God. The servants (those that are weaker in society) will feel the judgment of God, and the masters (those that are bosses over them) will feel the judgments of God. The maid, the mistress, the buyer, the seller, the lender, the borrower, the taker, the giver, the lover, the hater, the Christian, the atheist, the deaf, the hearing, the blind and the seeing, the rich, the poor, the adult, the child—every single being on this entire planet will feel the world shift, and they will ALL be without excuse."},{"kind":"para","text":"They are feeling it in Israel at this time, and they will certainly feel it worldwide when the times come for Christ’s second coming. Everyone will be without excuse, yet they will try to make up all sorts of excuses as to why it isn’t the Lord doing it. During the end times, they will be blaming the Christians for everything. It’s not the Christians themselves that are doing it; it’s the God of those Christians. They will still preach the same gospel message, and they will still give the same love that people deserve, but people will be far more intolerant of it than they ever have been before. Until the Lord comes again, the message does not change."}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"From the sounds of the last few chapters, there will be quite a bit of land that will be completely useless for a time. Some of these places are still quite useless today. They are remnants of the people and the pieces, but that is only to prove that God did something. God’s thumbprint is everywhere on this Earth. It’s obvious in our recounts of history. Anyone who talks about history will have to trace back the Lord’s obvious hand in it, and if they don’t, then they are not a trustworthy source of accurate historical acuity."}]},{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"It will be pain, and misery, and everything will vanish."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And death and hell were cast into the lake of fire. This is the second death. And whosoever was not found written in the book of life was cast into the lake of fire.","ref":"Revelation 20:14-15"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And God shall wipe away all tears from their eyes; and there shall be no more death, neither sorrow, nor crying, neither shall there be any more pain: for the former things are passed away.","ref":"Revelation 21:4"},{"kind":"para","text":"If you love the things of this world, you will not have the things of this world very long. Be prepared to lose whatever it is that you hold so tightly in this world. The only thing you cannot lose while you are here on this Earth is your salvation, but that doesn’t even belong here. Salvation belongs in eternity, and that is why you can’t lose it. You don’t hold it; the Lord does."}]},{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"We are all sinners."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For all have sinned, and come short of the glory of God;","ref":"Romans 3:23"},{"kind":"para","text":"We have turned this Earth into what it is. I know our generation likes to point fingers at everyone else for the hurts and flaws of our world, but the fingers really should be pointed at ourselves. I blame me for the Earth falling apart. I blame me for God’s wrath abiding on us. I blame me for the judgments that are going to come. I blame me for how messed up and wicked our society is today. I blame me for the lack of compassion and care for others there is in this world."},{"kind":"para","text":"But I blame God for salvation. I blame God for a second chance. I blame God for genuine, sacrificial love. I blame God for all the good things that I get here on this Earth even though I am a sinner. I blame God for not giving up on me. I blame God for anything good that comes out of me and the good that I can do for other people. I blame God for making things right and putting the Earth the way it is."},{"kind":"para","text":"Honestly, I know the first verse says the Lord is the one that puts the Earth upside down, but I blame the sinful nature of humankind (my sinful nature) for putting the world the wrong way. When God puts the world upside down, it’s because He is making it all right. He is putting it back where it is supposed to be. Anyone that tries to place the blame of their own sinful nature on this lost and sinful world does not have a genuine relationship with the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"I am to blame, and so is every single other human being on this planet. We must point the fingers back at ourselves because we are the issue, and God is the solution."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"If we say that we have no sin, we deceive ourselves, and the truth is not in us.","ref":"1 John 1:8"}]},{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Isaiah only sees a “few men left” to be acceptable for the Earth still standing. Noah was the only one left who allowed human nature to continue forward. When Christ returns, however, there will be no men left… What a miserable thought. Everyone will turn away from the Lord, and there will be nothing left in this Earth to save. It will all be given over to the curse, and everyone will suffer the consequences of their sinful actions."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Israelites were under a double curse, honestly. They were under the curse of sin and the curse of God’s broken law. Moses tells them the curses they will receive if they turn from the Lord and follow other gods in Deuteronomy:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But it shall come to pass, if thou wilt not hearken unto the voice of the LORD thy God, to observe to do all his commandments and his statutes which I command thee this day; that all these curses shall come upon thee, and overtake thee: Cursed shalt thou be in the city, and cursed shalt thou be in the field. Cursed shall be thy basket and thy store. Cursed shall be the fruit of thy body, and the fruit of thy land, the increase of thy kine, and the flocks of thy sheep. Cursed shalt thou be when thou comest in, and cursed shalt thou be when thou goest out. The LORD shall send upon thee cursing, vexation, and rebuke, in all that thou settest thine hand unto for to do, until thou be destroyed, and until thou perish quickly; because of the wickedness of thy doings, whereby thou hast forsaken me. The LORD shall make the pestilence cleave unto thee, until he have consumed thee from off the land, whither thou goest to possess it. The LORD shall smite thee with a consumption, and with a fever, and with an inflammation, and with an extreme burning, and with the sword, and with blasting, and with mildew; and they shall pursue thee until thou perish. And thy heaven that is over thy head shall be brass, and the earth that is under thee shall be iron. The LORD shall make the rain of thy land powder and dust: from heaven shall it come down upon thee, until thou be destroyed. The LORD shall cause thee to be smitten before thine enemies: thou shalt go out one way against them, and flee seven ways before them: and shalt be removed into all the kingdoms of the earth. And thy carcase shall be meat unto all fowls of the air, and unto the beasts of the earth, and no man shall fray them away. The LORD will smite thee with the botch of Egypt, and with the emerods, and with the scab, and with the itch, whereof thou canst not be healed. The LORD shall smite thee with madness, and blindness, and astonishment of heart: And thou shalt grope at noonday, as the blind gropeth in darkness, and thou shalt not prosper in thy ways: and thou shalt be only oppressed and spoiled evermore, and no man shall save thee. Thou shalt betroth a wife, and another man shall lie with her: thou shalt build an house, and thou shalt not dwell therein: thou shalt plant a vineyard, and shalt not gather the grapes thereof. Thine ox shall be slain before thine eyes, and thou shalt not eat thereof: thine ass shall be violently taken away from before thy face, and shall not be restored to thee: thy sheep shall be given unto thine enemies, and thou shalt have none to rescue them. Thy sons and thy daughters shall be given unto another people, and thine eyes shall look, and fail with longing for them all the day long: and there shall be no might in thine hand. The fruit of thy land, and all thy labours, shall a nation which thou knowest not eat up; and thou shalt be only oppressed and crushed alway: So that thou shalt be mad for the sight of thine eyes which thou shalt see. The LORD shall smite thee in the knees, and in the legs, with a sore botch that cannot be healed, from the sole of thy foot unto the top of thy head. The LORD shall bring thee, and thy king which thou shalt set over thee, unto a nation which neither thou nor thy fathers have known; and there shalt thou serve other gods, wood and stone. And thou shalt become an astonishment, a proverb, and a byword, among all nations whither the LORD shall lead thee. Thou shalt carry much seed out into the field, and shalt gather but little in; for the locust shall consume it. Thou shalt plant vineyards, and dress them, but shalt neither drink of the wine, nor gather the grapes; for the worms shall eat them. Thou shalt have olive trees throughout all thy coasts, but thou shalt not anoint thyself with the oil; for thine olive shall cast his fruit. Thou shalt beget sons and daughters, but thou shalt not enjoy them; for they shall go into captivity. All thy trees and fruit of thy land shall the locust consume. The stranger that is within thee shall get up above thee very high; and thou shalt come down very low. He shall lend to thee, and thou shalt not lend to him: he shall be the head, and thou shalt be the tail. Moreover all these curses shall come upon thee, and shall pursue thee, and overtake thee, till thou be destroyed; because thou hearkenedst not unto the voice of the LORD thy God, to keep his commandments and his statutes which he commanded thee: And they shall be upon thee for a sign and for a wonder, and upon thy seed for ever. Because thou servedst not the LORD thy God with joyfulness, and with gladness of heart, for the abundance of all things; Therefore shalt thou serve thine enemies which the LORD shall send against thee, in hunger, and in thirst, and in nakedness, and in want of all things: and he shall put a yoke of iron upon thy neck, until he have destroyed thee. The LORD shall bring a nation against thee from far, from the end of the earth, as swift as the eagle flieth; a nation whose tongue thou shalt not understand; A nation of fierce countenance, which shall not regard the person of the old, nor shew favour to the young: And he shall eat the fruit of thy cattle, and the fruit of thy land, until thou be destroyed: which also shall not leave thee either corn, wine, or oil, or the increase of thy kine, or flocks of thy sheep, until he have destroyed thee. And he shall besiege thee in all thy gates, until thy high and fenced walls come down, wherein thou trustedst, throughout all thy land: and he shall besiege thee in all thy gates throughout all thy land, which the LORD thy God hath given thee. And thou shalt eat the fruit of thine own body, the flesh of thy sons and of thy daughters, which the LORD thy God hath given thee, in the siege, and in the straitness, wherewith thine enemies shall distress thee: So that the man that is tender among you, and very delicate, his eye shall be evil toward his brother, and toward the wife of his bosom, and toward the remnant of his children which he shall leave: So that he will not give to any of them of the flesh of his children whom he shall eat: because he hath nothing left him in the siege, and in the straitness, wherewith thine enemies shall distress thee in all thy gates. The tender and delicate woman among you, which would not adventure to set the sole of her foot upon the ground for delicateness and tenderness, her eye shall be evil toward the husband of her bosom, and toward her son, and toward her daughter, And toward her young one that cometh out from between her feet, and toward her children which she shall bear: for she shall eat them for want of all things secretly in the siege and straitness, wherewith thine enemy shall distress thee in thy gates. If thou wilt not observe to do all the words of this law that are written in this book, that thou mayest fear this glorious and fearful name, THE LORD THY GOD; Then the LORD will make thy plagues wonderful, and the plagues of thy seed, even great plagues, and of long continuance, and sore sicknesses, and of long continuance. Moreover he will bring upon thee all the diseases of Egypt, which thou wast afraid of; and they shall cleave unto thee. Also every sickness, and every plague, which is not written in the book of this law, them will the LORD bring upon thee, until thou be destroyed. And ye shall be left few in number, whereas ye were as the stars of heaven for multitude; because thou wouldest not obey the voice of the LORD thy God. And it shall come to pass, that as the LORD rejoiced over you to do you good, and to multiply you; so the LORD will rejoice over you to destroy you, and to bring you to nought; and ye shall be plucked from off the land whither thou goest to possess it. And the LORD shall scatter thee among all people, from the one end of the earth even unto the other; and there thou shalt serve other gods, which neither thou nor thy fathers have known, even wood and stone. And among these nations shalt thou find no ease, neither shall the sole of thy foot have rest: but the LORD shall give thee there a trembling heart, and failing of eyes, and sorrow of mind: And thy life shall hang in doubt before thee; and thou shalt fear day and night, and shalt have none assurance of thy life: In the morning thou shalt say, Would God it were even! and at even thou shalt say, Would God it were morning! for the fear of thine heart wherewith thou shalt fear, and for the sight of thine eyes which thou shalt see. And the LORD shall bring thee into Egypt again with ships, by the way whereof I spake unto thee, Thou shalt see it no more again: and there ye shall be sold unto your enemies for bondmen and bondwomen, and no man shall buy you.","ref":"Deuteronomy 28:15-68"},{"kind":"para","text":"If you take the time to read this section in Deuteronomy (I know it’s lengthy), you will find that all of these curses come to pass on the Israelites. Line this up with what Isaiah is telling them will happen, and compare it with 1 & 2 Kings or 1 & 2 Chronicles. They were depraved from this second curse. The whole earth will still feel these curses as well, but not because of the breaking of the law of God. We will feel it because we are literal enemies of God. We will have to accept these curses through the denial of Christ’s sacrifice for us. We have to forcefully deny Christ in order to receive these curses to ourselves. We will have to literally reject truth and want the curses if we are going to take them because that is the only way to get to them. Why anyone would want to be cursed is beyond me, but we live in a world of people who love to be cursed."}]}]},{"start":7,"end":16,"title":"Sudden Destruction","entries":[{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Most miserable people will turn to drugs or alcohol to make themselves feel better, but when the Lord intervenes, nothing will suffice. You can try to drown your sorrows in the finest wine, but it won’t matter in the end. Even if it makes you feel better for a moment, you will sober up quickly, and everything will be back to the same way it was before."}]},{"start":8,"end":9,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Music won’t help either. When I go through some trouble or am in a position of deep trial, I like to listen to music. Sometimes it’s soft music, other times it’s music that matches the emotions I am feeling. But when the Lord has shaken this Earth, nothing will soothe us. Music will not be enjoyable to us, and alcohol will not even taste right anymore. Everything will be off, and nothing will give us satisfaction. Honestly, these are all cheap substitutes for what only the Lord can provide for His people."},{"kind":"para","text":"The people of Israel will see it and regret their decisions leading them into captivity. The people of the world when Christ returns will see it and regret their decisions as well. The people of Israel will turn back to the Lord (as we will see later on). The people of the world when Christ returns will NEVER turn back to the Lord. They will be like the people of Tyre (from our last chapter). They will have nothing to come back to because they will not turn to God in trust and belief. The unbelievers in the day of Christ will have nothing to come back to because the whole Earth will be new, and there will not be a place for them. Christ’s kingdom is for Christ’s followers only. That’s the cold truth. However, you can have access to that kingdom right now if you turn to Him."}]},{"start":10,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Where is the city of confusion? Well, I could argue that it’s Los Angeles. Right now, there are quite a few fires taking place, and most of the beach homes are burned to nothing. A lot of people have been forced to evacuate their lives and homes outside of the city because there are five different fires burning. They are living in confusion because of the fires, but they also are living in confusion because of their rapid acceptance of sin. It’s legal to rob people in LA. It’s legal to rape people in LA. It’s legal to kidnap and do all sorts of heinous things to children. It’s legal to even kill children in LA. People don’t know what gender they are, and they don’t know how to control their emotions, or what spiritual warfare really looks like. To the people of LA, that life is normal, however, it’s a city of confusion, and one day it will be broken down."},{"kind":"para","text":"Obviously, Isaiah isn’t talking about LA here. LA wasn’t even a thing when Isaiah wrote this. “City” means “in general a city.” In other words, it can be speaking about all of the cities. It can be speaking about the whole world as one collective city. A city can be accumulated into one setting if everyone living in them acts and does the same things. We make jokes about it all the time when we are driving. Someone is driving slow? “Oh, they must be from Dallas.” Someone is driving fast? “Oh, they must be from LA.” Someone is driving erratically? “Oh, they must be from Florida.” But if everyone in the whole world was driving fast, we would accuse everyone of being from LA. So Isaiah is likely lumping the cities together from what I’m gathering."}]},{"start":11,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"They are crying, ultimately, for relief. They still aren’t crying for mercy from the Lord. They think that wine is what will bring them joy. They need something to tide them over. It won’t work. The joy of drinking is gone. It would have never been sufficient for them anyway."}]},{"start":12,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Whatever city Isaiah is talking about, the end result will be the same. He could very well be talking about LA here, and the results will eventually look like this. LA is quite the lost city. I pray the Lord provides mercy on them."}]},{"start":13,"end":15,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Interestingly enough, there were people standing over the ash of their homes in LA singing hymns to the Lord. Not many, but enough that it got some recognition on social media. Where else can they turn when they have lost everything?"},{"kind":"para","text":"In the same way, there will be plenty of chaos and destruction before Christ’s second coming, but there will be a small remnant that will glorify the Lord. But what is that to the masses that are antichrist?"}]},{"start":16,"end":16,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"They will sing after everything has been destroyed, but they will only sing on the rubble of what once was. They could have had it all if they were following the Lord. They could have kept their riches and had eternal life. But because they treated their material possessions as their salvation, they will only have that to lean on. Yet that will be burned away."},{"kind":"para","text":"Isaiah sees the destruction (even though he can hear the singing) and he is undone by it. He finds it to be miserable. It will be quick as well. Everything will seemingly be going well, and then suddenly… destruction and chaos."}]}]},{"start":17,"end":20,"title":"Fear, Pit, Snare","entries":[{"start":17,"end":17,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is what the Earth will face. They will face worldly fear."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"The fear of man bringeth a snare: but whoso putteth his trust in the LORD shall be safe.","ref":"Proverbs 29:25"},{"kind":"para","text":"The children of God do not experience the same kind of fear. We are not afraid of God’s wrath. We are not afraid of God’s judgment. We know that the Earth deserves it honestly."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For ye have not received the spirit of bondage again to fear; but ye have received the Spirit of adoption, whereby we cry, Abba, Father.","ref":"Romans 8:15"},{"kind":"para","text":"The world will also face “the pit,” which refers to Hell or Death. People will be concerned about it to the point of worry, but they won’t do anything to save themselves."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Let us swallow them up alive as the grave; and whole, as those that go down into the pit:","ref":"Proverbs 1:12"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And I saw an angel come down from heaven, having the key of the bottomless pit and a great chain in his hand.","ref":"Revelation 20:1"},{"kind":"para","text":"Everyone will face the grave eventually, but the children of God do not experience the same kind of pit. They die without certainty, but God’s children are very clear about what happens to them when they die."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And these shall go away into everlasting punishment: but the righteous into life eternal.","ref":"Matthew 25:46"},{"kind":"para","text":"Then they face a snare. This simply means they will be deceived. They will think what they are doing and the direction they are going in is the right one. In fact, they will claim that all roads lead to the same place, but that simply is not true."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Enter ye in at the strait gate: for wide is the gate, and broad is the way, that leadeth to destruction, and many there be which go in thereat:","ref":"Matthew 7:13"},{"kind":"para","text":"The way to destruction is broad. It’s actually quite easy to fall into the snare of Satan. However, the children of God won’t be deceived so easily."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Because strait is the gate, and narrow is the way, which leadeth unto life, and few there be that find it.","ref":"Matthew 7:14"},{"kind":"para","text":"Jesus is the focal point, and He is the entrance. Therefore, we know that if there is any other way into life other than through Christ, it’s a snare, a trap, and Satan is trying to deceive."},{"kind":"para","text":"During Isaiah’s time, it seems everyone was falling into the snare of Satan. They thought they were doing right by the Lord by keeping their traditions, but that is not what God wanted. He wanted their hearts, not just their actions. He wanted their love for Him alone, not just a sacrifice to keep Him occupied. They missed that because Satan gave them other gods to worship."}]},{"start":18,"end":18,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Fear will lead people to do stupid things because they aren’t thinking about what to do. When I was dating Eva, she had a small dog that was outside with us while we were on the hammock. Her sister came out with a bigger dog, and the little dog started yapping and messing with the big dog. The big dog finally had enough and bit the little dog, puncturing its neck. The little dog had a harness on, and there was blood literally pouring out of the hole. Everyone started freaking out and panicking (screaming and crying), and I took the dog and plugged the hole with my finger. The dog started puffing up like a balloon, so I asked them to take the harness off (because I was busy holding the blood in). After some continued hysterics, they finally listened to me and took the harness off, but by that point, the dog was puffed up so much that the collar almost needed to be cut. They finally got it off, and we took the dog to the vet to see what they could do."},{"kind":"para","text":"Fear of losing the dog was what made everyone panic. When they panicked, they didn’t know what to do but scramble and cry. A city in destruction will face the same things because no one is clearheaded. So they scramble, and they fall into a pit. They try to look for safety but can’t find anything and instead are tricked into something that is actually even worse for them. When they get out of the pit, they fall for the traps of Satan. Satan will act like their comforter, and he might do a decent job at providing shelter and comfort for them for a time. Eventually, however, he will lead them astray, and the Lord will destroy them with him. It’s all simply because they have rejected Christ and followed after Satan. It’s all because they wanted the curses… They regret their desires for them, but now it’s too late."}]},{"start":19,"end":20,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"To Isaiah and the people of Israel, the entire Earth feels completely destroyed and useless. Eventually, the whole Earth will literally be destroyed and rendered useless. God will have to create a new Earth."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And I saw a new heaven and a new earth: for the first heaven and the first earth were passed away; and there was no more sea.","ref":"Revelation 21:1"}]}]},{"start":21,"end":23,"title":"God's Throwdown","entries":[{"start":21,"end":21,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Honestly, a good portion of this Earth will get what they deserve because they think they are so special. The ones that are “high ones” are the ones that point their fingers at everyone else (as we talked about at the beginning of this chapter). They are the ones that think that all of this is everyone else’s fault. They will receive their reward for not taking responsibility for their own sins."},{"kind":"para","text":"The rulers of this Earth (those that are self-proclaimed “leaders”) will face the same fate because they have the same perspective as everyone else. They want to blame everyone under them instead of shouldering the blame. We have talked about the importance of leaders taking the blame for the faults of those under them, yet we are getting further and further away from genuine leadership every day in our world."},{"kind":"para","text":"Even in the church, we don’t see leaders being leaders. They are just big prideful babies, to put it kindly."}]},{"start":22,"end":22,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"They will be taken out of Hell for a short time. They will experience what is referred to as \"the second death.\""},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And death and hell were cast into the lake of fire. This is the second death.","ref":"Revelation 20:14"},{"kind":"para","text":"That can all be talked about deeper in Revelation. These people will never receive comfort again where they are going. That was what they chose, and that is what they will have. The only relief they will face is when they come before the Lord in judgment just before their second death."}]},{"start":23,"end":23,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The sun and moon will be changed during that time as well. Nothing will ever look the same. The Lord will shine forth for us, and it will be as evident as the sun or the moon is right now. We will see it and know."},{"kind":"para","text":"Yet, there are moon deniers in our day. There are people who honestly and truly believe that the moon doesn’t actually exist. They think it’s a projection that the government has somehow placed in the sky. They are probably believers in a flat earth as well. Those same people would be hard-pressed to believe that the Lord’s judgment was being poured out when it comes to pass. They will be judgment deniers as well as moon deniers. They are God deniers honestly."},{"kind":"para","text":"God will reign, though, and it won’t be any more obvious than at that time. His judgments will be obvious, and His reign will be obvious."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":9},{"start":10,"end":10},{"start":11,"end":11},{"start":12,"end":12},{"start":13,"end":15},{"start":16,"end":16},{"start":17,"end":17},{"start":18,"end":18},{"start":19,"end":20},{"start":21,"end":21},{"start":22,"end":22},{"start":23,"end":23}],"verses":{"1":"Behold, the Lord maketh the earth empty, and maketh it waste, and turneth it upside down, and scattereth abroad the inhabitants thereof.","2":"And it shall be, as with the people, so with the priest; as with the servant, so with his master; as with the maid, so with her mistress; as with the buyer, so with the seller; as with the lender, so with the borrower; as with the taker of usury, so with the giver of usury to him.","3":"The land shall be utterly emptied, and utterly spoiled: for the Lord hath spoken this word.","4":"The earth mourneth and fadeth away, the world languisheth and fadeth away, the haughty people of the earth do languish.","5":"The earth also is defiled under the inhabitants thereof; because they have transgressed the laws, changed the ordinance, broken the everlasting covenant.","6":"Therefore hath the curse devoured the earth, and they that dwell therein are desolate: therefore the inhabitants of the earth are burned, and few men left.","7":"The new wine mourneth, the vine languisheth, all the merryhearted do sigh.","8":"The mirth of tabrets ceaseth, the noise of them that rejoice endeth, the joy of the harp ceaseth.","9":"They shall not drink wine with a song; strong drink shall be bitter to them that drink it.","10":"The city of confusion is broken down: every house is shut up, that no man may come in.","11":"There is a crying for wine in the streets; all joy is darkened, the mirth of the land is gone.","12":"In the city is left desolation, and the gate is smitten with destruction.","13":"When thus it shall be in the midst of the land among the people, there shall be as the shaking of an olive tree, and as the gleaning grapes when the vintage is done.","14":"They shall lift up their voice, they shall sing for the majesty of the Lord, they shall cry aloud from the sea.","15":"Wherefore glorify ye the Lord in the fires, even the name of the Lord God of Israel in the isles of the sea.","16":"From the uttermost part of the earth have we heard songs, even glory to the righteous. But I said, My leanness, my leanness, woe unto me! the treacherous dealers have dealt treacherously; yea, the treacherous dealers have dealt very treacherously.","17":"Fear, and the pit, and the snare, are upon thee, O inhabitant of the earth.","18":"And it shall come to pass, that he who fleeth from the noise of the fear shall fall into the pit; and he that cometh up out of the midst of the pit shall be taken in the snare: for the windows from on high are open, and the foundations of the earth do shake.","19":"The earth is utterly broken down, the earth is clean dissolved, the earth is moved exceedingly.","20":"The earth shall reel to and fro like a drunkard, and shall be removed like a cottage; and the transgression thereof shall be heavy upon it; and it shall fall, and not rise again.","21":"And it shall come to pass in that day, that the Lord shall punish the host of the high ones that are on high, and the kings of the earth upon the earth.","22":"And they shall be gathered together, as prisoners are gathered in the pit, and shall be shut up in the prison, and after many days shall they be visited.","23":"Then the moon shall be confounded, and the sun ashamed, when the Lord of hosts shall reign in mount Zion, and in Jerusalem, and before his ancients gloriously."}},
    "25": {"chapter":25,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: In our last few chapters we have gotten nothing but judgement after judgement, and pain after pain. It seems as if the Lord is completely done with His people. These people are so far away from the Lord that there is no turning them around. I believe the Lord has tried everything He can to get them to turn, yet they just simply won't listen. They are too attracted to their sin to turn back now. So the Lord let's them have what they want, and it's never worth it in the end."},{"kind":"para","text":"In this chapter, we finally get some good news. We get a bit of a break from doom and gloom and get to read about the praises of God's goodness through all of this. That is what we must remember by the way. We must remember that God is doing this because He is good and He is serving justice. It might not seem good to the people it is happening to, but it is certainly for a good reason that God is choosing them to place these burdens. They must turn to the Lord, and now they will have no choice but to turn back to God, or perish in their choice against Him."}],"previously":["In our last few chapters, we have encountered nothing but judgment after judgment and pain after pain. It seems as if the Lord is completely done with His people. These people are so far away from the Lord that there is no turning them around. I believe the Lord has tried everything He can to get them to turn, yet they simply won’t listen. They are too attracted to their sin to turn back now. So the Lord lets them have what they want, and it’s never worth it in the end. In this chapter, we finally get some good news. We get a bit of a break from doom and gloom and get to read about the praises of God’s goodness through all of this. That is what we must remember, by the way. We must remember that God is doing this because He is good and He is serving justice. It might not seem good to the people it is happening to, but it is certainly for a good reason that God is choosing them to place these burdens. They must turn to the Lord, and now they will have no choice but to turn back to God, or perish in their choice against Him."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":5,"title":"The Lord Exalted","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"We finally get some alleviation from the judgment here. I’m assuming this is a prayer or song of praise from Isaiah. He is exalting the Lord and praising Him, even after all the judgments and condemnations that he had just witnessed on all the nations he knows and loves."},{"kind":"para","text":"He can praise the Lord through the burdens only because he personally knows that God is always right. Even if the whole world thinks it’s wrong, God’s ways are always right. God is faithful and true no matter what. You can accuse God of a great deal of things, but nothing is more true than the fact that God is always going to make things right in this world, especially because everyone does the wrong things."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"It’s not about the power the Lord has to do it that we should be astounded by. It’s by the reason He has to do it. We live in a world where justice is not served. Every day, there are people being blamed for things they did not do, and guilt is pinned on them to try and make it right. Except, how can an innocent person make a wrong (that they didn’t commit) right? They would be hard-pressed to do it."},{"kind":"para","text":"The church is supposed to be a safe place for people like that to go. They are supposed to be able to go there and praise God for what He has done, and the people in the church are supposed to encourage and help that individual. That is not how the church is today, however, and most of these innocent people get swept into the back and forgotten about. How miserable the church is today."},{"kind":"para","text":"Brothers and sisters in Christ, we must notice the hurts of others. We must notice what they are going through. They need a people who can rally around them and encourage them. It is a shame on us when we can’t do that. Isaiah, no doubt, felt very much alone during his time of prophecying. I’m sure he had friends. Maybe that was the few good men he spoke about in the last chapter? They were just his friends. Or maybe they were just random people living in the land, I don’t know."},{"kind":"para","text":"It will seem, however, that Isaiah is the only one standing here at the end and praising Him. The first verse says, “thou art MY God;” and “I will exalt thee” and “I will praise thee.” He is praising God alone for the justice that is served here. It’s not even because these other people are upset with the Lord. Honestly, it’s because these other people STILL haven’t turned to God. It will take some time for them to finally turn back."}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There are a few theories based on this verse about what Isaiah is really talking about. One group believes that this is referring to a worldwide conversion to the Lord. There will be a large turning after the destruction. I don’t hold to that theory, but to each their own."},{"kind":"para","text":"Then there are people who say that this joy will be present during the kingdom reign of the Lord. That certainly can be the case; we know that there are going to be quite a few “terrible nations” still living during the reign of Christ according to Revelation."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And when the thousand years are expired, Satan shall be loosed out of his prison, And shall go out to deceive the nations which are in the four quarters of the earth, Gog and Magog, to gather them together to battle: the number of whom is as the sand of the sea. And they went up on the breadth of the earth, and compassed the camp of the saints about, and the beloved city: and fire came down from God out of heaven, and devoured them. And the devil that deceived them was cast into the lake of fire and brimstone, where the beast and the false prophet are, and shall be tormented day and night for ever and ever.","ref":"Revelation 20:7-10"},{"kind":"para","text":"Satan will gather the remaining evil people in the world, and God will deal with them all at once in one location. This can also be talking about the literal joy of the strong people (those that were able to take over these nations) and the literal fear of the terrible nations (those that took over these nations). This could very well be talking about Babylon, Assyria, and their confederates."},{"kind":"para","text":"God will certainly get their attention, but they won’t actually turn to God. Though Babylon is up in the air at a certain point in Daniel, it really seems as if these people turn for a time. Obviously, it doesn’t last forever…"}]},{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Some people believe in a post-tribulation rapture. I’m still on the fence about it. I have a lot of information stating we won’t be raptured until after the tribulation, but I also have quite a lot of information about how we will be raptured before. We can talk more about that in Revelation, but this verse does make it seem as if it were post-tribulation. However, I know for certain there will be people still being saved during the tribulation as well, so this verse could just be talking about those that are left behind during that time. They will have protection from what God pours out. They won’t have protection really from the world (the world will hate them), but the Lord will protect them from anything He means for the unrighteous."},{"kind":"para","text":"God is the strength of the Christian; He is our refuge and shadow. He provides for us even when the whole world is falling apart. While everyone else is in panic mode, we have a reason to praise Him."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Let them praise thy great and terrible name; for it is holy.","ref":"Psalm 99:3"}]},{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God is the only one who can destroy the higher powers of this Earth. A friend was asking about this verse the other day in Job:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"He is the chief of the ways of God: he that made him can make his sword to approach unto him.","ref":"Job 40:19"},{"kind":"para","text":"Whatever the behemoth is in these verses must have been pretty strong and mighty. Whatever it was, the only one that could put a stop to him was the Lord. We, during that time—the time of Genesis and Abraham—would have never had the ability to put that beast down, so we would have had to rely on the Lord. God Himself says that He was the one who could bring it down."},{"kind":"para","text":"God can take down the strongest and cruelest rulers in this world without a second thought. He can destroy them quickly and easily. If there is evil ruling in our leadership today, it is because the Lord has put them there for something. We will see their downfall in due time. The Lord will serve justice. Period."}]}]},{"start":6,"end":8,"title":"A Fat Feast","entries":[{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There will be a feast of some sort. We are told there is a feast in the last days as well:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And I heard as it were the voice of a great multitude, and as the voice of many waters, and as the voice of mighty thunderings, saying, Alleluia: for the Lord God omnipotent reigneth. Let us be glad and rejoice, and give honour to him: for the marriage of the Lamb is come, and his wife hath made herself ready. And to her was granted that she should be arrayed in fine linen, clean and white: for the fine linen is the righteousness of saints. And he saith unto me, Write, Blessed are they which are called unto the marriage supper of the Lamb. And he saith unto me, These are the true sayings of God.","ref":"Revelation 19:6-9"},{"kind":"para","text":"Isaiah speaks literally about the Israelites being brought back and provided for from this land, but it also foreshadows future judgment. We can also link this to Christ, as during His time, the Lord fed the people multiple times. He fed 5,000 people and 4,000 people on two separate occasions. However, the Last Supper of the Lord seems to better suit this specific verse, as well as the marriage supper. Although they might have had small provisions during that supper, it certainly meant great things to the disciples who were eating with Him. To them, it was like feasting on fat things. It was not just a supper; it was a feast. Every time we have communion, it should feel the same to us. Because of what the Lord did, that little cracker and that little juice should feel like a feast because He is so good. His sacrifice was not something small, mind you. It is a big deal to those who believe. Even to those who don’t believe, but they don’t understand how it can be a big deal. They don’t know what it’s like to be forgiven for their sins. Of course, to them, communion is just snack time at the church. Even to religionists, because they don’t understand the scope and depth that Christ’s sacrifice brings. It’s a fat feast for us who believe. Praise the Lord!"}]},{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There is a veil over us today. We are all separated from the Lord in presence. We cannot come into His presence until we are completely clean from sin."},{"kind":"para","text":"There’s a veil over this Earth, and the reason it exists is because of our sins. Once the Lord has finished His course, that veil will be removed, and we will have full access to the presence and comfort of God Almighty. What a glorious blessing we will get to behold."}]},{"start":8,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There's a few verses that should come to mind right here. Paul says that God swallows death up in victory through the cross of Christ!"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"So when this corruptible shall have put on incorruption, and this mortal shall have put on immortality, then shall be brought to pass the saying that is written, Death is swallowed up in victory.","ref":"1 Corinthians 15:54"},{"kind":"para","text":"John says that God will wipe away every tear in Revelation:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And God shall wipe away all tears from their eyes; and there shall be no more death, neither sorrow, nor crying, neither shall there be any more pain: for the former things are passed away.","ref":"Revelation 21:4"},{"kind":"para","text":"He says that His people will stop being mistreated. During the end times, the Christians (those who have turned to the Lord during the tribulation) will be the most mistreated group in the entire world. Once they endure, the Lord will remove the rebuke from His people. He will give victory over death, over pain, and over opposition. We are planted to win!"}]}]},{"start":9,"end":12,"title":"Destruction of Religion","entries":[{"start":9,"end":9,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"He has saved us. When we know Christ, we know the Lord’s salvation. Any saving that God does after that is just extended grace. To have God’s salvation is really the only reason we have to rejoice and be glad in Him. There’s nothing else in this life and world that can triumph over that. Disneyland might be a close second, but I would give it up in a heartbeat to have the Lord’s salvation."}]},{"start":10,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"For some reason, Isaiah wanted to pick on Moab here. Why Moab? Well, I honestly don’t know. I don’t see any commentaries really addressing why he chose Moab to pick on. I assume that Moab was like the Heathen believers. They were people who had a belief in God, but they didn’t have a relationship with Him. We talked about it a bit during the burden of Moab a few chapters back. I think that Moab was a very religious nation, but they didn’t have a relationship with the Lord. They didn’t understand what that meant. They thought of God as a judge that we must keep at arm’s length by doing good works. If we go to church on Sundays and give to the poor, then the Lord will be happy, and I can do anything else I want for the rest of the week. That is not how the Lord works, though. He has never worked like that since the beginning of time. I don’t know where religions get this so mixed up. All religions have that one thing in common. They all believe they have to work for their salvation. God doesn’t want that, and just like the Moabites who work for their salvation, those who believe in works righteousness in the end will be completely gotten rid of and “trodden down.”"}]},{"start":11,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God will get rid of the religionists in that day. The fake worshippers and the false worshippers will be gone. There is a difference between fake worshippers and false worshippers. Fake worshippers pretend like they belong to their religion. They do the things that everyone else does to just fit in. They are like Judas. False worshippers truly believe they are worshipping the Lord correctly. They have been taught and told how to do it by their church, so they stick to those methods. However, Scripture rebuts them. False worshippers are like the Pharisees. They have the idea of God correct, but they have not given themselves over to the Lord. They have a religion and not a relationship. The Lord has been looking to be with His people since the beginning of Scripture:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And I will walk among you, and will be your God, and ye shall be my people.","ref":"Leviticus 26:12"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And I will give them an heart to know me, that I am the LORD: and they shall be my people, and I will be their God: for they shall return unto me with their whole heart.","ref":"Jeremiah 24:7"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"My tabernacle also shall be with them: yea, I will be their God, and they shall be my people.","ref":"Ezekiel 37:27"},{"kind":"para","text":"And that will be His mission until the very last day."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And I heard a great voice out of heaven saying, Behold, the tabernacle of God is with men, and he will dwell with them, and they shall be his people, and God himself shall be with them, and be their God.","ref":"Revelation 21:3"},{"kind":"para","text":"God has been wanting to spend quality time with you since the beginning of time. He has done whatever He possibly can to get you to turn to Him and realize that. Our payment to Him, however, is good works and traditional deeds set forth by our religions that we personally made up."},{"kind":"para","text":"He doesn’t want religion. He doesn’t care if you’re Catholic or Baptist. He wants a relationship with you."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And Samuel said, Hath the LORD as great delight in burnt offerings and sacrifices, as in obeying the voice of the LORD? Behold, to obey is better than sacrifice, and to hearken than the fat of rams.","ref":"1 Samuel 15:22"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Behold, I stand at the door, and knock: if any man hear my voice, and open the door, I will come in to him, and will sup with him, and he with me.","ref":"Revelation 3:20"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And this is the will of him that sent me, that every one which seeth the Son, and believeth on him, may have everlasting life: and I will raise him up at the last day.","ref":"John 6:40"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Jesus saith unto him, I am the way, the truth, and the life: no man cometh unto the Father, but by me.","ref":"John 14:6"},{"kind":"para","text":"He has given us access, but we must come to Jesus Christ to get it. He wants us to come to Him the scriptural way, not the religious way. If you have to join a church to come to God, you have not been saved; you have been tricked. The church should do nothing more than teach you about what scripture says in your relationship with the Lord. That alone is the job of the church. Anything else—sacraments, works, sacrifices, candles, incense, or any other weird tradition the churches use today—is a facade for true worship, which is only found in literally spending time with God, loving Him to the fullest, and following what His Word alone tells us."},{"kind":"para","text":"It doesn’t tell us to do any of those things. It tells the Levites to do them, but we are not Levitical priests. In fact, I don’t believe there is a single Levite still doing these things today. Why? Well, because it’s useless now. Jesus Christ came and finished the law, and the works of Levitical priests would be rejecting that completed work. If your church does lawful things, they have rejected Christ; that’s just me being honest. They are serving the law of God, not the love of God. They have missed Christ’s sacrifice. That is why God will do away with them. He will bring them to nothing, and He has every right to. They are denying His greatest gift of all time."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":9},{"start":10,"end":10},{"start":11,"end":12}],"verses":{"1":"O Lord, thou art my God; I will exalt thee, I will praise thy name; for thou hast done wonderful things; thy counsels of old are faithfulness and truth.","2":"For thou hast made of a city an heap; of a defenced city a ruin: a palace of strangers to be no city; it shall never be built.","3":"Therefore shall the strong people glorify thee, the city of the terrible nations shall fear thee.","4":"For thou hast been a strength to the poor, a strength to the needy in his distress, a refuge from the storm, a shadow from the heat, when the blast of the terrible ones is as a storm against the wall.","5":"Thou shalt bring down the noise of strangers, as the heat in a dry place; even the heat with the shadow of a cloud: the branch of the terrible ones shall be brought low.","6":"And in this mountain shall the Lord of hosts make unto all people a feast of fat things, a feast of wines on the lees, of fat things full of marrow, of wines on the lees well refined.","7":"And he will destroy in this mountain the face of the covering cast over all people, and the vail that is spread over all nations.","8":"He will swallow up death in victory; and the Lord God will wipe away tears from off all faces; and the rebuke of his people shall he take away from off all the earth: for the Lord hath spoken it.","9":"And it shall be said in that day, Lo, this is our God; we have waited for him, and he will save us: this is the Lord; we have waited for him, we will be glad and rejoice in his salvation.","10":"For in this mountain shall the hand of the Lord rest, and Moab shall be trodden down under him, even as straw is trodden down for the dunghill.","11":"And he shall spread forth his hands in the midst of them, as he that swimmeth spreadeth forth his hands to swim: and he shall bring down their pride together with the spoils of their hands.","12":"And the fortress of the high fort of thy walls shall he bring down, lay low, and bring to the ground, even to the dust."}},
    "26": {"chapter":26,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: In our last chapter, we got a little break from the punishments and judgements of the Lord to read a song written by Isaiah. He is pleased to stand in the victory of the Lord, and there seems to be a small remenant still standing with him."},{"kind":"para","text":"In this chapter, Isaiah continues his song for the Lord, focusing on God's power, justice, and protection for His children during a time when the whole Earthy will seemingly be put to the test. That is God's ultimate purpose for pouring out His wrath. He is testing the Earth, and most people will fail the test because they don't have the answer (which is only found in Christ alone)."}],"previously":["In our last chapter, we took a break from the punishments and judgments of the Lord to read a song written by Isaiah. He is pleased to stand in the victory of the Lord, and there seems to be a small remnant still standing with him. In this chapter, Isaiah continues his song for the Lord, focusing on God’s power, justice, and protection for His children during a time when the whole Earth will seemingly be put to the test. That is God’s ultimate purpose for pouring out His wrath. He is testing the Earth, and most people will fail the test because they don’t have the answer (which is only found in Christ alone)."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":6,"title":"The Power of God","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"According to Revelation, there will be quite a few songs that the saints of God are going to be singing during \"that day\"."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And they sung as it were a new song before the throne, and before the four beasts, and the elders: and no man could learn that song but the hundred and forty and four thousand, which were redeemed from the earth.","ref":"Revelation 14:3"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And I beheld, and I heard the voice of many angels round about the throne and the beasts and the elders: and the number of them was ten thousand times ten thousand, and thousands of thousands;","ref":"Revelation 5:11"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And they sing the song of Moses the servant of God, and the song of the Lamb, saying, Great and marvellous are thy works, Lord God Almighty; just and true are thy ways, thou King of saints.","ref":"Revelation 15:3"},{"kind":"para","text":"It would seem as if every time God made any sort of movement, the Heavens find reason to sing. Something about God proving Himself brings His children praise. Salvation is a good reason to sing amen, isn’t it? We are protected by it, like walls and bulwarks protect a city. Our strong city is in the Lord alone."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"The rich man's wealth is his strong city: the destruction of the poor is their poverty.","ref":"Proverbs 10:15"}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"You know how you get to Heaven? It’s not through good works. It’s not through church ordinances. It’s not even through asking really hard. It’s about believing the truth and keeping Him."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Jesus saith unto him, I am the way, the truth, and the life: no man cometh unto the Father, but by me.","ref":"John 14:6"},{"kind":"para","text":"Maybe if we repeat this verse enough times, it will be so ingrained in our brains that we will know for certain that Jesus is the only way. That is my hope for this world, anyway. I want this whole world to have no excuse to be confused about how to get to Heaven."},{"kind":"para","text":"Jesus is the only way. If you can’t go to Jesus, you can’t go to Heaven. Period. He is the truth, and we must keep Him if we want access to the Father of all creation."}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is an interesting verse. I don’t feel a lot of peace on this Earth. I feel a lot of discomfort, especially as of late. I feel hurt and betrayed by many people. Often, I feel hurt and betrayed by the Lord Himself. I feel like He could be proving justice a lot more to the people who are mistreating me. But that, of course, is not up to me."},{"kind":"para","text":"Yet, Isaiah seems to think that those who keep their minds focused on the Lord will find peace. Certainly, that is a common theme of scripture:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Now the Lord of peace himself give you peace always by all means. The Lord be with you all.","ref":"2 Thessalonians 3:16"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"These things I have spoken unto you, that in me ye might have peace. In the world ye shall have tribulation: but be of good cheer; I have overcome the world.","ref":"John 16:33"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Now the God of hope fill you with all joy and peace in believing, that ye may abound in hope, through the power of the Holy Ghost.","ref":"Romans 15:13"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Follow peace with all men, and holiness, without which no man shall see the Lord:","ref":"Hebrews 12:14"},{"kind":"para","text":"I could go on, but the point is that true peace in this world is always tied to the Lord. If you don’t have the Lord, and especially Jesus Christ, you will not have real lasting peace. We must keep our minds on Him if we want peace. He will provide it in time if we are focused on Him and waiting on Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"I hate waiting, though. I’m sure you do too. But the Lord is always going to make the right decisions at the right time, and so we must respect His choices and anticipate His goodness in His time."}]},{"start":4,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Strength doesn’t belong to us. We don’t know what to do with power. When we get power, we abuse it. People who abuse power don’t even know they are doing so. They try to assume they are doing the right thing for the right reasons, but really it’s always for selfish gain. Ask your local politician if power is important to them, and they will tell you no. Yet they abuse their power to get their way all the time. They say they are doing it for a good reason, but it’s never actually benefiting anyone but themselves. Even in the church, sadly, I can pick on the church because I’m a part of it. We should be standing up against things that are wrong. God may have given your pastor power to do a lot of heinous things towards his followers, but God has also given every individual Christian the power to combat wrongdoing in the church. Sadly, most Christians don’t use their power to do that. We exercise meekness while the leaders abuse their power. Genuine children of God usually allow the Lord to bring justice. According to Isaiah, that is exactly what God will do in the end anyway."}]},{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"When God is done with the prideful, the people that will be walking on the ruins will be the humble. Those that have stayed the course and have kept in meekness will stand victorious. Right now, we are beaten down and forced to sit or kneel before the powers that be, but God will lift us up in the end."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Humble yourselves in the sight of the Lord, and he shall lift you up.","ref":"James 4:10"},{"kind":"para","text":"The world has a lot of power to push you down, but God has more power to keep you from staying down."}]}]},{"start":7,"end":10,"title":"Learning Righteousness","entries":[{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"We only have anything just or upright because the Lord is just and upright. If we think we have anything in ourselves that makes us good without God, we are lying to ourselves. Our goodness is dismal compared to what God says is good. We are inclined to think a stick in the mud is something good. The just are given their uprightness by the Lord. God is our goodness."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Every good gift and every perfect gift is from above, and cometh down from the Father of lights, with whom is no variableness, neither shadow of turning.","ref":"James 1:17"},{"kind":"para","text":"Again, the Lord will keep His children standing. I have no doubt that at the end of my life, I will be affirmed and fixed on God’s good graces. He will keep me standing in the end. I don’t feel like (at this moment in my life) I am standing. I feel like I’ve been shoved on the ground and spit on and run over a few times by this world (spiritually speaking), and it’s very difficult to continue to trek through this life most days. But I know that when I come to the end of my life, I will see what God has done, and I will be standing affirmative on His promises and on His leading."}]},{"start":8,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Without God’s judgment, we would never see justice for evil in this world. We don’t know how to serve justice without God. We would accuse innocent people all the time (we still do this), but the Lord has the right to put you in your place for making bad judgments. He allows us to judge, but we usually don’t judge correctly. We make absolute unrighteous judgments."},{"kind":"para","text":"So, because we make terrible judgments, we should want the Lord to judge, because He can ONLY make the righteous judgments we need. We need a balance in this Earth. Someday (before the Lord’s coming), it will seem like there is no balance. It will seem as if evil has completely reigned and won. However, those that are under the righteousness of God will stand on the rubble of evil, and we will be able to say, “O Lord, we waited for thee…” We will be able to look back and say, “I’m glad God had me wait.” The waiting seems painful right now, but the victory will be all the more sweeter because we waited."}]},{"start":9,"end":9,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"We should be searching for the Lord with everything in us. We must remember that Isaiah is writing this during a time of great turmoil in Israel. They are being taken from their homes, robbed of their freedoms and comforts, and completely ruined by the nations around them. They will not be coming back home for quite some time. Yet Isaiah finds reason to sing. Why? Well, he has no other choice but to seek out the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"With my very soul, I have sought out God in the night. There have been so many times when I have stayed up worrying about one thing or another, and the only place I have to go with these problems is to the Lord. When we go to Him with our whole soul, we will find rest in His direction and care. When we use our spirits to seek God right in the beginning of the day, we are doing whatever it takes to ensure His presence is with us. We should not want to move a muscle without the Lord’s presence. Yet, most of us go throughout our days without a care for God’s deliverance or direction on our lives."},{"kind":"para","text":"The part I find interesting about this verse, however, is the justification for God’s judgment. Some people have a hard time understanding how a loving God can judge the world and destroy it. A loving God can do that because we are not living in His love. He can do that because we are evil people. He will teach us (only through judgment) how to be righteous. He will show us what righteousness looks like. Righteousness to evil people is like a lamp that’s lit up in a dark room."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And the light shineth in darkness; and the darkness comprehended it not.","ref":"John 1:5"},{"kind":"para","text":"God's judgement makes us learn (quickly at that) how important righteousness should be to us."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Was then that which is good made death unto me? God forbid. But sin, that it might appear sin, working death in me by that which is good; that sin by the commandment might become exceeding sinful.","ref":"Romans 7:13"},{"kind":"para","text":"How serious is sin to us? How lightly do we take our evil ways? We might not call sin “sin,” and that is why judgment falls on us. We must treat sin as “exceedingly sinful” if we are going to learn the ways of righteousness and walk in the path of God’s grace. Otherwise, we are faced with God’s judgment, and we learn nothing but wrath and pain."}]},{"start":10,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The wicked of this world are always recognized. They like to be the center of attention, in all honesty. There are many preachers who desire the spotlight behind the pulpit. They think they are something special. That is their reward, though. That is all the favor they are going to get, because the Lord will not give them favor. The world will provide them with gifts and rewards, but the Lord will give them judgment. They cannot learn righteousness in their lives. Those who look to shine light on themselves are those who will not “behold the majesty of the Lord.” God will certainly give them attention, but it won’t be the attention they were hoping for. Let the wicked raise the wicked."},{"kind":"para","text":"The people of God must be content flying under the radar and waiting for the Lord to reward them. Perhaps that should be our new saying. Whenever there is a competition in our church (or in our work, or whatever it is that there shouldn’t be a competition in), we can be content to just say, “Let the wicked raise the wicked.”"}]}]},{"start":11,"end":15,"title":"Select Sheep","entries":[{"start":11,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Wicked people don’t pay attention to what the Lord is doing because they are too concerned about what other people are doing. They focus on their competition and don’t want to be dethroned from their positions. Little do they know that they don’t have any power above the Lord. In the end, their positions will be given to another person, who will likely squander it all. If we are going to set anything up for future generations, it should be the knowledge of coming to know the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"I think there are a lot of preachers today who are “called” to preach simply because their father or grandad was a preacher. They aren’t really called by the Lord, but they don’t know what else to do with their lives and feel like they are letting their families down if they don’t follow the same line of business. Honestly, that is all it is to them. It’s all just business. Lives of people… just business. Compassion for people… just business. Souls of people… just business. Ministering to people… just business. Pastors are businessmen today. They are not caring ministers who are looking to pour something into your life without a payment of some sort in return. They do it for filthy lucre."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Feed the flock of God which is among you, taking the oversight thereof, not by constraint, but willingly; not for filthy lucre, but of a ready mind;","ref":"1 Peter 5:2"},{"kind":"para","text":"They do it because they think that God wants them to do it, not because God has given them a heart to do it. That is their position, so therefore they have to do it. How ill-prepared they are when it comes to souls. How little you must think of people to treat them only as a business transaction and let them go. As long as we can keep their butts in their seats, we are satisfied with a simple “meeting” and a “I’m praying for you.” That’s not a relationship."},{"kind":"para","text":"A relationship (at least between brothers of the faith) should be more than just a “I’m praying for you.” Great. I’m glad you are praying for me. I don’t feel it though. I’ve made it a top ministry of mine to not just say I’m praying for someone. Rather, I go out of my way and visit them and pray WITH them. That is how you develop real relationships in ministry. You can’t minister to someone’s needs through a text or a phone call. You can minister to them through a quick lunch and a few words. No, we must go to where they live if we want to minister to people properly."}]},{"start":12,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"If the Lord doesn’t put the work in you, you will be doing evil works. I think a lot of people in church leadership are not doing what the Lord has put in them. They are doing what they have been trained and taught by their colleges. They are doing what their fathers and grandfathers did because it worked so well for them. We are not them, however, and the Lord has a different means of using you than He did for your fathers. If He wanted to just use you the same way, He would have let your fathers live longer and continued to use them. Why would He need you when He has the perfect specimen in your superiors? Perhaps your fathers were born in the wrong generations. They should have been born in YOUR generation so they can do their methods where YOU are supposed to be."},{"kind":"para","text":"I think a lot of pastors don’t have peace because they are trying to please the wrong people. They want to live up to the expectations of their mentors, not by the call and will of the Lord. The Lord tells you to do something, and the first instinct is to say, “Will pastor so-and-so do it that way?” We should not care how God is using other pastors in their churches when we are called to follow the Lord in our own. Ministry, however, is just one big competition, and that’s only because the Lord has not “wrought his works” in us. We have put our own desires in ourselves and have rejected the calling of the Lord by and large."}]},{"start":13,"end":13,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"If you read in 1 Samuel, you can tell that Samuel was not pleased with the idea of the people requesting a king. He didn’t want them to have a king because they were supposed to follow the Lord alone. Now that we are at this point in the history of Israel, we find out that Samuel had a right to be upset about this idea. These kings have led them into terrible circumstances, and they have no home to go to anymore."},{"kind":"para","text":"The king’s job, however, was to keep his focus on the Lord and be led by Him alone. That is not what happened. It didn’t happen like that because they are spoiled. Everything had been handed down to them, and so they abused their liberty as a cloak of maliciousness."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"As free, and not using your liberty for a cloke of maliciousness, but as the servants of God.","ref":"1 Peter 2:16"},{"kind":"para","text":"Leaders in the church have abused this same liberty. They have inherited their stance from a very wealthy church and now misuse the honor and privilege given to them through the hard work of their forefathers. They become prideful and arrogant, misusing their power, as we pointed out earlier. We can no longer rely on our leaders. You’d be hard-pressed to even trust the pastors in most churches today. That is just the sad truth. I’d say a good portion of pastors will abuse their position and power to protect the people they think deserve it the most. They want to protect some sheep—select sheep. The rest of the sheep can be thrown to the wolves if you are not worthy enough in their eyes."},{"kind":"para","text":"The only leadership that matters is the leadership of the Lord. Individually, we must follow Him. A pastor will ask you to follow him as he follows God, but the truth is, we don’t see pastors following God today. They lord over us and act as righteous kings, but they have turned from the Lord and are pulling people away with them. Don’t trust it. Turn to God alone, and worship His name. You don’t have to do that by the approval of your church leadership."}]},{"start":14,"end":14,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Those that live against the Lord are living in judgement by the way."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But I say unto you, That whosoever is angry with his brother without a cause shall be in danger of the judgment: and whosoever shall say to his brother, Raca, shall be in danger of the council: but whosoever shall say, Thou fool, shall be in danger of hell fire.","ref":"Matthew 5:22"},{"kind":"para","text":"They are so focused on keeping people at arm’s length that they don’t see how miserable they have made the Lord above them. They are in danger of judgment because they have hated those nearest them. They are evil to their brothers. It happens in the church quite a lot, honestly. There’s a schism in the church house today, and Satan loves to touch the nerves of those already hanging on a wire. If he can irritate you and place the blame on your family in God, it will cause discord among brethren. Satan is very good at doing this."},{"kind":"para","text":"Mature Christians, however, will work out whatever they can to make sure there is nothing severing a relationship with their congregants. If only one side cares enough to do something, it will never work out. It must be both players in the relationship making things work for the sake of Christ in order for everything to be amended. However, they are dead men walking, most of them. They don’t have Christ as the center of their relationship with people. Pastors and preachers today are just motivational speakers. Because of this, there is division, envy, and corralling of all sorts in the church, and there is no healing and encouragement among the brethren."}]},{"start":15,"end":15,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God can move a people that are dedicated to Him. God moves His own and crushes the enemy. If you are feeling moved, it might be the Lord’s pulling. If you are feeling crushed, it might be the Lord convicting. Either way, the Lord is doing something, and there is a reason to glorify Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"He has not just altogether given up on humanity because it is far too wicked. Rather, He continues to work on humanity until there is nothing left but rejectful people who will never turn to the Lord no matter how much God grants to them."}]}]},{"start":16,"end":19,"title":"A New Body","entries":[{"start":16,"end":16,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Usually, that’s the only reason people finally turn to the Lord. He gets you into a position where you will either have to suffer the consequences of your sin or turn to God and beg Him for grace. Sadly, most of us are stupid enough to reject God even though He’s the only salvation for us."},{"kind":"para","text":"For right now, we have the ability to turn to the Lord, and so we should take it. There will be a time when that won’t be the case, and those who have not taken Him must live in His judgments. If you haven’t paid attention to His judgments from our previous chapters, they were not fun for the nations."}]},{"start":17,"end":17,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This world is going to experience great suffering from their sins. They are going to have to go through the pain. There is no turning back once you are in labor. You can’t keep the baby inside. You have to go through the pain at that point. We have modern medicine to help with that now, but in those days, people were left to just deal with the pain. In the end times, that pain will be the same. We can’t drug ourselves to help feel less pain. We will just have to face it."}]},{"start":18,"end":18,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"All that suffering… and for what? What do we get in the end for living under God’s judgment? We don’t get triumph. We don’t overcome. We don’t get alleviation. We don’t get a reward. We don’t feel any better. Rather, we get more pain after this because we have rejected Christ. It really baffles me that there would be anyone during the last days who can see the wrath of God poured out and still blaspheme His name and reject Him. If I saw all these miraculous terrors happening around me, it would certainly make me believe in something higher than myself."},{"kind":"para","text":"Yet, it seems everyone is going to try and write off these hazards as science. They will probably call it global warming, or climate change, or whatever they call it these days. They will deny the existence of God, even if God was standing right in front of them. That is the image of evil."}]},{"start":19,"end":19,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There are a lot of debates about what is being said here. Some believe that the dead of the Earth (those that are saved) will get their bodies back from this Earth. When the new Earth comes, we will be resurrected into our old bodies. I hope we aren’t. Away with this sinful, dread-filled body. I believe what Isaiah is getting at is the immortality of saints. When we accept Christ, we become immortal."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For the wages of sin is death; but the gift of God is eternal life through Jesus Christ our Lord.","ref":"Romans 6:23"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For God so loved the world, that he gave his only begotten Son, that whosoever believeth in him should not perish, but have everlasting life.","ref":"John 3:16"},{"kind":"para","text":"But it won't be in our physical bodies that we raise again. Rather it will be our spirits."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Then shall the dust return to the earth as it was: and the spirit shall return unto God who gave it.","ref":"Ecclesiastes 12:7"},{"kind":"para","text":"But there is coming a day (for the saints) to dwell in a new Heaven and new Earth. It will be in renewed bodies. We will be completely new creatures:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For we commend not ourselves again unto you, but give you occasion to glory on our behalf, that ye may have somewhat to answer them which glory in appearance, and not in heart.","ref":"2 Corinthians 5:12"},{"kind":"para","text":"Our Earthly body aches, and our new body in the Lord's Spirit will be full of the spirit of God."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For we know that if our earthly house of this tabernacle were dissolved, we have a building of God, an house not made with hands, eternal in the heavens. For in this we groan, earnestly desiring to be clothed upon with our house which is from heaven: If so be that being clothed we shall not be found naked. For we that are in this tabernacle do groan, being burdened: not for that we would be unclothed, but clothed upon, that mortality might be swallowed up of life. Now he that hath wrought us for the selfsame thing is God, who also hath given unto us the earnest of the Spirit. Therefore we are always confident, knowing that, whilst we are at home in the body, we are absent from the Lord: (For we walk by faith, not by sight:) We are confident, I say, and willing rather to be absent from the body, and to be present with the Lord.","ref":"2 Corinthians 5:1-8"},{"kind":"para","text":"It will not be the body of this Earth. It will be the body of the Spirit that lives in me that you will see in eternity. It will be the spiritual body clothed by the Holy Ghost."}]}]},{"start":20,"end":21,"title":"Hiding In God","entries":[{"start":20,"end":20,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"We’ve already spoken about this, but it’s a good reminder. There’s a place to hide from the judgments of God, but it’s only found in the shadow and protection of God Himself. We have an invitation to come and be saved from His wrath. God loves us enough to give us a place to dwell with Him so we don’t have to suffer from our sins. Those that reject that protection will get what they ask for in all honesty."}]},{"start":21,"end":21,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There will be a lot of evil people put to death in the day of the Lord’s return. They had the chance for literally generations to turn to God. They still have the chance today as of this writing. I don’t know how much longer the Lord will wait. I hope He waits longer though. There are still family members who have not turned. I hope they don’t wait until it’s too late…"}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":9},{"start":10,"end":10},{"start":11,"end":11},{"start":12,"end":12},{"start":13,"end":13},{"start":14,"end":14},{"start":15,"end":15},{"start":16,"end":16},{"start":17,"end":17},{"start":18,"end":18},{"start":19,"end":19},{"start":20,"end":20},{"start":21,"end":21}],"verses":{"1":"In that day shall this song be sung in the land of Judah; We have a strong city; salvation will God appoint for walls and bulwarks.","2":"Open ye the gates, that the righteous nation which keepeth the truth may enter in.","3":"Thou wilt keep him in perfect peace, whose mind is stayed on thee: because he trusteth in thee.","4":"Trust ye in the Lord for ever: for in the Lord Jehovah is everlasting strength:","5":"For he bringeth down them that dwell on high; the lofty city, he layeth it low; he layeth it low, even to the ground; he bringeth it even to the dust.","6":"The foot shall tread it down, even the feet of the poor, and the steps of the needy.","7":"The way of the just is uprightness: thou, most upright, dost weigh the path of the just.","8":"Yea, in the way of thy judgments, O Lord, have we waited for thee; the desire of our soul is to thy name, and to the remembrance of thee.","9":"With my soul have I desired thee in the night; yea, with my spirit within me will I seek thee early: for when thy judgments are in the earth, the inhabitants of the world will learn righteousness.","10":"Let favour be shewed to the wicked, yet will he not learn righteousness: in the land of uprightness will he deal unjustly, and will not behold the majesty of the Lord.","11":"Lord, when thy hand is lifted up, they will not see: but they shall see, and be ashamed for their envy at the people; yea, the fire of thine enemies shall devour them.","12":"Lord, thou wilt ordain peace for us: for thou also hast wrought all our works in us.","13":"O Lord our God, other lords beside thee have had dominion over us: but by thee only will we make mention of thy name.","14":"They are dead, they shall not live; they are deceased, they shall not rise: therefore hast thou visited and destroyed them, and made all their memory to perish.","15":"Thou hast increased the nation, O Lord, thou hast increased the nation: thou art glorified: thou hadst removed it far unto all the ends of the earth.","16":"Lord, in trouble have they visited thee, they poured out a prayer when thy chastening was upon them.","17":"Like as a woman with child, that draweth near the time of her delivery, is in pain, and crieth out in her pangs; so have we been in thy sight, O Lord.","18":"We have been with child, we have been in pain, we have as it were brought forth wind; we have not wrought any deliverance in the earth; neither have the inhabitants of the world fallen.","19":"Thy dead men shall live, together with my dead body shall they arise. Awake and sing, ye that dwell in dust: for thy dew is as the dew of herbs, and the earth shall cast out the dead.","20":"Come, my people, enter thou into thy chambers, and shut thy doors about thee: hide thyself as it were for a little moment, until the indignation be overpast.","21":"For, behold, the Lord cometh out of his place to punish the inhabitants of the earth for their iniquity: the earth also shall disclose her blood, and shall no more cover her slain."}},
    "27": {"chapter":27,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: We have been reading great truths from Isaiah about the saints rejoicing over God's righteousness. When God brings justice, and He completes His perfection in this world, there is reason to rejoice and be glad."},{"kind":"para","text":"In fact, that is more of what we are going to get from this chapter. We can, and should, rejoice in the Lord's strength and provision for us. He gives us reason to sin to Him, and that is because He will vanquish and desolate sin and the power of it. This chapter is a great hope to every believer about the future promise of sin being destroyed."}],"previously":["We have been reading great truths from Isaiah about the saints rejoicing over God’s righteousness. When God brings justice and completes His perfection in this world, there is reason to rejoice and be glad. In fact, that is more of what we are going to get from this chapter. We can, and should, rejoice in the Lord’s strength and provision for us. He gives us reason to sin to Him, and that is because He will vanquish and desolate sin and its power. This chapter is a great hope to every believer about the future promise of sin being destroyed."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":1,"title":"Leviathan's Defeat","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"“In that day”… In what day? Well, it’s assumed that when Isaiah says “In that day,” he is talking about the second coming of the Lord, remember. He’s talking about the Great Tribulation era. “In that day” would assume “in the future.” Perhaps it’s the imminent future of Israel, but again, prophets speak in threes, so… Perhaps there was some sort of “leviathan” creature in scripture during that time. We get a glimpse of a creature like this in Job as well."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Canst thou draw out leviathan with an hook? or his tongue with a cord which thou lettest down?","ref":"Job 41:1"},{"kind":"para","text":"Actually, we get a much deeper look at this creature in that chapter of Job. “Leviathan” means “sea monster” or “dragon.” Even in this verse, it specifically says “crooked serpent.” There is only one that will come looking like a dragon…"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And the great dragon was cast out, that old serpent, called the Devil, and Satan, which deceiveth the whole world: he was cast out into the earth, and his angels were cast out with him.","ref":"Revelation 12:9"},{"kind":"para","text":"We also understand that God's Word is His \"great and strong sword.\""},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And he had in his right hand seven stars: and out of his mouth went a sharp twoedged sword: and his countenance was as the sun shineth in his strength.","ref":"Revelation 1:16"},{"kind":"para","text":"We can rightfully assume that when “leviathan” is mentioned in the Old Testament, it is speaking about the dragon. It’s speaking about Satan. The Lord will have His day with this old serpent, and He will completely destroy and defeat him. The Lord is more than capable of doing that."}]}]},{"start":2,"end":6,"title":"A Protected Garden","entries":[{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Talk about a shift. However, I think there is great reason for the saints to sing once Satan has finally been cast out of this world. We cannot wait for the day that sin is vanquished, and we can live freely without the power of sin."},{"kind":"para","text":"I think a lot of people ignore salvation or shun it because they can’t seem to believe that they are simply not a good enough person to get themselves into Heaven. They don’t think their sin is legitimate. You want to know how I know my sin is real? I struggle with it every day. Even Paul struggled with it."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For the good that I would I do not: but the evil which I would not, that I do.","ref":"Romans 7:19"},{"kind":"para","text":"Those who do not know the Lord are unaware of their true sinfulness. As a result, they have no problem with their sin and feel no remorse for mistreating, stepping on, rejecting, and absolutely destroying the most innocent among us, including children and infants. That is the sad world we live in."},{"kind":"para","text":"However, once Satan is gone and sin has been washed away, we will sing and rejoice because we will no longer have to worry about evil or sin. What a pleasant thought…"}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord will keep His vineyard and take care of His produce. That is His reward. He is rewarded by the growth of His children. Perhaps that is something you might want to read again. He is rewarded by the growth of His children."},{"kind":"para","text":"I think we try to please God in all sorts of unorthodox ways today. But the Lord is simply pleased with the fact that you know Him and that you are continuing to grow like fruit."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But grow in grace, and in the knowledge of our Lord and Saviour Jesus Christ. To him be glory both now and for ever. Amen.","ref":"2 Peter 3:18"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But speaking the truth in love, may grow up into him in all things, which is the head, even Christ:","ref":"Ephesians 4:15"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Being confident of this very thing, that he which hath begun a good work in you will perform it until the day of Jesus Christ:","ref":"Philippians 1:6"},{"kind":"para","text":"There are plenty of evil forces that try to harm the Lord’s garden. They attempt to make His wine taste bitter and empty. They strive to fill it with toxins that kill, rather than joy that fills. Honestly, I think Satan has been pretty successful at mixing the Lord’s wine."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Who hath woe? who hath sorrow? who hath contentions? who hath babbling? who hath wounds without cause? who hath redness of eyes? They that tarry long at the wine; they that go to seek mixed wine.","ref":"Proverbs 23:29-30"},{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord has woe, sorrow, and a contention with His problem children. We have babbling, wounds without cause, and redness of eyes against the Lord when we have allowed Satan to mix us up."},{"kind":"para","text":"God protects His vineyard, though. He is good at keeping the produce safe. Satan is a little nat that tries to get at us and our growth, but the Lord is doing everything to keep him from doing that. We are usually the ones that allow Satan to mix us up. We need to stop doing that."}]},{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Satan and evil will try. They will do whatever is in their own power to put a stop to God’s prosperity. They won’t succeed, but it will be a fight until the end. God (for the sake of sin and Satan) WILL have to make everything new eventually. Satan has left too much wreckage to keep the world this way. But verse 5 is how we really overcome:"}]},{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"To have the Lord on your side is the only way to have victory. The frustrating reality of our world is that you are either against the Lord or you are with the Lord. There is no middle ground. The reason it frustrates me is that there are a lot of “preachers” who think that the Lord’s judgment is a grand thing. They can really twist what scripture says in the book of Isaiah to be an extremely good thing from the Lord. “Kill all the sinners,” they might say. “Rain your terror down on them,” they might desire. They don’t care if their family is caught in the crossfire either."},{"kind":"para","text":"Honestly, I don’t want my family and friends to die and go to hell. I want them to turn to the Lord and live in victory. But the truth is, most of my friends and family have already made their decision about God. They have already rejected Him, and they don’t care that they are going to lose the battle against God. It’s almost like they enjoy being the enemy of God."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Ye adulterers and adulteresses, know ye not that the friendship of the world is enmity with God? whosoever therefore will be a friend of the world is the enemy of God.","ref":"James 4:4"},{"kind":"para","text":"They like what this world has to offer, and so they are sufficient with taking the cheap destructive things of this world rather than everlasting life which is freely given to anyone that believes."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"He that believeth on the Son hath everlasting life: and he that believeth not the Son shall not see life; but the wrath of God abideth on him.","ref":"John 3:36"},{"kind":"para","text":"I don’t want God’s wrath to be laid on my family. We were talking to my nephew (on my wife’s side) the other day when he came to visit us for Christmas. I’ve spoken to his father (my wife’s brother) for quite some time about the gospel message. I’ve tried to show him the truths of scripture and get him to turn to the Lord, but he kept changing the subject and saying very strange things that had nothing to do with the topic at hand. I’ve shared the gospel with my sister-in-law and her husband. I’ve shared the gospel with my wife’s father. It was shared with my wife’s mother. I’ve done whatever it takes to get the gospel over there, but most of them were pretty rejectful of it."},{"kind":"para","text":"My nephew came over, though, and he said, “What do you call the people in your church?” Thinking this was a trick question to try and make fun of us, I said, “We usually say, HEY YOU! Or call them by their name.” He said, “You don’t call them brother or sister?” I said, “Yeah, I suppose we do sometimes.” And he held my wife by the shoulders and said, “Well, you are now my sister.” When I tell you my heart sank, I don’t know if you understand the gravity of that truth."},{"kind":"para","text":"Strength is on the side of those who have turned to the Lord. The Lord is the only strength that can combat Satan and sin. If you do not have the Lord, you are against the Lord. If you are against the Lord, you are FOR Satan. Period. You love sin too much, and God hates it too much."}]},{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God’s chosen will fill this Earth. Right now, sin has filled the Earth. Satan’s chosen have tried to make it impossible to plant righteousness here in this soil. He has tainted the soil of mankind. But when God is done with His judgments, the soil will be new. It will only belong to Him, and Satan won’t be able to touch it ever again."},{"kind":"para","text":"Going back to my sin, I think that is the best way to tell that this spiritual battle is real. I might doubt a heck of a lot of things regarding the Bible. I might doubt some historical information. I might even sometimes doubt the motives of God, and whether or not He was real. It’s my sin, however, that brings me back to reality. My sin reveals the truth in me. I can’t wait to be rid of it."}]}]},{"start":7,"end":11,"title":"God Destroys The Old","entries":[{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Israel, at this time, serves as a small picture of the promise of salvation. We will see that God brings Israel back, but it is only after quite a brutal beating. It is only after they have died off and disappeared. Christ will also be brought back once this world has died off and disappeared. Christ came back to life the first time He came, but it was only after He had died off and disappeared. God is a God of reviving. He can resurrect anything we seem to deem completely gone and lost forever."},{"kind":"para","text":"The only way that a Christian can be completely destroyed and killed is if their God can be killed and destroyed. The Lord, however, is eternal. No one can kill our God. The world has already tried and failed."}]},{"start":8,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"To “debate” is to “contend.” The world can fight all they want against the actions and methods of the Lord, but the Lord will always come out on top. Ask any atheist if they have won their fight against the Lord yet. Honestly, I think atheists speak about the Lord more than most Christians today."}]},{"start":9,"end":9,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The offering of Christ is the fruit of sin being taken away. When we have Christ (and I mean truly have Him, and are completely sold out for Him), any altars or gods we used to serve will be thrown down and shattered. We will completely get rid of our old ways and wants. That is how we know we have our sins taken away."},{"kind":"para","text":"We will still struggle (Satan hasn’t been destroyed yet), but we will have the ability to overcome when we have the Savior. He will give us the choice to repent. That choice was not accessible before Christ. Israel will learn that in time. Well, a good portion of Israel will anyway. We see how large the Christian faith grows in the book of Acts."}]},{"start":10,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Our efforts, without the Lord, are done in vain. They deserve to be destroyed. God can build something far greater. We should want the Lord to completely destroy our old ways. We should want God to show no mercy for our past sins. He allowed us to have our ways, and we should be obliged to have His way when we no longer live in the past desires."},{"kind":"para","text":"I hate my past desires. They tear at me every day. My eyes and my heart deceive me, but the Lord is merciful to His own and unmerciful to our crutches of the past."}]}]},{"start":12,"end":12,"title":"One By One","entries":[{"start":12,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"He will not just swoop His arm across the Earth and gather every believer. He certainly could. I think He has the power to do that without accidentally gathering an unsaved person. However, He doesn’t like that kind of ministry. I think a lot of pastors would love to be able to just scoop the whole land into their church and call them family. They wouldn’t care if people were actually saved or living for the Lord or not. They just want numbers."},{"kind":"para","text":"However, the Lord wants to know us personally. He will gather us “one by one” and He will lead us individually. That is how a pastor should be, but that is not how pastors actually are. They are busy men. I get it. I’m thankful God is not too busy for His own."}]}]},{"start":13,"end":13,"title":"Israel Matters","entries":[{"start":13,"end":13,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This verse certainly insinuates that God will not be done with Israel. It is a very pointed verse. Of course, we read about Babylon in Revelation. But we also read about the tribes of Israel and twelve thousand people from each tribe being saved. We can certainly talk more about that in Revelation, but what does someone who believes that God is done with Israel do with a verse like this, I wonder? Do we know a time in history when this prophecy has been fulfilled? People might argue that it was fulfilled in the day of Christ, but it wasn’t literally fulfilled. We don’t read about Assyria or the outcasts of Egypt at all coming back to the land. We will read about Babylon. We know it will be destroyed. We know that God’s children will return, and the emphasis is placed on Judah specifically (which is the Babylonian captivity). But when do the outcasts in Assyria and Egypt come back and wholeheartedly worship? That will take place, no doubt, but it will be on a grander scale during the days of Revelation. Everything is done on a grander scale for the Great Tribulation period. Revelation is a grand book, no doubt. I’m not arguing against either theory (pro-Israel, anti-Israel), but I will say that God makes it clear in His Word that He never really gives up on Israel."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":9},{"start":10,"end":11},{"start":12,"end":12},{"start":13,"end":13}],"verses":{"1":"In that day the Lord with his sore and great and strong sword shall punish leviathan the piercing serpent, even leviathan that crooked serpent; and he shall slay the dragon that is in the sea.","2":"In that day sing ye unto her, A vineyard of red wine.","3":"I the Lord do keep it; I will water it every moment: lest any hurt it, I will keep it night and day.","4":"Fury is not in me: who would set the briers and thorns against me in battle? I would go through them, I would burn them together.","5":"Or let him take hold of my strength, that he may make peace with me; and he shall make peace with me.","6":"He shall cause them that come of Jacob to take root: Israel shall blossom and bud, and fill the face of the world with fruit.","7":"Hath he smitten him, as he smote those that smote him? or is he slain according to the slaughter of them that are slain by him?","8":"In measure, when it shooteth forth, thou wilt debate with it: he stayeth his rough wind in the day of the east wind.","9":"By this therefore shall the iniquity of Jacob be purged; and this is all the fruit to take away his sin; when he maketh all the stones of the altar as chalkstones that are beaten in sunder, the groves and images shall not stand up.","10":"Yet the defenced city shall be desolate, and the habitation forsaken, and left like a wilderness: there shall the calf feed, and there shall he lie down, and consume the branches thereof.","11":"When the boughs thereof are withered, they shall be broken off: the women come, and set them on fire: for it is a people of no understanding: therefore he that made them will not have mercy on them, and he that formed them will shew them no favour.","12":"And it shall come to pass in that day, that the Lord shall beat off from the channel of the river unto the stream of Egypt, and ye shall be gathered one by one, O ye children of Israel.","13":"And it shall come to pass in that day, that the great trumpet shall be blown, and they shall come which were ready to perish in the land of Assyria, and the outcasts in the land of Egypt, and shall worship the Lord in the holy mount at Jerusalem."}},
    "28": {"chapter":28,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: Our last chapter spoke a lot about the victory of the Lord during the time of tribulation. It was a future promise given to all of mankind, but He's using the land of Israel as a case in point. He will show the way in which they will come out of captivity as a small example of God's victory (through Christ of course) and how the rest of the world falls apart by fighting against the Lord and His leading."},{"kind":"para","text":"In this chapter, we will look back at Israel's northern kingdom and their coming captivity. Isaiah will use it as a warning for the southern kingdom (Judah) in hopes that they will turn back to the Lord and follow Him rather than reject Him and live against God. God doesn't want His children to fall away, and He certainly doesn't want His children to be led by lies from people who are supposed to be called by Him. They are doing it all in the name of the Lord, and mocking God by making His judgements little in their eyes."}],"previously":["Our last chapter spoke a lot about the victory of the Lord during the time of tribulation. It was a future promise given to all of mankind, but He’s using the land of Israel as a case in point. He will show the way in which they will come out of captivity as a small example of God’s victory (through Christ, of course) and how the rest of the world falls apart by fighting against the Lord and His leading. In this chapter, we will look back at Israel’s northern kingdom and their coming captivity. Isaiah will use it as a warning for the southern kingdom (Judah) in hopes that they will turn back to the Lord and follow Him rather than reject Him and live against God. God doesn’t want His children to fall away, and He certainly doesn’t want His children to be led by lies from people who are supposed to be called by Him. They are doing it all in the name of the Lord and mocking God by making His judgments little in their eyes."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":6,"title":"Ephraim's Loss","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Remember, when Isaiah mentions Ephraim, he is speaking about the northern kingdom. He is using the invasion of the north as an example to Judah and the south kingdom. If they don’t correct course, their fate will be the same, and they have seen how that looks from their brothers in the north. I think the “crown of pride” is a pretty befitting name. That is ultimately how they got into this mess."},{"kind":"para","text":"God has been good to the north, and there was no reason (at this point) for them to still go after their own desires and flesh. But they were too prideful to turn back. They were too far gone. “To be spiritually drunk is to be filled with pride.” J. Vernon McGee"}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God is going to use Assyria to put Israel back in its place. They have gotten away with their sins for far too long. They were doing worse things than the other countries surrounding them because they were accepting every sort of false worship and culture into their land more than any other land. The other lands only had their own gods and traditions. Israel had them all. They treated the gods like Pokémon."}]},{"start":3,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I have a strong desire to explain why God is doing this, here, again. I’ve explained it quite a few times at this point. If you really want to know how they got here, 1 & 2 Chronicles will give you a pretty apt understanding of it. 1 & 2 Kings is maybe a quicker view, but you don’t really get into the spiritual depravity of these kings unless you go to 1 & 2 Chronicles. God doesn’t just judge the actions of these kings; He judges the heart of them. He knows why they chose to do the things they did. They purposely went against the Lord in nearly everything they did. I believe a good portion of these kings were trying to provoke the Lord to anger. I think their whole intention was to see how angry they could make God. They did a pretty good job of it, and now the Lord is going to use His power and authority to let them have what they want. That is ultimately what is happening here."},{"kind":"para","text":"You say, “God is just going to destroy His own people. That doesn’t seem like a loving father to me.” This is what they asked for. They’ve asked for it for generations, and they have not desired to love the Lord in return. So God isn’t just giving up on His children; God is giving them what they want. Sadly, they will realize (too late) that this was not good for them. We always want things that are ultimately never going to give us satisfaction. We think it will, but it never does. The Lord loves His creation; I think we should understand that. We get a sort of calloused look at the Lord from a lot of preachers. We can trace a theme of love throughout scripture. The Lord also loves us enough to not let us continue down a dangerous path. He will, often, use the path we are on to show us why we shouldn’t stay on it. But He never just ignores us and lets us go. He won’t let a single one of these nations just go."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"If ye endure chastening, God dealeth with you as with sons; for what son is he whom the father chasteneth not? But if ye be without chastisement, whereof all are partakers, then are ye bastards, and not sons.","ref":"Hebrews 12:7-8"},{"kind":"para","text":"Everyone receives instruction by the Lord. Anyone who says they don’t believe in God has certainly felt the Spirit of God do something in their life. They probably didn’t like it, and so it’s better to reject conviction and ignore God than to accept conviction and learn from Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"But He doesn’t just give up on His creation. He certainly could; let’s get that clear. He has every right to just give up on us and ignore us, but He doesn’t. We have seen that there are some nations that the Lord wanted to just outright get rid of. Some are no longer around because of it (cough cough, Babylon, cough cough). He tells Saul to completely wipe out the Amalekites as well (knowing Saul won’t do what he’s supposed to)."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Thus saith the LORD of hosts, I remember that which Amalek did to Israel, how he laid wait for him in the way, when he came up from Egypt. Now go and smite Amalek, and utterly destroy all that they have, and spare them not; but slay both man and woman, infant and suckling, ox and sheep, camel and ass.","ref":"1 Samuel 15:2-3"},{"kind":"para","text":"These people were evil, and because Saul doesn’t destroy them all, you will see that it comes to bite him in the rear later on. But that’s a spoiler (if you haven’t already read 1 Samuel, I don’t know what you are doing here if not). The Lord gets rid of specific nations and people because they would never have turned to Him if He let them live, and they would have become a sinful power that this world could not handle. Eventually, the Lord would have to deal with them. That is how it will look during the Great Tribulation too. There will be a great power in this world, and we will not be able to deal with it. You will have to be an evil person if you don’t want to be attacked by this power. You will have to follow the orders of evil to survive, or you will have to go into hiding for the rest of your life until Jesus returns."}]},{"start":5,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"We will jump from a \"crown of pride\" to a \"crown of glory.” There's only one person that can wear that crown:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"I am the LORD: that is my name: and my glory will I not give to another, neither my praise to graven images.","ref":"Isaiah 42:8"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"That the God of our Lord Jesus Christ, the Father of glory, may give unto you the spirit of wisdom and revelation in the knowledge of him:","ref":"Ephesians 1:17"},{"kind":"para","text":"It will not be Israel that wears the crown, but the Earth will give glory to the Lord when He returns. “In that day” insinuates the last days. He will be a strong, righteous, and beautiful judge for this Earth that will know how to reign supreme and give everyone what they deserve."},{"kind":"para","text":"They say that Jesus came the first time to love and the second time to judge. Perhaps there is some truth to that, but Jesus came the first time for the same cause as well:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Jesus Christ the same yesterday, and to day, and for ever.","ref":"Hebrews 13:8"},{"kind":"para","text":"The first time He came, He taught us how to judge. The second time He comes, He will utilize what He taught."}]}]},{"start":7,"end":8,"title":"Spiritual Vomit","entries":[{"start":7,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is probably literal. I would imagine that the priests and “godly” men were in the temple just throwing parties rather than performing sacrifices. There was no “solemn” assembly; it was more of a rave. You would probably go in there and literally see vomit and filthiness on the tables and walls. It was probably treated more like a brothel in the Lord’s house. I also think this was a spiritual picture of the nation as well. I think the priests were spiritual representations of what the people’s hearts actually looked like."},{"kind":"para","text":"I think (spiritually) this is what a lot of churches look like today. They are spiritually drunk and swaying on this conviction and that conviction. They are drunk and hurting people, drunk with power. They don’t know how to judge correctly (righteously) and they abuse their power to hurt innocent people. This makes the church look quite filthy. Anyone who doesn’t know the Lord will see the church as white and new, but those who have known the Lord know the spiritual nature of a church. They can see the spiritual vomit on the walls, and it’s not pretty."},{"kind":"para","text":"It’s a wise leader’s task to hear the counsel of spiritual eyes rather than reject it. Alas, most spiritual leaders reject the spiritual eyes of others because the leaders are the ones throwing up on the church. They don’t want to blame themselves. They are behind the pulpits emptying themselves out rather than filling the hearers with God’s Word. I am full of failed leaders’ words. I just need Christ now."}]}]},{"start":9,"end":13,"title":"Trained For War","entries":[{"start":9,"end":9,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Spiritual milk is for those who are babies to the faith. These are the people who cannot see the spiritual vomit. They are brand new to the faith and think the church is so white and pure. I have yet to meet a “pure” church. I’ve seen a lot of well-meaning churches, but they are filled with vomit. Some pastors might want to try and address it, but I don’t think there are many that do (at least none I’ve met). Jesus calls those churches this:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! for ye are like unto whited sepulchres, which indeed appear beautiful outward, but are within full of dead men's bones, and of all uncleanness.","ref":"Matthew 23:27"},{"kind":"para","text":"What the priests and prophets are doing in Israel is akin to shoving meat down babies’ throats without caring for their well-being. There is a right way to feed people, but churches don’t look into that. Honestly, there are a lot of churches that do nothing but provide milk to their congregants. They have nothing but milk to feed on, and they never actually mature. Once they feel like they need more, the church is done with them."},{"kind":"para","text":"Israel, as I understand it, didn’t even try to feed their people with anything valuable. The priests and prophets were not doing their job. They were rejecting their calling to throw a party."}]},{"start":10,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Preparing people is a necessity in the house of God. It is the greatest call to unity within the church. If you are rejecting the opportunity for people to learn or for people to teach, you are only hurting your church. Truth must grow in you."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But speaking the truth in love, may grow up into him in all things, which is the head, even Christ: From whom the whole body fitly joined together and compacted by that which every joint supplieth, according to the effectual working in the measure of every part, maketh increase of the body unto the edifying of itself in love.","ref":"Ephesians 4:15-16"},{"kind":"para","text":"Pastors often have the unfortunate mindset that everyone must be on the same spiritual level. If you are new to the faith, they will either bring you up to everyone else’s speed or you will be forgotten about. When a person is saved, you must start your journey over again. Honestly, that is the job of the pastor. His job is to restart his journey to walk with people who are newly saved, as well as run back to the front where all the other people are."},{"kind":"para","text":"However, pastors don’t do that, and it’s felt by the congregants. Those who are ahead will either suffer, or those who are behind. Pastors usually only care for one group or the other, never both."}]},{"start":11,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"When someone is spiritually drunk, they are not going to impart any sort of living and actual truth. They will impart a “version” of what they think is true, but it doesn’t lead to anything absolute. The truth must be absolute. We must prove all things."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Prove all things; hold fast that which is good.","ref":"1 Thessalonians 5:21"},{"kind":"para","text":"Baby Christians don’t know how to do that yet, though. We should be teaching them how to prove what is right and what is wrong before we teach them any other doctrines. I want people to be able to point out my inconsistencies and flaws. They can’t prove God’s Word wrong, but they should definitely know how to line up God’s Word with mine to find the inconsistencies. Otherwise, we could teach whatever we wanted, and everyone would just have to believe it or get out of the church. That is wrong. That is not what God wants. He wants us to have right judgments. We (the individual people) need to know what is from God and what is not. If we can’t figure that out or learn it, we will be no different than any other religion or cult."}]},{"start":12,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"A pastor and preacher who genuinely cares about the souls of people will provide them with spiritual rest. I know I am making a lot of preachers and pastors angry right now by saying this. “Where is judgment, where is righteousness, where is truth?” Those are all things that can be taught, no doubt, in time."},{"kind":"para","text":"As Isaiah says, we need milk, and milk is found in teaching Christians to look up answers and giving them a place to rest. Over time, judgment, righteousness, truth, doctrine, and all the rest can be structured. God calls us to rest first, and that is through Jesus Christ alone."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Come unto me, all ye that labour and are heavy laden, and I will give you rest.","ref":"Matthew 11:28"},{"kind":"para","text":"He doesn’t say, “Come to me, and I will give you doctrine.” He doesn’t say, “Come to me and I will give you judgment.” He doesn’t even say, “Come to me and I will give you truth.” He certainly will give these things, but first He wants to give them rest. That is the first step of a man. However, that is not what the church teaches."},{"kind":"para","text":"The church teaches, “Come unto Jesus, or He will give you damnation.” They teach, “Come to Jesus, and you have a place to serve.” They teach, “Come to Jesus, and you can help in MY ministry.”"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For we which have believed do enter into rest, as he said, As I have sworn in my wrath, if they shall enter into my rest: although the works were finished from the foundation of the world.","ref":"Hebrews 4:3"},{"kind":"para","text":"What a great place for a man to start. If a new member can raise their hands, be saved, and serve right away, that church is not teaching a correct culture. He is not teaching them to rest first. That will weary people in their faith quite quickly. They might feel good for a time, but it’s superficial."},{"kind":"para","text":"Some people believe that is what holds their salvation. They say, “Well, I serve in my church, so that proves I’m saved.” God says, “You should start not by serving, but by resting.”"}]},{"start":13,"end":13,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is what happens when we don’t enter into the Lord’s rest first in our faith. We get a little thing here and a little thing there, and we think we are doing good by getting directly involved with our church in service. However, the rest is important because we learn the most when we are found sitting with Christ."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But Martha was cumbered about much serving, and came to him, and said, Lord, dost thou not care that my sister hath left me to serve alone? bid her therefore that she help me. And Jesus answered and said unto her, Martha, Martha, thou art careful and troubled about many things: But one thing is needful: and Mary hath chosen that good part, which shall not be taken away from her.","ref":"Luke 10:40-42"},{"kind":"para","text":"That is what the church should be helping new believers into. Those who have been saved for a while can be serving. Jesus isn’t saying that serving is a bad thing. We can get this wrong if we are not careful. Jesus cares about the servant, but we must start with rest. If we don’t, we will fall backward and be broken, snared, and taken by the enemy. We are not trained to fight against the enemy. We can only be trained for that through rest first. Instead, we are just thrown into battle."},{"kind":"para","text":"If our military today didn’t have a boot camp and training for the soldiers, showing them how to handle weapons, how to run and hide, and what it’s like to be in the middle of battle and trouble, but instead we just threw them out into the middle of war, we should not expect them to last very long. They will absolutely fall in battle. Yet, here we have thousands of churches worldwide literally doing that to their congregants every day. They are just thrown into the middle of spiritual warfare. A little information here, a little information there. We want to grow quickly in our faith, but that will never happen. That is what pastors promise. They say, “Well, we have a revival coming, and you can hear preaching for three days; it will spark your new life in Christ and grow you quickly.” They might say, “We have a couples’ weekend planned for our church, and there will be teaching for the night we are there that will change your marriage.” We think it will be one lesson or one getaway that will teach us what we need to know in faith. It will not be that."},{"kind":"para","text":"Spiritual maturity takes time, but it can’t take time if you are not giving time to it. It is first your responsibility to rest in the Lord and allow yourself to grow slowly. Let the Lord lead and make it obvious."}]}]},{"start":14,"end":17,"title":"Slow Judgement","entries":[{"start":14,"end":14,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Isaiah was speaking about the northern kingdom, but he was using it as an illustration for the southern kingdom. The people in the north were not going to take Isaiah’s word for it. They wouldn’t care what Isaiah said because they don’t truly believe in the God of Isaiah."},{"kind":"para","text":"Isaiah gives warning to the south, though, and they are far more inclined to believe what Isaiah is saying is actually true. Just by the fact that they have a live example up north proves that Isaiah is telling the truth. They should really consider his words here."}]},{"start":15,"end":15,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Really, they made a deal with Satan. That is what he is speaking about here. They think they have made a deal with a stand-up being. They have been tricked into believing that they can have the false gods with the real God of the universe. The northern kingdom had been living in that false idea for a long time, and it didn’t get them success. It got them in trouble."},{"kind":"para","text":"Once again (and I’m just being honest), the modern church has fallen for this same trap. They think they are on the right track, but ultimately they are just “playing” church. They have made a deal with the devil, not with the Lord. If the Lord is making financial deals with you over spiritual patience, you are probably not actually dealing with the Lord. God usually doesn’t make deals. He just tells you how it is, and you have to accept it. If there is a deal being made by God, you probably won’t like the outcome of your choices. Just ask Hezekiah. We will see that soon enough in this book…"}]},{"start":16,"end":16,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There is a sprinkling of Christ throughout these pages, done intentionally. God is always pointing His creation back to salvation and His children back to Himself. To the world, Christ is just a stone they stumble over. They get caught up and don’t realize who He is. They reject Him, saying, “I don’t want that foundation,” even though it’s the surest foundation they will ever find in the galaxy."},{"kind":"para","text":"Those who trip over Christ the most are the church. We get so stuck in our ways, like the Israelites, that we don’t want to give up anything we have been doing to follow Christ alone. That’s why He’s rejected by this world. He’s rejected in religions too. Religions tell you to do, and Christ tells you it’s done. Religions don’t like that, so they reject the message of Christ’s final sacrifice for mankind and tell you that you have to do something anyway."}]},{"start":17,"end":17,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Isaiah says that God will build up His judgment. It will come over time, rather than all at once. That is still true today. God judges still, but it usually pours out slowly. He will always make the truth known, and He will always do what is right; it just might take some time for us to see it because other things need to be set in place first. We must learn lessons slowly over time, just like a newborn Christian."}]}]},{"start":18,"end":22,"title":"Contending with God","entries":[{"start":18,"end":18,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Living in sin won't last forever. You might enjoy your time in sin now, but eventually it will become a burden to you. Sin always burdens those that are controlled by it."}]},{"start":19,"end":19,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Every day, it would become heavier and heavier. Most people, when being spiritually burdened, won’t know what it is. They dismiss it as just a mere mental problem or not taking enough vitamins. I am an advocate for addressing mental problems. I truly believe that we struggle just as much in our minds as we do in our spirits and bodies. Don’t get me wrong; I think people are very well inclined to suffer mentally, but the burdens of sin are a spiritual problem, not a mental one. You can, however, change your mind about sin."},{"kind":"para","text":"Someone might be enticed to lust and commit adultery. Perhaps they have an addiction to it. The Spirit tells your mind that it’s a bad idea. It’s a sin. Your brain knows it’s a sin. Your Spirit, however, is what will struggle with it. Your brain knows it’s wrong, but you fight against the Spirit (not your brain) to endeavor in that. Then it becomes a mental problem because you beat yourself up for not obeying the Lord’s spirit, and afterward, it becomes a bodily problem. It’s a spiritual problem that’s burdening you."},{"kind":"para","text":"To address spiritual problems, you require some spiritual help. You can receive that both from personal time with God and through spiritually led friends and the church. If the church is not willing to help you with your spiritual problems, then it is not a spiritually led church. There are a lot of churches that are mindfully led or bodily led, and few that are spiritually led. We need all three to minister correctly."}]},{"start":20,"end":20,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I used to stay at other people’s houses quite a bit when I was younger. I have slept in very difficult places. I’ve slept on floors, on tables, and in backyards. I don’t recommend any of them. One particular house I slept at, I didn’t have anything to cover me up. I just put my hoodie on and curled up into a ball. When I went to ask for a blanket, my friend was asleep on the floor, wrapped up in a rug. Yes, he wound himself into a rug to stay warm. That gave me the impression that he probably didn’t have any extra blankets."},{"kind":"para","text":"God is taking away their comfort from the land. They just won’t fit there anymore. They really haven’t fit in this land for quite some time. They have acted as strangers to it, defiling their own land given to them by the love and promises of the Lord. It’s a weird thing for people to do, mistreating their personal possessions. People spend gobs of money on cars, and then drive like it was given to them for free, or they are just easy and cheap to replace. I just don’t get it. Perhaps the Lord is confused about it too. I know He knows all things, but it certainly hurts Him to see His creation reject Him even though He gives every reason possible for them to trust Him and turn."}]},{"start":21,"end":21,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I think most of the land believed they could get away with their sins and deeds. They assumed that God didn’t care or wasn’t paying attention. Even though the prophets were telling the truth, the people didn’t believe it. The words of the prophets came to pass, yet people were still rejecting the truth of God. That is still much of the case today. Their unbelief won’t win them anything in the end, though. All it will get them is pain, both in this life and the one to come."},{"kind":"para","text":"Why Perazim and Gibeon? Well, the Lord has already accomplished great victories in these places before:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And David came to Baalperazim, and David smote them there, and said, The LORD hath broken forth upon mine enemies before me, as the breach of waters. Therefore he called the name of that place Baalperazim.","ref":"2 Samuel 5:20"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And it came to pass, as they fled from before Israel, and were in the going down to Bethhoron, that the LORD cast down great stones from heaven upon them unto Azekah, and they died: they were more which died with hailstones than they whom the children of Israel slew with the sword.","ref":"Joshua 10:11"},{"kind":"para","text":"The people of Judah would know this history fairly well I think. Yet, they seem to either not believe it, or not care enough for them to learn and turn towards the Lord."}]},{"start":22,"end":22,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"They mocked God. They seriously assumed that they could overthrow the rulership of God, and they mocked Him by literally turning away from Him. That just put them (and the people following them) into danger."},{"kind":"para","text":"By not doing what the Lord positions and calls you to do, it is a direct mocking toward the Lord. Pastors who don’t pastor are mocking God. Ministers who don’t minister are mocking God. Teachers who don’t teach are mocking God. It’s a foolish thing to mock the Lord. He will not just turn from your sin and error."}]}]},{"start":23,"end":29,"title":"Wise In Judgement","entries":[{"start":23,"end":23,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This call as been given quite a bit in the Old Testament, and it follows into the New Testament as well:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"To whom shall I speak, and give warning, that they may hear? behold, their ear is uncircumcised, and they cannot hearken: behold, the word of the LORD is unto them a reproach; they have no delight in it.","ref":"Jeremiah 6:10"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Son of man, thou dwellest in the midst of a rebellious house, which have eyes to see, and see not; they have ears to hear, and hear not: for they are a rebellious house.","ref":"Ezekiel 12:2"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And he said unto them, He that hath ears to hear, let him hear.","ref":"Mark 4:9"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"He that hath ears to hear, let him hear.","ref":"Matthew 11:15"},{"kind":"para","text":"It's still a call for the people of Earth today. It will be the same call given in the last days too:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"He that hath an ear, let him hear what the Spirit saith unto the churches; To him that overcometh will I give to eat of the tree of life, which is in the midst of the paradise of God.","ref":"Revelation 2:7"},{"kind":"para","text":"We are deaf and blind people. My dad used to call it “selective hearing.” We only hear what we want to hear. The rest of it is forgotten, as if it was never said at all. That is what we have spiritually. If it interests us, we will listen; if it doesn’t, we will ignore it. But none of us can say that we weren’t warned ahead of time."},{"kind":"para","text":"God doesn’t just say; He had it written down and then had it preserved for all of eternity. What excuse do we have now to reject the salvation of God?"}]},{"start":24,"end":24,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"If you don’t know the answer to these questions, we have a lot to work on here. Does a plowman plow to sow seeds? If not, what do you suppose he’s plowing for? Of course, it’s to start planting some seeds in the soil. He’s softening it so the seeds can root and then flourish."}]},{"start":25,"end":25,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"“Fitches” means “dill.” The sower plants all sorts of spices and herbs into the ground after he has tilled it. It is an assorted group. A farmer will also use the entire ground that was plowed to plant as much as possible. He will maximize his work to its fullest."}]},{"start":26,"end":26,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Through this work, God is teaching something. What is He teaching? Well, we will see in the next verse, but before we move on, can I just point out something? God only meant for plants to grow in one way. We don’t have any other means of growing plants. We have to do it His way (even still today). If we try to grow plants on any other sort of surface, it will not be successful. It must be soft ground, and it must be scattered appropriately and taken care of daily. We have to do it God’s way, or it won’t ever work."},{"kind":"para","text":"That, in itself, teaches us a valuable lesson. We might plant all sorts of crazy things, but we will have to do it in God’s way if we want to see any growth. A pastor who tries to usurp the authority of God to plant his garden will find his garden dead soon enough. Either that, or they will find a lot of bugs and little to no plants."}]},{"start":27,"end":28,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Even today, you have to collect and harvest your produce in a certain way. If you are too aggressive when gathering, you can hurt the plants and produce you are trying to harvest. This is a very important lesson for us to learn as leaders in the church. Isaiah literally says that this is a lesson from the Lord."}]},{"start":29,"end":29,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There will be some produce that you are going to have to break or beat to get out. That’s just their nature. They are difficult and stubborn, and so the best way to harvest is to cut, hit, or shake. That’s not always the case, but it’s probably more common than not. There are plenty of produce in this world that you just have to gently pick. That is how a pastor should view his church and his staff. The Lord will deal with people in the same way, and that is through wisdom and righteousness. He will be gentle with some and shake others. He knows who can handle what and what it will all ultimately lead to in the end anyway. We just have to wait on Him to give the direction."},{"kind":"para","text":"Everything, though, must be collected or cleaned up. Anything left behind is a very dishonoring thing. It dishonors the one that took the time to plant and grow it, and it dishonors the fruit from living up to its fullest potential. If you leave it on the vine to wither and drain away, you have wasted a good thing."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":9},{"start":10,"end":10},{"start":11,"end":11},{"start":12,"end":12},{"start":13,"end":13},{"start":14,"end":14},{"start":15,"end":15},{"start":16,"end":16},{"start":17,"end":17},{"start":18,"end":18},{"start":19,"end":19},{"start":20,"end":20},{"start":21,"end":21},{"start":22,"end":22},{"start":23,"end":23},{"start":24,"end":24},{"start":25,"end":25},{"start":26,"end":26},{"start":27,"end":28},{"start":29,"end":29}],"verses":{"1":"Woe to the crown of pride, to the drunkards of Ephraim, whose glorious beauty is a fading flower, which are on the head of the fat valleys of them that are overcome with wine!","2":"Behold, the Lord hath a mighty and strong one, which as a tempest of hail and a destroying storm, as a flood of mighty waters overflowing, shall cast down to the earth with the hand.","3":"The crown of pride, the drunkards of Ephraim, shall be trodden under feet:","4":"And the glorious beauty, which is on the head of the fat valley, shall be a fading flower, and as the hasty fruit before the summer; which when he that looketh upon it seeth, while it is yet in his hand he eateth it up.","5":"In that day shall the Lord of hosts be for a crown of glory, and for a diadem of beauty, unto the residue of his people,","6":"And for a spirit of judgment to him that sitteth in judgment, and for strength to them that turn the battle to the gate.","7":"But they also have erred through wine, and through strong drink are out of the way; the priest and the prophet have erred through strong drink, they are swallowed up of wine, they are out of the way through strong drink; they err in vision, they stumble in judgment.","8":"For all tables are full of vomit and filthiness, so that there is no place clean.","9":"Whom shall he teach knowledge? and whom shall he make to understand doctrine? them that are weaned from the milk, and drawn from the breasts.","10":"For precept must be upon precept, precept upon precept; line upon line, line upon line; here a little, and there a little:","11":"For with stammering lips and another tongue will he speak to this people.","12":"To whom he said, This is the rest wherewith ye may cause the weary to rest; and this is the refreshing: yet they would not hear.","13":"But the word of the Lord was unto them precept upon precept, precept upon precept; line upon line, line upon line; here a little, and there a little; that they might go, and fall backward, and be broken, and snared, and taken.","14":"Wherefore hear the word of the Lord, ye scornful men, that rule this people which is in Jerusalem.","15":"Because ye have said, We have made a covenant with death, and with hell are we at agreement; when the overflowing scourge shall pass through, it shall not come unto us: for we have made lies our refuge, and under falsehood have we hid ourselves:","16":"Therefore thus saith the Lord God, Behold, I lay in Zion for a foundation a stone, a tried stone, a precious corner stone, a sure foundation: he that believeth shall not make haste.","17":"Judgment also will I lay to the line, and righteousness to the plummet: and the hail shall sweep away the refuge of lies, and the waters shall overflow the hiding place.","18":"And your covenant with death shall be disannulled, and your agreement with hell shall not stand; when the overflowing scourge shall pass through, then ye shall be trodden down by it.","19":"From the time that it goeth forth it shall take you: for morning by morning shall it pass over, by day and by night: and it shall be a vexation only to understand the report.","20":"For the bed is shorter than that a man can stretch himself on it: and the covering narrower than that he can wrap himself in it.","21":"For the Lord shall rise up as in mount Perazim, he shall be wroth as in the valley of Gibeon, that he may do his work, his strange work; and bring to pass his act, his strange act.","22":"Now therefore be ye not mockers, lest your bands be made strong: for I have heard from the Lord God of hosts a consumption, even determined upon the whole earth.","23":"Give ye ear, and hear my voice; hearken, and hear my speech.","24":"Doth the plowman plow all day to sow? doth he open and break the clods of his ground?","25":"When he hath made plain the face thereof, doth he not cast abroad the fitches, and scatter the cummin, and cast in the principal wheat and the appointed barley and the rie in their place?","26":"For his God doth instruct him to discretion, and doth teach him.","27":"For the fitches are not threshed with a threshing instrument, neither is a cart wheel turned about upon the cummin; but the fitches are beaten out with a staff, and the cummin with a rod.","28":"Bread corn is bruised; because he will not ever be threshing it, nor break it with the wheel of his cart, nor bruise it with his horsemen.","29":"This also cometh forth from the Lord of hosts, which is wonderful in counsel, and excellent in working."}},
    "29": {"chapter":29,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: In our last chapter, it seems that Isaiah has turned the script towards Jerusalem. He has given every warning and situation possible to the northern kingdom, but they are lost. They don't turn to the Lord, and so the judgements are falling on them. Judah, however, is not too far behind. They are starting to fall away too, and Isaiah is using the northern kingdom as an example of what could happen to Judah."},{"kind":"para","text":"In this chapter, Isaiah continues to address the sins of Judah. God is basically telling Isaiah that judgement is going to come down on them. They aren't going to listen to the words of Isaiah (or any of the other prophets for that matter (just look at Jeremiah to see)), and they are going to lead themselves further and further away from the Lord. God's judgement is prepared, and WILL come to pass because of their desire to reject Him, and do their own things in their own ways."}],"previously":["In our last chapter, it seems that Isaiah has turned the script towards Jerusalem. He has given every warning and situation possible to the northern kingdom, but they are lost. They don’t turn to the Lord, and so the judgments are falling on them. Judah, however, is not too far behind. They are starting to fall away too, and Isaiah is using the northern kingdom as an example of what could happen to Judah. In this chapter, Isaiah continues to address the sins of Judah. God is basically telling Isaiah that judgment is going to come down on them. They aren’t going to listen to the words of Isaiah (or any of the other prophets for that matter; just look at Jeremiah to see), and they are going to lead themselves further and further away from the Lord. God’s judgment is prepared and WILL come to pass because of their desire to reject Him and do their own things in their own ways."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":4,"title":"Jerusalem's Judgement","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"“Ariel” means “Lion of God.” Obviously, Isaiah is using this name for Jerusalem in this instance. We can rightfully assume this for two reasons. First, this is the only time that anyone in scripture uses this name. Isaiah is giving it its purpose name here. It is certainly falling short of that purpose, though. The only one who will reveal that purpose is Jesus Christ."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And one of the elders saith unto me, Weep not: behold, the Lion of the tribe of Juda, the Root of David, hath prevailed to open the book, and to loose the seven seals thereof.","ref":"Revelation 5:5"},{"kind":"para","text":"That title is redeemed for Christ’s second coming. Secondly, there is no place called “Ariel” at that time. I can’t seem to dig one up anywhere. Besides that, if it was just a new city, they surely wouldn’t name it after the Lord at this time. Also, not to mention the fact that we have a detailed account about everywhere David lived, and Ariel was never on that list. God is telling them to just continue down their road. They aren’t listening to the Lord anyway."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There is a coming judgment to Judah. The reason for the distress they will face is because of the distress they have given the Lord. They have turned so far away, and the Lord knows they will continue to turn down the line, so He is going to have to give judgment. I’m thankful we serve a God who is willing to treat everyone equally. If I deserve judgment, then I should get judgment. I will be judged by the same standard as everyone else."},{"kind":"para","text":"Imagine if we didn’t have a God like this. Imagine our God was more like Satan. He created mankind to increase sin and then get them into a fiery torment for all of eternity. In fact, Hell would be a place made specifically for us and not for the angels. There would be no justice served anywhere, and there would be a whole group of this world that would still serve Satan, even though they know that they will end up in torment for all eternity. Thankfully, our God is not like this, and He is a just, righteous, and loving God who is not willing that any should perish."},{"kind":"para","text":"Satan would have never given himself for the sins of this world. He would have never proven his love to us if we were his creation. No other angel would have either. God is the only one that is just and good. His standards are the only perfect ones. Yet, we abuse Him. We mistreat Him. Judah, at this time, was the last remaining promise of the Lord. God will keep His promise, but the timeline is being shifted because of their rebellion towards Him. Of course, the Lord always knew this was going to take place, but He gave them every reason and possibility to turn before it was too late. In fact, it is still not too late if they just listen to Isaiah’s prophecy."}]},{"start":3,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"“As of one that hath a familiar spirit…” is an interesting choice to depict their coming judgment. They, obviously, won’t all be dead, but they would be so devastated that it would be basically the same thing. They are like living ghosts, walking around this Earth with no free will. Their freedom will be taken by the Lord, who is going to use Babylon to take away Judah’s freewill."},{"kind":"para","text":"We also get an interesting look at “familiar spirits.” There is one assumed instance in scripture where a witch brings back Samuel from the grave. In that instance, we are told that Samuel speaks to Saul in a seemingly loud voice. Of course, (in my opinion) I don’t think any of it is real. We can study that in 1 Samuel, though. God says that if familiar spirits were brought back, they would be whispering. I don’t think you would be able to even hear them, nor would you be able to tell who they were by a whisper. Ghosts only whisper. That’s a comfort for people who think that ghosts are real. But, we know that there is no such thing as “familiar spirits.” When we die, we are with God. Period."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"We are confident, I say, and willing rather to be absent from the body, and to be present with the Lord.","ref":"2 Corinthians 5:8"},{"kind":"para","text":"Paul asserts his certainty about the fact of death. He is confident that we do not remain here. The moment we die, we are with God. Furthermore, Paul addresses how he knows this to be true in the same chapter:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For we must all appear before the judgment seat of Christ; that every one may receive the things done in his body, according to that he hath done, whether it be good or bad.","ref":"2 Corinthians 5:10"},{"kind":"para","text":"God is using familiar spirits as an example, not as a literal representation of Judah. Some will probably die, but those that remain will be as good as dead (or at least feel it)."}]}]},{"start":5,"end":8,"title":"Protection For A Time","entries":[{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Jerusalem is, perhaps, one of the most destroyed cities in the world. It is always being captured. I don’t think it’s possible to walk anything the same today. The promises of capture here are very evident in our day-to-day lives. We know that God had kept His promise, but we can literally and physically see it with our own eyes. Nothing there is what it was originally. They may try to build this street or that place the same way it was built before, but it will never be the same."},{"kind":"para","text":"Solomon built the first temple we see in scripture, placed in Jerusalem. It will be destroyed. Another temple was erected later (we can read that in Nehemiah), but that is destroyed as well. Today, there is a temple there, but it is not the same one from scripture. It is not Solomon’s temple, that’s for sure. Whatever temple is built there again, it will not be the same thing as it was before."}]},{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I think most children are scared of thunderstorms and earthquakes. When I was younger, those things used to scare me. They don’t scare me so much anymore. Earthquakes aren’t all that fun, but thunderstorms are nonessential in my life. There was one, however, that put some fear into me when I was living in Texas. It blew whole trees down and the power stopped working for a little over a day. Most of the car covers (like the little ones that cars park under) were collapsed and destroyed, crushing the cars underneath them. The storm was so severe that you couldn’t see the cars directly in front of you while you were driving. Of course, I was driving on this day because it was a church day (every day was a church day when I was living in Texas)."},{"kind":"para","text":"To Jerusalem, it will be chaos. It will be a giant storm that passes through, and no one is going to be prepared for it. It will cause them to fear. Even a flame of devouring fire will appear and destroy them. Whether literal or symbolic, I don’t know. Perhaps it’s both. The storm that is coming is the nations that are surrounding Jerusalem. They are going to be destroyed by their enemies."}]},{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Honestly, God is going to still protect Judah for a time. He is not going to let the enemy win right off the bat. It will take time for them to take Judah. God is giving them every chance possible to stay the course and turn to Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"As we all know (unless you haven’t read 2 Kings or 2 Chronicles yet), they won’t turn. They will get more and more evil until the Lord has no choice but to let the enemy take them. This is how the other nations will feel when they can’t seem to take Jerusalem as easily as they hoped:"}]},{"start":8,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"These other nations will be passionate about taking over Jerusalem. They will want it with everything in their being. They are willing to do whatever it takes, but nothing will prosper them. Not yet, anyway. Assyria took the northern kingdom pretty easily, and they will come to try and take the south as well, but they won’t succeed. That should have been Judah’s first clue that God was on their side if they just turned. They seem to ignore it, though, and it will be a problem."},{"kind":"para","text":"During this time that Isaiah is speaking about, this is likely when Assyria was making threats to them. They felt as if there was nothing they could do, but God was going to protect them for now."}]}]},{"start":9,"end":12,"title":"A Faulty Lens","entries":[{"start":9,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"They are living in a dream, the people of Israel. They are ignoring the truth and living what they want to. If I can be honest (yet again), most of our church culture today is just like this. They start to get a spiritual high from what the Lord is doing in their churches and begin to stagger around in their spiritual pride. They get behind pulpits and preach a message of repentance, acceptance, and unity, but they are not personally involved with it. Actually, there are some church leaders who downright preach against specific individuals. They are very stern and strict about their love and care for anyone they don’t feel fits their code of conduct. They want to treat one group better than another group. That’s likely a lot of what’s happening with Jerusalem here."},{"kind":"para","text":"God gave them purpose, place, and direction, but they rejected it over and over again to do their own things. They wanted to turn the Lord’s house into something that was for themselves rather than pay close attention to the Lord. They wanted to spend time in their own desires rather than talk to the Lord and spend time with Him. That was what the temple was for. It was for spending time with God. They abused it though, and treated it like a house for any god they chose. Man… when will humanity learn? Perhaps never. Not while sin still exists."}]},{"start":11,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Their biggest issue in the land was that they had God’s Word, but they rejected it. They could access it quickly and open it anytime, yet they claimed, “No one can open this and understand it. It’s too deep. It’s too impossible. It’s too much. It’s too terrible. It’s too… whatever.” They always had an excuse for not reading God’s Word personally. Perhaps the leaders in the temple read it, but they saw what it said and didn’t want anyone else to read it so that things would change in the service of the temple. That was likely the biggest reason for it, and it’s still the reason today."},{"kind":"para","text":"Many religions today don’t encourage their congregants to read scripture by themselves. They claim it has to be interpreted or that a priest or leader must provide understanding. They hand you a Bible along with a missile that is supposed to help you understand scripture, or they give you a Bible and the Book of Mormon, or a Bible and the Apocrypha. In most religions, you have to read scripture through a lens. You can’t just read scripture. This is their way of keeping you from straying onto a path of truth. They just want you to accept their own personal words as truth, and the rest needs to be rejected and never thought of. It keeps you in their safe religious bubble. You miss out on the depths of God’s Word by viewing it through a lens, and you miss out on the connection with God if religion is your sole source of study."},{"kind":"para","text":"Sadly, they have learned this method from Israel. Israel started this whole thing because they liked to worship the false gods in other lands. They enjoyed their sin but didn’t want to completely turn away from the Lord (at least not at first). They wanted God and their sinful life. Eventually, they realized that it doesn’t work that way, so they kept God in the picture but viewed Him only through a lens of their own making. They viewed Him through a lens of false worship and idolatry. As long as God was a part of it (in their eyes), it was okay for them to experiment with whatever they wanted. He didn’t have to be the forefront; He just had to be there somewhere. That is not true."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Thou shalt have no other gods before me.","ref":"Exodus 20:3"},{"kind":"para","text":"That's literally the first commandment."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And thou shalt love the LORD thy God with all thine heart, and with all thy soul, and with all thy might.","ref":"Deuteronomy 6:5"},{"kind":"para","text":"Jesus copies this right into the New Testament church:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And thou shalt love the Lord thy God with all thy heart, and with all thy soul, and with all thy mind, and with all thy strength: this is the first commandment.","ref":"Mark 12:30"},{"kind":"para","text":"When we view God through a religious lens, we cannot love God the way He asks us to love Him."}]}]},{"start":13,"end":14,"title":"Spiritual Bully's","entries":[{"start":13,"end":13,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is the very definition of religious work. Isms today only care about what service looks like, not why we serve. Honestly (and I’m just being honest here, this is no stab or ploy), most of the churches I have been involved with have this same exact point of view. They don’t explain why we are doing these things. They say, “It’s the Baptist way,” or “This is the way we have always done it,” but really there is no rhyme or reason for it."},{"kind":"para","text":"They do mouth service (behind the pulpit, they just talk and preach their hearts out), and they do lip service (in front of the people, they just say “I’m praying for you” and walk away. I doubt any of these so-called “leaders” are actually even praying for you more than they just pray for your name), but they have no heart service (they don’t actually love you like they are supposed to. The Lord gives them a way to love people, but they reject it)."},{"kind":"para","text":"God is very particular about how Christians (especially church leaders) are to run in this life."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Jesus said unto him, Thou shalt love the Lord thy God with all thy heart, and with all thy soul, and with all thy mind. This is the first and great commandment. And the second is like unto it, Thou shalt love thy neighbour as thyself. On these two commandments hang all the law and the prophets.","ref":"Matthew 22:37-40"},{"kind":"para","text":"Most churches have one or the other. They either love God more than anything or love people more than anything. It’s bad to forsake one or the other. If you love God more than anything else and reject people because of your strict love for the Lord, the Lord is against this. He hates it."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"A new commandment I give unto you, That ye love one another; as I have loved you, that ye also love one another.","ref":"John 13:34"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Beloved, let us love one another: for love is of God; and every one that loveth is born of God, and knoweth God.","ref":"1 John 4:7"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And now abideth faith, hope, charity, these three; but the greatest of these is charity.","ref":"1 Corinthians 13:13"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Though I speak with the tongues of men and of angels, and have not charity, I am become as sounding brass, or a tinkling cymbal.","ref":"1 Corinthians 13:1"},{"kind":"para","text":"Love is the theme of faith. I could argue that if you don’t have love for the people around you, whether saved or not, you do not have genuine love for the Lord. However, there are churches that face the opposite problem. They love people more than they love God, and because of this, they are easily swayed. They can fall into all sorts of sins that will lead them away from the hope and faith of the Lord. It becomes more of a business meeting with the Lord, where we just get what we need so we can serve others."},{"kind":"para","text":"I honestly (and again, this is no stab or prod) think that nearly all churches are like this today, including my own. Serving people is great, but it should not be the priority. Ministering is a needed field today, but so is worship. We need to strike a good balance, and it seems that one of these always seems to slip away from us. We miss out on God’s blessings if we are not loving Him first and then loving everyone else secondly. Our love for God should show us how to love others. If it doesn’t, we probably don’t know God appropriately."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And be ye kind one to another, tenderhearted, forgiving one another, even as God for Christ's sake hath forgiven you.","ref":"Ephesians 4:32"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Forbearing one another, and forgiving one another, if any man have a quarrel against any: even as Christ forgave you, so also do ye.","ref":"Colossians 3:13"},{"kind":"para","text":"We don’t learn that lesson either, though, sadly. We don’t know how to love people like God loves us. We are selfish with our love. The Israelites were selfish too. They were claiming religion but just leading everyone away from the Lord. They loved people, but only if they would be willing to waver on their convictions. They were just spiritual bullies, honestly. That is what religions are—spiritual bullies."}]},{"start":14,"end":14,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"They are wise and prudent by their own standards, not by any spiritual ones. Again, that is a major problem in churches today. We don’t seem to understand this from the viewpoint of Israel. We can point the finger at everyone else, but we can’t seem to see ourselves in the mirror of scripture."},{"kind":"para","text":"Pastors and church leaders of all sorts today think they are something special. They act as if they are untouchable. That is my prayer towards them. I pray that the arrogant, prideful leaders would be touched by the Lord, and it would burn them. This includes me if I begin to act this way…"}]}]},{"start":15,"end":16,"title":"Profits for Prophets","entries":[{"start":15,"end":15,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Some people are tricked into their mode of religion, while others are doing it on purpose. I would argue that most of the false church leaders in our day are intentionally going against scripture. They know what scripture says, but instead of questioning their religious methods, they just accept it because it means a paycheck and a pat on the back from their superiors. Recognition is the name of the religious game. I hate it. It’s the same theme in every church in our modern day, by the way. It’s all about titles and climbing the corporate ladder. The moment that titles and church politics are introduced, I shy away from the ministry. It becomes about numerical success, abusing our positions, and less about serving and loving the Lord as well as one another. It becomes about profit and promotion, not calling and devotion. Pardon my French, but a church that falls for this trap deserves to die. The people of Judah deserve to be in this position for this little bit alone. This is not the limit of their sin, however. Their limits go to literal rape and abuse towards innocent people (and children at that). But if it were just abusing their religious standards and turning a profit, I think the Lord has every right to take that church out. He will in the end anyway."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Remember therefore from whence thou art fallen, and repent, and do the first works; or else I will come unto thee quickly, and will remove thy candlestick out of his place, except thou repent.","ref":"Revelation 2:5"},{"kind":"para","text":"I’m still waiting for the Lord to do this in quite a few vain and terrible churches today. Perhaps He already has removed the candle. They are just dark lighthouses now. They look like a lighthouse, but they don’t actually shine the light of the Lord. They have no light. They are profits, not prophets."}]},{"start":16,"end":16,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Yet that is what Israel was doing. They were rejecting the leading and obvious presence of the Lord. They were saying, “It wasn’t God that got us here, it was our own hands.” Whether church leaders openly say it or not, doesn’t matter. Most of them think this way too. God gives them good things, and they take the credit for it."},{"kind":"para","text":"My wife showed me a video the other day about a preacher who preached on who Jesus was. He labeled the things that Jesus wasn’t first, and then explained that He came to give Himself for our sins. It was a great clip, no doubt, but it was a stolen message. My wife said, “Haven’t I heard this before? I’m pretty sure we’ve heard another pastor say this exact same thing.” She is probably right. Pastors take the thoughts of other preachers all the time, and then don’t give credit to who and what it was from. They pawn it off as if it’s their own."},{"kind":"para","text":"The truth is still good no matter who it comes from. It’s right to give credit where credit is due, but as long as the truth is being proclaimed, it doesn’t matter to me who originally said it. The Lord, however, was being completely rejected. Every truth the Lord gave was rejected. The prophets will give absolutes to them, and warn them about the judgments (like Isaiah has been doing for the northern kingdom for some time now), and yet they don’t believe it (or possibly even care)."},{"kind":"para","text":"Churches that reject God’s truth from God’s Word are in danger of God’s judgment. They might think they are shining light, but all they are doing is harboring darkness in their walls."}]}]},{"start":17,"end":21,"title":"A Fruitful Field","entries":[{"start":17,"end":17,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Someday (and it still hasn’t happened yet), the Lord will make Jerusalem live its intended purpose. He will make them a people of His own, and they will live as a “fruitful field.” I don’t think that has ever been the case for Jerusalem since their captivity. I could be wrong. Perhaps there are far smarter people than me who can prove God’s Word wrong here, but I don’t think they will. The time is coming when God will set things straight in our world. Oh boy, I can’t wait for that."}]},{"start":18,"end":18,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Jesus proved this with His miracles over and over again."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And were beyond measure astonished, saying, He hath done all things well: he maketh both the deaf to hear, and the dumb to speak.","ref":"Mark 7:37"},{"kind":"para","text":"I love the book of Mark because it displays so many of God’s miracles to mankind. However, the whole essence of that book was to illustrate God’s ultimate salvation for mankind. It wasn’t just about the miracles; it was about the spirit of the people."},{"kind":"para","text":"Getting to physically see and hear again is great, and I think there are a lot of people who have reason to rejoice over that. But to be spiritually see and hear is far better. If I lost my sight and hearing today (God forbid), I would still be happy to have a spiritual walk that doesn’t require physical sight or physical hearing. It just requires the Holy Spirit of God."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"(For we walk by faith, not by sight:)","ref":"2 Corinthians 5:7"}]},{"start":19,"end":19,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I don’t want to brag (and I don’t mean it as an arrogant thought), but I am an extremely meek person. I know writing that down seems like a prideful thing to say, and it makes me lose credit for my meekness, but I am meek to a fault. I let so many things go. I don’t want to cause waves with people. I think there should be a time for people to use their power to stand up for what is right, but I usually just stay quiet and keep my mind to myself (except for in my notes, I feel open to be a little more transparent). I might say something here or there out of a desire to set records straight, but I usually just let the Lord work on people instead of me taking the initiative. I, honestly, let people walk all over me."},{"kind":"para","text":"With my family, it’s different. I don’t let people walk on them, but for me, I am at the bottom of the pile most of the time, trying to lift everyone up ahead of me. Sometimes I am such a pushover that I let people literally abuse me. I’ve been abused by leaders in the church, in fact. I usually don’t say anything about it. I am also a poor man. I don’t have much as far as financial gain is concerned. I can’t even afford a house in our current economy. So verses like this excite me! I can’t wait for everyone that has been abused and pushed to the side, and those that have not been able to “keep up with the Joneses” (so-to-speak) will have an increased joy, and a place to sit with the Lord."}]},{"start":20,"end":21,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There will be no excuse for anyone to deny the Lord when the “terrible one” is put into an eternity of torment. Yet, we will find that there are a lot of people who still hate the Lord, even in those days."},{"kind":"para","text":"But the Lord will do away with evil here. He will get rid of the high-minded, and He will do it through eliminating Satan and those who follow him. God ALWAYS makes wrongs right. He will ALWAYS serve justice in this world full of injustice. Praise God that He doesn’t let injustice win."}]}]},{"start":22,"end":24,"title":"A Promise","entries":[{"start":22,"end":23,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God will redeem His people. That’s a fact. It’s a promise. A guarantee. If you have any doubts, may you reread these verses again. If you are in the family of God (that is, to know Jesus Christ personally and accept His sacrifice for you), then you are redeemed and saved for the Lord. The Lord will take you to Himself (at least according to scripture). I can’t argue against this truth."},{"kind":"para","text":"We will see His promises come to fruition in time, and when we do, we can rejoice at the fact that He has kept His promise, just in the way He said He would. He always has, and He always will. Every promise given through Isaiah is a promise that has been kept by the Lord, including the coming of the Messiah. Jesus Christ is the solution for this world’s problem. We need Him."}]},{"start":24,"end":24,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Everyone’s going to learn in the end. I don’t believe there is a single person in this world today who is without excuse. All have heard about the Lord in one way or another. We have so many missionaries in our world today. Jesus is being preached. Whether or not people accept or reject it is not up to us, but the Lord leaves them without excuse."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For the invisible things of him from the creation of the world are clearly seen, being understood by the things that are made, even his eternal power and Godhead; so that they are without excuse:","ref":"Romans 1:20"},{"kind":"para","text":"There is no one that is unreachable to the Lord. He will do whatever it takes to seek you out. Whether you accept His seeking is entirely up to you."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For the Son of man is come to seek and to save that which was lost.","ref":"Luke 19:10"},{"kind":"para","text":"May you be in a place where you might be found."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":10},{"start":11,"end":12},{"start":13,"end":13},{"start":14,"end":14},{"start":15,"end":15},{"start":16,"end":16},{"start":17,"end":17},{"start":18,"end":18},{"start":19,"end":19},{"start":20,"end":21},{"start":22,"end":23},{"start":24,"end":24}],"verses":{"1":"Woe to Ariel, to Ariel, the city where David dwelt! add ye year to year; let them kill sacrifices.","2":"Yet I will distress Ariel, and there shall be heaviness and sorrow: and it shall be unto me as Ariel.","3":"And I will camp against thee round about, and will lay siege against thee with a mount, and I will raise forts against thee.","4":"And thou shalt be brought down, and shalt speak out of the ground, and thy speech shall be low out of the dust, and thy voice shall be, as of one that hath a familiar spirit, out of the ground, and thy speech shall whisper out of the dust.","5":"Moreover the multitude of thy strangers shall be like small dust, and the multitude of the terrible ones shall be as chaff that passeth away: yea, it shall be at an instant suddenly.","6":"Thou shalt be visited of the Lord of hosts with thunder, and with earthquake, and great noise, with storm and tempest, and the flame of devouring fire.","7":"And the multitude of all the nations that fight against Ariel, even all that fight against her and her munition, and that distress her, shall be as a dream of a night vision.","8":"It shall even be as when an hungry man dreameth, and, behold, he eateth; but he awaketh, and his soul is empty: or as when a thirsty man dreameth, and, behold, he drinketh; but he awaketh, and, behold, he is faint, and his soul hath appetite: so shall the multitude of all the nations be, that fight against mount Zion.","9":"Stay yourselves, and wonder; cry ye out, and cry: they are drunken, but not with wine; they stagger, but not with strong drink.","10":"For the Lord hath poured out upon you the spirit of deep sleep, and hath closed your eyes: the prophets and your rulers, the seers hath he covered.","11":"And the vision of all is become unto you as the words of a book that is sealed, which men deliver to one that is learned, saying, Read this, I pray thee: and he saith, I cannot; for it is sealed:","12":"And the book is delivered to him that is not learned, saying, Read this, I pray thee: and he saith, I am not learned.","13":"Wherefore the Lord said, Forasmuch as this people draw near me with their mouth, and with their lips do honour me, but have removed their heart far from me, and their fear toward me is taught by the precept of men:","14":"Therefore, behold, I will proceed to do a marvellous work among this people, even a marvellous work and a wonder: for the wisdom of their wise men shall perish, and the understanding of their prudent men shall be hid.","15":"Woe unto them that seek deep to hide their counsel from the Lord, and their works are in the dark, and they say, Who seeth us? and who knoweth us?","16":"Surely your turning of things upside down shall be esteemed as the potter's clay: for shall the work say of him that made it, He made me not? or shall the thing framed say of him that framed it, He had no understanding?","17":"Is it not yet a very little while, and Lebanon shall be turned into a fruitful field, and the fruitful field shall be esteemed as a forest?","18":"And in that day shall the deaf hear the words of the book, and the eyes of the blind shall see out of obscurity, and out of darkness.","19":"The meek also shall increase their joy in the Lord, and the poor among men shall rejoice in the Holy One of Israel.","20":"For the terrible one is brought to nought, and the scorner is consumed, and all that watch for iniquity are cut off:","21":"That make a man an offender for a word, and lay a snare for him that reproveth in the gate, and turn aside the just for a thing of nought.","22":"Therefore thus saith the Lord, who redeemed Abraham, concerning the house of Jacob, Jacob shall not now be ashamed, neither shall his face now wax pale.","23":"But when he seeth his children, the work of mine hands, in the midst of him, they shall sanctify my name, and sanctify the Holy One of Jacob, and shall fear the God of Israel.","24":"They also that erred in spirit shall come to understanding, and they that murmured shall learn doctrine."}},
    "30": {"chapter":30,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: Our last chapter was a warning towards Judah (specifically Jerusalem). God does not want to see them follow suit with the rest of Israel, and it seems that they are headed in that direction already. They haven't fully fallen into the same traps, but God knows they will eventually end up in the same position, and they will have to be taken over as well."},{"kind":"para","text":"In the meantime (in this chapter) God gives them direction. He gives them a place to go. Not to the other nations, but to Himself. He wants His people to turn to Him and trust in Him for comfort and guidance rather than to human authority and protection. If they choose to run for their lives, they will live lives always on the run. God is giving them His heart, and all they have to do is turn to Him and trust in it. For the time being, He is going to protect them, and He wants this to be a learning lesson for them to keep on course with the Lord rather than give themselves over to Satan and his evil ways."}],"previously":["Our last chapter was a warning towards Judah, specifically Jerusalem. God does not want to see them follow suit with the rest of Israel, and it seems that they are headed in that direction already. They haven’t fully fallen into the same traps, but God knows they will eventually end up in the same position and will have to be taken over as well. In the meantime, in this chapter, God gives them direction. He gives them a place to go, not to the other nations, but to Himself. He wants His people to turn to Him and trust in Him for comfort and guidance rather than to human authority and protection. If they choose to run for their lives, they will live lives always on the run. God is giving them His heart, and all they have to do is turn to Him and trust in it. For the time being, He is going to protect them, and He wants this to be a learning lesson for them to keep on course with the Lord rather than give themselves over to Satan and his evil ways."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":5,"title":"Nowhere To Run","entries":[{"start":1,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"If you haven’t noticed, every author in scripture has made a pretty big deal about how the Lord rescued the Israelites out of Egypt. Yet, here they are going back. It seems every time we find our Israelite family going into Egypt, it’s never a good thing. They are usually using Egypt to hide. If Egypt is a picture of the world, perhaps that is the picture for us. When we are going through uncertainty, where do we run first? Do we try to find things of the world to help us hide and numb our pain, or do we turn to the Lord with longing and questions?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Don’t get it twisted; there are some things in this world, given by God, that humans are actually supposed to enjoy. We have plenty of liberty to enjoy a great deal of things (just look at 1 & 2 Corinthians for examples of that), but we tend to abuse those things that the Lord is giving us. Medication is a useful tool, but it becomes a sin when we rely on it. Wine can be a fun celebration substance, but it can be a sin if we rely on it. Even your cellphone can be a great tool for ministry, but it can become a problem when we rely on it."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord wants us to turn to Him and get the answers and comfort we need. Yet, we are seeing the Israelites go to a place where they had been trapped for over four hundred years. They act as if it was the best place they could live, rather than in their God-given homeland."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Behold that which I have seen: it is good and comely for one to eat and to drink, and to enjoy the good of all his labour that he taketh under the sun all the days of his life, which God giveth him: for it is his portion.","ref":"Ecclesiastes 5:18"},{"kind":"para","text":"Recognize the “which God giveth him…” part. Enjoy it if the Lord has given it. Why? Why can’t we just rely on the world? There is plenty of medication today to keep me numb forever, so why can’t I just cling to that? Why turn to the Lord who will not give permanent relief?"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"These things I have spoken unto you, that in me ye might have peace. In the world ye shall have tribulation: but be of good cheer; I have overcome the world.","ref":"John 16:33"},{"kind":"para","text":"The world will not give us \"good cheer.” It will not help us overcome. It will only give us tribulation and trouble."}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is ultimately what trusting in the world looks like: shame and confusion. We are left more empty when we come to the world for help than when we arrived. The Lord gives us eternal solutions, while the world offers only temporal ones. Israel is going back to their captivity, and that is a huge mistake."}]},{"start":4,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"If you don’t get it at this point, you likely never will. Their efforts to hide in Egypt are futile. Not even the princes and ambassadors of the land could do anything to help them. They were completely confounded without the Lord, and they are not getting it."},{"kind":"para","text":"God can say, “You are not going to get help, you will only get shame and a reproach, they will only lead you into confusion…” a million times over, and people still won’t get it. We are such a dull creation. I don’t seem to learn very quickly. I make the same mistakes over and over again. I learn through time, but it takes me a lot longer than your average human. I have to test things differently every time to see if maybe the mistake was just a fluke. Surely it’s not, and I learn my lessons through hazards rather than through conviction."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is what is going on with Israel. They will learn, but it will be through the middle of hazard."}]}]},{"start":6,"end":7,"title":"Our Greatest Strength","entries":[{"start":6,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"They are nothing more than beasts looking for shelter. Interestingly enough, God says that the Egyptians will actually try to help and shelter them. However, He also says it’s done in vain. Their best efforts are still not enough to combat against the Lord. Their smartest solution for this situation? Sit still. Sometimes that is our smartest task forward. We are trying to fight our way through the trial, when God just tells us to sit still. That is our greatest strength."}]}]},{"start":8,"end":11,"title":"No Counsel","entries":[{"start":8,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"And here we are still reading about it today. Isaiah wrote it, but I don’t know how far in the future he thought this would go. He perhaps thought it would end when the Israelites were taken. As soon as Judah was gone, his words were gone too. The Lord doesn’t allow His words to disappear like that. If He wants them preserved, they will be preserved."},{"kind":"para","text":"I was talking to Eva about this the other day. Some people are under the belief that the Bible is not complete. That there are chapters, verses, or even whole books missing from it. That is why we have the likes of the Apocrypha, the Book of Mormon, and even some extra books for Genesis (like personal journals and whatnot, even though they weren’t writing these things down in the beginning because they didn’t have the resources, but what do I know?). There’s a group that believes there is a third Corinthians letter as well (actually, I am under that camp; Paul flat out tells us there was a letter prior to what we consider “1 Corinthians”). Perhaps there are some extra-curricular books that are no longer in scripture, but that is for a purpose. God has seen it fit to not preserve them. He preserves what will lead people to Jesus, and the rest must be thrown out and nonessential."},{"kind":"para","text":"Isaiah’s book leads to Christ. It is sprinkled with Christ in every page and chapter, and it’s one that shows the necessity of His coming because of how far gone all of Israel has become. And not just Israel only, but the entire world. He mentions all the surrounding areas of Israel because they will need a Savior too."}]},{"start":9,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Now, we might read this and think, \"Yeah, this is how they were acting. They were acting as if they just didn't want the Lord.” They weren't just ACTING like this though. They were LITERALLY saying it."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And the king of Israel said unto Jehoshaphat, There is yet one man, Micaiah the son of Imlah, by whom we may enquire of the LORD: but I hate him; for he doth not prophesy good concerning me, but evil. And Jehoshaphat said, Let not the king say so.","ref":"1 Kings 22:8"},{"kind":"para","text":"The whole nation was this way. They wanted to hear good things said about themselves and didn’t want to be corrected. Take an honest evaluation of yourself here. Do YOU like being corrected? I think it’s a human trait to want to just continue in your spiral and direction, even if it’s uncertain or difficult. The Lord can lead you in a better path, and if the path we took is no good, He will tell you. However, we don’t like hearing that we are making a mistake. Pastors certainly don’t like to hear it. As God’s leaders, they are supposed to have everything together and move in the right direction all the time, so if there is counsel telling them that they are making a mistake, they will fight against it with every fiber of their being. They want people to tell them GOOD things about themselves. You can’t do that though. We are told time and time again through scripture to seek righteous counsel."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"The way of a fool is right in his own eyes: but he that hearkeneth unto counsel is wise.","ref":"Proverbs 12:15"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Where no counsel is, the people fall: but in the multitude of counsellors there is safety.","ref":"Proverbs 11:14"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Hear counsel, and receive instruction, that thou mayest be wise in thy latter end.","ref":"Proverbs 19:20"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Without counsel purposes are disappointed: but in the multitude of counsellors they are established.","ref":"Proverbs 15:22"},{"kind":"para","text":"Solomon believed it was crucial to advise his children to listen to wise counsel. He emphasized the importance of seeking Godly advice from others, as it would guide them in the right direction. Interestingly, his son, who became the next king, chose to take counsel from very unwise individuals, leading to a split in Israel. Additionally, church leaders are responsible for giving good counsel."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"My son, forget not my law; but let thine heart keep my commandments:","ref":"Proverbs 3:1"},{"kind":"para","text":"They are to stand side-by-side with their congregants and give encouraging and good advice. Sadly, most pastors are calloused to the happenings in their congregations. They’ve seen and heard it all before, and so they don’t give any instruction, but just leave everyone to their own devices. They might give a passing glance at an issue, but they will just pawn your issue off to someone else because they are too busy with their church duties to deal with it."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is when the congregants go out of their way to take advice from a different source, and you know where it leads them? It gets them away from God, and they do it on purpose. Pastors give God a terrible image by not instructing and counseling their congregants."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Where there is no vision, the people perish: but he that keepeth the law, happy is he.","ref":"Proverbs 29:18"}]}]},{"start":12,"end":14,"title":"From Jars to Bricks","entries":[{"start":12,"end":13,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This seems to insinuate that they haven’t completely fallen victim to sin. They have been able to be (somewhat) protected. They are protected from themselves. Sometimes the Lord does that. He will block certain things and allow certain things in our lives just so we will turn to Him or learn a lesson. But imagine He gave us too much. We would certainly die in an instant from our sin."},{"kind":"para","text":"Now, those that are living in sin and don’t know the Lord are overtaken by their sin. These people, however, have been slowly falling away from the Lord through every generation. They knew God, but they didn’t serve Him alone. They served all their other gods more than the true God of Israel. So God has protected them from some things, but they have gotten so far away that God is just going to open the breach and let them be flooded by their own ways. That is what they wanted anyway, but they will find quite quickly that it was not worth their effort."}]},{"start":14,"end":14,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"They are stubborn pottery. God had been molding them for generations, piece by piece, and they have resisted His shaping and building. Israel was clay pottery. They were fragile and difficult. The church, however, is a new substance."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"In whom all the building fitly framed together groweth unto an holy temple in the Lord:","ref":"Ephesians 2:21"},{"kind":"para","text":"We are building blocks. We are bricks. We are stacked together and held strong by the glue of faith. We can still be broken, but it’s far harder to break a brick than it is to break pottery. Some of us might still be pottery, honestly. We are not molded into anything strong. We are too afraid to protect God’s house, so we are a vase in the middle of the house. That is not what God wants you to be. He wants you to be a strong brick, able to withstand the heat of trials. Actually, He would prefer you to be a gold brick."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"That the trial of your faith, being much more precious than of gold that perisheth, though it be tried with fire, might be found unto praise and honour and glory at the appearing of Jesus Christ:","ref":"1 Peter 1:7"},{"kind":"para","text":"There are not many things that are more resilient in this world than gold. Your spirit, on the other hand, is far more valuable and can be far more malleable with the help of God’s directives. It could also be argued that pottery represents a person’s heart and bricks represent a person’s faith. It’s harder to break someone’s faith than it is to break their heart."},{"kind":"para","text":"From personal experience, I think most church leaders don’t care about whether or not they are breaking your heart, as long as they feel like they are strengthening your faith."}]}]},{"start":15,"end":17,"title":"Wait and Rest","entries":[{"start":15,"end":15,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God has called them to rest. It was Egypt’s strength at the beginning of this chapter, and I truly believe it would have been Israel’s strength too. They would have been a world leader if they had stayed the course and waited on the Lord. That is, perhaps, our biggest mistake as well. We are too impatient. God works too slowly for us to just sit around and wait, so we take things into our own hands because we can deal with it now and then never have to worry about it again. However, when we deal with something, it always comes back to bite us. We never finish a job genuinely. Even this commentary will never actually be finished. The Lord is certainly leading me to write it, but once it’s done, there is still editing, transitioning, pulling quotes, advertising, printing, handling… the list goes on. Then I have the idea to write a teacher’s addition… We can never truly finish anything. Nothing on this planet will ever be finished because we are humans. But God finishes everything. When He’s done, He’s done. On the seventh day of creation, He rested from all His work because there was nothing else for Him to create. He created everything He needed to, and He was finished. We messed it all up by trusting in Satan, but God’s creation account was done. He will never have to create this Earth again. When He died on the cross, He said, “It is finished.” That means He finished salvation and finished the work of the law. He finished His course and gave humanity a way of escape from sin. The debt has been paid, and there is nothing else that can be done. Nothing you can do, nothing your pastor can do, nothing your priests can do, nothing that God can do any further. He has saved you, and He isn’t coming back to die again. He already did it once, forever."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For Christ also hath once suffered for sins, the just for the unjust, that he might bring us to God, being put to death in the flesh, but quickened by the Spirit:","ref":"1 Peter 3:18"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For in that he died, he died unto sin once: but in that he liveth, he liveth unto God.","ref":"Romans 6:10"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But this man, after he had offered one sacrifice for sins for ever, sat down on the right hand of God; From henceforth expecting till his enemies be made his footstool. For by one offering he hath perfected for ever them that are sanctified. Whereof the Holy Ghost also is a witness to us: for after that he had said before, This is the covenant that I will make with them after those days, saith the Lord, I will put my laws into their hearts, and in their minds will I write them; And their sins and iniquities will I remember no more. Now where remission of these is, there is no more offering for sin.","ref":"Hebrews 10:12-18"},{"kind":"para","text":"Now, what do we do? Well, God calls us to REST!"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"There remaineth therefore a rest to the people of God. For he that is entered into his rest, he also hath ceased from his own works, as God did from his. Let us labour therefore to enter into that rest, lest any man fall after the same example of unbelief.","ref":"Hebrews 4:9-11"},{"kind":"para","text":"If you don’t rest in the Lord and find time to just bask in His finished work, you will enter into temptation. You WILL become disobedient, just like the children of Israel. Be a BRICK! People want so badly to be a sword, a voice of reason, a title, a leader, or a valuable member. You will never be those things to anyone. The honest and cold-hearted truth is, churches (today) don’t care about lifting you up. You are better off fighting to be a brick in the church than fighting to be a soldier. It’s God’s Word that is a sword, not yours. Just help build the church, and reject the rest (even if your church leader tells you to be something different). God calls you to rest, and that is what bricks do."}]},{"start":16,"end":17,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"They wanted to run, and that is what they are going to do. God will give them their desire, but they will not find a place to rest. They will keep running, and they will either be overtaken or grow very weary. They are not going to get very far in their running, as there is always going to be someone or something chasing them. That is the reality for all of us today. Perhaps you are tired of your church’s ethics or tired of this person or that person. You can run, but you will always be running because there is no safe place here on Earth."},{"kind":"para","text":"It’s better to just wait on the Lord and rest. As much as I hate to say it, because I have felt this way more times than not, maybe He purposely has you in this stationary position so that you would just rest in Him. He doesn’t want you to move any further; He just wants you to rest a while until He puts things in the right places for you. I hate being stationary. I hate not knowing which way to go or if there is even a place for me. I feel so stuck and lost. But the Lord wants me to wait. What am I waiting for? I don’t know. I’m just waiting until He makes it obvious where I must move to next."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Wait on the LORD: be of good courage, and he shall strengthen thine heart: wait, I say, on the LORD.","ref":"Psalm 27:14"},{"kind":"para","text":"David is a great representation of what it looks like to be stuck waiting on God."}]}]},{"start":18,"end":22,"title":"God Waits","entries":[{"start":18,"end":18,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God waits for you. If you didn’t get anything else from this chapter, you should get this. He is waiting on you. YOU specifically. Not just everyone and everything else to move into place. He waits for you individually. He has His sights on your moving, and your going, and He wants to wait for you to catch up (or come back, because sometimes we might run ahead of Him). He waits for you."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is why we are considered “blessed” to wait for Him. He deserves our waiting. It’s something we must learn to do."}]},{"start":19,"end":19,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is the tender compassion that the Lord wants to give His creation. He wants them to need Him, to want Him, and to turn to Him rather than to their evil ways. Evil hearts will only get you so far. They might put you on a pedestal, but you will befriend all the wrong people and build up all the wrong leaders."},{"kind":"para","text":"Humble hearts will absolutely not get you to the top of anything. In fact, a humble heart is hardly ever noticed or recognized. Humble hearts are the easiest to break. May it not be God’s people that break them. It will be the Lord that lifts up the humble."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Humble yourselves in the sight of the Lord, and he shall lift you up.","ref":"James 4:10"},{"kind":"para","text":"If God lifts humble hearts, then we would be tasked with battling the Lord to try and hurt the humble. I’m pleading with everyone reading, take a good hard look at yourself. Who have you neglected? Who have you not given your time to? Who have you ignored because you just don’t want to deal with them? Are they humble hearts? How miserable you will feel to reject them when you have the opportunity to mold them."}]},{"start":20,"end":21,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I am a man who desires comfort and clarity. I want to know exactly what I am supposed to do and how to do it, with everything set up for me when needed. However, that is not how faith works. We have no idea what is coming, what fork in the road lies ahead, or what traps and trials the enemy has placed in front of us."},{"kind":"para","text":"Because of this, we must learn to be content with trusting God. He will eventually guide us in the right direction or help us out of the traps we have fallen into. While it might seem like it’s taking Him some time to reach us, usually, He has us waiting for a reason. He wants us to be guided by Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"Usually, if we fall into a trap, it is because we were not where we were supposed to be. That is a hard lesson to learn, but it’s one that we all learn at one point or another."}]},{"start":22,"end":22,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Their idols were their comfort, and our idols are OUR comfort today. We have idols, whether we want to admit it or not. We try to find comfort in the closest things to us. For some people, it might be medication; others could find comfort in alcohol. Some people find solace in their churches or in their friends. God wants us to be comforted, and we should understand that. But our ultimate comfort should come from Him. Oh, the joys of having so much comfort from the Lord that we never have to lean on any other kind of comfort in this world again."},{"kind":"para","text":"Don’t misconstrue this; perhaps you need a comforting voice and a guiding light from an individual on this Earth. Perhaps you need someone who can show you love, build you up, and point you in the right direction. I know I need it. We would do well to have godly counsel for such instances. But, ultimately, you must find deep and true comfort from the Lord. I’ve learned to never hold your church, their leaders, or any other trusted figure too close to you. They WILL let you down, and they WILL forsake you in time."}]}]},{"start":23,"end":26,"title":"Reflections of God","entries":[{"start":23,"end":25,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God wants to be our only source of providence too. He is the reason we are sustained. He is the reason you can afford to eat and drink right now. He is the reason you have something to talk about and a spirit to love withal. He is the reason we have to live and continue forward in this life. He is the reason for anything good on this Earth."},{"kind":"para","text":"He provides for us and for the animals around us. He gives us a place to rest and places to resupply. Sometimes we might have to wander for a bit before we get there, though."}]},{"start":26,"end":26,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I love the moon. I think there is something mystical and magical about it. There are nights (living in the high desert) where the moon is shining so bright that you can literally walk around out in the middle of nowhere and still see everything around you. There’s something extremely comforting about that glow. That is what the Lord will give us. It’s not just His material providence, but His comforting presence. I think the moon is a great picture of how God gives us His presence."},{"kind":"para","text":"The presence of God is like the sun. We know it’s there, but we can’t look directly at it without hurting our vision. Even if we wore glasses, we still chance damage to our retinas. We would have to look through some sort of glass or some sort of protection. That is the only way we can view the Lord as well. We can only look at the Lord through a glass."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For now we see through a glass, darkly; but then face to face: now I know in part; but then shall I know even as also I am known.","ref":"1 Corinthians 13:12"},{"kind":"para","text":"Eventually, through death, we will see the Lord face to face. We will not just see Him through a glass or some other means. Until then, we must see Him through a separate means. The sun cannot be viewed directly, but the moon can. It reflects the sun. If the moon is bright and full, we can get the full image of the sun without looking directly at it. We still experience the sun’s presence, but through a different means."},{"kind":"para","text":"God will always provide His presence. He might not be able to give you His full presence (because it would be overwhelming), but He gives you His presence in other ways (through His Spirit or through godly mentors). God gives reflections of Himself; we just have to wait and rest in Him to see it."}]}]},{"start":27,"end":33,"title":"A Victory Over Satan","entries":[{"start":27,"end":28,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God is going to take out the armies that try to harm His people. He has done that over and over again throughout the scriptures and the history of Israel. He has placed special care upon them repeatedly. He will do it again with Assyria, and He will take care of His chosen people. He will not allow Assyria to conquer them. If this proves anything, it should prove that the Lord loves Judah. He is giving them chance after chance to make things right. They will know the heart of God. They will see that God truly does love them. That He is giving them everything they need. They just need to rest in Him. They don’t need to run and hide; they need to turn and repent. That is what we need if we want to see God deal with our enemy of sin or trouble. We just need to turn to Him and trust that He is speaking the truth about His love."}]},{"start":29,"end":30,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The day is dark, but the Lord is good. He will give us a reason to sing because He is always on our side, and He will always show His love to us. He will always be the anchor for our souls and the light for our paths. He will always be the one who raises us up and protects us from harm. He will always be the one who feeds us, keeps us, guides us, and leads us. He will never leave us nor forsake us."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Be strong and of a good courage, fear not, nor be afraid of them: for the LORD thy God, he it is that doth go with thee; he will not fail thee, nor forsake thee.","ref":"Deuteronomy 31:6"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Let your conversation be without covetousness; and be content with such things as ye have: for he hath said, I will never leave thee, nor forsake thee.","ref":"Hebrews 13:5"},{"kind":"para","text":"God truly is good, all the time."}]},{"start":31,"end":33,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Tophet was apparently a very bad place. They performed the worst kinds of sacrifices and engaged in false worship in that land. He is going to light them up with nothing else to show for it. Perhaps He will place these types into the deepest parts of the pit of fire. That is what Tophet is—the hottest part of Hell. “Tophet” means “place of fire.” It was destined to be the worst kind of place. I believe there are layers to Hell, just as there are layers to a fire. The blue part is hotter than the yellow part, and the center of the fire is where the real heat resides. Hell will have heat differences as well. Satan will be in the deepest parts, and I assume these people will be there with him, for they are undoubtedly being used by him. That is who I believe “the king” is in this verse—Satan. And all of God’s children will rejoice when he is finally put into this place because we know that he will never be able to lead anyone astray ever again. God will keep Him locked in there for all of eternity."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":11},{"start":12,"end":13},{"start":14,"end":14},{"start":15,"end":15},{"start":16,"end":17},{"start":18,"end":18},{"start":19,"end":19},{"start":20,"end":21},{"start":22,"end":22},{"start":23,"end":25},{"start":26,"end":26},{"start":27,"end":28},{"start":29,"end":30},{"start":31,"end":33}],"verses":{"1":"Woe to the rebellious children, saith the Lord, that take counsel, but not of me; and that cover with a covering, but not of my spirit, that they may add sin to sin:","2":"That walk to go down into Egypt, and have not asked at my mouth; to strengthen themselves in the strength of Pharaoh, and to trust in the shadow of Egypt!","3":"Therefore shall the strength of Pharaoh be your shame, and the trust in the shadow of Egypt your confusion.","4":"For his princes were at Zoan, and his ambassadors came to Hanes.","5":"They were all ashamed of a people that could not profit them, nor be an help nor profit, but a shame, and also a reproach.","6":"The burden of the beasts of the south: into the land of trouble and anguish, from whence come the young and old lion, the viper and fiery flying serpent, they will carry their riches upon the shoulders of young asses, and their treasures upon the bunches of camels, to a people that shall not profit them.","7":"For the Egyptians shall help in vain, and to no purpose: therefore have I cried concerning this, Their strength is to sit still.","8":"Now go, write it before them in a table, and note it in a book, that it may be for the time to come for ever and ever:","9":"That this is a rebellious people, lying children, children that will not hear the law of the Lord:","10":"Which say to the seers, See not; and to the prophets, Prophesy not unto us right things, speak unto us smooth things, prophesy deceits:","11":"Get you out of the way, turn aside out of the path, cause the Holy One of Israel to cease from before us.","12":"Wherefore thus saith the Holy One of Israel, Because ye despise this word, and trust in oppression and perverseness, and stay thereon:","13":"Therefore this iniquity shall be to you as a breach ready to fall, swelling out in a high wall, whose breaking cometh suddenly at an instant.","14":"And he shall break it as the breaking of the potters' vessel that is broken in pieces; he shall not spare: so that there shall not be found in the bursting of it a sherd to take fire from the hearth, or to take water withal out of the pit.","15":"For thus saith the Lord God, the Holy One of Israel; In returning and rest shall ye be saved; in quietness and in confidence shall be your strength: and ye would not.","16":"But ye said, No; for we will flee upon horses; therefore shall ye flee: and, We will ride upon the swift; therefore shall they that pursue you be swift.","17":"One thousand shall flee at the rebuke of one; at the rebuke of five shall ye flee: till ye be left as a beacon upon the top of a mountain, and as an ensign on an hill.","18":"And therefore will the Lord wait, that he may be gracious unto you, and therefore will he be exalted, that he may have mercy upon you: for the Lord is a God of judgment: blessed are all they that wait for him.","19":"For the people shall dwell in Zion at Jerusalem: thou shalt weep no more: he will be very gracious unto thee at the voice of thy cry; when he shall hear it, he will answer thee.","20":"And though the Lord give you the bread of adversity, and the water of affliction, yet shall not thy teachers be removed into a corner any more, but thine eyes shall see thy teachers:","21":"And thine ears shall hear a word behind thee, saying, This is the way, walk ye in it, when ye turn to the right hand, and when ye turn to the left.","22":"Ye shall defile also the covering of thy graven images of silver, and the ornament of thy molten images of gold: thou shalt cast them away as a menstruous cloth; thou shalt say unto it, Get thee hence.","23":"Then shall he give the rain of thy seed, that thou shalt sow the ground withal; and bread of the increase of the earth, and it shall be fat and plenteous: in that day shall thy cattle feed in large pastures.","24":"The oxen likewise and the young asses that ear the ground shall eat clean provender, which hath been winnowed with the shovel and with the fan.","25":"And there shall be upon every high mountain, and upon every high hill, rivers and streams of waters in the day of the great slaughter, when the towers fall.","26":"Moreover the light of the moon shall be as the light of the sun, and the light of the sun shall be sevenfold, as the light of seven days, in the day that the Lord bindeth up the breach of his people, and healeth the stroke of their wound.","27":"Behold, the name of the Lord cometh from far, burning with his anger, and the burden thereof is heavy: his lips are full of indignation, and his tongue as a devouring fire:","28":"And his breath, as an overflowing stream, shall reach to the midst of the neck, to sift the nations with the sieve of vanity: and there shall be a bridle in the jaws of the people, causing them to err.","29":"Ye shall have a song, as in the night when a holy solemnity is kept; and gladness of heart, as when one goeth with a pipe to come into the mountain of the Lord, to the mighty One of Israel.","30":"And the Lord shall cause his glorious voice to be heard, and shall shew the lighting down of his arm, with the indignation of his anger, and with the flame of a devouring fire, with scattering, and tempest, and hailstones.","31":"For through the voice of the Lord shall the Assyrian be beaten down, which smote with a rod.","32":"And in every place where the grounded staff shall pass, which the Lord shall lay upon him, it shall be with tabrets and harps: and in battles of shaking will he fight with it.","33":"For Tophet is ordained of old; yea, for the king it is prepared; he hath made it deep and large: the pile thereof is fire and much wood; the breath of the Lord, like a stream of brimstone, doth kindle it."}},
    "31": {"chapter":31,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: Isaiah spent a good portion of our last chapter encouraging Jerusalem to turn to the Lord. Honestly, that was his main mission from the beginning of this book. That was Christ's main mission as well. The healing and miracles were great, but that was not His most prominent goal. His goal was to get people to trust in the Lord alone, and thousands of years later that is STILL the mission. Isaiah is using the flaws of the northern kingdom as an example of what NOT to follow and do."},{"kind":"para","text":"In this chapter, He gives some compelling arguments as to why you shouldn't trust this Earth to protect and help you. This Earth is feeble and flawed, and when we trust in anything here it never actually resolves any of our problems. We will find out what the things of this world ultimately get us when we trust in them in this chapter."}],"previously":["Isaiah spent a good portion of our last chapter encouraging Jerusalem to turn to the Lord. Honestly, that was his main mission from the beginning of this book. That was Christ’s main mission as well. The healing and miracles were great, but that was not His most prominent goal. His goal was to get people to trust in the Lord alone, and thousands of years later, that is still the mission. Isaiah is using the flaws of the northern kingdom as an example of what not to follow and do. In this chapter, he gives some compelling arguments as to why you shouldn’t trust this Earth to protect and help you. This Earth is feeble and flawed, and when we trust in anything here, it never actually resolves any of our problems. We will find out what the things of this world ultimately get us when we trust in them in this chapter."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":3,"title":"Trust God","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"You should feel personally afflicted here. Everything, may we remember, in scripture is focused on Christ. It’s focused on His first and second coming. He came once, and now we have a reason to trust in Him. He’s coming again, and so we still have reason to look to Him and seek Him out."},{"kind":"para","text":"Yet, we have a large group of Christians who turn away from the Lord when things are getting tough. They have a broken spirit, and the first person they blame is God. The church does something they don’t like, so therefore they will never trust God again, and they go back to the world. People are supposed to be representatives for the Lord, but I just have to tell you today that they really aren’t."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"He must increase, but I must decrease.","ref":"John 3:30"},{"kind":"para","text":"We are poor representatives of Christ. As a church, we are supposed to be more like Him every day, but I don’t see anyone striving for that. They strive to put themselves on top, but not to display Christ. Sadly, because we are like this, the church is useless if we are not loving people like Jesus loves us."},{"kind":"para","text":"We trust ourselves more than we trust the Lord. The Israelites fell for the same traps, and now they are going to suffer the consequences of their own power. Rejecting God and trusting the world always only gets you one thing, and it isn’t victory. Everyone tries to find help in all the wrong places when we can just look to Heaven and request support, and it will be granted to us."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"What God has said is final. Nothing you read in scripture was a mistake. He didn’t give prophecies and then take them back. He doesn’t give salvation and then reject salvation from you. He doesn’t provide the Holy Spirit and then take it away. When He saves you, it’s final. When He changes you, it’s final. When He says something to this world, it is final. That is how we know we can trust it."},{"kind":"para","text":"He doesn’t regret His answers, and He doesn’t change His mind about any matter. He WILL NOT call back His words. But because of this, He will also punish those He says He will punish and give justice to those that deserve His justice."}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"If it’s not obvious enough for you, Isaiah had to break down why they shouldn’t trust in these worldly things. You don’t trust in them because they are not eternal. If you are trusting in the world for eternal problems, you will never have victory. Honestly, if you trust in the world for any sort of problem you might be facing, you will just have more problems."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Egyptians were men, trying to help the Israelites with spiritual problems. The horses were just flesh, trying to help the Israelites with spiritual problems. If they wanted a solution, they needed God and His Spirit."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Some trust in chariots, and some in horses: but we will remember the name of the LORD our God.","ref":"Psalm 20:7"},{"kind":"para","text":"I suppose this might be a good time to evaluate yourself. When you have a problem, where are you likely to go? You probably look for a materialistic solution. I know I do more times than not. However, it doesn’t help, and we are left waiting on the Lord anyway. We should make Him our first stop so we know how to address the problems further, rather than our last resort when we have no other choice but to turn to Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Israelites were still not turning to Him. They needed to learn some hard lessons before their pride would be broken and they would finally trust in their Creator. That usually takes quite a bit of time."}]}]},{"start":4,"end":5,"title":"Children of God","entries":[{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God is our shepherd. A lot of pastors would probably agree that they are your “undershepherd.” However, this is not something that is spoken about in scripture. We do get this from Peter, though."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Feed the flock of God which is among you, taking the oversight thereof, not by constraint, but willingly; not for filthy lucre, but of a ready mind; Neither as being lords over God's heritage, but being ensamples to the flock. And when the chief Shepherd shall appear, ye shall receive a crown of glory that fadeth not away.","ref":"1 Peter 5:2-4"},{"kind":"para","text":"Honestly, I’m not sure you’d want most of these pastors to be your shepherd anyway. The Lord is our shepherd alone. He is the good shepherd:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"I am the good shepherd: the good shepherd giveth his life for the sheep.","ref":"John 10:11"},{"kind":"para","text":"As a pastor, they are supposed to do this too, but you won’t find many who would (if any at all). Because of this, we cannot trust them to defend us or lead us appropriately. We must ALL depend upon the Lord as our individual strength."},{"kind":"para","text":"The church should be unified under this same belief, but if no one else in the church is willing to turn to Christ in these matters, and if everyone is looking to your pastor, it is a wise man’s job to turn to Christ alone. HE saves. No one else is coming for you."}]},{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"We can tell birds apart. We know they are birds because of one specific thing that they do that none of the other creatures can do—that’s flying. It seems birds need to fly. There’s something in them that just jolts when they are born. They have the unction and desire to spread their wings."},{"kind":"para","text":"As birds have that need, the Lord has the need to defend His people. In this case, He is going to defend Jerusalem. They will, ultimately, reject it, but there will be a time when God will protect His children, and we have the opportunity to be under that protection if we choose to be. Today, He has called you into His protection."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But the Lord is faithful, who shall stablish you, and keep you from evil.","ref":"2 Thessalonians 3:3"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But let all those that put their trust in thee rejoice: let them ever shout for joy, because thou defendest them: let them also that love thy name be joyful in thee.","ref":"Psalm 5:11"},{"kind":"para","text":"Of course, this is a prophet, so his words are for the present, future, and end. Jerusalem is very specific. He will preserve Jerusalem in the fight against the Assyrians. He will keep them safe. He will bring them back when Babylon has completed its course. I do believe He will bring them back in the end as well. In the end, though, the world is included in this. We ALL get to be a part of God’s preservation if we are under His protection. Jerusalem is an image of God’s children. Egypt is an image of the world. If we are His children, we are protected. If we are children of the world… well, we are enemies of God."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Ye adulterers and adulteresses, know ye not that the friendship of the world is enmity with God? whosoever therefore will be a friend of the world is the enemy of God.","ref":"James 4:4"}]}]},{"start":6,"end":9,"title":"With Christ","entries":[{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God has granted this whole world the opportunity of repentance. Those who trust in Christ will turn to God, while those who do not trust in Christ will not. It’s really that simple. We have multiple examples of what the world turns into if we reject the Lord. We see what we start to become without Christ. We become quite evil, so evil that we abuse all of mankind around us. We become calloused and cold to this world and the people around us. Without Christ, the world turns to evil. Without Christ, we abuse people, hurt people, kill people, and rob people materially, spiritually, and mentally. Without Christ, we are just human flesh, with no spirit, relying on our own strength, and having no direction for trials. We are lost, unable to love, and are merely the sum of our actions. We are extremely evil without Christ. Sin becomes a friend to us, and there is nothing holding us back from exploring deeper and deeper into our sins."},{"kind":"para","text":"Those with Christ will fail, but at least they have a reason to try for humanity. With Christ, the world turns to good. With Christ, we love people, support people, heal people, and give to people mentally, spiritually, and materially. With Christ, we are a Spirit, filled with His Spirit, relying on His strength rather than our weaknesses. With Christ, we have an anchor to hold us through trials. With Christ, we are found, love like Him, and our sins are forgiven. We are hopeful when we have Christ. This is an evaluation for yourself. If you are with Christ, are you pursuing any of these things? If you are pursuing them, how successful are you? With Christ, you can do these things."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"I can do all things through Christ which strengtheneth me.","ref":"Philippians 4:13"},{"kind":"para","text":"The people of the world will find every reason to turn away from the Lord and trust in the world, but those that belong to God should find every reason possible to stay."}]},{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"We discussed this in the last chapter, but the truth is that we all struggle with idolatry in some form. We find comfort and ease from things on this Earth, and that is why many reject the Lord. Why accept Christ and His change when drugs will give me a good fix? The problem with drugs, though, is that they wear off. They also cause other bodily and mental problems. It’s as if the Lord has created our minds, bodies, and spirits to need Him."}]},{"start":8,"end":9,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"We will have victory, not by our own strength, but by the strength of the Lord. God makes it abundantly clear that trusting in our own strength will get us nowhere. We must trust God’s power and moving. Faith is a difficult thing to live with, but it’s the only requirement the Lord has in a relationship with Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"Nobody wants to live by faith. We all want to live by sight. But only those who live by faith first will see and feel God’s presence in their lives. It should be rightfully understood by the reader that God is not going to work without His signature somewhere. He always proves Himself in some way."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Prove all things; hold fast that which is good.","ref":"1 Thessalonians 5:21"},{"kind":"para","text":"We should test everything and be able to show the results. The Lord tests and always shows results. If anyone denies the Lord, it is because they deny the results of His actions. They will have to deny proof. “The princes shall be afraid of the ensign” tells us that they will see something to be afraid of. They will see some sort of sign. We don’t need to look for a sign to have faith in the Lord. We need the Lord to do what He says He will and trust His process to do it."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":9}],"verses":{"1":"Woe to them that go down to Egypt for help; and stay on horses, and trust in chariots, because they are many; and in horsemen, because they are very strong; but they look not unto the Holy One of Israel, neither seek the Lord!","2":"Yet he also is wise, and will bring evil, and will not call back his words: but will arise against the house of the evildoers, and against the help of them that work iniquity.","3":"Now the Egyptians are men, and not God; and their horses flesh, and not spirit. When the Lord shall stretch out his hand, both he that helpeth shall fall, and he that is holpen shall fall down, and they all shall fail together.","4":"For thus hath the Lord spoken unto me, Like as the lion and the young lion roaring on his prey, when a multitude of shepherds is called forth against him, he will not be afraid of their voice, nor abase himself for the noise of them: so shall the Lord of hosts come down to fight for mount Zion, and for the hill thereof.","5":"As birds flying, so will the Lord of hosts defend Jerusalem; defending also he will deliver it; and passing over he will preserve it.","6":"Turn ye unto him from whom the children of Israel have deeply revolted.","7":"For in that day every man shall cast away his idols of silver, and his idols of gold, which your own hands have made unto you for a sin.","8":"Then shall the Assyrian fall with the sword, not of a mighty man; and the sword, not of a mean man, shall devour him: but he shall flee from the sword, and his young men shall be discomfited.","9":"And he shall pass over to his strong hold for fear, and his princes shall be afraid of the ensign, saith the Lord, whose fire is in Zion, and his furnace in Jerusalem."}},
    "32": {"chapter":32,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: In our last chapter, Isaiah continues to give warnings to the people of Judah about what will take place if they don't turn to the Lord, or if they continue in their spiral away from the Lord. They are commissioned to trust God, remember they are the children of God, and to turn to salvation (which is found in Jesus Christ alone). Of course, we know, they won't listen and eventually they learn the hard way what this world looks like when we are against the Lord and leading others astray."},{"kind":"para","text":"I have to say, you start reading these dismul stories (at least from my viewpoint) and you start to lose some sense of hope. You feel as if there is a lot of burden pressing against you even though most of this has already happened to Israel, and you know you are secure from any wrath that is to come in the future, it's still a heavy burden knowing that God will pour this out on mankind, and there will be people who you might know and love who will face it. But this chapter brings a lot of alleviation. It brings hope and security to the believers. It's a chapter that can't be overlooked or just read through quickly. It's a rich chapter about the kingdom of God! This chapter (if anything) should give every believer the strength and courage to keep fighting for the salvation of those around you. It should give us a reason to give others Christ. Because we will give account to the Lord, we must not leave a stone unturned. We are tasked with a job, and we should do that job if we are going to please our Father."}],"previously":["In our last chapter, Isaiah continues to give warnings to the people of Judah about what will take place if they don’t turn to the Lord or if they continue in their spiral away from Him. They are commissioned to trust God, remember they are the children of God, and to turn to salvation, which is found in Jesus Christ alone. Of course, we know they won’t listen and eventually learn the hard way what this world looks like when we are against the Lord and leading others astray. I have to say, when you start reading these dismal stories (at least from my viewpoint), you begin to lose some sense of hope. You feel as if there is a lot of burden pressing against you even though most of this has already happened to Israel. You know you are secure from any wrath that is to come in the future, but it’s still a heavy burden knowing that God will pour this out on mankind, and there will be people you might know and love who will face it. However, this chapter brings a lot of alleviation. It brings hope and security to the believers. It’s a chapter that can’t be overlooked or just read through quickly. It’s a rich chapter about the kingdom of God! This chapter, if anything, should give every believer the strength and courage to keep fighting for the salvation of those around you. It should give us a reason to give others Christ. Because we will give account to the Lord, we must not leave a stone unturned. We are tasked with a job, and we should do that job if we are going to please our Father."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":8,"title":"A Righteous King","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There is only one King who will reign in righteousness. We have had a couple of presidents who have been righteous, but they were not even close to proper rulers. Israel only had a handful of righteous kings, but that didn’t get them into prosperity because there were far more kings ruining it for everyone than there were leading people to the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"No, there will be a King of this Earth who will reign in righteousness, and He alone will be worthy of the throne. His name, of course, is Jesus Christ. That is what He will be doing when He returns. He will not come back as merely a servant; He will come back as a King. It could be argued that the first time He came, He established His kingdom."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And when he was demanded of the Pharisees, when the kingdom of God should come, he answered them and said, The kingdom of God cometh not with observation: Neither shall they say, Lo here! or, lo there! for, behold, the kingdom of God is within you.","ref":"Luke 17:20-21"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And saying, The time is fulfilled, and the kingdom of God is at hand: repent ye, and believe the gospel.","ref":"Mark 1:15"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Jesus answered and said unto him, Verily, verily, I say unto thee, Except a man be born again, he cannot see the kingdom of God.","ref":"John 3:3"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And as ye go, preach, saying, The kingdom of heaven is at hand.","ref":"Matthew 10:7"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And Pilate wrote a title, and put it on the cross. And the writing was, JESUS OF NAZARETH THE KING OF THE JEWS.","ref":"John 19:19"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For the kingdom of God is not meat and drink; but righteousness, and peace, and joy in the Holy Ghost.","ref":"Romans 14:17"},{"kind":"para","text":"Jesus never denied God's kingdom, and He never denied His rulership. He is King."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Which in his times he shall shew, who is the blessed and only Potentate, the King of kings, and Lord of lords;","ref":"1 Timothy 6:15"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"These shall make war with the Lamb, and the Lamb shall overcome them: for he is Lord of lords, and King of kings: and they that are with him are called, and chosen, and faithful.","ref":"Revelation 17:14"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And he hath on his vesture and on his thigh a name written, KING OF KINGS, AND LORD OF LORDS.","ref":"Revelation 19:16"},{"kind":"para","text":"There is no mistaking who it is that needs to rule our world. No one else is suited for that position. We’ve seen too many people try to rule even the smallest portions of the world and fail miserably."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I think it should also be established that Jesus will not just be a ruler. He is still the Savior. He doesn’t change His roles, just His placement. He is ruling and reigning from Heaven now, but when He returns, He will rule and reign here on Earth (before our eyes). But He is still the Savior. He is still the protector of mankind. He is still a trusted source to run to during those days."},{"kind":"para","text":"The major problem is that no one (left on Earth) will ever trust Him, and so they will reject Him, and He will have to get rid of them when the time comes. Only those who have turned to Him before His return will be saved because they believed in Him by faith. You cannot turn to Christ after seeing Him. He requires your faith."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But without faith it is impossible to please him: for he that cometh to God must believe that he is, and that he is a rewarder of them that diligently seek him.","ref":"Hebrews 11:6"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For by grace are ye saved through faith; and that not of yourselves: it is the gift of God: Not of works, lest any man should boast.","ref":"Ephesians 2:8-9"},{"kind":"para","text":"It's not just about BELIEVING there is a God. It's about having purposeful and actual FAITH in God."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Thou believest that there is one God; thou doest well: the devils also believe, and tremble.","ref":"James 2:19"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Now faith is the substance of things hoped for, the evidence of things not seen.","ref":"Hebrews 11:1"},{"kind":"para","text":"This Man (Jesus Christ) will be a hiding place, and a covert. He will be our river of living water, and a great rock in a weary land, even while He is reigning and ruling here on Earth."}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Everyone in this world will be enlightened with the presence of the Lord. He will provide us with a deeper and more appropriate sight. We will hear and understand far better than we ever have before. His presence gives us greater perspective."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For this people's heart is waxed gross, and their ears are dull of hearing, and their eyes they have closed; lest at any time they should see with their eyes, and hear with their ears, and should understand with their heart, and should be converted, and I should heal them. But blessed are your eyes, for they see: and your ears, for they hear. For verily I say unto you, That many prophets and righteous men have desired to see those things which ye see, and have not seen them; and to hear those things which ye hear, and have not heard them.","ref":"Matthew 13:15-17"},{"kind":"para","text":"Once again, only those who have Christ will perceive who He truly is. Even though all the evidence is before them, they will reject and hate Him. They didn’t learn from His first coming, so what makes us think anyone will learn at His second?"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"In whom the god of this world hath blinded the minds of them which believe not, lest the light of the glorious gospel of Christ, who is the image of God, should shine unto them.","ref":"2 Corinthians 4:4"},{"kind":"para","text":"I know before I was saved, all of this God stuff was just a big question mark. None of it made sense. My brother bought me my first Bible, and I brought it to school. I wanted to understand what he saw in this book. I got in trouble for reading it during my lunch hour. I was by myself. The yard duty said that she would confiscate it if I took it out again. That led to even bigger question marks. Why did she care if I was reading this book? Isn’t that what the school wants me to do—read and learn? Apparently, anything other than the Bible, I guess. So I tucked it away and never took it out again (I was a pretty good kid and hardly ever got into trouble at that time anyway). I would pick it up at home from time to time but still never got it. Interesting stories. About all I could say. It wasn’t until I just accepted that Christ was the Savior that my eyes and ears were opened. Suddenly I understood this book, and I related to the preaching. A whole new realm was opened to me, and I could witness spiritual things. Now I’m writing commentaries…"},{"kind":"para","text":"Faith is the key to this spiritual ignition. If you don’t have the key, your walk cannot start with the Lord. You will never have ears or eyes for His Word without faith to guide you."}]},{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Jesus’ presence will also make people understand, and the quiet will preach! Possibly even sing! If you are not a preacher or a singer here on Earth, don’t fret; the Lord will make you one when He returns."},{"kind":"para","text":"It is another thing that I never thought I would become. I would purposely fail classes in school if it meant I had to get up in front of people and give a report. I loathed it. Yet, God has called me to literally do exactly that about His Word. He calls us all to preach the scriptures and witness to people."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And he said unto them, Go ye into all the world, and preach the gospel to every creature. He that believeth and is baptized shall be saved; but he that believeth not shall be damned.","ref":"Mark 16:15-16"},{"kind":"para","text":"Mark, the writer of the Gospel of Mark, was not even present when Jesus commissioned the disciples. Yet, we know that Mark becomes a valuable preacher of the gospel in the Book of Acts, as well as according to Peter and Paul. He took the commission to his own heart, and God greatly used him. Anyone who takes the commission seriously will be a great vessel for the Lord’s work."},{"kind":"para","text":"However, when He comes again, we will not really have a need to preach to the lost of this world. Why does God give us a tongue to speak at all? Well, we are supposed to use our tongues to edify and fellowship with the saints. We are not solemnly called to preach to the lost; we are called to preach to the saved."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Wherefore comfort yourselves together, and edify one another, even as also ye do.","ref":"1 Thessalonians 5:11"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Not forsaking the assembling of ourselves together, as the manner of some is; but exhorting one another: and so much the more, as ye see the day approaching.","ref":"Hebrews 10:25"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Iron sharpeneth iron; so a man sharpeneth the countenance of his friend.","ref":"Proverbs 27:17"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"That which we have seen and heard declare we unto you, that ye also may have fellowship with us: and truly our fellowship is with the Father, and with his Son Jesus Christ.","ref":"1 John 1:3"},{"kind":"para","text":"That is a neglected trait in our modern churches today, but we will never neglect it again when Jesus returns. We might not know what to say to our neighbors in the faith today, but we will in eternity."}]},{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I have a lot of political jokes to say here, but I will not stoop to such a crass and degrading level. Obviously, a “vile person” is someone who does evil things, and they overflow with their evil. That will not happen anymore when Jesus is present. Things will be set right, and people will act right. Jesus will provide an attitude check. Jesus already provides this, but it seems some people don’t understand the hint. It’s an important reminder to us to look to God rather than to people today. Even our own leaders will fail. Some (I firmly believe) fail on purpose. They want to make enemies of the people under them. Church leaders even. That’s not how God wants us to lead, but we don’t understand that for some reason. In Jesus’ presence, however, we will get the hint and we will learn quickly. Don’t trust in God’s creation to help you. God’s creation can teach you, but they can’t help you. Only the Lord will do that…"}]},{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Here’s some news that you might not have known. A vile person will speak villany, and that person will do evil things to you. He will tell you to do one thing and never actually do it himself. He will also lie to you about the Lord, and you will walk away from him feeling more hungry and more thirsty, even if he offers you food and a drink."},{"kind":"para","text":"Sadly, I know far too many people who are like this. They are too much a part of the world. Even people who are leaders in churches can be like this. They are leaders by title, not by calling. Jesus has a place for them, and certainly a purpose for them."}]},{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"An evil man doesn’t care about what is right; they just care about themselves. Honestly, that is the perfect way for us to figure out if someone has pure intentions or evil intentions. Is this going to benefit them, or is this going to benefit others? If it’s just to benefit them, then your best bet is to abstain from getting involved. Be on guard, even in the most trusted places, about what you are doing and who you are doing it for."}]},{"start":8,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Just as the evil of people will be on full display, the generosity of people will be too. If I can be honest, these perhaps walk hand-in-hand. A generous giver is not necessarily a bad thing, but in our modern world, it’s usually for an evil reason that anyone is giving so generously. Not always, but usually. More often than not, the giver is getting something out of it, and that is the only reason they give. It’s not so they can just show love; it’s so they can get a return."},{"kind":"para","text":"If someone is giving to a church, it’s usually for a purpose. They are giving towards something, not just because they want to show love. And, honestly, the preachers are usually asking you to give for something, and hardly ever asking you to give simply because you have a heart to give. No, there is always a motive, and that usually leads to evil generosity. We give liberally because we want to receive liberally. The pastor of my church always says, “What you give is what you will get. Sow the things you need to receive.” Noble thought and cause, and I am accustomed to believe him."},{"kind":"para","text":"However, we should not just be giving so we get something from it. That is not the biblical way of giving. Rather, we should give because we have a heart for it. No one can give us a heart of giving unless we have a heart from God. It’s not about what can benefit me. It’s about what can benefit everyone around me. Give because you love God and you love your brothers and sisters in the church. If there’s something tied to your giving, it’s better to refrain from giving. Whatever you are giving for will ultimately be your reward."}]}]},{"start":9,"end":15,"title":"Freedom Rings","entries":[{"start":9,"end":9,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Yeah, woman! You careless daughters! It might seem strange that Isaiah is just pointing out women here. The truth is, women are not very good at listening, is why… I’m just kidding! Please don’t hurt me. Honestly, he probably points out women specifically for a couple of reasons. One is that they are far more inclined to listen than men are. Men are really just flat-out dumb. Two is because God considers the land of His people as His daughter."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Rejoice greatly, O daughter of Zion; shout, O daughter of Jerusalem: behold, thy King cometh unto thee: he is just, and having salvation; lowly, and riding upon an ass, and upon a colt the foal of an ass.","ref":"Zechariah 9:9"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Sing, O daughter of Zion; shout, O Israel; be glad and rejoice with all the heart, O daughter of Jerusalem.","ref":"Zephaniah 3:14"},{"kind":"para","text":"He also considers His church as His bride:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And I John saw the holy city, new Jerusalem, coming down from God out of heaven, prepared as a bride adorned for her husband.","ref":"Revelation 21:2"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For thy Maker is thine husband; the LORD of hosts is his name; and thy Redeemer the Holy One of Israel; The God of the whole earth shall he be called.","ref":"Isaiah 54:5"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And the Spirit and the bride say, Come. And let him that heareth say, Come. And let him that is athirst come. And whosoever will, let him take the water of life freely.","ref":"Revelation 22:17"},{"kind":"para","text":"Either way, we should all be listening to Isaiah's prophecy here, because it will be of prominent importance that we get this right:"}]},{"start":10,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There will be trouble on this Earth. Isaiah isn’t sugarcoating it. God, ultimately, has revealed everything that will take place. He is warning the people of Israel here, but (honestly) we are the ones that must heed the warnings. It is all broughten back up again in Revelation. God doesn’t make us go through anything without warning."},{"kind":"para","text":"How many years and decades would it take for the whole world to finally accept the warnings and turn towards the Lord? Apparently, it will never happen. We don’t like to listen. We are rebellious towards God. By the fact that Isaiah has to tell them to be troubled and to “gird sackcloth” proves that no one actually cares about what God is telling them. They are living fancy and fine lives without the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"But when the Lord starts taking things away from them, they are all going to wish they had paid closer attention when they had the chance. Same goes for us."}]},{"start":13,"end":14,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Things will look very bleak and sad in their future. Things will look bleak and sad for us as well. Actually, today, things are quite bleak and sad in our world. I don’t think there is any nation that is living in “prosperity” today. The US is eroding every second of every day. It would be a miracle to see the cost of living get easier in our country, but I don’t think I’m going to see that in my lifetime. Perhaps the Lord is preparing His coming again? I don’t know. But we will see (and already should know at this point) that God is going to have His way with Israel."},{"kind":"para","text":"All these things have come to pass. The palaces are forsaken, the cities were left in multitudes, the forts and towers became nothing more than shelters for wild animals. They lost everything. They will come back to the land, but they will still be owned by Rome when they do. There is only one thing that can help them, can you guess what it is? It’s listed in our next verse:"}]},{"start":15,"end":15,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The Spirit of God sets us free."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And ye shall know the truth, and the truth shall make you free.","ref":"John 8:32"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Now the Lord is that Spirit: and where the Spirit of the Lord is, there is liberty.","ref":"2 Corinthians 3:17"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For God hath not given us the spirit of fear; but of power, and of love, and of a sound mind.","ref":"2 Timothy 1:7"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"If the Son therefore shall make you free, ye shall be free indeed.","ref":"John 8:36"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Stand fast therefore in the liberty wherewith Christ hath made us free, and be not entangled again with the yoke of bondage.","ref":"Galatians 5:1"},{"kind":"para","text":"Praise the Lord that He has poured His Spirit down on us. Evil people will do evil things, and they will probably get away with it here on Earth. However, righteous people will live in the Spirit of God and will always be free from evil people’s reign of terror."},{"kind":"para","text":"We might live in the world with evil, but we will always have freedom with the Spirit of God. We could be in jail and still be free with God’s Spirit. Why? Because we know we are not shackled to Hell after this life is over."}]}]},{"start":16,"end":20,"title":"God's Character","entries":[{"start":16,"end":17,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Perhaps you read this and think, “What good is righteousness in a fruitful field? What good is judgment in the wilderness? This all seems kind of random.” It’s more of an overall occurrence. We should pay attention to the Godly attributes here."},{"kind":"para","text":"Judgement in the wilderness:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For he shall have judgment without mercy, that hath shewed no mercy; and mercy rejoiceth against judgment.","ref":"James 2:13"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"So then every one of us shall give account of himself to God.","ref":"Romans 14:12"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For we must all appear before the judgment seat of Christ; that every one may receive the things done in his body, according to that he hath done, whether it be good or bad.","ref":"2 Corinthians 5:10"},{"kind":"para","text":"Righteousness in the fruitful field:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"If ye know that he is righteous, ye know that every one that doeth righteousness is born of him.","ref":"1 John 2:29"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Blessed are they that keep judgment, and he that doeth righteousness at all times.","ref":"Psalm 106:3"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For Christ is the end of the law for righteousness to every one that believeth.","ref":"Romans 10:4"},{"kind":"para","text":"Righteousness to Peace:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Now the Lord of peace himself give you peace always by all means. The Lord be with you all.","ref":"2 Thessalonians 3:16"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"If it be possible, as much as lieth in you, live peaceably with all men.","ref":"Romans 12:18"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Let him eschew evil, and do good; let him seek peace, and ensue it.","ref":"1 Peter 3:11"},{"kind":"para","text":"Quietness from Righteousness:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"The LORD shall fight for you, and ye shall hold your peace.","ref":"Exodus 14:14"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Wherefore, my beloved brethren, let every man be swift to hear, slow to speak, slow to wrath:","ref":"James 1:19"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And that ye study to be quiet, and to do your own business, and to work with your own hands, as we commanded you; That ye may walk honestly toward them that are without, and that ye may have lack of nothing.","ref":"1 Thessalonians 4:11-12"},{"kind":"para","text":"Assurance from the Spirit:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"The Spirit itself beareth witness with our spirit, that we are the children of God:","ref":"Romans 8:16"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"These things have I written unto you that believe on the name of the Son of God; that ye may know that ye have eternal life, and that ye may believe on the name of the Son of God.","ref":"1 John 5:13"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Yea, though I walk through the valley of the shadow of death, I will fear no evil: for thou art with me; thy rod and thy staff they comfort me.","ref":"Psalm 23:4"},{"kind":"para","text":"“Judgement...righteousness...peace...quietness...assurance...\" That is what our world will face when God has finally arrived here. The only reason we might not experience this in our lives today (even as Christians) is because there is still too much evil in this world. Sadly, evil voices drown out the characteristics of God. Eventually God will be vary clear. He is the only voice we will hear!"}]},{"start":18,"end":19,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God’s people always have a promise of safety. You can take that to the bank. Any time you are feeling overwhelmed by the enemy, or you feel like you are too far gone from the Lord, remember that God reminds His people throughout His entire Word that He is their safety. He will not leave you without a place to go."},{"kind":"para","text":"We might feel like we are in a season of wandering in the wilderness, but just like the Israelites, God will never leave you wandering without Him. He is there, and He will guide you if you will have Him."}]},{"start":20,"end":20,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"After all is said and done, we are left with only one more thing in our lives. The last character trait of the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"Blessing:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But my God shall supply all your need according to his riches in glory by Christ Jesus.","ref":"Philippians 4:19"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"The LORD bless thee, and keep thee:","ref":"Numbers 6:24"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And of his fulness have all we received, and grace for grace.","ref":"John 1:16"},{"kind":"para","text":"We can only receive the Lord’s blessings when we are under His salvation. We must accept who scripture says He is and then live in that salvation through faith, always believing and forever trusting. He will guide and bless because of it. When He returns, that will be the only way we live. We will forever live in His blessings, with nothing doubting, nothing confusing, and nothing holding us back—just blessings."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":9},{"start":10,"end":12},{"start":13,"end":14},{"start":15,"end":15},{"start":16,"end":17},{"start":18,"end":19},{"start":20,"end":20}],"verses":{"1":"Behold, a king shall reign in righteousness, and princes shall rule in judgment.","2":"And a man shall be as an hiding place from the wind, and a covert from the tempest; as rivers of water in a dry place, as the shadow of a great rock in a weary land.","3":"And the eyes of them that see shall not be dim, and the ears of them that hear shall hearken.","4":"The heart also of the rash shall understand knowledge, and the tongue of the stammerers shall be ready to speak plainly.","5":"The vile person shall be no more called liberal, nor the churl said to be bountiful.","6":"For the vile person will speak villany, and his heart will work iniquity, to practise hypocrisy, and to utter error against the Lord, to make empty the soul of the hungry, and he will cause the drink of the thirsty to fail.","7":"The instruments also of the churl are evil: he deviseth wicked devices to destroy the poor with lying words, even when the needy speaketh right.","8":"But the liberal deviseth liberal things; and by liberal things shall he stand.","9":"Rise up, ye women that are at ease; hear my voice, ye careless daughters; give ear unto my speech.","10":"Many days and years shall ye be troubled, ye careless women: for the vintage shall fail, the gathering shall not come.","11":"Tremble, ye women that are at ease; be troubled, ye careless ones: strip you, and make you bare, and gird sackcloth upon your loins.","12":"They shall lament for the teats, for the pleasant fields, for the fruitful vine.","13":"Upon the land of my people shall come up thorns and briers; yea, upon all the houses of joy in the joyous city:","14":"Because the palaces shall be forsaken; the multitude of the city shall be left; the forts and towers shall be for dens for ever, a joy of wild asses, a pasture of flocks;","15":"Until the spirit be poured upon us from on high, and the wilderness be a fruitful field, and the fruitful field be counted for a forest.","16":"Then judgment shall dwell in the wilderness, and righteousness remain in the fruitful field.","17":"And the work of righteousness shall be peace; and the effect of righteousness quietness and assurance for ever.","18":"And my people shall dwell in a peaceable habitation, and in sure dwellings, and in quiet resting places;","19":"When it shall hail, coming down on the forest; and the city shall be low in a low place.","20":"Blessed are ye that sow beside all waters, that send forth thither the feet of the ox and the ass."}},
    "33": {"chapter":33,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: I likened our last chapter as an oasis in a time of trouble. Obviously we have been reading quite extensively about the coming judgement of all the lands around Israel at this time. We have come to the part about Judah (Jerusalem in particular) and what will ultimately happen if they continue to turn from the Lord. These things DO come to pass, but a victory comes as well. There's a promise of reconnection to the Lord at a later time, and what it will look like for the people to live in victory. This is all a small picture of that victory for the world in the last days as well. Those that know Christ are going to dwell in victory."},{"kind":"para","text":"In this chapter, we start off with a \"woe\" but this time it's against those that are not close to Christ. Those that have Christ will not face this woe. They will not be affected by it at all. God protects His own, and this last woe will show that the judgements of God are ONLY meant for those without Him. Those that are near God will dwell in safety and supplication. It's still a good and powerful chapter for us who belong to Christ, but a dismal and sad chapter for those that don't know Him."}],"previously":["I likened our last chapter to an oasis in a time of trouble. Obviously, we have been reading quite extensively about the coming judgment of all the lands around Israel at this time. We have come to the part about Judah (Jerusalem in particular) and what will ultimately happen if they continue to turn from the Lord. These things do come to pass, but a victory comes as well. There is a promise of reconnection to the Lord at a later time, and what it will look like for the people to live in victory. This is all a small picture of that victory for the world in the last days as well. Those who know Christ are going to dwell in victory. In this chapter, we start off with a “woe,” but this time it’s against those who are not close to Christ. Those who have Christ will not face this woe. They will not be affected by it at all. God protects His own, and this last woe will show that the judgments of God are only meant for those without Him. Those who are near God will dwell in safety and supplication. It’s still a good and powerful chapter for us who belong to Christ, but a dismal and sad chapter for those who don’t know Him."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":2,"title":"A Spoiled Land","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"We spoke about sowing and reaping briefly in our last chapter, and we will discuss it again several times over. However, this is Isaiah’s way of putting it: you are going to get what you give. If you give out treacherous things, you are going to take in treacherous things. Some people might refer to it as “karma,” but the Lord refers to it as judgment."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For with what judgment ye judge, ye shall be judged: and with what measure ye mete, it shall be measured to you again.","ref":"Matthew 7:2"},{"kind":"para","text":"During the time of Isaiah, judgment was set to fall upon Assyria, which was planning to take the land of Judah. They would not succeed, as they were biting off more than they could chew. Honestly, they probably would have been fine taking it, but they went to the king of that day, Hezekiah, and tried to play God. They acted as if there was no God in Israel anymore, and if there was one, He was certainly not on their side, given that Assyria had taken the Northern Kingdom without much effort. Judah was a smaller takeover, so Assyria believed they could take it quite easily. The conversation, if you are willing to dig a little deeper, happens in 2 Kings chapter 18."},{"kind":"para","text":"However, there is a woe to this land because of their evil way of taking it. When they are finished, they will be “spoiled.” “Spoiled” means “to deal violently with” or “to devastate.” In other words, they are going to get the same treatment from the Lord as they are giving out to the land of Israel. I believe that if they hadn’t mocked their God, the Lord would have let Assyria take this land quite easily too. But they messed it up for themselves, and it will be a different land that comes in to take it. Babylon will be a much stronger and more prosperous land than Assyria. However, Assyria still stands today, whereas Babylon is in ruins."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Isaiah, though he knows the sin and times of the land, is still pleading with the Lord for mercy and gentleness. The land doesn’t deserve these righteous prayers. It goes to show that no matter how terrible the people of your native country may be, if you are called by the Lord, you should earnestly plead for God’s mercy on their behalf."},{"kind":"para","text":"I am assured that the people of the United States do NOT deserve God’s mercy. Most of them are very anti-biblical. We would be hard-pressed to go to a spot (especially in California) where we can freely worship and grow together without someone coming in and making a complaint about it. And it wouldn’t just be a complaint; it would be threats and action."},{"kind":"para","text":"We have had our share of threats before, and it has not been fun. I’ve been threatened with death for preaching God’s Word, I’ve been threatened with robbery, I’ve been threatened with shootings and bombings, I’ve been threatened with retaliation (simply for studying the Bible), and beatings for praying. I’ve been threatened by all sorts of nonsense that really has no place in our modernly “evolved” world, and yet I am tasked (like Isaiah here) to pray for God’s mercy on their behalf."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But I say unto you, Love your enemies, bless them that curse you, do good to them that hate you, and pray for them which despitefully use you, and persecute you;","ref":"Matthew 5:44"},{"kind":"para","text":"I know there will be a time coming throughout the world where hate will reign supreme amongst the anti-biblical crowds. They will threaten jail against us next. We are still tasked to pray for mercy on them."},{"kind":"para","text":"We may not realize it, but we are all on this ship together. If it sinks, we sink with it. But those that accept Christ will have the strength of the Lord and the salvation of the Lord. That is really what the prayer is about. People have safety with God, and those that deserve it are those that will turn to Him."}]}]},{"start":3,"end":4,"title":"Caterpillers and Locusts","entries":[{"start":3,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God will scatter the enemies. His strength brings deliverance. Those that don’t belong will be left in ruins or running for their lives. He knows how to separate His children from those who are not. He can separate the goats from the sheep."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"When the Son of man shall come in his glory, and all the holy angels with him, then shall he sit upon the throne of his glory: And before him shall be gathered all nations: and he shall separate them one from another, as a shepherd divideth his sheep from the goats: And he shall set the sheep on his right hand, but the goats on the left.","ref":"Matthew 25:31-33"},{"kind":"para","text":"If there are billions of sheep and goats all mixed together, it would be a difficult task for me to be able to separate which from which. Honestly, I would probably miss quite a few if I tried, likely in the millions. But Jesus will have no problem sorting them out. I assume He will just have to wave a finger or say a word, and they will all just scatter out of the sheep, whereas the sheep will just stay still. Or, perhaps, when the Lord says a word, the goats faint, and the sheep move to His right side. That’s probably a better guess."},{"kind":"para","text":"In the end, they will be like caterpillars, trying to find a place to rest around all of the leftover corpses that won’t have a place to give them rest. That’s the image Isaiah uses. The lost are like caterpillars, and the Lord’s judgments and separations are like locusts. Personally, I like Jesus’ version of it (goats and sheep) better, but you will have to understand it one way or another."}]}]},{"start":5,"end":6,"title":"Attributes Continued","entries":[{"start":5,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Again, God’s traits are going to be absolutely evident in those days. “Judgement…righteousness…wisdom…knowledge…stability…strength…salvation…treasure…” They are all attributes of the Lord given to us as a blessing. We have a few new ones since our last chapter."},{"kind":"para","text":"Wisdom in Thy Times:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But the wisdom that is from above is first pure, then peaceable, gentle, and easy to be intreated, full of mercy and good fruits, without partiality, and without hypocrisy.","ref":"James 3:17"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Happy is the man that findeth wisdom, and the man that getteth understanding.","ref":"Proverbs 3:13"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For I will give you a mouth and wisdom, which all your adversaries shall not be able to gainsay nor resist.","ref":"Luke 21:15"},{"kind":"para","text":"Knowledge From Wisdom:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"The fear of the LORD is the beginning of knowledge: but fools despise wisdom and instruction.","ref":"Proverbs 1:7"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"My people are destroyed for lack of knowledge: because thou hast rejected knowledge, I will also reject thee, that thou shalt be no priest to me: seeing thou hast forgotten the law of thy God, I will also forget thy children.","ref":"Hosea 4:6"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For to one is given by the Spirit the word of wisdom; to another the word of knowledge by the same Spirit;","ref":"1 Corinthians 12:8"},{"kind":"para","text":"Stability in a Shaky World:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But the Lord is faithful, who shall stablish you, and keep you from evil.","ref":"2 Thessalonians 3:3"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"That Christ may dwell in your hearts by faith; that ye, being rooted and grounded in love,","ref":"Ephesians 3:17"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For who is God, save the LORD? and who is a rock, save our God?","ref":"2 Samuel 22:32"},{"kind":"para","text":"Strength from the Lord:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"The LORD is my strength and my shield; my heart trusted in him, and I am helped: therefore my heart greatly rejoiceth; and with my song will I praise him.","ref":"Psalm 28:7"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And he said unto me, My grace is sufficient for thee: for my strength is made perfect in weakness. Most gladly therefore will I rather glory in my infirmities, that the power of Christ may rest upon me.","ref":"2 Corinthians 12:9"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"I can do all things through Christ which strengtheneth me.","ref":"Philippians 4:13"},{"kind":"para","text":"Salvation Radiant From Christ:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Not by works of righteousness which we have done, but according to his mercy he saved us, by the washing of regeneration, and renewing of the Holy Ghost;","ref":"Titus 3:5"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"That if thou shalt confess with thy mouth the Lord Jesus, and shalt believe in thine heart that God hath raised him from the dead, thou shalt be saved.","ref":"Romans 10:9"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Neither is there salvation in any other: for there is none other name under heaven given among men, whereby we must be saved.","ref":"Acts 4:12"},{"kind":"para","text":"Treasure Overflowing:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For where your treasure is, there will your heart be also.","ref":"Luke 12:34"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Again, the kingdom of heaven is like unto treasure hid in a field; the which when a man hath found, he hideth, and for joy thereof goeth and selleth all that he hath, and buyeth that field.","ref":"Matthew 13:44"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"In whom are hid all the treasures of wisdom and knowledge.","ref":"Colossians 2:3"},{"kind":"para","text":"Once again, these blessings come from being in the presence and family of the Lord. If you are not a sheep, you will not have these things. Rather, you will be like the goats, fainting and pleading with the Lord at the last moment, but it will be too late by then. It will be your death and damnation if you wait too long. That is why the message of preaching is so important today. There are many people who need to turn. They know that there is a God, and perhaps they need better clarity. Others are just too stubborn and won’t turn no matter what you might give them. They have decided their fate. I would still hope they would turn…"},{"kind":"para","text":"The attributes of the Lord are far better than the treasures of this world. Perhaps we can look at these attributes in the same light as the world for a second. Let’s list them again, but this time we will focus on how the world will give them to you."},{"kind":"para","text":"Judgement:"},{"kind":"para","text":"The world judges today, that is for sure. They have their own warped version of judgment. The funny thing is, if you judge them, they tell you that we aren’t supposed to judge if we are Christians. That is not true. In fact, we have the greater ability to judge because we know what righteousness looks like. We judge based on the righteous standard of God."},{"kind":"para","text":"They judge based on their own standards, which are usually even too high for themselves to personally reach. Judgment by the world is tainted with their sin-sickness. They judge based on what makes themselves feel better. The Lord judges based on what is good and right for everyone."},{"kind":"para","text":"Righteousness:"},{"kind":"para","text":"To the world, righteousness is having more money and a bigger house. They think that power and position are what give them the proper ability to reign. That is simply not the case with the Lord. His Spirit provides true righteousness, and righteousness, once again, can only be found in the standards of the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"Lean on your money and position all you want; eventually, you will just be thrown to the side when it starts to crumble or fall apart."},{"kind":"para","text":"Peace:"},{"kind":"para","text":"There is none here. People have been searching for world peace for decades, and they will never find it. There’s nothing more peaceful than to know that your sins are forgiven and you have a home in Heaven. But that peace won’t rest in anything here on Earth. It only rests in the promises of God."},{"kind":"para","text":"Quietness:"},{"kind":"para","text":"It should make you laugh to think about this one. We can’t find quietness anywhere on this Earth. We could go out into the middle of the desert, and there are still people being loud. We will even run into loud animals."},{"kind":"para","text":"Assurance:"},{"kind":"para","text":"Our world doesn’t deal with assurance; they deal with insurance. They know something bad will happen, and they want you to plan for that rather than assuring you that nothing bad will happen. You will not find assurance here because they are right; something bad WILL happen."},{"kind":"para","text":"Blessing:"},{"kind":"para","text":"This only comes about on this Earth if you sneeze."},{"kind":"para","text":"Wisdom:"},{"kind":"para","text":"What the world views as wisdom is not what real wisdom looks like. Wisdom is Christ. Period. We have explored this deeply when we went through Proverbs. If you need a refresher on what earthly wisdom looks like, refer to Proverbs. Earthly wisdom is called “foolishness” there."},{"kind":"para","text":"Knowledge:"},{"kind":"para","text":"The world actually has some knowledge. They can learn and create all sorts of magnificent things. However, their knowledge amounts to nothing more than what they can fit in this world."},{"kind":"para","text":"Real knowledge is eternal. It’s the ability to see far past this world and to see far past this universe. It’s the ability to grow in eternal things and in the place where the Lord dwells."},{"kind":"para","text":"Stability:"},{"kind":"para","text":"Another one that should make you laugh. Everything here is futile. If evolution were real, this word doesn’t exist in it. There is no stability on this planet or in this life. Everything will come to an end over time."},{"kind":"para","text":"Strength:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Because the foolishness of God is wiser than men; and the weakness of God is stronger than men.","ref":"1 Corinthians 1:25"},{"kind":"para","text":"Treasure:"},{"kind":"para","text":"There are a lot of “valuable” things on this Earth. Again, though, value is truly found in stability, and if the things here will vanish away over time, then these things are not stable. If you put value in your car, you will know what I’m talking about. Your car depreciates in value over time, and eventually, it will need to be scrapped because it has run its course. Houses will not stand forever either. There is nothing of real value here on Earth. Everything is just superficial and fake. So if you looked at these same attributes of the Lord and tried to place them on anything here on Earth, there is NO comparison."}]}]},{"start":7,"end":9,"title":"No Hope On Earth","entries":[{"start":7,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The “valiant” ones would probably insinuate people of higher rank, such as world leaders. They put their hope in worldly strength, and as we’ve already pointed out, the world’s strength is still weaker than God’s weakness. They were trying to promote peace and safety, but God turned that upside down. This is why you don’t trust political leaders. Our politicians today tout a “peace” message. They even write up “peace treaties” to suffice their fights. Israel and Hamas have a peace treaty right now, but it is falling apart as we speak. They are trying to promote “world” peace, which is their own personal version of peace. You will not find appropriate peace in this world without the Lord. You will just be left weeping bitterly if you try to take the world’s version of peace. Everything, when it’s in our own power, will lie in waste, and there will be no negotiations when the Lord has come to wipe out the evil on this Earth. He will not allow evil to reign."},{"kind":"para","text":"It’s kind of fascinating, though, that the term, here, for “valiant ones” is not written anywhere else in scripture. The Hebrew word is only found here, and it has thrown a lot of scholars off as to what it actually means. I think it’s pretty obvious, but perhaps it’s a bit of a mistranslation? “Valiant ones” means “hero.” It’s the world’s version of a Savior. This world puts a lot of trust and power into political leaders, so I think it’s right to assume that it’s the world powers that will be in tears here. Even if it’s not, our next verse still gives a broad definition of these tears."}]},{"start":9,"end":9,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"These places are known for specific traits. Lebanon is known for its trees, but they won’t be there anymore. Sharon was a peaceful place, but it will turn into a wilderness. Bashan and Carmel are fruitful places that won’t grow anything anymore. They will all come to nothing and become useless to this world. That is why the Earth will mourn. Not just the people of the Earth either; the Earth itself will feel sick at the Lord’s coming."}]}]},{"start":10,"end":12,"title":"Trust In Q-Tips","entries":[{"start":10,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord is humble. We should get that straight. He can literally do away with this entire planet at any moment He wants to, but He waits. He is patient. We are not deserving of His patience. I think that is God’s weakness if I’m honest. His weakness is the desire for everyone on Earth to repent and turn to Him. Because of this, He is patient. He is waiting. He is giving humanity chance after chance."},{"kind":"para","text":"But eventually, He will be done. We will get to a point where He will rise, and He will be exalted. We will see His glow and we will know that He is the Lord. He will wait, though, until the world has been brought low from its pride."}]},{"start":11,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Have you ever been around a morning coffee breath person? My wife used to complain all the time about a man she worked with. He always had coffee breath, and she had to work in the same office with him, often in close quarters. She didn’t know what to do. She would offer him mints, but she didn’t want to be rude and just tell him how much his breath stinks. “Your breath, as fire, shall devour you…” I’m sure that is a poor example, but the feeling is similar. It will be by your own power and tongues that get you into trouble. We are told multiple times in multiple ways throughout history that our greatest enemy is ourselves. We are our own worst enemy, truly. We get in our own ways, both by rejecting the Lord and treading our own paths, and by tripping over ourselves. We will not be prosperous in our own power when the Lord comes. We will be lacking, because the only one that can supply anything will be God Himself. If we don’t have Him, we won’t have what we need…"},{"kind":"para","text":"I was called a “Q-Tip” recently. I know the brother meant well. There has been a lot of disunity in the church, and this brother reached out to try and get me to meet a new member. I told him that I was not sure if I could be of any help. I said, “The church has tied my hands from serving and helping, so I don’t really know what I can do.” He said, “John, you’re like a Q-Tip. You might just be sitting in a drawer, but you will be really useful and needed eventually.” He’s right, I guess. Except Q-Tips are thrown away when you’re done. You can get reusable ones, but I’m not too sure about them. Sadly, I think most of us treat God like a Q-Tip. We think we don’t need Him until the time calls for it. The problem is, He’s our last Q-Tip, and if we have misplaced Him, we are not going to have His help when the time comes. We must hold onto the Lord every day. We must keep Him in our arms. He is more than a Q-Tip. He is a lifeline. He is your anchor. He is your Judge, your righteousness, your peace, your quietness. He is your assurance, your blessing, your wisdom, your knowledge. Your stability, your strength, and your treasure. Nobody finds these characteristics in a Q-Tip. If you do, you will not have the Q-Tip for very long. Even if it gets wet, it falls apart. Q-Tips are not made to last forever. Nor would you want them to (I refuse to imagine what a Q-Tip might look like after a long time of use)."}]},{"start":12,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is the sad reality of the world that puts their trust in a Q-Tip. They are used, rather than using everything else. They had a time of abusing their treasures, but now they will burn with their treasures for all of eternity. In the grand scheme of things, nothing on this Earth is worth an eternity of torment and suffering."},{"kind":"para","text":"It is, however, possible to live life to the fullest and still keep a Spirit of faith and righteousness. Living life to its fullest doesn’t mean you have to live a life of sin. In fact, true fulfillment in this life is only found in living it for the Lord."}]}]},{"start":13,"end":16,"title":"Far And Near","entries":[{"start":13,"end":13,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There are only two types of people in this world: those that are far off and those that are near to the Lord. At this time, those that are far off would insinuate the Gentiles, while those that are near were the Israelites. In the end times, those that are far off will be those without Christ, and those that are near will be those in Christ’s salvation. Either way, whether with Christ or against, you WILL hear what the Lord is doing."}]},{"start":14,"end":14,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God is a consuming fire:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For our God is a consuming fire.","ref":"Hebrews 12:29"},{"kind":"para","text":"He was a pillar of fire to the Israelites as well:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And the LORD went before them by day in a pillar of a cloud, to lead them the way; and by night in a pillar of fire, to give them light; to go by day and night: He took not away the pillar of the cloud by day, nor the pillar of fire by night, from before the people.","ref":"Exodus 13:21-22"},{"kind":"para","text":"These are the two references to God. Those that are far away will only see the Lord as a “consuming” fire. They cannot “dwell with the devouring fire.” They will be devoured by God’s closeness. They cannot be in His presence and live."},{"kind":"para","text":"Those that are close, however, see Him as a pillar of fire. He leads and guides them on their path. They can stay close to Him without being burned. There are sinners everywhere, the difference is whether or not you have Christ. If you have Him, you can stay close. If you don’t… well, God cannot dwell with you unless you want to be burned."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Therefore because the king's commandment was urgent, and the furnace exceeding hot, the flame of the fire slew those men that took up Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego. And these three men, Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego, fell down bound into the midst of the burning fiery furnace. Then Nebuchadnezzar the king was astonied, and rose up in haste, and spake, and said unto his counsellors, Did not we cast three men bound into the midst of the fire? They answered and said unto the king, True, O king. He answered and said, Lo, I see four men loose, walking in the midst of the fire, and they have no hurt; and the form of the fourth is like the Son of God.","ref":"Daniel 3:22-25"},{"kind":"para","text":"Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego could handle the fire because they were already close to the Lord. The men who threw them in could not because they were far from God. We get this image over and over again throughout scripture."}]},{"start":15,"end":16,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The rest of the world may struggle to grow a single thing, yet those with the Lord will somehow miraculously have all their needs met. God can literally rain food down from the sky if He so chooses. The only ones that will be blessed by it are those that are under the salvation of God, though. People far off will see it, but they won’t dare come to try and steal it. They will be too scared of God’s presence to try and enter in."}]}]},{"start":17,"end":24,"title":"A Place Far Off","entries":[{"start":17,"end":17,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I cannot wait to see God face to face. It seems as if Heaven is so far away. I am thirty-two years old as of this writing, and it seems like I have so much more life to live. I want to see the Lord now. I want to be face to face with God. I cannot, however, until He either returns or I am taken home by His Will."}]},{"start":18,"end":18,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Another indication of those who belong to God is whether His presence brings you terror or glory. If it’s terror, you are likely in the wrong camp, friend. He wants us to get excited about His coming to us. He wants us to be assured and confident in His presence. If we are not, we must get that fixed right away by God’s Word!"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"He which testifieth these things saith, Surely I come quickly. Amen. Even so, come, Lord Jesus.","ref":"Revelation 22:20"},{"kind":"para","text":"Quickly is not quick enough. But I will be a patient boy."}]},{"start":19,"end":19,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"We will be protected. Bringing it back to the present of Isaiah, he is speaking about the southern kingdom here. We can’t forget that these are imminent dangers presented here. Assyria will not get them. They are the ones with a “stammering tongue.” We know this because we see a spokesman for Assyria try to talk in their Hebrew tongue and fail miserably in 2 Kings 18."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Then said Eliakim the son of Hilkiah, and Shebna, and Joah, unto Rabshakeh, Speak, I pray thee, to thy servants in the Syrian language; for we understand it: and talk not with us in the Jews' language in the ears of the people that are on the wall.","ref":"2 Kings 18:26"},{"kind":"para","text":"I assume this Rabshakeh character wasn’t very good at speaking in Hebrew. Either way, they are protected from this people of “deeper speech.” Though they got their brothers in the north, God is going to protect Judah for a time longer. Even after they are taken, God still protects them. He brings them back in time."}]},{"start":20,"end":21,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"“Quiet” is brought up again here. Jerusalem, today, is anything but quiet. They literally have a place called “The Wailing Wall” where Jews go (still today) to pray and cry to the Lord. As long as there is sin, there is a reason to cry and wail. Someday, though, the Lord will be present, and when He is, He will bring us a quiet habitation, and rivers and streams will flow from Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"Interestingly enough, there have never been any rivers and streams in or around Jerusalem. So something miraculous will have to take place to have rivers and streams in this location. It’s obviously a spiritual implication as well. But, just as a reminder, prophecies work in threes, and so I have to assume this will be literal as well. Either way, God will be our source of sustainability. He is the only reason we will be able to live in a time of great turmoil if we see it."}]},{"start":22,"end":22,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"What a verse! I don't think I have to comment on this verse, it can speak for itself."}]},{"start":23,"end":24,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Another great verse states, “The last shall be first.” There will be no more sickness from our sin. We will live in God’s forgiveness as well as God’s health. True health is spiritual. If we are physically healthy but spiritually sick, we will die from a sickness called sin. If we are physically sick but spiritually healthy, we will have everlasting life. If we are physically and spiritually healthy, we will have everlasting life."},{"kind":"para","text":"Obviously, the important factor is the health of your spirit. Physical health will not profit you anything, whether you are sick or healthy. Spiritual health means everything."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":9},{"start":10,"end":10},{"start":11,"end":11},{"start":12,"end":12},{"start":13,"end":13},{"start":14,"end":14},{"start":15,"end":16},{"start":17,"end":17},{"start":18,"end":18},{"start":19,"end":19},{"start":20,"end":21},{"start":22,"end":22},{"start":23,"end":24}],"verses":{"1":"Woe to thee that spoilest, and thou wast not spoiled; and dealest treacherously, and they dealt not treacherously with thee! when thou shalt cease to spoil, thou shalt be spoiled; and when thou shalt make an end to deal treacherously, they shall deal treacherously with thee.","2":"O Lord, be gracious unto us; we have waited for thee: be thou their arm every morning, our salvation also in the time of trouble.","3":"At the noise of the tumult the people fled; at the lifting up of thyself the nations were scattered.","4":"And your spoil shall be gathered like the gathering of the caterpiller: as the running to and fro of locusts shall he run upon them.","5":"The Lord is exalted; for he dwelleth on high: he hath filled Zion with judgment and righteousness.","6":"And wisdom and knowledge shall be the stability of thy times, and strength of salvation: the fear of the Lord is his treasure.","7":"Behold, their valiant ones shall cry without: the ambassadors of peace shall weep bitterly.","8":"The highways lie waste, the wayfaring man ceaseth: he hath broken the covenant, he hath despised the cities, he regardeth no man.","9":"The earth mourneth and languisheth: Lebanon is ashamed and hewn down: Sharon is like a wilderness; and Bashan and Carmel shake off their fruits.","10":"Now will I rise, saith the Lord; now will I be exalted; now will I lift up myself.","11":"Ye shall conceive chaff, ye shall bring forth stubble: your breath, as fire, shall devour you.","12":"And the people shall be as the burnings of lime: as thorns cut up shall they be burned in the fire.","13":"Hear, ye that are far off, what I have done; and, ye that are near, acknowledge my might.","14":"The sinners in Zion are afraid; fearfulness hath surprised the hypocrites. Who among us shall dwell with the devouring fire? who among us shall dwell with everlasting burnings?","15":"He that walketh righteously, and speaketh uprightly; he that despiseth the gain of oppressions, that shaketh his hands from holding of bribes, that stoppeth his ears from hearing of blood, and shutteth his eyes from seeing evil;","16":"He shall dwell on high: his place of defence shall be the munitions of rocks: bread shall be given him; his waters shall be sure.","17":"Thine eyes shall see the king in his beauty: they shall behold the land that is very far off.","18":"Thine heart shall meditate terror. Where is the scribe? where is the receiver? where is he that counted the towers?","19":"Thou shalt not see a fierce people, a people of a deeper speech than thou canst perceive; of a stammering tongue, that thou canst not understand.","20":"Look upon Zion, the city of our solemnities: thine eyes shall see Jerusalem a quiet habitation, a tabernacle that shall not be taken down; not one of the stakes thereof shall ever be removed, neither shall any of the cords thereof be broken.","21":"But there the glorious Lord will be unto us a place of broad rivers and streams; wherein shall go no galley with oars, neither shall gallant ship pass thereby.","22":"For the Lord is our judge, the Lord is our lawgiver, the Lord is our king; he will save us.","23":"Thy tacklings are loosed; they could not well strengthen their mast, they could not spread the sail: then is the prey of a great spoil divided; the lame take the prey.","24":"And the inhabitant shall not say, I am sick: the people that dwell therein shall be forgiven their iniquity."}},
    "34": {"chapter":34,"intro":[{"kind":"scripture","text":"If ye were of the world, the world would love his own: but because ye are not of the world, but I have chosen you out of the world, therefore the world hateth you.","ref":"John 15:19"},{"kind":"para","text":"The world can only protect you for so long though, because the Lord overcomes the world through His judgement and power. The world has limited power, God's power is limitless."}],"previously":["In our last couple chapters, we have gotten the fate of God's children when judgement comes. God will take care of His own, and He will protect His own against anything He might be pouring out on this Earth. If we are hurt in this life (as a Christian) it is not God hurting us, but the world. In this chapter, we get the fate of the world. If we are hurt (as an unbeliever), it is not the world hurting us, but God."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":4,"title":"The World's Fate","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Supposedly, the most stolen book in the entire world is the Bible. Perhaps it is stolen mostly from hotel rooms, but I am sure people steal them from bookstores as well. Something in this book is valuable enough to get people to steal it. Maybe they steal it because it’s easy. Maybe it’s an accident, though if there are this many people doing it, I can’t see how it would be an accident."},{"kind":"para","text":"Supposedly, the most sold book in the world is also the Bible. So, we can determine that it’s valuable. What makes it valuable is not some sort of magic that comes from the pages. It’s not even the simple notion that people will learn how to be a good person by it, or that it will tell us about Jesus. No, I think the reason it is so popular around the world is because of the truth that pours out of it."},{"kind":"para","text":"Whether you deny God or deny Jesus is your choice, but the bottom line is, there is no denying that the pages of scripture reveal prophecy. They reveal it in a magical way, absolutely. These pages are used to gain wisdom and knowledge, but they also teach us judgment and warn us of terrible things to come. In fact, if you look around your world right now, you will see that the pages of scripture are extremely evident. It is an impossible thing to deny Bible prophecy."},{"kind":"para","text":"Because of this, it should be an impossible thing to deny Jesus and God as well, but some people don’t seem to want to correlate the two. Either way, the whole Earth has heard, and they have listened, and if anyone is fooled by the ploys of Satan (at this point), they are doing it on purpose."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Now we have some different characteristics of God."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Indignation of the Lord:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For the wrath of God is revealed from heaven against all ungodliness and unrighteousness of men, who hold the truth in unrighteousness;","ref":"Romans 1:18"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For, behold, the LORD cometh out of his place to punish the inhabitants of the earth for their iniquity: the earth also shall disclose her blood, and shall no more cover her slain.","ref":"Isaiah 26:21"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"The Lord knoweth how to deliver the godly out of temptations, and to reserve the unjust unto the day of judgment to be punished:","ref":"2 Peter 2:9"},{"kind":"para","text":"His Fury Upon Armies:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Behold, a whirlwind of the LORD is gone forth in fury, even a grievous whirlwind: it shall fall grievously upon the head of the wicked.","ref":"Jeremiah 23:19"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Now will I shortly pour out my fury upon thee, and accomplish mine anger upon thee: and I will judge thee according to thy ways, and will recompense thee for all thine abominations.","ref":"Ezekiel 7:8"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Who can stand before his indignation? and who can abide in the fierceness of his anger? his fury is poured out like fire, and the rocks are thrown down by him.","ref":"Nahum 1:6"},{"kind":"para","text":"He Utterly Destroyed:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But thou, O God, shalt bring them down into the pit of destruction: bloody and deceitful men shall not live out half their days; but I will trust in thee.","ref":"Psalm 55:23"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Wise men lay up knowledge: but the mouth of the foolish is near destruction.","ref":"Proverbs 10:14"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Whose end is destruction, whose God is their belly, and whose glory is in their shame, who mind earthly things.)","ref":"Philippians 3:19"},{"kind":"para","text":"Delivered Them To The Slaughter:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"I have set the point of the sword against all their gates, that their heart may faint, and their ruins be multiplied: ah! it is made bright, it is wrapped up for the slaughter.","ref":"Ezekiel 21:15"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"I will bring them down like lambs to the slaughter, like rams with he goats.","ref":"Jeremiah 51:40"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And there shall be upon every high mountain, and upon every high hill, rivers and streams of waters in the day of the great slaughter, when the towers fall.","ref":"Isaiah 30:25"},{"kind":"para","text":"It puts a different perspective on God’s person, doesn’t it? To His children, He has a completely different approach. To the lost… well, it won’t be fun. The next verse gives us even further clarity:"}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Why anyone would choose to be on this side of the Lord is beyond me. I just don’t think they take the Lord seriously, is why… Though God has certainly proven this fact over and over again. People today just want to ignore the facts, though."},{"kind":"para","text":"Our era likes to make up their own ideas of what is true and what is not, and if you don’t accept what they made up as a version of truth, you are their enemy. It’s quite absurd. Our leaders have approved this, though, and that is why we are in this predicament."},{"kind":"para","text":"Our state leaders give false preachers power and try to snuff out anyone who would combat these loudmouths with any sort of viable truth."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And judgment is turned away backward, and justice standeth afar off: for truth is fallen in the street, and equity cannot enter.","ref":"Isaiah 59:14"},{"kind":"para","text":"Spoiler alert: history has repeated itself multiple times. Yet somehow, there are a lot of people who deny the coming judgment of God, even though this world has been judged multiple times by the Lord."}]},{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I do believe this will be literal. I think the clouds will LITERALLY roll back like a scroll, and the saints and angels of the Lord (with Jesus as the forefront) will descend here on Earth for the last battle."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And the heaven departed as a scroll when it is rolled together; and every mountain and island were moved out of their places.","ref":"Revelation 6:14"},{"kind":"para","text":"Though I don’t know if I will call it a battle, it will be assured to this Earth that they will fail, and the end has come. This “battle” is already won by the Lord. Isaiah says it will be like a “leaf falleth off from the vine…” When leaves do that, they cannot be put back on. They are forever off of that vine. That is how sure judgment is going to come on this Earth."}]}]},{"start":5,"end":7,"title":"Cursed People","entries":[{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God holds His sword up there until the time of judgment. He is waiting for a day when He will use it on those who are against Him. He calls out Idumea. “Idumea” means “Red.” It’s another name for “Edom.” Why He calls it by this name here, I don’t really know. They are the descendants of Esau, though, and those are the people of the curse. The Israelites are the people of the blessing. Today, the church is the children of the blessing, and the world is the children of the curse."},{"kind":"para","text":"Esau was a rebellious man. We studied all of this in Genesis, but as a refresher, he was not a man searching for the Lord. He was a man of the world, and he loved the things of the world. Loving the things of the world makes you a person of God’s curse."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Love not the world, neither the things that are in the world. If any man love the world, the love of the Father is not in him. For all that is in the world, the lust of the flesh, and the lust of the eyes, and the pride of life, is not of the Father, but is of the world. And the world passeth away, and the lust thereof: but he that doeth the will of God abideth for ever.","ref":"1 John 2:15-17"},{"kind":"para","text":"There is no payout for loving the world. There's an eternal payout for loving the Lord."}]},{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There will be many people who suffer the consequences of fighting against the Lord. It will likely be more against God than for Him during the time of great tribulation. Most of this world will be lost and headed for a slaughter. Only a remnant will actually turn to God."}]},{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"“Unicorns” means “Aurochs” or “Wild Bulls.” They don’t exist today, but there is evidence of a beast of some sort that would match this description. The land will be given over to wild animals, which is the point. It will not be a place of habitation; it will be a place of blood and suffering. I don’t think anyone (in their right mind) would choose to live in a place where there is violence and torment. Yet, we have a whole world that rejects the Lord to live in such a place."}]}]},{"start":8,"end":12,"title":"Completely Devastated","entries":[{"start":8,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"That is what it is, mind you. I know we’ve spoken about why God is doing this quite a bit in these pages, but I want to make sure it’s driven home to the reader. God is exacting judgment on the world because the world asks for it. They ask for it by their lawless deeds and abuse of mankind. Being evil will be just as normal as drinking water in those days, and no one will think of it as a problem when the time comes. In fact, they will think of it as a solution. They get what they want by stepping on the innocent people who could never give anyone anything anyway. It’s kill or be killed at that point."},{"kind":"para","text":"Those with money will have the ability to make sure they stay on top of the power chain, and those without will be persecuted, used as property, or abused and killed. The land will have laws, but they will be laws of terrible consequence, and they will call it normal and righteous. Their laws will include tormenting and mutilating people. It’s already begun in most of the world today. The stand is for mutilating children specifically. These countries want to reach the kids because they know how weak and innocent children are. They can be easily manipulated, and their minds can be altered quite easily."},{"kind":"para","text":"Instead of teaching them good and powerful things, we teach them evil and terrible things. Now we have a generation that throws a tantrum when they can’t get their way and mistreats and even murders people to get what they want. And the powers that be let them. It will be a common thing in those days, even more common than today."}]},{"start":9,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There will be a reminder to the people of what God did there. There are always reminders of God’s workings here on this Earth. Once again, people have to purposely ignore proof and evidence in order to deny God and Christ. They have to reject historians and downright ignore science and facts that are literally punching them in the face."},{"kind":"para","text":"If the destruction of this city (that is, the city of unbelievers), and the neverending smoke rising for the world to see is not enough for people to believe, then it should be evident to us that they are purposely rejecting truth. Seriously, it’s a very possible theme in the future. We have a lot of people denying truth all the time today."},{"kind":"para","text":"There are people who deny the Titanic actually sank. People deny that the Earth is round. They deny simple math equations, and they can’t seem to tell me if the sun is hot or cold. They deny that there is a creator and deny the proof of the builder. It wouldn’t surprise me if there are people who deny oxygen. It’s kind of fascinating to me."}]},{"start":11,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Again, we will see it become a wilderness. It’s uninhabitable. There’s nothing that can survive in that land except for animals. God will still take care of the animals, it seems. Everyone who sees it, though, will live in confusion."},{"kind":"para","text":"Even the stones will be emptied. I assume the judgment of the Lord will hallow out the stones? A rock will just be a dirt clod. Nothing will stand affirmative. Everything, including the Earth itself, will erode and fall apart."}]},{"start":12,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This will be the most devastating part for them. They have placed so much trust in their world leaders. They believe they will live in prosperity because of the evil leadership over them. As long as they follow the guidance of those in power, they think they will be fine. They will have all their needs met because they are working alongside their government."},{"kind":"para","text":"The sad reality is that the world powers will abandon them when the going gets tough. Everyone will gather to hear the next move now that there is so much destruction and nowhere to turn, but the world leaders will not be found. They will hide away somewhere. They will abandon the people who trusted them, leaving those people alone without any hope of rebuilding or direction."},{"kind":"para","text":"If you are going to put your trust and hope into something, may it be in something that never dies."}]}]},{"start":13,"end":15,"title":"A Place of Horrors","entries":[{"start":13,"end":13,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"\"Dragons\" means “Serpents.\" We have already covered this before, but just in case you forgot... Dragons are not real. Snakes are though."}]},{"start":14,"end":14,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"“Satyr” means “Demon possessed goat” or a “sacrificial animal.” I sure hope that if this is talking about demons, they are crying in the end. I hope they cry over their failed choice of rejecting the Lord. I don’t think they will be crying over that though. I think they will be crying because they know their time of fun and possession is over. They will have to be put into Hell for eternity at this point, and they can’t roam on the Earth like they do today. It will be a noisy place is really what this verse is insinuating. Crying demon-possessed goats and high-pitched screeching owls will be making all sorts of noise because they can, and that is what the land represents. It just represents pain and agony, and when we are in pain and agony, crying and screeching is all that we can muster."}]},{"start":15,"end":15,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"All these creatures are fierce and scary. It’s going to be a place of people’s nightmares. It will look like it’s haunted, that’s how foul it will become."},{"kind":"para","text":"I like going to haunted mazes and things of that nature. I know, judge me all you want, and call me a heretic, but it’s true. I think they are fun. They are made to give you an adrenaline rush, like a rollercoaster is made to do so. The only difference is I’m on the ground when it happens, and the danger is not actually imminent. It’s all staged and fake. But this place… I don’t think I could ever imagine walking in this land. This place truly is a place of horrors."}]}]},{"start":16,"end":17,"title":"Assurance","entries":[{"start":16,"end":16,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The book of the Lord is accurate and true. It is absolute. The people who steal this book should open it and read the dangers of this world. The people who buy this book should open it and see how serious the Lord is about the coming judgments. Either way, this book is here for us to take seriously!"},{"kind":"para","text":"This is no game, it’s no laughing matter, it’s not a lighthearted lesson for the children. No, this is serious business that needs to be taken very carefully and methodically. We need to search the Lord out and rest in Him if we do not want to be in this land of dread when the time comes. Be on the positive characteristics side of the Lord. Don’t be on the side of slaughter and cursing."}]},{"start":17,"end":17,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"For at least 1,000 years, their eventual possession is Hell. According to Revelation, they will live in a land of dread. It will be filled with wild animals, blood, stink, screaming, clamoring, crying, destruction, fire, and chaos. During this time, they will have children, and there will be generations over those thousand years. However, it will not be enjoyable to raise a child in those days without the Lord. The children raised in that land will undoubtedly be hardened. That is why they come to try and make war with Jesus:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And when the thousand years are expired, Satan shall be loosed out of his prison, And shall go out to deceive the nations which are in the four quarters of the earth, Gog and Magog, to gather them together to battle: the number of whom is as the sand of the sea. And they went up on the breadth of the earth, and compassed the camp of the saints about, and the beloved city: and fire came down from God out of heaven, and devoured them. And the devil that deceived them was cast into the lake of fire and brimstone, where the beast and the false prophet are, and shall be tormented day and night for ever and ever.","ref":"Revelation 20:7-10"},{"kind":"para","text":"We are certain that these things will come. There are people who want to deny it, but the proof of it is already being displayed by the erosion of our world today. We must be prepared. That is why Isaiah is writing this. That is why Revelation exists today. It is not there to scare the saints; it is there to prepare the saints. If we avoid those books because we are scared, we will never be ready to take up our crosses and follow Him."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":10},{"start":11,"end":11},{"start":12,"end":12},{"start":13,"end":13},{"start":14,"end":14},{"start":15,"end":15},{"start":16,"end":16},{"start":17,"end":17}],"verses":{"1":"Come near, ye nations, to hear; and hearken, ye people: let the earth hear, and all that is therein; the world, and all things that come forth of it.","2":"For the indignation of the Lord is upon all nations, and his fury upon all their armies: he hath utterly destroyed them, he hath delivered them to the slaughter.","3":"Their slain also shall be cast out, and their stink shall come up out of their carcases, and the mountains shall be melted with their blood.","4":"And all the host of heaven shall be dissolved, and the heavens shall be rolled together as a scroll: and all their host shall fall down, as the leaf falleth off from the vine, and as a falling fig from the fig tree.","5":"For my sword shall be bathed in heaven: behold, it shall come down upon Idumea, and upon the people of my curse, to judgment.","6":"The sword of the Lord is filled with blood, it is made fat with fatness, and with the blood of lambs and goats, with the fat of the kidneys of rams: for the Lord hath a sacrifice in Bozrah, and a great slaughter in the land of Idumea.","7":"And the unicorns shall come down with them, and the bullocks with the bulls; and their land shall be soaked with blood, and their dust made fat with fatness.","8":"For it is the day of the Lord's vengeance, and the year of recompences for the controversy of Zion.","9":"And the streams thereof shall be turned into pitch, and the dust thereof into brimstone, and the land thereof shall become burning pitch.","10":"It shall not be quenched night nor day; the smoke thereof shall go up for ever: from generation to generation it shall lie waste; none shall pass through it for ever and ever.","11":"But the cormorant and the bittern shall possess it; the owl also and the raven shall dwell in it: and he shall stretch out upon it the line of confusion, and the stones of emptiness.","12":"They shall call the nobles thereof to the kingdom, but none shall be there, and all her princes shall be nothing.","13":"And thorns shall come up in her palaces, nettles and brambles in the fortresses thereof: and it shall be an habitation of dragons, and a court for owls.","14":"The wild beasts of the desert shall also meet with the wild beasts of the island, and the satyr shall cry to his fellow; the screech owl also shall rest there, and find for herself a place of rest.","15":"There shall the great owl make her nest, and lay, and hatch, and gather under her shadow: there shall the vultures also be gathered, every one with her mate.","16":"Seek ye out of the book of the Lord, and read: no one of these shall fail, none shall want her mate: for my mouth it hath commanded, and his spirit it hath gathered them.","17":"And he hath cast the lot for them, and his hand hath divided it unto them by line: they shall possess it for ever, from generation to generation shall they dwell therein."}},
    "35": {"chapter":35,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: Our last chapter was a bit bleak. We looked at the characteristics of God again, but this time it was aimed at the evil of this world. He does not feel the same way about these people as He does with His own children. He will treat them quite differently. They will not enjoy what the Lord will do to them, but it's something that needs to take place if God is going to set things right."},{"kind":"para","text":"In this chapter, we get a promising glimpse of the new world during the Lord's reign. Things will happen that seem to be impossible to us today, and we will live in peace and safety like we never have before. The Christians will actually live as they were intended to for thousands and thousands of years, and they will work in unity and gladness!"}],"previously":["Our last chapter was a bit bleak. We looked at the characteristics of God again, but this time it was aimed at the evil of this world. He does not feel the same way about these people as He does with His own children. He will treat them quite differently. They will not enjoy what the Lord will do to them, but it’s something that needs to take place if God is going to set things right. In this chapter, we get a promising glimpse of the new world during the Lord’s reign. Things will happen that seem to be impossible to us today, and we will live in peace and safety like we never have before. The Christians will actually live as they were intended to for thousands and thousands of years, and they will work in unity and gladness!"],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":2,"title":"Deserts In Bloom","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"“…for them…” indicates the saved, specifically Israel in this scene, but for the whole Christian community when the Lord has finished His judgment. The land will be given back to those it rightfully belongs to. This Earth doesn’t belong to Satan. Satan has tried to take it with everything he has (and his limited power), but it belongs to the Lord. It always has and it always will. The Lord intends the righteous to dwell here, and that is who He is going to give it to."},{"kind":"para","text":"When it’s all said and done, the Earth will be made completely new, and the desert will rejoice and prove it by blossoming. The desert blossoms. It will be quite the thing to behold. We have seen this actually happen in the desert near us called “Death Valley.” It’s named such because it gets into record heat temperatures there during the summer. Many people have died there, and you can’t really build homes or anything sustainable because of the heat. Hence the name. However, one particular season it got an abundance of rain which had never been seen before, and after a couple of days, the desert was colorful and full of life. It looked like a completely different place!"},{"kind":"para","text":"That is how the entire world will be; it will look like a completely different place once the Lord renews it. It will be brighter and better than it ever has before."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The literal Earth will sing out with joy to the Lord. Lebanon, Carmel, and Sharon were all places of immense growth and fertility. Just like the ease of growing in those places, the deserts will be the same. There won’t be a single part of the ground that can’t produce life. I believe that was the way in which it was always intended to be."},{"kind":"para","text":"I am sure that the Garden of Eden was an extremely fertile place. You wouldn’t have to do much work to make your plants grow there. You would just plant, wait, and reap. It probably happened quickly too. But because of the fall, the ground (like our hearts) is stubborn. It won’t just give us produce; we have to work for it."},{"kind":"para","text":"Not in the Millennium. Our world will grow its produce, and it will be easy and light work for us. That is, perhaps, what our main objective could be. We are tending our gardens in the new world. We are told we will reign with the Lord, but we will also be living with Him."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"It is a faithful saying: For if we be dead with him, we shall also live with him: If we suffer, we shall also reign with him: if we deny him, he also will deny us: If we believe not, yet he abideth faithful: he cannot deny himself.","ref":"2 Timothy 2:11-13"},{"kind":"para","text":"So we certainly won't be bored in eternity. We will all have something to do, and a purpose to do it, and it's all to bring glory and presence to the Lord."}]}]},{"start":3,"end":4,"title":"A Man's Character","entries":[{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"While we are here before the Lord’s return, we live in weakness. We have “weak hands” and “feeble knees,” some weaker and feebler than others. This is why church community is important. While going soulwinning is a great tool and something that should be put on the hearts of every Christian, encouraging the saints should be at the top of our priority list."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Christians have weak hands and feeble knees too, and we need to be strengthened and confirmed about the Lord’s return. Strengthening comes from reminding the believers about His future (and current) promises. Confirmation comes from continuously proving God’s Word as evident and necessary in the lives of believers."},{"kind":"para","text":"Strengthen the weak hands! Give the saints reason to strive! Confirm the feeble knees! Give them ground to stand on!"}]},{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"We have \"fearful hearts.” So now we have some characteristics of the Christian."},{"kind":"para","text":"Weak Hands:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Therefore I take pleasure in infirmities, in reproaches, in necessities, in persecutions, in distresses for Christ's sake: for when I am weak, then am I strong.","ref":"2 Corinthians 12:10"},{"kind":"para","text":"Feeble Knees:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"I am feeble and sore broken: I have roared by reason of the disquietness of my heart.","ref":"Psalm 38:8"},{"kind":"para","text":"Fearful Heart:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Men's hearts failing them for fear, and for looking after those things which are coming on the earth: for the powers of heaven shall be shaken.","ref":"Luke 21:26"},{"kind":"para","text":"But the Lord provides us with new characteristics that we can obtain right now. We don’t have to wait for the millennium reign to take on the Lord’s life for us. We are given:"},{"kind":"para","text":"Strength:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And he said unto me, My grace is sufficient for thee: for my strength is made perfect in weakness. Most gladly therefore will I rather glory in my infirmities, that the power of Christ may rest upon me.","ref":"2 Corinthians 12:9"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"The righteous cry, and the LORD heareth, and delivereth them out of all their troubles.","ref":"Psalm 34:17"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Likewise the Spirit also helpeth our infirmities: for we know not what we should pray for as we ought: but the Spirit itself maketh intercession for us with groanings which cannot be uttered.","ref":"Romans 8:26"},{"kind":"para","text":"Confirmation:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Even as it is meet for me to think this of you all, because I have you in my heart; inasmuch as both in my bonds, and in the defence and confirmation of the gospel, ye all are partakers of my grace.","ref":"Philippians 1:7"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"In whom ye also trusted, after that ye heard the word of truth, the gospel of your salvation: in whom also after that ye believed, ye were sealed with that holy Spirit of promise, Which is the earnest of our inheritance until the redemption of the purchased possession, unto the praise of his glory.","ref":"Ephesians 1:13-4"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Cast thy burden upon the LORD, and he shall sustain thee: he shall never suffer the righteous to be moved.","ref":"Psalm 55:22"},{"kind":"para","text":"God's Vengeance:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Dearly beloved, avenge not yourselves, but rather give place unto wrath: for it is written, Vengeance is mine; I will repay, saith the Lord.","ref":"Romans 12:19"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"O LORD God, to whom vengeance belongeth; O God, to whom vengeance belongeth, shew thyself.","ref":"Psalm 94:1"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And I will execute great vengeance upon them with furious rebukes; and they shall know that I am the LORD, when I shall lay my vengeance upon them.","ref":"Ezekiel 25:17"},{"kind":"para","text":"Recompense:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Seeing it is a righteous thing with God to recompense tribulation to them that trouble you;","ref":"2 Thessalonians 1:6"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For we know him that hath said, Vengeance belongeth unto me, I will recompense, saith the Lord. And again, The Lord shall judge his people.","ref":"Hebrews 10:30"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"To me belongeth vengeance, and recompence; their foot shall slide in due time: for the day of their calamity is at hand, and the things that shall come upon them make haste.","ref":"Deuteronomy 32:35"},{"kind":"para","text":"Salvation:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Salvation belongeth unto the LORD: thy blessing is upon thy people. Selah.","ref":"Psalm 3:8"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"That if thou shalt confess with thy mouth the Lord Jesus, and shalt believe in thine heart that God hath raised him from the dead, thou shalt be saved.","ref":"Romans 10:9"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Neither is there salvation in any other: for there is none other name under heaven given among men, whereby we must be saved.","ref":"Acts 4:12"},{"kind":"para","text":"These are not things we develop in ourselves. We can’t develop them ourselves even if we tried to. These are things that the LORD has to develop in a person."},{"kind":"para","text":"When we have the Lord, we are not living solemnly in our weak and fragile bodies. We might still have weak bodies, but we have strong spirits because it is no longer OUR spirit that resides in us. It is God’s Spirit that gives us strength and renews us to continue forward."}]}]},{"start":5,"end":7,"title":"No More Needs","entries":[{"start":5,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"My wife works with special needs children. She really enjoys her job and finds these kids to be a gift from the Lord. Most of the world has already written these young ones off because they can’t keep up with us. Not my wife, though. She doesn’t want to leave them behind. It truly breaks her heart when the school system gives up on them or transfers these students to a school that won’t help serve them. She is hurt when kids are failed and not growing."},{"kind":"para","text":"When the end comes, all special needs will be put to rest. We will all have eyes to see the supernatural, ears to hear the spiritual, bodies to feel the eternal, and mouths to speak the truth. There will be no overlooking an individual, no ignoring a need for a brother, no fleshly drag to keep us from serving, and no way for us to deceive our neighbors in the Lord. These are all struggles in our modern bodies, and we will not do away with them until we are with the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"Our sinful flesh doesn’t allow us to live appropriately (even when we are called Christians). Christians struggle with their flesh too. They just have an escape whereas the world does not. I can’t wait until I don’t have to struggle with myself anymore."}]},{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"We won’t be hurt by animals, insects, poisoning, heat, dehydration, or any sort of lacking substance that we might need today. You will be able to visit places where there are snakes and not have to worry about getting bitten or dying. We have spoken about this before in this book, but everything will be peaceful."},{"kind":"para","text":"It will be a place where we can rest, live, and grow together with the people of God. It will be what church is supposed to be today. We won’t be in want of anything because God will provide us with everything we will ever need, and the Earth (for the first time) will be in unity under the Lord for the rest of eternity."}]}]},{"start":8,"end":10,"title":"The Highway","entries":[{"start":8,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"In the book of Acts, as the church is started, the Apostles are given the title “The People of The Way.” Jesus is the Way, and they lived as people of the Way, which is the only way into this eternal kingdom. It’s through Jesus Christ. He is the highway. He is called “The way of holiness.” The only way you can pass over into this land is to be a man of the way—a “wayfaring” man."},{"kind":"para","text":"We might be fools, but when we have Christ, He keeps us on the right track. We cannot fall off this way once we have Him, though we make plenty of mistakes, as Isaiah is saying. We are really just dumb, yet the Lord keeps us on the way. It’s not possible for us to be lost again once we start on this highway."}]},{"start":9,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Knowing there is an eternal joy coming should provide us with a slight glimpse of joy today. We might find a lot of reasons to live in sorrow and sighing. People whom we love and trust cause us quite a bit of grief and pain. But eternity is coming, and when it does, we will have joy and gladness, and all that sorrow and sighing will feel and seem like a distant memory."},{"kind":"para","text":"Nothing can attack us in this new way. There is no demon or wicked evil in this world that can rob us of our way to the Lord. In fact, if someone kills us on our journey here, they just get us to the Lord quicker. They just bring us to joy sooner than we anticipated. But in this new kingdom, nothing will be able to hurt or harm us. We will be on a highway of safety, able to be with the Lord and have His protection. That is where we are headed."},{"kind":"para","text":"We are headed on the way of holiness, and we must maintain course until we get there. The highway to the Lord is a straight path. If you turn to the left or right, you are responsible for your actions. Just walk straight."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":10}],"verses":{"1":"The wilderness and the solitary place shall be glad for them; and the desert shall rejoice, and blossom as the rose.","2":"It shall blossom abundantly, and rejoice even with joy and singing: the glory of Lebanon shall be given unto it, the excellency of Carmel and Sharon, they shall see the glory of the Lord, and the excellency of our God.","3":"Strengthen ye the weak hands, and confirm the feeble knees.","4":"Say to them that are of a fearful heart, Be strong, fear not: behold, your God will come with vengeance, even God with a recompence; he will come and save you.","5":"Then the eyes of the blind shall be opened, and the ears of the deaf shall be unstopped.","6":"Then shall the lame man leap as an hart, and the tongue of the dumb sing: for in the wilderness shall waters break out, and streams in the desert.","7":"And the parched ground shall become a pool, and the thirsty land springs of water: in the habitation of dragons, where each lay, shall be grass with reeds and rushes.","8":"And an highway shall be there, and a way, and it shall be called The way of holiness; the unclean shall not pass over it; but it shall be for those: the wayfaring men, though fools, shall not err therein.","9":"No lion shall be there, nor any ravenous beast shall go up thereon, it shall not be found there; but the redeemed shall walk there:","10":"And the ransomed of the Lord shall return, and come to Zion with songs and everlasting joy upon their heads: they shall obtain joy and gladness, and sorrow and sighing shall flee away."}},
    "36": {"chapter":36,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: The last few chapters of warning, and clarity, have been something hopeful for the reader. I'm sure it was hopeful for the people of Israel as well, knowing that they will eventually have a future hope promised from the Lord. That future home, however, won't come until quite some time, and the future home for the believer (today) won't come for even longer. I look forward to being in the land of the Lord someday. I can't wait to see my Savior face to face."},{"kind":"para","text":"In this chapter, we get a bit of a break from prophecy. This is something that has been warned about though, but the people of Israel either forget, or just weren't paying attention. Either way, they are confronted by Assyria and threatened, and it throws them for a loop."}],"previously":["The last few chapters of warning and clarity have been something hopeful for the reader. I’m sure it was hopeful for the people of Israel as well, knowing that they will eventually have a future hope promised from the Lord. That future home, however, won’t come until quite some time, and the future home for the believer (today) won’t come for even longer. I look forward to being in the land of the Lord someday. I can’t wait to see my Savior face to face. In this chapter, we get a bit of a break from prophecy. This is something that has been warned about though, but the people of Israel either forget or just weren’t paying attention. Either way, they are confronted by Assyria and threatened, and it throws them for a loop."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":3,"title":"Assyria Confronts Jerusalem","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God was allowing Assyria to prosper significantly, and it seemed as though nothing could stop them. However, Isaiah made it well known that the Lord would protect Judah for a season. He declared that Assyria would not be successful in taking Jerusalem. Despite this, Assyria did capture the fortified cities, leaving Jerusalem vulnerable to an easy attack. I have mentioned this account before, which is found in 2 Kings, but we will read it again here from Isaiah’s perspective."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Rabshakeh appears to be Sennacherib’s right-hand man and serves as the spokesperson for the land. His mission is to persuade the people of Jerusalem that they have no hope in their God and that they will be handed over to Sennacherib’s forces, just like all the other nations before them. However, there is one thing Rabshakeh overlooked: the people of Jerusalem have a Godly prophet (or a few, but that’s beside the point). It would be wise for them to heed the advice of this prophet."}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"These three men were Hezekiah’s representatives. It would be dangerous for Hezekiah to show up there. If they killed the king, the city would certainly fall. But again, the Lord is their protection, so they should go to the Lord in this moment. May we also remember that Shebna is not a great man. We spoke about it briefly before."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Thus saith the Lord GOD of hosts, Go, get thee unto this treasurer, even unto Shebna, which is over the house, and say...He will surely violently turn and toss thee like a ball into a large country: there shalt thou die, and there the chariots of thy glory shall be the shame of thy lord's house.","ref":"Isaiah 22:15;18"},{"kind":"para","text":"He’s not going to chance hurting his country, at least not yet. He is just as scared as everyone else. It really goes to show that making a name for yourself is not all that it’s cracked up to be. In the end, you could just be taken captive anyway."}]}]},{"start":4,"end":10,"title":"No Protection","entries":[{"start":4,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"We have read this before in 2 Kings, so if you want a recap, you can go there. However, we have gained a deeper understanding of Jerusalem’s current confederacy with Egypt. We know that Egypt will be in the middle of this judgment with all the other nations as well, but the people of Israel were to be confederate with the Lord, not with the Egyptians. So Rabshakeh is right in saying this. He is right in his evaluation of their strength. They will not prosper with Egypt as their protection. But he will, however, get some information wrong:"}]},{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The altar he speaks about here is not the altar of the Lord. He’s talking about the high places that were never taken down. He doesn’t know that those places were not meant for the Lord. This proves their hand against the Assyrians right here. But they won’t recognize it."},{"kind":"para","text":"Now, I’m not a huge fan of repeating myself throughout this commentary, but I think there is an importance of remembering and reevaluating the turn of events. This is, again, from the eyes and perspective of Isaiah. He was the prophet for Hezekiah during this time, so Isaiah has more details. However, we read in 2 Kings a little more of the event taking place from the king’s perspective. In Chronicles, we read it from the Lord’s perspective."},{"kind":"para","text":"Why does the Lord repeat Himself like this? Well, He wants to be sure we get the idea. Jeremiah will detail the falling away into captivity quite clearly, and the minor prophets will give their perspectives. You might wonder why there are four gospels. Four perspectives!"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"This is the third time I am coming to you. In the mouth of two or three witnesses shall every word be established.","ref":"2 Corinthians 13:1"},{"kind":"para","text":"None of this world can say these events didn’t happen. Though there are plenty of people who try to deny the historical accuracy of scripture, there are far too many witnesses against them for us to deny their retelling. Plus, the Lord has written it in such a way that if you don’t take the account of a prophet (who wouldn’t lie about the accounting), or if you don’t want to take the perspective of a scribe (whose whole job was to literally retell events accurately or die), then you might take the perspective of the Lord (who quite literally cannot lie). Take your pick."},{"kind":"para","text":"So God repeats Himself, that way the readers and hearers have no excuse. None of us can say, “Oh, I wish I had known.” Hezekiah has already heard (no doubt) that Assyria won’t prosper against them, but this is going to shake him up still because Rabshakeh is claiming that their own God isn’t even going to protect them. They have proof that their God won’t protect them by the fact that they took their brothers up north."}]},{"start":8,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is a jab. He lets it be quite well known that they don’t have the army to stand against Assyria. Even if they could spare horses for them, they still wouldn’t be able to go up against the Assyrians."}]},{"start":9,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I have reason to believe that the Lord DIDN’T talk to Rabshakeh, however, I’ll humor him. If the Lord did speak to him and tell him to come up against this land, it was for this particular purpose right here. He wants to get the people of Jerusalem to TURN to Him. He wants their faith and prayers. If imminent danger doesn’t get God’s creation to turn to the Lord in disparity, nothing ever will…"}]}]},{"start":11,"end":12,"title":"Language Barrier","entries":[{"start":11,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I assume they say this because he was not very good at speaking Hebrew. He’s trying his best though. The Israelites were probably not very good at speaking in the Syrian language either, but they could understand it at least. There might have been some words that Rabshakeh didn’t say correctly, and so they were having a hard time keeping up with his threat. But I’m sure the message came through clear enough. If it didn’t, they’ll understand the next words."}]},{"start":12,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Rabshakeh turns around and says, “Maybe you’ll understand this. I’ve been sent to let you know that this place is going to eat their own dung and drink their own piss.” He’s not going to change up his message to appease them. He’s trying to show strength, and they are trying to insult him."}]}]},{"start":13,"end":21,"title":"Turn to Assyria","entries":[{"start":13,"end":13,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"He isn’t going to be bullied or pressured. This was a tactic of power. If they didn’t get it then, they will certainly get it now."}]},{"start":14,"end":17,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I want to pause here for a moment. “A land like your own…” Their land was never called “a land of corn and wine, a land of bread and vineyards.” Their land was always referred to by the Lord as something far different."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And I have said, I will bring you up out of the affliction of Egypt unto the land of the Canaanites, and the Hittites, and the Amorites, and the Perizzites, and the Hivites, and the Jebusites, unto a land flowing with milk and honey.","ref":"Exodus 3:17"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But I have said unto you, Ye shall inherit their land, and I will give it unto you to possess it, a land that floweth with milk and honey: I am the LORD your God, which have separated you from other people.","ref":"Leviticus 20:24"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Hear therefore, O Israel, and observe to do it; that it may be well with thee, and that ye may increase mightily, as the LORD God of thy fathers hath promised thee, in the land that floweth with milk and honey.","ref":"Deuteronomy 6:3"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For the children of Israel walked forty years in the wilderness, till all the people that were men of war, which came out of Egypt, were consumed, because they obeyed not the voice of the LORD: unto whom the LORD sware that he would not shew them the land, which the LORD sware unto their fathers that he would give us, a land that floweth with milk and honey.","ref":"Joshua 5:6"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"In the day that I lifted up mine hand unto them, to bring them forth of the land of Egypt into a land that I had espied for them, flowing with milk and honey, which is the glory of all lands:","ref":"Ezekiel 20:6"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And they told him, and said, We came unto the land whither thou sentest us, and surely it floweth with milk and honey; and this is the fruit of it.","ref":"Numbers 13:27"},{"kind":"para","text":"This is another sure sign to the people of Jerusalem that these Assyrians know nothing about this land or its people. This should have brought even more comfort to those listening because Rabshakeh doesn’t have all his facts straight. They don’t want a land of corn and wine. Perhaps, at this moment, they do. Maybe that is the world’s version of the promised land. It was a land full of things that fill them and cause them to err. But the Lord wanted the land to be sweet and plentiful. The land, though, is not recognized as such to the rest of the world. That’s because the people of the land were living just like the rest of the world. They were not living like the people of God. That’s why Rabshakeh couldn’t tell the difference between the altar of the Lord and the high places that they falsely worshipped on. At this time, they are just a land full of substance, not of Spirit."}]},{"start":18,"end":20,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"He makes a point. No one else could stop them. Why would this little town of Jerusalem be able to stop him now? It would seem as if all odds are against them at the moment."}]},{"start":21,"end":21,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"They don’t say a single thing, and I’m sure it was eating at them. They probably either wanted to stand up for themselves or cry out loud. But they just held their peace and waited for Rabshakeh to finish before evaluating and crying to the king. They kept to the king’s command, like they were supposed to. If only they listened to the Lord so well."}]}]},{"start":22,"end":22,"title":"Undone","entries":[{"start":22,"end":22,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"They left the wall, walked down towards the king’s place, and then started tearing their clothes and crying. They held their peace at least until they were out of sight from any of the people of Assyria. We are left on a small cliffhanger, but we should also know what happens next. We are told they are secure from anything the Assyrians might try to do, and God is going to keep that promise. They know they will have a fall, but it certainly won’t be from Assyria. If you don’t know what happens next, I just gave you a major spoiler. However, you should have already known that was going to take place. If you have forgotten it within the short time of studying this book, then you can understand why the Israelites may have forgotten it from months (possibly even years) ago. They should have been more serious about this beforehand though. They were constantly warned about the Assyrians. They were warned about what the Lord would do. I’m sure they just didn’t believe it. Now that it’s in front of their faces, they don’t know what to do but scramble towards the king and hope that he has some sort of solution. Let me just tell you now, the king will not have an answer. He won’t know what to do. But he does the smartest thing any person of leadership should do, and that is turn to the Lord for answers."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":10},{"start":11,"end":11},{"start":12,"end":12},{"start":13,"end":13},{"start":14,"end":17},{"start":18,"end":20},{"start":21,"end":21},{"start":22,"end":22}],"verses":{"1":"Now it came to pass in the fourteenth year of king Hezekiah, that Sennacherib king of Assyria came up against all the defenced cities of Judah, and took them.","2":"And the king of Assyria sent Rabshakeh from Lachish to Jerusalem unto king Hezekiah with a great army. And he stood by the conduit of the upper pool in the highway of the fuller's field.","3":"Then came forth unto him Eliakim, Hilkiah's son, which was over the house, and Shebna the scribe, and Joah, Asaph's son, the recorder.","4":"And Rabshakeh said unto them, Say ye now to Hezekiah, Thus saith the great king, the king of Assyria, What confidence is this wherein thou trustest?","5":"I say, sayest thou, (but they are but vain words) I have counsel and strength for war: now on whom dost thou trust, that thou rebellest against me?","6":"Lo, thou trustest in the staff of this broken reed, on Egypt; whereon if a man lean, it will go into his hand, and pierce it: so is Pharaoh king of Egypt to all that trust in him.","7":"But if thou say to me, We trust in the Lord our God: is it not he, whose high places and whose altars Hezekiah hath taken away, and said to Judah and to Jerusalem, Ye shall worship before this altar?","8":"Now therefore give pledges, I pray thee, to my master the king of Assyria, and I will give thee two thousand horses, if thou be able on thy part to set riders upon them.","9":"How then wilt thou turn away the face of one captain of the least of my master's servants, and put thy trust on Egypt for chariots and for horsemen?","10":"And am I now come up without the Lord against this land to destroy it? the Lord said unto me, Go up against this land, and destroy it.","11":"Then said Eliakim and Shebna and Joah unto Rabshakeh, Speak, I pray thee, unto thy servants in the Syrian language; for we understand it: and speak not to us in the Jews' language, in the ears of the people that are on the wall.","12":"But Rabshakeh said, Hath my master sent me to thy master and to thee to speak these words? hath he not sent me to the men that sit upon the wall, that they may eat their own dung, and drink their own piss with you?","13":"Then Rabshakeh stood, and cried with a loud voice in the Jews' language, and said, Hear ye the words of the great king, the king of Assyria.","14":"Thus saith the king, Let not Hezekiah deceive you: for he shall not be able to deliver you.","15":"Neither let Hezekiah make you trust in the Lord, saying, The Lord will surely deliver us: this city shall not be delivered into the hand of the king of Assyria.","16":"Hearken not to Hezekiah: for thus saith the king of Assyria, Make an agreement with me by a present, and come out to me: and eat ye every one of his vine, and every one of his fig tree, and drink ye every one the waters of his own cistern;","17":"Until I come and take you away to a land like your own land, a land of corn and wine, a land of bread and vineyards.","18":"Beware lest Hezekiah persuade you, saying, the Lord will deliver us. Hath any of the gods of the nations delivered his land out of the hand of the king of Assyria?","19":"Where are the gods of Hamath and Arphad? where are the gods of Sepharvaim? and have they delivered Samaria out of my hand?","20":"Who are they among all the gods of these lands, that have delivered their land out of my hand, that the Lord should deliver Jerusalem out of my hand?","21":"But they held their peace, and answered him not a word: for the king's commandment was, saying, Answer him not.","22":"Then came Eliakim, the son of Hilkiah, that was over the household, and Shebna the scribe, and Joah, the son of Asaph, the recorder, to Hezekiah with their clothes rent, and told him the words of Rabshakeh."}},
    "37": {"chapter":37,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: In our last chapter, we see some people of Assyria come and take down the defenced cities surrounding Jerusalem (where king Hezekiah was reigning). Rabshakeh (a messenger for the king of Assyria) makes some pretty pointed threats at these people if they don't comply. Instead of threating them back, they just listen to the words, and go to the king crying about the situation. We were left off on a cliffhanger about how the king would take the news, but the Lord completes this story right here in this chapter."},{"kind":"para","text":"We will see what Hezekiah's leadership really consists of by the way in which he approaches this problem. Honestly, that is the best way to see your leaders strength. How does he deal with a trial? If he can't deal with major issues appropriately, he should not be trusted to lead people through their own issues."}],"previously":["In our last chapter, we see some people of Assyria come and take down the defended cities surrounding Jerusalem, where King Hezekiah was reigning. Rabshakeh, a messenger for the king of Assyria, makes some pretty pointed threats at these people if they don’t comply. Instead of threatening them back, they just listen to the words and go to the king, crying about the situation. We were left off on a cliffhanger about how the king would take the news, but the Lord completes this story right here in this chapter. We will see what Hezekiah’s leadership really consists of by the way in which he approaches this problem. Honestly, that is the best way to see your leader’s strength. How does he deal with a trial? If he can’t deal with major issues appropriately, he should not be trusted to lead people through their own issues."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":4,"title":"Prayer & Presence","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Assyria has made their threats, and now Hezekiah, the King of Judah, has heard about it, and it bothers him. However, he should have known what was going to happen. He was told by Isaiah that he would be fine in this situation, but now that he’s faced with it, he is worried."},{"kind":"para","text":"Prophets were not just messengers for the Lord; they were preachers. They warned people about the things that were coming. Noah warned people before the flood as well:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And spared not the old world, but saved Noah the eighth person, a preacher of righteousness, bringing in the flood upon the world of the ungodly;","ref":"2 Peter 2:5"},{"kind":"para","text":"Obviously, Noah took God’s warnings seriously, and if God brings a warning to you, it would be wise to share that warning with others around you. I think it’s kind of odd that so many churches reject the calling on a person’s life rather than edify and encourage that calling. Someone might have a calling to start a Bible study, and the pastor says, “Good luck with that.” Or perhaps they have a calling to open-air preach, and the pastor says, “Good luck with that.” Or maybe they have a calling to start a disabled ministry, or a prison ministry, or a retirement home ministry, and the pastor says, “Good luck with that.” Where is the Godly encouragement that scripture commands of us? Where is the hope and building up of the saints?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Callings are warnings from the Lord in a way. If you don’t follow the Lord’s calling, I promise you, your life will be miserable. It will always feel like you are missing something until you do what God wants you to do. The church should take that seriously. It doesn’t just become a spiritual strain on the believer; it becomes an emotional and physical strain as well. I’ve had callings on my life that I have had to skip out on. Not because I personally wanted to skip them, but because the church rejected me and told me I was no good at it. I sat in hurt for months, and the church never addressed it or cared. In fact, most churches probably wouldn’t have cared if I even ever came back. That happens to far more people than it rightfully should. There might be some callings that you just can’t help in, but we should be doing our best to link up with the people of the church to explore, develop, and encourage every human’s calling to love the Lord and love others better than we do right now. That’s the old church, though, and I don’t see that coming in our lifetime."},{"kind":"para","text":"If we are not busy developing and encouraging the calling of God in the lives of other people, we are doing what Jerusalem is doing here. We have heard the warning, but we reject the message of God, and when the time comes to confront a problem, we are completely confused and lost, and the person with a calling is the only one that any of us can depend on. We don’t seem to go to the Lord in those instances. If we did, we would probably be led to simply listen to the person with the calling to begin with."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"And now they want Isaiah’s help. Now that they are backed into a corner with nowhere else to turn, they look for the man of God. And like a good man of God, you know where Isaiah is? Where he said he would be. Isaiah could be found. Most of our preachers and pastors today are difficult to get ahold of…"}]},{"start":3,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"It seems they don’t ask for direction. Perhaps they already knew that the Lord was listening and so He was going to do whatever He saw fit. They just ask for prayer. Isaiah is more than just a man of prayer. Don’t get me wrong, I find nothing wrong with prayer. In fact, it is the cog that brings power to our faith, but there’s still more to do than just pray. If I’m honest, I am not a huge fan of people who don’t talk to me or show any kind of connection to me that come up to me and say, “Hey, I’m praying for you.” My thoughts are always, “Really? What are you praying for? Is it to get to know me better because your prayer is not working?” No, there has to be more than prayer if you want to make a connection."},{"kind":"para","text":"Recently, a brother in Christ had lost his son. I haven’t been leading the lifegroup that he’s involved in for a while (long story), but I knew that I needed to go visit him and see how he and his wife were doing. I reached out to the new leader of the lifegroup, and this leader said, “I never know what to do in this situation. Do I reach out to them or just give them space?” I think a lot of well-meaning leaders just give people space. But that is not what people need. They need encouragement. They need love and compassion from their church. I wrote back, “Let me tell you now that people need your presence more than your prayers. That is what ministry is. If they get upset with your presence, it’s not you they are upset with. We are called to weep with those who weep, and you can do that in closeness with them. Some people may be far off, and you’ll have to weep from a distance, but when it’s in your power to visit the saints, DO IT.” We cannot wash our brothers’ and sisters’ feet from a distance. What a crying shame that we have the power to help and stand with our hurting brothers in Christ, and we choose not to do it… Isaiah will not just pray. He will be present."}]}]},{"start":5,"end":7,"title":"Isaiah Answers","entries":[{"start":5,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord gives comfort. He doesn’t say, “Were you not listening before? I TOLD you that you would be taken care of. Why are you worried?” Rather, God just repeats Himself and adds a few other details to give clarity. Some sort of report is going to come to Assyria, and these men will go back and die a different way. Hezekiah was going to just have to trust the Lord here."}]}]},{"start":8,"end":13,"title":"Rabshakeh Reminds Hezekiah","entries":[{"start":8,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Rabshakeh returns because he hears a rumor. When he gets back home, he sees that Libnah has started to fight against Assyria. He wants to go deal with Jerusalem too, but he has to fight this battle in the meantime. So he is going to send a message back to Jerusalem for what will happen after he deals with Libnah."}]},{"start":9,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Rabshakeh says, “Don’t trust the Lord’s advice. Don’t believe what God is telling you.” By that one statement alone, we can know that this person is absolutely wrong. This, if anything, should boost the confidence of Hezekiah in the Lord. It would certainly boost my confidence."}]},{"start":11,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I’ll answer on behalf of Hezekiah. No, the false gods of the other nations have not rescued their own people. Why? Well, it’s because they are false gods. The God of Israel is the only true God, and that is why their God will give them rescue from Assyria."}]},{"start":13,"end":13,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Destroyed and taken down, they were only because they didn’t trust in the God of creation. They trusted in fake gods that they made themselves. We have the same choice when faced with any battle today as well. Will we find comfort and strength in something we just make up, or are we going to trust in the Lord to provide like He says He will?"}]}]},{"start":14,"end":20,"title":"Hezekiah's Prayer","entries":[{"start":14,"end":14,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is the wisest decision a leader can make. He tried Isaiah, and Isaiah already gave him an answer. Now he is going to go before the Lord personally and make sure what Isaiah said was true. Every man of God should always go to the Lord to line things up. If something doesn’t add up, you can bet that it isn’t the Lord that is wrong about it. It will be the advice or ideas of the man."},{"kind":"para","text":"Sometimes it won’t line up from the speaker behind the pulpit either. That’s when you know they got it wrong. You can confront the preacher and ask him about it, or you can ignore it. If they get mad when you confront them, it’s likely they are not trusted sources anyway. They just want to say stuff and not be questioned. Question everything, friend. That is a rule to live by."}]},{"start":15,"end":16,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Notice that Hezekiah takes the letter of Rabshakeh and approaches God with the truth. He says, “These gods are not You. These gods are not real. YOU alone are the God of all the kingdoms of the earth.” He knows who he is praying to, and he knows that this God is a God that will answer back if He so sees fit. He answers the believers today too."},{"kind":"para","text":"Some people claim they hear an audible voice from the Lord. I don’t know if I necessarily believe that. I hear His Word come back to me. He speaks to me through the account that has already been given. “When we pray, we speak to God. When we read, God speaks to us. It is far better that He speak to me, than that I should speak to Him.” D.L. Moody"},{"kind":"para","text":"God speaks to us through His Word, and He provides answers to us that we never thought could be answered. He’s a God that cares about us deeply."}]},{"start":17,"end":20,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is quite the prayer. God knows all of this. He sees it. He hears it. Before Hezekiah did anything, He was already moving things for these people. God wants to hear the prayers of Hezekiah, though. That certainly pleases God. And because Hezekiah went to the Lord this way, God will answer Hezekiah. God is pleased by all of His children coming to Him in prayer."}]}]},{"start":21,"end":25,"title":"God Responds","entries":[{"start":21,"end":21,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Pause. We understand and know that Isaiah was not present when Hezekiah prayed. Because of this, the fact that Isaiah knows what Hezekiah said and that he prayed would give great comfort to Hezekiah."}]},{"start":22,"end":22,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is what God thinks of Assyria’s threat. He says they are a laughingstock for their words. Sennacherib is a comedian, thinking that he can defy the Lord and take His people still. It’s quite possible that God would have allowed Assyria to take Judah if they were a little more humble about it. If they had not boasted of their pride, Judah was an easy target as well."},{"kind":"para","text":"But because they put themselves over God and called Him a liar, He is going to prove Himself to this nation, and they will not have the strength they thought they had. It’s a dangerous thing to get God involved in a heated conversation. God will judge now because Rabshakeh added God to the conversation."}]},{"start":23,"end":23,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"By their words, they have reproached, blasphemed, exalted themselves, and lifted their eyes up against the Lord. Because of this, the Lord is going to make sure their acts don’t follow their words. They have dug a hole for themselves to fall into."}]},{"start":24,"end":24,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The Assyrians think they have unlimited power. Let’s bring this down to a spiritual level for a second, because I believe it’s important that the Bible is applicable to us, especially since we often become quite high-minded. There are many leaders in the church, or even in big business, who begin to believe they are “untouchable” like the Assyrians think here. They believe the Lord has given them unlimited power."},{"kind":"para","text":"God will absolutely deal with those false preachers. They are not untouchable. They are not God. They might like to pretend they are, but they truly are not."}]},{"start":25,"end":25,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God doesn’t have to worry about these vague and useless threats against Him. He is not hurt by wicked people’s words. That is the only way an atheist tries to hurt God. He either throws insults against the Lord and His people or tries to hurt God’s people. Either way, there’s no way for the Lord to be touched by these weak beings."},{"kind":"para","text":"The only way the Lord is hurt is through their rejection of Him, and all that does is give Him the power and ability to send you into judgment. You literally give Him a reason to put you into torture for all of eternity. That’s not what He wants, but He will certainly give you what YOU want in the end."}]}]},{"start":26,"end":29,"title":"God Reminds","entries":[{"start":26,"end":27,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God has done it before, and He will do it again. Israel was able to obtain this land because the Lord provided them with victory. They can save this land if they depend on the Lord for victory once more."},{"kind":"para","text":"Hezekiah is currently depending on God, and Assyria is causing chaos for themselves by attempting to defy God. Therefore, God is going to remind them who holds all power."}]},{"start":28,"end":29,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"It’s not just God’s people they were trying to attack. It was God Himself they thought they could get one over on. The power they received to take all these other nations really just got to their heads. They became arrogant. They became prideful. God has a few things to say about pride:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"When pride cometh, then cometh shame: but with the lowly is wisdom.","ref":"Proverbs 11:2"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Every one that is proud in heart is an abomination to the LORD: though hand join in hand, he shall not be unpunished.","ref":"Proverbs 16:5"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Pride goeth before destruction, and an haughty spirit before a fall.","ref":"Proverbs 16:18"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But he giveth more grace. Wherefore he saith, God resisteth the proud, but giveth grace unto the humble.","ref":"James 4:6"},{"kind":"para","text":"The list honestly goes on. God has a lot to say about pride. He doesn’t just let the prideful get what they want. He deals with people of pride, and they usually are left with nothing but ruin when all is said and done. They will have wished they treated people better when the Lord finishes with them."}]}]},{"start":30,"end":32,"title":"The Remnant Survive","entries":[{"start":30,"end":30,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God is going to prove His words here by giving them supplication for the next three years. They will thrive in their land and won’t have to depend on anyone or anything around them. They will be safe there for a time."}]},{"start":31,"end":32,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There is a remnant that will return to the Lord and His land. They will be saved by the Lord’s hand. This is a foreshadow, absolutely. Not just to the children of Judah, but to the world, which will be saved during the time of tribulation."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Even so then at this present time also there is a remnant according to the election of grace.","ref":"Romans 11:5"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And the dragon was wroth with the woman, and went to make war with the remnant of her seed, which keep the commandments of God, and have the testimony of Jesus Christ.","ref":"Revelation 12:17"},{"kind":"para","text":"There is certainly going to be a small remnant of believers here on Earth, and Satan will always be trying to get rid of God’s people. Honestly, that will be Satan’s ultimate downfall. He can’t let God’s people go. He will search them out, even if it means his own death. That’s how much Satan hates you today. He is doing whatever it takes to make sure you are isolated, alone, and hurt by this world. He’s quite good at it, honestly."}]}]},{"start":33,"end":35,"title":"Safe From Assyria","entries":[{"start":33,"end":35,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God is promising protection here. He will personally see to the safety of this city. Assyria will not have a foothold here, and God is going to keep good on His promise. Furthermore, God is going to prove Himself to Hezekiah and the people of Judah. This should spark some sort of revival in the land (or at least you would think it would)."}]}]},{"start":36,"end":38,"title":"Sennacherib's Pride","entries":[{"start":36,"end":36,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"One hundred and eighty-five thousand people died suddenly. That should have sobered up Assyria quickly."}]},{"start":37,"end":37,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Sennacherib, the king of Assyria, went into hiding, running just as God had predicted. Despite this, he won’t learn anything from the experience, though he acknowledges losing this battle in a miraculous way. A prideful person like him won’t give honor to the victor when they lose, as they are unwilling to let go of their pride to encourage someone else. According to some scholars, this incident is recorded by the scribes of Sennacherib, with a journal account stating, “I attacked Hezekiah of Judah who had not subjected himself to me, and took forty-six fortresses, forts, and small cities. I carried away captive 200,150 people, big and small, both male and female, a multitude of horses, young bulls, asses, camels, and oxen. Hezekiah himself I locked up in Jerusalem like a bird in its cage. I put up banks against the city. I separated his cities whose inhabitants I had taken prisoners from his realm and gave them to Mitiniti, king of Ashdod, Padi, king of Ekron, and Zilbel, king of Gaza, thus diminishing his country. And I added another tax to the one imposed on him earlier.” Bultema"},{"kind":"para","text":"Whether this account is accurate or not, I cannot say, but you can verify it for yourself if you ever visit the British Museum. Sennacherib was proud of how he treated Jerusalem and the surrounding people, feeling satisfied with how Hezekiah was left."}]},{"start":38,"end":38,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"His own children don’t seem to like him. He was prideful, and he died a shallow and disgraceful death. That will forever be his legacy. Dead worshipping a false god by his own two sons."},{"kind":"para","text":"But Hezekiah can rest assured that God kept His word. He can have full confidence in God now that he has seen God provide, and will continue to see God provide… right?"}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":10},{"start":11,"end":12},{"start":13,"end":13},{"start":14,"end":14},{"start":15,"end":16},{"start":17,"end":20},{"start":21,"end":21},{"start":22,"end":22},{"start":23,"end":23},{"start":24,"end":24},{"start":25,"end":25},{"start":26,"end":27},{"start":28,"end":29},{"start":30,"end":30},{"start":31,"end":32},{"start":33,"end":35},{"start":36,"end":36},{"start":37,"end":37},{"start":38,"end":38}],"verses":{"1":"And it came to pass, when king Hezekiah heard it, that he rent his clothes, and covered himself with sackcloth, and went into the house of the Lord.","2":"And he sent Eliakim, who was over the household, and Shebna the scribe, and the elders of the priests covered with sackcloth, unto Isaiah the prophet the son of Amoz.","3":"And they said unto him, Thus saith Hezekiah, This day is a day of trouble, and of rebuke, and of blasphemy: for the children are come to the birth, and there is not strength to bring forth.","4":"It may be the Lord thy God will hear the words of Rabshakeh, whom the king of Assyria his master hath sent to reproach the living God, and will reprove the words which the Lord thy God hath heard: wherefore lift up thy prayer for the remnant that is left.","5":"So the servants of king Hezekiah came to Isaiah.","6":"And Isaiah said unto them, Thus shall ye say unto your master, Thus saith the Lord, Be not afraid of the words that thou hast heard, wherewith the servants of the king of Assyria have blasphemed me.","7":"Behold, I will send a blast upon him, and he shall hear a rumour, and return to his own land; and I will cause him to fall by the sword in his own land.","8":"So Rabshakeh returned, and found the king of Assyria warring against Libnah: for he had heard that he was departed from Lachish.","9":"And he heard say concerning Tirhakah king of Ethiopia, He is come forth to make war with thee. And when he heard it, he sent messengers to Hezekiah, saying,","10":"Thus shall ye speak to Hezekiah king of Judah, saying, Let not thy God, in whom thou trustest, deceive thee, saying, Jerusalem shall not be given into the hand of the king of Assyria.","11":"Behold, thou hast heard what the kings of Assyria have done to all lands by destroying them utterly; and shalt thou be delivered?","12":"Have the gods of the nations delivered them which my fathers have destroyed, as Gozan, and Haran, and Rezeph, and the children of Eden which were in Telassar?","13":"Where is the king of Hamath, and the king of Arphad, and the king of the city of Sepharvaim, Hena, and Ivah?","14":"And Hezekiah received the letter from the hand of the messengers, and read it: and Hezekiah went up unto the house of the Lord, and spread it before the Lord.","15":"And Hezekiah prayed unto the Lord, saying,","16":"O Lord of hosts, God of Israel, that dwellest between the cherubims, thou art the God, even thou alone, of all the kingdoms of the earth: thou hast made heaven and earth.","17":"Incline thine ear, O Lord, and hear; open thine eyes, O Lord, and see: and hear all the words of Sennacherib, which hath sent to reproach the living God.","18":"Of a truth, Lord, the kings of Assyria have laid waste all the nations, and their countries,","19":"And have cast their gods into the fire: for they were no gods, but the work of men's hands, wood and stone: therefore they have destroyed them.","20":"Now therefore, O Lord our God, save us from his hand, that all the kingdoms of the earth may know that thou art the Lord, even thou only.","21":"Then Isaiah the son of Amoz sent unto Hezekiah, saying, Thus saith the Lord God of Israel, Whereas thou hast prayed to me against Sennacherib king of Assyria:","22":"This is the word which the Lord hath spoken concerning him; The virgin, the daughter of Zion, hath despised thee, and laughed thee to scorn; the daughter of Jerusalem hath shaken her head at thee.","23":"Whom hast thou reproached and blasphemed? and against whom hast thou exalted thy voice, and lifted up thine eyes on high? even against the Holy One of Israel.","24":"By thy servants hast thou reproached the Lord, and hast said, By the multitude of my chariots am I come up to the height of the mountains, to the sides of Lebanon; and I will cut down the tall cedars thereof, and the choice fir trees thereof: and I will enter into the height of his border, and the forest of his Carmel.","25":"I have digged, and drunk water; and with the sole of my feet have I dried up all the rivers of the besieged places.","26":"Hast thou not heard long ago, how I have done it; and of ancient times, that I have formed it? now have I brought it to pass, that thou shouldest be to lay waste defenced cities into ruinous heaps.","27":"Therefore their inhabitants were of small power, they were dismayed and confounded: they were as the grass of the field, and as the green herb, as the grass on the housetops, and as corn blasted before it be grown up.","28":"But I know thy abode, and thy going out, and thy coming in, and thy rage against me.","29":"Because thy rage against me, and thy tumult, is come up into mine ears, therefore will I put my hook in thy nose, and my bridle in thy lips, and I will turn thee back by the way by which thou camest.","30":"And this shall be a sign unto thee, Ye shall eat this year such as groweth of itself; and the second year that which springeth of the same: and in the third year sow ye, and reap, and plant vineyards, and eat the fruit thereof.","31":"And the remnant that is escaped of the house of Judah shall again take root downward, and bear fruit upward:","32":"For out of Jerusalem shall go forth a remnant, and they that escape out of mount Zion: the zeal of the Lord of hosts shall do this.","33":"Therefore thus saith the Lord concerning the king of Assyria, He shall not come into this city, nor shoot an arrow there, nor come before it with shields, nor cast a bank against it.","34":"By the way that he came, by the same shall he return, and shall not come into this city, saith the Lord.","35":"For I will defend this city to save it for mine own sake, and for my servant David's sake.","36":"Then the angel of the Lord went forth, and smote in the camp of the Assyrians a hundred and fourscore and five thousand: and when they arose early in the morning, behold, they were all dead corpses.","37":"So Sennacherib king of Assyria departed, and went and returned, and dwelt at Nineveh.","38":"And it came to pass, as he was worshipping in the house of Nisroch his god, that Adrammelech and Sharezer his sons smote him with the sword; and they escaped into the land of Armenia: and Esarhaddon his son reigned in his stead."}},
    "38": {"chapter":38,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: In our last chapter, Isaiah gives Hezekiah a word of victory. God promises to protect Jerusalem from the attacks of Assyria, and gives the people of Judah providence for at least three years. Hezekiah can rest assured that God is going to keep to His promise, and that they will be safe from the impending doom all around them."},{"kind":"para","text":"In this chapter, we get a little deeper of a look at Hezekiah. We get what is bothering him during this time, and we see what kind of man he is when the Lord confronts him with some important news. If only he stayed on this course for the rest of his life and rulership. Sadly, he will make a grave mistake that will be noted later."}],"previously":["In our last chapter, Isaiah delivers a message of victory to Hezekiah. God promises to protect Jerusalem from the attacks of Assyria and provides the people of Judah with providence for at least three years. Hezekiah can rest assured that God will keep His promise and that they will be safe from the impending doom surrounding them. In this chapter, we gain a deeper insight into Hezekiah. We learn what is troubling him during this time and observe his character when the Lord confronts him with important news. If only he had maintained this course throughout his life and rulership. Sadly, he will make a grave mistake that will be noted later."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":8,"title":"Hezekiah's Death Sentence","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"“In those days” is obviously speaking about the days of the Assyrian war. “In that day” is talking about the future. So while things were looming for Hezekiah and the people concerning Assyria, their king (Hezekiah) was dealing with some sort of sickness. Now Isaiah has the daunting task of telling Hezekiah he’s going to die during a time when they should be celebrating victory. Of course, this is a retelling of this event through the eyes of Isaiah. We have read about this situation in 2 Kings, which helps us know the full scope of what is about to happen."}]},{"start":2,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Hezekiah was one of the good kings. He did a lot for the Lord, that’s to be sure. I believe his faith is what saved him and this nation from so many disasters. He could live a long, full life if he kept his sight focused on God. However, he wasn’t completely righteous. He still had the terrible sin of idolatry to deal with, and Hezekiah never did. He never took down the high places. The high places were what kept bringing all of Israel into trouble and turmoil. Worshiping false gods was a sure way to have God on your bad side. It’s still a terrible sin to fall into today. Most worship their money today. Even church leaders worship it. Mega churches are a prime example of it if I can be honest…"}]},{"start":4,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God already promised that He will defend Jerusalem from Assyria. He is going to keep this promise, even though He is making Hezekiah a new promise. God can add promises to promises. He is good at juggling all His promises. He gave a sign to Hezekiah that they will be self-sustaining for three years by their own produce. Now He’s going to give a new sign to Hezekiah that the promise of fifteen years of more life is going to be kept."}]},{"start":7,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"We gain a clearer picture in 2 Kings. The choice is left to Hezekiah about which way the sun should go. He thinks the sun going forward ten degrees is too obvious, but the sun going backward is unheard of. So the Lord grants His request to bring the sun back ten degrees. And then we are opened up to what God has said since the beginning of this book."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Ah sinful nation, a people laden with iniquity, a seed of evildoers, children that are corrupters: they have forsaken the LORD, they have provoked the Holy One of Israel unto anger, they are gone away backward.","ref":"Isaiah 1:4"},{"kind":"para","text":"Just as the sun goes backwards, the people of Judah certainly will as well."}]}]},{"start":9,"end":20,"title":"Hezekiah's Psalm","entries":[{"start":9,"end":9,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Hezekiah, of course, is going to rejoice. He’s ecstatic that God would grant him a longer time on this Earth. He still had plenty of reigning and ruling to do. You’d think with his new life that he had been given, he would clean up Judah and start putting in work to protect them, and take down anything that is related to idol worship. That, of course, won’t happen. Hezekiah (and Judah) will regret these extra fifteen years of life."}]},{"start":10,"end":14,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Hezekiah truly and deeply thought his life was over. He believed there was no hope for him. The sickness must have been quite serious for him to have these thoughts about his last moments on Earth, especially when Isaiah came to tell him the news that he wouldn’t survive. He thought he wouldn’t get to grow old and that God was dealing with him quickly. He believed everything would break and fall apart. Perhaps this sickness made him feel like all his bones were broken. He “chattered” like a crane, possibly due to a fever that made him feel achy and cold. He was begging for mercy. These were his thoughts in the last moments of his life."},{"kind":"para","text":"It doesn’t seem as if he prayed for healing; he just prayed for relief. God went above and beyond his simple prayers and gave him his true desires. I think Hezekiah came to terms with simply dying, but he didn’t want to die in this way. He wanted to die a righteous death and from old age. He couldn’t understand how a sickness could kill him rather than nobility."}]},{"start":15,"end":15,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There was nothing more he could do. To him, the Lord made the choice. It was up to the Lord to decide. And as miserable as that might sound to us, it truly is up to the Lord to decide. He chooses your fate. He chooses your destination. He has it all planned out and prepared for you and everyone else on this planet. He is the holder and ruler of all souls, no matter what or where they might be."},{"kind":"para","text":"As a believer, I could understand the comfort of respecting God’s decision with your death. If I had a deadly disease, it is up to the Lord to do what He wants with me. The problem for me lies in those around me. I am confident in my own salvation, but I can’t be quite as confident with my daughters, my wife, or my mother. Their salvation is their own. I don’t hold the Lamb’s Book, so I just have to pray and hope that they truly understood the scriptures about believing and trusting in Christ’s death for them."},{"kind":"para","text":"The fact that Hezekiah was so undone about this decision kind of tells me his level of faith. He, perhaps, is a believer, but his faith was quite weak if he was not willing to let go of this world to be with the Lord. Then again, I could understand not wanting to die a painful death. Perhaps that was his biggest worry."}]},{"start":16,"end":17,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"These are deep words spoken here. This is the look of salvation. This is what the realization of a man who has had his burdens lifted looks like. What a stark difference from what is written above. The first part of it is the way in which a weak man would write. The second part of this letter is the way in which a saved man would write. His sins are forgiven, and his soul is delivered! What a glorious day it is for any man on this Earth to have this take place in their own lives."}]},{"start":18,"end":18,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Another fantastic verse! The grave is a place of sorrow, and death is a place of mourning. There is no praise or celebration in the grave or death. When you are in “the pit” (whether eternally or physically, it doesn’t matter), there is no hope—not just for the truth of God, but for life and growth in general."},{"kind":"para","text":"However, it is a very important reminder to the readers here. You only have a limited time to learn and grow in the Lord. You are only given a short while to hope in truth, so give this life your best effort to learn from the Lord and grow in Him. I guarantee there will be no man who dies who says, “I wish I would have enjoyed the world more.” No, they will all say, “I wish I would have spent more time getting to know the Lord more.”"}]},{"start":19,"end":19,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Both in the present and in the afterlife, only the living will praise God. Those destined for Hell will not get to praise God. They will be shouting, but it won’t be praises; it will be shouts of pain. Only the living have shouts of praise. You’ll be shouting both ways, but that is the ultimate decision for every person on Earth. Do you want an eternity shouting praise, or an eternity shouting pain?"}]},{"start":20,"end":20,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Hezekiah was a songwriter, I’m sure of it. David was a songwriter as well. Hezekiah didn’t request his songs to be written into a book, perhaps this is one of them. It is written almost identically to a psalm, going from terror to praise in one symphony of God’s providence and salvation."},{"kind":"para","text":"The interesting part of this verse is “sing MY songs… the days of our life in the house of the Lord…” I think there are a lot of people singing their own songs in God’s house today. They play and sing what THEY want, rather than what the Lord wants. They look to tote their own talent in front of an audience. It’s a show, not worship. I can’t imagine getting on stage and acting so pious in front of the Lord. The people might clap their hands and act like monkeys, but it’s the Lord’s viewpoint that I am concerned with."},{"kind":"para","text":"Choosing and playing songs is a gift from the Lord that should be properly prayed for and geared toward worshipping in God’s house. The saddest part is, I don’t think Hezekiah spends the rest of his days singing to the Lord. He will forget this promise here…"}]}]},{"start":21,"end":22,"title":"The Heart of Scripture","entries":[{"start":21,"end":22,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Isaiah clarifies, at the end for some reason, how he was able to heal Hezekiah and Hezekiah’s request to prove that he was going to live. It was a boil that bothered him. That doesn’t seem like it would be much of a problem. People get boils quite a bit in this world, and it usually doesn’t bring them to their deathbed. It will pop over time, and then you just go about your business like usual. This was a different kind of monster, I guess. But we already knew this information from 2 Kings, and I believe that is why Isaiah doesn’t put too much emphasis on it. He wants us to pay attention to the words being spoken here, more than the miracles or the actions. That’s what the gospels want to focus on as well. Matthew is a prime example of focusing on the words of Jesus. Isaiah is a prophet. Words are his forte. He knows that words are methodical and important, and so he wants you to think in that same sense as you read through God’s Word. It’s not just about the scenes; it’s about the heart behind those scenes. That is what God emphasizes as well."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"I the LORD search the heart, I try the reins, even to give every man according to his ways, and according to the fruit of his doings.","ref":"Jeremiah 17:10"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Create in me a clean heart, O God; and renew a right spirit within me.","ref":"Psalm 51:10"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Keep thy heart with all diligence; for out of it are the issues of life.","ref":"Proverbs 4:23"}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":9},{"start":10,"end":14},{"start":15,"end":15},{"start":16,"end":17},{"start":18,"end":18},{"start":19,"end":19},{"start":20,"end":20},{"start":21,"end":22}],"verses":{"1":"In those days was Hezekiah sick unto death. And Isaiah the prophet the son of Amoz came unto him, and said unto him, Thus saith the Lord, Set thine house in order: for thou shalt die, and not live.","2":"Then Hezekiah turned his face toward the wall, and prayed unto the Lord,","3":"And said, Remember now, O Lord, I beseech thee, how I have walked before thee in truth and with a perfect heart, and have done that which is good in thy sight. And Hezekiah wept sore.","4":"Then came the word of the Lord to Isaiah, saying,","5":"Go, and say to Hezekiah, Thus saith the Lord, the God of David thy father, I have heard thy prayer, I have seen thy tears: behold, I will add unto thy days fifteen years.","6":"And I will deliver thee and this city out of the hand of the king of Assyria: and I will defend this city.","7":"And this shall be a sign unto thee from the Lord, that the Lord will do this thing that he hath spoken;","8":"Behold, I will bring again the shadow of the degrees, which is gone down in the sun dial of Ahaz, ten degrees backward. So the sun returned ten degrees, by which degrees it was gone down.","9":"The writing of Hezekiah king of Judah, when he had been sick, and was recovered of his sickness:","10":"I said in the cutting off of my days, I shall go to the gates of the grave: I am deprived of the residue of my years.","11":"I said, I shall not see the Lord, even the Lord, in the land of the living: I shall behold man no more with the inhabitants of the world.","12":"Mine age is departed, and is removed from me as a shepherd's tent: I have cut off like a weaver my life: he will cut me off with pining sickness: from day even to night wilt thou make an end of me.","13":"I reckoned till morning, that, as a lion, so will he break all my bones: from day even to night wilt thou make an end of me.","14":"Like a crane or a swallow, so did I chatter: I did mourn as a dove: mine eyes fail with looking upward: O Lord, I am oppressed; undertake for me.","15":"What shall I say? he hath both spoken unto me, and himself hath done it: I shall go softly all my years in the bitterness of my soul.","16":"O Lord, by these things men live, and in all these things is the life of my spirit: so wilt thou recover me, and make me to live.","17":"Behold, for peace I had great bitterness: but thou hast in love to my soul delivered it from the pit of corruption: for thou hast cast all my sins behind thy back.","18":"For the grave cannot praise thee, death can not celebrate thee: they that go down into the pit cannot hope for thy truth.","19":"The living, the living, he shall praise thee, as I do this day: the father to the children shall make known thy truth.","20":"The Lord was ready to save me: therefore we will sing my songs to the stringed instruments all the days of our life in the house of the Lord.","21":"For Isaiah had said, Let them take a lump of figs, and lay it for a plaister upon the boil, and he shall recover.","22":"Hezekiah also had said, What is the sign that I shall go up to the house of the Lord?"}},
    "39": {"chapter":39,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: In our last chapter, God gives Jerusalem some alleviation from the enemy. However, in the midst of all this chaos, Hezekiah becomes deathly sick. He is told that he is going to die, but he prays to the Lord for healing and God gives him fifteen more years of life for his prayer. Sadly, those fifteen years will be a bad idea, because it's by his poor choices that will get the generations to follow into some terrible chaos and they will eventually lose everything."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is what this chapter is about. I apologize for it being short ahead of time. The chapter itself is short, but we also have already spoken about all of this in Kings and Chronicles, and it shouldn't be a surprise to us at this point. Isaiah will have to confront Hezekiah for a grave mistake he is about to make regarding the people of Babylon."}],"previously":["In our last chapter, God provides Jerusalem with some relief from the enemy. However, amidst all this chaos, Hezekiah becomes deathly ill. He is informed that he will die, but he prays to the Lord for healing, and God grants him fifteen more years of life in response to his prayer. Sadly, those fifteen years will prove to be a poor decision, as his bad choices will lead the generations that follow into terrible chaos, resulting in the eventual loss of everything. That is the focus of this chapter. I apologize in advance for its brevity. The chapter itself is short, but we have already discussed this in Kings and Chronicles, so it shouldn’t come as a surprise to us at this point. Isaiah will have to confront Hezekiah for a grave mistake he is about to make concerning the people of Babylon."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":2,"title":"Babylon's Gift","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"It’s a kind gesture, but we will see that it won’t be done out of the kindness of their heart. Perhaps we can give Merodachbaladan the benefit of the doubt. Maybe he truly did mean it as a kindness to Hezekiah. Maybe he was just showing support. Maybe he wasn’t too thrilled about Assyria either and so he wants to make an ally with Jerusalem. These could be legitimate things at the start."},{"kind":"para","text":"“Merodach” means “a rebel,” and “Baladan” means “not the Lord.” His name literally means a “rebel against the Lord.” He will not be calling on Jerusalem for safety or help. He’s using this opportunity to gain some power and control. If Assyria couldn’t do it, and Babylon succeeds at it, it will prove greater power against Assyria."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Why does Hezekiah show them this? Well, your guess is as good as mine. I’m not exactly sure why he went straight to his treasures with the people of Babylon. Perhaps he wanted to show off his riches because he was fearful of losing all of this. But that is not why the Lord saves him. In fact, I believe the Lord knew this was going to take place, but the salvation of Hezekiah was to bring glory back to God, not glory to his riches."},{"kind":"para","text":"Hezekiah misses the mark, and he does it with the enemy. He shows them everything. He shows them where everything is hiding, what the best way to get into his household would be, and how fragile his walls are. He shows them how rich and powerful the kingdom was (or once was) and how valuable everything is if anyone (cough cough) decided to try and come in and take it for themselves. He was proud of his possessions (only given to him by the Lord, mind you), and he wanted everyone else to be proud of it as well."},{"kind":"para","text":"I suppose Hezekiah thought they were friends now because they gave him a present, but he really should have just provided glory back to God and His miraculous healing."}]}]},{"start":3,"end":4,"title":"Isaiah Confronts Hezekiah","entries":[{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Isaiah has the difficult task of confronting the king with this matter. I have no doubt that Isaiah already knew who these people were and where they came from. He didn’t need to ask this question because I am assured that the Lord had already told him. Isaiah wanted to see if Hezekiah would be honest, and quite frankly, when we are asked a question about something we did wrong, it brings us new perspective. Sometimes we don’t see our flaws until someone comes to us questioning them."},{"kind":"para","text":"At this question, Hezekiah says, “They are come from a far country unto me, even from Babylon.” And then it should have clicked. A prick to the conscience should have run through his veins, and he should have thought, “Wait… Babylon has never been very friendly with us. Something is wrong here.” That doesn’t seem to be the case, though, and he doesn’t seem to think there is anything wrong with having these guests over."}]},{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Again, another question that Isaiah already knew the answer to. But Hezekiah still isn’t getting the hint… We are told in Chronicles the type of riches that Hezekiah had:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And Hezekiah had exceeding much riches and honour: and he made himself treasuries for silver, and for gold, and for precious stones, and for spices, and for shields, and for all manner of pleasant jewels; Storehouses also for the increase of corn, and wine, and oil; and stalls for all manner of beasts, and cotes for flocks.","ref":"2 Chronicles 32:27-28"},{"kind":"para","text":"Hezekiah, because of this specific instance here, will be the last wealthy king of Jerusalem. Their wealth was never actually in their materials anyway. Their wealth should have been in the Lord. That is a stark lesson for all of us reading. In the future, the wealthiest king they are going to have is Jesus Christ. But His wealth is not found here on this Earth. His wealth is in Heaven. It’s in God’s kingdom. His wealth is in having the salvation of the Lord, and that is where we find our wealth as well. The poorest among us are wealthy if we have Christ’s salvation."},{"kind":"para","text":"Hezekiah isn’t “setting his affections on things above.” Rather, he loves his material gain. I believe that is why he was so persistent in his prayer not to die. He didn’t want to leave his material possessions behind. God knows this, and so He is going to use this for the future of Jerusalem. Thankfully, God does, because we all need the example of what is more prosperous to us. Is it material wealth, or spiritual?"}]}]},{"start":5,"end":8,"title":"Good of the Lord","entries":[{"start":5,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Everything will be gone. Babylon is going to take it all. If I heard this with my own ears, I would be distressed. I would be heartbroken and ashamed. I would think, “Why did I show them everything? Why didn’t I just keep my mouth shut?” Let’s see how Hezekiah reacts to this:"}]},{"start":8,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"He thinks this prophecy is good. He might think it’s good because he likes Babylon, or he might think it’s good because Babylon can help Judah grow richer in the long run. But I don’t think he quite understands the issue here. They are going to be taken."},{"kind":"para","text":"Furthermore, he says, “Well at least it isn’t going to happen in my days. I will live in peace, and it will just be my children that have to deal with it.” I don’t know about you (perhaps you are not a father), but I worry about my child’s future. The world is not getting easier or safer. So I am constantly preparing my children to live in a world that is terribly difficult, and what they might eventually have to face up against."},{"kind":"para","text":"I don’t want them to cower down and be calloused to the people around them. I don’t want them to put their trust in riches and wealth. I want them to fight for the Lord, and I want them to be bold when they do it. I don’t think there are a lot of people who think like this. I think most people think like Hezekiah. He can make the mess, but he won’t have to worry about cleaning it up. How miserable of a generation we are if we think like this."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":8}],"verses":{"1":"At that time Merodachbaladan, the son of Baladan, king of Babylon, sent letters and a present to Hezekiah: for he had heard that he had been sick, and was recovered.","2":"And Hezekiah was glad of them, and shewed them the house of his precious things, the silver, and the gold, and the spices, and the precious ointment, and all the house of his armour, and all that was found in his treasures: there was nothing in his house, nor in all his dominion, that Hezekiah shewed them not.","3":"Then came Isaiah the prophet unto king Hezekiah, and said unto him, What said these men? and from whence came they unto thee? And Hezekiah said, They are come from a far country unto me, even from Babylon.","4":"Then said he, What have they seen in thine house? And Hezekiah answered, All that is in mine house have they seen: there is nothing among my treasures that I have not shewed them.","5":"Then said Isaiah to Hezekiah, Hear the word of the Lord of hosts:","6":"Behold, the days come, that all that is in thine house, and that which thy fathers have laid up in store until this day, shall be carried to Babylon: nothing shall be left, saith the Lord.","7":"And of thy sons that shall issue from thee, which thou shalt beget, shall they take away; and they shall be eunuchs in the palace of the king of Babylon.","8":"Then said Hezekiah to Isaiah, Good is the word of the Lord which thou hast spoken. He said moreover, For there shall be peace and truth in my days."}},
    "40": {"chapter":40,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: In our last chapter, Hezekiah gave too much information to the people of Babylon, and because of it, the city of Jerusalem is going to be taken into captivity. If he had just kept quiet about it, I think they would have been relatively safe for a time longer. At least the downfall of Jerusalem wouldn't have been on the shoulders of Hezekiah (though he doesn't seem to care because he knows it will not be in his lifetime that he will have to deal with it)."},{"kind":"para","text":"In this chapter, Isaiah calls the people to comfort each other. This is an important chapter for Israel (of course), and it's going to be something that needs to take place when the captivity comes. However, it is an extremely needed ministry in our world today (one that is extremely lacking). May we apply this chapter to our own lives as we read, and find reason to comfort the saints around us while we have the opportunity to do so."}],"previously":["In our last chapter, Hezekiah gave too much information to the people of Babylon, and because of it, the city of Jerusalem is going to be taken into captivity. If he had just kept quiet about it, I think they would have been relatively safe for a time longer. At least the downfall of Jerusalem wouldn’t have been on the shoulders of Hezekiah (though he doesn’t seem to care because he knows it will not be in his lifetime that he will have to deal with it). In this chapter, Isaiah calls the people to comfort each other. This is an important chapter for Israel (of course), and it’s going to be something that needs to take place when the captivity comes. However, it is an extremely needed ministry in our world today (one that is extremely lacking). May we apply this chapter to our own lives as we read, and find reason to comfort the saints around us while we have the opportunity to do so."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":2,"title":"A Call For Comfort","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"In our last chapter, we saw that Hezekiah doesn’t care about the future of Jerusalem. He only cares that he personally won’t have to deal with it. That is the problem with most leaders today, if I can be honest. Even leaders in the church don’t seem to think about the future of their congregation. They just care about what they are setting up for right now. They want to make sure that their own needs are taken care of at the very least."},{"kind":"para","text":"God says, “Comfort my people.” Isaiah says, “Saith YOUR God.” It’s not just his God. It’s the land’s God. It’s the saved God. It’s the one that created you, loves you, and gave His life for you to have a home and His presence in eternity. That’s a comfort to God’s people. Sadly, I see a lot more dysfunction happening in the church than I see unity or comfort. A lot of people feel bitter entering the church house. Not because the truth is not being preached behind the pulpit. I think there are a lot of great preachers out there. Rather, it’s because the person preaching the message won’t provide you with comfort. They won’t care."},{"kind":"para","text":"We should be comforting and encouraging every saint in the Lord. If we are very choosy and selective of who gets our time, and for what reason, then we are just playing a part, not acting in genuine faith and compassion. I, for one, am growing quite weary of phony Christians acting like they care, only to leave me high and dry the moment I truly need help. Too many people are being left without comfort in the church. They will say, “The Holy Spirit will comfort you, if you don’t have comfort you must not know Christ.”"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But the Comforter, which is the Holy Ghost, whom the Father will send in my name, he shall teach you all things, and bring all things to your remembrance, whatsoever I have said unto you.","ref":"John 14:26"},{"kind":"para","text":"But they seem to miss all the times that the Lord tells His people to comfort each other."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Look not every man on his own things, but every man also on the things of others.","ref":"Philippians 2:4"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But whoso hath this world's good, and seeth his brother have need, and shutteth up his bowels of compassion from him, how dwelleth the love of God in him?","ref":"1 John 3:17"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Bear ye one another's burdens, and so fulfil the law of Christ.","ref":"Galatians 6:2"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"This is my commandment, That ye love one another, as I have loved you.","ref":"John 15:12"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Wherefore comfort one another with these words.","ref":"1 Thessalonians 4:18"},{"kind":"para","text":"Sadly, you are not going to find many comforting voices in this world today. Obviously it was a problem during the days of Isaiah as well, or else he wouldn't have to say this."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"You know why Jerusalem is going to face such a big problem? You know why they need comforting? Because they are sinners. It’s the same reason you and I need comforting today as well. We are sinners. However, we have a pardon from the Lord. Jesus Christ pardoned us by paying our sin debt on the cross."},{"kind":"para","text":"Of course, you and I know that we don’t just stop sinning because the Lord paid our fine. Except, now we have an advocate with the Father, which is Jesus Christ."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"My little children, these things write I unto you, that ye sin not. And if any man sin, we have an advocate with the Father, Jesus Christ the righteous: And he is the propitiation for our sins: and not for ours only, but also for the sins of the whole world.","ref":"1 John 2:1-2"},{"kind":"para","text":"Obviously, that doesn’t give us a right to sin, but when we make mistakes, the “pardon” we spoke about gives us a way for God to work on us. You can bet any money that if God has purchased you, He is going to mold you for the rest of your life. That is something to be comforted by. It’s a comfort to the Christian to know that God is not going to just give up on you because you made a mistake. He is not going to forsake you or bring down His wrath because of your sin. His wrath is saved for the unrighteous, not for those who are being worked on. His love comes down on His own, and that might look like scolding, shaping, and molding. You will be chastised for iniquity. Those who don’t have the Lord will not receive chastisement; they will receive judgment and wrath. That’s the difference."}]}]},{"start":3,"end":5,"title":"Everything Changes For the Lord","entries":[{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"It seems that this prophecy is about John the Baptist according to the gospels. It’s still on theme though. Those words “Prepare ye the way of the Lord, make straight in the desert a highway for our God” were supposed to be comforting to the hearers. It’s a cry for comfort to the people. It’s comfort because the Savior has come and has made access to His salvation. That is where ultimate comfort truly does come from."},{"kind":"para","text":"However, we should still be people of great comfort to the saved. When we speak, and we are more comforting to the lost than we are to the saved, we have our priorities mixed up. Honestly, I could argue that you are preaching a false message if you are not able to comfort those that know the Lord."}]},{"start":4,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"When the Lord saves, everything is flipped over. The deepest pits become the highest mountains, and the highest mountains become the deepest pits. Everything that is crooked will be made straight, and suddenly your ground is easier to walk along (it’s not so rough anymore). The entire world will see the Lord’s work. There will just be some that deny it to the very end, sadly."},{"kind":"para","text":"Why would they deny it? Well, they just don’t want to believe. Even if all the evidence was smacking them in the face over and over again, they will reject the obvious signs of truth right in front of them."}]}]},{"start":6,"end":8,"title":"Comfort From The Lord","entries":[{"start":6,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This should sound familiar to us:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For all flesh is as grass, and all the glory of man as the flower of grass. The grass withereth, and the flower thereof falleth away:","ref":"1 Peter 1:24"},{"kind":"para","text":"Obviously, Peter got some inspiration from the Holy Ghost to quote such a fine verse: “We are like grass.” Is that comforting to you? Does being grass bring you comfort? Does knowing that grass just fades away help you to continue forward? The emphasis is placed on the wrong part of these verses. We are like grass, yes, but God’s Word is not. His Word stands forever. It doesn’t fade away like we do. That is why we must hold onto His Word. Our roots must be dug into God’s Word if we are going to be strongly planted. We might not be strong, but we can place any bet on the Lord to give strength and to BE our strength. We don’t last forever, but the Lord does! It’s a place we can go to when we are needing asylum."},{"kind":"para","text":"Perhaps, today, you feel quite hurt and weary. Maybe you are going through something that you just can’t gain any comfort in. Maybe the church has forsaken you, or your job, or your family, or your friends… Whatever it is, God’s Word can be your comforting place. Just stay there for a season. Stay there and hide away. Push the rest to the side and find comfort from the Lord. Sometimes that is the only place you will find comfort in this world. I’m sure Isaiah wanted comfort as well, but he never got it from the people around him. He only found his comfort from the Lord."}]}]},{"start":9,"end":11,"title":"The Gathering of the Lord","entries":[{"start":9,"end":9,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The gospel is a powerful tool. It brings comfort to those who are seeking it, but it also brings comfort to the preacher. I find no greater comfort in this life than to teach the Bible to others. It reminds me of what I need to hold close to in my times of trouble and pain. To have that taken away from me is quite catastrophic. I would have no choice but to shout from the tops of the mountains!"}]},{"start":10,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Jesus came the first time with a strong hand. His reward was with Him, and salvation is His reward. His work was before Him, and He is still working on us today."},{"kind":"para","text":"Again, this is a three-fold prophecy. It’s about their return to the land, but it’s also about the first coming of Christ. Then it’s about His second coming as well. We are still a work that is before Him."}]},{"start":11,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"We’ve talked extensively before about how terrible of a person you would have to be to mistreat a pregnant woman. You would have to be downright evil to try and hurt someone with a baby. Yet, most of the world seems to hurt those specific people. To be pregnant today is a scary thing. The only thing they want from you at the hospital is to abort the child. They don’t care how long you’ve waited to have a kid; they just want to offer abortion and try to sway you into it. If you don’t take it, they make everything difficult on you until the baby is born."},{"kind":"para","text":"That’s not how the Lord leads, though. He feeds His flock, and He gathers His lambs, even carrying them. He leads the pregnant gently. He doesn’t try to scare them off or pawn them onto a different shepherd. He loves His own more than He loves anything else. He has a deep and honest love for you if you know Him personally. He would go to the ends of the Earth for you. In fact, He truly has."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For the Son of man is come to seek and to save that which was lost.","ref":"Luke 19:10"}]}]},{"start":12,"end":17,"title":"Directing God","entries":[{"start":12,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"According to Google, the ocean weighs 1.4 x 10^18 metric tons. What does that mean? I still don’t know. With all this technology, we can’t measure the water’s weight. Isaiah says, “Who has measured it in the hollow of their hands?” No one. Except the Lord. God knows the weight of mountains and the balance of hills. He knows the weight of all the dust on Earth, and it’s not just a guess of measurement. He knows exactly how much it all weighs, just by holding it in His hand. That’s quite astounding to me. No one else might think that’s amazing, but I certainly do."}]},{"start":13,"end":13,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Good question! If we could teach God or lead God, we would be God. He can’t be taught by any other because He is all-knowing. It’s an important reminder, by the way. We don’t tell God what to do; God tells us what to do. There are some prayers today who think they can direct the Lord in whatever direction they intend, but that is not up to humankind."},{"kind":"para","text":"When we pray, we are not directing anything for the Lord. We pray because we are asking the Lord for something, not because we are demanding it. If we demand anything from the Lord, I am assured that God will not answer you."}]},{"start":14,"end":14,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Whoever that was would be God. However, God doesn’t need to be taught anything; He needs to teach us. That’s why there is such a strong emphasis in scripture about teaching appropriately. A lot of teachers today think they need to teach God, rather than the other way around. They say, “No, this is what God means by saying this,” rather than, “No, this is what God says.” Take His Word as absolute, not as symbolic."},{"kind":"para","text":"Some might argue with me about Revelation and prophecies, but I would bet any money that the prophecies can be taken literally too. In fact, we have seen that to be true with Isaiah already, but we will also see it to be true in the future of Israel (and the world) as well. God teaches us; it’s not the other way around. Some of us should first learn to listen to God before doing any sort of teaching for the Lord."}]},{"start":15,"end":15,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Here’s a comfort: everything is little in the hands of the Lord. He is able to count, comfort, and direct everything right from the palm of His hand. Honestly, that is the only reason (I personally believe) that we are not hurling towards the sun and impending doom. The only way we will be destroyed is through His directive and choice."}]},{"start":16,"end":16,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"You can sacrifice the entire world to the Lord, and it still wouldn’t be enough for His majesty and glory. This particular verse would be considered blasphemy by many modern religionists today (or even back then). However, that was not what God wanted. He didn’t want sacrifice for the sake of sacrifice. He wanted obedience. He wanted His people to listen. That is still what He wants today, to be honest."},{"kind":"para","text":"We think we will earn favor with the Lord by simply doing. We won’t. In fact, if we neglect comforting people because we are too busy with the Lord’s work, we are going directly against His Word and command for us. How sad and miserable we are to reject the need for comfort to God’s people…"}]},{"start":17,"end":17,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Does God not care about the nations? Does He not care about the millions of innocent people? That’s not what Isaiah is saying here. He is saying that the things they could offer are literally nothing to Him. He doesn’t need your offerings. He doesn’t need your money, or your sacrifices. He needs your obedience and ear. He wants you to hear Him and do what He has instructed."},{"kind":"para","text":"However, we want to see something tangible, and so we ignore His Words to try and do His Work, and that never actually amounts to anything pleasing to the Lord. The Lord is disgusted by works without heart."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And Samuel said, Hath the LORD as great delight in burnt offerings and sacrifices, as in obeying the voice of the LORD? Behold, to obey is better than sacrifice, and to hearken than the fat of rams.","ref":"1 Samuel 15:22"}]}]},{"start":18,"end":26,"title":"Comparing God","entries":[{"start":18,"end":18,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Good question. If I asked some of the greatest preachers to give me a worldly example to explain God, you know what great thing they would compare the Lord to? An egg. They would compare God to an egg. Some might compare Him to a fire. Even that pales in comparison. Don’t get me wrong, I think the egg analogy is fine. Three parts to one egg. But I feel like we could do better than that."},{"kind":"para","text":"Than again, Jesus Himself didn’t compare the Lord to anything particularly grand. He compared God to bread, a vine, a door, a light, a path, a shepherd… These are not all that glorious in our eyes of the world. When someone asks me, I usually point back to His name. He is God. You need all three characters in that name to make up the name. God without G is just od. God without O is just Gd. God without D is just Go. It won’t work unless you have all three characters together. They (together) make His name. Even that truly pales in comparison to who He actually is."},{"kind":"para","text":"Isaiah makes a strong point here. He compared the Lord to a shepherd a moment ago. That doesn’t even measure up to God’s goodness and comfort."}]},{"start":19,"end":20,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"We try to place so much value into our idols on this Earth. We use some of the most expensive materials to make our graven images. You know what? That still doesn’t compare to the value of the Lord. We cannot find anything here on this Earth that measures up to God’s amazing glory."}]},{"start":21,"end":23,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Atheists might claim they don’t know or haven’t heard, but they do. They just deny and reject the stories they’ve been told. They know there is a God; they just don’t want to acknowledge Him. They surely understand, but they choose to be ignorant. They can’t deny the obvious proofs of God’s creation and continual saving of this world."},{"kind":"para","text":"They say, “If God is good, why doesn’t He get rid of evil?” Then when God does get rid of evil, they say, “How could a loving God do such a thing?” They don’t understand how justice and righteousness work. They want God to do it their way. They want God to judge who they want to judge and save who they want to save. They want to be in the place of God. I’m thankful they aren’t. I would not be worthy enough to be saved by them. Honestly, they would probably hate me for who I am."},{"kind":"para","text":"God is able to make righteous choices and judgments. We might not understand why He chooses the people He does, but we can rest assured that He has a good reason for choosing them. If it were me, everyone would be destined for Hell because everyone here is terribly evil. Yes, that includes my wife and children. Imagine if I had that power and I sent them directly to Hell because they did something that truly upset me. What a terrible judge I am…"}]},{"start":24,"end":24,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Because they are not rooted in God’s Word, they may falter. Remember, it’s God’s Word that will stand the tests of time. We won’t, but if we are planted in His Word, His Word will shield us."}]},{"start":25,"end":25,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The kings of this Earth don’t even compare to the sovereign ruling of the Lord. Nothing here can compare. There is nothing equal to Him. Not even the holiest person on this Earth can compare to the Lord. We can’t even point to the most valuable things, like gold and jewels, to compare the Lord to."}]},{"start":26,"end":26,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There are over eight billion people on this planet, and God knows your name. He knows every single person individually. Whether you want to know Him or not, He knows everything about you. He even has the number of hairs counted on your head. That should bring you great comfort. Unless you don’t know Him. If you don’t know Him, you should be worried about how much He knows about you."}]}]},{"start":27,"end":31,"title":"God Is There","entries":[{"start":27,"end":27,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"He is speaking to Jacob and to Israel. It is argued that Jacob represents the worldly man, while Israel symbolizes the saved one. Perhaps that is how God is viewing this situation at the moment. He is addressing both the saved and the unsaved, as they both face the same question: “Why do you say God’s way is hidden from you, and God is not judging properly?”"},{"kind":"para","text":"The saved and the unsaved struggle with the same dilemma. God doesn’t seem to be doing what we want. The truth is, God hardly ever does what we want. However, He always does what He wants. He has a plan and purpose for every move He makes, and He is going to work and do what is best for all of humanity and all of eternity. Thank God He does. Otherwise, as I’ve said before, no one would be saved."}]},{"start":28,"end":28,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"When it seems as if the world is getting away with evil, and the Lord is remaining silent, you can rest assured that God is doing something from His throne. He is willing and ready to save and rescue. He is usually waiting for something, though, and nine times out of ten, it’s for His children to turn to Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"The reason we are in so much turmoil today, quite frankly, is only because we have turned away from the Lord. He gets His children’s attention the best when we realize that what we wanted actually wasn’t good for us. He doesn’t faint, though. He is there, and He is not tired of His ruling. He hasn’t given up on us (though I wouldn’t blame Him if He did). He loves us too much to just give up on us."}]},{"start":29,"end":29,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"He doesn’t faint; He gives power to the faint. He is not weak; He gives strength to the weak. God gives to those who need it and those who turn to Him for help. He wants to help you prosper. He wants to give you courage and strength in times when you need it the most."},{"kind":"para","text":"He wants you to turn to Him first, though, and that requires us to put our guards down and get on our knees in a mode of trust and worship. We must give up ourselves if we want to gain the Lord."}]},{"start":30,"end":31,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"If young people are weary, there is a problem. I think we are living in an age (in America) where young people have never been more tired. They are tired of the lies, the hypocrisy, the disunity, and the lack of communication. They are tired of running and helping, and they are tired of trying to figure out the right things on their own. They are tired, and we haven’t helped comfort them at all. Those who are older only look out for themselves today. We are not helping our young people, and because of it, they are faint and weary."},{"kind":"para","text":"When we have the Lord in our lives, it should motivate us to help those around us (no matter their age, gender, or color). We should be helping to strengthen our brothers in the Lord and giving them footing to “renew their strength… mount up with wings… run… and walk…” These are things that we are able to grow in, every one of us. And when we have a community (like a church), we should be helping others do the same. That is what a comforting church does. They help the congregation renew their strength."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Create in me a clean heart, O God; and renew a right spirit within me.","ref":"Psalm 51:10"},{"kind":"para","text":"They help their brothers in Christ mount up with wings:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Ye have seen what I did unto the Egyptians, and how I bare you on eagles' wings, and brought you unto myself.","ref":"Exodus 19:4"},{"kind":"para","text":"They help others continue their run:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Know ye not that they which run in a race run all, but one receiveth the prize? So run, that ye may obtain.","ref":"1 Corinthians 9:24"},{"kind":"para","text":"They help the faint get up and walk:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"I therefore, the prisoner of the Lord, beseech you that ye walk worthy of the vocation wherewith ye are called, With all lowliness and meekness, with longsuffering, forbearing one another in love; Endeavouring to keep the unity of the Spirit in the bond of peace.","ref":"Ephesians 4:1-3"},{"kind":"para","text":"Is this what we are doing for our community? Are we helping them grow in these areas of faith? If we aren't, we must beginning this journey starting today."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":9},{"start":10,"end":10},{"start":11,"end":11},{"start":12,"end":12},{"start":13,"end":13},{"start":14,"end":14},{"start":15,"end":15},{"start":16,"end":16},{"start":17,"end":17},{"start":18,"end":18},{"start":19,"end":20},{"start":21,"end":23},{"start":24,"end":24},{"start":25,"end":25},{"start":26,"end":26},{"start":27,"end":27},{"start":28,"end":28},{"start":29,"end":29},{"start":30,"end":31}],"verses":{"1":"Comfort ye, comfort ye my people, saith your God.","2":"Speak ye comfortably to Jerusalem, and cry unto her, that her warfare is accomplished, that her iniquity is pardoned: for she hath received of the Lord’s hand double for all her sins.","3":"The voice of him that crieth in the wilderness, Prepare ye the way of the Lord, make straight in the desert a highway for our God.","4":"Every valley shall be exalted, and every mountain and hill shall be made low: and the crooked shall be made straight, and the rough places plain:","5":"And the glory of the Lord shall be revealed, and all flesh shall see it together: for the mouth of the Lord hath spoken it.","6":"The voice said, Cry. And he said, What shall I cry? All flesh is grass, and all the goodliness thereof is as the flower of the field:","7":"The grass withereth, the flower fadeth: because the spirit of the Lord bloweth upon it: surely the people is grass.","8":"The grass withereth, the flower fadeth: but the word of our God shall stand for ever.","9":"O Zion, that bringest good tidings, get thee up into the high mountain; O Jerusalem, that bringest good tidings, lift up thy voice with strength; lift it up, be not afraid; say unto the cities of Judah, Behold your God!","10":"Behold, the Lord God will come with strong hand, and his arm shall rule for him: behold, his reward is with him, and his work before him.","11":"He shall feed his flock like a shepherd: he shall gather the lambs with his arm, and carry them in his bosom, and shall gently lead those that are with young.","12":"Who hath measured the waters in the hollow of his hand, and meted out heaven with the span, and comprehended the dust of the earth in a measure, and weighed the mountains in scales, and the hills in a balance?","13":"Who hath directed the Spirit of the Lord, or being his counsellor hath taught him?","14":"With whom took he counsel, and who instructed him, and taught him in the path of judgment, and taught him knowledge, and shewed to him the way of understanding?","15":"Behold, the nations are as a drop of a bucket, and are counted as the small dust of the balance: behold, he taketh up the isles as a very little thing.","16":"And Lebanon is not sufficient to burn, nor the beasts thereof sufficient for a burnt offering.","17":"All nations before him are as nothing; and they are counted to him less than nothing, and vanity.","18":"To whom then will ye liken God? or what likeness will ye compare unto him?","19":"The workman melteth a graven image, and the goldsmith spreadeth it over with gold, and casteth silver chains.","20":"He that is so impoverished that he hath no oblation chooseth a tree that will not rot; he seeketh unto him a cunning workman to prepare a graven image, that shall not be moved.","21":"Have ye not known? have ye not heard? hath it not been told you from the beginning? have ye not understood from the foundations of the earth?","22":"It is he that sitteth upon the circle of the earth, and the inhabitants thereof are as grasshoppers; that stretcheth out the heavens as a curtain, and spreadeth them out as a tent to dwell in:","23":"That bringeth the princes to nothing; he maketh the judges of the earth as vanity.","24":"Yea, they shall not be planted; yea, they shall not be sown: yea, their stock shall not take root in the earth: and he shall also blow upon them, and they shall wither, and the whirlwind shall take them away as stubble.","25":"To whom then will ye liken me, or shall I be equal? saith the Holy One.","26":"Lift up your eyes on high, and behold who hath created these things, that bringeth out their host by number: he calleth them all by names by the greatness of his might, for that he is strong in power; not one faileth.","27":"Why sayest thou, O Jacob, and speakest, O Israel, My way is hid from the Lord, and my judgment is passed over from my God?","28":"Hast thou not known? hast thou not heard, that the everlasting God, the Lord, the Creator of the ends of the earth, fainteth not, neither is weary? there is no searching of his understanding.","29":"He giveth power to the faint; and to them that have no might he increaseth strength.","30":"Even the youths shall faint and be weary, and the young men shall utterly fall:","31":"But they that wait upon the Lord shall renew their strength; they shall mount up with wings as eagles; they shall run, and not be weary; and they shall walk, and not faint."}},
    "41": {"chapter":41,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: I think it's sufficient to say that the last chapter was more about who God is. It really highlighted the importance of comforting everyone with the fact that God is on the throne, and He is the one that dictates and controls this Earth. He can bless and guide, and He (alone) can judge and turn away. That's what makes God so mighty and great. He has the power to do it, and He has the right."},{"kind":"para","text":"In this chapter, it is less about who God is, and more about what He does. He provides for mankind, but He meets with people individually to do it. We might all be blessed by one man's blessing from the Lord, but the real blessed one is the one in which God bestows the blessing upon. God WILL prove Himself to anyone that asks and desires to genuinely know Him."}],"previously":["I think it’s sufficient to say that the last chapter was more about who God is. It really highlighted the importance of comforting everyone with the fact that God is on the throne, and He is the one that dictates and controls this Earth. He can bless and guide, and He (alone) can judge and turn away. That’s what makes God so mighty and great. He has the power to do it, and He has the right. In this chapter, it is less about who God is, and more about what He does. He provides for mankind, but He meets with people individually to do it. We might all be blessed by one man’s blessing from the Lord, but the real blessed one is the one in which God bestows the blessing upon. God WILL prove Himself to anyone that asks and desires to genuinely know Him."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":7,"title":"The Righteous","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Honestly, there should be nothing that keeps humankind from coming closer to the Lord. God has given us a place of renewal and rest right here on Earth."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Come unto me, all ye that labour and are heavy laden, and I will give you rest.","ref":"Matthew 11:28"},{"kind":"para","text":"Judgement is a scary word for most people. I hear a lot of this world say, “You can’t judge me.” Yet, those same people judge everyone else all the time. Judgement is a good thing. There are literally series of shows based on only judging. Judging food, clothes, hair, tattoos, cake, singing, dancing, and judging talent of any kind. We consume those shows up, but can’t handle when someone judges us on those same things."},{"kind":"para","text":"Furthermore, we can’t handle when a godly man judges us about our ungodly deeds. Yet, that is how God will judge us whether we like it or not. I’d rather receive a bad judgement here on Earth and change than to receive a bad judgement from the Lord and have no more time to change. That is where all of mankind is heading. The point of this life is to get ready for that day of judgement. You are either being prepared for it now, or you are going to be terrified when the day comes."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"In the day of Isaiah, there was not much “righteousness” going on. Perhaps Isaiah was one of the few, but that’s about it. We had minor prophets and a few others that could be added to the list, but they all had their flaws, including Isaiah. They were righteous, however, by the Lord’s judgment."},{"kind":"para","text":"But there is a man who deserves the nations and to rule over kings, and it’s no one on this Earth. Jesus Christ is the only ruler of kings who is worthy to be called a “righteous man.”"}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"True, lasting safety belongs to the Lord. I have noticed that many commentators reference these verses to Cyrus of Babylon. Others reference Abraham as the one Isaiah is speaking about. Perhaps he is, I don’t know. But I think this easily references Christ. He is a righteous man, and He rules over the kings. He passed safely (at least until it was time for Him to sacrifice Himself). Interestingly enough, He still passes safely by ways He has not gone with His feet. He uses OUR feet to pass around this world today. We are His messengers. We are not messengers for Abraham. We are not messengers for Cyrus either. Perhaps the next verse can make it clearer."}]},{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Obviously, God has proven Himself over and over again to these nations, specifically to the people of Israel. They could rest assured that He did it once before, and He certainly can do it all again. The part that strikes me is that He calls Himself “the first” and then refers to Himself as “WITH the last…”"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"I am Alpha and Omega, the beginning and the end, the first and the last.","ref":"Revelation 22:13"},{"kind":"para","text":"This is another one of those verses that proves the Godhead. Jesus is the first and the last, but God is the first, and Jesus is the last. So He is the last as well, but He is also with the last. If that is not a direct reference to Jesus, I don’t know what is."}]},{"start":5,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"We will all be judged by the Lord. Those that belong to the Lord, and those that don’t, will receive judgment from God. They will not, however, receive the same judgment. Those that don’t have the Lord certainly have a reason to worry about the coming judgment of God. Those with the Lord know the judgment is coming and can easily say, “Be of good courage.” Judgment, to the Christian, is a good thing, both here and in eternity."},{"kind":"para","text":"A Christian that says they don’t want to be judged is fooling themselves. They are hiding something. They don’t want to be judged because they don’t want to fix whatever they have wrong with them. God will judge that, though. Again, I’d rather have my judgment on this Earth to fix it than wait for eternity and never have a chance to right my wrongs."}]},{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is how they made idols back then. They would create something to suit their current needs, thinking that the thing they just made up for their temporary cause was something to be worshiped. Really, they were just worshiping themselves. This is what they wanted the real God to be like. Perhaps they made an idol that would bless them with children. Someone might have said, “You know, I couldn’t have kids once before, but I made this idol, and it worked for me! You should try it!” And this poor Israelite man did, and you know what? It worked for him! Now he puts his trust in this made-up god and casually turns away from putting the true God in first place."},{"kind":"para","text":"God is not going to be happy with that man. God will certainly judge that man. That man will literally live in judgment from the Lord. Honestly, serving other gods is not even the real issue. The real issue is forsaking the true God of the universe. When we serve other gods, we completely forsake the Creator and start to turn everything we serve into sin. We start serving ourselves more than others, and that is something that God is not happy with. In fact, we start to inflict damage on others by serving idols."}]}]},{"start":8,"end":16,"title":"The Enemies End","entries":[{"start":8,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God has a chosen people, who (at the moment) are not acting like chosen people. They are acting like the rest of the world. Because of this, God is going to give them over to their desires and to their enemies. They want to live like the enemy; they can live WITH the enemy. It’s not all that it’s cracked up to be. Until the chosen lineage turns back, there will be no blessing or prosperity in God’s land."}]},{"start":9,"end":9,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The Israelites were not “taken from the ends of the earth.” When we pick up the story of these people from Genesis, we see that they stay relatively central to this land. They never go to any other countries to live. From Genesis to Revelation, they remain very local to the land of Canaan. Therefore, God is speaking about a broader lineage. It’s whomever He chooses."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But ye are a chosen generation, a royal priesthood, an holy nation, a peculiar people; that ye should shew forth the praises of him who hath called you out of darkness into his marvellous light:","ref":"1 Peter 2:9"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Ye have not chosen me, but I have chosen you, and ordained you, that ye should go and bring forth fruit, and that your fruit should remain: that whatsoever ye shall ask of the Father in my name, he may give it you.","ref":"John 15:16"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Whereunto he called you by our gospel, to the obtaining of the glory of our Lord Jesus Christ.","ref":"2 Thessalonians 2:14"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"I have said, Ye are gods; and all of you are children of the most High.","ref":"Psalm 82:6"},{"kind":"para","text":"God has chosen a people. Throughout all of scripture, God has left that choice open-ended. There have been people (several times through scripture) who were included in the chosen lineage that were not Israelites. Obviously, the children of Jacob have a few family members outside the royal lineage."},{"kind":"para","text":"But if we just look at the children of Judah (which leads to Christ and that is really who Isaiah is focusing on here), we can see there are quite a few women in particular who don’t belong in that “chosen” lineage."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Abraham begat Isaac; and Isaac begat Jacob; and Jacob begat Judas and his brethren; And Judas begat Phares and Zara of Thamar; and Phares begat Esrom; and Esrom begat Aram; And Aram begat Aminadab; and Aminadab begat Naasson; and Naasson begat Salmon; And Salmon begat Boaz of Rachab; and Boaz begat Obed of Ruth; and Obed begat Jesse; And Jesse begat David the king; and David the king begat Solomon of her that had been the wife of Urias; And Solomon begat Roboam; and Roboam begat Abia; and Abia begat Asa; And Asa begat Josaphat; and Josaphat begat Joram; and Joram begat Ozias; And Ozias begat Joatham; and Joatham begat Achaz; and Achaz begat Ezekias; And Ezekias begat Manasses; and Manasses begat Amon; and Amon begat Josias; And Josias begat Jechonias and his brethren, about the time they were carried away to Babylon: And after they were brought to Babylon, Jechonias begat Salathiel; and Salathiel begat Zorobabel; And Zorobabel begat Abiud; and Abiud begat Eliakim; and Eliakim begat Azor; And Azor begat Sadoc; and Sadoc begat Achim; and Achim begat Eliud; And Eliud begat Eleazar; and Eleazar begat Matthan; and Matthan begat Jacob; And Jacob begat Joseph the husband of Mary, of whom was born Jesus, who is called Christ.","ref":"Matthew 1:2-16"},{"kind":"para","text":"Now, obviously, this mostly showcases the men in the lineage. However, some of these men came to be through terrible circumstances, and they were not Israelites. Starting with Judah, who did some terrible things to have children, I won’t speak too deeply about that here (we can look at that in Genesis)."},{"kind":"para","text":"We have Boaz and Rahab (or Rahab). Rahab was a harlot from Jericho. Following them is Obed of Ruth. Ruth was a Moabitess. Obviously, if there is a woman referenced in the lineage, it’s likely because they didn’t belong in the chosen lineage. Yet, the Lord chose these two."},{"kind":"para","text":"Time permits me to speak about Bathsheba (who was an Israelite) who marries David in an unholy way, or about some of the people who come after Solomon who were not very righteous men. Then we have the Gentiles who were saved in the book of Acts, and the people all around the world today who continuously call upon the name of the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"We didn’t talk about some of these other characters who were called by the Lord out of nowhere, like Melchizedek, who just appears suddenly and then never shows back up again (until the book of Hebrews). It is evident that God has left the door of salvation wide open for anyone willing to come to Him and turn from their idols and sins."},{"kind":"para","text":"That’s the part that holds us back, though. We don’t want to give up what we hold so tightly to, to hold onto the Lord."}]},{"start":10,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"What a popular verse. For good reason, too. I wrote a three hundred and sixty-five-day devotional on the topic of biblical fear. There are two types of fear in this world: the fear of man and the fear of God."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And fear not them which kill the body, but are not able to kill the soul: but rather fear him which is able to destroy both soul and body in hell.","ref":"Matthew 10:28"},{"kind":"para","text":"Those who have the Lord have no reason to fear His judgment. We have a reason to fear not having Him, though. We would be wise to ensure we do not end up in Hell if we believe there is justice for the evil in this world. I think everyone wants to see justice served. Sadly, all of those same people would end up on the wrong side of justice because they don’t realize how evil and wayward they are."},{"kind":"para","text":"But if the Lord is with you, you have nothing to fear. He will give us strength; He will hold us up with His own righteousness. We don’t have to muster up anything (as if we could) when He comes to this Earth."}]},{"start":11,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Obviously, this can apply to you as well, but not over petty, meaningless fights you might have with your neighbor. As much as I’d like to see God hurt and break the teeth of those who have made my life difficult, I much rather they just know the Lord and turn from their wickedness right now. Evil people will get what they deserve in the end, and that’s all fine and well, but it won’t be without Christians warning them first."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But I say unto you, Love your enemies, bless them that curse you, do good to them that hate you, and pray for them which despitefully use you, and persecute you;","ref":"Matthew 5:44"},{"kind":"para","text":"The best way to love an enemy is to pray for their soul."}]},{"start":13,"end":13,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"He is not going to just tell you to be comforted. He will actually hold your hand through the trial. He will literally and physically help you. That is His promise. He doesn’t just let you deal with the burden on your own. He shoulders the burden with you."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Casting all your care upon him; for he careth for you.","ref":"1 Peter 5:7"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Cast thy burden upon the LORD, and he shall sustain thee: he shall never suffer the righteous to be moved.","ref":"Psalm 55:22"},{"kind":"para","text":"You will carry it with His help. That is what the church should be doing for the believers by the way. The church is supposed to be a community of burden bearers."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Bear ye one another's burdens, and so fulfil the law of Christ.","ref":"Galatians 6:2"},{"kind":"para","text":"I still have yet to find a church that would be willing to do this with it's congregants."}]},{"start":14,"end":14,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"We are just worms in the grand scheme of things. I don’t amount to much really. But I am one valuable worm if God is going through the trouble to protect and save me with His own life. When we have the Lord, we are no longer just worms squirming for forgiveness. No, we are a new creature, and we become His valuable sheep. I’d rather be a sheep than a worm. I suppose either way, I would be chosen. But to be fish bait is not exactly the way in which I would hope my life would be spent. Though we are called to be “fishers of men,” I don’t think being bait was exactly the plan that Jesus had in mind. We are supposed to hold the fishing pole, not the one being eaten by the fish."}]},{"start":15,"end":15,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"What an interesting thing for a fish to do. I don’t see many farmers going out with sharp-toothed fish and reaping their fields. Obviously, this is deeper than just a word picture. We are given a symbol here. We become useful tools for the Lord’s work of reaping. We are going to tear down and uproot what is evil, and we only have to do that through our words. We don’t have to literally beat the gospel into people. If we give the gospel without motive, the Holy Spirit will do the stabbing for you."}]},{"start":16,"end":16,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The enemy will just be chased by the wind when we stand in the strength of the Lord. That is fantastic news for us. God will carry the enemy away, rather than the enemy carrying the people of God away. That will only happen if we are righteous before the Lord, though. We must have faith and a relationship with Him if we want to be on the side of victory."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Devil tries to trick you into thinking that this world is worth giving up God over, but it’s not. Nothing here will last."}]}]},{"start":17,"end":20,"title":"The God Of Impossibility","entries":[{"start":17,"end":17,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The Israelites were tasked with taking care of the poor:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"He that hath pity upon the poor lendeth unto the LORD; and that which he hath given will he pay him again.","ref":"Proverbs 19:17"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"If there be among you a poor man of one of thy brethren within any of thy gates in thy land which the LORD thy God giveth thee, thou shalt not harden thine heart, nor shut thine hand from thy poor brother:","ref":"Deuteronomy 15:7"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For the poor shall never cease out of the land: therefore I command thee, saying, Thou shalt open thine hand wide unto thy brother, to thy poor, and to thy needy, in thy land.","ref":"Deuteronomy 15:11"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Only they would that we should remember the poor; the same which I also was forward to do.","ref":"Galatians 2:10"},{"kind":"para","text":"They neglected the poor, and so do we today, but God will not neglect them. A righteous poor man will be taken care of. God will not forsake His own. It makes no difference to Him if you are rich or poor. He loves His own children."},{"kind":"para","text":"While the church might forsake you, the Lord will not. While the world might forsake you, the Lord will not. While your family might forsake you, the Lord will not. While your friends might forsake you, the Lord will not. Your job, your passions, your abilities, your circumstances may all forsake you, but the Lord would never do it if you belong to Him!"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Let your conversation be without covetousness; and be content with such things as ye have: for he hath said, I will never leave thee, nor forsake thee.","ref":"Hebrews 13:5"},{"kind":"para","text":"THAT is a comforting thought."}]},{"start":18,"end":18,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God is a God of impossible things."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For with God nothing shall be impossible.","ref":"Luke 1:37"},{"kind":"para","text":"That is really difficult (for some reason) for many of us to fathom. We can’t understand how God can do all things, yet cannot sin. How can He do all things, yet can’t lie? How can He do all things, yet can’t do this or that or create this? It’s not that He can’t do everything. There are just some things He simply won’t do. He won’t lie. He has the power to do so, but He has no reason to do it. So lying is not in His vocabulary, because what does He have to lie about? When we lie, we do it to hide something. We do it out of guilt. God is not guilty of anything, and He has nothing to hide."},{"kind":"para","text":"God can do a great deal of things, but He is waiting for some things to take place before He does something like turning the wilderness into pools of water. I can’t imagine how that might look. It would look a lot like a lush, green, and comfortable paradise if the Lord is involved with forming it."}]},{"start":19,"end":20,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"These things should be able to grow in these places. Only God can make things grow where it was barren soil before. Farmers can try their hardest to grow crops in Death Valley, but it would certainly be a wasted effort. No, it would have to be the Lord that grows it, and He certainly CAN (He already has, like I’ve said, you need to see pictures of green Death Valley to really understand how amazing that is)."},{"kind":"para","text":"God will grow even the hardest of hearts as well. He is capable of doing that. He’s done it to hundreds before, and there’s nothing stopping Him from doing it again. We should be in prayer for those that have hard hearts. God can grow something there."}]}]},{"start":21,"end":24,"title":"Debate the Lord","entries":[{"start":21,"end":21,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God wants you to confront Him. Those who don’t believe have an open invitation to God’s throne. You have a call to confront the Lord with your unbelief. It’s written right here. Produce your cause. Tell the Lord directly why you don’t believe Him. Tell Him directly why you would rather worship false idols. What is the reason? I guarantee if you said it out loud to the face of the Lord, you would realize how silly and childish it is."}]},{"start":22,"end":22,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God is challenging the false worshippers as well. Bring your ideas and thoughts of who God is, and dictate what you believe will be the case. You debate with the Lord. You tell God what is going to happen. That’s a funny thought, isn’t it? I saw a video of a man who said he would confront God if He was real. He said, “If I die and I have to face God, I will just say, ‘How dare you create so much evil, and hate, and hurt, and do nothing about it! How dare you trick people, and hurt people, and laugh from above while staying out of it.’” He had a lot of insults to give to the Lord. But really, it’s going to look quite funny when he stands before the Lord speechless because he was completely wrong about the Lord. He won’t be saying anything of this nature to the Lord. He wouldn’t even be able to stand and look the Lord in the face because of his unbelief."},{"kind":"para","text":"Imagine a man coming to the Lord and saying, “Obviously the world has been around for billions of years and it was all formed by an accident.” That is what people say today. They would tell the Lord we all came from monkeys, and the Lord would look at them and laugh. I think He would find their theories and illogical arguments quite humorous. He would laugh because they hold no weight, and He has already given proof, as well as truth, to the beginning of the universe. Some “scientists” (if we can call them that) believe the Earth is getting better over time. Sane, rational thinking people would disagree entirely."}]},{"start":23,"end":23,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"If everyone had the decision to rule like God, we would be doomed. One person might think that stealing and murder were righteous. Another might believe that everyone needs to be gay or transgender, leaving no ability to have children ever again. Another person might think that everyone needs to bow down to them, allowing them to abuse their powers over the entire world, killing and destroying anyone who doesn’t obey."},{"kind":"para","text":"Others might mistreat the rich and lift up the poor. Some might send the righteous to hell, while the unrighteous would rule and reign. We all have warped ideas of what is good and godly and what is righteous in our own eyes. God is the only one who has the proper standard and knowledge of how to judge righteously. That is the standard by which we all have to make our judgments. Otherwise, it will be evil even if we mean it for the right reasons."}]},{"start":24,"end":24,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Anyone who worships a person or a false idol is just as unrighteous as the person they worship. Yet, that is the majority of this world. People literally worship government officials. They will go to the ends of the earth to stand up for their president, even if their president is unrighteous and evil."},{"kind":"para","text":"People also worship musicians and actors. They follow them around, stalk them, try to get pictures with them, and never leave them alone. People worship CEOs and billionaires all the time. We live in a terrible world of false worship."},{"kind":"para","text":"You know why it’s a problem to worship these people? Because they all make terrible decisions. They will do unrighteous things. Let me reemphasize: they WILL do unrighteous things."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For all have sinned, and come short of the glory of God;","ref":"Romans 3:23"},{"kind":"para","text":"Everyone is a sinner. We are all unrighteous. We have all gone against the Lord, and we will all continue to sin as long as we are in this mortal, evil body. That is why the standards of worship should be placed on the Lord alone. Worshipping anything else, whether on this Earth or in the universe, is a perfect way to lead yourself into a major letdown."}]}]},{"start":25,"end":29,"title":"God Is True","entries":[{"start":25,"end":25,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Certainly, this is speaking about Cyrus. According to Ezra, Cyrus will take over Babylon in the future, and he comes from the north, specifically Persia. Cyrus will also bring the people of Judah back to their land."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Now in the first year of Cyrus king of Persia, that the word of the LORD by the mouth of Jeremiah might be fulfilled, the LORD stirred up the spirit of Cyrus king of Persia, that he made a proclamation throughout all his kingdom, and put it also in writing, saying, Thus saith Cyrus king of Persia, The LORD God of heaven hath given me all the kingdoms of the earth; and he hath charged me to build him an house at Jerusalem, which is in Judah.","ref":"Ezra 1:1-2"},{"kind":"para","text":"Of course, this could easily be Jesus spoken of for the people of Christ. He is the prince of peace and the potter. He will mold us and shape us. Cyrus was no perfect man, but Jesus certainly is."}]},{"start":26,"end":26,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Call upon any god you choose, and they will not answer. But the Lord of creation, the God of the Bible, will answer. He always answers His children and those who genuinely need Him. The other gods won’t answer because they don’t exist. The God of the universe will answer because He is very real and very capable."},{"kind":"para","text":"As I’ve said before, we can certainly have a debate. You bring your gods and the proof of them, and I’ll bring my Bible and the proof of Him. We will measure up whose God is real. Atheists can bring their evidence of there being no God, and I’ll bring my evidence of there being a God. We can measure up whose God is real. Baseless theories and assumptions are no match for the accuracy and historical facts of scripture."}]},{"start":27,"end":28,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This reminds me of the people in Exodus right after they were taken out of Egypt to worship the Lord in the wilderness:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And when the people saw that Moses delayed to come down out of the mount, the people gathered themselves together unto Aaron, and said unto him, Up, make us gods, which shall go before us; for as for this Moses, the man that brought us up out of the land of Egypt, we wot not what is become of him. And Aaron said unto them, Break off the golden earrings, which are in the ears of your wives, of your sons, and of your daughters, and bring them unto me. And all the people brake off the golden earrings which were in their ears, and brought them unto Aaron. And he received them at their hand, and fashioned it with a graving tool, after he had made it a molten calf: and they said, These be thy gods, O Israel, which brought thee up out of the land of Egypt.","ref":"Exodus 32:1-4"},{"kind":"para","text":"How shallow and miserable. They must have looked at that idol and thought, “Wow, there is nothing like it! Let’s ask it a question and see what answers come from it.” Once the question is asked, nothing happens, and they all just anticipate in silence. They think, “Huh, maybe we should dance to it so it proves its powers like they do in Egypt!” and they started dancing, and Moses comes down and is distraught by their actions. Of course, we can read what happens to them in Exodus. But it’s the same today as well. False religions and atheists have the same mindset about their idols. They put their faith and trust into nothing and wait and anticipate the answer to come from it in time. Over time, though, that usually fails. The only way for it to NOT fail is if we keep adding something to our idols. When we do that, we just keep falling deeper and deeper into a lie until we are so convinced in lies that we believe it to be the truth."}]},{"start":29,"end":29,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"That’s all faith is to the world today. They trust and believe in vanity and nothing. They try to make it valuable and something of substance by throwing money at it, but in the end, it will never suffice. It will never serve them, and it will never give them what they need. It will never reveal the truth to them either. It can’t speak the truth, obviously. The faith of this world is just wind and confusion. That is all you will pull away from false worship of any kind on this Earth."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For God is not the author of confusion, but of peace, as in all churches of the saints.","ref":"1 Corinthians 14:33"},{"kind":"para","text":"If worship and truth is confusing to you, you either need to confront God with it, or it simply just isn't from the Lord (therefore isn't true)."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":9},{"start":10,"end":10},{"start":11,"end":12},{"start":13,"end":13},{"start":14,"end":14},{"start":15,"end":15},{"start":16,"end":16},{"start":17,"end":17},{"start":18,"end":18},{"start":19,"end":20},{"start":21,"end":21},{"start":22,"end":22},{"start":23,"end":23},{"start":24,"end":24},{"start":25,"end":25},{"start":26,"end":26},{"start":27,"end":28},{"start":29,"end":29}],"verses":{"1":"Keep silence before me, O islands; and let the people renew their strength: let them come near; then let them speak: let us come near together to judgment.","2":"Who raised up the righteous man from the east, called him to his foot, gave the nations before him, and made him rule over kings? he gave them as the dust to his sword, and as driven stubble to his bow.","3":"He pursued them, and passed safely; even by the way that he had not gone with his feet.","4":"Who hath wrought and done it, calling the generations from the beginning? I the Lord, the first, and with the last; I am he.","5":"The isles saw it, and feared; the ends of the earth were afraid, drew near, and came.","6":"They helped every one his neighbour; and every one said to his brother, Be of good courage.","7":"So the carpenter encouraged the goldsmith, and he that smootheth with the hammer him that smote the anvil, saying, It is ready for the sodering: and he fastened it with nails, that it should not be moved.","8":"But thou, Israel, art my servant, Jacob whom I have chosen, the seed of Abraham my friend.","9":"Thou whom I have taken from the ends of the earth, and called thee from the chief men thereof, and said unto thee, Thou art my servant; I have chosen thee, and not cast thee away.","10":"Fear thou not; for I am with thee: be not dismayed; for I am thy God: I will strengthen thee; yea, I will help thee; yea, I will uphold thee with the right hand of my righteousness.","11":"Behold, all they that were incensed against thee shall be ashamed and confounded: they shall be as nothing; and they that strive with thee shall perish.","12":"Thou shalt seek them, and shalt not find them, even them that contended with thee: they that war against thee shall be as nothing, and as a thing of nought.","13":"For I the Lord thy God will hold thy right hand, saying unto thee, Fear not; I will help thee.","14":"Fear not, thou worm Jacob, and ye men of Israel; I will help thee, saith the Lord, and thy redeemer, the Holy One of Israel.","15":"Behold, I will make thee a new sharp threshing instrument having teeth: thou shalt thresh the mountains, and beat them small, and shalt make the hills as chaff.","16":"Thou shalt fan them, and the wind shall carry them away, and the whirlwind shall scatter them: and thou shalt rejoice in the Lord, and shalt glory in the Holy One of Israel.","17":"When the poor and needy seek water, and there is none, and their tongue faileth for thirst, I the Lord will hear them, I the God of Israel will not forsake them.","18":"I will open rivers in high places, and fountains in the midst of the valleys: I will make the wilderness a pool of water, and the dry land springs of water.","19":"I will plant in the wilderness the cedar, the shittah tree, and the myrtle, and the oil tree; I will set in the desert the fir tree, and the pine, and the box tree together:","20":"That they may see, and know, and consider, and understand together, that the hand of the Lord hath done this, and the Holy One of Israel hath created it.","21":"Produce your cause, saith the Lord; bring forth your strong reasons, saith the King of Jacob.","22":"Let them bring them forth, and shew us what shall happen: let them shew the former things, what they be, that we may consider them, and know the latter end of them; or declare us things for to come.","23":"Shew the things that are to come hereafter, that we may know that ye are gods: yea, do good, or do evil, that we may be dismayed, and behold it together.","24":"Behold, ye are of nothing, and your work of nought: an abomination is he that chooseth you.","25":"I have raised up one from the north, and he shall come: from the rising of the sun shall he call upon my name: and he shall come upon princes as upon morter, and as the potter treadeth clay.","26":"Who hath declared from the beginning, that we may know? and beforetime, that we may say, He is righteous? yea, there is none that sheweth, yea, there is none that declareth, yea, there is none that heareth your words.","27":"The first shall say to Zion, Behold, behold them: and I will give to Jerusalem one that bringeth good tidings.","28":"For I beheld, and there was no man; even among them, and there was no counsellor, that, when I asked of them, could answer a word.","29":"Behold, they are all vanity; their works are nothing: their molten images are wind and confusion."}},
    "42": {"chapter":42,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: In our last chapter, God has given pretty clear provision for the saved and for the those that turn to Him in faith. He has a place for them, and He has a victory if they endure with the Lord. Those that are against the Lord will be met with terrible trouble and turmoil that will not be a thrilling conclusion for their legacies and future."},{"kind":"para","text":"In this chapter, we see the term \"elect\" pop up. I want to do my best to clear up and clarify what that term means, and how it is used by the Lord. It's a word that has started a lot of debates in Christian circles, but I think the debates are ultimately wearisome and meaningless. Both sides of the debate are wrong, and I am hoping to show why and in which way we can utilize this knowledge from scripture in our own lives to come to terms with God's elect, and how that effects us as God's saved."}],"previously":["In our last chapter, God has given pretty clear provision for the saved and for those who turn to Him in faith. He has a place for them, and He has a victory if they endure with the Lord. Those who are against the Lord will be met with terrible trouble and turmoil that will not be a thrilling conclusion for their legacies and future. In this chapter, we see the term “elect” pop up. I want to do my best to clear up and clarify what that term means and how it is used by the Lord. It’s a word that has started a lot of debates in Christian circles, but I think the debates are ultimately wearisome and meaningless. Both sides of the debate are wrong, and I am hoping to show why and in which way we can utilize this knowledge from scripture in our own lives to come to terms with God’s elect and how that affects us as God’s saved."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":4,"title":"The Elect","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"In modern Christianity, there is a problem with the word “elect.” It comes with a whole slew of assumptions, primarily the Calvinistic approach. I’ve experienced some strain regarding my stance on this topic. For a long time, I fought against the title of Calvinist. People were calling me this, and I didn’t even know why. I eventually discovered that it’s because I believe that the Lord saves by His own means, and it has nothing to do with our personal efforts. That’s not a Calvin theory; it is a Bible truth."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For by grace are ye saved through faith; and that not of yourselves: it is the gift of God: Not of works, lest any man should boast.","ref":"Ephesians 2:8-9"},{"kind":"para","text":"Why they associated me with Calvin is beyond my comprehension. I think the real issue is with this word “elect.” That was a word that came up a lot. One particular person asked me, “If you had to choose between Calvinism or Arminianism, which would you choose?” Again, I didn’t know how to answer. I knew that I didn’t believe much of anything from the Arminian standpoint, but I had some things align with the Calvinistic viewpoint. May I remind you, this was taking place in Texas, which is funny. I said, “I don’t know. Both of them have their flaws, but I would have to lean more towards the Calvinistic viewpoints.” That certainly made them fly off the handle. They called me a Calvinist. I said, “Are you a Republican or a Democrat?” He said, “Well, I’m certainly not voting for Hillary.” I said, “So you lean towards Republican. They have standards that you agree with, and that is why you lean in their direction. However, I guarantee they have some standards that you are NOT okay with. Maybe it’s the stance on abortion. Perhaps the stance on homosexuality. Could be a stance on laws and regulations. Neither side of the political aisle is perfect, but you have chosen a side nevertheless, because it’s impossible to walk right in the middle. That is how I feel about Calvinism and Arminianism.”"},{"kind":"para","text":"Honestly, it is still how I mostly feel. I do not agree with a great deal of things that Calvinists believe, and if I had to choose between the two, I would lean towards Calvinism. But may I suggest a third option? Honestly, this verse gives us a third option above and beyond either the Calvinistic viewpoint or the Arminian viewpoint, AND it’s found in the very word for “elect.” Look at these verses and tell me if you can spot what the third option is:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For there shall arise false Christs, and false prophets, and shall shew great signs and wonders; insomuch that, if it were possible, they shall deceive the very elect.","ref":"Matthew 24:24"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And shall not God avenge his own elect, which cry day and night unto him, though he bear long with them?","ref":"Luke 18:7"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Who shall lay any thing to the charge of God's elect? It is God that justifieth.","ref":"Romans 8:33"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Put on therefore, as the elect of God, holy and beloved, bowels of mercies, kindness, humbleness of mind, meekness, longsuffering;","ref":"Colossians 3:12"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Paul, a servant of God, and an apostle of Jesus Christ, according to the faith of God's elect, and the acknowledging of the truth which is after godliness;","ref":"Titus 1:1"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Elect according to the foreknowledge of God the Father, through sanctification of the Spirit, unto obedience and sprinkling of the blood of Jesus Christ: Grace unto you, and peace, be multiplied.","ref":"1 Peter 1:2"},{"kind":"para","text":"From this, you might be thinking, “Yeah! More verses about that problem word ‘elect’—how is that going to help me?” Well, every time it’s mentioned, it’s tied to God’s name. Even in this verse here, God is the one speaking about the elect. And you know who the elect He is speaking about is? It’s His own Son, Jesus Christ."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Who hath saved us, and called us with an holy calling, not according to our works, but according to his own purpose and grace, which was given us in Christ Jesus before the world began,","ref":"2 Timothy 1:9"},{"kind":"para","text":"There is a third option to pursue, and that is Biblicism. It is about God’s Word being true. We cannot get hung up on who is elect and who is not, because that is not our place to judge. That is the Lord’s place to judge. We must give the gospel to every creature, and the Lord will sort out who is saved and who is not."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"So then it is not of him that willeth, nor of him that runneth, but of God that sheweth mercy.","ref":"Romans 9:16"},{"kind":"para","text":"And you might say, “Well yeah! That’s what the Calvinists believe too! So you fall under that umbrella.” They believe it because the Bible says it pretty flat out and plainly. However, the problem arises when they start to add stipulations to God’s Word. They do what Paul says is not possible:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Wherein I suffer trouble, as an evil doer, even unto bonds; but the word of God is not bound.","ref":"2 Timothy 2:9"},{"kind":"para","text":"The world may try to silence the Christian, but they will never succeed. They may attempt to keep the Bible out of the lives of humanity, but God’s Word will always accomplish what God wants it to. They might try to prevent people from ever being “elected,” but God will always search and save the lost when they are willing to trust Him. The key issue here is the word “will.” You can’t use the term “free will” with a Calvinist. They believe that it’s God’s Will and nothing more. That is why many Calvinists believe that if you have sin in you, you are not saved. Period. That is simply not true. In fact, it couldn’t be further from the truth."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"If we say that we have no sin, we deceive ourselves, and the truth is not in us.","ref":"1 John 1:8"},{"kind":"para","text":"God does not treat people like puppets. He will use people, but only if they are compliant. I know some people are under the impression that God can use a person like a puppet, and they pull from Pharaoh and King Saul to prove their point. However, both of those people were already heading in the direction that the Lord said He would allow for them. Pharaoh was already hardening his heart before the Lord said He would allow it, and Saul was already becoming evil before the Lord gave him an evil spirit. Those were the choices they made themselves without the Lord’s approval on the matter. God stamped His approval eventually, and that was to their own detriment, but He allowed them the freedom to choose their path."},{"kind":"para","text":"In fact, if we looked at both of those characters, God’s presence was still with both of them. God gave Pharaoh a hard heart, but Moses was the soft heart that Pharaoh needed. Instead of Pharaoh trusting Moses and the heart behind Moses, he wanted to fight against it. He physically proved what God said He was going to do to him. Same with Saul. God said He would give him an evil spirit, but God left His own spirit with him through David, and Saul proved (outwardly) how much he hated the spirit of God by trying to kill David quite a few times."},{"kind":"para","text":"And all of this goes against the word “elect.” God elects based on free will. And every Calvinist is shunning me at the moment. But it’s true!"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"The Lord is not slack concerning his promise, as some men count slackness; but is longsuffering to us-ward, not willing that any should perish, but that all should come to repentance.","ref":"2 Peter 3:9"},{"kind":"para","text":"Yet, according to the Calvinist, there are just some people put on this Earth who God will purposely not save because He doesn’t want them to repent and turn to Him. They were made to bring disgrace to the Lord. I don’t believe that. I believe He knows who will call upon Him and who will not before the world was even formed. He knew it. But He doesn’t create people just to do evil and die. No, according to scripture, He wants even the most evil among the planet to turn to Him. Even Judas Iscariot, but I’m not going to get into that in this setting."},{"kind":"para","text":"My point is, God’s elect are not just forcefully chosen by the Lord. His elect are those who are willing to turn to Him and follow Him. Those are the people He elects. The same with our president today. I may not agree with the president about everything, but there are a great deal of people who do, and they will follow their president to the ends of the Earth. They are the president’s elect. The president did not choose them, but he loves them because they are for him. The Lord chooses us, but it’s from the choice we ultimately make. If we follow Him, He will be with us."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Submit yourselves therefore to God. Resist the devil, and he will flee from you. Draw nigh to God, and he will draw nigh to you. Cleanse your hands, ye sinners; and purify your hearts, ye double minded.","ref":"James 4:7-8"},{"kind":"para","text":"This verse insinuates action. We must get closer to God if we want God to get closer to us. We must “submit” to the rule of God, otherwise we are likely submitting to Satan. Let me put it this way: God’s elect (if I may) are not those that He chooses. God’s elect is Jesus Christ alone. The Israelites are looked at as “the elect,” but not all of them were saved."},{"kind":"para","text":"We are going through a book of scripture where the majority of Israel (including Judah at this moment) has largely turned away from the Lord. That is not what an “elect” person would do. Rather, Jesus is the only elect one on this Earth, and those that turn to Christ with their lives and faith will belong in the Lord’s “elect” as well. Christ is the only reason that any of us have a foot to stand on."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"This is a faithful saying, and worthy of all acceptation, that Christ Jesus came into the world to save sinners; of whom I am chief.","ref":"1 Timothy 1:15"},{"kind":"para","text":"He came to save the sinner, not the elect. Those who turn to Him in trust are those who will be saved. Those who turn to Jesus are “elected” because they have the “elect.” Don’t get mad at me for the statement; get mad at God that He would leave His salvation open to the entire world!"},{"kind":"para","text":"And we know that this verse here (in Isaiah) is about Christ because the attributes only belong to one person. He says His Spirit will be put on “him.” Singular. “He” singular shall bring forth judgment to the Gentiles. That man is Jesus Christ, the truly elect of God."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Who shall not cry? Well, Jesus of course. Yet, we know that He did cry. He cried over the death of loved ones and moved with compassion for the lost. Rather, He didn’t cry in pity against the injustices. Honestly, He stayed fairly quiet about the government’s injustices to His people. That was not the main focus of His coming."},{"kind":"para","text":"He never lifted Himself up in pride or power. He never forced people to hear His words and obey His commands. He left the choice up to us. Again, it goes against the Calvin viewpoint, but that is just the Bible for you."}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"We are not the elect without Christ. Rather, God calls us a “bruised reed.” We are simply bent out of shape, and the Lord could have sent Christ to beat us back into straightness, but He didn’t. He didn’t “break” us to make us whole again. He didn’t just send His Son to judge and destroy us. No, “A bruised reed shall he NOT break…” A smoking flax would be those that reject the Lord and continue on their path of destruction. The Lord didn’t put that flame out. Honestly, He could have. He could have just ended everything on His first coming to this Earth. Those that trusted in the Lord before His birth would be saved, and those that didn’t… Well, the future would not exist for them, we will just say. But Jesus didn’t do that. Why? Why wouldn’t He just keep the elect here and put out the rest of the world? Well, that’s because He wants the world to continue their choice for Him. He wants MORE people under His umbrella of salvation. He came to this Earth to prove the way to God is through Him alone."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Jesus saith unto him, I am the way, the truth, and the life: no man cometh unto the Father, but by me.","ref":"John 14:6"},{"kind":"para","text":"If you were on the fence about God’s presence and salvation before, you will certainly be assured through Jesus’ sacrifice for you. The world is busy doing their judging, and He will be busy aligning judgment with Truth."},{"kind":"para","text":"The world says this, but what does God say? This lie states this, but what does God say? The government is telling us to do this, but what does God say?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Jesus always pointed to the best way, rather than to the world’s power way. He put God’s kingdom first, and He made it clear that we should be doing the same in every judgment or decision we might try to make."}]},{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Jesus didn’t fail; that is absolutely true. However, I do wonder if He felt discouraged. There were times when His disciples were hurting Him rather than helping Him. The moment that Judas betrayed Jesus, though it didn’t take Him by surprise, really hurt Him. You know it had to hurt the other disciples who witnessed it. We see this as the “ultimate betrayal in history,” yet we are equally responsible for the betrayal by rejecting the Lord. That cannot feel good to God, and I don’t think it was very “encouraging” to Christ."},{"kind":"para","text":"But Jesus found courage in the Lord, and I know that is the only reason He continued to move forward. That is, perhaps, the only reason that many of us will be able to move forward as well. We must sit and wait for the Lord to encourage us so we can do the hard things for Him. If He doesn’t give us the strength to do it, we should probably not do it."}]}]},{"start":5,"end":9,"title":"Jesus Above All","entries":[{"start":5,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Once again, the Lord Jesus Christ embodies all of this. He is righteous, led by the Lord, and kept for a perfect moment by God. He was given God’s covenant to bring to the people (salvation) and a light to those that the world thought could never be reached (the Gentiles)."},{"kind":"para","text":"He physically and spiritually opened the eyes of the blind and physically and spiritually released prisoners so they can be free to walk in light. Jesus Christ is the only elect, and if you can’t get your head around that idea here, you will always have a convoluted outlook on the rest of scripture."}]},{"start":8,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is another verse that proves that it is Jesus Christ that God is talking about here. God’s glory isn’t given to anyone else, yet He will give it to His Son (and He just spoke about that in the previous verses of this chapter). That is another reason we can know that Jehovah (creator God) and Jesus Christ (the Son of God) are one. If God gives Jesus glory, then that signifies that Jesus must be God. I remember this was one of the verses I had written down when the ladies about “God the Mother” showed up to my door. He, alone, is God. There is no one beside Him, and there is no glory given to anything or anyone else. If there was, God would cease to be God. Imagine how chaotic the world would be without a supreme author. It’s because of this that His Will for mankind is not to choose this or that person for this or that cause. Rather, He will put all His choice onto His own Son, and THAT will be the only image of a truly elect person we will ever see."},{"kind":"para","text":"If we lived by the standards of Calvin (acclaimed by his followers today), the only way for us to be “elect” is if we were as perfect as Jesus. We never will be that perfect. Even if we completely lived as a hermit and never sinned again, we will always fall short of God’s glory. Jesus didn’t, however, and He walked PERFECTLY before the Lord. That is the only reason that there can be only ONE elect on this Earth and in eternity. We must hide under that election and find safe passage there."}]},{"start":9,"end":9,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This reminds me of another verse in scripture:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Therefore if any man be in Christ, he is a new creature: old things are passed away; behold, all things are become new.","ref":"2 Corinthians 5:17"},{"kind":"para","text":"Funny enough, the only way to become “new” is through Jesus Christ alone. We must have the elect if we want the old to pass away. God gives gifts of provision and vision for the future before they are presented to us."},{"kind":"para","text":"We can look at the judgments of the world and feel defeated, or we can look at the glories of God and feel assured. God’s prophecies are actually gifts to mankind. Sadly, most of mankind has rejected the prophecies and mistreated the preachers because they don’t sound good for them."},{"kind":"para","text":"They know that they are against the Lord and that they will experience God’s judgment, not God’s mercy. They can change that, though, if they take the preacher’s word seriously."}]}]},{"start":10,"end":13,"title":"No Idols","entries":[{"start":10,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"At the time of this writing, these places were giving glory to literally everything else except the Lord. They had their idols and their lifestyles, and they didn’t want to change for anyone or anything. God is giving them the opportunity to turn to Him. These are people, no doubt, who were not the “elect” of God. Why would God call these people if they were not elect? Well, again (to further prove the point that God has been making since the beginning of time), the choice is up to the individual. The only elect one is Jesus. Period. The Israelites would only be considered as “elect” if they believed in the Savior for salvation alone. Otherwise, they are the chosen, but they are not the elect. Perhaps that is where a lot of the problem resides. There is a difference between chosen and elect. I’ve seen it happen in many churches. The staff is chosen, but only a few people are elected to actually be on staff. It breeds a “competition” in the church if I can be honest. I used to run that race, but that is a dismal and terrible race to run. No, the only race worth running is the one for the Lord. He not only has chosen me, He has elected me through Jesus Christ. It is by design that I was placed into this world, and He knew exactly where I need to be in order for me to turn to Him and enter the battle of faith. It hasn’t always been fun, but it has always been worth it. God (arguably) has chosen the entire world, but only those that cling to Jesus will be elected."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For God so loved the world, that he gave his only begotten Son, that whosoever believeth in him should not perish, but have everlasting life.","ref":"John 3:16"}]},{"start":13,"end":13,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"You will never win a battle against the creator of the universe. That sounds like a no brainer, but you'd be surprised as to how many people think they can get one over on God and win. They truly are blind."}]}]},{"start":14,"end":17,"title":"A Backwards World","entries":[{"start":14,"end":14,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Honestly, if you look throughout 1 and 2 Kings, God should have (in our eyes) done something a long time ago to these kingdoms. Particularly (at this writing), He is speaking about Judah. That’s all that’s left. He has kept quiet about the whole affair of Judah, but He is being taken to a point where He HAS to say and do something about their wickedness. He HAS to put an end to their terror. Honestly, it’s more like a bandaid that has to be torn off. He has been trying to protect and heal this nation for years, and they won’t stop bleeding. So He just has to rip the bandaid off, and He will have to take time to do surgery to repair them. They are certainly going to be left with scars. Again (arguably), the most scarred nation on Earth is likely the nation of Israel. Yet, somehow, they keep going."}]},{"start":15,"end":16,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There is a great difference illustrated between the elect and the nonelect here. One scenario involves the mountains and hills being destroyed, and the herbs lying waste. There will be no rivers, and pools and everything will look very dry and bothersome. The other scenario is being led by the Lord while in complete blindness. That is what we look like, mind you. We look like we are just feeling around in the dark, uncertain of what is out there. The Lord reveals those things to us if we would let Him. He will give us a place to go and a way to see those things that are good for us. I would rather be blind to this world and led by the Lord than to be led by the world and blind to the Lord."}]},{"start":17,"end":17,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Honestly, I don’t see how they feel anything good from trusting in made-up gods. Even still today, atheists don’t believe in the Lord, yet they believe in themselves. They believe in science and manmade evaluations. They put themselves as gods and call that “normal.” It’s really just childish and sad from a Christian’s perspective. They look at the Christian as childish for believing in a creator of all things, but they don’t see how worshipping false idols is childish. How strangely backwards this world is."}]}]},{"start":18,"end":22,"title":"Cascading Grace","entries":[{"start":18,"end":19,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Here’s what God thinks of His own “elect,” if you will. He calls His own “blind” and “deaf.” At this time, the Israelites were rejecting everything that the Lord was doing and giving to them. They didn’t seem to want the Lord’s provision in their lives at all. They wanted their own ways and thoughts for everything here. If I can be brutally honest here, God’s elect are still very much like this today. That is why election means nothing by the world’s definition. It is also why that word is not ascribed to us, but rather only to His Son. Christ was never blind or deaf to the moving and calling of God. We (the saved) almost always are. We are even blind and deaf to the callings on the people around us as well. Another reason we cannot ascribe this word “elect” to us. It can only be ascribed to Jesus. We are simply benefactors to God’s goodness because He has given us a way to graft into His salvation and election. All we can do for our election (according to scripture) is to make it sure."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Wherefore the rather, brethren, give diligence to make your calling and election sure: for if ye do these things, ye shall never fall: For so an entrance shall be ministered unto you abundantly into the everlasting kingdom of our Lord and Saviour Jesus Christ.","ref":"2 Peter 1:10-11"},{"kind":"para","text":"Only through Jesus do we have that entrance and ability to be \"elected.\""}]},{"start":20,"end":21,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Jesus’ righteousness is the only reason that God has not done away with this Earth. It’s the only reason that we have a chance and ability to be considered part of “the elect.” Without the righteousness of Jesus, we would all be doomed for His wrath, and there would be no hope or chance for us to ever be saved. Without God’s elect, we are God’s enemy."}]},{"start":22,"end":22,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Again, these would be considered as “God’s elect.” They aren’t elect though. They are chosen. They can only be elect if they have the Savior. There were a few “elect” members there that would be saved from God’s judgment here. Isaiah was one of those “elect” because he has trusted in the “elected.” Jesus Christ is the elected; we are the benefactors of God’s grace. We would not have the ability to know God’s love without Jesus Christ being elected by the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"Water illustrations (in my personal opinion) are so weak, but that is what I’m going to use in this example. If I am filling a cup with water, I can fill it to the brim. That is what most people are; they are a full cup of water. However, Jesus was filled to the brim and continuously filled. When you fill a cup past the brim, it starts to overflow. I don’t know if you have ever seen a cup fountain before, but someone stacks cups on top of each other and fills the top cup. Once it’s full, it runs out into the other cups, which are filled past their brim, and it cascades into filling the cups below that and so forth until all the cups are full and the water is just spilling onto the floor."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is Jesus. God has filled Him with grace overflowing, and it trickles down into those under His salvation. It overflows from us into those around us and so on and so forth. Cascading grace. It only starts with ONE cup. It starts only with Jesus."}]}]},{"start":23,"end":25,"title":"God's Wrath Poured Out","entries":[{"start":23,"end":23,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"No one. That is why the world needed Jesus. We are noncompliant to the Lord. We need a perfect man, and that can only be God in the flesh."}]},{"start":24,"end":25,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord is going to pour His wrath on “him,” that is to say, “Jacob.” Israel can be saved, but only through the elect. God will have to pour His wrath on the elect (who is Jesus) if the world is going to be saved. And God does this through the crucifixion:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Herein is love, not that we loved God, but that he loved us, and sent his Son to be the propitiation for our sins.","ref":"1 John 4:10"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And he is the propitiation for our sins: and not for ours only, but also for the sins of the whole world.","ref":"1 John 2:2"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But God commendeth his love toward us, in that, while we were yet sinners, Christ died for us. Much more then, being now justified by his blood, we shall be saved from wrath through him.","ref":"Romans 5:8-9"},{"kind":"para","text":"This will be better illustrated in Isaiah 53, but I don't want to spoil anything yet because it's just too good!"}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":9},{"start":10,"end":12},{"start":13,"end":13},{"start":14,"end":14},{"start":15,"end":16},{"start":17,"end":17},{"start":18,"end":19},{"start":20,"end":21},{"start":22,"end":22},{"start":23,"end":23},{"start":24,"end":25}],"verses":{"1":"Behold my servant, whom I uphold; mine elect, in whom my soul delighteth; I have put my spirit upon him: he shall bring forth judgment to the Gentiles.","2":"He shall not cry, nor lift up, nor cause his voice to be heard in the street.","3":"A bruised reed shall he not break, and the smoking flax shall he not quench: he shall bring forth judgment unto truth.","4":"He shall not fail nor be discouraged, till he have set judgment in the earth: and the isles shall wait for his law.","5":"Thus saith God the Lord, he that created the heavens, and stretched them out; he that spread forth the earth, and that which cometh out of it; he that giveth breath unto the people upon it, and spirit to them that walk therein:","6":"I the Lord have called thee in righteousness, and will hold thine hand, and will keep thee, and give thee for a covenant of the people, for a light of the Gentiles;","7":"To open the blind eyes, to bring out the prisoners from the prison, and them that sit in darkness out of the prison house.","8":"I am the Lord: that is my name: and my glory will I not give to another, neither my praise to graven images.","9":"Behold, the former things are come to pass, and new things do I declare: before they spring forth I tell you of them.","10":"Sing unto the Lord a new song, and his praise from the end of the earth, ye that go down to the sea, and all that is therein; the isles, and the inhabitants thereof.","11":"Let the wilderness and the cities thereof lift up their voice, the villages that Kedar doth inhabit: let the inhabitants of the rock sing, let them shout from the top of the mountains.","12":"Let them give glory unto the Lord, and declare his praise in the islands.","13":"The Lord shall go forth as a mighty man, he shall stir up jealousy like a man of war: he shall cry, yea, roar; he shall prevail against his enemies.","14":"I have long time holden my peace; I have been still, and refrained myself: now will I cry like a travailing woman; I will destroy and devour at once.","15":"I will make waste mountains and hills, and dry up all their herbs; and I will make the rivers islands, and I will dry up the pools.","16":"And I will bring the blind by a way that they knew not; I will lead them in paths that they have not known: I will make darkness light before them, and crooked things straight. These things will I do unto them, and not forsake them.","17":"They shall be turned back, they shall be greatly ashamed, that trust in graven images, that say to the molten images, Ye are our gods.","18":"Hear, ye deaf; and look, ye blind, that ye may see.","19":"Who is blind, but my servant? or deaf, as my messenger that I sent? who is blind as he that is perfect, and blind as the Lord's servant?","20":"Seeing many things, but thou observest not; opening the ears, but he heareth not.","21":"The Lord is well pleased for his righteousness' sake; he will magnify the law, and make it honourable.","22":"But this is a people robbed and spoiled; they are all of them snared in holes, and they are hid in prison houses: they are for a prey, and none delivereth; for a spoil, and none saith, Restore.","23":"Who among you will give ear to this? who will hearken and hear for the time to come?","24":"Who gave Jacob for a spoil, and Israel to the robbers? did not the Lord, he against whom we have sinned? for they would not walk in his ways, neither were they obedient unto his law.","25":"Therefore he hath poured upon him the fury of his anger, and the strength of battle: and it hath set him on fire round about, yet he knew not; and it burned him, yet he laid it not to heart."}},
    "43": {"chapter":43,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: In our last chapter, we spoke quite a bit about the term \"elect\" as it's used in scripture. We spoke about how it is usually misrepresented in religions and Christian circles today, and how we should view it from an overarching Biblical framework. It's a Bible word that God uses to describe His Son."},{"kind":"para","text":"In this chapter we are going to hang on that theme, and the Lord is going to give some insight as to what it looks like to live as the Lord's elect."}],"previously":["In our last chapter, we discussed the term “elect” as it is used in scripture. We explored how it is often misrepresented in religions and Christian circles today and emphasized the importance of viewing it from an overarching Biblical framework. It is a Bible word that God uses to describe His Son. In this chapter, we will continue on that theme, and the Lord will provide insight into what it means to live as the Lord’s elect."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":7,"title":"Gather His People","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"We should probably recognize the way in which Isaiah writes these next few chapters. He is talking in the present tense, acting as if God has already done these things when, in fact, He won’t do them until a future time. Why would He say, “I have redeemed thee,” when the redemption spoken about here is through Jesus Christ, who is yet to come? Well, there are probably a few reasons for this."},{"kind":"para","text":"Firstly, it’s likely that the Lord has already lived out those times. He is in the future and at the beginning all at once. He stands outside of time, so He is able to be through all time at the same time."},{"kind":"para","text":"Secondly, God has redeemed His people several times over. It might still be a future promise to them, but it’s a promise they can depend on because the Lord has proven to always keep His promises. The same way in which the Israelites were saved back in the Old Testament is the same way in which we are saved today. They had to put their faith and trust in the Lord. If you haven’t realized that by this point, I don’t think you’ll ever understand the entirety of scripture. It’s a redemption story from Genesis to Revelation."},{"kind":"para","text":"Thirdly, God wants to provide hope as if the promise has already been kept. Again, if God says He will do it, then you can bet that He WILL do it. Those who accept His promises will be able to live in His promises RIGHT NOW. They don’t have to wait for Him to prove it because they know He will. God is a God of promises, and if He says He has promised you something, then you can rest assured that He will keep that promise, which gives us the opportunity to live in the promise now (even if we don’t see it until the distant future)."},{"kind":"para","text":"So when we read God saying that He has already done something, but we know that it hasn’t come quite yet, we can know that it’s because it will absolutely happen no matter what the world may try to do to stop it."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Recognize a few things here: Why would you need the Lord to pass through water with you? Granted, it could be talking about literal water here, but it’s obviously much deeper than that. The water in our life is usually tumultuous. If we have to walk through it, we usually have to do it alone. Even if your family is by your side through a storm, they could never understand your specific feelings on the matter, just like you could never truly understand theirs. However, the Lord understands, and that is how He walks through the water with you."},{"kind":"para","text":"Walking through fire is even harder. Again, this could be talking about literal fire, but it’s obviously much deeper than that. In fact, fire will be something that is brought up over and over again in scripture as being intense trials."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"That the trial of your faith, being much more precious than of gold that perisheth, though it be tried with fire, might be found unto praise and honour and glory at the appearing of Jesus Christ:","ref":"1 Peter 1:7"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"The fining pot is for silver, and the furnace for gold: but the LORD trieth the hearts.","ref":"Proverbs 17:3"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For thou, O God, hast proved us: thou hast tried us, as silver is tried.","ref":"Psalm 66:10"},{"kind":"para","text":"Water is difficult trials, but fire is testing trials. How much you can take of either is fully dependent upon how close you are to the Lord."}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The nations around Israel were there to push the Israelites in the proper direction. Egypt and Ethiopia were not kind people to Israel, but in the grand scheme of things, it brought Israel into a closer and deeper relationship with God. Now that they are not a problem, the Israelites think they have it made. That is why the Lord is going to have them fall back in line. They need to be trained, again. Sometimes that is what the Lord might do with us as well. We might feel pretty good about our standings in most areas of sin, but there could be one specific blind spot that we just can’t seem to let go of or get over. God will send us into training over and over again until we distance ourselves further and further away from it. It’s not a one-time thing and done. Anyone that tells you repentance is a one-time thing is fooling themselves and trying to take you down with them. They will act perfect and collected, but behind the scenes, everything is falling apart. You can almost guarantee that they are struggling with a sin somewhere, but they are just good at hiding it."}]},{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"That word “love” seems to be diminishing in meaning these days. Love is truly only skin deep in this world. But the Lord knows literally everything about you. He knows your thoughts, your sins, your wants and desires, and the filthiness you have said and done. He knows it all. And if you are His, He truly and deeply loves you. It’s a love we can never understand."},{"kind":"para","text":"We have the death on the cross as proof of that love, but we still don’t know the depths of God’s love for us. Perhaps when we get into eternity and see the Lord face to face, we will finally understand the kind of love that God has for His people. Until then, all we can do is read it and dig deep into God’s Word to try and find out how far God’s love will go."}]},{"start":5,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Eventually, God will gather all His people to Himself. He will gather the Israelites, but He will also gather “every one that is called” by His name. That is you and me today. We will be gathered with the Lord and His people in the future, and we will all be under His authority, power, and reign, worshipping and singing praises to His name."}]}]},{"start":8,"end":13,"title":"God's Deep Love","entries":[{"start":8,"end":9,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There are a lot of history “experts” in our world today. They act and claim that they know all things and are assured of all things. They say, “There is no God. The Earth has been around for billions and billions of years, and it was all started by accident.” Yet they can’t show us one chaotic thing that has become organized creation. You can’t get order from chaos, which is why. Furthermore, they have no proof that what they are saying is true."},{"kind":"para","text":"I’ll keep the proof of God’s Word as legitimate proof, and they can keep their own theories as their “proof” (if you can even call it that). I can just make up whatever I wanted to and call it “science” today, and people would have to believe it. In fact, if I take God out of the equation altogether and just make something up, people would certainly believe it. They become skeptical only if the Lord is mentioned somewhere. The most trusted source of truth is the questionable one to the world today. Yet, the least tested source of truth doesn’t need to be questioned at all. Doesn’t that seem absurd to anyone else, or is it just me?"}]},{"start":10,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Here we have the ultimate purpose of life. The purpose for your existence today is to know God and believe Him. God’s will for your life is to know and believe Him. His reason for keeping you on this Earth is to know and believe Him. John Bunyan said, “What God says is best is best, though all the men in the world are against it.” The part in all of this that baffles me, however, is the “before me…” part. Was there anything before God? Not according to God!"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"I am Alpha and Omega, the beginning and the ending, saith the Lord, which is, and which was, and which is to come, the Almighty.","ref":"Revelation 1:8"},{"kind":"para","text":"He is the beginning. He was not just in the beginning, He physically and literally IS the beginning of everything. I will never understand that until eternity."}]},{"start":11,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God alone is the Savior of this world, not just of the Israelites, but of the entire world. When we read about Jesus and His acclamation of the Godhead, we are assured that He is fully God because there is no other Savior in eternity except God. Once again, our existence is to believe God, and if God says He is the only Savior, then we would do well to believe Him."}]},{"start":12,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God proves His salvation, and He still proves it today. The proof is in the saved person’s life. There are many people who are under the impression that people simply cannot change. There are individuals in this world who are so calloused by past sins that they will forever be stuck in that mode of thinking until the day they die. However, I have seen genuine change in calloused people hundreds of times because of the Lord’s salvation. God can change people, but He only changes those who actually desire to be changed by Him. He will not touch a man who remains hardhearted. He will only change a man who is willing to be broken down first."},{"kind":"para","text":"Every religion in this world forces some sort of steps program for genuine change. Not scripture. God says, “I will save you, and I will change you if you would just trust me.” Religion says, “You must do XYZ, and be consistent for this many years, and pray, and confess, and be baptized, and get involved, and do this and that if you want to have a chance at genuine change.” That has never worked for anyone. Some people may have tricked themselves into believing it works for them, but it certainly doesn’t bring any sort of lasting change. After a while, church work just becomes a burden because the heart didn’t change, just your mind on it. If you want genuine life change, it must start with your heart."}]},{"start":13,"end":13,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The work that God does will be done, period. No one has to let it happen; He will just do it, and you will either have to accept it or reject it. Either way, God will do what He must with or without your approval on the matter. He has to. Otherwise, things will become chaotic, and evil will reign. That’s proven by the fact that God has waited for Israel to make things right and turn to Him for literally generations."},{"kind":"para","text":"People say, “Why doesn’t God put a stop to it?” and then they say, “Why is God so harsh?” God has proven all your questions; you just don’t want to see the purposes behind why He does what He does. You just see it from your own standards of goodness, rather than the overall standards of goodness, which is for the sake of eternity."}]}]},{"start":14,"end":21,"title":"Redeemed Chosen","entries":[{"start":14,"end":14,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Judah is going to be trained. That is why the enemy appears in our lives. We must be trained, and we must learn to rely on the Lord and follow Him in sincerity and truth. If we can’t do that, we will be controlled by the enemy, and that never pays out anything important in the end. The rewards of the enemy are all imitations of the real thing. They look real, but they aren’t."}]},{"start":15,"end":15,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Why is God doing this? Why is God going to lead them into captivity? Well, this verse answers it. He is the Lord, the Holy One, the creator of Israel, and their King. Their other kings have failed them too many times. They were supposed to look to the Lord. Because they didn’t, the whole nation fell apart. So the Lord has to remind them who it is that is really in charge here. It isn’t the king they selected or that was raised in the castle. No, the real King sits above the kings of the Earth and has been calling for their attention for generations now."}]},{"start":16,"end":17,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God has proven His power and providence to this nation over and over again. He will prove it again to them. They will see what God can and has done for them, and they will be without excuse to follow Him. Sadly, they will get comfortable without Him even in captivity, and they will have to learn to come back and worship Him alone again. They will, for a time..."}]},{"start":18,"end":18,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Looking ahead is what the Old Testament really shined on. They were to spend their days looking forward to their redemption. They needed to see what Christ would do for them if they would just stay faithful."},{"kind":"para","text":"We, today, don’t dwell on the past, of course. We think back to Christ’s death, but we still have future promises from the Lord to think on and look forward to. Christ has saved us in the past, but He has not finished His promises for our future. Perhaps you feel alone; God promises to be with you if you just hold on to Him:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Yea, though I walk through the valley of the shadow of death, I will fear no evil: for thou art with me; thy rod and thy staff they comfort me.","ref":"Psalm 23:4"},{"kind":"para","text":"Maybe you feel scared; God promises to give you strength if you rely on Him:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Fear thou not; for I am with thee: be not dismayed; for I am thy God: I will strengthen thee; yea, I will help thee; yea, I will uphold thee with the right hand of my righteousness.","ref":"Isaiah 41:10"},{"kind":"para","text":"It could be that you feel burdened; God promises to give you rest if you would leave your burdens with Him:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Come unto me, all ye that labour and are heavy laden, and I will give you rest. Take my yoke upon you, and learn of me; for I am meek and lowly in heart: and ye shall find rest unto your souls. For my yoke is easy, and my burden is light.","ref":"Matthew 11:28-30"},{"kind":"para","text":"It would certainly seem as if God is taking His sweet time getting to these promises in your life. That’s okay. He has a time frame that He is working on, and He WILL accomplish these promises in your life. You might just have to wait a little while longer. If God does not fulfill His promises to His children, He is not a God that can be trusted to worship or depend on. Don’t worry about the past; worry about God’s promises for your future."}]},{"start":19,"end":19,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God is going to do a new thing. Well, it’s new to us anyway. Nothing is new to the Lord. He has seen and heard it all for eternities past and eternities future. He will make all things new, though, and we will be the benefactors of His transformation."},{"kind":"para","text":"There are things in this mortal body that I just absolutely hate. They are the old things that I can’t seem to get rid of. One is feeling pain. I don’t like pain. Another is feeling depressed. I hate sorrow; emotional or mental sorrow is worse than feeling physical pain in my opinion. Another is anxiety. Yet, God does a new thing in me."},{"kind":"para","text":"I know I am not where I should be in my faith, but I am not where I once was, and I’m glad that there is an obvious sign of progress when I think back at the man I was becoming before the Lord versus the man I have become WITH Him."}]},{"start":20,"end":20,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The chosen people will always have a place to rest and providence from the Lord. We discussed the differences between the chosen and the elect in our last chapter, but this is a good verse to illustrate it further. God’s chosen will always have rest. Who is chosen by the Lord? Well, it’s those He knows will come to Him. They are chosen. The elect is Jesus. The chosen will come to the elect in time."}]},{"start":21,"end":21,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The chosen need to be molded into the elect. That is how salvation works. We don’t usually accept Christ right off the bat, but if the Lord knows you are going to eventually accept Him, that means you are a chosen man, and He will mold you into His elect for when the time comes to take Christ. He forms people for an overarching purpose to be determined. That purpose is to (once again) know Him and believe Him."}]}]},{"start":22,"end":24,"title":"Weary of God","entries":[{"start":22,"end":22,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Do you feel wearied by the Lord? If I can be honest here, I have had a few times in my walk where I have felt wearied by ministry and by following the Lord. The reason I felt so weary was not because of my faith in God, but because of my work in this world. I was doing things for the wrong reasons. If you feel wearied today, it is not because your faith is a burden. Rather, if you feel weary today, it is because you are doing the right things (perhaps) for the wrong reasons. You are not doing it because you love the Lord, but rather because you feel like you HAVE to."},{"kind":"para","text":"There are a lot of preachers and pastors who are weary today, and it’s only because they have the wrong motives for their ministries. They minister because it’s their title. Honestly, that is a good way to test a minister and calling. Would you do what God wanted you to do if it was done for free? If you are not willing to put everything aside to pursue a calling even for free, you are not called to it by God. Most pastors would stop ministry altogether if they were no longer getting paid by the church. That is a sad reality. The only thing that keeps them from getting weary is a paycheck… That seems like a heavy burden to carry to me."}]},{"start":23,"end":23,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Honestly, if you think about the Israelites and the Law of Moses, it would become quite a wearisome thing to have to live by. Over time, it becomes mundane and repetitive, and I could certainly understand why they would need some sort of refreshing to continue their tradition and keeping of the law. However, that was not the way in which they were supposed to keep the law. They were supposed to keep the law out of love for the Lord, not out of necessity for their sins."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is the argument in my opinion: A man becomes weary because he has lost his love for the Lord, not because he has been too faithful. Something somewhere is off, and that needs to be addressed so you can feel refreshed in your service, rather than continuing to shoulder through it as if it will eventually go away. Being weary from the Lord’s work usually doesn’t go away if you wait long enough. It becomes more burdensome, honestly."},{"kind":"para","text":"What you need to do is take a step back, take a break, recalibrate, refocus, and spend time with the Lord simply speaking to Him and studying Him before going back to serving Him. Really, that is what He wants more than your service; He wants your presence. That is what any child of God should want as well. More than lavishing gifts on us, we should just want God’s presence. The same goes with the ministers in the church. The congregants would much rather have your presence than for you to give them things or buy them food."}]},{"start":24,"end":24,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The real problem is not with how weary we are of the Lord; the problem is with how weary the Lord is with us. We can either be a blessing to the Lord and others or a burden to the Lord and others. Honestly, I think there are far too many well-meaning Christians who are weary to the Lord rather than a blessing because they think their greatest sacrifice is service rather than presence."},{"kind":"para","text":"When we get to Heaven, I think most of the accounts people will be giving will not be based on how much good we did for humanity. Rather, I think the Lord is going to confront us and say, “How much quality time did you spend with me and with others?” I think nearly all of us are going to miss that mark entirely, and our account will look quite dismal."},{"kind":"para","text":"Seriously, if you look at the letters of the Apostles, that was the number one theme they clung to. They noted how important unity was and how important quality time together was both in the Lord and in the church. Yet, I’ve never seen a preacher preach on the necessity of spending time with each other. Rather, they preach about what actions we should be taking as members of the church. We have missed the mark…"}]}]},{"start":25,"end":28,"title":"No Sin","entries":[{"start":25,"end":25,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God has the power to literally remove your sins. It’s not that He will just forget them; He will literally take them away as if you never did it. You might say, “Well Jonathan, I am still a sinner though. I will still have some account of my unrighteousness because I am a Christian who sins.” Not according to God here in Isaiah. Apparently, your sins will be completely wiped away. He will look at your account and say, “There is no transgression here.”"},{"kind":"para","text":"Even if you were to have a heart attack in the middle of a sin you are committing, you will be forgiven only because of the elect’s sake. You will be forgiven because you have Christ. That is how the grace of God works, my friend, and it’s a wonderfully undeserving trait that the Lord has provided for everyone of His chosen. That is why He has elected Christ to be the Savior. That is what we are being saved from."}]},{"start":26,"end":26,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God wants to work with you. This verse emphasizes the importance of spending quality time with the Lord while you are here. That is what God will take account of. When we have Him as our forefront and put Him in first place in our lives, we have an advocate with the Father!"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"My little children, these things write I unto you, that ye sin not. And if any man sin, we have an advocate with the Father, Jesus Christ the righteous: And he is the propitiation for our sins: and not for ours only, but also for the sins of the whole world.","ref":"1 John 2:1-2"},{"kind":"para","text":"What a beautiful gift to mankind."}]},{"start":27,"end":27,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The world is full of sin, and mankind is born into sin, so there is nothing we can do to get us out of sin. Except the Lord has provided a way out. Remember, He will remove our sins if we turn to Him. He will completely forgive us in an instant if we would just trust Him. He has given us every reason possible to love Him, trust Him, and receive Him, but we try and make every excuse possible to forsake it."},{"kind":"para","text":"Don’t forsake it. Don’t forsake the time you get to spend with the Lord either. That is the most precious time you will ever get here on Earth. There is no wasted time when it’s spent sitting with the Lord, either by prayer or by study."}]},{"start":28,"end":28,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Jacob can be viewed as the chosen, and Israel as the elect. Even the elect, at this time, were not living right by the Lord. I believe they were still saved; they were just wayward and backslidden. They had to learn the hard way that the lifestyle they were leading was not what God wanted. They certainly will learn their lesson, and it’s obvious that they know what they are supposed to be doing because Daniel (and his friends) will be some of the people who know the Lord, yet are taken into captivity with the rest of their people. They are elect men, thrown in with the chosen simply because the majority of Israel has turned its back on God."},{"kind":"para","text":"God will take care of them, though, that is clear through the book of Daniel. He will take care of you too, if you turn to Him and trust Him. Even in the midst of captivity, you will reign with the Lord. He will provide for His children."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":9},{"start":10,"end":10},{"start":11,"end":11},{"start":12,"end":12},{"start":13,"end":13},{"start":14,"end":14},{"start":15,"end":15},{"start":16,"end":17},{"start":18,"end":18},{"start":19,"end":19},{"start":20,"end":20},{"start":21,"end":21},{"start":22,"end":22},{"start":23,"end":23},{"start":24,"end":24},{"start":25,"end":25},{"start":26,"end":26},{"start":27,"end":27},{"start":28,"end":28}],"verses":{"1":"But now thus saith the Lord that created thee, O Jacob, and he that formed thee, O Israel, Fear not: for I have redeemed thee, I have called thee by thy name; thou art mine.","2":"When thou passest through the waters, I will be with thee; and through the rivers, they shall not overflow thee: when thou walkest through the fire, thou shalt not be burned; neither shall the flame kindle upon thee.","3":"For I am the Lord thy God, the Holy One of Israel, thy Saviour: I gave Egypt for thy ransom, Ethiopia and Seba for thee.","4":"Since thou wast precious in my sight, thou hast been honourable, and I have loved thee: therefore will I give men for thee, and people for thy life.","5":"Fear not: for I am with thee: I will bring thy seed from the east, and gather thee from the west;","6":"I will say to the north, Give up; and to the south, Keep not back: bring my sons from far, and my daughters from the ends of the earth;","7":"Even every one that is called by my name: for I have created him for my glory, I have formed him; yea, I have made him.","8":"Bring forth the blind people that have eyes, and the deaf that have ears.","9":"Let all the nations be gathered together, and let the people be assembled: who among them can declare this, and shew us former things? let them bring forth their witnesses, that they may be justified: or let them hear, and say, It is truth.","10":"Ye are my witnesses, saith the Lord, and my servant whom I have chosen: that ye may know and believe me, and understand that I am he: before me there was no God formed, neither shall there be after me.","11":"I, even I, am the Lord; and beside me there is no saviour.","12":"I have declared, and have saved, and I have shewed, when there was no strange god among you: therefore ye are my witnesses, saith the Lord, that I am God.","13":"Yea, before the day was I am he; and there is none that can deliver out of my hand: I will work, and who shall let it?","14":"Thus saith the Lord, your redeemer, the Holy One of Israel; For your sake I have sent to Babylon, and have brought down all their nobles, and the Chaldeans, whose cry is in the ships.","15":"I am the Lord, your Holy One, the creator of Israel, your King.","16":"Thus saith the Lord, which maketh a way in the sea, and a path in the mighty waters;","17":"Which bringeth forth the chariot and horse, the army and the power; they shall lie down together, they shall not rise: they are extinct, they are quenched as tow.","18":"Remember ye not the former things, neither consider the things of old.","19":"Behold, I will do a new thing; now it shall spring forth; shall ye not know it? I will even make a way in the wilderness, and rivers in the desert.","20":"The beast of the field shall honour me, the dragons and the owls: because I give waters in the wilderness, and rivers in the desert, to give drink to my people, my chosen.","21":"This people have I formed for myself; they shall shew forth my praise.","22":"But thou hast not called upon me, O Jacob; but thou hast been weary of me, O Israel.","23":"Thou hast not brought me the small cattle of thy burnt offerings; neither hast thou honoured me with thy sacrifices. I have not caused thee to serve with an offering, nor wearied thee with incense.","24":"Thou hast bought me no sweet cane with money, neither hast thou filled me with the fat of thy sacrifices: but thou hast made me to serve with thy sins, thou hast wearied me with thine iniquities.","25":"I, even I, am he that blotteth out thy transgressions for mine own sake, and will not remember thy sins.","26":"Put me in remembrance: let us plead together: declare thou, that thou mayest be justified.","27":"Thy first father hath sinned, and thy teachers have transgressed against me.","28":"Therefore I have profaned the princes of the sanctuary, and have given Jacob to the curse, and Israel to reproaches."}},
    "44": {"chapter":44,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: In our last chapter, God spoke specifically about the importance and prominence of His children being under His authority. As if it wasn't already obvious enough for us (and for them in Jerusalem), God wants His children to be set apart from the rest of the world, and so He will do things in this life to mold us into that."},{"kind":"para","text":"In this chapter, we see more of God's molding taking place. We read about God's Spirit being given, and end this chapter on what idols (that we make with our own hands) will really do for us. We have a choice to place our faith into today. We can choose to trust God, or we can choose to trust our own hands. However, I recognize that it's usually my own hands that let me down more than anyone elses..."}],"previously":["In our last chapter, God spoke specifically about the importance and prominence of His children being under His authority. As if it wasn’t already obvious enough for us (and for them in Jerusalem), God wants His children to be set apart from the rest of the world, and so He will do things in this life to mold us into that. In this chapter, we see more of God’s molding taking place. We read about God’s Spirit being given, and we end this chapter on what idols (that we make with our own hands) will really do for us. We have a choice to place our faith into today. We can choose to trust God, or we can choose to trust our own hands. However, I recognize that it’s usually my own hands that let me down more than anyone else’s…"],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":5,"title":"The Spirit of God","entries":[{"start":1,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There are a great many things that we rightfully have a reason to fear, but when the Lord tells us to “fear not,” He has a reason for it. They are about to head into captivity. They are about to be completely taken away from their homeland and used as slaves in someone else’s land. They are going to lose it all, and God tells them to “fear not”? It’s a hard thing to listen to the Lord’s “fear nots” in scripture."},{"kind":"para","text":"God is telling Israel not to fear the things that are coming to pass because God knows the ultimate purpose. I’m glad He doesn’t just say “Don’t fear” and then not tell you WHY you shouldn’t fear. Rather, He explains His purpose over and over again. The main purpose for them not to fear is because of Christ, who has been spoken about multiple times throughout this book of the Bible, and He will be spoken about more to come. The next verse gives the illustration of Christ:"}]},{"start":3,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God’s Spirit is going to be poured out on His people, and that is obviously evident today. Those who have Christ possess the Spirit of Christ, which gives us the power to “fear not.” He has provided us with a way to escape and a form of safety through His Spirit alone. However, there are people today who have “abused” that Spirit for personal gain. They claim to be healers, prophets, and all sorts of Holy Spirit warriors, but in reality, they just hide behind the Holy Spirit and act a part. Believers are not in control of the Holy Spirit! I want to get that through everyone’s heads ahead of time."},{"kind":"para","text":"When we study the book of Acts, we will see the Holy Spirit do quite a great deal for the believers, but you will recognize that not a single person dictates what the Holy Spirit will do. They all just accept the Holy Spirit’s moving. If you have the Holy Spirit of God, you will notice that He gives you callings and leads you to people and ways that you never thought you would meet or go down. He gives you boldness and peace that you don’t understand to do things that you should be worried about doing. If He doesn’t provide peace, you probably shouldn’t do it. The Holy Spirit will be the guide to God’s elect."},{"kind":"para","text":"Why? Well, it’s because as an “elect” person, we will still make wrong decisions. That is why being “elect” doesn’t mean what the Calvinists think it means. The Holy Spirit still needs to guide us even if we are saved because we will always choose to go the opposite way of the Lord. The Spirit is there to remind us and point us back into the right direction. We certainly can ignore the Spirit, but we can’t do it comfortably if we truly are children of God."}]},{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The Spirit of God is what places us under the authority and family of the Lord. It is the only reason we can say, “We belong to the Godly lineage.” I can’t say I’m a Jew, but I CAN say I am a child of God. Sadly, there are many Jews who cannot say they are God’s children. They live in the Old Testament and shun God’s name, thinking it’s still their “good works” that get them to Heaven. That has never been the way it has worked, and as we have studied, we have recognized that God calls for relationship more than sacrifice, over and over again."},{"kind":"para","text":"If it was just sacrifice and physical works, Israel would have never been involved with captivity to begin with. In fact, Moses wouldn’t have had to say anything at all about a possible captivity if the law is what kept them with the Lord. Rather, he mentions the necessity to love the Lord again and again, with all their heart, soul, and mind, and Jesus reminds the people of this as well in the gospels."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And thou shalt love the LORD thy God with all thine heart, and with all thy soul, and with all thy might.","ref":"Deuteronomy 6:5"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Jesus said unto him, Thou shalt love the Lord thy God with all thy heart, and with all thy soul, and with all thy mind.","ref":"Matthew 22:37"},{"kind":"para","text":"And yet, the problem still remains in religious circles, including the Jewish ones. People still try to work their way to the Lord and reject the simplicity of the Gospel message. They don’t believe in the love of God because they have only put their trust in the law of God. God will always just be a judge in their eyes until they learn God’s grace and position for them. I can faithfully say that I am a child of God only because I know that Jesus gave me the privilege to do it."}]}]},{"start":6,"end":8,"title":"No Other God","entries":[{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This has already been mentioned quite a few times. Why would God keep bringing this up? Well, it seems that the world has a problem with idols. Even today, as I’ve already mentioned before, there are people who believe in a “Mother God.” They think this god has to be included in the family in order for Jesus to be born, completely getting rid of the concept of Mary. They worship a false god to make sense of their religious viewpoint."},{"kind":"para","text":"Then you have people who worship Mary for a whole different reason. But the thing that God reminds all of us is that He (alone) is the only one that is worth the worship. If Mary was a figure that we had to worship, He would have made that clear from the beginning of scripture. Same with saints, same with angels, same with a “mother” god. But instead, He keeps repeating the fact that He is the only God that exists, and the only one that can be rightfully worshipped."},{"kind":"para","text":"The gospel message, honestly, is that plain and clear. There’s only one God, and you should love Him with everything you have."}]},{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God knows and sees all things, even before they happen. There is no one else in history who can predict the future so perfectly. There is no one who can prove salvation and righteousness like the Lord. The Lord alone is the standard of all perfect and righteous actions and devices. We are not. We might try to take the credit, but we use His righteousness to make any good thing here on Earth. It’s His judgments we base ours off of, and it’s His Spirit that leads us in the way we should go. We know what is good only because God’s Spirit knows what is good."},{"kind":"para","text":"Most of us would not consider murder to be something good. Rather, feeding the poor is something that we deem as “good.” Yet, we have plenty of people who deem murder as good today and feeding the poor as a wasted effort. Those people who have this warped thought process are unsaved people, that’s to be sure. They don’t have the mind of God or of His Spirit. They have their own version of righteousness, and that is what gets them into situations like the Israelites are facing here. Honestly, they are not doing anything new. But the Lord is doing something new. He is going to give His Spirit to His children so they can always be guided by His righteousness and goodness."}]},{"start":8,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Don’t forget, He is the only God. When He makes a promise in scripture, He is the only one to blame for whether or not it’s kept. If you feel like God has wronged you, you don’t go to the church and curse them out. If God has wronged you, and you want to air your concerns to Him, He has ears to hear. Bring your burdens to Him, and He will listen. Whether atheist or believer, it doesn’t matter; God can take your concerns."},{"kind":"para","text":"Honestly, I think that is why there are any sort of atheists today. It’s not because they don’t believe in God; it’s because God didn’t show up for them when they needed Him the most. How that might have looked, I can’t tell you, but I know that God shows up in some fashion to any problem that we call to Him for. We just want Him to work according to our own righteousness and thoughts, rather than Him doing what He knows is right."}]}]},{"start":9,"end":11,"title":"Serving Masters","entries":[{"start":9,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Honestly, you can evaluate people’s idols today and ask them the same question: Do their idols actually profit them anything? Will they stand up for them in the end? Will their acclaimed idols save them from anything? Their idols don’t even know who they are or care that they exist. Be careful idolizing anything on this Earth."},{"kind":"para","text":"People are weak and feeble, and they will abuse and misuse those around them to get themselves on top. Those are not the kinds of people you want to idolize. No, the Lord alone is worthy to be praised and worshipped, because He will not misuse you. He will not abuse you. The world will abuse you, but the Lord will prosper you."}]},{"start":11,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I have, especially lately, seen droves of people putting their trust into the wrong things. People depend on and respect the position of president in our country to the highest extremes. There are individuals who truly believe their president can do no wrong. Additionally, there are people who believe their government has their best interest at heart. Perhaps we can bring it home to you. There are many people who think very highly of their own pastor, preacher, teacher, or boss in their work and jobs. There are far too many willing participants who would do anything for their church leaders. Yet, I’ve never met a church leader who will not, in some way (usually purposely from my experience), let you down. You are serving the wrong person if you are let down by your leader (I’m preaching to myself here)."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And whatsoever ye do, do it heartily, as to the Lord, and not unto men;","ref":"Colossians 3:23"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For do I now persuade men, or God? or do I seek to please men? for if I yet pleased men, I should not be the servant of Christ.","ref":"Galatians 1:10"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For they loved the praise of men more than the praise of God.","ref":"John 12:43"},{"kind":"para","text":"Perhaps we should put it to the test. When your pastor makes a mistake, is your first action to forgive, or to address the mistake? If it’s not to address the mistake, you are putting too much trust in your pastor. Good leaders can take critical objections to their deeds and wrongdoings and are willing to examine themselves to see if they are in the right spirit."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Examine yourselves, whether ye be in the faith; prove your own selves. Know ye not your own selves, how that Jesus Christ is in you, except ye be reprobates?","ref":"2 Corinthians 13:5"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For if a man think himself to be something, when he is nothing, he deceiveth himself.","ref":"Galatians 6:3"},{"kind":"para","text":"Faulty leaders will often pass the blame back onto you and call it a “you” problem. Either way, we should not be serving our church leaders; we should be serving the Lord alone if we are going to do anything right."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"When a man's ways please the LORD, he maketh even his enemies to be at peace with him.","ref":"Proverbs 16:7"},{"kind":"para","text":"Maybe that is what we should be testing. Do those who wrong you, including your church leaders, feel like they are missing out when you serve the Lord? Do they wonder what it is about you that keeps you going? I presently need growth in this area, to be sure, but I know that the Lord is working on me here to see what I can do for HIS service (not my church’s)."}]}]},{"start":12,"end":17,"title":"Worshipping Residue","entries":[{"start":12,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Do you see how much work you put in for your idols? The idols don’t give you anything in return for that work either. Isaiah won’t stop just at the smiths either. We will see the amount of work that each person might put in for their fake gods. Perhaps it’s a little different in our age. There are still people making their own gods, that is to be sure, but they are not as common as the people who worship money. You put more work in for your money than your money can put in for you, and you feel tired and empty when everything is said and done. Money is a poor master because it won’t bring you anything truly fulfilling."},{"kind":"para","text":"Look to Elon Musk today. The richest man in the world is currently trying to help our government officials stop wasting money. Why? Is it because he personally gets something out of this? Will he get more money? Perhaps he will. But I believe, based on interviews from his past and the way in which he handles himself, he’s doing it to try and help the American citizens. Not because he truly desires to make everyone else rich, but because he already has all the money in the world and that hasn’t filled his longings. He is thinking, no doubt, that if he serves and helps his country in this way, it will make him feel good for his efforts. The truth is, it will probably make him feel really good to give failed money back to the people who have spent it on their own government for no reason. But that good feeling won’t last forever. He will have to try and fill it with something else. That something else, to Elon Musk anyway, is trying to go to Mars. Once that happens, he will still feel empty. Nothing will ever be fulfilling without the Lord. We know this to be true because of everything that Solomon says about riches in Ecclesiastes. It is all meaningless without the Lord providing it. These idols that are being worked on will not provide anything fulfilling. They will just rob you as you try and fill yourselves with their purpose."}]},{"start":13,"end":15,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Carpentry is a little more my speed. I can understand this better than smithing. God makes a very important point here. The idols are a lot of work to make, and never pay off to the idolizer, and in the end, you are just stuck with the idols’ residue."},{"kind":"para","text":"When I worked in carpentry, we had a lot of sawdust flying everywhere. About once a month, I was tasked with sweeping up the sawdust in the shop and putting it into bags (including the sawdust that is collected inside the machines we used). It took a couple of hours to sweep up and gather all the dust. I’d put it in garbage bags, and you know what we would do with them? We’d throw them away. They couldn’t be used for anything else."},{"kind":"para","text":"The work to plant trees, wait for them to grow, chop them down, and then cut them up for fire and food was enough work. Add false worship to the list, and you are just adding extra work. They had one use, and the main use wasn’t for what all that hard work amounted to. Their use was to burn the leftover pieces to keep themselves warm and cozy and to cook their own meals. At the end of the day, they are still laboring for their false gods. The Lord doesn’t ever call us to labor; He continuously calls His children to rest."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And he said, My presence shall go with thee, and I will give thee rest.","ref":"Exodus 33:14"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Rest in the LORD, and wait patiently for him: fret not thyself because of him who prospereth in his way, because of the man who bringeth wicked devices to pass.","ref":"Psalm 37:7"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Take my yoke upon you, and learn of me; for I am meek and lowly in heart: and ye shall find rest unto your souls.","ref":"Matthew 11:29"},{"kind":"para","text":"Church work should be a restful work. Yet (once again) I have yet to meet a leader who doesn't do things chaotically and sporadically. Nothing is ever done decently and in order under most church leaders today."}]},{"start":16,"end":17,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Look at this for a second: The residue is for false worship, and the main parts of the wood are for providence. The residue, remember, is the part that we usually threw away when I worked in carpentry. Not the world. They found value in the residue and worshipped it. That is really all you are left with when you put your trust in anything but the Lord. That’s all money really is. It’s wood residue."}]}]},{"start":18,"end":20,"title":"Whispering Idols","entries":[{"start":18,"end":18,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Which one? The idol, or the idolizer? Well, both honestly. God has shut the eyes and hearts of those who desire to worship anything but Him. They won’t understand the Lord’s ways until they are willing to let go of their own ways. God’s ways are unreachable to them."},{"kind":"para","text":"They claim to be experts in God’s ways and try to prove Christians wrong all the time, but they never really understand His ways. How could they when they only want to live for their wood residue?"}]},{"start":19,"end":19,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"False worship and false idols are sinful ways of bending to the will of your environment rather than bending to the will of logic. We have a whole cult of religions today that believe in pantheism. God is just a force that is around them and in all things, rather than a creator and King of all things. God is not in the wind and storms; He is the still small voice."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And he said, Go forth, and stand upon the mount before the LORD. And, behold, the LORD passed by, and a great and strong wind rent the mountains, and brake in pieces the rocks before the LORD; but the LORD was not in the wind: and after the wind an earthquake; but the LORD was not in the earthquake: And after the earthquake a fire; but the LORD was not in the fire: and after the fire a still small voice.","ref":"1 Kings 19:11-12"},{"kind":"para","text":"God speaks to you through His Word, not through the wind or through the trees. God is personable, not a fluke force. He answers directly, not through His creation. Yet, when we worship our money, or we worship the trees, or we worship this Earth, we are bending to the will and power of the wind and forces that are obviously not worthy to be worshipped."},{"kind":"para","text":"If you’ve ever lived in a windy place, you know the desire to stay out of it as much as possible. I have grown to hate the wind. I know the Lord has made it for a purpose, but I can’t stand it out here. It gets so crazy that there are great dust storms that roll through and actually cause a lot of damage. But I love the Lord who made the wind, and so I respect that He has a purpose for it whether I like it or not. However, I won’t worship the wind. There is no way I can worship it because it has no eyes, or brains, or heart, or hearing. It’s just a force that blows (pardon my pun)."}]},{"start":20,"end":20,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I believe false idols whisper too. They just whisper lies. The Lord is a still small voice that whispers peace. God’s voice says, “You have me, so you have enough.” Idols’ voices say, “You need more, I am not enough.” You’ll always be pursuing after false idols if you listen to their lies. God provides rest if you would listen to His truth."}]}]},{"start":21,"end":23,"title":"The Redeemed","entries":[{"start":21,"end":22,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God has been molding these people for a very long time. He has the power and authority to destroy them all for their many sins that have built up over time. Instead, He is looking to forgive them. He is looking to continue to mold them. He wants them to prosper for Him, and that can’t happen if they are all dead and done away with."},{"kind":"para","text":"He doesn’t look back at their past sins and say, “Because your grandfathers have done this and that, I will wipe you out.” Rather, He says, “Because YOU have not turned to me, I will mold you.” These people were going to be shaped for God’s intended purpose. They were malleable. No other nation would be as willing as Israel. So He is going to put them in their proper place in His proper timing."}]},{"start":23,"end":23,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Again, Isaiah is using present terms. God has not technically redeemed Israel yet. They are still extremely wayward. But the Lord WILL redeem them in time. That is a promise that is going to be kept. The people of Israel will be back in their homeland, and the Lord Jesus Christ is going to walk among them and (once again) mold these people, and then sacrifice Himself on the cross to give the world full access to God’s throne."},{"kind":"para","text":"No idol would do that for you. Your money will not be enough to give you access to God’s throne of grace and mercy. No. Only your humility will get you there. God is not looking for the elected today. You might pride yourself as being “the elected,” but what God really wants is for you to be the “redeemed.” Redemption is all that matters to your soul’s path in this life, and if we are looking to be “elected” by the Lord, we must get our hopes down for it. May we seek redemption. May we seek to be purchased out of our slavery and into His service."}]}]},{"start":24,"end":28,"title":"Everything We Need","entries":[{"start":24,"end":28,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There’s obviously a lot to unpack here. These verses illustrate what God is more than capable of doing, and the proof is that He has done it before. He is a redeemer, a creator, and a sustainer. He is a judge, a changer, and a prover. He is a truth bearer, a message giver, and a healer. He is a director, a provider, and a Savior. God is quite a great deal of things, but these are the things that He wants to be for His people."},{"kind":"para","text":"He wants to be their all-in-all so that no one will ever cry for want. He wants those who depend on Him to be taken care of by Him. He loves us so much that He wants to be everything we need, so we might not ever have to worry about those things again. God is, honestly, too good for us. We are certainly undeserving. And these are just a few things the Lord wants to give His children. Throughout His Word, we see that God is a lot more than just this list prescribed here. He is everything we need, and all we need. No idol can do that for you."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":10},{"start":11,"end":11},{"start":12,"end":12},{"start":13,"end":15},{"start":16,"end":17},{"start":18,"end":18},{"start":19,"end":19},{"start":20,"end":20},{"start":21,"end":22},{"start":23,"end":23},{"start":24,"end":28}],"verses":{"1":"Yet now hear, O Jacob my servant; and Israel, whom I have chosen:","2":"Thus saith the Lord that made thee, and formed thee from the womb, which will help thee; Fear not, O Jacob, my servant; and thou, Jesurun, whom I have chosen.","3":"For I will pour water upon him that is thirsty, and floods upon the dry ground: I will pour my spirit upon thy seed, and my blessing upon thine offspring:","4":"And they shall spring up as among the grass, as willows by the water courses.","5":"One shall say, I am the Lord's; and another shall call himself by the name of Jacob; and another shall subscribe with his hand unto the Lord, and surname himself by the name of Israel.","6":"Thus saith the Lord the King of Israel, and his redeemer the Lord of hosts; I am the first, and I am the last; and beside me there is no God.","7":"And who, as I, shall call, and shall declare it, and set it in order for me, since I appointed the ancient people? and the things that are coming, and shall come, let them shew unto them.","8":"Fear ye not, neither be afraid: have not I told thee from that time, and have declared it? ye are even my witnesses. Is there a God beside me? yea, there is no God; I know not any.","9":"They that make a graven image are all of them vanity; and their delectable things shall not profit; and they are their own witnesses; they see not, nor know; that they may be ashamed.","10":"Who hath formed a god, or molten a graven image that is profitable for nothing?","11":"Behold, all his fellows shall be ashamed: and the workmen, they are of men: let them all be gathered together, let them stand up; yet they shall fear, and they shall be ashamed together.","12":"The smith with the tongs both worketh in the coals, and fashioneth it with hammers, and worketh it with the strength of his arms: yea, he is hungry, and his strength faileth: he drinketh no water, and is faint.","13":"The carpenter stretcheth out his rule; he marketh it out with a line; he fitteth it with planes, and he marketh it out with the compass, and maketh it after the figure of a man, according to the beauty of a man; that it may remain in the house.","14":"He heweth him down cedars, and taketh the cypress and the oak, which he strengtheneth for himself among the trees of the forest: he planteth an ash, and the rain doth nourish it.","15":"Then shall it be for a man to burn: for he will take thereof, and warm himself; yea, he kindleth it, and baketh bread; yea, he maketh a god, and worshippeth it; he maketh it a graven image, and falleth down thereto.","16":"He burneth part thereof in the fire; with part thereof he eateth flesh; he roasteth roast, and is satisfied: yea, he warmeth himself, and saith, Aha, I am warm, I have seen the fire:","17":"And the residue thereof he maketh a god, even his graven image: he falleth down unto it, and worshippeth it, and prayeth unto it, and saith, Deliver me; for thou art my god.","18":"They have not known nor understood: for he hath shut their eyes, that they cannot see; and their hearts, that they cannot understand.","19":"And none considereth in his heart, neither is there knowledge nor understanding to say, I have burned part of it in the fire; yea, also I have baked bread upon the coals thereof; I have roasted flesh, and eaten it: and shall I make the residue thereof an abomination? shall I fall down to the stock of a tree?","20":"He feedeth on ashes: a deceived heart hath turned him aside, that he cannot deliver his soul, nor say, Is there not a lie in my right hand?","21":"Remember these, O Jacob and Israel; for thou art my servant: I have formed thee; thou art my servant: O Israel, thou shalt not be forgotten of me.","22":"I have blotted out, as a thick cloud, thy transgressions, and, as a cloud, thy sins: return unto me; for I have redeemed thee.","23":"Sing, O ye heavens; for the Lord hath done it: shout, ye lower parts of the earth: break forth into singing, ye mountains, O forest, and every tree therein: for the Lord hath redeemed Jacob, and glorified himself in Israel.","24":"Thus saith the Lord, thy redeemer, and he that formed thee from the womb, I am the Lord that maketh all things; that stretcheth forth the heavens alone; that spreadeth abroad the earth by myself;","25":"That frustrateth the tokens of the liars, and maketh diviners mad; that turneth wise men backward, and maketh their knowledge foolish;","26":"That confirmeth the word of his servant, and performeth the counsel of his messengers; that saith to Jerusalem, Thou shalt be inhabited; and to the cities of Judah, Ye shall be built, and I will raise up the decayed places thereof:","27":"That saith to the deep, Be dry, and I will dry up thy rivers:","28":"That saith of Cyrus, He is my shepherd, and shall perform all my pleasure: even saying to Jerusalem, Thou shalt be built; and to the temple, Thy foundation shall be laid."}},
    "45": {"chapter":45,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: In our last chapter, the Lord revealed His future promise of His Spirit which will be gifted to His children who turn to Him. He also spoke about the negative impacts worshipping false idols will lead His people to. Obviously it leads to nothing valuable, and it leaves you wanting more, and will never fulfil you. Only GOD will fulfil His creation. He has sense the beginning, and He still will today."},{"kind":"para","text":"In this chapter, we get quite an amazing prophecy about a man named Cyrus. Honestly, I couldn't find too much information on this man. He is something astounding, and a power to be reckoned with during his reign, yet I think because he was so involved with the Lord that he didn't find reason to gloat or pride himself with his reign and power. That is why God will greatly use him (among other reasons we will get to in this chapter)."}],"previously":["In our last chapter, the Lord revealed His future promise of His Spirit, which will be gifted to His children who turn to Him. He also spoke about the negative impacts worshipping false idols will lead His people to. Obviously, it leads to nothing valuable, leaves you wanting more, and will never fulfill you. Only God will fulfill His creation. He has since the beginning, and He still will today. In this chapter, we get quite an amazing prophecy about a man named Cyrus. Honestly, I couldn’t find too much information on this man. He is something astounding and a power to be reckoned with during his reign. Yet, I think because he was so involved with the Lord, he didn’t find reason to gloat or pride himself with his reign and power. That is why God will greatly use him (among other reasons we will get to in this chapter)."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":7,"title":"Accuracy of Prophecy","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Now, before we continue, you might be asking \"Who in the world is Cyrus?” Perhaps you saw his name mentioned in the last chapter. The last verse speaks about him;"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"That saith of Cyrus, He is my shepherd, and shall perform all my pleasure: even saying to Jerusalem, Thou shalt be built; and to the temple, Thy foundation shall be laid.","ref":"Isaiah 44:28"},{"kind":"para","text":"I purposely didn’t speak about him because the Lord spends a great deal of time prophecying about him in this chapter. Based on what Isaiah is writing here, you’d think that this Cyrus fellow is a good, upright, righteous, Godly Israelite who will rescue his people. “Cyrus” means “Possess thou the furnace.” It doesn’t sound like a very upright name. In fact, it’s not even a Jewish name. He will be the king of Persia and will be responsible for taking over Babylon when the time comes, making it possible for the Israelites to return to Jerusalem after their exile. This (supposedly) is written around 150-200 years before Cyrus is even in power. That’s an amazing prophecy that will be literally fulfilled. The crazier part is that God will use a pagan king to do His work better than He can use His own children to do His work."},{"kind":"para","text":"Obviously, everything that Isaiah has made mention of already throughout this book has been for a literal time. But this prophecy is going to be used to drive the nail of prophecy further into the picture. When Cyrus comes on the scene (two hundred years later), the Israelites will have to bring this book back to remembrance, and it should certainly (and will certainly) spark a revival of faith for God’s people. Too bad the embers of revival don’t last forever. Honestly, I don’t think revival fire ever lasts very long. A few years max, if I can be honest."},{"kind":"para","text":"Furthermore, if Isaiah is right about this Cyrus fellow (and he certainly is), the Israelites can trust that Isaiah is one hundred percent accurate about the Savior being born of a virgin and His ultimate crucifixion (which will be talked about in Isaiah 53). This is further proof (specifically to the Jews) that Jesus is actually the Christ, according to Isaiah’s prophecy. If they can’t take Isaiah’s prophecy as literal for Jesus, then they certainly shouldn’t take it literal for Cyrus, and yet the Jews know that Cyrus was a very real person who did exactly what God says he would do. Furthermore, it’s a testament to the Jews (and Christians) as to the salvation belonging to the world, not just the Jews alone. God saves EVERYONE, yet there are a lot of people who will reject it even with all the proof at their disposal. Ask any Gentile believer today if they are truly saved, and if they truly are saved, they will tell you the truth of their salvation only through Jesus Christ alone."}]},{"start":2,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Cyrus will be a man greatly used by God. It’s such a shame that there is not enough information about this man other than at his tomb. He is a man used by God, that is to be sure. Why preachers don’t preach more about this, I can’t say. It’s quite an exciting bit of history and information that is very useful in leading up to the Savior."},{"kind":"para","text":"Cyrus had a lot of faith in the Lord to do the things that God is ultimately going to call Him to do. He will be a world power at a point in history, and yet there will be very little boasting about him except in scripture. God boasts of this man right here, and he will do a very good thing for God’s children that (honestly) should have made them think a little higher about God’s salvation. But sinners will sin, so…"}]},{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"He has chosen a great many people today who don’t know Him. But they will. They won’t be able to deny the Lord any longer. They won’t be able to continue to reject God after the amazing salvation He is going to provide for His people, even through this great man of faith, further sealing the deal through Jesus Christ."}]},{"start":5,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"May we not forget now that God is doing this by His own power, and there is nothing else dictating His actions. People might ask why this person or that person is saved. They might ask why the Lord has chosen the Israelites. They might ask why He will eventually end the entire world and life as we know it. They might ask why He put the tree of the knowledge of good and evil in the garden. They might ask why He even created Satan to begin with. They might ask why He allows such evil and sin in this world. They might ask why He is still waiting for His judgment and second coming. They might ask why He doesn’t prove Himself with more obvious signs. They might ask why He has chosen very specific things as “sins” on this Earth."},{"kind":"para","text":"They might ask a great deal of things about the Lord (all of which has been answered one way or another throughout history, and even in this very commentary you are holding), but the real bottom line answer is it’s because He is the Lord, and there is none else, there is no God beside Him. He knows what to do, and He always does what is right. Whether we know what He does things or not, doesn’t matter. He has the right to literally do whatever He wants to if He is God."}]},{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"And some will say, “So we can blame God for the evil here on Earth,” and to that I say, “Yes.” God creates evil. He says it Himself right here. He also created darkness. There’s a purpose for both of those things."},{"kind":"para","text":"If we just look at evil alone, we will see that evil has a purpose of balance. It has a necessity to show us what is good. Without evil, we wouldn’t be able to find peace. Without sadness, we would have no reason to rejoice. Without suffering, we wouldn’t know what it’s like to be at ease. Without hurt, we wouldn’t need healing. Without sin, we wouldn’t need a Savior. Without hate, we wouldn’t grow in love."},{"kind":"para","text":"You see what darkness brings us if we use it correctly? It brings us to the light. It brings us to what is good and right. It trains our conscience. That is why evil and darkness are necessary in our world today."}]}]},{"start":8,"end":8,"title":"Heaven Today","entries":[{"start":8,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"It’s such a beautiful verse labeled here. We should want Heaven to be here. We should want righteousness to reign. We should desire the world to see and know salvation. I, personally, want nothing more than for the love of God to shine forth into this world. Sadly, we are not going to get that when there is a very large group of people who are just plain evil. They don’t see the evil in this world as a means to grow correctly. They hold to the evil, and they shun the light, clinging to darkness so tightly that they attack anyone who tries to show them a better way."},{"kind":"para","text":"I think that is why religions are so popular. They help you cling to your darkness rather than teach you how to live in the light. I can understand it honestly. I used to love my darkness too. I lived there for so long, and I didn’t ever see a way out of it. I just had to be okay with letting it rule me from time to time. It certainly did until Jesus revealed His salvation to me. The light burned for a moment, but I realized that I liked the light more. Now the Lord trains me to walk in light rather than darkness, and that is His goal for every person in this world."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But if we walk in the light, as he is in the light, we have fellowship one with another, and the blood of Jesus Christ his Son cleanseth us from all sin.","ref":"1 John 1:7"},{"kind":"para","text":"We have the ability to walk in the middle of darkness, as if Heaven has actually come down to Earth. We have the freedom, privilege and right to live as if we are in Heaven early. We don't have to wait to get there before living like we belong."}]}]},{"start":9,"end":10,"title":"Can We Question God?","entries":[{"start":9,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I question the Lord’s choices quite a bit if I can be honest here. He does a lot of things that make me wonder and worry. Do I have the right to question Him? Well, according to Isaiah, yes. Isaiah is not saying that we can’t question God’s process. He is, however, saying that we cannot fight against it. We can’t “strive” with the Lord. We must, rather, thrive by God’s choices for us."},{"kind":"para","text":"We have the right, as potsherds, to ask why we are being fashioned in that way. However, we don’t have the right to reject God’s directives and leading in our lives. He has the right to make whatever He wants with us, and we have the necessity to accept that He knows what He’s doing when He makes us."}]}]},{"start":11,"end":13,"title":"God's Creation","entries":[{"start":11,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Now we have a direction command from God to question Him. He tells the Israelites, “Ask me what is going to happen.” He knows what will come next, and if we are uncertain about the direction, He is the best person to ask. He, however, is not a person we can combat with. We will certainly lose every time we try to prevent the Lord from doing what He wants to do with us."}]},{"start":12,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God didn’t create everything by accident. We might have read the beginning of scripture where Moses says, “God created the Heaven and the Earth,” and thought, “Boy, that seems too simple. There needs to be more here.” I know there is a whole slew of men today trying to prove Genesis wrong. If they are successful at proving Genesis wrong (which is impossible, for no man has successfully proven any part of scripture wrong), they would also have to prove God wrong by His own words here in Isaiah. And again in the New Testament:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For by him were all things created, that are in heaven, and that are in earth, visible and invisible, whether they be thrones, or dominions, or principalities, or powers: all things were created by him, and for him:","ref":"Colossians 1:16"},{"kind":"para","text":"And again at the end times:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And I saw a new heaven and a new earth: for the first heaven and the first earth were passed away; and there was no more sea.","ref":"Revelation 21:1"},{"kind":"para","text":"It would take generations of research and study from people to try and prove one verse wrong, let alone every verse of the Bible. Yet, we have no generation who can do it, and no generation ever will. If God Himself tells us that He made the Earth, then I would be extremely foolish to take everyone else’s word for it."},{"kind":"para","text":"Actually, I’ve seen this happen in every sort of art form. I’ve heard songs that I’ve really enjoyed and have shared them with others who think they know everything about music. They claim a specific thing about them or the song that is supposed to be true. I look it up from the artist who wrote the song, and it’s a completely different story than what my friend told me. I have a choice to either trust my friend’s version of it or trust the artist’s version of it. It would be unwise of me to trust anyone other than the person who created it as to the interpretation of it. Yet that is what we do with the world. We trust everyone else’s theories and ideas on it over what God (the Creator) says."}]},{"start":13,"end":13,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Cyrus will do it. All of this will be true of Cyrus. He will have no other reason to do it other than to please God. He has everything at his fingertips, and by all means, there is absolutely no reason for Cyrus to do this, other than he is being directed by a much higher power than himself or the riches he can obtain on this Earth. In fact, by giving up the Israelites, it would seem he is losing more than he’s gaining. But that is what the Lord says will happen, and by all means, that is what the Lord is going to do."}]}]},{"start":14,"end":17,"title":"World Without End","entries":[{"start":14,"end":14,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"According to this passage, Israel will eventually be the world power. Whether literal or not, I could not say. Though I am under the impression (once again) that prophecies are three-fold. So it is likely that the Lord is still not done with Israel. They will become a power much bigger than they ever have been. Honestly, the power belongs to the Lord. That is where God is driving this nation. So the world power, in time, will be God over everything. He will be the world power, and it will be due to His children lifting Him back to where He belongs and shunning any other powers that try to overthrow Him. That will be due to the church being where they are supposed to be. The state of the church today, however, is much like Israel. We have fallen enormously away from keeping God first and presenting Him as our power and director. It’s usually the pastors that put themselves first. God will deal with that in time."}]},{"start":15,"end":15,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God isn't \"hiding\" in the sense that He doesn't want to be seen. Rather He is holding back His presence because of His power and holiness. If He revealed His power, the world is over."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And what is the exceeding greatness of his power to us-ward who believe, according to the working of his mighty power, Which he wrought in Christ, when he raised him from the dead, and set him at his own right hand in the heavenly places, Far above all principality, and power, and might, and dominion, and every name that is named, not only in this world, but also in that which is to come:","ref":"Ephesians 1:19-21"},{"kind":"para","text":"If He revealed His face, your life is over."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And he said, Thou canst not see my face: for there shall no man see me, and live.","ref":"Exodus 33:20"},{"kind":"para","text":"In the same essence, He has given us His presence and power through another means. A means we are able to handle. The Holy Spirit is the presence of God. Jesus Christ is the face of God. He has proven Himself multiple times to us, and we are too stiff-necked to accept Him."}]},{"start":16,"end":16,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"A life that is led by your idols (i.e. money) is a life of confusion. God is not the author of that life."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For God is not the author of confusion, but of peace, as in all churches of the saints.","ref":"1 Corinthians 14:33"},{"kind":"para","text":"Rather God gives us a better life:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For God hath not given us the spirit of fear; but of power, and of love, and of a sound mind.","ref":"2 Timothy 1:7"},{"kind":"para","text":"That is the life that is promised to the believer, not the nonbeliever."}]},{"start":17,"end":17,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The believer has a \"world without end.” The nonbeliever has an end to his world."}]}]},{"start":18,"end":19,"title":"God Gave Creation","entries":[{"start":18,"end":18,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Better than just saying, “God created Earth, and He created everything in it,” we should say, “God created the Earth specifically FOR creation.” He created Earth for us. He doesn’t need a place to dwell because He already has one. He wants us to enjoy His creation. It’s a beautiful thing honestly. There is a lot on this Earth that can bring us joy."},{"kind":"para","text":"I feel joy when I watch TV. I feel joy when I rest on a nice, comfortable bed. I feel joy when I spend time with friends and family. I feel joy when I have coffee or energy drinks. I feel joy eating fruit. I feel joy looking at nature, hiking, planting flowers and trees. I feel joy watching the rain and bundling up during the cold. I even feel joy watching birds and feeding fish. There is plenty on this Earth to enjoy."},{"kind":"para","text":"Sin, however, causes all the joyous things of God to become unbearable. We are sinners. We ruin the good things of God. But God wants to redeem the good things we ruin. He wants to change everything here back to its intended purpose. That is a great way to view the Lord and find joy in this world."}]},{"start":19,"end":19,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God always speaks the truth. He always reveals the truth. He always proves Himself, and He always makes His Word loud, clear, and obvious. God's Word will always be heard through every generation for all of eternity."}]}]},{"start":20,"end":25,"title":"A Justifier","entries":[{"start":20,"end":20,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God calls the world away from their idols. He calls us to trust in Him, not in our resources. If we can enjoy God’s presence and goodness, we can enjoy His creation. Honestly, I could argue that the reason a man might not enjoy God’s creation is because he is not at peace with God’s presence."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Peace I leave with you, my peace I give unto you: not as the world giveth, give I unto you. Let not your heart be troubled, neither let it be afraid.","ref":"John 14:27"}]},{"start":21,"end":21,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God is a Savior. He alone is to be trusted for our salvation. We cannot leave our salvation dependent on any simple man’s hands. If God is your Savior, you do not need a priest. If He is your Savior, you don’t need a preacher. If He is your Savior, you don’t need a pastor. If He is your Savior, you don’t need a king. If He is your Savior, you don’t need a candle, you don’t need beads, you don’t need confessions, or works, or intercessors. All we need is Him. He is enough."},{"kind":"para","text":"If He is not enough, everything He says about Him being enough will be counted as a lie, and the entirety of the Bible is useless to you. If God says He is enough, you can guarantee He is enough."}]},{"start":22,"end":22,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Look to Him alone. Why would you want to rob God of His power in salvation? Why would you want to worship false gods? Don’t you understand how terrible that venture has been for the Israelites yet? They tried to do the same things, and it only angered the Lord, not gifted His children. That should be a wake-up call to anyone who worships angels, saints, or any other Bible character. God’s children were not made to worship each other. We were made to worship the Lord and enjoy His creation with His authority and presence."}]},{"start":23,"end":23,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Paul repeats this:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"That at the name of Jesus every knee should bow, of things in heaven, and things in earth, and things under the earth; And that every tongue should confess that Jesus Christ is Lord, to the glory of God the Father.","ref":"Philippians 2:10-11"},{"kind":"para","text":"God says it, and He cannot take back His Words. He didn’t make a mistake when He said He ALONE will save. He ALONE will provide. He doesn’t need help to give to His children. He owns the whole world, and He is more than capable of making decisions with His own possessions. He doesn’t need angels either. Hey, He doesn’t even need you and me. Yet He loves everything He creates, and He is going to do everything He says."},{"kind":"para","text":"God’s Words (just the things He says) alone have more power than any angel or saint has in the tip of their pinkies. You would be far wiser to trust in God’s power and reject the world if you are going to maintain truth and righteousness. God always will provide for His creation. You can’t depend on anything else in creation (whether in Heaven or on Earth) to keep that kind of promise."}]},{"start":24,"end":25,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God is our justifier."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"That being justified by his grace, we should be made heirs according to the hope of eternal life.","ref":"Titus 3:7"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Therefore being justified by faith, we have peace with God through our Lord Jesus Christ:","ref":"Romans 5:1"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Moreover whom he did predestinate, them he also called: and whom he called, them he also justified: and whom he justified, them he also glorified.","ref":"Romans 8:30"},{"kind":"para","text":"He (once again) alone will provide the defense for His children. You might have wondered why I am so serious about the necessity to soulwin for the heart. I’ve talked about the necessity to love someone more than debate someone several times over. You can always win a debate and lose a man’s spirit. Letting go of what you know to be the truth to let the other side vent their thoughts is the ultimate way to show love. You can give truth, which is (of course) important. But love is equally as important when it regards witnessing to someone."},{"kind":"para","text":"The reminder is that God will have the final say. He will prove the truth to them. You give the truth; God will prove it. You plant the seed; God will make it grow. From there, you can just listen and love. That is a proper way to soulwin. That is what God wants. If we do it any other way (i.e., try and prove the other party wrong), we are trying to be the justifier. Don’t rob God of His justification. He deserves the glory for a man’s soul."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":10},{"start":11,"end":11},{"start":12,"end":12},{"start":13,"end":13},{"start":14,"end":14},{"start":15,"end":15},{"start":16,"end":16},{"start":17,"end":17},{"start":18,"end":18},{"start":19,"end":19},{"start":20,"end":20},{"start":21,"end":21},{"start":22,"end":22},{"start":23,"end":23},{"start":24,"end":25}],"verses":{"1":"Thus saith the Lord to his anointed, to Cyrus, whose right hand I have holden, to subdue nations before him; and I will loose the loins of kings, to open before him the two leaved gates; and the gates shall not be shut;","2":"I will go before thee, and make the crooked places straight: I will break in pieces the gates of brass, and cut in sunder the bars of iron:","3":"And I will give thee the treasures of darkness, and hidden riches of secret places, that thou mayest know that I, the Lord, which call thee by thy name, am the God of Israel.","4":"For Jacob my servant's sake, and Israel mine elect, I have even called thee by thy name: I have surnamed thee, though thou hast not known me.","5":"I am the Lord, and there is none else, there is no God beside me: I girded thee, though thou hast not known me:","6":"That they may know from the rising of the sun, and from the west, that there is none beside me. I am the Lord, and there is none else.","7":"I form the light, and create darkness: I make peace, and create evil: I the Lord do all these things.","8":"Drop down, ye heavens, from above, and let the skies pour down righteousness: let the earth open, and let them bring forth salvation, and let righteousness spring up together; I the Lord have created it.","9":"Woe unto him that striveth with his Maker! Let the potsherd strive with the potsherds of the earth. Shall the clay say to him that fashioneth it, What makest thou? or thy work, He hath no hands?","10":"Woe unto him that saith unto his father, What begettest thou? or to the woman, What hast thou brought forth?","11":"Thus saith the Lord, the Holy One of Israel, and his Maker, Ask me of things to come concerning my sons, and concerning the work of my hands command ye me.","12":"I have made the earth, and created man upon it: I, even my hands, have stretched out the heavens, and all their host have I commanded.","13":"I have raised him up in righteousness, and I will direct all his ways: he shall build my city, and he shall let go my captives, not for price nor reward, saith the Lord of hosts.","14":"Thus saith the Lord, The labour of Egypt, and merchandise of Ethiopia and of the Sabeans, men of stature, shall come over unto thee, and they shall be thine: they shall come after thee; in chains they shall come over, and they shall fall down unto thee, they shall make supplication unto thee, saying, Surely God is in thee; and there is none else, there is no God.","15":"Verily thou art a God that hidest thyself, O God of Israel, the Saviour.","16":"They shall be ashamed, and also confounded, all of them: they shall go to confusion together that are makers of idols.","17":"But Israel shall be saved in the Lord with an everlasting salvation: ye shall not be ashamed nor confounded world without end.","18":"For thus saith the Lord that created the heavens; God himself that formed the earth and made it; he hath established it, he created it not in vain, he formed it to be inhabited: I am the Lord; and there is none else.","19":"I have not spoken in secret, in a dark place of the earth: I said not unto the seed of Jacob, Seek ye me in vain: I the Lord speak righteousness, I declare things that are right.","20":"Assemble yourselves and come; draw near together, ye that are escaped of the nations: they have no knowledge that set up the wood of their graven image, and pray unto a god that cannot save.","21":"Tell ye, and bring them near; yea, let them take counsel together: who hath declared this from ancient time? who hath told it from that time? have not I the Lord? and there is no God else beside me; a just God and a Saviour; there is none beside me.","22":"Look unto me, and be ye saved, all the ends of the earth: for I am God, and there is none else.","23":"I have sworn by myself, the word is gone out of my mouth in righteousness, and shall not return, That unto me every knee shall bow, every tongue shall swear.","24":"Surely, shall one say, in the Lord have I righteousness and strength: even to him shall men come; and all that are incensed against him shall be ashamed.","25":"In the Lord shall all the seed of Israel be justified, and shall glory."}},
    "46": {"chapter":46,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: God has made mention of the false worship that Israel has succumb too. He doesn't like it, and He has done a lot of talking against it so there should be no excuse for these people to continue in it... right? Well that's the problem here. They find some reason to keep with their traditions and false worship, and the Lord is trying to provide them with every purpose NOT to continue down this road."},{"kind":"para","text":"In this chapter, the Lord will use the idols of Babylon to prove His point. At this time, Babylon has not touched Jerusalem. They are seen as a friend at the moment. Eventually it will be Babylon that holds the world power, and they will take Jerusalem when the time comes. At the moment, the biggest power seems to be Assyria, with Persia closely following. The hearers of this word during the time of Isaiah will probably think it's kind of strange that he would speak about Babylon at all in this way. But, in time, they will (hopefully) come to realize that God has been warning them about what will take place, but they were too stubborn and ignorant to comply and listen."}],"previously":["God has made mention of the false worship that Israel has succumbed to. He doesn’t like it, and He has spoken against it extensively, so there should be no excuse for these people to continue in it… right? Well, that’s the problem here. They find some reason to keep with their traditions and false worship, and the Lord is trying to provide them with every purpose NOT to continue down this road. In this chapter, the Lord will use the idols of Babylon to prove His point. At this time, Babylon has not touched Jerusalem. They are seen as a friend at the moment. Eventually, it will be Babylon that holds the world power, and they will take Jerusalem when the time comes. At the moment, the biggest power seems to be Assyria, with Persia closely following. The hearers of this word during the time of Isaiah will probably think it’s kind of strange that he would speak about Babylon at all in this way. But, in time, they will (hopefully) come to realize that God has been warning them about what will take place, but they were too stubborn and ignorant to comply and listen."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":2,"title":"Added Burdens","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Bel is a chief Babylonian deity, while Nebo is also a deity, but he just looked over learning and letters. Supposedly, this Nebo fellow was used again throughout history in Greek, Latin, and Egyptian cultures. He was the same as “Hermes,” “Mercury,” and “Thoth.” “Nebo” means “prophet.” They were being carried around for the pagan people to worship and bow down to. Seeing as God has been on a roll at calling out the sin of idolatry, He is going to use Babylon’s idolatry problem to reveal why they won’t always prosper. As long as Babylon rejects the Lord, the Lord cannot continuously provide them with victory. God is giving them victory for a time, only so He can get His children to turn back to Him. Once that happens, Babylon and their gods will fall."},{"kind":"para","text":"God points out, however, that these idols are already a burden to these people. If we really think about it, our money burdens us if we depend on it. We stress out about bills and finances all too often. We depend on money too much. Even preachers preach about money too much. They think their greatest resource is their money. Don’t get me wrong, money (itself) is not necessarily a bad thing. It’s our dependency on it that makes it bad. We are consumed by it, rather than us consuming it. That’s a heavy burden. The idols of Babylon were burdening their beasts as well, as they had to haul these things around. Our idols burden our entire households. Babylon’s great fall should serve as a warning and example to every reader about the importance of watching out for idols in your own life. God will certainly use them as an example to the Israelites in the near future."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Idols burden us. I think it is important for us to get this into our brains because we are all too accustomed to trust everything except the Lord. The Lord, when we trust in Him, carries our burdens. We have spoken about this quite a bit already, but just in case you need a reminder:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Come unto me, all ye that labour and are heavy laden, and I will give you rest. Take my yoke upon you, and learn of me; for I am meek and lowly in heart: and ye shall find rest unto your souls. For my yoke is easy, and my burden is light.","ref":"Matthew 11:28-30"},{"kind":"para","text":"We can either let the cares and materials of this world weigh us down, or we can trust the Lord and accept His mercy and grace for us. I’ve heard people say, “Well, you can’t just lay there and expect the Lord to lavish His goodness on you.” And to that, I say, “Yes, you can.” In fact, we get that image throughout all of scripture. Whenever we see people in action without the leading of the Lord, they are prone to fall into some sort of sin or another. When we just lay there and wait for the Lord, the Lord gifts us. He really wants us to simply rest and trust in Him. There are far too many people getting themselves into trouble because they are doing things by their own wills and trusting in their surroundings rather than waiting for the Lord and trusting in Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"Our worship of anything other than the Lord is a burden. Perhaps you worship angels or saints. Maybe you don’t want to call it worship, but if you pray to them, it’s a sign of worship. Maybe you worship them, and you use candles, pray specific types of prayers, and have to memorize what saint does what thing in order to pray and live properly. Perhaps you worship your priest or the pope. Whatever it is, if it’s in anything except the Lord alone, it will certainly be a burden. This is why I could never join the Catholic Church. It’s not because of their traditions and their false and unbiblical way of serving and service. It’s simply because they have too many other things to remember and worship, and that is too much of a burden for anyone to carry. The Lord wants us to be burdenless, and when we add any sort of worship outside of specifically worshipping the Lord, we are just adding burdens to ourselves."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Cast thy burden upon the LORD, and he shall sustain thee: he shall never suffer the righteous to be moved.","ref":"Psalm 55:22"},{"kind":"para","text":"When we carry the burden, we suffer the reproach. However, when we go to the Lord and say, “God, I don’t know how I’m going to do this, please help me with it,” HE carries the burden and gets it done. You can either pray to a dead saint who cannot lift your burden, or pray to a living God who is daily concerned about your burdens."}]}]},{"start":3,"end":7,"title":"God Carries","entries":[{"start":3,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"All children (no matter where they are from or who) are a gift from the Lord."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Lo, children are an heritage of the LORD: and the fruit of the womb is his reward.","ref":"Psalm 127:3"},{"kind":"para","text":"No child is an accident. They might be an accident to you, but they were purposely made by the Lord for His glory and calling. God gifts mankind with children, and He wants us to enjoy having a family. We’ve also talked about this several times over. But this verse illustrates His presence in our lives. He carries us and is there every step of the way. God is extremely concerned about your burdens."},{"kind":"para","text":"There are a lot of people who are under the impression that God just simply does not care, and when we look at our situations from our point of view, we might not see God working on our behalf. I think that is why a lot of people don’t trust or go to the Lord. They just don’t have the vision to see His work. But God is there, and He is working, and He cares very much about what direction you take. He gives you multiple directions; He gives you more than one option every day, through every circumstance."},{"kind":"para","text":"We are tasked with choosing which option to take. We can go against what pleases God, ultimately trying to please ourselves, or we can take the option that we know for certain will honor the Lord, and the gift is far off in the distance. Either way, the Lord is concerned about your burdens, and He will not leave you if you are His child."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Let your conversation be without covetousness; and be content with such things as ye have: for he hath said, I will never leave thee, nor forsake thee.","ref":"Hebrews 13:5"}]},{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I think this is a trick question. There are a lot of people who would try to point out things in this world that they believe would stand toe to toe with the Lord. They would say, money, or gold, or some sort of valuable possession they claim for themselves. God could certainly stand up against them. You’d think that would be what the Lord would have used when explaining who He is in the book of John. But He doesn’t."},{"kind":"para","text":"Actually, He doesn’t use anything that seems very valuable in this world. Bread is not all that valuable compared to gold. Yet that is what the Lord uses to describe Himself. Bread certainly isn’t equal to God and cannot be compared to Him. But that is what He chose, and that is His use. He is a sustainer and provider for His children, a never-ending one at that. God is good at everything, all the time."}]},{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"They add value to their fake gods, but God is still more valuable than that. Prayer beads can cost around $10-$20, depending on where you want to buy them. Candles, once again depending on the brand and saint, can cost anywhere from $2-$200. There are also prayer cloths, prayer tokens, and prayer meetings that all cost your money. You want to pray to the genuine piece of burnt bush that God spoke to Moses through? You can, for a price. Yet, the Lord does His work for free. He saves for free. His salvation should cost us everything. It should cost us our lives. But instead of you spending your life to receive salvation, He gives you life when you receive it."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"The thief cometh not, but for to steal, and to kill, and to destroy: I am come that they might have life, and that they might have it more abundantly.","ref":"John 10:10"},{"kind":"para","text":"If your religion is taking your money for your salvation, you will never be able to pay it off. Rather, you will always be in debt to your religion, even after you die. There is no hope for a man who dies in His debt. But Jesus paid it all, and it has been freely given to anyone who wants to accept it. No money needed. No good works needed. Just simple faith and trust in His finished work on the cross."}]},{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Their fake gods will not protect them. Trusting in your prayer beads, in your giving, and in the amount of money you might spend to try and maintain your faith and standing will only make you heavier. We cannot depend on any of that. We should only be dependent on the Lord. God says, “This is what it looks like to carry your idols. Now let’s look at what it looks like for ME to carry YOU.”"}]}]},{"start":8,"end":11,"title":"God Alone","entries":[{"start":8,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Remember how much effort it is for you to carry these heavy idols. Don’t forget the amount of work and money it takes to maintain these things. He tells the people to remember them because God is going to remind them of what they SHOULD be doing:"}]},{"start":9,"end":9,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Did you forget this yet? Isaiah has been sure to pen this same exact saying over and over again at this point, and we should probably pay attention if God repeats Himself."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"I am the LORD, and there is none else, there is no God beside me: I girded thee, though thou hast not known me: That they may know from the rising of the sun, and from the west, that there is none beside me.","ref":"Isaiah 45:5-6"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Thus saith the LORD, The labour of Egypt, and merchandise of Ethiopia and of the Sabeans, men of stature, shall come over unto thee, and they shall be thine: they shall come after thee; in chains they shall come over, and they shall fall down unto thee, they shall make supplication unto thee, saying, Surely God is in thee; and there is none else, there is no God.","ref":"Isaiah 45:14"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For thus saith the LORD that created the heavens; God himself that formed the earth and made it; he hath established it, he created it not in vain, he formed it to be inhabited: I am the LORD; and there is none else.","ref":"Isaiah 45:18"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Tell ye, and bring them near; yea, let them take counsel together: who hath declared this from ancient time? who hath told it from that time? have not I the LORD? and there is no God else beside me; a just God and a Saviour; there is none beside me. Look unto me, and be ye saved, all the ends of the earth: for I am God, and there is none else.","ref":"Isaiah 45:21-22"},{"kind":"para","text":"Do we get it yet? You’d think the Israelites would have gotten it, but they don’t. They don’t get it for quite some time, in fact. They will still be led into captivity because they don’t pay attention to this very important reminder that Isaiah has made over and over again. He ALONE is God, and He ALONE should be worshipped, and He ALONE will provide for His children."}]},{"start":10,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"These idols have done nothing but require you to carry them. The Lord doesn’t ask for that. He wants to carry YOU. But we forget. We forget how the Lord has carried the Israelites through so many things for generations. We forget that the Lord has given them miracles, stood up for them, provided for them, and given them every possible reason to continually follow HIM alone. We forget that He requires only one thing from us, and that is that we just trust Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"He has established His consistency throughout history. He has not stopped providing since the beginning of time, and yet we can still find an excuse not to trust Him? His counsel is the only counsel that will stand the test of time, and His direction is the only direction that we will all eventually go in. He calls the birds, executes counsel from a “far country,” He speaks, and He delivers. He always has, He always will."},{"kind":"para","text":"If we are found on the wrong side of the battle with the Lord, it will only be because we have not gotten it into our heads that He (alone) deserves our full cooperation and attention. If we do not give that to Him and spread that acceptance to other idols in our lives, we will all face the same consequences that the Israelites do. Maybe not at such a grand scale, but it will still be too heavy a burden for us to handle without Him."}]}]},{"start":12,"end":13,"title":"Salvation is Near","entries":[{"start":12,"end":13,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God’s salvation and righteousness are right in front of every human being today. Every person in our world (if not every, at least 99%) has heard of the name of Jesus. That is quite a name. He IS salvation. If there are any who have not received Christ to themselves, it is not because salvation and righteousness are too far from them. No. God has made it very simple for any human being (including a child) to find Him and take hold of His providential salvation. We just have to be willing to trust Him when He gives it."},{"kind":"para","text":"We cannot take His salvation and then give it back, though. There are some people who believe they can. Once you are saved and you have come to the truth, it is impossible to be unsaved. You would have to simply reject the salvation that is near to you, but you cannot take it off. I will tell you now, though, that rejecting what Christ has already given to you is as equal of a burden as worshipping false idols. It will never pay off."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":9},{"start":10,"end":11},{"start":12,"end":13}],"verses":{"1":"Bel boweth down, Nebo stoopeth, their idols were upon the beasts, and upon the cattle: your carriages were heavy loaden; they are a burden to the weary beast.","2":"They stoop, they bow down together; they could not deliver the burden, but themselves are gone into captivity.","3":"Hearken unto me, O house of Jacob, and all the remnant of the house of Israel, which are borne by me from the belly, which are carried from the womb:","4":"And even to your old age I am he; and even to hoar hairs will I carry you: I have made, and I will bear; even I will carry, and will deliver you.","5":"To whom will ye liken me, and make me equal, and compare me, that we may be like?","6":"They lavish gold out of the bag, and weigh silver in the balance, and hire a goldsmith; and he maketh it a god: they fall down, yea, they worship.","7":"They bear him upon the shoulder, they carry him, and set him in his place, and he standeth; from his place shall he not remove: yea, one shall cry unto him, yet can he not answer, nor save him out of his trouble.","8":"Remember this, and shew yourselves men: bring it again to mind, O ye transgressors.","9":"Remember the former things of old: for I am God, and there is none else; I am God, and there is none like me,","10":"Declaring the end from the beginning, and from ancient times the things that are not yet done, saying, My counsel shall stand, and I will do all my pleasure:","11":"Calling a ravenous bird from the east, the man that executeth my counsel from a far country: yea, I have spoken it, I will also bring it to pass; I have purposed it, I will also do it.","12":"Hearken unto me, ye stouthearted, that are far from righteousness:","13":"I bring near my righteousness; it shall not be far off, and my salvation shall not tarry: and I will place salvation in Zion for Israel my glory."}},
    "47": {"chapter":47,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: In our last chapter, God has made it very clear to the reader (namely those in Israel) that He (alone) will carry them and save them. All they must do is trust and turn to Him. He has opened the door of salvation for them, but they must walk through it to be saved. He will make that clearer when Christ comes to Earth and physically saves them from their sins. In this instance, they are faced with a captivity by the people of Babylon. It's a warning that God has been giving them for a long time, and yet they don't seem to be learning anything about it."},{"kind":"para","text":"In this chapter, the warning is now facing Babylon. Babylon doesn't know what they are going to do yet. Perhaps they are scheming and planning for the opportunity to take over Israel, but that won't happen quite yet. The Lord provides a very clear cut prophecy about what will happen to this land when all is said and done, but (obviously) the Babylonians won't believe it, and that is exactly why they fall into what God will speak about in this chapter."}],"previously":["In our last chapter, God has made it very clear to the reader, namely those in Israel, that He alone will carry them and save them. All they must do is trust and turn to Him. He has opened the door of salvation for them, but they must walk through it to be saved. He will make that clearer when Christ comes to Earth and physically saves them from their sins. In this instance, they are faced with a captivity by the people of Babylon. It’s a warning that God has been giving them for a long time, and yet they don’t seem to be learning anything about it. In this chapter, the warning is now facing Babylon. Babylon doesn’t know what they are going to do yet. Perhaps they are scheming and planning for the opportunity to take over Israel, but that won’t happen quite yet. The Lord provides a very clear-cut prophecy about what will happen to this land when all is said and done, but (obviously) the Babylonians won’t believe it, and that is exactly why they fall into what God will speak about in this chapter."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":7,"title":"Babylon's Demise","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God has had quite a few prophecies about Babylon throughout this book of scripture. He has warned Israel several times over, but Babylon should be heeding these warnings too. Their seat will be on the throne for a time being, but eventually, they will be called off the throne to sit on the dust of the ground. They will not be called “tender and delicate” any longer. Well, were they ever called this? Perhaps at a time. Once they rise to power, they won’t be looked at as tender or delicate, and once they fall from power, they won’t be looked at as anything more than a mystery."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And upon her forehead was a name written, MYSTERY, BABYLON THE GREAT, THE MOTHER OF HARLOTS AND ABOMINATIONS OF THE EARTH.","ref":"Revelation 17:5"},{"kind":"para","text":"They will be a mystery in their downfall, and they will be a mystery to the world when they arise again in the end times. Of course, it is hugely possible that the next “Babylon” won’t be the same Babylon. It will be a worldwide Babylon, likely to take over a continent or specific country. Heck, America could be the next Babylon. It will, however, be met with the same end as THIS Babylon Isaiah is talking about. Again, prophecies work in three folds, and this prophecy will be no different. They will have power and throne, but they will lose it all, and only become nothing more than a distant memory (if anyone remembers it at all)."},{"kind":"para","text":"Babylon is spoken about in scripture quite a lot if you haven’t noticed. Yet, when we hear anything about the Bible, we don’t often hear things about Israel’s captivity, or about the lands and people around Israel. We like to focus on Israel. That is, of course, for good reason seeing as God chose that land to do the majority of His work in the Old Testament. He prepared that land to start Christianity, and the church that we know today. These other lands surrounding the Israelites were important too, because they helped to shape this land into what we might see today."}]},{"start":2,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Obviously, this is quite embarrassing. No one wants to be seen walking around naked and without. Well, maybe there are some people who like it today. There are a lot of places that find this to be normal. Some countries have dedicated beaches for it. We have a street that is somewhat close by in Lancaster that has a row of motels that serve out prostitutes. If you drive by there, you will see a lot of nearly nude women walking around the streets looking to make deals. Honestly, it’s quite disturbing."},{"kind":"para","text":"Israel had not gotten that low yet. Eventually, they will. Jerusalem will be taken captive by Babylon, and Babylon is going to hugely mistreat them. God will (eventually) put Babylon in its place, but other things need to take place first. Babylon will fall, though, and we all know this to be true historically."}]},{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God may exact punishment on the nations around Israel, but He will redeem His own. Praise the Lord that He is more than capable of rescuing His people while dealing with those who aren’t His. He can separate the two."},{"kind":"para","text":"When I am at my in-laws’ house, it’s pretty common for my nieces to get into arguments. Sisters just can’t seem to get along. I usually don’t say anything but tell them to be quiet. But when my own daughter gets involved, it involves me too. So I have to deal with my daughter. I’m able to help my daughter in those situations to make the right choice and get the true answers about the situation. I would assume any father would be willing to do that. I tend to give my daughter the benefit of the doubt and usually take her word for situations. I will dig deeper by asking questions to my nieces, but nine times out of ten, they line up with what my daughter had mentioned. We’ve taught her to speak the truth when asked because the truth will be revealed eventually anyway."},{"kind":"para","text":"God has taught us quite a lot if we are His children, and so He can easily figure out who is speaking the truth and who is not. Honestly, He doesn’t even need to use us to figure that out; He already knows. Anyone who is not His child is a liar."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"God forbid: yea, let God be true, but every man a liar; as it is written, That thou mightest be justified in thy sayings, and mightest overcome when thou art judged.","ref":"Romans 3:4"},{"kind":"para","text":"That’s a good rule of thumb for every single one of us to live by. Why do we believe liars? Everyone is a liar. We should expect that no matter who we talk to (my daughter included), they are likely going to embellish the truth or lie to us. God, however, never lies."}]},{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"They aren’t considered “The lady of the kingdoms” yet, not until they take Jerusalem. They are rising to power quite rapidly, though. Eventually, they will be a very strong and prosperous nation. I think that is where nations go wrong, honestly. We get too much prosperity, and we abuse it, thinking ourselves as something special. That only leads to our downfall."},{"kind":"para","text":"America is a prosperous nation. It has been for a very long time. If something happens here in America, the whole world seems to find out about it quickly. But I can see it crumbling. I can see it falling apart because we are too arrogant and prideful. Wealth, truly, blinds our eyes to what is really important. Wealth does not give us more of what we want. Wealth only robs us of what is ultimately important."},{"kind":"para","text":"I’ve heard people argue about “wealthy Christians” more times lately than I’d like to hear. No, it is not a sin to have wealth and be a Christian. Yet, it’s the “Christians” who have wealth who seem to always falter on their convictions and faith. Those that have next to nothing yet remain faithful to Christ always seem to hold onto the Lord tighter. A poor man’s faith is far more solid than a rich man’s faith. Babylon will become quite rich, and it will eventually lead them into destruction."}]},{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"If Babylon heard this message, they would think, “Wait, we can take Jerusalem? We can take these people captive?” They would probably miss the part where God says, “I have polluted mine inheritance, and I have given them into your hand.” It was God’s work that got this done. God is going to give His own people over to the Babylonians. Babylon, of course, won’t see that though, and they will put all the victory onto their own pride and strength."},{"kind":"para","text":"If they didn’t, and they gave God the glory (which would have never happened anyway), God would have blessed them beyond how they were blessed. But they squander it. Of course, they squander it. They will do just like the Israelites have done. They will abuse the gift of God for something it was never meant to be used for, and it will cause them to lose everything."}]},{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Perhaps Babylon’s viewpoint was that God didn’t take care of His own people, so why would He take care of them? They might have clung a little tighter to their own gods because the God of Israel didn’t seem to be very merciful. The thing is, they didn’t know what the Israelites had been doing against their God. They didn’t just reject the God of the Bible; they literally profaned Him. They did the complete opposite of everything their God told them to do, and (worse yet) they did things to try and purposely attack their own God, provoking Him to anger."},{"kind":"para","text":"See, the God of scripture does get angry. People don’t understand how a loving God can be angry with His own creation, but the truth is, if He didn’t get angry and didn’t do anything about the evil on this Earth, it would be much harder to believe that this God really actually exists. There is no other God that will get angry or correct His creation. Only the God of the Bible has ever (and will ever) do that. I believe that gives every person more of a reason to respect and trust the Lord with their lives. He will always do what’s right and always correct what’s wrong."}]}]},{"start":8,"end":11,"title":"Pride's Character","entries":[{"start":8,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There are many people who think quite highly of themselves. They truly believe they are untouchable. I’ve even seen it in the eyes of pastors. Pride and arrogance get into their blood in some fashion, and they walk, talk, and act as if they can do anything, and everyone will kiss their feet for it. They honestly think they could dropkick a baby and be praised. And you know what? There are people who would praise their pastor for that. We are not called to praise our pastor. We are called to praise the Lord. When we think we are something special, all we are doing is filling ourselves up with… well… ourselves! We are so full of ourselves. We can either be our own best friend or our greatest enemy. I think if you struggle with yourself, you are on the right track for the Lord. There should be no greater struggle in this world than with your own sins. If we don’t struggle with ourselves at all, we are likely far more accepting of pride and arrogance, ultimately leading to a path that rejects the ways of the Lord. We become our own gods in our own eyes. We try to speak like Him as well by saying, “I am, and none else beside me…”"},{"kind":"para","text":"Arrogance is a rotten fruit. It’s a fruit that grows from the same stock as the Spirit’s fruit. The Spirit’s fruit is love, and arrogance can be grown from that too. It produces joy, and arrogance can be produced from that too. It produces peace, and longsuffering, and gentleness, goodness, faith, meekness, and temperance, and arrogance can all be grown from those same exact characteristics of the Spirit. Why? Is it because God’s Spirit cannot be controlled? No. It’s because we like to take hold of the good things of God and spoil them with our own characteristics. All we bring to the table of God’s fruit-bearing as human beings is hate, sadness, restlessness, eagerness, brute force, sin, worry, pride, and need. That’s not a good trade-off. That is, however, the type of fruit we grow. We don’t grow anything good without the Lord. These are all bad things to grow and walk in. The Lord wants us to take His fruit and produce more like that, not like ourselves. Our arrogance, however, gets in our way, and we think if we just add a little of ourselves to these fruits, we can make them more palatable. You’re just choking yourself when you add your own growth to the Spirit’s fruit."}]},{"start":9,"end":9,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"To the Babylonians (and honestly, to the world), it will be a very quick and painful letdown for this country. Babylon will fall, and it will happen rapidly. God gives the reason for it as well. We already knew the reason; He has made that very clear over and over again through the words of Isaiah. God is not playing around when it comes to false worship and abusing mankind. This is no game or joke to the Lord. People’s lives really matter to God, and when there are people in this world abusing people, misusing people, or otherwise trying to hurt people (physically, mentally, or spiritually doesn’t matter), the Lord is going to do something about it. God will judge these people who do these things."},{"kind":"para","text":"There is nothing worse, in my personal opinion, than to lose my family. Babylon will become childless and a widow all at once."}]},{"start":10,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Again, God sees all. Those secret sins that you may be enticed into are not a secret to the Lord. Everything is open and revealed to Him. When you feel convicted for it, you receive that feeling because the Lord is working on you."}]},{"start":11,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God gives three very specific issues that the Babylonians will face. \"evil...mischief...and desolation…\" Evil will fall on the prideful because the acts of prideful people are evil."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Pride goeth before destruction, and an haughty spirit before a fall.","ref":"Proverbs 16:18"},{"kind":"para","text":"Prideful people always produce mischief."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Why boastest thou thyself in mischief, O mighty man? the goodness of God endureth continually.","ref":"Psalm 52:1"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"He that deviseth to do evil shall be called a mischievous person.","ref":"Proverbs 24:8"},{"kind":"para","text":"All, ultimately, pride will leave you in desolation."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"How are they brought into desolation, as in a moment! they are utterly consumed with terrors.","ref":"Psalm 73:19"},{"kind":"para","text":"And it’s all brought on by their own pride. The Lord is certainly the authority of it, but it was not His desire to destroy whole nations like this. His desire was that His creation would live correctly and how they were made to in the beginning. We, instead, like to listen to Satan and follow the shackles of sin rather than the freedom of salvation. Until we turn to the Lord, we will always be stuck in these three characteristics of pride."}]}]},{"start":12,"end":15,"title":"A Speck in Time","entries":[{"start":12,"end":13,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God is actually requiring these people to test their idols against the Lord. These people can use their pride, their arrogance, their personal strengths, and wisdoms to see if they are a match (even a little bit) to the Lord’s power and wisdom. God can do this rightfully because there is no one that can stand up to Him and win. They will all utterly miss the mark. Our greatest strengths on this Earth are no match for the God of the universe."},{"kind":"para","text":"Even if you don’t believe in God specifically, our greatest achievements are nothing compared to the vast expanse of the galaxy we live in, let alone everything that surpasses it. You are just a small atom compared to the rest of space and time. Nothing we create, do, or think will ever match up to the might and length of the universe, and it will never match up to the love and grace of the Lord."}]},{"start":14,"end":15,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"They will live a vagabond life, being nomads who wander from land to land, never finding a place to rest. Only the Lord could give rest, remember. We have spoken quite prolifically about the Lord’s rest, and at this point, we should realize that God is the giver of the finer things in this life. Wealth, honor, and power are all very useful and interesting things, but that is not important to life. God’s rest, mercy, grace, love, and relationship are all that should matter to us."},{"kind":"para","text":"We seem to usually forsake and miss those things, though, because we are so focused on ourselves. When we focus on ourselves, we will miss what’s important, and everything that we had will come to nothing more than “stubble” and charred wreckage. Ask the Babylonians. Ask the nation that will rise to power in the end times as well. Ask any rich man who has now lost it all."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":9},{"start":10,"end":10},{"start":11,"end":11},{"start":12,"end":13},{"start":14,"end":15}],"verses":{"1":"Come down, and sit in the dust, O virgin daughter of Babylon, sit on the ground: there is no throne, O daughter of the Chaldeans: for thou shalt no more be called tender and delicate.","2":"Take the millstones, and grind meal: uncover thy locks, make bare the leg, uncover the thigh, pass over the rivers.","3":"Thy nakedness shall be uncovered, yea, thy shame shall be seen: I will take vengeance, and I will not meet thee as a man.","4":"As for our redeemer, the Lord of hosts is his name, the Holy One of Israel.","5":"Sit thou silent, and get thee into darkness, O daughter of the Chaldeans: for thou shalt no more be called, The lady of kingdoms.","6":"I was wroth with my people, I have polluted mine inheritance, and given them into thine hand: thou didst shew them no mercy; upon the ancient hast thou very heavily laid thy yoke.","7":"And thou saidst, I shall be a lady for ever: so that thou didst not lay these things to thy heart, neither didst remember the latter end of it.","8":"Therefore hear now this, thou that art given to pleasures, that dwellest carelessly, that sayest in thine heart, I am, and none else beside me; I shall not sit as a widow, neither shall I know the loss of children:","9":"But these two things shall come to thee in a moment in one day, the loss of children, and widowhood: they shall come upon thee in their perfection for the multitude of thy sorceries, and for the great abundance of thine enchantments.","10":"For thou hast trusted in thy wickedness: thou hast said, None seeth me. Thy wisdom and thy knowledge, it hath perverted thee; and thou hast said in thine heart, I am, and none else beside me.","11":"Therefore shall evil come upon thee; thou shalt not know from whence it riseth: and mischief shall fall upon thee; thou shalt not be able to put it off: and desolation shall come upon thee suddenly, which thou shalt not know.","12":"Stand now with thine enchantments, and with the multitude of thy sorceries, wherein thou hast laboured from thy youth; if so be thou shalt be able to profit, if so be thou mayest prevail.","13":"Thou art wearied in the multitude of thy counsels. Let now the astrologers, the stargazers, the monthly prognosticators, stand up, and save thee from these things that shall come upon thee.","14":"Behold, they shall be as stubble; the fire shall burn them; they shall not deliver themselves from the power of the flame: there shall not be a coal to warm at, nor fire to sit before it.","15":"Thus shall they be unto thee with whom thou hast laboured, even thy merchants, from thy youth: they shall wander every one to his quarter; none shall save thee."}},
    "48": {"chapter":48,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: In our last chapter, God spoke about the demise of Babylon, the problem with pride (and the real reason Babylon will not stand), and how small we are compared to the length of time and eternity. Obviously the Lord has all things planned out. It was a short chapter, but it was a powerful chapter."},{"kind":"para","text":"I believe this chapter is just as powerful. We will really look at the depths of God's heart and lvoe for creation, and why He makes it so much a point to warn His children, draw in His creation, and provide them with hope and direction in such a perverse and demented world."}],"previously":["In our last chapter, God spoke about the demise of Babylon, the problem with pride (and the real reason Babylon will not stand), and how small we are compared to the length of time and eternity. Obviously, the Lord has all things planned out. It was a short chapter, but it was a powerful chapter. I believe this chapter is just as powerful. We will really look at the depths of God’s heart and love for creation, and why He makes it so much a point to warn His children, draw in His creation, and provide them with hope and direction in such a perverse and demented world."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":11,"title":"What Is Love?","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Remember: “Jacob” means “Holder of the heel.” It’s the worldly name for God’s children. They hold onto the heels of this world, and that is what they depend on. But when they came forth “out of the waters of Judah,” that is to say, “Into their Promised Land,” they were the children of Israel. They are the children of God. “Israel” means “Wrestles With God.” Boy, have they wrestled with Him. Isaiah is a book that testifies to that fact. But arguably, they might be living in Israel, but they are not genuine Israelites if they are rejecting the Lord. They are not truly God’s children if they are not living for Him. That is how it is in this world today."},{"kind":"para","text":"I’ve heard people say, “We are all made in the image of God, so we are all God’s children.” No. There are some people who hate God and have rejected Him through and through. They are not God’s children. They are certainly God’s creation, but far from being a child of God. Furthermore, we have people in the church who play the part of God’s child, who are actually not God’s children. Going to church makes you as much a child of God as going into a garage makes you a car. It’s funny that this world measures people based on their location. “Oh, you go to that church. You must be strict and very legalistic.” Or, “Oh, that church is super open and easily swayed.” Or, “Oh, that’s a mega church, you must be rich.” The church doesn’t make a person, but people DO make up the church. Genuine believers are what a real church looks like. It’s not about how many people GO to church, it’s about how many people STAY in church."},{"kind":"para","text":"There’s a problem with a church if they are just going through new people like some sort of factory. I see that all too often in most churches today. They can’t keep people. They aren’t really LOOKING to keep people. They just want to reach the next one, and the next one, and the next one, and all the other people they reached before just get thrown into the dust and left behind. Honestly, that is how you can tell whether a person who claims to be “of God” is truly FROM God. Do they care enough about you to maintain a relationship with you? If not, they are probably just faking their belonging in the church."},{"kind":"para","text":"There were people in Israel who were Israelites by blood, but not by faith. Rather, they were Jacobites (if I can say that). What makes them Israelites was their following of the Lord. What makes you and me a Christian today is not by what church we go to, or what others may refer to us as (or what we might refer to ourselves as for that matter). Rather, what makes us Christians is our following of the Lord. God is our Shepherd, or God is our judge. If He is our judge, we must get that fixed to have the leading of God before we are cast into captivity. I believe those that followed the Lord would face trials of all sorts from the sins of those people around them, but the Lord would protect and guide those that truly belong to Him. He won’t let them face captivity without a helpful hand from Him. He will provide peace to those that are held captive in His presence. Just look to the book of Daniel for that proof. Those that call themselves Israelites but reject the Lord are not true Israelites."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"People who are genuine will not have to tell you they are. Real faith-filled leaders don’t have to tell people they are leading. People will just know it. God’s sheep are not stupid; they can make decisions for themselves. Honestly, that is what the church should be focused on. It’s what Israel should have been focused on as well. They should have been focused on preparing people to make decisions without the presence of holy leaders."},{"kind":"para","text":"We should be being prepared (by our church) to be our own holy leaders. We should know how to make decisions on our own. We should always have the church to go back to, to learn more and lean on God’s people and presence, but we should (by and large) be able to make righteous decisions based on our own faith and mind."}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Think about all the amazing things God created. Consider the planets and their usefulness. Reflect on the moon and sun, the stars, and the vastness of space. Think about the trees, animals, and fish. Consider the water, land, and their inhabitants. Think about the sky, technology, skyscrapers, and buildings. Reflect on the finer things in life. Now, think about free will. We can find beauty in everything, but there isn’t much beauty in free will. God created it, though. We can make our own decisions by our own means. He is able to make all these things (just by speaking it, by the way), and He can control all of His creation, but His human creation is the most stubborn. We take all the good things of God (including free will) and use them against God. We are such strange and depraved creatures."}]},{"start":4,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I know we have talked at length about this already, but I think it’s a good thing to be reminded of as much as possible. God doesn’t need YOU to prove His characteristics. He can certainly prove it Himself. He has, in fact, proved Himself to these people (and to us) more times than we deserve. They cannot look back and say, “Our idols did it!” No, they didn’t even have the idols back then like they do now. It could only be God. Their idols didn’t do anything. Their own hands didn’t even do it for them. It was the Lord that provided every step of the way for them. God was also the one to provide WARNING for them. They will gladly take God’s goodness but reject God’s warning. Does that sound familiar to you?"},{"kind":"para","text":"If you are a red-blooded human being today, you will also agree that God has been good to you. Whether you believe in a divine power or not, there is good in this life that you can trace back to SOMETHING (even if you don’t want to call it “God”). We have no problem accepting the good things God gives us. But when it comes to warning, judgment, and protection, we say, “God hates us.” We are viewing God’s guidance and protection wrong. God warns because He loves us."},{"kind":"para","text":"I have had this internal struggle myself if I can be honest (as I’m sure I’m not alone). Someone has done something wrong to me, and I want nothing more than to get even with them. I want to make them hurt like they have made me hurt. I want them to understand what I am going through because THEY are making me go through it. Usually, I bite my tongue and wait for the Lord to deal with it. But if I took a quick evaluation and asked myself the right questions, I would realize there is depth to the way I feel. It’s not just surface-level retaliation. It’s a deep passion for something. I hurt because I thought I could trust that person. If someone can hurt you, it’s not because they didn’t matter to you. Rather, their opinion HAS to matter if you are hurt by something they do. You care about them, and they didn’t reciprocate that care for you. That is why it hurts. You showed love, and they forsook it."},{"kind":"para","text":"I believe that is how the Lord feels. He shows love, and we forsake it. He doesn’t give us warnings because He hates us. He doesn’t correct us because we are not important to Him. He does these things because He loves us, not because we deserve it. We certainly do deserve correction and warning, but only so we can turn and recognize the love of God from it."}]},{"start":6,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God revealed things to these people that they would have never known any other way. He protected them through His Word and directives, providing them with every reason and position possible to trust His Word on the matter. However, there were several kings who forsook the Lord’s directives because they came from the mouth of someone who spoke a lot about God’s warnings and chastisement. Instead of taking those words seriously, they were offended and shut the mouths of the prophets."},{"kind":"para","text":"We can read about Jezebel and the terrible things she did to the prophets of God because she was offended by the Lord’s warnings, rather than accepting God’s warning and turning to Him for guidance. God gave every Israelite warning through His Word, and the majority rejected it. They couldn’t say that God didn’t send messengers, nor could they say that God didn’t try to help. They couldn’t say that God was not on their side. God did it all for them, but they only wanted to hear what was good from God, not what they could correct."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And the king of Israel said unto Jehoshaphat, There is yet one man, Micaiah the son of Imlah, by whom we may enquire of the LORD: but I hate him; for he doth not prophesy good concerning me, but evil. And Jehoshaphat said, Let not the king say so.","ref":"1 Kings 22:8"},{"kind":"para","text":"This king (one example out of many) shunned God's Word because it hurt his feelings, rather than listen to God's Word because it gave Him opportunity for growth. So many of us fall for the same traps..."}]},{"start":8,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Let me let you in on a little secret from the Lord here. Honestly, it shouldn’t be a secret at this point, because I’ve made mention quite a few times about it already (but in case you forgot): God knows you are a sinner. He knows you are going to sin. He knows it’s in your nature to do the wrong thing, and that all children must be trained to do the right thing. We can be just as keen on that as well. We are sinners as well. But we are able to walk into any room (including in the church) and rightfully judge that every person in there is struggling with sin."},{"kind":"para","text":"Perhaps there are some who are not struggling with it. If they are not, then you are assured that they do not know the Lord. Those are your two options in this life honestly. You are either struggling with sin, or you are not a child of God. Even still, while these people were sinners, God gave them love and warning. He still wanted them to listen. Even while they were against Him, He still showed His love!"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But God commendeth his love toward us, in that, while we were yet sinners, Christ died for us.","ref":"Romans 5:8"},{"kind":"para","text":"We might not be God’s children, but He still loves His creation. He still loves the sinner who doesn’t struggle with sin. However, only those who are in a relationship with Him can work on their sin problem. Those who know God personally will struggle with sin. They will feel the hurt that God feels when they sin against Him. That is genuine love to the Lord. That’s how we know we love God, when we are hurt by the things that hurt the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Israelites, at this time, were not concerned about what was hurting God. They were concerned about what felt good to themselves. God would just have to accept it, or be forsaken, and God certainly won’t accept it…"}]},{"start":9,"end":9,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God also knows the future hope and promise for these people. Because He knows the future, He can make promises that will be kept. And because of this, He knows where to place His love. When you are His child, He isn’t seeing your current sin; He is seeing your future righteousness. He knows that you can be worked on, and He knows there is a future turnaround for His own. You might not care about whether you hurt Him or not now, but you (perhaps) will care about it in the future. That is what He sees when He calls a man. He sees what they can become, not what they currently are."},{"kind":"para","text":"If God chose me based on who I am today, I can confidently say it’s not because I am anything special. In fact, I know for sure that there is nothing special about me. But the Lord knows there is something redeemable for me. He knows something about my future that I haven’t the slightest clue about. I feel like a failure, but God sees something victorious for my future. I have given up on me, but God continues to work on and mold me into what He sees coming up in my life."}]},{"start":10,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"What a verse. I think we all want to be refined with silver. We want a profitable refining. If we are going to go through pain, we want there to be some sort of value when we come out of it. But that is not how God refines His children. I think we learn the most when we are going through deep trials. If we were refined with silver, we would have our needs met and wouldn’t have to worry about the trial. We wouldn’t take the trial seriously. Rather, God has to remind you of who you belong to. The best way to do that is through affliction. Not only that, but God refines us in this way to give the rest of the world an example of how to deal with these problems."}]},{"start":11,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"When the world faces a problem, people often create their own ways to deal with it. They say, “Well, this has been what worked best for me, so this will be the way others should do it too.” However, God says, “I give my own children problems so they can be an example of God’s way of doing it, rather than the world’s way of dealing with it.” We tend to miss that mark, though."},{"kind":"para","text":"There is no greater time that people will pay attention to you than when you are facing affliction. It seems you are invisible to the church until you are in the midst of a deep and painful trial, then it’s like you are the most important person in others’ lives (at least for a time). That is not how it should be between God’s children. God never wanted that, and yet it’s still something we can’t seem to learn."},{"kind":"para","text":"God says here, “I give trials to strengthen you. I give them to prove my life for you and for others. I give them so you grow closer to me, and closer to each other.” Yet, through trials, we seem to distance ourselves from everyone else. That is not what God wants."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But grow in grace, and in the knowledge of our Lord and Saviour Jesus Christ. To him be glory both now and for ever. Amen.","ref":"2 Peter 3:18"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And this I pray, that your love may abound yet more and more in knowledge and in all judgment;","ref":"Philippians 1:9"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But speaking the truth in love, may grow up into him in all things, which is the head, even Christ:","ref":"Ephesians 4:15"},{"kind":"para","text":"The sermon of growing in love is lacking in the church today."}]}]},{"start":12,"end":16,"title":"God's Cry For Creation","entries":[{"start":12,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"If there is anyone worth listening to in this life it is certainly the Lord. Yet, He is the one that we most often ignore."}]},{"start":13,"end":13,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"You know why we haven’t spiraled uncontrollably towards the sun? You know why the Earth hasn’t imploded beyond belief, and how the galaxy still rotates appropriately today? You know how the moon hasn’t crashed down on us and completely destroyed our planet? You know how meteors haven’t come and completely annihilated all life as we know it? Well, the Lord commands them. Space rocks listen to the Lord better than we do…"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And he answered and said unto them, I tell you that, if these should hold their peace, the stones would immediately cry out.","ref":"Luke 19:40"}]},{"start":14,"end":15,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God calls for His creation and cries for us. He is paying attention, and our pains are not lost on Him. He cares very much about what we are doing and how we are treating each other. My daughter has recently been a good example of selflessness. We have a three-month-old now, and Melody is eleven years old. Novalee sleeps in her room, but Melody gets up in the night to put her pacifier back in her mouth and helps her to go back to sleep. We never told Melody to do this; she took it upon herself to get up and take care of her sister. Why? Well, it’s because she loves her sister and is willing to be up all night to take care of her. There is no ultimatum to it; she just wants her sister near her."},{"kind":"para","text":"My mom, apparently, confronted Melody about it and told her that it was not her job to take care of her sister and that we should be getting up for that. She’s right. But it’s also admirable that her sister would want to get up and take care of her at all. That is what my mom is missing in this picture. Melody is displaying Christ’s sacrifice by doing this. If I was at my in-laws’ house and their baby was crying, I wouldn’t just leave the baby there and say, “Well, that’s her parents’ job to deal with.” No, I would try and help the baby if she was crying (I think any sane human would)."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord loves us in the same way. He hears our cries, He cries with us, and He feels our pains with us. He is involved with our pains and desires. The Lord here, specifically, is pointing out the Babylonians. Even if they, who are not Israelites, turn to Him, He will call them."}]},{"start":16,"end":16,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Is this not the message of Christ? It is, of course, Isaiah who is speaking these words, but it’s the same cry of Christ. It’s the same cry of God since the beginning of time. Since the very first sin, God has been calling out to His creation. Since God has created man, He has been seeking a relationship with man. God loves us. There is no denying that. If we deny the love of God, we are denying all truth. God IS love."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"He that loveth not knoweth not God; for God is love.","ref":"1 John 4:8"},{"kind":"para","text":"God IS truth."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Jesus saith unto him, I am the way, the truth, and the life: no man cometh unto the Father, but by me.","ref":"John 14:6"},{"kind":"para","text":"These two concepts go hand in hand. That is why we say that we must “love people into the truth.” We cannot force them, debate them into it, or convince them into it. We must simply love them and speak the truth in that love. The only ultimatum a person may have for speaking the truth to someone else is from a heart of love. Otherwise, the truth is likely not genuine."}]}]},{"start":17,"end":19,"title":"God Leads Peacefully","entries":[{"start":17,"end":17,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Real richness comes from learning how to grow closer to God. When we do that, we have a sure foundation and a true direction. That’s what God wants for His creation. He wants to provide them with assurance and peace as we trek this very difficult terrain of life."},{"kind":"para","text":"Life is not easy. I hope there is no one who believes life is easy. If there is a man who thinks life is easy, he is a man who has not lived at all. Real life experiences trials, and trials are hard. But they are always worth it if directed by the Lord."}]},{"start":18,"end":19,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"When we listen to the Lord, and follow His paths, we are assured. God's peace is unfathomable."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And the peace of God, which passeth all understanding, shall keep your hearts and minds through Christ Jesus.","ref":"Philippians 4:7"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Peace I leave with you, my peace I give unto you: not as the world giveth, give I unto you. Let not your heart be troubled, neither let it be afraid.","ref":"John 14:27"},{"kind":"para","text":"We have all confidence in every decision we make when it is bathed in faith towards the Lord. We no longer jump to whatever decisions we want. We are led by decisions from the Lord. Wherever God leads, that is the best way to go. Period."}]}]},{"start":20,"end":22,"title":"Peace to Us","entries":[{"start":20,"end":20,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There will be a song when they return to their land. They will be able to worship and rejoice that God keeps His promises. He will. We can know it because we are reading about the past, and historically we can see it. However, we can rest assured in His promises because He has kept them for us who read this today as well."},{"kind":"para","text":"Prophecies were for the Israelites, but they are also for Christ’s disciples. We are His disciples if we are following Him. So the promises are just as good for you as well. It might not be from physical captivity, but it will be for your spiritual one. That is a great assurance to you."}]},{"start":21,"end":21,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Isaiah provides proof of God’s providence. God provided water from a rock and food from the sky for His children. This occurred during a time when they were not in obedience to the Lord. God showed love and compassion for His wayward creation. He still shows His love today, even if the majority of the world is living in opposition to the Lord."}]},{"start":22,"end":22,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There is peace that passes all understanding to the people who are following the Lord. There is no peace, however, to those that are against Him. You know why we don't have world peace? Well, I'll let you connect the dots."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":9},{"start":10,"end":10},{"start":11,"end":11},{"start":12,"end":12},{"start":13,"end":13},{"start":14,"end":15},{"start":16,"end":16},{"start":17,"end":17},{"start":18,"end":19},{"start":20,"end":20},{"start":21,"end":21},{"start":22,"end":22}],"verses":{"1":"Hear ye this, O house of Jacob, which are called by the name of Israel, and are come forth out of the waters of Judah, which swear by the name of the Lord, and make mention of the God of Israel, but not in truth, nor in righteousness.","2":"For they call themselves of the holy city, and stay themselves upon the God of Israel; The Lord of hosts is his name.","3":"I have declared the former things from the beginning; and they went forth out of my mouth, and I shewed them; I did them suddenly, and they came to pass.","4":"Because I knew that thou art obstinate, and thy neck is an iron sinew, and thy brow brass;","5":"I have even from the beginning declared it to thee; before it came to pass I shewed it thee: lest thou shouldest say, Mine idol hath done them, and my graven image, and my molten image, hath commanded them.","6":"Thou hast heard, see all this; and will not ye declare it? I have shewed thee new things from this time, even hidden things, and thou didst not know them.","7":"They are created now, and not from the beginning; even before the day when thou heardest them not; lest thou shouldest say, Behold, I knew them.","8":"Yea, thou heardest not; yea, thou knewest not; yea, from that time that thine ear was not opened: for I knew that thou wouldest deal very treacherously, and wast called a transgressor from the womb.","9":"For my name's sake will I defer mine anger, and for my praise will I refrain for thee, that I cut thee not off.","10":"Behold, I have refined thee, but not with silver; I have chosen thee in the furnace of affliction.","11":"For mine own sake, even for mine own sake, will I do it: for how should my name be polluted? and I will not give my glory unto another.","12":"Hearken unto me, O Jacob and Israel, my called; I am he; I am the first, I also am the last.","13":"Mine hand also hath laid the foundation of the earth, and my right hand hath spanned the heavens: when I call unto them, they stand up together.","14":"All ye, assemble yourselves, and hear; which among them hath declared these things? The Lord hath loved him: he will do his pleasure on Babylon, and his arm shall be on the Chaldeans.","15":"I, even I, have spoken; yea, I have called him: I have brought him, and he shall make his way prosperous.","16":"Come ye near unto me, hear ye this; I have not spoken in secret from the beginning; from the time that it was, there am I: and now the Lord God, and his Spirit, hath sent me.","17":"Thus saith the Lord, thy Redeemer, the Holy One of Israel; I am the Lord thy God which teacheth thee to profit, which leadeth thee by the way that thou shouldest go.","18":"O that thou hadst hearkened to my commandments! then had thy peace been as a river, and thy righteousness as the waves of the sea:","19":"Thy seed also had been as the sand, and the offspring of thy bowels like the gravel thereof; his name should not have been cut off nor destroyed from before me.","20":"Go ye forth of Babylon, flee ye from the Chaldeans, with a voice of singing declare ye, tell this, utter it even to the end of the earth; say ye, The Lord hath redeemed his servant Jacob.","21":"And they thirsted not when he led them through the deserts: he caused the waters to flow out of the rock for them: he clave the rock also, and the waters gushed out.","22":"There is no peace, saith the Lord, unto the wicked."}},
    "49": {"chapter":49,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: In our last chapter, God gives this amazing love letter to His creation. You can tell throughout all of scripture that everything God does is out of a desire to prove His love. Even when He allows us to be held captive, or when He allows the enemy to win, He does it from a bout of love that cannot be understood by anyone in the world without know who He is first. It is a great chapter, and a great reminder even to the most mature of Christians."},{"kind":"para","text":"In this chapter, we look at God's proven victory. It's another fantastic chapter about how (no matter what the world might try to throw God's way) God will ALWAYS be victorious. He will always do what is right, and He will never fail to keep His promises. Through Jesus Christ, every promise of God IS kept. Even still today. We can hold to the promises of God because Jesus is still alive!"}],"previously":["In our last chapter, God gives this amazing love letter to His creation. You can tell throughout all of scripture that everything God does is out of a desire to prove His love. Even when He allows us to be held captive, or when He allows the enemy to win, He does it from a love that cannot be understood by anyone in the world without knowing who He is first. It is a great chapter and a great reminder even to the most mature of Christians. In this chapter, we look at God’s proven victory. It’s another fantastic chapter about how (no matter what the world might try to throw God’s way) God will always be victorious. He will always do what is right, and He will never fail to keep His promises. Through Jesus Christ, every promise of God is kept. Even still today. We can hold to the promises of God because Jesus is still alive!"],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":4,"title":"Victory in God","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Isaiah presents an interesting thought here. Obviously he is not the first to think of this:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For thou hast possessed my reins: thou hast covered me in my mother's womb.","ref":"Psalm 139:13"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Before I formed thee in the belly I knew thee; and before thou camest forth out of the womb I sanctified thee, and I ordained thee a prophet unto the nations.","ref":"Jeremiah 1:5"},{"kind":"para","text":"Think about the significance of that for your life. God knew you before you were born. Arguably, He knew you before He even created humanity. He created everything for this specific moment right now. He knew what you would do, He knew where you would go, and He called you right from the womb. He calls the whole world, by the way. People say, “God only calls the elect.” God calls the world, but not everyone will turn to Him:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For many are called, but few are chosen.","ref":"Matthew 22:14"},{"kind":"para","text":"It’s a valuable thing to realize the calling of God. By the way, God’s calling for your life is not the work of the ministry. Perhaps you have a calling for that, but that is not what God calls you into. He might prepare you for it. He might give you joy in doing it. He might give you opportunities to use it. But God calls every human being for one specific purpose. That purpose is to know Him and spend time with Him. That is your calling. That is all He wants from His creation, and especially from the human race. We are so busy human doing, and they are not human being…"}]},{"start":2,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God is working on this nation. He has used this nation for a great many things, and the world would certainly have to question how this nation still existed (and still exists today). From the beginning, it would seem as if this nation was doomed. Jacob was the second child, mind you. Jerusalem, in general, if you think about it, and Judah was a very sinful lineage. From the beginning, it would seem that there was no actual redemptive quality about this line of Israel. Yet God had worked on it. God has used it. God will continue to use it, and it will be through that line that the Savior is born."},{"kind":"para","text":"I do, however, think that Isaiah is speaking a little more personally here. Of course, Isaiah is not the first prophet for the Israelites. There have been many throughout the history of Israel. But Isaiah feels like his words (no doubt) were like a sharp sword. Everything he said inflicted some sort of pain on those who heard it. The only reason that it hurt those around him was because what he was saying was absolutely true. Those words should have been used for correction. Instead, everyone just left Isaiah feeling defeated and offended. Isaiah was probably not a very liked prophet. No prophet was liked much. Even still today, there are preachers and pastors who uphold the truth with love, and they are not very liked by our world. Even in the church. You either say nice things about your fellow Christian, or you get punished for speaking anything that might make them feel bad."},{"kind":"para","text":"God’s message can be a bit painful if you are not living correctly for Him. That’s not the messenger’s fault, though. It’s not Isaiah’s fault that people were hurt by the word of God. That was the hearers’ fault for not listening to God’s word to begin with."}]},{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Can we recognize something about God here? Everything the Lord does is counted as a victory. There is not a single thing He has ever done throughout history that can be counted as a loss or as a defeat. Even His own death was victorious."},{"kind":"para","text":"Think about this verse from the Lord’s perspective for a moment. He has felt like He has done everything He possibly could to get His children into their proper standing and heading in the right direction. But instead of His children thanking Him and following His Will, they reject Him and push against everything He wants for them. God says, “I spent all the time and strength for no reason. You guys are still headed down a sinful and dull path.”"},{"kind":"para","text":"Even while His children are falling away, God WILL still have the victory! There might not be many examples of it right now, but there will be to come, and Heaven will be filled with the proof that God IS and has always BEEN victorious."}]}]},{"start":5,"end":6,"title":"Not Chosen","entries":[{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Remember, Isaiah is the one saying this. Isaiah is being a mouthpiece for the Lord, but it won’t be Isaiah that brings Jacob back to the Lord. I think we understand that. By the time Judah falls back in line with God, Isaiah will just be a memory. Rather, this (once again) is from the perspective of the Lord. Jesus Christ will be the successful one to bring back and reconcile God’s people."},{"kind":"para","text":"More interesting is the last part of this verse. Even if the church never started, even if the people never believed, even if there was no witness to the happening of the cross, Christ will still be glorified in the eyes of the Lord. Nobody could have seen the Lord’s sacrifice, yet God would have still been the strength of Jesus. The debt was paid whether we witnessed it or not. The forgiveness for sin has been given whether we want to accept it or not. Christ did what He did, not for you to simply bear witness to it. He did it to please the Father, and there is nothing more that pleases God than faith and repentance."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But without faith it is impossible to please him: for he that cometh to God must believe that he is, and that he is a rewarder of them that diligently seek him.","ref":"Hebrews 11:6"},{"kind":"para","text":"Christ pleased God alone by going to the cross and dying for the sins of the world. We are the benefactors of His sacrifice, though. He pleased God, and that pleases the Christian. Why? Well, it’s because we are sinful creatures who could never please God in the way Christ did. We would utterly fail every single time we ever tried."}]},{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"What a fantastic promise is written in this verse here. Every person who heard it, no doubt, scoffed at Isaiah. Salvation, in their own eyes, only lay in the faith of the Jews. The Israelites were the only ones they believed deserved the salvation of the Lord. Since the beginning, however, God has been leaving the door open for outsiders. He has always desired the whole world to come to Him, but it was only this nation that turned to Him over and over again."},{"kind":"para","text":"When Jesus comes, however, the whole world will see that salvation is not meant for just a limited few. Imagine if the Lord only allowed the Jews salvation. How miserable a God we would have. How miserably vain and terrible all of creation would be. How miserable our lives would be if we were not a part of the chosen race. This is why people have a disdain for Calvinism, honestly. Calvinists act like the Jews of the New Testament. Salvation only belonged to them. They were the chosen ones."},{"kind":"para","text":"Jesus turned that all around by being a “light to the Gentiles, that thou mayest be my salvation unto the end of the earth.” Praise the Lord, His salvation is not limited. Anyone who calls themselves the “elect” is limiting the salvation of God, and I have no doubts that God will deal with those types quite easily and quickly."}]}]},{"start":7,"end":7,"title":"More Power","entries":[{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is another interesting thought: the rejection of Israel actually provided power to the gospel. That’s another victory sign of the Lord. The more people that reject Him, the more powerfully obvious His Word becomes. It’s actually a wild thing to think about! God’s Word is written in such a way that rejection provides more power to His Word. It’s giving me a headache even thinking about it right now… Everyone will despise the Lord, but there will be a time when even the kings of the Earth will bow down before Him."}]}]},{"start":8,"end":13,"title":"God's Salvation","entries":[{"start":8,"end":9,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God is King, yes, but He is also approachable. God has made His salvation effectual in such a way that we can accept it (undeservingly) yet hold it close as if it’s personable, yet open to the whole world. It’s yours, and yet it’s everybody’s. It’s an individual decision, yet it’s open to all."},{"kind":"para","text":"Furthermore, God is King; He has authority over everything. He could send anyone anywhere for any reason He wants. Yet, it’s God Himself who was seeking the lost. It is the light of the world that came into darkness to show Himself. He came to the prisoners of sin to set them free, giving them a direction to go in."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"The Spirit of the Lord is upon me, because he hath anointed me to preach the gospel to the poor; he hath sent me to heal the brokenhearted, to preach deliverance to the captives, and recovering of sight to the blind, to set at liberty them that are bruised,","ref":"Luke 4:18"}]},{"start":10,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Obviously, there is much more of a spiritual application here, but there will be a day when we will not have to worry about any of that. We won’t have to worry about food or water. We won’t have to worry about labor or weariness. We will be with the Lord, and He will supply us with everything we need. That is what a good friend should do, by the way. When we are feeling weak and defeated, the Lord should prepare men to be capable of giving encouragement and water to the needy. How rare a character trait that is today."},{"kind":"para","text":"God provides the needs for the hurting Christian, though. That is who we truly must depend on. God has had to remind me of that over and over again lately."}]},{"start":11,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"To a Christian led by the Lord, there is no impossible route. Every way the Lord leads is a journey that God will guide. Abraham was commissioned to simply get his family and leave."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Now the LORD had said unto Abram, Get thee out of thy country, and from thy kindred, and from thy father's house, unto a land that I will shew thee: And I will make of thee a great nation, and I will bless thee, and make thy name great; and thou shalt be a blessing: And I will bless them that bless thee, and curse him that curseth thee: and in thee shall all families of the earth be blessed.","ref":"Genesis 12:1-3"},{"kind":"para","text":"He was not told where he was going, just given a direction to follow. He embarked on a journey through deserts, mountains, and all sorts of rough terrain, simply because he was instructed to travel. Not once do we hear him complaining about the difficulty of the trek. Although he doubted God several times and even went his own way for a period, he worshipped the Lord wherever he went. He set up testimonies there of God’s future promises. That is what we should all be doing. Instead of complaining about the path that the Lord has led us on, we should probably figure out what kind of testimony we want to leave in those areas."}]},{"start":12,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"“Sinim” means “thorns.” The location of this place is debatable. Some say it was Egypt, while others suggest it was China. Strong’s Concordance simply describes it as “a people living at the extremity of the known world.”"},{"kind":"para","text":"Whoever they are, they can be included in the promise if they are willing to come to the Lord. No matter who YOU are today, you are included if you would like to come to the Lord. Again, God’s salvation is not limited."}]},{"start":13,"end":13,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Those who limit the salvation of the Lord can never truly sing songs of joy. They cannot sing songs of glory to the Lord. Why would they sing? Are they singing because God’s arm cannot save everyone? Are they singing because they are one of the elected? Are they singing because there is a world out there that has turned from the Lord, and God will have His vengeance on them? Are they singing for any other reason than the fact that God will comfort His people and give them mercy? If so, that is false worship."},{"kind":"para","text":"Singing will only occur to God’s children when they are willing to see the least likely of the world come to Christ because we know God’s salvation is open to anyone who is willing to call out to God."}]}]},{"start":14,"end":21,"title":"Surprised By the Lord","entries":[{"start":14,"end":14,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"How many times have you said this about the Lord? I have lost count of how many times I have thought this same thing. I know a lot of preachers will tell you how sinful you are for ever questioning God or wondering if God is paying attention."},{"kind":"para","text":"You are not alone in your thoughts. Every great character of faith has thought this. Noah thought it (as he was floating above the floods of the world, he imagined that the Lord might have forgotten about him):"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And God remembered Noah, and every living thing, and all the cattle that was with him in the ark: and God made a wind to pass over the earth, and the waters asswaged;","ref":"Genesis 8:1"},{"kind":"para","text":"Moses thought it (as he was tasked with talking to Pharoah about letting God's people go):"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And Moses said unto the LORD, O my Lord, I am not eloquent, neither heretofore, nor since thou hast spoken unto thy servant: but I am slow of speech, and of a slow tongue.","ref":"Exodus 4:10"},{"kind":"para","text":"David thought it:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"How long wilt thou forget me, O LORD? for ever? how long wilt thou hide thy face from me?","ref":"Psalm 13:1"},{"kind":"para","text":"Arguably, even Jesus thought it:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Now from the sixth hour there was darkness over all the land unto the ninth hour. And about the ninth hour Jesus cried with a loud voice, saying, Eli, Eli, lama sabachthani? that is to say, My God, my God, why hast thou forsaken me?","ref":"Matthew 27:45-46"},{"kind":"para","text":"Granted, on the cross of Christ, He was never forsaken. This was a quote from David, and another proven prophecy fulfilled. However, Jesus certainly felt that the Lord was turning away from the sin happening to His own Son. In that moment, Jesus cried out to God, His Father. That is the real example that is given. These other characters of the faith just cried out for attention. Jesus cried out for closeness. The others cried out to God for attention, while Jesus cried out for closeness. Jesus already had God’s attention, and He knew it. We should know it too. If we are going to take the example of any faith character, it should always be Jesus. If He felt forsaken, what would He do? Well, He would cry for closeness to God. He would cry out to the Lord for peace and closure."},{"kind":"para","text":"Zion was not doing that, though. They simply questioned God (like we all do) and said, “God doesn’t care about us. He has forsaken us. Let us do what we think is best.” Whenever we do what we think is best, it usually ends very poorly. Thankfully, God gives us a reminder that He IS paying attention. He hasn’t turned away from your trouble. He hasn’t left you in the dust."}]},{"start":15,"end":15,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"A woman who forgets her infant child is no mother at all. The fact that the Lord can even say this should bring some pain to our souls. It certainly brings hope to them. A woman today could go through hours of anguishing birth pains and yet somehow forget to feed her child. God says they “may forget.” The more important thing to note, however, is that God promises here that He will “not forget thee.” He cares more for His children than some mothers on this Earth do for their own flesh and blood. How does God prove that love? Well, He answers that in the next verse:"}]},{"start":16,"end":16,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I knew a sweet older lady who loved this verse dearly. She showed me her Bible, which was basically tearing at the seams with how many notes and how worn it was from her using it for so many years. She showed me her favorite verse, which was highlighted. She said, “Do you want to know how I know my name is engraved in the hands of God?” I replied, “Sure!” She said, “Because His hands were pierced with my name.” What a powerful testimony and what a powerful verse."},{"kind":"para","text":"God proved His love by piercing His hands with your name. He proved His love by sacrificing His own life for you. You can never say that God does not love you. Anyone who struggles with understanding God’s love does not understand God’s sacrifice."}]},{"start":17,"end":17,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God’s children will be set free. They might be physically held captive in these books, but we are spiritually held captive until the Lord sets us free. God will use the happenings of Israel to display a spiritual need for the world."},{"kind":"para","text":"Israel always thought that God was a God of physical prosperity. He certainly is, and can be. But the Lord values your spiritual prosperity far more than your physical one. You can be physically poor and spiritually wealthy. Woe to those who are spiritually poor and physically wealthy."}]},{"start":18,"end":18,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Most of us don’t see the glory of God because we are too busy looking down. I, personally, tend to look down when I walk. I look down a lot when I talk. I look down when I pray. I look down when I am on stage. I look down if I am in front of people. I look down when I read my Bible. I look down for almost everything. God tells us, over and over again throughout His Word, to look UP."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And when these things begin to come to pass, then look up, and lift up your heads; for your redemption draweth nigh.","ref":"Luke 21:28"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"I will lift up mine eyes unto the hills, from whence cometh my help. My help cometh from the LORD, which made heaven and earth.","ref":"Psalm 121:1-2"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Lift up your eyes on high, and behold who hath created these things, that bringeth out their host by number: he calleth them all by names by the greatness of his might, for that he is strong in power; not one faileth.","ref":"Isaiah 40:26"},{"kind":"para","text":"I miss what God does when I look down. I miss His goodness when I am depressed. I miss His moving when I am looking down. God wants us to be uplifted. God wants us to look up. There’s a perspective shift when we do this. Looking vertically first causes everything horizontally to fall into place."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Set your affection on things above, not on things on the earth.","ref":"Colossians 3:2"}]},{"start":19,"end":19,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God doesn’t just save us; He leads us away from danger. We have a new direction to go. Before we had the Lord, we were stuck going in one direction. We never even thought we could go in a different direction. We thought the path towards the Lord was only meant for other people, and it could never be for us. It was meant for a man far superior to me, a man who could be changed."},{"kind":"para","text":"I didn’t realize that we can ALL be changed if we would allow the Lord to do it. He changes us and sets us in a different direction, away from destruction. We just tend to sometimes look back. There was a woman who did that once, and it didn’t work out for her…"}]},{"start":20,"end":20,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is the real concern to me. I know what I believe. I know what my wife believes. I have a pretty good assumption of what my daughter believes. But what will happen to my daughter’s children, or their children after them? Does the faith die somewhere in my lineage? I pray to the Lord that it’s not the case."},{"kind":"para","text":"If the Israelites are an example, that is likely what will take place. Somewhere along my lineage, we will fall away from the Lord, and God is going to have to cause a great distress to the world to get us back on track (perhaps that would be His second coming, I do not know)."}]},{"start":21,"end":21,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"To know my children are saved is the greatest blessing of all. Honestly, I was surprised when my daughter accepted Christ. It’s something I had prayed for, but I thought she would be a lot like me. She wouldn’t consider it until she was far older and had to go through some terrible circumstances to get there. I’m glad she didn’t. I pray the Lord that He surprised me with my daughter’s salvation at a good young age. I pray that happens with her children as well, and it happens with my newborn."},{"kind":"para","text":"That will be what it’s like for the Israelites when they come back to their land. They will think and feel as if they had lost everything. Truly, they will have. But God will give them more than they had before, and it will be a double blessing to them, knowing that they could easily lose it all if they live unrighteously before the Lord. Anyone who isn’t living righteously before God doesn’t know what true loss is like. Being lost after knowing the Lord is a very painful journey that most Christians will experience at one point in their faith or another."}]}]},{"start":22,"end":23,"title":"Building a Life","entries":[{"start":22,"end":22,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"You know what salvation brings (obviously besides a home in Heaven and forgiveness of sins)? It brings peace. It makes you love your children a little harder and hold them a little closer. It makes you love your wife a little deeper and care for her a little better. It makes you see your neighbor as valuable and serve people a little more frequently."},{"kind":"para","text":"It gives you the ability to see the world from the eyes of a loving, gracious, and merciful God while the rest of the world sees itself as evil and oppressed. God has a very different viewpoint of you than everyone else does of you. You will see from the Lord’s perspective in this world, and (quite frankly) we need more of that today."}]},{"start":23,"end":23,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I think there is a lot of depth we can pull from this verse. Obviously, this is speaking about Israel (of course). The nations that have taken them captive will come to worship the Lord through these people. It will be a complete turnaround for God’s children. Those people who took them and mistreated them will be looking for mercy from them."},{"kind":"para","text":"It’s also a future hope for the church (or at least for the Lord in the future age). One day, scripture says that every knee will bow (we read about that a couple of chapters back already). I believe that day will only come when the Lord returns for the second time and completely ends evil on this Earth. That is when every knee will buckle. That is when the “kings” will be “nursing fathers” for God’s children. That is when the people who martyred, hated, and hurt the children of God will lick the dust of your feet. Not what I want for them, but it’s what they will end up doing because of their desire to fight against the Lord (who, once again, is always victorious)."}]}]},{"start":24,"end":26,"title":"Burying Yourself","entries":[{"start":24,"end":25,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Future generations benefit from your faith today. That is something we often don’t think about. We are so caught up with our personal examples that we tend to forget that there is a generation that will be here when we die. Our example means nothing if we are not teaching and training those under us to take up the mantle, so to speak. They need to know how to lead, what to do, and what faith looks like. They need to see you living in a way that sets them up for success, not just setting yourself up for it. Success can be better defined as giving the next generation a strong foundation. That’s not the world’s idea of success, though. Today, success means “I have more than you.” God doesn’t want that to be our definition of success. He wants our definition to be “I’ll give you more than me.” Feeding the homeless (in the world’s eyes) is giving them enough to suffice them. That, to them, is success. Feeding the homeless (in the Lord’s eyes) is giving them more than you have. That is what success looks like."}]},{"start":26,"end":26,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The most powerful ones of this world will become the weakest ones of this world. That is how we will know that God is on the throne. He will exalt the weak and humble the strong. I love seeing a prideful man humbled. It’s one of the greatest gifts of life. Why? Well, because I know how it feels to be put in my place. The Lord will put all the evil in this world in their place, and they will face the consequences of their own pride. It will return back onto themselves."},{"kind":"para","text":"Whatever mountain you build in this life will be the mountain you’re buried in. It will be the mountain that covers you. Will it be a mountain of pride? Will it be a mountain of evil and error? Will it be a mountain of pain and suffering? A mountain of wealth and fortune? Or, will it be a mountain of grace? A mountain of love? A mountain of selflessness? A humble mountain. A humble mountain is much softer to be buried by than a prideful one."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":9},{"start":10,"end":10},{"start":11,"end":11},{"start":12,"end":12},{"start":13,"end":13},{"start":14,"end":14},{"start":15,"end":15},{"start":16,"end":16},{"start":17,"end":17},{"start":18,"end":18},{"start":19,"end":19},{"start":20,"end":20},{"start":21,"end":21},{"start":22,"end":22},{"start":23,"end":23},{"start":24,"end":25},{"start":26,"end":26}],"verses":{"1":"Listen, O isles, unto me; and hearken, ye people, from far; The Lord hath called me from the womb; from the bowels of my mother hath he made mention of my name.","2":"And he hath made my mouth like a sharp sword; in the shadow of his hand hath he hid me, and made me a polished shaft; in his quiver hath he hid me;","3":"And said unto me, Thou art my servant, O Israel, in whom I will be glorified.","4":"Then I said, I have laboured in vain, I have spent my strength for nought, and in vain: yet surely my judgment is with the Lord, and my work with my God.","5":"And now, saith the Lord that formed me from the womb to be his servant, to bring Jacob again to him, Though Israel be not gathered, yet shall I be glorious in the eyes of the Lord, and my God shall be my strength.","6":"And he said, It is a light thing that thou shouldest be my servant to raise up the tribes of Jacob, and to restore the preserved of Israel: I will also give thee for a light to the Gentiles, that thou mayest be my salvation unto the end of the earth.","7":"Thus saith the Lord, the Redeemer of Israel, and his Holy One, to him whom man despiseth, to him whom the nation abhorreth, to a servant of rulers, Kings shall see and arise, princes also shall worship, because of the Lord that is faithful, and the Holy One of Israel, and he shall choose thee.","8":"Thus saith the Lord, In an acceptable time have I heard thee, and in a day of salvation have I helped thee: and I will preserve thee, and give thee for a covenant of the people, to establish the earth, to cause to inherit the desolate heritages;","9":"That thou mayest say to the prisoners, Go forth; to them that are in darkness, Shew yourselves. They shall feed in the ways, and their pastures shall be in all high places.","10":"They shall not hunger nor thirst; neither shall the heat nor sun smite them: for he that hath mercy on them shall lead them, even by the springs of water shall he guide them.","11":"And I will make all my mountains a way, and my highways shall be exalted.","12":"Behold, these shall come from far: and, lo, these from the north and from the west; and these from the land of Sinim.","13":"Sing, O heavens; and be joyful, O earth; and break forth into singing, O mountains: for the Lord hath comforted his people, and will have mercy upon his afflicted.","14":"But Zion said, The Lord hath forsaken me, and my Lord hath forgotten me.","15":"Can a woman forget her sucking child, that she should not have compassion on the son of her womb? yea, they may forget, yet will I not forget thee.","16":"Behold, I have graven thee upon the palms of my hands; thy walls are continually before me.","17":"Thy children shall make haste; thy destroyers and they that made thee waste shall go forth of thee.","18":"Lift up thine eyes round about, and behold: all these gather themselves together, and come to thee. As I live, saith the Lord, thou shalt surely clothe thee with them all, as with an ornament, and bind them on thee, as a bride doeth.","19":"For thy waste and thy desolate places, and the land of thy destruction, shall even now be too narrow by reason of the inhabitants, and they that swallowed thee up shall be far away.","20":"The children which thou shalt have, after thou hast lost the other, shall say again in thine ears, The place is too strait for me: give place to me that I may dwell.","21":"Then shalt thou say in thine heart, Who hath begotten me these, seeing I have lost my children, and am desolate, a captive, and removing to and fro? and who hath brought up these? Behold, I was left alone; these, where had they been?","22":"Thus saith the Lord God, Behold, I will lift up mine hand to the Gentiles, and set up my standard to the people: and they shall bring thy sons in their arms, and thy daughters shall be carried upon their shoulders.","23":"And kings shall be thy nursing fathers, and their queens thy nursing mothers: they shall bow down to thee with their face toward the earth, and lick up the dust of thy feet; and thou shalt know that I am the Lord: for they shall not be ashamed that wait for me.","24":"Shall the prey be taken from the mighty, or the lawful captive delivered?","25":"But thus saith the Lord, Even the captives of the mighty shall be taken away, and the prey of the terrible shall be delivered: for I will contend with him that contendeth with thee, and I will save thy children.","26":"And I will feed them that oppress thee with their own flesh; and they shall be drunken with their own blood, as with sweet wine: and all flesh shall know that I the Lord am thy Saviour and thy Redeemer, the mighty One of Jacob."}},
    "50": {"chapter":50,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: In our previous chapters, God has been making it a point to lead everything to the salvation message. There is an ultimate purpose behind all of this and it's a future use of turning back to the Lord in trust and faith. God wants His children to lean on Him, not on their material possessions. We get gifted with so much from the Lord that it falls apart when we start hoarding His gifts and rejecting His presence."},{"kind":"para","text":"In this chapter, that is what God will point out. He will point out the purpose of this trial and dilemma that Israel is going through, and He will point to how they have been treating Him, and what His future salvation will lead to (and look like). Salvation was not an easy gift to give. We didn't make it easy on the Lord to provide His salvation for us. It had to be done through immense pain, persecution, and suffering, and Isaiah is going to point out how that looked from the eyes of Christ in this chapter (and in the chapters to come)."}],"previously":["In our previous chapters, God has been making it a point to lead everything to the salvation message. There is an ultimate purpose behind all of this, and it’s a future use of turning back to the Lord in trust and faith. God wants His children to lean on Him, not on their material possessions. We are gifted with so much from the Lord that it falls apart when we start hoarding His gifts and rejecting His presence. In this chapter, that is what God will point out. He will highlight the purpose of this trial and dilemma that Israel is going through, and He will point to how they have been treating Him and what His future salvation will lead to (and look like). Salvation was not an easy gift to give. We didn’t make it easy on the Lord to provide His salvation for us. It had to be done through immense pain, persecution, and suffering, and Isaiah is going to point out how that looked from the eyes of Christ in this chapter (and in the chapters to come)."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":3,"title":"Rejects","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"So here’s the heart of the problem. We can spend a lot of time questioning God and blaming Him for all the problems we are facing, but in all reality, it is our own faults that we find ourselves in these predicaments. God says, “Did I put you here? Did I sell you to these people? Was it me that disowned you?” Of course, that’s not the case. God doesn’t run away from His responsibilities over His own children. In fact, even in the middle of suffering, God is there watching over us and planning pinpoint specific methods and directions for every individual. He doesn’t just wait up there to try and destroy you the moment you do something wrong."},{"kind":"para","text":"Often times (at least from personal experience and that of the proof of scripture), God allows quite a bit of resistance before He finally just lets you have what you think you want. He will warn, and warn, and drive against your desires. He will show you why it might be a bad idea. He will give every specific reason for you not to go down that path, but it’s up to us with which path we might take. It is by our own devices that we are sold to the enemy. We sell ourselves when we are not willing to obey and listen to the Lord. That is the truth of it. And yet God is there to buy you back. Like a wayward wife who has been doing all sorts of heinous things behind her husband’s back, He waits to forgive you the moment you turn to Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"I don’t know about you, but I would certainly have a hard time forgiving my wife if she was living in a way that completely sold herself against me. Why would anyone forgive someone that has completely mistreated your trust over and over again? Why would I have put someone like that back in my life? I would constantly worry that she would do it all over again. Not to boast for myself or anything, but I have never given her a reason to do something so serious as to cheat on me or break our bonds and trust. We have been quite open and determined towards each other, and it would seem very pointed if she was trying to hurt me by acting as if we were not married or (worse yet) dating other people. Everyone would know that she was just trying to hurt me. That makes her look evil. Yet that is how we treat the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"Whether we believe in the Lord or not, God’s creation has largely rejected Him. Even worse is there are Christians who have simply turned away from the Lord. These are God’s own people. Yet, God is there, ready to forgive. And the moment He forgives, it is as if none of those things ever happened. I pray I can be just as forgiving. God can do that, though, because He knows your heart’s true desires. We can only see actions."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God came to save, yet there were not many who wanted it. Jesus’ whole purpose in life and ministry was to save the wayward. He wanted to give hope and redemption to the lost culture of this world. I think every human can look out and have a desire to see this world change. We are all born with an innate nature to see people turn to good things and do what is right. But we cannot change people. There is nothing we can do or say that would get people to truly change from their ways of living. They would have to do that themselves, and as long as what they are doing feels good to themselves, they won’t change. They might attempt it, but it won’t last."},{"kind":"para","text":"No. True, lasting change does not happen by self-will and overcoming personal perseverance. It can only come through the gospel. The Gospel changes a mind. It rewires our brains. It tells us, “Hey, those things that you think are good are not accepted by the Lord.” At that moment, we don’t simply stop what we are doing, but we certainly begin to resist. We suddenly don’t want to hurt our creator with those things anymore. He loves us enough to die for us; we should love Him enough to give up our sins. Honestly, that is the most beautiful thing about the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord could have said, “I have died for you, now you must die for me,” but that is not what He recounts. He says, “I have died for you, now you accept that love and live in it.” Though, if you look at all the other religions, that is ultimately what they are saying. They are saying, “You must DIE for your God in order for you to be accepted.” God says, “You must accept my death in order to have a relationship with me.”"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For if, when we were enemies, we were reconciled to God by the death of his Son, much more, being reconciled, we shall be saved by his life. And not only so, but we also joy in God through our Lord Jesus Christ, by whom we have now received the atonement.","ref":"Romans 5:10-11"}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God hurts when His creation rejects Him. Actually, all of Heaven hurts because of it. In the end times, there will be major signs that God is hurting from the majority rejection of His creation:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And I beheld when he had opened the sixth seal, and, lo, there was a great earthquake; and the sun became black as sackcloth of hair, and the moon became as blood;","ref":"Revelation 6:12"},{"kind":"para","text":"People will witness the literal change of the Earth and sky, yet they will still reject the Lord. They will continue to live in their sins, and as the Lord demonstrates His hurt from it, it will only cause this world to reject God more. It’s like seeing a crying child who was abandoned by its parents and then punching it in the face for crying. To some people, that thought-provoking image might be funny, but to those with compassion, we know that it would be wrong and cruel."},{"kind":"para","text":"God is hurt by rejection. He is not necessarily hurt by unbelief. He is not hurt by your sin (especially if you are His child). He is hurt by your continual rejection and desire to go the opposite way from Him. The best representation of this is found in Isaiah 53, but I can’t spoil anything just yet because it’s such a good chapter. It’s really the meat of this book. Just know this: you might reject the Lord, but the Lord will never reject you."}]}]},{"start":4,"end":9,"title":"The Lord Feels","entries":[{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Honestly, we could acclaim that Solomon was the wisest man to have ever lived, but there is no one wiser than our Lord Jesus Christ. He is the embodiment of Wisdom, as we have spoken about extensively in Proverbs. Wisdom IS Christ. He was gifted the “tongue of the learned” because He was the originator of the tongue. The reason for this is so He can encourage and comfort those who are in hurt and struggle. He wants to “speak a word in season to him that is weary.” A well “seasoned” word of encouragement during a difficult time in someone’s life can make the difference between fate and futility."},{"kind":"para","text":"There are a lot of people on the verge of giving up. What they might be giving up, I could not say. It varies from person to person. We, as believers with the ability to understand and preach the word, are capable of giving direction, encouragement, and compassion to those who are struggling in the fight of life and faith. Yet, I don’t see many standing up and speaking up. I see a lot of people cowering down and hiding from those who are hurt. The church is for people who need help and community. If we are only focused on our church brand, the church’s looks, the way we act, or the events we put on, we are missing the only important ministry the Lord has given us: loving on hurting people."},{"kind":"para","text":"I have counseled (more times than I’d like to admit in several churches now) so many people who feel rejected by their pastors. They feel as if they don’t matter, as if they are just another burden to add to the shelf of church hurts. They feel used honestly, and for good reason. A word in season would have made the difference between suffering alone and hope in community. The bigger problem is, if people don’t find encouragement and help with their faith in the church, they will certainly find it in the world, and that won’t be beneficial for people but for a short time."},{"kind":"para","text":"If you are a believer in Christ, you have also been given “the tongue of the learned” through the Holy Spirit of God. He gives you the ability to provide absolute truths to others that this world cannot provide. They will tell you what feels good, but that’s about it. Church leaders must be zealous for this ministry if they want to prepare the church for spiritual warfare within the church. That is ultimately what we need to consider the most, if I can be honest. We are so caught up reaching the lost that we forsake the saved right under our noses, and they are the pillars and gap fillers."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And I sought for a man among them, that should make up the hedge, and stand in the gap before me for the land, that I should not destroy it: but I found none.","ref":"Ezekiel 22:30"}]},{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Christ sets the example here. If we want to successfully minister to people and show genuine compassion and correct direction in this life, we must not reject the Lord. Rejecting God is the same as rebelling against Him. Nobody likes a rebellious person unless it’s for the right cause. Is rebelling against the Lord the right cause? I don’t see how it ever could be. He is nothing but good to us and has given us no reason to rebel against Him. Satan has done nothing but evil things to us, and we accept him as if he were our god. We have everything so backwards…"}]},{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I have no doubt that Isaiah faced persecution, but this is certainly the perspective of Christ:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Then did they spit in his face, and buffeted him; and others smote him with the palms of their hands, Saying, Prophesy unto us, thou Christ, Who is he that smote thee? Now Peter sat without in the palace: and a damsel came unto him, saying, Thou also wast with Jesus of Galilee.","ref":"Matthew 26:67-69"},{"kind":"para","text":"Isaiah didn’t deserve this treatment, but it could certainly be counted as deserved for his sins. He was still a sinner, but a changed man by the Lord. There is no sin found in Christ:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Who did no sin, neither was guile found in his mouth:","ref":"1 Peter 2:22"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For we have not an high priest which cannot be touched with the feeling of our infirmities; but was in all points tempted like as we are, yet without sin.","ref":"Hebrews 4:15"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For he hath made him to be sin for us, who knew no sin; that we might be made the righteousness of God in him.","ref":"2 Corinthians 5:21"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And ye know that he was manifested to take away our sins; and in him is no sin.","ref":"1 John 3:5"},{"kind":"para","text":"If there was anyone who deserved this kind of treatment, it definitely was not the Son of God. Yet, it says here that He “gave” Himself to this treatment. He allowed it for the sake of salvation. He wanted the world to be saved, and this was the only way they would see their need for salvation."},{"kind":"para","text":"If people cannot see their injustice in killing and crucifying an innocent man who never did anything worthy of this kind of punishment, they were and will always be lost to the Lord. I don’t see how anyone can look to the cross and not feel anguish for what humanity has done to this innocent man (whether He was truly God or not). It should open our eyes to how dastardly our human nature truly is and how far gone away from good and righteousness we have gotten."}]},{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"We all should know, at least in some way, that going to the cross was a difficult thing for the Lord to experience. He had the ability to feel no pain, but He chose to suffer. As I typed that sentence, it astounds me to think about. We go through pains in this life by “happenstance.” Trials and tests come without our knowing. If we were given the option between going through the trial with pain or without pain, we would ALL choose to go through it without pain. Yet it’s the pain that makes us stronger."},{"kind":"para","text":"Jesus could plan for His pain. He could have chosen to reject any sort of pain and still have died a cruel death. But He wanted to experience the pain. Why? Well, because it proves His love all the more. You cannot look at the suffering on the cross as a cruel thing from God. No. The suffering on the cross was an image of God’s love for you. He proved it by His suffering. That is how we can ultimately prove ALL love on this Earth."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"I thank my God always on your behalf, for the grace of God which is given you by Jesus Christ; That in every thing ye are enriched by him, in all utterance, and in all knowledge; Even as the testimony of Christ was confirmed in you: So that ye come behind in no gift; waiting for the coming of our Lord Jesus Christ:","ref":"1 Corinthians 1:4-7"},{"kind":"para","text":"The word for “Charity” in Greek is the same as the word used for “Sacrificial love.” The type of love that Jesus displayed on the cross was a “Charity” love. Charity gives. Jesus gave His love to humanity, but only through His suffering. He felt the pain, yet He did it with joy because He knew that God would help Him every step of the way. And the Lord did!"},{"kind":"para","text":"This is why I don’t hold to the assertion that Jesus went to Hell after He died. Not only is that not the reward for a saved man (and I don’t think I have to argue the notion that Jesus was a saved man), but it’s also not likely how He went through that suffering with joy. He had joy to suffer on the cross because it meant eternity with His Father. That’s the picture He painted for every believer. We can have joy to suffer too, because we have eternity with our Father through Jesus’ gift of salvation to us."},{"kind":"para","text":"Jesus kept course, and He proved that living for the Lord is worth suffering on this Earth for. What a strange sentence to write out, but it’s true. If you are going to live for the Lord, you will suffer for it. Jesus thought it was worth dying for. Do we feel the same way about our faith?"}]},{"start":8,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Jesus stands for Himself. Honestly, Jesus stands for everyone that belongs to the Lord. No one can fight against Him and win. People try. Satan certainly tries. He tries to attack Christ by attacking the Lord’s children. He attacks Christ by attacking Christians. But Jesus has the final say. Jesus has the victory. He is already living in victory. The resurrection is proof of Jesus’ victory. Not even death itself can stand up against Jesus and win. Death may “defeat” us, but it will not defeat the Lord. The defeat of death (to a believer) is but a moment in time. The defeat of death (to an unbeliever) is an eternal mistake."}]},{"start":9,"end":9,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord doesn't age. We are bound by time and death. The Lord is bound by nothing. He stands outside of it all. We must look quite silly to the Lord when we live against Him. How small and sad our lives are without the directives of God."}]}]},{"start":10,"end":11,"title":"Two Lights","entries":[{"start":10,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God invites us to “trust in the name of the Lord, and stay upon his God.” By the way, in God’s name (alone) there is great power. Just trusting in the NAME of Jesus is sufficient enough. The name, of course, is attached to the person and purpose. But Jesus (God with Us) is what we must believe and trust in if we want to search out the truths of the gospel."},{"kind":"para","text":"Without trusting in the name, we are never going to trust in the legitimacy of the biblical accounts. It was not Muhammad or Buddha whose name is written in these pages. It is Jesus Christ."}]},{"start":11,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is religion. In verse 10, we have the life of a believing man who is invited to trust in the Lord’s light for guidance and assurance of salvation. In contrast, religion, as described in verse 11, invites you to create your own light to walk in, trusting in your own guidance and assurance of salvation. The problem is, when I am left to my own devices, I always make the wrong choice. This is why religion is vain, dead, and all works and no faith. You cannot have the light of the Lord when you are trying to create your own. God says you will “lie down in sorrow” for trying it your own way. Our way of doing things always leads us to more pain. The Lord’s way of doing things might lead us to pain, but we will gladly suffer for our faith to increase in Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"When we suffer without Him, we do not strengthen our faith; we callous our hearts. When we suffer with Him, we strengthen our faith and lean more into His arms. If suffering and trials do not lead you to trust God more, you are not suffering for the faith; you are suffering for yourself. That only leads to sorrow."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":9},{"start":10,"end":10},{"start":11,"end":11}],"verses":{"1":"Thus saith the Lord, Where is the bill of your mother's divorcement, whom I have put away? or which of my creditors is it to whom I have sold you? Behold, for your iniquities have ye sold yourselves, and for your transgressions is your mother put away.","2":"Wherefore, when I came, was there no man? when I called, was there none to answer? Is my hand shortened at all, that it cannot redeem? or have I no power to deliver? behold, at my rebuke I dry up the sea, I make the rivers a wilderness: their fish stinketh, because there is no water, and dieth for thirst.","3":"I clothe the heavens with blackness, and I make sackcloth their covering.","4":"The Lord God hath given me the tongue of the learned, that I should know how to speak a word in season to him that is weary: he wakeneth morning by morning, he wakeneth mine ear to hear as the learned.","5":"The Lord God hath opened mine ear, and I was not rebellious, neither turned away back.","6":"I gave my back to the smiters, and my cheeks to them that plucked off the hair: I hid not my face from shame and spitting.","7":"For the Lord God will help me; therefore shall I not be confounded: therefore have I set my face like a flint, and I know that I shall not be ashamed.","8":"He is near that justifieth me; who will contend with me? let us stand together: who is mine adversary? let him come near to me.","9":"Behold, the Lord God will help me; who is he that shall condemn me? lo, they all shall wax old as a garment; the moth shall eat them up.","10":"Who is among you that feareth the Lord, that obeyeth the voice of his servant, that walketh in darkness, and hath no light? let him trust in the name of the Lord, and stay upon his God.","11":"Behold, all ye that kindle a fire, that compass yourselves about with sparks: walk in the light of your fire, and in the sparks that ye have kindled. This shall ye have of mine hand; ye shall lie down in sorrow."}},
    "51": {"chapter":51,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: The last few chapters have been very encouraging and uplifting to the people of God. As a reader, we have the great privilege to look back at the history of Israel and learn some lessons for the future of this world. They only had the ability to simply listen to Isaiah or reject Isaiah (you can take a guess as to what they choose to do). It's been a great joy to read this past few chapters, and they have been a huge help to me (as a studier) to learn some lessons and fix some practices."},{"kind":"para","text":"This chapter is just as good, but with a much deeper and more difficult message. Of course the message is for Israel, but it certainly resonates with our generation today, and with where I see the future generations going from here. God's truth lasts for all ages, and it would be triumphantly wise of us to listen to His warnings, and take His examples of providence (as well as chastisement) seriously."}],"previously":["The last few chapters have been very encouraging and uplifting to the people of God. As a reader, we have the great privilege of looking back at the history of Israel and learning some lessons for the future of this world. They only had the ability to simply listen to Isaiah or reject Isaiah (you can take a guess as to what they chose to do). It’s been a great joy to read these past few chapters, and they have been a huge help to me (as a studier) to learn some lessons and fix some practices. This chapter is just as good, but with a much deeper and more difficult message. Of course, the message is for Israel, but it certainly resonates with our generation today and with where I see the future generations going from here. God’s truth lasts for all ages, and it would be triumphantly wise of us to listen to His warnings and take His examples of providence (as well as chastisement) seriously."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":3,"title":"Digging Roots","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This chapter is going to be an evaluation of the people of Israel. God starts off by calling these people to remember where they came from and how they got here. It has only been by the grace of God and the gifting of God that they have survived this long. It will only be, then, by the rejection and burden of the Lord that they will also lose it all. He asks them to look to Him, though, and He has not given up on hoping for their obedience. He still calls out to this world today. He calls out to every being in His creation. He calls out to the leaders and to the lowlifes. He calls out to the preachers and to the listeners. He calls out to the saints and to the sinners."},{"kind":"para","text":"Yet, we see most people have a hard time accepting and listening. Some think that the Lord is different from what scripture says He is. They have this idea that God is just angry with mankind all the time, and honestly, who could blame Him if He was? Some think that He is all love, and there are no consequences from the Lord for actions. God is just. He is a balanced weight. He can take care of the fool and the wise in His own way. He will give what is just for your cause. Period."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God has provided examples throughout history of His goodness, and they all knew and believed in Abraham. In fact, I think most of the world believes there was a man named Abraham quite some time ago. Abraham has made such an impact that it would be futile to try and deny his existence. Yet, Jesus is far more recent, and more people want to try and contest His actual existence, even though there is far more evidence of Jesus than there is of Abraham. But I digress."},{"kind":"para","text":"Abraham was a man full of faith. We can look back on his story and see him being continually pushed into submission, but he emerges in the end with his faith full to the brim, even overflowing. God took this one man and made a multitude of people from him. He took Sarah and blessed her with a child. By the faith of this one man, all these people were able to be moved into this land and into God’s promises. Yet, they don’t seem to think that God is a just, wise, and giving God. They are living in opposition to the Lord and have rejected the historical accuracy of God’s goodness towards them, even though they have been stubborn and difficult to reach."},{"kind":"para","text":"Every step of the way, from Genesis to Isaiah (and from Isaiah to Revelation), God’s people have pushed against God. We do not make anything easy for the Lord, and yet God is patient and willing. We have given Him every reason to give up, and He still hasn’t given up. But the truth is in the faith promises. Abraham knew what God promised, but he only moved by faith that the promise would actually be kept. He didn’t get to see God’s promises kept; he just needed to believe God would keep them."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Israelites, at this moment in history, can look back and trace God’s movement throughout all their generations, seeing the promises that God has so obviously kept, and know that God will keep His future promises as well. Notice that God does not bring them back to Adam and Eve but brings them to Abraham and Sarah. Why? Wouldn’t it be wise for the Lord to bring them all the way back to the initial promise? Well, the promise of the land doesn’t come until Abraham. The promise of the people doesn’t come until Abraham and Sarah. The fact that these people are even alive and have the ability to reject God is because God kept a promise to Abraham. If not for Abraham, these people would have been done away with a long time ago."},{"kind":"para","text":"Furthermore, Abraham had to experience a lot of the world’s culture and fight through it multiple times over for the sake of his faith in the Lord. If Abraham can do it alone (with only the help of his family against the culture of the world), they can do it with the help of their whole culture."}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Now we are called to the very beginning. We are called to Eden. He speaks specifically about Zion here. He wants to rescue His people there. David had made this Zion place a monument to God’s presence and authority. God wants to bring that picture back to it. It will become like Eden, which is the Lord’s garden. He says, “Joy and gladness shall be found therein, thanksgiving, and the voice of melody.”"},{"kind":"para","text":"Eden must have been quite a beautiful place to live. Everything had to be perfect. I’m sure someday we will see it, but for the time being, we can only imagine what it was like. Zion will be a place like that at some point in history, and I believe the Lord will turn it into this image He is presenting here."}]}]},{"start":4,"end":6,"title":"True Evolution","entries":[{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"We must remember, once again, that prophecies are three-fold. This case has not been lost on us. We can sometimes think that when God speaks about “His people,” He is talking about the church. That is true, too. However, God specifically mentions Israel as well. If God didn’t want Israel as a part of the future promise (like some are inclined to believe), then He would not mention Israel that way, or He would say in some way that Israel refers to the church when it’s mentioned. Of course, that isn’t the case. The case is that God loves the Israelites and loves His people. That is why it’s worded like this by Paul:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For I am not ashamed of the gospel of Christ: for it is the power of God unto salvation to every one that believeth; to the Jew first, and also to the Greek.","ref":"Romans 1:16"},{"kind":"para","text":"The promises of God were to the Jews first. Whether we want to accept that or not doesn’t change the fact that Jesus came to the Israelites for His ministry, rather than to or through another nation. He came to the Jew first. He came to Israel first. If that offends you, I don’t know what to tell you. You will have to be upset with God that He isn’t done with Israel yet. The promises of God are kept through Jesus Christ, who is a Jew, and to His people, who also were Jews. Then it came to the rest of the world, and we are grafted into that lineage because of Jesus Christ alone."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Jews probably don’t like it. Most probably hate it, in fact. That is likely the reason why they don’t want to accept Christ. They don’t want tainted blood in their lineage. But all their blood is tainted since the beginning. Their ancestors were having children with people from all sorts of walks of life, especially in the days of Isaiah. That is why they have all fallen for so much idolatry and iniquity. They have forsaken the Lord’s commands for purity and holiness to chase after fleshly gods that make them feel good. In order to do that, though, they would marry and sleep with people who belonged to those fake gods. There is no such thing as a pure-blooded Jew today. They are all Jews by country, not by lineage."}]},{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Once again, the promise is given to the Israelites, and the world. We are benefactors of God's promise here. He says His \"righteousness\" is near. That is Jesus Christ. He is the righteous one."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"My little children, these things write I unto you, that ye sin not. And if any man sin, we have an advocate with the Father, Jesus Christ the righteous: And he is the propitiation for our sins: and not for ours only, but also for the sins of the whole world.","ref":"1 John 2:1-2"},{"kind":"para","text":"It’s an interesting picture God is painting in this particular verse. He has said several times before that we can trust in His “name” as salvation. In this verse, He says that people from all walks of life (that is, the isles) will trust in His arm, not just His name. That is a present part of God. It’s not just a thought, prayer, or idea; it’s a physical presence of the Lord. We will be able to lean on God’s physical arm for strength and help. I believe that will be literal in some ways for some people, but it’s also a very obvious and spiritual connection to the Holy Ghost, which is given to everyone who believes. He provides an arm for every believer to lean on. He knows you won’t find any arms to lean on here, so He provides His own."}]},{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"When we look to the Earth, do we see prosperity, unity, and immense growth? Perhaps there was a time we could have looked at this planet and said that it was seemingly moving in the right direction. However, as long as I’ve been alive, it feels (to me anyway) that things are progressively getting worse. I think the main goal for every person before they leave this Earth is to leave it a little better than when they came in. The truth is, though, that we will not be able to do that. The Earth is rusted. It’s corroded. As time goes on, the Earth becomes more and more devolved. This puts a pretty significant plot hole in the idea that evolution could ever have been real. Nothing on this Earth has evolved. We have only seen evidence of devolution (devil-ution; you see what I did there?)."},{"kind":"para","text":"God has given us permission to look upon the Earth in our day and evaluate its trajectory. Since the time of Isaiah’s writing, it has not changed today. The heavens are still vanishing away like smoke, and the earth is still waxing old like a garment, and everyone is going to die in like manner. But there is ONE change in history. There is ONE thing that seems to evolve through time (though it doesn’t change, it just gets bigger and more precious). That is God’s promises. His salvation promise is forever, and His righteousness will never end. We cannot leave this world better than when we came, but our souls can. Our souls go to a better place when we have the Lord. THAT is true progress. Without God’s salvation and presence, we will just regress with the rest of the world."}]}]},{"start":7,"end":8,"title":"Obvious Actions","entries":[{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Following the Lord will always experience pushback from this world. Anyone who desires to live in righteousness, even if they don’t talk to anyone else about it, will always be viewed as weird and cruel. This world hates righteousness, and so they will hate you for living in it. Arguably, because the world hates righteousness, they hate the Lord who is connected to it. Righteousness only comes from Him, so they are ultimately saying that they hate their Creator. The reason they hate Him so much is because He is against everything they think is good."},{"kind":"para","text":"I kind of laugh at the news at this point. The mainstream media today has lost all hope. They have gone so overboard with this thing and that thing, and have become a very vocal voice for politics today. We don’t listen to a news network anymore because they are honest and truthful. We listen to them because they are a part of our political party and agenda now. But the news is full of obvious stories today, and it makes me chuckle. “This just in, a liar was actually found lying today. There’s footage of a baby crying. A thief was caught stealing. A murderer murdered someone.” It’s unbelievable to this world that sinners do what sinners do. They are shocked and appalled that a liar would lie. This is news to the world. How is that anything new to this world? How is this at all surprising to anyone?"},{"kind":"para","text":"If men are standing against you for living righteously, or they are trying to tear your faith down, don’t be surprised. Sinful people are going to do sinful things. That should not surprise a Christian. That should not surprise this world. The news and media just look stupid at this point. They have no idea what to say and do, and they are completely dumbfounded by the fact that people will do what they have always done. Shocker."}]},{"start":8,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God’s salvation and love do not fail; they will never go away. It is interesting that God ties His salvation as something that “shall be for ever” with righteousness. There are many people who believe that this world cannot be saved once the tribulation comes or once the rapture happens. We still have a great mystery from the Lord, and that is when the rapture will take place. However, the greater mystery is why God would allow open access to salvation during that time when He knows that everyone in the world is ultimately just going to reject it anyway."},{"kind":"para","text":"His salvation can still be reached, though, until Christ’s second coming. Once that happens, judgment is here. Beforehand, Jesus pays your fine. If you wait until He returns again, He becomes your judge."}]}]},{"start":9,"end":11,"title":"Humility and Pride","entries":[{"start":9,"end":9,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"\"Rahab\" means \"breadth\" or “pride.\" It's usually associated with Egypt. The Lord has cut pride, and wounded the dragon from the beginning of time."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Thou hast broken Rahab in pieces, as one that is slain; thou hast scattered thine enemies with thy strong arm.","ref":"Psalm 89:10"},{"kind":"para","text":"God speaks about crushing Satan’s head in Genesis as the final blow to Satan’s attack on mankind. Eventually, the Lord will completely destroy the dragon, not just wound him. I’m glad the Lord speaks on this matter because we would be completely lost and hopeless if He didn’t give us the avenue of overcoming this."},{"kind":"para","text":"Another acclamation of evolution is our personal ability to overcome by our own strength and virtue. If God had never said that pride was wrong, we would live in pride. Actually, those who don’t know the promises and strength of the Lord do live in pride. They are always prideful people who live against God. That is a good litmus test in your church and in your workforce. Is the person prideful? If yes, you can bet any money that they are not following the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord teaches us over and over throughout His Word about the importance of rejecting pride. He gives us every avenue possible to humble ourselves. That is the truest sign of a believer; it’s their humility."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Every one that is proud in heart is an abomination to the LORD: though hand join in hand, he shall not be unpunished.","ref":"Proverbs 16:5"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But he giveth more grace. Wherefore he saith, God resisteth the proud, but giveth grace unto the humble.","ref":"James 4:6"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Pride goeth before destruction, and an haughty spirit before a fall.","ref":"Proverbs 16:18"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"The fear of the LORD is to hate evil: pride, and arrogancy, and the evil way, and the froward mouth, do I hate.","ref":"Proverbs 8:13"},{"kind":"para","text":"These are just to name a few. God wants HUMBLE followers. Not prideful ones."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Let nothing be done through strife or vainglory; but in lowliness of mind let each esteem other better than themselves.","ref":"Philippians 2:3"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For whosoever exalteth himself shall be abased; and he that humbleth himself shall be exalted.","ref":"Luke 14:11"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"By humility and the fear of the LORD are riches, and honour, and life.","ref":"Proverbs 22:4"},{"kind":"para","text":"We have motivation by God Himself to put ourselves last on the list. He tells us to put Him first and everyone else second. The “everyone else” category is prioritized based on your gifted relationships. For example, if you are married, your spouse comes first, then your kids, followed by your family, and then your friends, and so on. The greatest sign of humility is being able to put others’ needs before your own."},{"kind":"para","text":"The people of Israel, at this time, were completely selfish in their needs. They wanted to please themselves and enjoy their own lots in life without restrictions. They got that for a while and began to abuse it into extreme living. Now the Lord must remind them who they are supposed to belong to. God is going to humble them. That is something to take courage in."},{"kind":"para","text":"We might see prideful people coming out victorious for a long time, but we can rest assured that God will bring judgment to them in time. They will have to face the Lord, and they will be humbled eventually. You will either be humbled, or you will be a joke."}]},{"start":10,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God made ways for His people. He has made impossible ways for His people to obey Him. He has done things that most people still don’t believe He has done. The proof is in the people, though. The fact that God has not completely destroyed this Earth is a testament enough that God is still working. He, honestly, should just end it, though, because this world is increasingly evil. We are falling apart."}]},{"start":11,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Again, Zion is a very specific place that the Lord mentions here. I don’t know of a time in history where the people of Israel have returned to Zion with gladness and joy. Honestly, throughout history, it seems the Israelites have continuously gotten the short end of the stick. The Jews are probably the most mistreated group in history. Yet, they are still preserved today. That is a pretty obvious sign that God is not done with the nation or its people (though they are the express image of rebellion against the Lord today if you look to that nation)."}]}]},{"start":12,"end":16,"title":"God's Comfort","entries":[{"start":12,"end":13,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God asks a profound question here. He begins by reminding the reader that He is able and willing to comfort His people if they are able and willing to receive it. Then He poses a deep question: Is it important for us to fear men and not look to God, who has done amazing and great things for His creation? He then asks, “Where is the fury of the oppressor?” This is a significant question for God to ask every generation."},{"kind":"para","text":"While we are not faced with exile in America (at least not yet), we do encounter oppressors. There are people who try to destroy our faith or take away God’s goodness in our lives. This question can be directed to you, the reader, today. Where is the fury of the oppressor? Your oppressor is Satan. That is the one we have to watch out for."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Be sober, be vigilant; because your adversary the devil, as a roaring lion, walketh about, seeking whom he may devour:","ref":"1 Peter 5:8"},{"kind":"para","text":"The only reason we should “worry” about Satan is because we are not “worrying” about the presence of the Lord. When we forget God, we certainly will remember Satan. He’s like a thorn in the side of a believer. He speaks lies to us all the time. But God’s voice is always stronger. It’s not always louder, but it’s always brighter."}]},{"start":14,"end":16,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"We are going to worry about something somewhere somehow. Our worry could be, “What are we going to do now? Where is our money coming from now? How are we going to be able to survive now? How can we pay for food now?” When really, our question should be, “God, will you supply our needs for us?” When we have a focus on the Lord and His providence, He is always faithful to come through for us in one way or another."},{"kind":"para","text":"I don’t know how many times I have made stupid decisions with finances or have given to others without having the means to support myself or my family, and I get caught worrying about it. If you are someone who worries about that stuff, you are not alone, and you are not a bad, faithless Christian because of it. But I have always gone to the Lord, and that is the secret to how I am still surviving today. By all other means (from the outside perspective), there is no reason for me to be surviving right now. Yet, I go to God in fervent prayer and trust, and God has met EVERY SINGLE NEED EVERY SINGLE TIME. I have too many stories to even count at this point. There is no other way I can describe these providences other than saying it was all God."},{"kind":"para","text":"God is a faithful protector and a faithful provider for His children. He continuously meets our needs if we trust Him for it. He knows the mistakes we make, and He doesn’t hold it against us. Unless you are purposely making the mistake against the Lord, the Lord will always provide for your needs and give you what He knows you deserve. Whether that be good or bad, God will give you what you deserve. There is nothing like the warm embrace and comfort of the Lord on the life of a believer."}]}]},{"start":17,"end":20,"title":"An Accepting Culture","entries":[{"start":17,"end":17,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Look at the way He addresses His people here. He says, “Awake, awake, stand up…” It seems that much of this world is asleep. God’s own people are seemingly sleeping. They are physically awake but spiritually asleep. That is the state of the church today. I don’t see a church that is spiritually alive. Perhaps they start off with a spiritual awakening, but they end up prideful and tired. They don’t keep the wake because they become spiritually dead and physically alive. They become too person-centered and move away from centering Christ in everything; truly, that is the only way to be awake. Christ must be the center:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And he is the head of the body, the church: who is the beginning, the firstborn from the dead; that in all things he might have the preeminence.","ref":"Colossians 1:18"},{"kind":"para","text":"If Christ is the center of attention in all things, He will wake it up. He will make it live. He will make it worthwhile. Otherwise, it sleeps. Sleep isn’t necessarily a bad thing, but when it’s a time of chaos, war, or decline, we should probably wake up for it. If we stay sleeping, we will be hurt, killed, or crushed by the enemy. God gifts us with seasons of rest, but in seasons of war, we must be awake."}]},{"start":18,"end":18,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The fact remains true, and we have spoken about it before: we cannot trust anything here on this Earth to suffice for what only God can provide for us. Anything we lean on here will fall apart. There is nothing here that can lead us properly. We must depend on the directives and leadings of the Lord if we want to move forward anywhere. Otherwise, we will be led astray."}]},{"start":19,"end":20,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God has been in a mode of judgment to these people, and they seem to not be getting it. Maybe they do get it, but they reject it. Even the young men are growing weary. They are suffering greater loss than their parents. Honestly, that is my biggest concern in our age. My daughters are going to have a very difficult time in their generation because the generations preceding them are setting up a great downfall for them. We have let too much go over the line. We are far too accepting of everything at this point, and it hasn’t made us a united people; only a superficial people. If we are too accepting, we will become too ignorant. It causes us to waver on convictions and truth. It makes it so that nobody can live responsibly if everything everyone does is righteous by the standards of the world."},{"kind":"para","text":"Eventually, I foresee a future (likely in my own children’s generation, if not the generation after) where murder and rape will be largely accepted. We might say, “There’s no way, that would NEVER happen.” It has before. It was accepted in the time of Isaiah. In fact, cannibalism was also widely accepted. We will eventually get back to that in this world again because (as I’ve already stated) we are not evolved creatures; we are devolved creatures. Evolution says we start off as nothing and we become something. Scripture says we start off as everything and we became nothing. God made us in His image, and we tried to taint it right from the start. Adam had it all, and then lost it all because he wanted more. Arguably, the first sin problem was not simply a disobedience problem. The first sin problem was a lust problem. He wanted something he shouldn’t want. Sin entered before the bite of the fruit, not after. But it was by His actions that cursed all men forever. So because of this, we have devolved through every generation."},{"kind":"para","text":"There have been some highs, I’ll give the world that much. The Lord has given prosperity to Israel in several cases for several generations, and He has given prosperity to the world in several cases for several generations, but just like Israel, we abuse God’s goodness to us and fall away from those gifts, leading us into evil intents. And instead of us learning our lesson and turning back to God, we push the line of acceptance so we don’t have to change. We just become okay with the new norm. We just say, “Well, things are still good, so I’ll just be accepting of this murder and rape culture because I certainly can’t change it.” No. You can’t change it. But God can. That is the lesson we should be learning from these chapters in this book. Instead, we don’t wake up to the needs of our culture, and so we make half-hearted decisions while we sleep, and things spiral downwards even faster."},{"kind":"para","text":"It is interesting that we become accepting of everything over time. It’s like all sin is interconnected in some way. If we accept murder, we have to accept rape, and we have to accept abortions, and we have to accept child mutilation and pornography. We have to accept drugs, and abuse of alcohol, we have to accept heresy and blasphemy. We have to accept all parts of the sinful culture or none of it. They all seem to link together. That is why we can’t accept something like the homosexual culture. Homosexuality is a sin for a few different reasons that I won’t get into here, but the one thing they know how to do (for the most part) is care about people. There are some homosexuals who are not caring at all, and they are kind of irritatingly evil (annoying even). But the main reason we cannot accept this culture is not because it’s a sin. Rather, the main reason is because it’s connected to the other cultures. If we push the line a little to accept homosexuality, then we have to push it a little further to accept transgenders. If we push the line to accept transgenders, then we have to push it a little further to accept child sex changes. If we push the line to accept child sex changes, then we have to push it a little further to accept child sex trafficking. If we accept that, we have to push it further to accept human trafficking, and then further to accept drug trades, and then further to accept abortion, then further to accept rape, and then further to accept murder… you see how this goes. That is where we are headed."},{"kind":"para","text":"We have already accepted homosexuality in our culture, and we have pushed the line to transgenders, as well as sex changes for children. Child sex trafficking is next on the list, and that is already a huge problem in our country as it is. According to a study on “justice.gov,” children who are commonly trafficked are “children of color, LGBT children, and children from lower income families and communities.” According to the “Safe House Project,” they claim that “Every 2 minutes a child is sold.” They say that there are “4.8 million people” who are victims of sex trafficking, and “300,000” are taken from America every year. They start with 12-year-olds mostly and they are held captive for “23.4 months before they can either escape, die, or be set free.” Yet we don’t see much of the media or communities speaking about this. You know what makes it even worse? According to this study, “Over 40% of minor victims of trafficking are first sold by a family member.” Before too long, though, we will have pushed the line to accepting this altogether, and children will just be birthed for this cause. It seems so cruel and unjust, and even typing about it is making me sick. We cannot continue to push the line of acceptance because the people that suffer the most from it are the most vulnerable (i.e., the children)."}]}]},{"start":21,"end":23,"title":"Abuse of People","entries":[{"start":21,"end":21,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"These people are drunk with sin. We are afflicted with it as well. Being drunk with wine is one thing, but being drunk with sin is a whole different issue. At least if you are drunk with wine, you are hurting yourself. Being drunk with sin hurts other people."}]},{"start":22,"end":23,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Honestly, this could have been quite literal. It is likely that the people who took over the land of Israel used the bodies of those people to pave their roads between the lands. We know that this is something they will be doing in the end times. They will be persecuting and executing all sorts of people for either following the Lord or, at the very least, not following them."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And there was given unto him a mouth speaking great things and blasphemies; and power was given unto him to continue forty and two months. And he opened his mouth in blasphemy against God, to blaspheme his name, and his tabernacle, and them that dwell in heaven. And it was given unto him to make war with the saints, and to overcome them: and power was given him over all kindreds, and tongues, and nations.","ref":"Revelation 13:5-7"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And I saw the woman drunken with the blood of the saints, and with the blood of the martyrs of Jesus: and when I saw her, I wondered with great admiration.","ref":"Revelation 17:6"},{"kind":"para","text":"God will, eventually in time, turn this around back to these people again. The world will continue to push for more acceptance of more things, and there will be a lot of innocent and wholehearted people who will suffer the consequences of it. The more time that goes by, the greater this damage will be. Eventually, the whole world will be accepting, and when that happens, the Lord promises to pour out His wrath and exact revenge on the evil of this world. Praise the Lord for that!"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Dearly beloved, avenge not yourselves, but rather give place unto wrath: for it is written, Vengeance is mine; I will repay, saith the Lord.","ref":"Romans 12:19"},{"kind":"para","text":"Give room for the Lord to repay, but don’t keep silent while the world pushes the line of acceptance. Be a voice of reason and righteousness. Be like Isaiah in the middle of a perverse culture. Be like Jesus in the midst of great idolatry and religious restrictions. Stand up for the Lord against all odds."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":9},{"start":10,"end":10},{"start":11,"end":11},{"start":12,"end":13},{"start":14,"end":16},{"start":17,"end":17},{"start":18,"end":18},{"start":19,"end":20},{"start":21,"end":21},{"start":22,"end":23}],"verses":{"1":"Hearken to me, ye that follow after righteousness, ye that seek the Lord: look unto the rock whence ye are hewn, and to the hole of the pit whence ye are digged.","2":"Look unto Abraham your father, and unto Sarah that bare you: for I called him alone, and blessed him, and increased him.","3":"For the Lord shall comfort Zion: he will comfort all her waste places; and he will make her wilderness like Eden, and her desert like the garden of the Lord; joy and gladness shall be found therein, thanksgiving, and the voice of melody.","4":"Hearken unto me, my people; and give ear unto me, O my nation: for a law shall proceed from me, and I will make my judgment to rest for a light of the people.","5":"My righteousness is near; my salvation is gone forth, and mine arms shall judge the people; the isles shall wait upon me, and on mine arm shall they trust.","6":"Lift up your eyes to the heavens, and look upon the earth beneath: for the heavens shall vanish away like smoke, and the earth shall wax old like a garment, and they that dwell therein shall die in like manner: but my salvation shall be for ever, and my righteousness shall not be abolished.","7":"Hearken unto me, ye that know righteousness, the people in whose heart is my law; fear ye not the reproach of men, neither be ye afraid of their revilings.","8":"For the moth shall eat them up like a garment, and the worm shall eat them like wool: but my righteousness shall be for ever, and my salvation from generation to generation.","9":"Awake, awake, put on strength, O arm of the Lord; awake, as in the ancient days, in the generations of old. Art thou not it that hath cut Rahab, and wounded the dragon?","10":"Art thou not it which hath dried the sea, the waters of the great deep; that hath made the depths of the sea a way for the ransomed to pass over?","11":"Therefore the redeemed of the Lord shall return, and come with singing unto Zion; and everlasting joy shall be upon their head: they shall obtain gladness and joy; and sorrow and mourning shall flee away.","12":"I, even I, am he that comforteth you: who art thou, that thou shouldest be afraid of a man that shall die, and of the son of man which shall be made as grass;","13":"And forgettest the Lord thy maker, that hath stretched forth the heavens, and laid the foundations of the earth; and hast feared continually every day because of the fury of the oppressor, as if he were ready to destroy? and where is the fury of the oppressor?","14":"The captive exile hasteneth that he may be loosed, and that he should not die in the pit, nor that his bread should fail.","15":"But I am the Lord thy God, that divided the sea, whose waves roared: The Lord of hosts is his name.","16":"And I have put my words in thy mouth, and I have covered thee in the shadow of mine hand, that I may plant the heavens, and lay the foundations of the earth, and say unto Zion, Thou art my people.","17":"Awake, awake, stand up, O Jerusalem, which hast drunk at the hand of the Lord the cup of his fury; thou hast drunken the dregs of the cup of trembling, and wrung them out.","18":"There is none to guide her among all the sons whom she hath brought forth; neither is there any that taketh her by the hand of all the sons that she hath brought up.","19":"These two things are come unto thee; who shall be sorry for thee? desolation, and destruction, and the famine, and the sword: by whom shall I comfort thee?","20":"Thy sons have fainted, they lie at the head of all the streets, as a wild bull in a net: they are full of the fury of the Lord, the rebuke of thy God.","21":"Therefore hear now this, thou afflicted, and drunken, but not with wine:","22":"Thus saith thy Lord the Lord, and thy God that pleadeth the cause of his people, Behold, I have taken out of thine hand the cup of trembling, even the dregs of the cup of my fury; thou shalt no more drink it again:","23":"But I will put it into the hand of them that afflict thee; which have said to thy soul, Bow down, that we may go over: and thou hast laid thy body as the ground, and as the street, to them that went over."}},
    "52": {"chapter":52,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: Our last chapter was a very swift reminder to all of us about how important it is to stand up for the Lord while we have the opportunity to do so. Not for the sake of protecting God, but for the sake of protecting the next generation from the evils of this world. When we don't live for the Lord, we will live for this world, and that has accumulated to nothing more than abusing the innocence of people, and taking away their ability to make wise choices."},{"kind":"para","text":"In this chapter, we are going to get the directives from the Lord to make a way for Christ. Isaiah will speak about the necessity to put on strength, and walk in the ways of the Lord. He will end this chapter with how Christ will captivate the world by His sacrifice, which is a perfect lead into chapter 53 which speaks very deeply about the Lords crucifixion. But that's a spoiler."}],"previously":["Our last chapter was a very swift reminder to all of us about how important it is to stand up for the Lord while we have the opportunity to do so. Not for the sake of protecting God, but for the sake of protecting the next generation from the evils of this world. When we don’t live for the Lord, we will live for this world, and that has accumulated to nothing more than abusing the innocence of people and taking away their ability to make wise choices. In this chapter, we are going to get the directives from the Lord to make a way for Christ. Isaiah will speak about the necessity to put on strength and walk in the ways of the Lord. He will end this chapter with how Christ will captivate the world by His sacrifice, which is a perfect lead into chapter 53, which speaks very deeply about the Lord’s crucifixion. But that’s a spoiler."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":3,"title":"Put on Christ","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Once again, that certainly hasn’t happened. In the church house today, we have all walks of life entering in. That certainly isn’t a bad thing. So when the Lord says “put on thy strength,” He is not speaking specifically about “beautiful garments.” Rather, the strength of Israel and the strength of God’s children is only one thing:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And also the Strength of Israel will not lie nor repent: for he is not a man, that he should repent.","ref":"1 Samuel 15:29"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"The LORD also shall roar out of Zion, and utter his voice from Jerusalem; and the heavens and the earth shall shake: but the LORD will be the hope of his people, and the strength of the children of Israel.","ref":"Joel 3:16"},{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord is the strength of a people. If you are feeling weak, or you are feeling defeated, uncertain, and completely undone; find strength in the Lord and \"put\" Him on."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But put ye on the Lord Jesus Christ, and make not provision for the flesh, to fulfil the lusts thereof.","ref":"Romans 13:14"},{"kind":"para","text":"If it is possible to put Christ on, then it certainly must be possible to take Christ off. I think a lot of Christians today forget their strength at home. They wake up and search for everything else to give them strength. They have their coffee (or energy drinks, depending on what kind of person you are), they watch their news, they put on clothes for the day, do their hair, find their keys, phones, and wallets, and head out the door for the day. It’s a pretty average start to the day."},{"kind":"para","text":"But God says, “Put on thy strength,” and we forget that at home. Somewhere in there should have been prayer or scripture reading. Somewhere in that morning routine should call for God providing strength and direction for your day. We are too often like the Israelites, living fancy lives with fancy things, and putting the Lord on the list (but somewhere down towards the end of all things). Make it a habit to put on Jesus Christ each day. It will certainly be your strength."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"If we took a quick evaluation of the world today, we would see that everyone is walking around as if they are subjects to slavery. They do the same mundane routines every morning and work the same hours every day, doing the same exact job all the time. Sloughing through life like that will get tedious and boring."},{"kind":"para","text":"God calls the Israelites to live in the newness of life. He says, “Get up, and sit down!” Well, which one is it, Lord? Do you want us to stand or sit? Remember yesterday when God told us to awake? Well, that is what I believe He is saying here. Wake up, sit down for a moment, and evaluate the Lord. Loosen the shackles of life for a moment and spend some time with the Lord. He has given you the freedom to do that every morning. No matter what the government might say, the Lord is always freely available through prayer. That is one of the best things about prayer; you can do it anytime, anywhere, for any reason. The world won’t get it, but the Lord loves it. But God gives us the opportunity to spend time with Him and to be free from the bondage of sin and mundanity."}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is a very forward verse. The Jews today still believe that their money will solve their problems. Strangely enough, most Jewish people are looked at as rich in the eyes of Americans. There are jokes about how greedy and money-hungry Jewish people are. Whether those jokes are true or not doesn’t really matter. The Lord does not redeem you with money. He doesn’t even want your money. You can do whatever you want with your money; He just wants your life. He wants your soul. And He will redeem your life by giving His own life in exchange. That’s a pretty sweet deal if you ask me. I get to live the life of Christ, and He gets to own me? How is that a bad thing by any measure?"},{"kind":"para","text":"In the Old Testament, especially, slave owners were supposed to treat their slaves with so much compassion that when the time came for the slave to pay off their debt, they wouldn’t want to leave. A slave would actually ask to stay, and the master would have the right to redeem them. He didn’t redeem them with money. He redeemed them by poking an awl through their ear and nailing them to the doorpost."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Then thou shalt take an aul, and thrust it through his ear unto the door, and he shall be thy servant for ever. And also unto thy maidservant thou shalt do likewise.","ref":"Deuteronomy 15:17"},{"kind":"para","text":"That seems like a weird way to bind a contract. Well, in those days, they didn’t have contracts like we do now. They did things physically to make up for promises, and they would usually do it in a very public place for the whole city to see so they could bear witness to the promise being kept. This particular gesture, however, was a private one done in the domain of someone’s private house. The ear piercing would be enough of a reminder of who they are and how they live."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord doesn’t require us to pierce our ear to His doorpost, but the contract for being His follower is still binding. The Holy Spirit is the awl we receive for being a saved Christian."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"In whom ye also trusted, after that ye heard the word of truth, the gospel of your salvation: in whom also after that ye believed, ye were sealed with that holy Spirit of promise, Which is the earnest of our inheritance until the redemption of the purchased possession, unto the praise of his glory.","ref":"Ephesians 1:13-14"},{"kind":"para","text":"Praise the Lord; He has proof of His redemption. If you want to know the best way to find out whether or not you have Christ, it’s through the pain of trials. The fact that you love the Lord so much and the world pushes every which way against you is a pretty prominent fact that the Holy Spirit is working in you. This is a very important truth regarding Jesus Christ being with you."},{"kind":"para","text":"Putting on Christ doesn’t simply mean you remember your salvation. It means living and acting like Him towards everyone else around you. Put on Christ so they can see His love for people, not your need from people."}]}]},{"start":4,"end":6,"title":"He's Always There","entries":[{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"If you read in Genesis, Egypt seems to be the happening place for most of the original characters of the faith. Abraham goes there, Isaac goes there, Jacob goes there, and the children of Jacob live there. Then all the Israelites who were living there became slaves to the Egyptians, seemingly out of nowhere. They were given safety, but eventually, their time came when they had to go to the land of Promise. The Lord had promised that lineage that they would inherit a land, and that land wasn’t found in Egypt. So the oppression had to come. They HAD to get moving. They were too comfortable in Egypt, but that is not where they belonged."},{"kind":"para","text":"We, too, are too comfortable in this world. That is why affliction and testing come. It’s to get us uncomfortable enough to move. Where that might be is not up to you or me. It’s up to the Lord. He will direct your moving in whichever way He sees fit."}]},{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Every day, you sell yourself. I think that should be understood. You are either selling yourself to other people, to the world, or to the Lord. Someone is buying a piece of you every day. You show up to work to earn a paycheck; they are buying a piece of your time. They are paying you so they can use you. That is really what is happening (as strange as it may be to think of it this way). You are worth something to them."},{"kind":"para","text":"The difference between a man being bought out of necessity and a man being bought out of the Will of the Lord is how they find joy in their work. My wife works for a school district that (in my opinion) doesn’t deserve her. The leaders in that district abuse her kindness and hard work ethic and then drag her through the mud when she asks any questions. They are so rude and terrible to her person and soul. She keeps going in, though. Why? Well, she loves the kids she gets to work with. That is what she is there for. God has called her to work with children with special needs, and she loves to do it because she loves kids. She’s really the perfect person for the job."},{"kind":"para","text":"You will be bought by the world in some fashion or another, but you should not be “taken away for nought” or rather “for nothing.” People are willing to sell themselves for far less than what they enjoy because they don’t mind being a slave to this world. Christians, however, should find value in their work and value in the people they work with. That’s not usually the case, though. The Lord is calling the Israelites to sell themselves to Him, not to this world, which will mistreat them. However, they aren’t going to listen."}]},{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God says, “Hey! I know you don’t want to believe it, but it really is me. I am here. I have told you all along that I am here.” I can take a pretty deep look at my life and see (now in perspective) that God was always there. He was always trying to get my attention one way or another. I could never see it though. I never saw His presence and pleading. I never saw His goodness and leading. All I ever saw was the pain of this world. I was a very observant child. I watched. People thought I was mentally retarded (some might still think it), but I wasn’t. I was just a watcher. I evaluated people and things. I knew how people felt and I understood how to feel that same way with them. Little did I know that God was there looking at me the same way. I saw pain and hurt in people’s lives and thought, “How unfortunate, I really wish there was more I could do.” I would be an ear to hear for them, but it only led me to believe that this world was doomed to utter failure. However, the Lord would use that later on. He uses it today. I am still an ear to hear, but now I have the Lord to guide me to speak. While I was always telling others, “Hey, I am here for you. It’s me, Jonathan. I am ready when you are to talk,” the Lord was doing the same thing to me."},{"kind":"para","text":"He doesn’t leave us guessing. He doesn’t want us to simply search for Him and then walk away once we found Him. He wants us to come to Him as an ear to hear. He wants us to know that He is there, and it is not some phony god or person that is doing it. It’s interesting to me that people would pray to saints or angels (or even through them). We see several times in scripture that God wants to be right in front of people to confront them with nothing in the middle in the way. God wants to be the direct messenger for His people, not the angels. He could send angels to get these people’s attention, but that is not the way in which He wants you to trust Him. He wants you to trust Him FIRST before you have a relationship with Him. He wants your heart before your eyes. Usually, we won’t give Him anything until He proves Himself first, but He has been there all along waiting for you. At least, in my life, He has proved Himself more times than I can count, and yet I never saw it. I never saw it because I was not looking. This is a plea to look for the Lord today. He is there, and He is waiting to hear from you."}]}]},{"start":7,"end":10,"title":"The Good News","entries":[{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is for the saints. By the way, a “saint” is not a sinless person. I don’t know why we have adapted that definition to this word today in our modern culture, but that was not how it was always meant to be. A saint is simply a saved sinner. It is someone who has placed their trust in Jesus Christ. The letters that Paul wrote to the churches throughout the world at that time were to “saints” of the church. That would be the saved people, not just the apostles or disciples in leadership. That is why we have names in scripture of people who are referred to as “saints” but no other information about them. They are just simply saved people."},{"kind":"para","text":"If saints were sinless people, Peter wouldn’t continually keep messing up after the church was founded. Boy, the amount of mistakes that guy made during the ministry of Christ and after Christ ascended. But the commission is to bring good tidings and peace, which is the essence of the gospel message. That is what gospel means. “Gospel” means “good news.” Jesus brought the gospel first through His life ministry and sacrifice. The good news is, God took your place on the cross. He took the punishment for your sins. Christ suffered an excruciating death here on Earth, so you wouldn’t have to face a never-ending torment there in eternity. All that He requires is for you to believe the gospel. Believe the good news of His sacrifice. Believe that is why He died. He died for you. The moment you understand that is the moment you turn from death to life, and the Lord has your soul reserved for eternity. Salvation has been published for generations, and it is only the people’s responsibility to reach out and grab it with everything they’ve got."}]},{"start":8,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Who are the “watchmen”? Perhaps they are the saints who have been saved for so long, waiting for others to be saved. Maybe they are the angels who have been watching the work of the gospel with anticipation and hope that people will be subject to it. Perhaps they are the loved ones in eternity who have taken hold of Christ before their passing and are waiting and watching until their families come to see them in eternity. I don’t really know, but I know that the Lord has put them up high, and those who take Christ will meet with them “eye to eye.”"}]},{"start":9,"end":9,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This verse calls for joy and singing. But that is not what we have in this world:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For we know that the whole creation groaneth and travaileth in pain together until now. And not only they, but ourselves also, which have the firstfruits of the Spirit, even we ourselves groan within ourselves, waiting for the adoption, to wit, the redemption of our body.","ref":"Romans 8:22-23"},{"kind":"para","text":"We are in pain here on Earth, and the pain seems to be growing stronger and stronger the longer we stay here. Yet, God calls us to sing and live joyfully as if there is something to be excited about. And, honestly, there IS something to be excited about! He has given us redemption and salvation! That is a good reason to rejoice and sing."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Make a joyful noise unto the LORD, all ye lands. Serve the LORD with gladness: come before his presence with singing.","ref":"Psalm 100:1-2"}]},{"start":10,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I can’t think of a single place in this world that has not heard the gospel yet. Everyone, at this point, knows about the salvation of Jesus Christ. If there are people who don’t know, it is either because they haven’t been listening or because they are so far off the radar and impossible to get to for mere humans to reach them."},{"kind":"para","text":"There are probably tribes and the like all over the world that are difficult to reach because they are savages or dangerous. But I am certain that God has sent people their way several times over. I’ve heard testimonies of missionaries almost dying from trying to reach a specific tribe with the gospel, and that tribe has killed other people like them before. Yet, for some reason, the tribe heard out this particular preacher. The Lord was able to reach the hearts of many through the sacrifice of faithful children. I wish it didn’t have to be like that, but the Lord wants His salvation to be preached throughout “the ends of the earth.”"}]}]},{"start":11,"end":12,"title":"Our Reward","entries":[{"start":11,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God has been calling out His people for quite some time now. Even before Isaiah wrote this book and preached this message, God has been trying to reach His people for generations. They are too stubborn and prideful to listen to Him, though. But He hasn’t stopped. He still calls out. He still wants them to walk away from this sinful lifestyle of idolatry (the “unclean thing”) so that God’s creation will bear the “vessels of the Lord.”"},{"kind":"para","text":"To carry the Lord’s instruments and be a willing vessel for His use is something that all of creation would benefit from. We would benefit from it the most because everyone would be putting others before themselves. That is what scripture teaches you. The world tells you to put your own needs first. God tells us to look out for others. He doesn’t say we shouldn’t take care of ourselves, but He certainly doesn’t tell us to ONLY worry about ourselves. We are to examine ourselves, resolve our hangups, spend time with the Lord, and then utilize that experience to encourage and pour into others. When we take the time to do that, God rewards us."},{"kind":"para","text":"According to Isaiah, the reward for a faithful man is God Himself. That’s a GREAT reward. Others scoff and mock the Lord, but for those who work for Him, there is nothing better than to have Him with us. I hate not knowing where the Lord is. I hate it more than any physical pain I can experience. I don’t like physical pain either, but I would prefer that than to not know where God is in my life."}]}]},{"start":13,"end":15,"title":"The World Watches","entries":[{"start":13,"end":13,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"“Prudently” means “to have insight” or “to act wisely.” God wants His people to be prudent. He wants us to deal “wisely.”"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"I wisdom dwell with prudence, and find out knowledge of witty inventions.","ref":"Proverbs 8:12"},{"kind":"para","text":"Dealing prudently means dealing with others with wisdom. How does wisdom appear when you are trying to impart it to others? It manifests with patience and poise. It resembles a person who genuinely cares about the other individual rather than attempting to “win” that person. I believe the term “soulwinning” is somewhat calloused for reaching the lost. We don’t “win” anything. The Lord wins when the person converts to His child, but that is it. If we “win” them into our church, we haven’t actually won anything. We must deal with them “prudently” when they become saved. That is where the real win is. It’s a win because there are no pastors and church leaders doing that. It’s as if they checked off a box the moment you got saved, and now you are someone else in the church’s problem to deal with. That’s not prudent leadership. That’s foolish leadership. Read this in Jeremiah:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Woe be unto the pastors that destroy and scatter the sheep of my pasture! saith the LORD.","ref":"Jeremiah 23:1"},{"kind":"para","text":"This whole chapter from Jeremiah is really good for this specific topic, but we will just stop at this first verse. Unwise church leaders will “scatter the sheep.” “Sheep” meaning “saved Christians who belong to the Lord.” These are people who can have been saved anywhere from one second to fifty years. There are a lot of pastors scattering sheep so they can go and gather more that aren’t his own. He neglects his own sheep to go after wolves. If you want to be a “prudent” leader, do the opposite of scattering sheep."}]},{"start":14,"end":14,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"“Astonied” means “to be desolate” or “to stun.” “Visage” means “sight, appearance, or vision.” People will be stunned by the return of Jerusalem. They perhaps were when they came back from their exile to the Babylonians. This small nation came back to where they belonged. People will be stunned when they see the change in your life too. They will certainly have a hard time grappling with it."},{"kind":"para","text":"I think that is why most of my wife’s side of the family doesn’t want to take Christ for themselves. They don’t want to believe that Christ has actually changed my wife. Perhaps they liked the old sinful Eva more. But the Lord has changed her, and there is no going back to that old sinful way. They will have to watch her continually change for the Lord and become more like Him every day. “His form” changes our form. His death on the cross changes our lives. His form transforms us."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But made himself of no reputation, and took upon him the form of a servant, and was made in the likeness of men: And being found in fashion as a man, he humbled himself, and became obedient unto death, even the death of the cross.","ref":"Philippians 2:7-8"},{"kind":"para","text":"That is what we are going to be witnessing in the next chapter. These last two verses really drive us into the topic for the next chapter which I am really excited to delve deeper into."}]},{"start":15,"end":15,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"People will be in awe of Christ’s death. They won’t know what to think. Even Pilate had a hard time wrapping his head around the murder of this man. He didn’t want to do it because it didn’t make any sense. Their justification to kill an innocent Jew (one of their own) was meaningless compared to the murderers and thieves they put on the cross. You’d have to be quite a despicable man to be crucified, and Christ was not. People may have been offended by what He said, but He never did anything deserving of that kind of punishment. Yet, the Jews were very direct in giving Him this punishment. They were acting quite barbaric. You know you might be making a mistake if a leader like Pilate tries to stand up against the notion. By all other means, these leaders liked to crucify people like this. But this didn’t even make sense. The leaders are stunned by this prospect, and even still today (as we think about His crucifixion and unjust treatment) it should leave us speechless. Not even an atheist can justify this kind of treatment, and they literally hate God. How disgusting of a human being you would have to be to want, respect, and hope for the murder of innocent humans on this Earth. I couldn’t even treat a fly like that… The fact of the matter is, even still (today) Christ puts a stop to people. The mere mention of His name gets people thinking. That is a powerful testimony."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":9},{"start":10,"end":10},{"start":11,"end":12},{"start":13,"end":13},{"start":14,"end":14},{"start":15,"end":15}],"verses":{"1":"Awake, awake; put on thy strength, O Zion; put on thy beautiful garments, O Jerusalem, the holy city: for henceforth there shall no more come into thee the uncircumcised and the unclean.","2":"Shake thyself from the dust; arise, and sit down, O Jerusalem: loose thyself from the bands of thy neck, O captive daughter of Zion.","3":"For thus saith the Lord, Ye have sold yourselves for nought; and ye shall be redeemed without money.","4":"For thus saith the Lord God, My people went down aforetime into Egypt to sojourn there; and the Assyrian oppressed them without cause.","5":"Now therefore, what have I here, saith the Lord, that my people is taken away for nought? they that rule over them make them to howl, saith the Lord; and my name continually every day is blasphemed.","6":"Therefore my people shall know my name: therefore they shall know in that day that I am he that doth speak: behold, it is I.","7":"How beautiful upon the mountains are the feet of him that bringeth good tidings, that publisheth peace; that bringeth good tidings of good, that publisheth salvation; that saith unto Zion, Thy God reigneth!","8":"Thy watchmen shall lift up the voice; with the voice together shall they sing: for they shall see eye to eye, when the Lord shall bring again Zion.","9":"Break forth into joy, sing together, ye waste places of Jerusalem: for the Lord hath comforted his people, he hath redeemed Jerusalem.","10":"The Lord hath made bare his holy arm in the eyes of all the nations; and all the ends of the earth shall see the salvation of our God.","11":"Depart ye, depart ye, go ye out from thence, touch no unclean thing; go ye out of the midst of her; be ye clean, that bear the vessels of the Lord.","12":"For ye shall not go out with haste, nor go by flight: for the Lord will go before you; and the God of Israel will be your reward.","13":"Behold, my servant shall deal prudently, he shall be exalted and extolled, and be very high.","14":"As many were astonied at thee; his visage was so marred more than any man, and his form more than the sons of men:","15":"So shall he sprinkle many nations; the kings shall shut their mouths at him: for that which had not been told them shall they see; and that which they had not heard shall they consider."}},
    "53": {"chapter":53,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: Our last chapter was really just a lead up to this chapter. We spoke about the necessity to live IN the Lord, not just with the Lord in mind. We talked about the fact that God is always there for us, and willing to give Himself for us, which is the good news of the gospel. He talked about how He is our greatest reward, and how living like He is our reward changes the eyes of this world."},{"kind":"para","text":"This chapter, however, is one of my all time favorite chapters in all of scripture. It gives us the mind of Christ in those last dreaded moments of His life, and what it was all for. There's so much I would love to spend some time on in this chapter, but I am going to do my best to give the most important details their due diligence, and leave the rest of the commentary for studying further into some deeper topics. This chapter will be primarily focused on the Lord's sacrifice, the promise of salvation, and why God had to give His life in this way for the sins of the world."}],"previously":["Our last chapter was really just a lead-up to this one. We spoke about the necessity of living IN the Lord, not just with the Lord in mind. We discussed the fact that God is always there for us, willing to give Himself for us, which is the good news of the gospel. He emphasized how He is our greatest reward, and how living as if He is our reward changes the perspective of this world. This chapter, however, is one of my all-time favorite chapters in all of scripture. It gives us the mind of Christ in those last dreaded moments of His life and what it was all for. There’s so much I would love to spend some time on in this chapter, but I am going to do my best to give the most important details their due diligence and leave the rest of the commentary for studying further into some deeper topics. This chapter will be primarily focused on the Lord’s sacrifice, the promise of salvation, and why God had to give His life in this way for the sins of the world."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":3,"title":"The Thoughts of Christ","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The key to this entire chapter (and that of the gospel message) is found right here in this verse. It’s the word “believed.” God’s arm has been revealed to all of humanity through Jesus Christ’s death on the cross, and the only requirement for salvation in this world is to “believe.” So, who has believed the report? It’s only those who look into the perfect law of liberty:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But whoso looketh into the perfect law of liberty, and continueth therein, he being not a forgetful hearer, but a doer of the work, this man shall be blessed in his deed.","ref":"James 1:25"},{"kind":"para","text":"That perfect law of liberty was nailed to the cross for you and for me, allowing us access to the freedom He can provide. There will be a lot of focus on the cross of Christ in this chapter, and I find it to be the most needful doctrinal truth in all of scripture because it leaves every single person in this world without excuse."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord Jesus Christ was simply a man on the outside, but one hundred percent God on the inside. There were certainly several occasions in the gospel accounts that showcase His deity. He was able to heal people with physical and deadly illnesses. He brought people back from the dead using only His words. He brought faith to the unbelieving, sat with sinners, and loved the poor (or those of the lowest degree)."},{"kind":"para","text":"There is a lot of proof to His divinity, and I think that is certainly important to look at, but what He really showcased (more than anything according to John) is His humanity. He wanted all of mankind to know that He was treated much in the same way as everyone else (possibly even worse most of the time) yet He never retaliated or boasted. He was a simple man to the world. There is no beauty that we should desire Him."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"He came unto his own, and his own received him not.","ref":"John 1:11"},{"kind":"para","text":"What a sad verse. God came to us, and we still rejected Him. The Israelites, specifically, will become “dry ground” because of their rejection of God, and yet the Lord will plant His Son right in the middle of the dryness. He will cause His Son to flourish, grow, and prosper into hope."},{"kind":"para","text":"There are pictures online that you can look at that display this very image. Look up pictures of a very dry lake bed with a single flower growing out of it. The surrounding picture looks like doom and apocalyptic, but the flower gives you a picture of hope for that land. If one flower can grow there, what’s stopping the other flowers from growing?"},{"kind":"para","text":"In the day of Christ, they won’t seem to carry about the single flower until that flower directly affects them. Jesus will eventually captivate the world, but He didn’t start that way. People just thought of Him as an interesting man, not the Son of God."}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This gives us an interesting picture into Christ’s psyche. Perhaps you look at the life of Christ as joyous and purposeful. Maybe you view His life as judgmental and bold. Yet Isaiah describes His life as “sorrows, and… grief.” If you feel sorrow and grief, you are in good company, for even God Himself feels it. I don’t know why Christians shun these emotions when our own Lord and Savior lived His life this way. He, however, didn’t let the sorrow and grief stop Him from following God. Instead, He used these emotions to give Him greater compassion for those who were also living in sorrow and grief. He hurt for and with the world as He ministered to its needs. Can we think of one leader (even in the workforce) that works with this mentality? Probably not. Every leader I’ve ever seen looks to act powerful and together. That was not the cause of Christ. He came to hurt with us, and by hurting with us, it gave Him more compassion. The more sorrow we afflicted Him with, the more power in love grew within Him. The more we despise Him, the more relevant His salvation becomes to this world. Like I’ve said before, the more we reject the scripture, the more power it holds to truth."},{"kind":"para","text":"I want us to look at something interesting here, though, and it will be something that we must pay attention to throughout the rest of this chapter as well. Notice the way in which Isaiah speaks about the life of Christ. He is speaking in past tense. “He IS…” “We HID…” “He WAS…” Christ has not come yet. He is still a promise for the future, yet Isaiah is acting as if He was already here. The promise was so sure and secure in the Lord that Isaiah could treat the promises of God as if they were already kept. They certainly will be kept. They will be kept in the exact way that Isaiah has mentioned. If you haven’t gotten it by now, you certainly never will. Isaiah has been speaking about Jesus since the beginning. He has been prophesying about how He will be born:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Therefore the Lord himself shall give you a sign; Behold, a virgin shall conceive, and bear a son, and shall call his name Immanuel.","ref":"Isaiah 7:14"},{"kind":"para","text":"What His ultimate purpose is for coming:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And in that day thou shalt say, O LORD, I will praise thee: though thou wast angry with me, thine anger is turned away, and thou comfortedst me. Behold, God is my salvation; I will trust, and not be afraid: for the LORD JEHOVAH is my strength and my song; he also is become my salvation.","ref":"Isaiah 12:1-2"},{"kind":"para","text":"And how He will save the world:"}]}]},{"start":4,"end":6,"title":"The Sacrifice","entries":[{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God is bearing the grief and sorrows of the world at this time, but He will do so in human form when Christ comes to minister. Curiously enough, according to Isaiah, Jesus Christ was “smitten of God.” To be sure, the world will certainly be the cause of putting Christ on the cross, but it will be agreed upon by the Lord. Since the beginning of time, God has made it very clear that the only sacrifice that will suffice for humanity will be Himself. He will have to show us the way. Christ, in fact, IS the way. His cross bore our sins, but His life bore our griefs and sorrows. That doesn’t seem very fun. Yet, in nearly every message He preached to His disciples, He says we should be walking with joy:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Hitherto have ye asked nothing in my name: ask, and ye shall receive, that your joy may be full.","ref":"John 16:24"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And ye now therefore have sorrow: but I will see you again, and your heart shall rejoice, and your joy no man taketh from you.","ref":"John 16:22"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"These things have I spoken unto you, that my joy might remain in you, and that your joy might be full.","ref":"John 15:11"},{"kind":"para","text":"How can He have joy, yet carry our griefs and sorrows? We can have joy in the Lord, and griefs in the world. That is how Jesus lived. That is the example He set before us. That is how we must live before the Lord has well. It was not that Jesus just felt grief. No, He BORE OUR griefs. He carried our pains with joy."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Looking unto Jesus the author and finisher of our faith; who for the joy that was set before him endured the cross, despising the shame, and is set down at the right hand of the throne of God.","ref":"Hebrews 12:2"},{"kind":"para","text":"That's the griefs of the whole world by the way. And you know what? He still gladly carries them today, and reminds the believer to leave your pains and sorrows at His cross:"}]},{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Again, He “was.” Now, anyone hearing Isaiah at this pivotal moment would wonder who He is even talking about. The Lord hasn’t done this. How could Isaiah act as if He already has? There are a lot of religions and cults that try to get rid of this entire chapter of Isaiah today. They try to play it off as if Isaiah doesn’t really mean what he says here. It must be some sort of mistake. Yet everything that Isaiah has written about leads to this very important moment in this book. He has been leading up to this time, and now it is important to listen because the salvation of your soul depends upon it."},{"kind":"para","text":"The people of the Old Testament had the daunting task of believing this promise was going to eventually be kept. The people of the New Testament (i.e., the church today) have the important task of believing this promise has already been kept. Isaiah wrote it as if the promise HAS been kept before the promise was ever fulfilled. Why? Well, this truth is timeless. It’s for all generations. He WAS wounded for our transgressions."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Then Pilate therefore took Jesus, and scourged him. And the soldiers platted a crown of thorns, and put it on his head, and they put on him a purple robe,","ref":"John 19:1-2"},{"kind":"para","text":"He WAS bruised for our iniquities:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And said, Hail, King of the Jews! and they smote him with their hands.","ref":"John 19:3"},{"kind":"para","text":"The chastisement of our peace WAS upon Him:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Then came Jesus forth, wearing the crown of thorns, and the purple robe. And Pilate saith unto them, Behold the man! When the chief priests therefore and officers saw him, they cried out, saying, Crucify him, crucify him. Pilate saith unto them, Take ye him, and crucify him: for I find no fault in him. The Jews answered him, We have a law, and by our law he ought to die, because he made himself the Son of God.","ref":"John 19:5-7"},{"kind":"para","text":"With His stripes we ARE healed:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"When Jesus therefore had received the vinegar, he said, It is finished: and he bowed his head, and gave up the ghost.","ref":"John 19:30"},{"kind":"para","text":"All of these things ARE absolutely, one hundred percent confirmed, and all that is required to take hold of this truth is to do as verse one says, and BELIEVE it:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Jesus saith unto him, Thomas, because thou hast seen me, thou hast believed: blessed are they that have not seen, and yet have believed.","ref":"John 20:29"},{"kind":"para","text":"Belief is the greater blessing. The world would argue against that, though. They would say that seeing is the greater blessing. Sometimes I think about how I would have been if I was a disciple of Jesus. I would have loved to be Peter, or Andrew, or John the Revelator. I would have loved to be one of Jesus’ inner circle."},{"kind":"para","text":"But then I think about the fact that I would have had to witness His death on the cross. I couldn’t bear the sight. I’m sufficient to just believe without seeing it. It’s sufficient for me to receive all the rewards of salvation without actually seeing the death of Jesus physically. What is written about it is sufficient for me to see. That, itself, is enough for me to be hurt by, let alone being a disciple to see this treatment on such a loving and innocent man of God."}]},{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Isaiah gives the reason for all of this right here in this verse: God must take the sacrifice because we have gone astray. God loves us too much to leave us in wander and sin. He wants us to know that love by His humanity and sacrifice for us. I’ve said it before, and I think it bears repeating. I know why we would want to go to God. I cannot fathom why God would want to go to us."},{"kind":"para","text":"Before I was a Christian, I struggled with the concept that a man could claim Himself to be God. That was a difficult thing for me to believe. Now I believe it, and the thing that is difficult for me to believe now is how God can become man. There is only one conclusion that it really all boils down to, and it’s something the scriptures repeat over and over again: God loves us and wants us to be in His presence."},{"kind":"para","text":"The greatest reward a man will ever receive is the reward of God’s face looking into our face. To be able to see God and live is what I am looking forward to. I don’t need anything else."}]}]},{"start":7,"end":9,"title":"The Proof of His Sacrifice","entries":[{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This will be an obviously fulfilled prophecy:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"When Pilate therefore heard that saying, he was the more afraid; And went again into the judgment hall, and saith unto Jesus, Whence art thou? But Jesus gave him no answer. Then saith Pilate unto him, Speakest thou not unto me? knowest thou not that I have power to crucify thee, and have power to release thee?","ref":"John 19:8-10"},{"kind":"para","text":"Christ has the power to put a stop to all of this before He is sent to the cross, yet He never uses His power to do it. He doesn't even pray that the Lord would put a stop to it. He does pray from the cross, but it's not a prayer for Himself. This is the prayer He prays:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Then said Jesus, Father, forgive them; for they know not what they do. And they parted his raiment, and cast lots.","ref":"Luke 23:34"},{"kind":"para","text":"He prays for those that are crucifying and torturing Him. I’m sorry, but my last thought while being tortured by mankind is that they would be forgiven. Yet that is Jesus’ FIRST thought. He wants God to forgive the wickedness of the people literally murdering an innocent man for no reason other than they had their feelings hurt. Even in that prayer from the cross, we see Jesus’ salvation for humanity. That is why He was on the cross after all. It was for the salvation of wicked people like them."}]},{"start":8,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Here’s where the rubber meets the road. A lot of people have asked, “Who did Jesus actually die for?” Some say that He died for the elect—those who turn to Christ are who Jesus died for. Others say it was for the world, meaning everyone has a chance to receive Christ’s sacrifice because of it. I say it’s for both. Scripturally, it lines up the best. Isaiah says it was “for the transgression of my people…” Isaiah claims it for Israel. Christ died for the world, but salvation only belongs to the repentant sinner."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For whosoever shall call upon the name of the Lord shall be saved.","ref":"Romans 10:13"},{"kind":"para","text":"Anyone can be saved, but not everyone will be saved. Christ died for the world, but only those who turn to Him in faith, believing that He died and rose again, will have salvation. His death on the cross was the access to salvation for all, while His resurrection three days later was the access to His believers. I think if Jesus simply died on the cross and didn’t show Himself three days later, there would still be people who believed. It wouldn’t be as many perhaps, but there would still be believers because of the number of people He helped heal and change, even causing the blind to see and the deaf to hear."},{"kind":"para","text":"However, the fact that He showed Himself alive three days later gives extremely strong validity to His salvation. The disciples were certainly changed by it, so much so that every single one of them gave their lives to continue to serve the Lord after His ascension. Who would die for something that they haven’t actually witnessed? The faith of the Apostles is what increases the faith of us today. We believe their word because their word seems to be absolutely accurate. If you don’t want to take their word for it, take Isaiah’s word for it. Everything Isaiah says aligns perfectly with what the gospel message represents."},{"kind":"para","text":"Someone has to be true, and if the five different accounts of Christ’s ministry and cross are not enough, perhaps the changed life of a man of God will help you see and believe. If not, then you will have to purposely shun all the evidence in front of you. But the death of Christ still gives you access. You have until your own death to make your decision. However, we don’t know when our own death will be…"}]},{"start":9,"end":9,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Jesus was crucified between two actual thieves and murderers. He was killed in the same manner as a wicked person would be killed. He was buried in a borrowed grave; Joseph of Arimathea gave his own grave to the Lord’s body, and that was likely a quite expensive burial plot."},{"kind":"para","text":"And the reason He was treated this way? “Because he had done no violence, neither was any deceit in his mouth.” Isaiah says He was treated with this disrespect because He did nothing wrong. That is all it takes to make the world angry with you. You simply have to live in line with the Lord…"}]}]},{"start":10,"end":12,"title":"The Offering","entries":[{"start":10,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"We would probably do best to break this verse down because it can be a little confusing if we just mush it all together and don’t think too long about it. First, Isaiah says that it “pleased” God to bruise Jesus. Why would God be pleased at the sacrifice, suffering, and death of His own Son? We will have to draw from several locations in scripture, but one thing we must understand before going to the rest of scripture is that sin requires a sacrifice."},{"kind":"para","text":"Without using scripture at all, think about your own sins. What do you think you need to sacrifice to dwell in sin? Let’s start with something small, like lying. I don’t think anyone would be too upset by telling little lies. No matter how big the lie might be, there is still a sacrifice for it. You sacrifice trust with the person you are lying to. You sacrifice the relationship. You sacrifice dignity and care. These are just a few from something as small as lying."},{"kind":"para","text":"Maybe we look at something a little deeper, perhaps addiction. You sacrifice trust still, but you sacrifice it usually with the people you love the most. You sacrifice your own freedom and self-control. You sacrifice critical thinking and the ability to evaluate. These are just a few sacrifices. We could look at murder, or adultery, or idolatry, or stealing, and so on, and see that every sin we commit requires a sacrifice, and it’s not always a sacrifice to ourselves. I’d say, often times (more than not), you are forced to sacrifice someone you love for your personal sin."},{"kind":"para","text":"God made a way, in the Old Testament, to sacrifice an animal instead. Of course, we can look at Leviticus for obvious signs of this:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For the life of the flesh is in the blood: and I have given it to you upon the altar to make an atonement for your souls: for it is the blood that maketh an atonement for the soul.","ref":"Leviticus 17:11"},{"kind":"para","text":"There’s life in the blood, and a sacrifice must be made for your sins. You either sacrifice those around you or sacrifice your income. In the end, there must be a sacrifice made. Now, let’s look to Jesus. First, I want to point out something in Deuteronomy:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"The fathers shall not be put to death for the children, neither shall the children be put to death for the fathers: every man shall be put to death for his own sin.","ref":"Deuteronomy 24:16"},{"kind":"para","text":"Yet, here we are with Jesus giving His life for the sins of the world. These were not His sins He is dying for; they are your sins that He is dying for. How can He do that when the law of Moses strictly says that another man cannot be put to death for someone else’s sins? Well, that’s where this verse in Isaiah comes in. God allowed another man to be sacrificed in your place! How? Well, He never sinned! That makes Him the perfect sacrifice for you."},{"kind":"para","text":"The lambs of the Old Testament could not offer themselves as a sacrifice. You would have to choose and offer the sacrifice yourself. Jesus, on the other hand, willingly offered Himself."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"The next day John seeth Jesus coming unto him, and saith, Behold the Lamb of God, which taketh away the sin of the world.","ref":"John 1:29"},{"kind":"para","text":"The only reason that God was pleased with this sacrifice was because Jesus (alone) met the righteous and perfect standards of God’s law. Lambs could not do that. So it pleased God to give His own life’s blood for the sin of humanity. It then says that God had “put him to grief.” God allowed the grief of the world to lay on the shoulders of His Son. And, in all honesty, He is the only one that can carry that kind of grief. Imagine if the Lord put sorrow and grief on your shoulders. I’m sure He has before. How heavy was that burden for you to carry? I have no doubt you struggled carrying it, and you might carry it for a long time. But the burden and grief of sin can be placed on the shoulders of Jesus and be put to death at the cross! That’s why He carried our grief."},{"kind":"para","text":"Now Isaiah speaks in future tense. He says, “WHEN you will make his soul an offering for sin.” That’s a future realization. They can look back at this chapter of Isaiah and say, “Dang… He was right… Here I am sacrificing this man…” Of course, no one is going to think about Isaiah when they hang the Lord on the cross, except for the disciples."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"That the saying of Esaias the prophet might be fulfilled, which he spake, Lord, who hath believed our report? and to whom hath the arm of the Lord been revealed?","ref":"John 12:38"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And the scripture was fulfilled, which saith, And he was numbered with the transgressors.","ref":"Mark 15:28"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For I say unto you, that this that is written must yet be accomplished in me, And he was reckoned among the transgressors: for the things concerning me have an end.","ref":"Luke 22:37"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"That it might be fulfilled which was spoken by Esaias the prophet, saying, Himself took our infirmities, and bare our sicknesses.","ref":"Matthew 8:17"},{"kind":"para","text":"And that’s just to name a few from only Isaiah 53 alone. But even while they might not have thought about what they were doing to the Lord on the cross, Jesus certainly saw and thought about them according to Isaiah. He says, “He shall see his seed, he shall prolong his days, and the pleasure of the Lord shall prosper in his hand.” He willingly took the cross because he saw the generations to follow coming to Him through it. He knew that this was the only way to get the attention of the world and provide an appropriate sacrifice for every generation forward."},{"kind":"para","text":"Jesus Christ thought of YOU while on the cross (at least according to Isaiah). If you know Jesus Christ today, you are part of His lineage, you are part of his “seed.” You are the fruit of His labor! Your fruit on the Lord’s account. What a glorious blessing to be thought of by the Lord, but even more awe-inspiring to know He thought of you while He was dying. That was what gave Him motivation to take the punishment on the cross."}]},{"start":11,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Jesus bore your iniquities. He satisfied the law of God and completed the sacrifice for Him. Of course, we can better understand this in the book of Hebrews (as well as the gospels), but Isaiah is preparing for those books to be written. He is giving the testament beforehand so that there is not a single soul without excuse."},{"kind":"para","text":"You have the proof before Jesus. You have the proof during Jesus. You have the proof after Jesus. If you don’t believe based on every bit of evidence that is literally flashing you in the face, you are just stubborn and willingly ignorant. There is nothing you can do for a person that rejects the truth when it’s right in front of their faces."}]},{"start":12,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"To the world, the Lord Jesus Christ was just one of the many sinners who end up dying. However, to the Lord, there is a portion divided to Him, and He divides it to the “strong.” Who are the strong? Paul puts it this way:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Therefore I take pleasure in infirmities, in reproaches, in necessities, in persecutions, in distresses for Christ's sake: for when I am weak, then am I strong.","ref":"2 Corinthians 12:10"},{"kind":"para","text":"The strong are those who are weak. Weakness in the flesh often equates to strength in the Spirit. When we give up our strength for the Lord, He gives us strength in faith. Jesus Christ divides God’s strength and power to the strong because “he hath poured out his soul unto death.” He poured out His Spirit, and those who take His Spirit are then made strong by His Spirit."},{"kind":"para","text":"Numbered with the transgressor simply means that He was counted as one of us. He wasn’t a transgressor Himself, but He was certainly treated like one. And that (because He never transgressed) means that He can make “intercession for the transgressors.” Perhaps we should define these words. “Intercession” means “to reach.” “Transgressors” means “To rebel” or “revolt.” Jesus was able to “reach” the holiness of God because of His sinlessness and bring it to YOU, who are a “transgressor” or “rebel” against the Lord. That’s what His sacrifice did for you. He reached God, even while you rebelled against Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"The people who hung Him on the cross thought they were doing some sort of justice for His Words, but really they were doing exactly what the Lord wanted them to do. They were murdering His Son. That should be the wake-up call for every single person reading. God wanted them to murder His Son because it shows how depraved and sinful we are (transgressors) and how Holy, Just, and Careful God is (intercessor). Praise the Lord He set the standard and showed that it could be accomplished through His Son, because I would never be able to find favor with God otherwise."},{"kind":"para","text":"I love Jesus, and I only love Him because He first loved me and proved that love by dying for my transgressions on the cross. My sins put Him there, but my faith makes Him live."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":9},{"start":10,"end":10},{"start":11,"end":11},{"start":12,"end":12}],"verses":{"1":"Who hath believed our report? and to whom is the arm of the Lord revealed?","2":"For he shall grow up before him as a tender plant, and as a root out of a dry ground: he hath no form nor comeliness; and when we shall see him, there is no beauty that we should desire him.","3":"He is despised and rejected of men; a man of sorrows, and acquainted with grief: and we hid as it were our faces from him; he was despised, and we esteemed him not.","4":"Surely he hath borne our griefs, and carried our sorrows: yet we did esteem him stricken, smitten of God, and afflicted.","5":"But he was wounded for our transgressions, he was bruised for our iniquities: the chastisement of our peace was upon him; and with his stripes we are healed.","6":"All we like sheep have gone astray; we have turned every one to his own way; and the Lord hath laid on him the iniquity of us all.","7":"He was oppressed, and he was afflicted, yet he opened not his mouth: he is brought as a lamb to the slaughter, and as a sheep before her shearers is dumb, so he openeth not his mouth.","8":"He was taken from prison and from judgment: and who shall declare his generation? for he was cut off out of the land of the living: for the transgression of my people was he stricken.","9":"And he made his grave with the wicked, and with the rich in his death; because he had done no violence, neither was any deceit in his mouth.","10":"Yet it pleased the Lord to bruise him; he hath put him to grief: when thou shalt make his soul an offering for sin, he shall see his seed, he shall prolong his days, and the pleasure of the Lord shall prosper in his hand.","11":"He shall see of the travail of his soul, and shall be satisfied: by his knowledge shall my righteous servant justify many; for he shall bear their iniquities.","12":"Therefore will I divide him a portion with the great, and he shall divide the spoil with the strong; because he hath poured out his soul unto death: and he was numbered with the transgressors; and he bare the sin of many, and made intercession for the transgressors."}},
    "54": {"chapter":54,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: Though Isaiah 53 is considered as one of my favorite passages of scripture (because it talks so heavily about the Lord's death and resurrection (as well as His final victory over sin and death)), this chapter of Isaiah is a good coupling with it."},{"kind":"para","text":"In this chapter we will focus on the victory of God's saved. When we trust in the sacrifice of Christ, we have the opportunity to live in the victory of the redeemed, and we can display that in our lives today, rather than wait for eternity to apply the benefits of God's salvation."}],"previously":["Though Isaiah 53 is considered one of my favorite passages of scripture (because it talks so heavily about the Lord’s death and resurrection, as well as His final victory over sin and death), this chapter of Isaiah is a good coupling with it. In this chapter, we will focus on the victory of God’s saved. When we trust in the sacrifice of Christ, we have the opportunity to live in the victory of the redeemed, and we can display that in our lives today, rather than wait for eternity to apply the benefits of God’s salvation."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":3,"title":"Losing Focus","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I think it should be well understood by all the readers following along with me that the purpose of the text, the placement of the text, and the direction of the text is not lost on me. I understand just as well as everyone that this is talking about Israel. I know that we are focusing on the captivity and the eventual redemption (as well as salvation) of God’s chosen people, Israel."},{"kind":"para","text":"We’ve looked (since the beginning of the Bible) at this lineage quite in depth at this point, and while there are a lot of other nations warring and happening behind the scenes, the focus of the Old Testament has been Israel. However, Israel was to be set forth as an example for this world to follow. They were to be separate from everyone else in the world and be the righteous and chosen lineage."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And ye shall be unto me a kingdom of priests, and an holy nation. These are the words which thou shalt speak unto the children of Israel.","ref":"Exodus 19:6"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying, Take the Levites from among the children of Israel, and cleanse them. And thus shalt thou do unto them, to cleanse them: Sprinkle water of purifying upon them, and let them shave all their flesh, and let them wash their clothes, and so make themselves clean. Then let them take a young bullock with his meat offering, even fine flour mingled with oil, and another young bullock shalt thou take for a sin offering. And thou shalt bring the Levites before the tabernacle of the congregation: and thou shalt gather the whole assembly of the children of Israel together: And thou shalt bring the Levites before the LORD: and the children of Israel shall put their hands upon the Levites: And Aaron shall offer the Levites before the LORD for an offering of the children of Israel, that they may execute the service of the LORD. And the Levites shall lay their hands upon the heads of the bullocks: and thou shalt offer the one for a sin offering, and the other for a burnt offering, unto the LORD, to make an atonement for the Levites. And thou shalt set the Levites before Aaron, and before his sons, and offer them for an offering unto the LORD. Thus shalt thou separate the Levites from among the children of Israel: and the Levites shall be mine. And after that shall the Levites go in to do the service of the tabernacle of the congregation: and thou shalt cleanse them, and offer them for an offering. For they are wholly given unto me from among the children of Israel; instead of such as open every womb, even instead of the firstborn of all the children of Israel, have I taken them unto me.","ref":"Numbers 8:5-16"},{"kind":"para","text":"Obviously, that didn’t last forever, and so the chapters proceeding Genesis talk about that separation that God’s people slowly started to face. Now we come to a book and chapter like this, and it seems as if all hope is lost. Yet, the Lord wants God’s people to sing. This is why I have made the argument to compare Old Testament Israel with the church (if I haven’t made that clear enough). Besides the fact that prophets speak in threes, the people of Israel are supposed to be an example of what the future church will look like. Instead, they are a prime example of what the future Christians will look like. You might ask, “What do you mean by that? Are you saying that Christians are wayward and there is no hope?” Kind of, yes. I am saying that we are far too much like the people of Israel in the church today. Honestly, from what I’ve seen (and this is just an honest assessment based on the church today from a personal perspective, as well as from many bouts of counseling others through church hurts), the modern church is dead. It’s an act. It’s just business. I hate even saying that, but it’s absolutely true. Instead of the church being centralized around giving, we are centralized around money. Instead of the church being centralized around loving, we are centralized around attendance. Instead of the church being centralized around ministering (or selfless acts of service), we are centralized around hierarchy and leadership. Instead of the church being centralized around compassion, we are centralized around power. Instead of the church being centralized around Jesus, we are centralized around our pastor. You see the problem? Don’t tell me your church doesn’t do this, because I am absolutely certain it does. The moment a man gets involved with anything (spiritual or worldly) is the moment that we start to shy away from the main themes of this world. The truth is, we just want to hear good things and pay to watch a show. That is not church. The church is seriously dead, but the Christians are not. Though they might be few, there are Christians in the world that care very much about the Lord’s work and the ministering of people. They think they have to have a church to back them up in their labors, but the church hardly ever will. You either back up the church, or you are on your own in God’s calling for you. Those are your two options. What God is displaying to the Israelites is not that they are supposed to support the church. He’s displaying the opposite. He’s showing that the church (i.e., God’s orchestrated house) is supposed to support His children (i.e., God’s called-out people). When God has a calling for you, it is extremely rare that anyone (including in the church house sadly) will back you up. However, in our modern worship, we are supposed to back up everything the church wants to do without question. Isaiah is putting a very stern stop to that. Look at this first verse alone (and I’ll do my best to break it down):"},{"kind":"para","text":"\"Sing, O barren, thou that didst not bear;\""},{"kind":"para","text":"God is not calling them collectively; He’s calling them individually. Wouldn’t it be great if they had a place to go so they could sing together? If only God allowed such a place as this…"},{"kind":"para","text":"Barren indicates that they are childless. What a tragedy for them. It’s still a tragedy today, but I don’t think a lot of people care too much about it. Maybe your soul is barren today? Maybe it doesn’t have to be about having children? Either way, the Lord wants you (the reader) to sing, even though we have a lot of reasons to mourn."},{"kind":"para","text":"\"break forth into singing, and cry aloud, thou that didst not travail with child:\""},{"kind":"para","text":"Again, God is still commissioning the individuals. The calling is for one person, yet for everyone at the same time."},{"kind":"para","text":"\"for more are the children of the desolate than the children of the married wife, saith the LORD.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"This is a really sad thought, and if we put it into our modern vernacular, we see that it’s still the case today. Again, we don’t have to look at it as having children. We are certainly barren in soul, joy, love, compassion, and spirit, for this world robs you of all of this. Yet, God is calling us to sing. He is calling His children away from their time of mourning."},{"kind":"para","text":"Honestly, Israel didn’t have to enter this time of captivity. They didn’t have to go away from the Lord. If the Israelites are a picture of the future church, it is no wonder we have disgraced our places of worship. We have all fallen for the same traps, and we all do it together. If we took our individual callings more seriously, perhaps the church would finally turn around. But the modern church (just like Israel) has tricked its people into thinking we are headed in the right direction. We see numerical growth and assume that is a sign of God’s providential prosperity. No."},{"kind":"para","text":"I don’t know about you, but I want a church that is more than just numbers and large checks. I want a community of people reminding me which direction I’m supposed to be facing. People who are willing to love me like the Lord loves me. People who are willing to be honest and are willing to share their hurts and temptations with their community without being judged and forced out. Yet, we don’t have that. Israel didn’t have that either, and here they are desolate and “barren.” Maybe every church has to face this large battle in order to learn as well?"}]},{"start":2,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"If you think the Jewish community struggles with our last chapter, this certainly can’t be any easier. Even (or should I say especially) in Isaiah’s day, the Gentiles were looked at as less than and dirty compared to the Jews. Still today, the Jewish culture is often the most resistant and hostile towards the truth of Jesus Christ, and they view themselves in a much higher standard than the rest of the world. God NEVER intended that. Honestly, God humbled these people from the very beginning. He had to keep reminding them who they belonged to and how they became so prosperous. I think He is still reminding them today, and He will continue to remind them even until the very last days of our world."},{"kind":"para","text":"But the fact of the matter is, God is not going to bless you with more if you are not willing to accept little from Him first. A little bit from the Lord is a lot more than what we can handle as it is. He will give you more when you are ready to receive little first. That starting point (according to Isaiah) is to have some joy and singing first before God starts building your faith and house. Recognize that for a second because I think church leaders really struggle here. If you see your church growing, and that is all that excites you, you are looking at the wrong thing. If church growth is more important to you than spiritual growth, you have a dead church. It’s not a church at all. It’s a business."},{"kind":"para","text":"This doesn’t mean that we can’t rejoice over the fact that our church is growing (I think that is all well and fine), but if that is our focus, we have lost our church. Spiritual growth is far more important than numerical growth, and I’ll repeat that fact until I am buried in my grave, and then I’ll put it on my tombstone."}]}]},{"start":4,"end":6,"title":"Living In New Life","entries":[{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"When we are saved, do we forget everything else that happened to us? Obviously not. So does that mean that God is lying here? Well, the Lord is speaking to Israel as individuals, but He is also speaking to them as a whole. When God says that He loves the whole world and gave Himself for it, He is speaking about the whole world, but it’s individuals that receive the benefits of salvation. In the same sense, that is how He is speaking to the Israelites (and that of all humanity through every word in the Bible)."},{"kind":"para","text":"Generations might pass by, but they won’t focus on the deep regretful mistakes of their ancestors in this moment. They will just be past stories. That is how it is when we become a child of God. We don’t forget our past sins (or that of our present ones), but we know we are living in forgiveness for them. God is a forgiving God, undeservingly forgiving."},{"kind":"para","text":"It frustrates me to see Christians who struggle with sin on a daily basis be put to shame by mature Christians. I don’t even know if I should call them mature if they are mistreating young Christians in the faith. That’s not a mature thing to do. Rather, we should be encouraging and helping those that are struggling. They should understand that God still loves them."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"We then that are strong ought to bear the infirmities of the weak, and not to please ourselves.","ref":"Romans 15:1"},{"kind":"para","text":"Instead, “mature” Christians will point out all the times that God has judged His children in the Old Testament. Yes, we have read a lot of judgments from the Lord. But that is not all God has done. I think Jonah is a great book to see God’s love and forgiveness in action."},{"kind":"para","text":"Again, these were not just little mistakes and sins that the Israelites were delving into. Rather, they were purposely doing it without any sort of remorse or struggle against it (or their conscience). It was almost as if they didn’t have a conscience at all. There’s a very stark difference between a person who is willfully rejecting God and doing evil to mankind, and a person who is simply struggling with their own sin and begging for God to forgive them."},{"kind":"para","text":"God has forgiven them on the cross. He made that very clear when He was dying there. Your sins are forgiven because He did the work for you, even the sins you have yet to commit. But your sins should certainly break your heart enough to turn to God and continually ask for forgiveness and strength to continue to fight. Then we can join with those in the church who are capable of keeping you focused and encouraged in your fight (if there is a church who will do it)."}]},{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God is the husband of the church, and Jesus Christ is the bridegroom. We will not be married to the Lord until eternity, but that will come in due time. It is, seriously, right for Him to own us in this way. He can lead us far better than we can lead ourselves, and if we are going to follow the Lord correctly, we should be engaged to Him until that fateful day."},{"kind":"para","text":"The part of this verse that I find interesting is the “God of the whole earth shall he be called.” Is He not already called this? Well, of course, He is the God of the entire Earth, but not the entire Earth has accepted that title. Eventually, there will be a day where the whole Earth will call Him God, and there will be no such thing as an atheist or a nonbeliever. Everyone will dwell with the Lord, and they will know Him more personally than we ever can now."}]},{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Can I just point out something that I don’t think is talked about enough? Marriage is a very important focal point to the Lord throughout scripture. He has used this specific symbol as a means of testimony, salvation, and commitment—promises that should never be broken."},{"kind":"para","text":"Obviously, Moses wrote up a bill of divorcement because we are sinful and hardhearted people, but in the marriage of the Lord, there is no breaking it off. We are married when we come into this world. You probably don’t know it."},{"kind":"para","text":"Marriage is not about rings, contracts, and sharing a bank account. Marriage is spiritual. It’s supernatural. It’s deeper than what we see with our eyes. It’s a spiritual intertwining of one spirit to another spirit until they become one spirit together."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Wherefore they are no more twain, but one flesh. What therefore God hath joined together, let not man put asunder.","ref":"Matthew 19:6"},{"kind":"para","text":"When we come into this world, our spirit knits to it. We marry the world as soon as we leave the womb. We are enamored by creation. Why wouldn’t we be? I’ve watched my newborn daughter look at this world in amazement. I didn’t really pay attention to this with my firstborn (but I wasn’t a Christian at that time). With my second-born, I can see in her eyes a light of excitement and joy as she sees, hears, and tastes things for the first time. It’s like a spark of envy or pride when it clicks in her brain. That is what it’s like for all of us in this world."},{"kind":"para","text":"You can tell it in a newborn, but you might not be able to see it in yourself. You married the world the day you came into it, and you have been growing that relationship further and further along as you live and grow. However, someday you will see how abusive and misleading that relationship really is. You will see that it’s actually taking away everything good in you. What you once saw as joy and excitement will become mundane, ordinary, and evil. Some people don’t mind that. But when Christ gets a hold of your heart, you will start to understand how superficial your marriage really is."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is what the divorce papers that Moses created represent. It’s our ability to separate ourselves from this world and be engaged to the truth. There is no separating from that though. If we are in Christ, when we do worldly things, it is equivalent to cheating on our spouse. Christ won’t call off the wedding, but He will certainly not allow you to do it without a conversation or a thought. You WILL feel convicted."},{"kind":"para","text":"I hope this analogy is not taken the wrong way; I’m not saying it’s okay to get a divorce in this life. Jesus says divorce is only okay for ONE reason, and that is from adultery (a spouse cheating). But, truly, if you are married to the world, the world cheats on you every day. You are okay to divorce yourself from it. Christ could never do that. He is wholly dedicated to you no matter how muddied your life has become. He will work with you as He works on you. That’s what true love looks like."}]}]},{"start":7,"end":10,"title":"Everlasting Covenant","entries":[{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"To the Israelites, it seems as if, by the fact that they are going into captivity and losing everything, God is done with them. It appears as though God is never going to forgive them. However, God has made it clear that forgiveness is coming in the future. For this time, however, it will seem as if they are forsaken. They have been, honestly. They haven’t been forgotten, though. God is forsaking them because of their willingness to completely turn away and reject the Lord. But God is not going to simply leave them in their sins. They will see that God has a purpose for this action in the future, and that purpose is ultimately to get them (and you) to turn back to Him and pursue Him with everything you have."},{"kind":"para","text":"I can easily attest to this verse. I have made a lot of dumb mistakes, and I have felt far from God a few times in my walk (and perhaps it will happen again, God forbid, in the future), but I always see God make a turnaround. I always see Him come back for me. I might not know what He is doing in the moment, but I can trust that He has a right reason to do it because the end results are always worth it (if I can just wait with patience for Him)."}]},{"start":8,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"What a verse! Can we just dwell in this verse for a moment? I can’t possibly be the only one who has felt as if they are constantly under God’s wrath. I can’t be the only one who senses God’s disappointment and disapproval for my actions and deeds. His wrath to us, however, is “little.” It’s the size of an atom compared to the wrath the rest of the world will feel. It can’t even really be considered wrath because of how seemingly small it is compared to what God can actually do."},{"kind":"para","text":"That little wrath is only for a moment, and it’s replaced with something far greater, which is His promise of “everlasting kindness” and “mercy.” The moment that we can feel His kindness and mercy is the moment we understand His redemption. May that be a reminder to every reader today. God’s kindness and mercy (according to His own words here) are “everlasting.” “Everlasting” means “forever,” or “always.” Better put, “continuous existence,” or “perpetual.” You will never lose it, in other words, no matter what you do after you’ve been redeemed. That is a peaceful thought to us. It’s a peaceful thought to me anyway. It’s further clarified in Ephesians."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"In whom ye also trusted, after that ye heard the word of truth, the gospel of your salvation: in whom also after that ye believed, ye were sealed with that holy Spirit of promise, Which is the earnest of our inheritance until the redemption of the purchased possession, unto the praise of his glory.","ref":"Ephesians 1:13-14"}]},{"start":9,"end":9,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God uses water extensively throughout His Word as a symbol of various things. He has used the Jordan River as a symbol of new life. In the Old Testament, wells symbolize His provision. In the New Testament, water is used as a symbol of salvation through baptism. Additionally, in the book of Revelation, water is depicted as the main source of eternity. Furthermore, at Jacob’s well, water symbolizes God’s continuous mercy and forgiveness (kindness) to a Samaritan woman in the gospel."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Jesus answered and said unto her, Whosoever drinketh of this water shall thirst again: But whosoever drinketh of the water that I shall give him shall never thirst; but the water that I shall give him shall be in him a well of water springing up into everlasting life. The woman saith unto him, Sir, give me this water, that I thirst not, neither come hither to draw.","ref":"John 4:13-15"},{"kind":"para","text":"Here, God is using the waters of Noah as a symbol. Water is God’s testimony to mankind. The waters of Noah were a symbol of God’s judgment and wrath. God placed a rainbow in the sky, promising that He would never flood the Earth to destroy everything and everyone again. All we would have to do is look into the sky to be reminded of God’s promise of salvation."},{"kind":"para","text":"In the same sense, the cross is our physical symbol of God’s promise being kept. We will never have to worry about sin destroying us ever again if we are under the promise of the cross. All we must do is look to the cross to be reminded of God’s promise. Best yet, the cross is open for everyone until the world is destroyed. Noah’s ark was open for everyone too, but no one would believe Noah until it was too late. Thankfully, there are people who believe the Lord’s message on the cross. Sadly, there are still far too many who don’t believe it."}]},{"start":10,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is the peace of a Christian. Everything around us can fall apart, and we may lose everything in this world. However, we are no longer married to it, so it doesn’t matter. Because we are married to the Lord, the world can go to nothing, and we will still have God’s covenant of peace and mercy on us. That is far better than anything we can obtain in this world anyway."},{"kind":"para","text":"The edenic covenant will end (has ended with Jesus rising from the dead, and will be sealed when Satan is in Hell forever). The Noahic covenant will end. The Abrahamic covenant has an end. The Israelite covenant will end. The Davidic covenant ends with Christ. But the covenant of salvation (i.e., the covenant of God’s kindness, peace, and mercy) is everlasting. There is no end to it, and that is not just given to a handful of people or a specific lineage. It’s given to the world to possess and trust!"}]}]},{"start":11,"end":14,"title":"God's Currency","entries":[{"start":11,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I’ve heard a lot of people say that all roads lead to the same Heaven. Some say that finding the right path is difficult, and we must trust our own hearts to find it. I’ve even heard people say that it’s impossible to find the right path, so it’s best to just follow the movement of better people. However, God is painting a much different picture of His path to salvation here. He says the path to salvation is colorful and paved with precious stones. The gates to salvation are overtly obvious to anyone passing by. So why do people have such a hard time figuring out which path is the Lord’s path today? Well, it’s because it seems too obvious. It seems as if it’s too easy."},{"kind":"para","text":"I have the daunting privilege to homeschool my daughter. I tell people that I am in whatever grade she’s currently in because I’m learning everything all over again. There are some tests she has to take. If it’s a multiple-choice test, there are times when I will read it and think, “This seems way too easy to be the right answer; she’s in fifth grade, there’s no way her test is in first-grade standards.” And I have to figure out the deeper meaning. I’d say ninety-nine percent of the time, the easiest answer is usually the right answer. We just like to overcomplicate things. I’m sure you have struggled with this same lesson as well. Why do we do this to ourselves? It really is our own brains doing it. We can’t just accept the fact that easy can mean right."},{"kind":"para","text":"Maybe you’ve seen the Colgate commercials with the old man swishing mouthwash, and his daughter comes in and asks him what he’s doing. He says, “If it’s burning, it’s working.” This was to promote their new mouthwash that doesn’t burn when you use it. We think that pain means success. We think that struggle means victory. We think that good works mean salvation. We don’t understand it when God says, “It is finished” and gives you salvation in front of your face. That doesn’t seem right to us because that is not what the world deems as “success.” Working for it means success. Being gifted these things means we didn’t earn it, and it is depreciated in value. That is not how God’s currency works. His value is your trust. That’s all He wants."}]},{"start":13,"end":13,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"To live in a world where everyone has simply trusted in God would be calming and peaceful. I can imagine the joy on every person’s face. The ability to never have to worry about locking a door again, or making a mistake, or falling into a sinful habit would be liberating. We would no longer need to concern ourselves with food, rent, or trying to look the best and impress our bosses or leaders. Difficult talks with people we don’t agree with or debates with political opposites would be a thing of the past. That is the world we will eventually have, but that is not the world we have at the moment."}]},{"start":14,"end":14,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I say we will “eventually” have that world, but we can start living in that way right now if we wanted to. We are currently redeemed (if you have the Lord), and so He has given you the right and ability to live as if Heaven was already here. We don’t though. We live in opposition to the world because the world has a very loud voice. Also, because the world is your ex-spouse, they won’t leave you alone until they try and destroy your new marriage."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"What therefore God hath joined together, let not man put asunder.","ref":"Mark 10:9"},{"kind":"para","text":"May we learn to live as if we are not in this world. May we live as if we are truly engaged to the Lord in anticipation of the day He calls us home to Him."}]}]},{"start":15,"end":17,"title":"Nothing In This World","entries":[{"start":15,"end":15,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God is our strength. Perhaps your enemies won't physically fall, but if you have the Lord, you have a strong mental and spiritual presence with you. They might destroy your physical body, but they can never win over your spiritual one. They might try and warp your mind, but your love of God will hold the test of time."}]},{"start":16,"end":17,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"When everything is said and done, you are either going to rejoice on the side of the Creator of all things, or you are going to try and fight against the Creator using His creation. If a painting I drew tried to fight against me, I don’t think I would have much trouble winning. If a child I created tried to fight me, I don’t think it would be difficult for me to win. That is how we are viewed by the Lord. We are just small children, and when we don’t know Him, it’s like a little three-year-old trying to punch the Lord. It just isn’t going to work, and it will look quite sad and pathetic. There is nothing in this world that will win against your faith in the Lord. If there is something, you did not have a genuine faith, my friend."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":9},{"start":10,"end":10},{"start":11,"end":12},{"start":13,"end":13},{"start":14,"end":14},{"start":15,"end":15},{"start":16,"end":17}],"verses":{"1":"Sing, O barren, thou that didst not bear; break forth into singing, and cry aloud, thou that didst not travail with child: for more are the children of the desolate than the children of the married wife, saith the Lord.","2":"Enlarge the place of thy tent, and let them stretch forth the curtains of thine habitations: spare not, lengthen thy cords, and strengthen thy stakes;","3":"For thou shalt break forth on the right hand and on the left; and thy seed shall inherit the Gentiles, and make the desolate cities to be inhabited.","4":"Fear not; for thou shalt not be ashamed: neither be thou confounded; for thou shalt not be put to shame: for thou shalt forget the shame of thy youth, and shalt not remember the reproach of thy widowhood any more.","5":"For thy Maker is thine husband; the Lord of hosts is his name; and thy Redeemer the Holy One of Israel; The God of the whole earth shall he be called.","6":"For the Lord hath called thee as a woman forsaken and grieved in spirit, and a wife of youth, when thou wast refused, saith thy God.","7":"For a small moment have I forsaken thee; but with great mercies will I gather thee.","8":"In a little wrath I hid my face from thee for a moment; but with everlasting kindness will I have mercy on thee, saith the Lord thy Redeemer.","9":"For this is as the waters of Noah unto me: for as I have sworn that the waters of Noah should no more go over the earth; so have I sworn that I would not be wroth with thee, nor rebuke thee.","10":"For the mountains shall depart, and the hills be removed; but my kindness shall not depart from thee, neither shall the covenant of my peace be removed, saith the Lord that hath mercy on thee.","11":"O thou afflicted, tossed with tempest, and not comforted, behold, I will lay thy stones with fair colours, and lay thy foundations with sapphires.","12":"And I will make thy windows of agates, and thy gates of carbuncles, and all thy borders of pleasant stones.","13":"And all thy children shall be taught of the Lord; and great shall be the peace of thy children.","14":"In righteousness shalt thou be established: thou shalt be far from oppression; for thou shalt not fear: and from terror; for it shall not come near thee.","15":"Behold, they shall surely gather together, but not by me: whosoever shall gather together against thee shall fall for thy sake.","16":"Behold, I have created the smith that bloweth the coals in the fire, and that bringeth forth an instrument for his work; and I have created the waster to destroy.","17":"No weapon that is formed against thee shall prosper; and every tongue that shall rise against thee in judgment thou shalt condemn. This is the heritage of the servants of the Lord, and their righteousness is of me, saith the Lord."}},
    "55": {"chapter":55,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: In our last chapter, God spoke to the church (the Israelites specifically) about the salvation that He provides and the provision that He can give to us if we just simply turn to Him and trust in Him. Obviously the Israelites don't know how good God has been to them, and so they are not going to listen to the Lord in this prospect, but in time God's people will learn that He is serious about His promises."},{"kind":"para","text":"In this chapter, He doesn't just speak to the saved. He doesn't just speak to the church. He isn't just speaking to the people who will eventually come to Him. He's speaking to the world. He's opening the door of salvation wide open for the entire world to see and hear and grow by."}],"previously":["In our last chapter, God spoke to the church, specifically the Israelites, about the salvation He provides and the provision He can give to us if we simply turn to Him and trust in Him. Obviously, the Israelites don’t know how good God has been to them, and so they are not going to listen to the Lord in this prospect. However, in time, God’s people will learn that He is serious about His promises. In this chapter, He doesn’t just speak to the saved. He doesn’t just speak to the church. He isn’t just speaking to the people who will eventually come to Him. He’s speaking to the world. He’s opening the door of salvation wide open for the entire world to see, hear, and grow by."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":5,"title":"Open The World","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Our last chapter was an invitation to Israel, or rather to the saved. It was an open invitation for the children of God to come before Him and receive forgiveness for their transgressions and sins. This chapter opens with an invitation to the rest of the world—an invitation to the lost. Look at how gracious God is to them. He says, “Are you poor and needy? Come to the waters (that is God’s testimony, remember?) and you can have it without price.” He says, “I will provide for you, and you don’t have to worry about providing for yourselves in this cruel, calloused world.”"},{"kind":"para","text":"Again, people refrain from coming to God all the time because they think there’s a catch. They think it’s too easy. The world has tricked itself into thinking that hard work is the only way to prosper with God. That could not be further from the truth. Don’t fall for the tricks of the world. God is opening the door of invitation, and all you have to do is take His provision and live in it. I find no better rest than when I am with the Lord."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"In Proverbs, Solomon, arguably the wisest man to have ever lived, speaks about a table that is set. He tells people about two tables in two different houses. You can read this in Proverbs chapter 9, but to summarize, the two tables set up are one of Wisdom (i.e., God) and one of foolishness (i.e., the World). The table of wisdom has food that will fill you up; it’s food with substance. The table of the foolish is filled with candy. If I were a child, I would have probably gravitated towards the table with candy. I would have loved that far more than the table with substance. However, as a mature adult, the table of candy looks enticing, but I would much rather have a full meal than something superficial."},{"kind":"para","text":"The world has been buying their life, and all it has given them is more fake things. Have you ever purchased something that you thought was going to help fix a specific problem, or that you thought would be extremely useful for one thing or another, only to find out that it doesn’t work or do what it says it’s supposed to do? The world is full of false advertisements. Even the term “quick divorce” doesn’t mean what people are hoping. We buy into such cheap thrills thinking that it’s going to solve our problems, and we are always let down in the end. It’s never worth the money nor the hassle."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord says, “You have spent your money in this life, and what has it ultimately given you? Do you feel more successful? Do you feel more valuable?” Perhaps you do feel successful and valuable by your purchases. If you do, that is the sum of your personal value. People want to talk about net worth. They want to act as if their value equates to their resources. If your value is intrinsic by your blood, genes, or material possessions, you are not worth much more than what you can simply find here on Earth. In fact, everyone roughly has the same value in the end. However, the Lord is offering a buyout. He’s offering to buy YOU and your debts (or your materials that you think hold you in so much value)."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For ye are bought with a price: therefore glorify God in your body, and in your spirit, which are God's.","ref":"1 Corinthians 6:20"},{"kind":"para","text":"When He buys you, your worth is not found in anything here on Earth. Your worth is found in a Heavenly realm. It's found in the place in which the Lord sits. I don't know about you, but an eternal value sounds far more important than an Earthly one. If we find value in creation, imagine how much more value there is in the Creator of creation!"}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is quite the promise. Once again, there are a great deal of Jewish people who don’t believe that anyone else can be “graffed in,” as Paul calls it. If you are not of the Jewish bloodline, you are not going to be saved by the Lord. If you are not a part of the Jewish church, the Jewish traditions, and the Jewish way of living, you are not going to ever face the Lord. In their eyes, you are always lost."},{"kind":"para","text":"I’ve known people of Jewish descent who have turned to Jesus, and instead of their family questioning or being curious about what their child is doing, they instead hold a funeral for their child. They pretend and act as if they are dead. The person who has turned to Christ is disowned and never spoken to by their families again. Yet, we have read over and over again throughout the Old Testament (and specifically with Isaiah) that God gives mercies to the outsiders of the Jewish lineage. He’s giving the “everlasting covenant” to the world here. He’s offering it to those outside of the Israelite family."},{"kind":"para","text":"Everything (so far) that Isaiah has preached on has been in direct opposition to everything that the current Jewish culture holds so high and dear to themselves. I truly wonder what they do with a book like this? They can’t just outright twist the scripture here. It would be impossible! This is obviously so direct about opening the covenant of David to the entire world, and yet there are people who still try and twist this to mean something completely different. If they twist this portion, they will have to twist the rest of the Bible to make it make sense, and it would never actually match up."},{"kind":"para","text":"I’ve said it before, the best commentary of the Bible is the Bible itself, and if there are things that are not lining up in scripture for you, it is likely because you are trying to twist it into what it wasn’t meant to mean."}]},{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God speaks to David about a future promise of a “wise” king who will sit on his throne. David and Israel initially thought that king was Solomon. Solomon was indeed a wise king, but he was not the king God was talking about. God was referring to Jesus in the promise—the Savior King. It is Jesus who will be our witness, the leader of our salvation, and the one who will command the people. He has done it, and He will continue to do it until the end of the age. Jesus is the name to trust and the name to lean on. It is His name and person that give us salvation and direction."},{"kind":"para","text":"You might say that you don’t believe in Jesus. You might think He was just a good teacher, a good preacher, or a good man of many talents. You might not believe in His resurrection or His acclamations about Himself. There are certainly things that I find very hard to understand in faith and scripture. I’m still learning much as I go along in this life, even while I am typing up this commentary. But there is one thing I know: I have never been let down when I lean on Jesus. The pastors I’ve met, the friends I’ve made in the faith, the converts I’ve gotten to know, and the world around all of that (even in the church) have let me down too many times to count. But Jesus never has when I’ve trusted in Him. He has always been a strong foundation for me to stand on."},{"kind":"para","text":"Honestly, I’m waiting for my foundation of faith to crumble. I’m waiting for the day that the Savior will show me something that I just can’t follow. Yet, He hasn’t. I’ve only been saved for a short eleven years, but in those eleven years, I have not found a single reason to ever recant my faith. Every time I try to look for one, He just gives me more reasons to trust Him. I don’t understand these people who are “deconstructing” their faith. I think they believe that there is too much clutter in their faith, and it’s becoming too difficult to keep track of. It’s as if their faith was primarily placed on their service, not on the finished work of Christ. But instead of throwing out all the clutter, they literally get off the foundation of truth to pursue a different foundation. Maybe those other foundations are sturdy, but I am absolutely one hundred percent sure that those other foundations will fall apart in due time. It’s only a matter of waiting."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For other foundation can no man lay than that is laid, which is Jesus Christ.","ref":"1 Corinthians 3:11"}]},{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I’m sure there are quite a few nations that the Israelites didn’t know about. I don’t even know if Isaiah knew about the rest of the world’s people. America wasn’t a thing yet. England didn’t exist the way it does today. But there were people still living in these areas. There were things happening behind the scenes of scripture leading us to where we are now while all of this was taking place."},{"kind":"para","text":"God promises salvation to the entire world. He gives it freely, without price. And notice the phrasing here: “…and nations that knew not thee shall run unto thee…” We are not just bystanders seeing something shiny. No, we have heard about the Messiah. I didn’t hear it from a Jewish man by the way. I heard about the Messiah from a Gentile like me. I came to Him from a very far country. Once I knew who He was, and what He can do, I didn’t just search for Him. I RAN to Him. I wanted to be by Him quickly, and everyone that finds faith in Jesus will know exactly what I am talking about."}]}]},{"start":6,"end":9,"title":"A Higher Way","entries":[{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There is a twofold thought process that we need to consider here. Firstly, there is the understanding that we should be seeking God. Calvinists might suggest that we should not be doing that. However, the Lord is (and has been for the Israelites as well) asking that this world looks for Him too. Additionally, God will seek us."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For the Son of man is come to seek and to save that which was lost.","ref":"Luke 19:10"},{"kind":"para","text":"Notice the way in which Jesus says this. He says, “The Son of ‘man’ is coming to seek.” As one hundred percent human, Jesus came to seek. He gave us an example of what we (the saved) should be doing. We should be seeking. We cannot save, however. That is not our responsibility. But we should take note of how Jesus sought people, because that is a very important message that is lost in our churches today. We should do some seeking as well."},{"kind":"para","text":"Arguably, those who come to God are those who are seeking Him anyway. Those who don’t care to find God rarely ever turn to Him if we witness to them. God calls us to seek Him in return for His seeking of us."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"All that the Father giveth me shall come to me; and him that cometh to me I will in no wise cast out.","ref":"John 6:37"},{"kind":"para","text":"We come to Him, and He comes to us. Secondly, this verse signifies that there will likely be a time when God cannot be found. How is that the case? Where is He going? One day, there will be no point in seeking after the Lord because He will have done away with this world and the wickedness here. He will have destroyed it all, and that time you have for seeking Him will be over because He will have gotten rid of everything that rejects and defies Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"Here’s what I’ll say: I am assured that it is not by my own efforts that I am saved today. I could not lift a single finger to get my salvation. I couldn’t work my way to it even if I tried. Yet, the Lord is worth a lifetime of searching to find if that were the way in which I had to find Him. I wish I would have known how valuable He was when I was younger because I would have had so much more to offer this world than I did. However, I didn’t spend my life searching for Him. He spent my life searching for me, and it wasn’t until I was much older (with my first child at that) when I realized who and what He was doing. I’m just glad He allowed me to come to Him before it was too late."}]},{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"It doesn’t matter your background or ethnicity. It doesn’t matter to God what you did, or what you thought about doing. When we turn to Him and repent—that is, forsaking our ways and thoughts—God “abundantly” pardons. He says, “I know who you were, but I will not hold that against you if you just follow me and forsake all those old ways.”"},{"kind":"para","text":"People who are “deconstructing” often find their old selves somewhere in the pile of rubble they called “faith.” When they do, they don’t toss it out and start building again. No. They put their old man back on and start walking in their unrighteousness again. Yet, if they are still willing to forsake it and turn to the Lord, He still promises “abundant pardon.”"},{"kind":"para","text":"God is righteous and just, but He is also merciful and good. Will there be consequences? Probably. The world is good at making you face your consequences. It’s good at reminding you of who you used to be. But the Lord will deal with those consequences with you, and His Spirit provides peace to work through some of the toughest trials you might ever have to face."}]},{"start":8,"end":9,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"A Jewish believer might find it challenging to accept something like this. Any sort of religionist today argues with God here. They think they have the mind of God in their religious practices. They say, “Well, God says this, and He commands us to perform rituals and sacraments in this way or that way, for this cause or that cause, this reason or that reason…” But the truth is, His ways are higher than our ways. His thoughts are higher than our thoughts. That might sound difficult to understand for you, but we cannot possibly know the depths of God’s character."},{"kind":"para","text":"If we look at the fruit of the Spirit (and we have several times over already), we might be able to say, “Yeah, I know what love is. I know what joy, peace, and patience look like.” You probably have a degree of understanding of it, but not to the point of God’s version of it. God’s love, joy, peace, and patience for you surpass any sort of knowledge you can obtain in this life. Think of the highest form of love in your life. Everyone has some measure of it somewhere or somehow. Once you get the highest measure of love on this Earth, that is but the lowest understanding of it in the character of God. God’s love far surpasses what we can fathom. That’s how His sovereignty works. It’s above and beyond our really small understanding of it. His ways are always higher than our ways."},{"kind":"para","text":"I laugh when I see churches perform ritualistic ceremonies today. It makes me giggle that they think they have the ways of God locked down to their incense and candle swinging. Like, is that the best we can come up with to identify the Lord’s glory and salvation? It makes me squirm to see little kids (who don’t know the Lord personally) take part in ritualistic services. First communions, infant baptisms, confessional booths, mediatory prayers, set and repeated prayers, candles to saints and angels are such a low and dismal form of displaying God’s highest ways on this Earth. Perhaps that is their excuse for it. They are doing it in “humility.” But really, all it does is show the world how cheap and small we view our God."},{"kind":"para","text":"God’s ways are far higher than our ways, so why are we still seeking to do things in our own ways? Wouldn’t it make sense to just follow the Lord’s ways and seek that with everything we have? I suppose that’s the best way we can surmise a false church when they have settled for their own ways and have stopped pursuing what God’s way (the Bible) says."}]}]},{"start":10,"end":13,"title":"God Accomplishes","entries":[{"start":10,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Even God’s way of preaching is higher than our ways of preaching and reaching. His Word will literally do what He wants it to. The last time Israel could bank on God’s Word for them was with Solomon. There have been glimpses and shimmers of God’s Word throughout 1 and 2 Kings, but the people have largely turned away from Him and anything He has to say. Look what is said about Samuel;"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And Samuel grew, and the LORD was with him, and did let none of his words fall to the ground.","ref":"1 Samuel 3:19"},{"kind":"para","text":"Samuel’s way of preaching was found in God’s way of preaching. He looked for the higher way. He wanted it to be God’s power, God’s Words, God’s moving, God’s protection, God’s direction, God’s abilities, character, and compassion that was displayed through his own meager and small way of preaching. Because of that, God greatly used Samuel."},{"kind":"para","text":"I don’t think a lot of people in the modern church are used by God today. They might pat themselves on the back and use the numbers of hands raised as their testing level of how good they can think themselves as, but really God’s way is far higher than these low, small thoughts that these preachers have for themselves. What I find fascinating and funny is that God uses the rain (the rain He controls) as an example of His Word (the Word He controls). It goes where He wants it to, and it does what it’s intended to. This is a very important message for every believer who tells people about Jesus. Even if it’s three words like “Jesus loves you,” God can and will use that. He will use His Word."},{"kind":"para","text":"God tells us that Jesus loves humanity. His Word displays that through every bout of scripture. That includes this section here. God is going to use His high Word to accomplish His high tasks. He did that when He created the Earth, and He has done it through the ministry and sacrifice of Jesus, as well as the continual outpouring of the prophets. God’s way of doing things is far better than our ways of doing things, so it only stands to reason that we take His way of doing them and apply them to our meager efforts. The end result will be a higher way than anything we can do on our own."},{"kind":"para","text":"In fact, God is taking the reins. He is saying, “I’m going to do it, because you guys aren’t listening. I will be taking this into my own hands so you can see how it’s done.” And when we allow the Lord to control the narrative and the work, and the outcome, this is what we are left with:"}]},{"start":12,"end":13,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"If we just allow God to do things His way, instead of taking things into our own hands and demolishing the good things of God, we would find “…joy…peace…singing…clapping…everlasting signs…” and comfort (hence the thorn into fir trees, and briers into myrtle trees)."},{"kind":"para","text":"That sounds far better than any religious service I’ve been to. I want that instead of religion. I want God’s way instead of the church’s way. I want His peace, instead of the world’s peace. Why should we ever settle for religious practices when we can have God’s personal working instead?"}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":9},{"start":10,"end":11},{"start":12,"end":13}],"verses":{"1":"Ho, every one that thirsteth, come ye to the waters, and he that hath no money; come ye, buy, and eat; yea, come, buy wine and milk without money and without price.","2":"Wherefore do ye spend money for that which is not bread? and your labour for that which satisfieth not? hearken diligently unto me, and eat ye that which is good, and let your soul delight itself in fatness.","3":"Incline your ear, and come unto me: hear, and your soul shall live; and I will make an everlasting covenant with you, even the sure mercies of David.","4":"Behold, I have given him for a witness to the people, a leader and commander to the people.","5":"Behold, thou shalt call a nation that thou knowest not, and nations that knew not thee shall run unto thee because of the Lord thy God, and for the Holy One of Israel; for he hath glorified thee.","6":"Seek ye the Lord while he may be found, call ye upon him while he is near:","7":"Let the wicked forsake his way, and the unrighteous man his thoughts: and let him return unto the Lord, and he will have mercy upon him; and to our God, for he will abundantly pardon.","8":"For my thoughts are not your thoughts, neither are your ways my ways, saith the Lord.","9":"For as the heavens are higher than the earth, so are my ways higher than your ways, and my thoughts than your thoughts.","10":"For as the rain cometh down, and the snow from heaven, and returneth not thither, but watereth the earth, and maketh it bring forth and bud, that it may give seed to the sower, and bread to the eater:","11":"So shall my word be that goeth forth out of my mouth: it shall not return unto me void, but it shall accomplish that which I please, and it shall prosper in the thing whereto I sent it.","12":"For ye shall go out with joy, and be led forth with peace: the mountains and the hills shall break forth before you into singing, and all the trees of the field shall clap their hands.","13":"Instead of the thorn shall come up the fir tree, and instead of the brier shall come up the myrtle tree: and it shall be to the Lord for a name, for an everlasting sign that shall not be cut off."}},
    "56": {"chapter":56,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: Our last chapter looked at the invitation of the world to salvation. It wasn't just the Israelites that had the right to God's good gift of salvation. God wanted everyone to know the door was open for anyone that was willing to walk through it. In fact, most of the Israelites that heard our last chapter probably wouldn't have been pleased with Isaiah's prophecy on the matter. They believed they deserved God's salvation alone, and that God should only serve them. They have it completely backwards."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is what this chapter is about, actually. It's about showing how backwards they have it. It's about the anticipation of God's promises, and it's about what true worship and true dedication in the Lord really looks like. It's not about God serving us. It's about us serving God!"}],"previously":["Our last chapter explored the invitation of the world to salvation. It wasn’t just the Israelites who had the right to God’s good gift of salvation. God wanted everyone to know the door was open for anyone willing to walk through it. In fact, most of the Israelites who heard our last chapter probably wouldn’t have been pleased with Isaiah’s prophecy on the matter. They believed they deserved God’s salvation alone and that God should only serve them. They have it completely backwards. That is what this chapter is about, actually. It’s about showing how backwards they have it. It’s about the anticipation of God’s promises and what true worship and true dedication in the Lord really look like. It’s not about God serving us. It’s about us serving God!"],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":2,"title":"Salvation Is Near","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord has been preparing this nation for His coming salvation for generations. He has made great promises to this nation, yet they seem to forget about them as they trek through life and toil through this world. The world entices them away from the promises of God, and that is really what the world is good at. There was a time in this world when things were created specifically to fix a problem or solve an issue that humans didn’t have a solution for. Now, things are created to distract us. Cellphones are useful for a great deal of things, but from what I’ve seen, everyone seems to use their cellphones for social media and what they call “Doom Scrolling.” We invent things to distract us; they are things to entertain us. That is what the world wants to do for the masses. They don’t want to solve any true issues; they just want to make you look the other way because the world is a cruel, dark place that doesn’t need to be illuminated upon, or we will see what it really looks like."},{"kind":"para","text":"God has been giving this nation reminders about the salvation that He has been promising since the beginning of time, and they seem to ignore it every time He brings it up. I think that was His plan all along, quite frankly. He knew they would reject and deny it, and that would lead them into their sins further and further until they were so far gone that the Lord would bring His salvation at their lowest point. God needed their attention. What is a better way to get a person’s attention than when they have nothing else to turn to? If you are like me, you probably don’t like going to see a doctor all too often. I have had nothing but bad experiences at doctor’s offices and from doctors in general. I try to avoid going to the hospital for anything (even if I broke my leg, I don’t know if I’d want to go). But if I was truly sick and in immense pain, I would have no choice but to go see a doctor in hopes that they will give me something to alleviate my hurts. They usually have something when I go there to help, but they also have some sort of ultimatum. Sadly, I have to wait until I just can’t take it anymore before I finally decide to turn to a doctor."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is how the Israelites have been with the Lord. They don’t want to go and see Him because they have had small glimpses of bad experiences with Him. Honestly, there have been some things that God has done that would make even the readers wonder in awe. So these people are worried they might do something else to make the Lord angry, and they could even die from their getting close to Him. The truth is, the people who have died from getting too close to the Lord were simply not listening. The Lord warned all these people about these things. It was not as if God didn’t say anything and waited until people started dying before He pronounced the problem. Rather, He tells you your problems, gives you the solution, and it is up to you to follow. Most of the time, the Israelites didn’t. If they would just look throughout their lineage and history, they would not just see God judging them and destroying them. Instead, they would see God protecting, guiding, strengthening, healing, caring, and training them. The people loved the world, though. The world was good at numbing them from spiritual, mental, and physical conflict. It’s easy to fall for the traps of this world, and I say this as a Christian man. If you are a perfect Christian today, you can argue with my analysis all you want, but the truth of the matter is, you are struggling with pride by the very thought that you don’t struggle with any other type of sin."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"If we say that we have no sin, we deceive ourselves, and the truth is not in us. If we confess our sins, he is faithful and just to forgive us our sins, and to cleanse us from all unrighteousness. If we say that we have not sinned, we make him a liar, and his word is not in us.","ref":"1 John 1:8-10"},{"kind":"para","text":"The problem was not with their enticements with the world, mind you. Their problem was with the willful rejection of the Lord to follow sin instead of Him. Because of it, they ended up doing some very evil and despicable things. Furthermore, they encouraged the evil already present in the world to do more evil. Because, if God’s children can do it, why can’t everyone else, right?"}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Blessed is the repenter. God has the right to bless people who have turned away from following the rudiments of the world to pursue the righteousness of God. Yet, there wasn’t much blessing going on during the time of Isaiah. If these people had listened to Isaiah and the Lord here, they would have seen God’s salvation come sooner. In fact, the cities around them would also benefit from their repentance."},{"kind":"para","text":"Sin ripples and causes others to err. But repentance also ripples and causes others to be blessed. I suppose it depends on the individual about which one they would like to provide for their neighbors around them."}]}]},{"start":3,"end":5,"title":"A Better Name","entries":[{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God opens the blessing to all if He has blessed one. Think about it; if you are in a good mood during the day, you will treat others with a better mood, which will change their mood and so on and so forth. If the law of “good moods” works in that way, why wouldn’t the law of repentance work the same?"},{"kind":"para","text":"There is no one who can separate themselves from the salvation of the Lord once they have it. Once they have it, everyone sees a different side of you and wonders, “How can I have that?” The best news is, they can have that same Spirit too through the Lord. God will not close off His grace and salvation for a select few. I’m sorry if that upsets you, but that is just His nature. If you are upset because the most sinful person you know can and should come to the Lord (with an open invitation from the Lord), there is something wrong with your faith and heart."}]},{"start":4,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"“Eunuchs” can be an assortment of people. Some of them were emasculated, so we could rightfully place them in the “handicap” category, and that is likely how they were looked at. God opens the invitation for those that are strangers, those that are extremely distant from Him, and those that may not ever have an understanding of who He is to come to Him and have a great place of dwelling with Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"I’ve seen a lot of handicapped people in my life, many of them quite recently as my wife is a teacher for special needs children. Some of these kids are… interesting. They curse up a storm (most of the time out of randomness), they can be mean and cruel and start throwing things (sometimes for no reason), and they are often wandering both in mind and body. Some of these children can’t even talk. There have been some in wheelchairs who have never been able to walk, and they can’t write, and they don’t know how to respond to questions, or take tests, or do anything without the help of other people. You might read that and think, “Boy, they got it rough. What does God do with them? Can they even be saved without the knowledge of Jesus?” My short answer is yes. You should see their face light up when they see something they like. Perhaps they can never fully understand the Lord’s mercy and sacrifice, but God has a special place for them in eternity."},{"kind":"para","text":"According to this verse, God gives the handicapped a “name better than of sons and daughters.” He calls them “royalty.” They are the weakest among us, we could argue. Yet, in eternity, they will be the people sitting on thrones. That is an amazing thing to me."}]}]},{"start":6,"end":12,"title":"Real Success","entries":[{"start":6,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There are a few things that should be pointed out in these verses. First, God calls the furthest of strangers to Him. If they are willing to follow the Lord, the Lord is more than willing to accept them. He says that they should keep His “sabbath from polluting it.” Now, there’s a lot of debate about what the sabbath ultimately means, when we should be celebrating it, and why it’s important to the law. I’ve spoken about this more times than I care to. The sabbath is an Old Testament law, and like all Old Testament laws, it was to represent our sinful nature. It just showed us how sinful we are. Can we attest to any times in scripture (old or new testament) where the Lord dwells on the sabbath? Every day should be a sabbath for a Christian, arguably, but the sabbath is not about simply keeping the law. You misunderstand God’s law if you think it’s simply about obeying it. We should “observe,” which means to “look into” His law. Furthermore, when Christ died, we are no longer under the law, but under grace. So the argument would have to be against Christ and against Paul:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Let no man therefore judge you in meat, or in drink, or in respect of an holyday, or of the new moon, or of the sabbath days:","ref":"Colossians 2:16"},{"kind":"para","text":"If there is a Seventh Day Adventist, a Jewish Rabbi, or some sort of other Sabbath day worshipper who tries to stop you from worshipping God on Sundays, or whichever days you have available to worship God, bring them to this verse."}]},{"start":8,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Jesus didn’t shy away from the outcasts. It wasn’t the religionists that Jesus went after. He didn’t go to those that were well off in their churches or those that were keeping the law to the letter. He didn’t try to search for those that were “good” wholesome Christians trying to do good wholesome things."},{"kind":"para","text":"Rather, He went to those that were neglected. He went to the homeless. He went to the outcasts and the hurt. He talked about Samaritans quite a bit. He spoke to a few Samaritan women about salvation. They were looked at as outcasts by Jewish society, but not to Jesus. Those were the people He cared about the most. They felt alone and without any hope, and He only went to them. He shunned and preached against the religionists, in fact. They were some of His enemies. Take that into perspective with your religious affiliations."}]},{"start":9,"end":9,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This seems to be a different look at the people of the land. He refers to them as “beasts of the field, come to devour.” At the time of Isaiah’s writing, that is how they were acting. They were not acting like humans. They were not caring for one another. They were acting like beasts and animals that would rip someone’s head off if they got too close. They were barbaric. Not just the Israelites either. Most of the world had turned that way. Israel didn’t help them out of it though; they just joined into it."},{"kind":"para","text":"Imagine our churches today. They are supposed to be places of equipping and holiness. Instead, we see many of them as “beasts of the field, come to devour.” They are looking to try and implement the world into their congregation and want to make everyone feel welcome. So what do they do? They waver on the truth. They start accepting things that God has openly and repeatedly said through His word and in your own conscience that were wrong. He hates many of the things the churches are doing today. Even the best churches today still have something that the Lord hates (usually it’s a prideful pastor, but it can delve even deeper than that)."},{"kind":"para","text":"I’ve seen churches openly stand up for homosexuality. I’ve seen churches openly stand up for murdering babies. I’ve seen churches openly stand up for assassinating a president. They’ve openly stood up for burning down “rival” churches (rival meaning these churches were preaching the opposite of them). I’ve seen church leaders actually smile and applaud over their congregants leaving the church. The invitation is still open to these beasts. They just have to be willing to repent."}]},{"start":10,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is the look of the modern church. It really pains me to equate this, but it’s absolutely true to the letter. The leaders of our modern church are like dumb dogs who cannot bark. They are lazy and love to slumber. Perhaps it’s not a physical laziness that we might see (though I’ve known pastors who are never present for their congregation, so maybe it is also a physical laziness). But some pastors can just be spiritually or mentally lazy. They don’t do their homework before giving a sermon on Sundays. Perhaps they don’t have any real heart for the person they are supposed to be mentoring and counseling. That is a lazy heart if they show no genuine compassion for your hurts."},{"kind":"para","text":"They are also “greedy dogs” who only do their ministry if it means some sort of gain for themselves. They don’t do it because they were called to do it. They do it because they get a paycheck. And they won’t do it with any sort of zeal. They will just do it because that is their title and so that is their position. I hate lazy pastors. Yet, that seems to be the way of the modern church. They are just shepherds who cannot understand. I find that part interesting honestly. It says they “cannot” understand, but I could argue that they simply just don’t want to understand. They often don’t care about their flock. They just care about how they look to the outside world. It’s disgusting and disgraceful. That is what a lazy and uncaring pastor is; disgraceful. God is graceful. He pours grace out. Uncaring pastors are disgraceful. They rob your grace."}]},{"start":12,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Let’s hope that tomorrow is not like today. I’ve heard pastors on a victory high, talking about the numbers from their church on a given Sunday. They discuss how many people attended, how many raised their hands, how many signed up to serve, and how many signed up to be baptized, and the list goes on. They say, “Next week will be even bigger because of this event or that event.” Yet, they fail to realize that they are looking at the wrong things. Numbers are interesting and great, but how many of those people are being discipled? How many of them are actually belonging to the church? How many were actually stopped and talked to after the service? Do they actually care about serving the Lord, or are they more concerned about serving the church? There is a stark difference between being motivated by your flesh and being motivated by God’s Spirit."},{"kind":"para","text":"I am a firm believer that there is only a small percentage of people who go to church who actually serve from God’s Spirit. Sadly, most pastors don’t even serve from the right spirit. They have the same mentality as the Israelites did: “Come to our church, we will do all the same things we’ve been doing for years and years before. Tomorrow will be just the same as it was yesterday, and we will do it even more.” If you are a Christian, you should want your tomorrow to look different than your today. Success is not based on numerical growth. It’s not based on how much fun you had. It’s not even based on how big your church is and how many people showed up to your planned events. This is what success looks like:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Fulfil ye my joy, that ye be likeminded, having the same love, being of one accord, of one mind.","ref":"Philippians 2:2"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Finally, be ye all of one mind, having compassion one of another, love as brethren, be pitiful, be courteous:","ref":"1 Peter 3:8"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Now I beseech you, brethren, by the name of our Lord Jesus Christ, that ye all speak the same thing, and that there be no divisions among you; but that ye be perfectly joined together in the same mind and in the same judgment.","ref":"1 Corinthians 1:10"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Finally, brethren, farewell. Be perfect, be of good comfort, be of one mind, live in peace; and the God of love and peace shall be with you.","ref":"2 Corinthians 13:11"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"That ye may with one mind and one mouth glorify God, even the Father of our Lord Jesus Christ.","ref":"Romans 15:6"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Behold, how good and how pleasant it is for brethren to dwell together in unity!","ref":"Psalm 133:1"},{"kind":"para","text":"A church that is of one mind, which is the mind of Christ rather than the mind of the Pastor, will achieve “perfect” unity. That is what success looks like. It looks like a group of people united in serving the Lord with His mind and compassion for humanity."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":9},{"start":10,"end":11},{"start":12,"end":12}],"verses":{"1":"Thus saith the Lord, Keep ye judgment, and do justice: for my salvation is near to come, and my righteousness to be revealed.","2":"Blessed is the man that doeth this, and the son of man that layeth hold on it; that keepeth the sabbath from polluting it, and keepeth his hand from doing any evil.","3":"Neither let the son of the stranger, that hath joined himself to the Lord, speak, saying, The Lord hath utterly separated me from his people: neither let the eunuch say, Behold, I am a dry tree.","4":"For thus saith the Lord unto the eunuchs that keep my sabbaths, and choose the things that please me, and take hold of my covenant;","5":"Even unto them will I give in mine house and within my walls a place and a name better than of sons and of daughters: I will give them an everlasting name, that shall not be cut off.","6":"Also the sons of the stranger, that join themselves to the Lord, to serve him, and to love the name of the Lord, to be his servants, every one that keepeth the sabbath from polluting it, and taketh hold of my covenant;","7":"Even them will I bring to my holy mountain, and make them joyful in my house of prayer: their burnt offerings and their sacrifices shall be accepted upon mine altar; for mine house shall be called an house of prayer for all people.","8":"The Lord God, which gathereth the outcasts of Israel saith, Yet will I gather others to him, beside those that are gathered unto him.","9":"All ye beasts of the field, come to devour, yea, all ye beasts in the forest.","10":"His watchmen are blind: they are all ignorant, they are all dumb dogs, they cannot bark; sleeping, lying down, loving to slumber.","11":"Yea, they are greedy dogs which can never have enough, and they are shepherds that cannot understand: they all look to their own way, every one for his gain, from his quarter.","12":"Come ye, say they, I will fetch wine, and we will fill ourselves with strong drink; and to morrow shall be as this day, and much more abundant."}},
    "57": {"chapter":57,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: In our last chapter, we focused on God's importance in serving Him. He is our salvation, and His name is the only one worth serving while we are here on this Earth. Without Him, we would be destined to failure. We would be destined to the grave and into harsher problems that we wouldn't be able to deal with in our own strength."},{"kind":"para","text":"In fact, that is what this chapter looks at. It contrasts the differences between a righteous person, and a wicked person, and why God treats them accordingly. We are going to look at how God gifts based on what actions we take, versus how the world gifts by our actions. One is temporary, the other is eternal."}],"previously":["In our last chapter, we focused on God’s importance in serving Him. He is our salvation, and His name is the only one worth serving while we are here on this Earth. Without Him, we would be destined to failure. We would be destined to the grave and into harsher problems that we wouldn’t be able to deal with in our own strength. In fact, that is what this chapter looks at. It contrasts the differences between a righteous person and a wicked person and why God treats them accordingly. We are going to look at how God gifts based on what actions we take, versus how the world gifts by our actions. One is temporary, the other is eternal."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":2,"title":"The Righteous Perish","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"In our modern day, righteous men don’t just simply perish; they are abused. If you are a righteous man living your life for the Lord in our era, it is quite likely that you will be very much alone in your endeavors. Even the churches today abuse the righteous, hardworking, and loving Christians in their toils. It’s as if people have nothing better to do than to hate on those who are actually making a change."},{"kind":"para","text":"The funny thing is, the people who hate the righteous so much are often those who used to love these same people when they were in the world just like them. Once a man changes his ways, you can physically see the people who never actually cared about the person to begin with. When you turned to the Lord in your life, you probably noticed that as well. The moment you started following Christ and began telling your family about it, your own family became an enemy to you. You seem to hit a nerve when it comes to following Jesus. I’m not exactly sure why other than this world simply hates God."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There is hope for a righteous man. While the world tries to tear the righteous down and completely reject them, the Lord gives them a place of rest. The world hates me, but the Lord loves me. I’d rather have the love of God than the love of the world anyway. If the world can turn its back so quickly on me for following what is true, right, and good, then why would I ever trust the world again with anything I have? I will not (and cannot) ever depend on the world again, and I am completely fine with that. I have the Lord to shepherd and guide me."},{"kind":"para","text":"With that said, it would be wise for the people of this world to utilize the righteous while they can. Some day there won’t be many righteous people left. Everyone will, eventually, be given over to their own devices, and when that happens, they will regret not having followed the righteous into truth and holding them much higher. Just look at the picture of Christ’s crucifixion. All the disciples and the people that Jesus was able to heal were completely burdened by the fact that their Savior was just killed. They thought all hope was lost. If they could kill this innocent man for seemingly no reason, what’s stopping them from killing any worshippers of God? Honestly, nothing is stopping them."},{"kind":"para","text":"At the end of the day, I guarantee the disciples wished they had spent more exclusive time with Jesus once He was placed on that cross. They regretted not being more involved with Christ. Thankfully, Christ shows Himself to them after His resurrection and then gives them the Holy Spirit to continually work with Him even after He’s gone, but they shouldn’t have waited so late to really get to know Christ. I think if you are a pastor today, there is a great need for you to get to know your faith congregants. You can’t get to know them better after they are dead and gone, and you will regret not taking the time with them while they are here. Sadly, I don’t see pastors thinking that way though, and the majority of the congregants who are righteous and good are neglected and forgotten."}]}]},{"start":3,"end":10,"title":"A Need For Change","entries":[{"start":3,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Now we have a look at the absolute opposite of the righteous. Obviously, the Lord is contrasting the two here. He is detailing His plans for those who follow after Him and His ways, and the plans for those who completely reject Him and His ways. These are very choice words as well. God calls the unrighteous, “sons of the sorceress, the seed of the adulterer and the whore.” In other words, you come from a line of evil. He also gives a very detailed picture of what these people do. They are people who “sport” themselves. They lift themselves up and think they are something special. Prideful people, really. They “draw out the tongue.” They are not people who use their time and speech for encouraging and helping their fellow man. They are people who use their time and speech to belittle people and tear people apart (again, as if they have nothing better to do with their time). They are a “seed of falsehood.” That is a sad characteristic to be given to a man. There’s nothing good about me if I am just from a family of lies and deceit. There are many in our world who come from such families, and they are no wiser to the truth. In fact, they are truth deniers through and through. You can literally punch them in the face with the truth, and they still wouldn’t believe it. They are just arrogant and ignorant. Foolish would be a better name for them."}]},{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"We may not have idols “under every green tree” and we may not be “slaying the children in the valleys under the clifts of the rocks,” but we have the same tendencies as them. We live in California at the moment, and their new motto is “A sanctuary for abortions.” When your state motto represents child murder, I think you have a pretty big problem. Slaying children, in our day and age, is actually quite a normal thing. I assume they counted it normal during the days of Isaiah as well, because God has to address it quite a few times. He always links it to wickedness as well. That’s not by accident. Killing children is evil. Period. I shouldn’t have to say that, but it seems our world doesn’t seem to get it."},{"kind":"para","text":"Worshipping idols and lifting yourselves up in pride is also evil. But worshipping idols and killing children (though related) are very different kinds of evil. Honestly, that is the reason most people kill their babies today. They do it because of their worship of their idol called money. They either don’t have enough to support a child, so they kill it, or they have too much to give to a child, so they kill it. Their god is money, and nothing (not even a child) is going to get in the way of that."}]},{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"These wicked people are even worshipping the rocks according to the Lord here. It’s not making God happy that they are doing this. Actually, I have reason to believe that these people were doing it to try and appease the God of Israel. They were doing it out of a traditional, law-abiding act of worship towards their God (the God of Moses). The problem was, they were not doing it because they truly loved the Lord. They were doing it to try and appease the Lord so they could continue on in their sins. They did it to simply get the Lord out of the way and worship their fake gods (whom they loved more). Sadly, I think that is still the case today."},{"kind":"para","text":"We go to church on Sundays, not because we love the Lord and we want to get closer to Him. We do it to give Him His time (that we believe is due to Him) and we can have the rest of the week to ourselves to do whatever we like. Sundays are for God, the rest of the week is for us. I think that is how most pastors worship too honestly. I’ve seen many church leaders only show up to specific things for a moment, but they are only focused on Sundays. God would likely view those people in the same way as He views the Israelites here. They are not doing anything for the Lord; they are simply doing it to get the Lord out of the way."}]},{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"It’s possible that these people were actually making their beds on top of mountains. They did a lot of false worship in high places, which is something that God talks about being a very bad thing throughout 1 and 2 Kings. I’ve said this before, but I think it’s good to repeat myself sometimes: it is said that these high places represent a god or goddess of lust. Perhaps some sort of sexual gifting from whatever god they are sacrificing to. They do these things in high places for everyone to see. It’s a free show, honestly, and who doesn’t like a free show? Sex sells, even in our age today. I couldn’t imagine the things they likely witnessed, and I’m not sure I would want to imagine it."}]},{"start":8,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Going back to the “whore” remark from verse 3, God says they are this way because they are serving false gods. Not just serving these gods, but actually sacrificing things to those gods. For instance, they might sacrifice a child to these false gods in hopes for riches in return. They might sacrifice their children’s virginity for hopes of some sort of personal gain. They sacrifice themselves and their time (as well as freedom) to these gods for aid and personal alleviation. They are scratching an itch that only sin will cure."},{"kind":"para","text":"The problem with curing an itch with sin is that it usually leaves you feeling more itchy. Sin is a disease, and it burns and itches just like any other disease. Some of these people do it to try and earn fame from their sacrifices. They are famous now; they are written in God’s Holy Word. But they are not famous for anything good. God doesn’t remember them for their good deeds. He will only remember them as people who “set their bed” in the wrong places and did evil things to innocent people."},{"kind":"para","text":"Honestly, God will only remember you in one of two ways. He will either remember you for turning to Him for salvation, or He will remember you for your wickedness."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"My little children, these things write I unto you, that ye sin not. And if any man sin, we have an advocate with the Father, Jesus Christ the righteous:","ref":"1 John 2:1"}]},{"start":9,"end":9,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Here’s the cold hard truth: If there are any people in Hell today, it is not because they were just too ignorant. It wasn’t because they simply didn’t know, or no one told them. Rather, they are in Hell because they put themselves there. That was their own personal choice."},{"kind":"para","text":"God has given every possible reason and motive to get you to turn to Him. If you spend your life walking away from Him, you only walk in one other direction, and that is into eternal hell-fire. That’s on you. No one else can be blamed for that when people have told you the truth about eternity. God will always reveal His truth to you one way or another, and it is up to you to either listen to Him or reject and run from Him."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Not every one that saith unto me, Lord, Lord, shall enter into the kingdom of heaven; but he that doeth the will of my Father which is in heaven. Many will say to me in that day, Lord, Lord, have we not prophesied in thy name? and in thy name have cast out devils? and in thy name done many wonderful works? And then will I profess unto them, I never knew you: depart from me, ye that work iniquity.","ref":"Matthew 7:21-23"},{"kind":"para","text":"What a sad ending to a hard fought life. Fight in this life all you want, but if you don't have Christ your fight is in vain."}]},{"start":10,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I’ve known a lot of very talented, very rich, and very (seemingly) successful people. They put on a great show in front of everyone. Behind the scenes, however, it is all falling apart. I knew one particular man who seemed to have everything. He had a multimillion-dollar home, children, a multimillion-dollar RV, a backyard overlooking the valley, a nice big pool, real granite countertops, a thriving business, and a life that most Americans would kill to get. Yet, his marriage was falling apart. He wasn’t sure what he was going to get at any given moment from his wife, and he was constantly afraid that divorce papers were going to suddenly end up in front of him. He tried to get help from multiple people, but nothing seemed to be working. No matter what he was doing, it just didn’t seem like it was enough. Everything looked fine to the outside world, but if you were on the inside, you could see that he was burdened."},{"kind":"para","text":"Living a life of sin (no matter how much materialistic items you have around you) will begin to weary you. Because you view your materials as your source of success, those are the things you will lean on, and you’ll never know how hopeless you really are. Your salvation is in your own hand. That is how you end up in hell. When we place our salvation in ourselves, we will always fail ourselves, and we will never see our need to change from our sins."}]}]},{"start":11,"end":14,"title":"Gambling Life","entries":[{"start":11,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Honestly, if we evaluated our excuses and purposes, who or why is it that we choose to live this way? We have no reason to lie, yet that is something we always fall back on for some reason. We are afraid to tell the truth, why? We have no reason to steal, yet that is something we always fall back on for some reason. We are afraid to miss out on something, why?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Some would probably argue that it’s our environment and the people who raised us, but the man I was just speaking about, who was rich, was raised in a rich family. Yet, he struggled with all the same sins as everyone else. We are afraid to listen to the Lord because the pleasures and rewards for sinning are immediate, whereas the pleasures and rewards for righteousness are usually delayed. God seems to delay His reward for those who follow Him, and so most people don’t think it’s worth it to wait. However, the gifts and pleasures of sin only last for a season."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Choosing rather to suffer affliction with the people of God, than to enjoy the pleasures of sin for a season;","ref":"Hebrews 11:25"},{"kind":"para","text":"But the gifts and pleasures of righteousness last for eternity:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Esteeming the reproach of Christ greater riches than the treasures in Egypt: for he had respect unto the recompence of the reward.","ref":"Hebrews 11:26"},{"kind":"para","text":"The riches of eternity are far more valuable and heavier than the riches of this world. The delayed rewards of God are always far more worth the wait than the instant draining rewards of this world."}]},{"start":12,"end":14,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"If you trust your own hands more than you trust the hands of God, God will let you save yourself. God doesn’t rob you of your own free will. He can still use you, even if it’s unintentional to you, but He will ultimately let you drown in your own desires. He does it to show you how small and sad those desires actually are. They look like they are worth something, but you will just come back feeling empty, and by the time everything is said and done, God will give you a look at your life and say, “Was that worth it?” What a great question to ask ourselves by the way. Was what we did today (for or against the Lord) worth our time and effort? Was it worth our reward? Was it worth what we lost and what we gained? Was it worth the consequences in the future? Let’s hope so."},{"kind":"para","text":"It’s funny, I was talking to someone the other day about gambling. We had won some scratchers (they were a gift to us), and we’ve just been turning them in and getting more scratchers. It has been a neverending game, it seems. When we brought it to my in-laws, my brother-in-law said, “Doesn’t that book of yours say something about gambling being a sin?” I said, “Not that I know of, can you show me where it says that?” He just shrugged and laughed. Honestly, I can argue that every single day of our lives is a gamble. We are gambling on every single action we make. The consequences of our actions will always be up in the air, and we will never know what the end results will be until (sometimes) much later. Life is one big gamble, and the Lord knows it. That is not to say that I condone gambling (especially if you have a problem or addiction), but it is to say that we never know what life is going to throw at us at any given second. God can give you big rewards for your actions, or we might face a storm. Either way, if we are in the hands of the Father, He knows how to guide and control your circumstances. It is far wiser (if you are going to gamble) to bet on things related to God’s promises. His salvation and will are always a winning ticket."}]}]},{"start":15,"end":21,"title":"Where Is Peace?","entries":[{"start":15,"end":15,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"You want to bet on something that is sure to win? Bet on God’s love and holiness. Bet on His perfection and standards. Bet on His salvation and providence. Betting on anything here is definitely a gamble, but betting on God in eternity is a sure win every time. He will always be in His place, and He will always save those who have a “contrite” and “humble spirit.” Those people are His people. They mimic His Spirit. If we need revival, bet on His Spirit and be humble."}]},{"start":16,"end":16,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"By the way, every spirit that is here on this Earth was made by the Lord. There have been movies and even actually people who portray this idea that they sold their souls to the devil. Sir (or ma'am), your soul was given to the devil the day you were conceived;"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Behold, I was shapen in iniquity; and in sin did my mother conceive me.","ref":"Psalm 51:5"},{"kind":"para","text":"You cannot sell it to him. He already had it. You can, however, sell it to the Lord. God will purchase it. He will buy all your sin with it too, and then He will clean you up and turn you around to face Him. He will lead you and give you a path to follow. He will love you and take care of you. He will give you peace and safety. He will give you providence and assurance. He will give you salvation and boldness. He will give you your life’s needs and overflow you with grace."},{"kind":"para","text":"Satan would never do this for you. The devil’s rewards only rob you of life and joy. God’s rewards are continually gifting. It’s like having two buckets that you need to fill with water. The Satan bucket has a hole in it. You can keep pouring your life (water) into the Satan bucket, but it just keeps running out. The God bucket is a new bucket. There is no hole in it. If you fill that bucket, it doesn’t deplete; it will just begin to overflow after you have filled it. That is how life looks in this world. Why waste your time on a bucket that will never be full?"}]},{"start":17,"end":17,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God has to punish the wicked in this way. It’s kind of funny. Of course, it’s not funny that people purposely try to hurt the Lord. But it is funny that people are hurt the most by God giving them over to their devices. God punishes the wicked by giving them what they want. Eventually, one day, God will stop giving them what they want and just start getting rid of them. They will be so full of themselves that they will never turn to God anymore. This world is headed in that direction. We see more and more of it every single day. Just driving on the road, we see plenty of it."}]},{"start":18,"end":18,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is God’s way of doing things now. He has not given up on humanity yet. There are still people who are willing to repent and turn towards the Lord. As long as there are still people who can be saved, God will not give up on us. There will be a time in the future, though, where no one will turn to God anymore. When that day comes, it will spell disaster for anyone still here on Earth."}]},{"start":19,"end":19,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God wants to heal people and give His salvation to His creation. He doesn’t want anyone to be lost or hurting, nor does He want His creation to be hurting each other. He desires for everyone to know Him, love Him, serve Him, and love and serve others. However, that is not the world we will live in. As long as there are people who reject the Lord today, there will be wars and fighting."}]},{"start":20,"end":21,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Think about it. Have you noticed that a lot of people are calling for “world peace,” yet we have not obtained it? Do we know why? Well, it’s because of our wickedness. The people who call for peace are the same people who don’t know what peace even looks like. They have a rough idea of what peace is and think the only way to get peace is by destroying anyone who doesn’t agree with them. That is the least peaceful method I’ve heard to achieve peace. They think that once their enemies are out of their way, they will have world peace."},{"kind":"para","text":"The truth is, the wicked could run the world (and one day they certainly will), but they still won’t be able to find peace here. Why? Because they are not peaceful people. There is no such thing as peace in this world full of wickedness."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Peace I leave with you, my peace I give unto you: not as the world giveth, give I unto you. Let not your heart be troubled, neither let it be afraid.","ref":"John 14:27"},{"kind":"para","text":"The world has an idea of peace, but that is not what real peace is. Really, peace is only found in Christ and His finished work on the cross. The Christians who truly know and fully believe in that are the most peaceful people I have ever met. Without it, it’s a phony peace. It’s a conditional peace. It’s only a temporary peace (if it’s peace at all). You don’t find peace by attacking your enemies. You find peace by accepting the Lord."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":9},{"start":10,"end":10},{"start":11,"end":11},{"start":12,"end":14},{"start":15,"end":15},{"start":16,"end":16},{"start":17,"end":17},{"start":18,"end":18},{"start":19,"end":19},{"start":20,"end":21}],"verses":{"1":"The righteous perisheth, and no man layeth it to heart: and merciful men are taken away, none considering that the righteous is taken away from the evil to come.","2":"He shall enter into peace: they shall rest in their beds, each one walking in his uprightness.","3":"But draw near hither, ye sons of the sorceress, the seed of the adulterer and the whore.","4":"Against whom do ye sport yourselves? against whom make ye a wide mouth, and draw out the tongue? are ye not children of transgression, a seed of falsehood.","5":"Enflaming yourselves with idols under every green tree, slaying the children in the valleys under the clifts of the rocks?","6":"Among the smooth stones of the stream is thy portion; they, they are thy lot: even to them hast thou poured a drink offering, thou hast offered a meat offering. Should I receive comfort in these?","7":"Upon a lofty and high mountain hast thou set thy bed: even thither wentest thou up to offer sacrifice.","8":"Behind the doors also and the posts hast thou set up thy remembrance: for thou hast discovered thyself to another than me, and art gone up; thou hast enlarged thy bed, and made thee a covenant with them; thou lovedst their bed where thou sawest it.","9":"And thou wentest to the king with ointment, and didst increase thy perfumes, and didst send thy messengers far off, and didst debase thyself even unto hell.","10":"Thou art wearied in the greatness of thy way; yet saidst thou not, There is no hope: thou hast found the life of thine hand; therefore thou wast not grieved.","11":"And of whom hast thou been afraid or feared, that thou hast lied, and hast not remembered me, nor laid it to thy heart? have not I held my peace even of old, and thou fearest me not?","12":"I will declare thy righteousness, and thy works; for they shall not profit thee.","13":"When thou criest, let thy companies deliver thee; but the wind shall carry them all away; vanity shall take them: but he that putteth his trust in me shall possess the land, and shall inherit my holy mountain;","14":"And shall say, Cast ye up, cast ye up, prepare the way, take up the stumblingblock out of the way of my people.","15":"For thus saith the high and lofty One that inhabiteth eternity, whose name is Holy; I dwell in the high and holy place, with him also that is of a contrite and humble spirit, to revive the spirit of the humble, and to revive the heart of the contrite ones.","16":"For I will not contend for ever, neither will I be always wroth: for the spirit should fail before me, and the souls which I have made.","17":"For the iniquity of his covetousness was I wroth, and smote him: I hid me, and was wroth, and he went on frowardly in the way of his heart.","18":"I have seen his ways, and will heal him: I will lead him also, and restore comforts unto him and to his mourners.","19":"I create the fruit of the lips; Peace, peace to him that is far off, and to him that is near, saith the Lord; and I will heal him.","20":"But the wicked are like the troubled sea, when it cannot rest, whose waters cast up mire and dirt.","21":"There is no peace, saith my God, to the wicked."}},
    "58": {"chapter":58,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: In our last chapter, we got a very bleak description of what happens to the land of Moab if they don't turn to the Lord. Actually, the way it's written, it seems that these things are finality. This IS what will happen to Moab. We will see that by the end of this chapter here."},{"kind":"para","text":"In this chapter, we get what COULD happen if Moab decides to turn to the Lord and repent of their wickedness. They could be prospering, and they could be protected. They could even be a safe place for those looking for a fresh start after the rest of the lands are captured by Assyria. Of course, this is not the path that Moab will take, and so the last chapter will become their reality."}],"previously":["In our last chapter, God emphasized the theme of expressing the cares of this world versus the cares of the Lord. We often choose to reject the most needful things in life because we want to simply enjoy our lives, knowing our days are numbered. To us, enjoying life means doing whatever we want, however we want, whenever we want. However, God’s version of joy is knowing Him and serving Him. Having lived on both sides of that lifestyle, I can honestly say that serving God has been far more enjoyable and more blessed. In this chapter, God pushes the envelope further by challenging their vain traditions and rituals. He examines the things they are doing, thinking they are all doing the right things, and points out why it’s all wrong and must be stopped and changed. This is a very useful chapter for combating modern-day religious practices and aligning them with God’s genuine heart."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":5,"title":"Mercy Is A Theme","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There's a lot of times in scripture when God calls for crying. He tells us to hurt together:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And whether one member suffer, all the members suffer with it; or one member be honoured, all the members rejoice with it.","ref":"1 Corinthians 12:26"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"A time to weep, and a time to laugh; a time to mourn, and a time to dance;","ref":"Ecclesiastes 3:4"},{"kind":"para","text":"He tells us to feel hurt and mourn for our sins and evil acts:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For his anger endureth but a moment; in his favour is life: weeping may endure for a night, but joy cometh in the morning.","ref":"Psalm 30:5"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Be afflicted, and mourn, and weep: let your laughter be turned to mourning, and your joy to heaviness.","ref":"James 4:9"},{"kind":"para","text":"We are told to mourn over loss, difficulty and sin:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Blessed are they that mourn: for they shall be comforted.","ref":"Matthew 5:4"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Then David and the people that were with him lifted up their voice and wept, until they had no more power to weep.","ref":"1 Samuel 30:4"},{"kind":"para","text":"Even God weeps:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Jesus wept.","ref":"John 11:35"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Precious in the sight of the LORD is the death of his saints.","ref":"Psalm 116:15"},{"kind":"para","text":"Crying (in the eyes of the world) is not a very sought after ministry. The Lord commands it though, and it would be wise to listen to that command if we are going to be proper ministers:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Rejoice with them that do rejoice, and weep with them that weep.","ref":"Romans 12:15"},{"kind":"para","text":"In this instance, the Lord is telling the prophet to weep. Jeremiah was known as the “weeping prophet,” but I believe that every Christian leader should have the ability to genuinely weep with the hurting, sick, and sinful. We should not grow calloused to the sins of our culture, nor should we try to sugarcoat the truth to make it more palatable. We should speak the truth with sensitivity, not wavering on core truths. I think there is an acceptable time to stay silent on some topics of truth and lies, but there is never a time to keep silent on core absolutes."},{"kind":"para","text":"I know we have spoken about this before, but I want us to look at it again as a reminder of how seriously the Lord takes the pleas and cries of His called-out leaders. I’ve met far too many leaders in the church (especially) who cannot feel a single thing for a hurting soul. They are so far detached from their own emotions that they can’t seem to grasp the emotions and hurts of others. Honestly, I think a good portion of them felt alone in their hurts, and so they just treat everyone else the same way they were treated rather than turning the tide and doing the right thing."},{"kind":"para","text":"A man of God who can genuinely feel your hurt is a wasted and neglected ministry today. I have only met (perhaps) two or three genuine people who have cared enough about my hurts to actually try and lift them with me. I’ve strived my best to cry aloud to those around me and be a burden carrier. All men of God should not just be lifting their voice like a trumpet. All men of God should be able to cry aloud, too."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"You might read this and think, “Is God complimenting them here? Didn’t He have nothing but bad news about the people of Israel before? He was saying they were wayward, and now He’s saying they are righteous?” No, they were doing good godly things, but they were not doing them for good godly purposes. Like I’ve said, they had a notion to do what was good in the eyes of God (their traditions, their services, their sacraments, and sacrifices), but they didn’t do it so they could dedicate themselves to the Lord. They did it to get the Lord out of the way. I fear that is still the main problem in religion today."},{"kind":"para","text":"Think about it. Every religious service I have ever been to has been met with traditional expectations, mundane repetitions, and quickly getting service and ministry out of the way, for what? I suppose it’s probably for the same reasons as the Israelites. They wanted to get God out of the way so they could do what really brings them joy. Instead of finding joy in God’s ministry, they found joy in worldly services more. Worshipping God was a necessity, while worshipping themselves (and their false gods) was a privilege. Is that not the same in churches today?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Show me a church today that is thriving, and I will show you the saints who enjoy their toils versus the saints who are just there because they need to get God out of the way for their week. You’d be surprised (I think) at how many people just go to church because they have to, not because they want to."}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"They want God to give them something in return for their good service and obedience. Again, there is no heart behind their ministry. A heartless ministry is, in my opinion, the coldest ministry of all. How shallow and evil a man must be to have no true love for those that God has placed in his life. If members from the congregation can just disappear without the pastor searching for them (with everything they have), that pastor has no heart."}]},{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Jesus preaches a similar message in ministry:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Moreover when ye fast, be not, as the hypocrites, of a sad countenance: for they disfigure their faces, that they may appear unto men to fast. Verily I say unto you, They have their reward. But thou, when thou fastest, anoint thine head, and wash thy face; That thou appear not unto men to fast, but unto thy Father which is in secret: and thy Father, which seeth in secret, shall reward thee openly.","ref":"Matthew 6:16-18"},{"kind":"para","text":"In those days, I’m sure they wore old clothes, stopped bathing, and gave up something for their fast. Perhaps they took their fasting really seriously, fearing that God would ultimately destroy them if they didn’t stick to it. However, the fasts were for the wrong reasons. They were for the same reasons as everything else they did—they just wanted a spiritual pat on the back from their God for doing something He commanded. Today, the Catholic Church puts ash on their faces to symbolize their fasting. They literally go against what God and Jesus tell His believers to do. They just have to spend a little bit of time in their ritual, and God will allow them some pleasures of sin for a season. That’s not how this works. Fasting, honestly, should be something every child of God does forever. We should be in a constant mode of fasting, to the point where we want and try to push everything to the side to praise and spend time with the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"God will mention more about what He’s looking for in a moment, but I think it’s important that we evaluate our ritualistic doings in our faith. Perhaps your church does a season of fasting. It’s fine; there’s nothing I will say against it. If your church leader feels like this is a good time to fast, then perhaps that’s for a reason. However, if it’s the same routine every year, at the same time every year for the same purposes every year, it has not simply become a tradition… It has become a ritual. There is a difference between the two. Traditions can become problems if they lose their meaning. Rituals are problems simply by doing them in general. Some traditions can be good. All rituals are never good. The problem with the modern church is not that we have too many traditions (it’s a problem still to be sure). The problem with the modern church is that we have too many rituals. We do it because we’ve always done it, and nothing more. How silly of a “church leader” to repeat the same mundane mistake every single year simply because that is what they have always done."},{"kind":"para","text":"Rituals are for religions. Traditions are for immediate families. Relationships are for the church. To figure out which place you stand, you must know what you are doing in the faith and why you are doing it."}]},{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is actually a really good verse from the Lord here. He asks four simple questions about your ritual of fasting. He first asks, “Did I tell you to do these fasts?” Technically, God does require a fast in the books of Moses."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Also on the tenth day of this seventh month there shall be a day of atonement: it shall be an holy convocation unto you; and ye shall afflict your souls, and offer an offering made by fire unto the LORD. And ye shall do no work in that same day: for it is a day of atonement, to make an atonement for you before the LORD your God.","ref":"Leviticus 23:27-28"},{"kind":"para","text":"That is not what they are doing here, however. They are not fasting for the Day of Atonement. They are doing it to try and earn some spiritual currency from the Lord, like a child would do for their parents. “If I do plenty of good stuff now, my parents will go a little easier on me if I get into trouble later.” It doesn’t work that way with the Lord. God, actually, never really commissions His children to fast. He gives some examples about what it might look like, but never fully tells them to fast very often. There are so many interpretations of fasting today because there isn’t much information about how to do it in the Bible. Fasting, then, should be done from a heart longing for connection with God. Any other form of fasting is heretical."},{"kind":"para","text":"He then asks, “a day for a man to afflict his soul?” In other words, “Did I tell you to fast so you can just make yourself feel bad?” Nope. He never commanded that. Not once. If your soul is afflicted while fasting, it is not so that you can earn spiritual points with God. If it’s afflicted, it should be the Lord that is afflicting it. It should lead the believer to repent of something that is afflicting them. It’s to make them change course and follow the Lord correctly. He asks, “is it to bow down his head as a bulrush, and to spread sackcloth and ashes under him?” Again, this is to just show face. It has nothing to do with genuine conviction. A convictionless fast is really just willing starvation. There’s no benefit to it. Your own health doesn’t even benefit by a fast with no conviction from the Lord. It’s meaningless and cruel to yourself."},{"kind":"para","text":"The last question asks, “wilt thou call this a fast, and an acceptable day to the Lord?” Yes, the religious elites WILL call it a fast. Looking the part is far better (in the eyes of the religious) than actually following the Lord. You may be fooling all the people around you. Your religious leaders might be fooled. Your congregation might be fooled. The world (and social media followers) might be fooled. Your friends and family might be fooled. Even mainstream media might be fooled. But the Lord will not be fooled by such hypocritical worship. This is not the type of fasting He has called for. Here’s what God wants instead:"}]}]},{"start":6,"end":8,"title":"The Pride of Moab","entries":[{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Let’s compare the questions. Do you think God would want you to fast to look like you are grieving, or do you think the Lord would want you to fast because of the evil and unfair treatment of His creation? Do you think the Lord would want you to fast because your religion tells you to (or because it’s just common tradition at this point), or do you think the Lord would want you to fast because it will give you a tender heart for the hurting and helpless?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Consider the difference between fasting to earn points and fasting to give help. Are you fasting because you were told to, or because you are longing? Are you fasting because you have to, or because you need to? If you answered any of these questions because of the former, your fasting is ritualistic, my friend. You are not worshipping God; you are worshipping self. That’s not just my interpretation of scripture; that is God’s literal word to you."},{"kind":"para","text":"Everything in scripture that God says for us to do is meant for a longing purpose, not a judgment purpose. He wants us to turn to Him. That’s literally all He wants. It’s so sad that we neglect this calling from the Lord because we are too entrenched in our rituals to notice. That is what the Israelites were doing, and it is going to bring them judgment instead of avoiding judgment. God doesn’t stop there either…"}]},{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Here’s a good fast idea. Perhaps you are fasting from specific types of food. Maybe, like my niece, you are fasting from junk food. Instead of simply giving up on it, you can give what you would usually eat to those who are truly and genuinely starving. Give your bread to the poor. Use what you are fasting from to help those around you. You see how that becomes a more productive fast? Fasting should certainly be a means of bringing you closer to God, and if you are fasting correctly, it will also bring a means to more compassion for the people around you. If you feel miserable when you fast, you might not be fasting for the right reasons."}]},{"start":8,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Not only does giving to those in need make you personally feel better, but it also gives you life. The conscience that God has given you will actually ignite with joy when you fast like this. It brings you into a more personal connection with God. He is our reward when we fast for Him. Don’t fast out of necessity from your church or religion; fast out of your necessity for His presence."}]}]},{"start":9,"end":12,"title":"The Tears of God","entries":[{"start":9,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God has turned His back on the Israelites because they are performing their rituals against His commands. He has been warning them about doing things this way, and they have openly ignored, mocked, and forsaken His commands. Now the Lord has no choice but to give a final warning and let them go on their own downward spiral."},{"kind":"para","text":"However, God is still there. He is still waiting. He is still longing for His children to turn. He will not make them do it; He wants them to love Him enough to want to do it on their own. When they lose all of God’s goodness, they will see what they were missing and will take God’s relationship far more seriously. If these people had repented of their ways, God would have actually kept them from captivity. History would be so much different if the people of Judah had just listened."}]},{"start":11,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"When we see Jesus fast for forty days and nights, we might wonder if He ate anything. It says after He had fasted, He “hungered,” which implies that He hadn’t eaten anything for more than a month. That is an impossible feat for any mere human to take on, but I do believe it is possible for a mere human to do if the Lord is truly leading them in it."},{"kind":"para","text":"I believe it was in Jesus’ humanity that He took on the task of fasting. It was in His humanity that He defeated Satan and the temptations as well. He proved that God is able to take care of you if you are serious about searching for Him. That same hope and help is for you too, if you are willing to turn and follow Him in sincerity and conviction."}]},{"start":12,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"If Israel had turned, they would have paved quite the road into the future. They would have likely been a force to be reckoned with. I think Jesus would have come and strengthened the Israelites further. But we know that they won’t turn. We know they will keep on their path, and we know that eventually Christ will come, and He will have to die for the sins of the world. We know that the Israelites are all sinners just like us, and if we had it our way in those days as well, we would have fallen for the same dumb traps that they did. I know this to be true because we still fall into the same dumb traps that they did today. We are shallow and dull people, and sin has a very loud voice."}]}]},{"start":13,"end":14,"title":"The Fate of Moab","entries":[{"start":13,"end":14,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This all derives from one specific and small word: “If.” In other words, God is saying, “You are doing your own pleasure when you should be worshipping me. You are finding delight and honor in your own acts of worship, and you are going your own ways, living in your own pleasures, and making up your own words. Because of that, you are going to be in low places and starving.”"},{"kind":"para","text":"God would have provided the ability to “ride upon” the high places of the earth. They would have been at the top of the world. They would have been the pinnacle of worship and service. Only if they turn the way they are doing things to keeping God first and letting Him be their life’s purpose."},{"kind":"para","text":"Their life’s purpose was to live it to the fullest. Their life’s purpose was to experience everything as much as possible without worrying about any repercussions. Their life’s purpose was to sin. God has never wanted that. He has always wanted to enjoy life with us. We are just too stubborn and spoiled to let Him in."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":10},{"start":11,"end":11},{"start":12,"end":12},{"start":13,"end":14}],"verses":{"1":"Cry aloud, spare not, lift up thy voice like a trumpet, and shew my people their transgression, and the house of Jacob their sins.","2":"Yet they seek me daily, and delight to know my ways, as a nation that did righteousness, and forsook not the ordinance of their God: they ask of me the ordinances of justice; they take delight in approaching to God.","3":"Wherefore have we fasted, say they, and thou seest not? wherefore have we afflicted our soul, and thou takest no knowledge? Behold, in the day of your fast ye find pleasure, and exact all your labours.","4":"Behold, ye fast for strife and debate, and to smite with the fist of wickedness: ye shall not fast as ye do this day, to make your voice to be heard on high.","5":"Is it such a fast that I have chosen? a day for a man to afflict his soul? is it to bow down his head as a bulrush, and to spread sackcloth and ashes under him? wilt thou call this a fast, and an acceptable day to the Lord?","6":"Is not this the fast that I have chosen? to loose the bands of wickedness, to undo the heavy burdens, and to let the oppressed go free, and that ye break every yoke?","7":"Is it not to deal thy bread to the hungry, and that thou bring the poor that are cast out to thy house? when thou seest the naked, that thou cover him; and that thou hide not thyself from thine own flesh?","8":"Then shall thy light break forth as the morning, and thine health shall spring forth speedily: and thy righteousness shall go before thee; the glory of the Lord shall be thy reward.","9":"Then shalt thou call, and the Lord shall answer; thou shalt cry, and he shall say, Here I am. If thou take away from the midst of thee the yoke, the putting forth of the finger, and speaking vanity;","10":"And if thou draw out thy soul to the hungry, and satisfy the afflicted soul; then shall thy light rise in obscurity, and thy darkness be as the noon day:","11":"And the Lord shall guide thee continually, and satisfy thy soul in drought, and make fat thy bones: and thou shalt be like a watered garden, and like a spring of water, whose waters fail not.","12":"And they that shall be of thee shall build the old waste places: thou shalt raise up the foundations of many generations; and thou shalt be called, The repairer of the breach, The restorer of paths to dwell in.","13":"If thou turn away thy foot from the sabbath, from doing thy pleasure on my holy day; and call the sabbath a delight, the holy of the Lord, honourable; and shalt honour him, not doing thine own ways, nor finding thine own pleasure, nor speaking thine own words:","14":"Then shalt thou delight thyself in the Lord; and I will cause thee to ride upon the high places of the earth, and feed thee with the heritage of Jacob thy father: for the mouth of the Lord hath spoken it."}},
    "59": {"chapter":59,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: In our last chapter God speaks to the religionists about their ritualistic practices. We talked about the difference between what a tradition is, versus what a ritual is. Rituals are not God's directives, and religions have a hard time avoiding rituals. The Israelites couldn't seem to get away from them either, and it causes some pretty great grief against the nation and it's people. We talked about why we fast, and what the Lord is looking for in a person who fasts, ending it on the power of God and His gift of power to those that are genuine followers and are faithful to Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"In this chapter, God makes it absolutely clear that religious practices are not helpful to the people who follow them. He looks at what our own works gets us into, and why we must reject our rituals, so we can start new in our faith with the Lord. The moment we receive Christ, EVERYTHING is new (including our purposes and works)."}],"previously":["In our last chapter, God spoke to the religionists about their ritualistic practices. We discussed the difference between what a tradition is and what a ritual is. Rituals are not God’s directives, and religions often struggle to avoid them. The Israelites couldn’t seem to escape rituals either, which caused significant grief for the nation and its people. We explored why we fast and what the Lord seeks in a person who fasts, concluding with the power of God and His gift of power to those who are genuine followers and faithful to Him. In this chapter, God makes it absolutely clear that religious practices are not beneficial to those who follow them. He examines what our own works lead us into and why we must reject our rituals to start anew in our faith with the Lord. The moment we receive Christ, everything is new, including our purposes and works."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":8,"title":"Becoming A Boss","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Our biggest problem (or at least it’s one of my biggest problems) is that we think that God is either too big and grand to care about us, or He hates us too much to change anything. Neither one of those things is true. God’s hand is at the perfect length to save. He is more than capable of doing above and beyond what we even know is possible."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But Jesus beheld them, and said unto them, With men this is impossible; but with God all things are possible.","ref":"Matthew 19:26"},{"kind":"para","text":"We cannot set a limit on God. If we are prone to doing that, God will not reach us appropriately. He will still call us, but He will purposefully withhold His hand from reaching simply because we are limiting Him, and He wants our full trust in faith."},{"kind":"para","text":"Furthermore, we think that when God is too busy, He won’t listen or care about our wants and prayers. He is looking for perfection, and we certainly don’t hit that mark, so why even bother with coming to the Lord to begin with? The problem isn’t that we don’t meet God’s standards. That will always, of course, be a problem. The problem is that we don’t even try to please the Lord. We won’t meet His standards, but He has given us access to ways that we can."},{"kind":"para","text":"We might not be able to reach the Lord with our hands and ears, but He has no problem reaching us with His hands and ears. The only reason it might not seem as if God cares or is listening is because of this:"}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God has chosen not to hear because they have chosen not to obey. God is giving them the same treatment that they are giving Him. We have turned away, and we don’t think much about the penalties of that action. We have no problem facing away from the Lord. However, the moment that God turns away, we think, “The audacity! How could He turn His back on me?” We don’t see how ridiculous we are."},{"kind":"para","text":"Let’s place you in the role of the Lord for a quick second (I’m not a fan of doing this, but I think it’s sufficient to take this perspective for this case scenario). You see a lot of sin, evil, and wrong here on this Earth. You watch as your creation starts to turn against itself and abuse itself, completely ignoring your love, care, and direction for them. They start doing things that are unfathomable to the human mind and eye, and you are tasked with having to watch all of it. It doesn’t please you. It hurts you. If you have a child, the last thing you should want for them is to become prostitutes, or murderers, or thieves and liars. The last thing you’d want them to do is try to replace you with a different father. At least I hope you wouldn’t want that from your kids. It’s hard to say these days. It seems like most parents today don’t seem to care very much about their children or what it is that they are doing. They let them go off wherever they want whenever they want."},{"kind":"para","text":"Our neighbor’s son is about nine years old, and I see him on his hoverboard riding around the streets and neighborhoods. I’ve seen him playing in the front yard at night (almost to midnight). I also have seen him pulling weeds and shopping trees that are starting to sprout too close to their house. I’ve seen him taking the trash out, unloading groceries, and raking the leaves. All of this without a single adult present with him. He’s out there doing all of this by himself (I’m sure he was told to do most of this by his parents). I don’t know how life is in the house, but from the perspective outside, I assume they are not very concerned about what their son is doing as long as he’s out there doing his chores first."},{"kind":"para","text":"Now, the Lord does not work that way with His children. He might commission you to do something, and it might feel as if you are on your own, but He would never have you do something that He would not gladly go with you to. Whenever I ask my daughter to clean out the cat litter box, I don’t just send her out there and hope she does an okay job. I stand out there with her and help her with whatever she needs. I’m beside her while she does it. That is part of being a family. You do everything together. I think it’s weird that our world has tried to normalize a lonely and secluded lifestyle. Even in married couples, it seems that they are often living two separate lives. If we are a family, we should move forward together, or not at all. If we fail, we fail together. If we succeed, we succeed together. That is a picture of a strong family. That is the picture of God’s presence in the life of a believer."},{"kind":"para","text":"The people of Israel were not looking at the Lord as a unifying God. They were looking at Him as a judge (and He is), and they were looking at Him as an enemy. They just wanted to get Him out of the way so they could live in their sins. That is why God can’t unify with them, and it’s why they can’t be blessed. This is not like “Oh, I accidentally sinned. I said this, or did that, and now the Lord is going to be angry at me.” No. The types of things that the Israelites were doing were far more heinous and evil. Look at what the Lord has seen the majority of His children doing:"}]},{"start":3,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is some messed-up stuff. Their hands were tainted because of the bloodshed (probably literal) that they have shed. They have killed other people both in spirit and physically. They weren’t defending themselves; they were just murdering because that was the common theme of their day. They wanted to be like the rest of the nations and try to grow themselves by their own strength. God let them do that for a time, but it’s only making them more and more sinful and out of control. When God gives us over to our own devices, it’s the innocent people under you that are hurt the most. You will likely prosper by your own hands, but you will have to do it on the necks and shoulders of needy and hurt people. If you want to reach the top by your own strength, here’s how you do it in ten easy steps:"},{"kind":"para","text":"Step 1: Forsake your family. They are just in the way. Step 2: Avoid being home. Let your wife take care of the kids as much as possible. Step 3: Don't be distracted. Don't stay in a church community, and definitely don't find friends outside of your work. Step 4: Treat the poor and needy like they are trash. That is ultimately what they are. Step 5: Steal someone else's hard work, and pawn it off as if it were your own. Step 6: Sear your conscience. It only gets in the way when you have to do the tough things without thinking or caring. Step 7: Act like you are already on top. Every real leader knows they are a leader, and therefore they can act like they are in charge of everyone. Step 8: Spend a lot of money on yourself. You have to spend money to make money remember? Step 9: If someone else is acting like a leader (or trying to do a better job than you), make sure to make their lives miserable so they will want to either submit to your authority or completely walk away from the work. Step 10: Spread lies about the person that is actually in charge so that everyone around you will hate them, dethrone them, and place you at the top."},{"kind":"para","text":"This is exactly how to become a great boss. There’s a difference between a boss and a leader, by the way. If you want to be a boss, that’s how you do it. If you want to be a leader, do the opposite of these things. You might read this list and think, “This is such a sad and pathetic lifestyle to live.” Yet, that is exactly how the Israelites were living, and it’s how a good portion of our world still lives today!"},{"kind":"para","text":"If you have worked in any sort of secular workforce, you have either seen this happen or were the person causing it to happen. What’s even more frustrating is that this happens all the time in the church house as well. Everyone is fighting for a top position. God hates this. In fact, He hates it so much that He literally turns Himself away from His own people who act like this."},{"kind":"para","text":"I don’t feel too bad when a church starts to defile their hands, speak lies and perverseness, reject justice and truth, and speak vanity to try and cause mischief. I don’t feel too bad because I know that God will have the final say. I know that if it’s hurting me because of these things, it’s also hurting God because of these things. If God and I are hurt by the same problems, then that means we are on the same side, and as long as God is on my side, I don’t have to worry about the final outcome (because God will have the final say)."}]},{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Basically, people are just setting up traps to try and destroy and hurt others. They might act nice and enticing, but at the end of the day, they are just going to catch you and poison you. Honestly, I think a lot of relationships are like that today. I’ve met far too many people who have this idea that a friendship (a true one) is transactional. “I’ll help you if you are able to do something for me.” What a terrible friend to have. Friendships should be unconditional. I’m friends with you because I love you. If you have to receive something from someone to be their friend, you are not loving them."},{"kind":"para","text":"Someone said, “The opposite of love is not hate, it’s fear, and if you are afraid to speak to someone or are afraid of being hurt, then you don’t actually love that person.” The main issue with the people of Israel is that they were only looking out for themselves. That is the main issue in every culture. Sin makes us selfish. Grace makes us selfless. Fear holds us back. Love gives us boldness. Iniquity makes us calloused. Righteousness makes us care. Religion makes us inward-focused. Relationship makes us outward-focused."}]},{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Here’s a really important verse to consider. I know that a lot of churches and religions will teach you to work your way into God’s good graces, but God says here, “Your works are works of iniquity, and they will not be able to cover you.” No matter how much you try to work for the Lord’s salvation and presence, God will not receive you in them. It is only through trust in His Son that God will receive you. There is nothing else you can do. Cover yourself in “good” works all you want. At the end of the day, God still won’t accept them."}]},{"start":7,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is, honestly, the very definition and character of a religious man. They try and try and try. They do and do and do. They work and work and work. They pray and pray and pray. They cry and cry and cry. All for what? They might even mean to do the right things, and have the right methods and rituals. They might mean good by their actions and ways of worship. But without Christ as their starting point, it’s all in vain. Christ must be the start of your faith, not just the add-on."},{"kind":"para","text":"If you have been doing these rituals your entire life, it makes sense to think that these are the right things to do. But the moment you come to the knowledge that Christ died for you, and you place your faith in Him, you MUST stop these other rituals. How could you continue to live in these traditions knowing full well that Christ is enough? If you have turned to Christ, you will know full well that your old rituals, habits, and traditions don’t even come close to measuring up to His sacrifice. They become absolutely unnecessary at that point."}]}]},{"start":9,"end":11,"title":"Religious Lifestyles","entries":[{"start":9,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Here’s how you look to us non-religious folk. The religious person just looks like a man walking in darkness, like a man who cannot see. A religious man always stumbles and falls. They are always hungry and sad. They look for judgment and can’t find it because they are looking at their rituals as the final say rather than at God’s Word for it."},{"kind":"para","text":"They want salvation but can’t receive it because they are trying to get it by their own minds and power. You cannot save yourself by your own craftiness. You are not a strong enough person. You will always let yourself down. That is what God has been implying and directly saying to mankind since Genesis."}]}]},{"start":12,"end":15,"title":"Truth Is Gone","entries":[{"start":12,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is the crazy part. The more good we try to do through religious practices, the more sin is applied to our works. The more things we attempt to justify, the more condemned we become. The crazier part is that “we know them.” We know what our shortcomings are. We try to work on them in our own power, and we continuously fail. We cannot do it. The more we try to do it on our own, the deeper into a hole we get ourselves. We must rely and trust in the Lord to overcome. That is something that seems to take a lifetime to remember and understand."}]},{"start":13,"end":13,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I’m willing to bet that these people didn’t think their actions were going like this. If you were to ask a truly religious man if they felt like they were transgressing, lying against the Lord, departing away from God, speaking oppression and revolt, and planning and speaking lies from your heart towards everyone around them (including towards the Lord), they would probably tell you they are good devout men of God. I have no doubt that they think themselves pretty highly. And, I believe that is their ultimate demise. They think they are too good for God."},{"kind":"para","text":"They will say, “I am a good person, I do all the right things, and I keep God first. I go to church every Sunday, and I pray every day, open my Bible three times a day, and I give to the poor.” They are probably telling the truth. But that is not what God is looking for. He’s looking for a relationship, not a checklist. He would still bless you if you were a sinful person, and don’t do all the right things, or don’t always keep Him first. He would still bless you if you didn’t go to church every Sunday, or pray every day, or read your Bible at all. He would still bless you if you didn’t give to the poor, or do what the world’s definition of good is."},{"kind":"para","text":"Why would He bless someone that doesn’t seem to be doing anything? Because He is personally blessed that you want to know Him at all. That is all He wants. He just wants you to know Him. The rest doesn’t matter to Him. The keeping of the law was not there so you can become a perfect person. The law is simply there so you can know Him better. So you can rely on Him more. He is fully aware that the law is impossible for you to keep, and even if it were entirely possible to keep all four hundred laws, He is still only concerned about how close you are to Him."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But let him that glorieth glory in this, that he understandeth and knoweth me, that I am the LORD which exercise lovingkindness, judgment, and righteousness, in the earth: for in these things I delight, saith the LORD.","ref":"Jeremiah 9:24"},{"kind":"para","text":"I could argue, in fact, that keeping the law without a relationship with the Lord will only get us further away from Him. Why do we need God if we can just do it all on our own? That was the Jews’ biggest downfall, and it will be ours as well if we trust our religious works more than His finished sacrifice."}]},{"start":14,"end":15,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Truth has failed in our generation, not because the truth is wrong. If it is wrong, then it’s not the truth. Rather, truth has failed because it has been rejected. It has been shunned and repressed. Truth was an enemy to the people of Israel, and history teaches us that making truth our enemy only leads us into terrible consequences. Yet, here we are in our era, falling for the same traps that they did."},{"kind":"para","text":"Truth, today, is an enemy to the majority of our world. It’s an enemy to the church today. It’s an enemy to the religious, the self-righteous, and the sinner. If truth is our enemy, then so is Godly provision. If truth is our enemy, then so is righteousness and judgment. If we make truth our enemy, we must make lies and sin our friends."},{"kind":"para","text":"Truth only falls in the streets because we have put it there, not because it has no power. In the end, truth will always be there for anyone willing to pick it up. Until then, we become deaf religionists if we are not willing to accept the truth."}]}]},{"start":16,"end":19,"title":"A Set Standard","entries":[{"start":16,"end":16,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The reason Christ has to come is because there was no man willing to turn to the Lord and follow. There was no man able to save God’s people. Jesus had to give Himself because the world’s sin is far too great. God has made every possible effort for mankind to turn to Him, and we have made every possible effort to reject it."},{"kind":"para","text":"Christ is our intercessor, and if we still go to Hell after this life is done, that will only be by our own doing. We cannot place any sort of blame on the Lord when we have rejected His good gift of obvious salvation. Everyone knows about the sacrifice of Jesus, but not everyone believes it."}]},{"start":17,"end":17,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Paul references this later in Ephesians, where he talks about the “Armor of God” and describes every piece of it in detail. Isaiah is establishing God’s own personal duty to save His people. God, Himself, is putting on the breastplate of righteousness and the helmet of salvation. He is leading the fight for truth by preaching with vengeance and zeal. He is the perfect person (literally) for the job. He knows what standards need to be met, and He is the only person with the power and capability to do it. Why would we not trust Him for it when He sets the standards and meets them Himself?"}]},{"start":18,"end":18,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"To be an enemy of the Lord is one of the most sad realities in this life. We are all enemies of God until we have Jesus. The moment we accept Christ, we become children of God. If we have not done that, we will continually be an enemy of God, no matter how much “good” and law we might keep and do."}]},{"start":19,"end":19,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Every culture, every person, every mind worships something. Even atheists worship a god. It might not be the God of the Bible or a god from other religious groups, but they worship something. Most likely, they worship themselves, but it’s still worship. Perhaps they worship science. Either way, there is no tongue (even tribal) that has not thought about some sort of greater being. If they haven’t heard about Jesus, they have likely made up some sort of god to worship. There’s something within our DNA that must worship. That doesn’t exist in any other animal, which is why we can rightfully assess that we are not evolved. There’s an innate desire within our code that makes us worship a creator of some sort."},{"kind":"para","text":"Every person in the world believes in some sort of higher power (even the atheist). God (the highest power) is going to let His presence be made very well known. There is no one on this planet that can accept the idea that everything is an accident. That would be scientifically impossible to get this much order from so much chaos. He is obviously known by His creation, but it is up to every individual to trust Him and know His sacrifice. We must share the sacrifice of God because it’s the most important bit of information a person can ever have."},{"kind":"para","text":"We might question the creation account. We might question David’s story, or the story of Noah and the flood. We might question the choice of Moses and the people of Egypt. We might question the existence of Babylon, or even the reality of a man named Isaiah ever existing. But the one thing we must know for sure is if Christ was real, and if He was, did He rise again from the dead? That is something we should be dwelling on more than anything else. Everyone has their agendas, but Christ only wants you to answer one question:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"He saith unto them, But whom say ye that I am?","ref":"Matthew 16:15"},{"kind":"para","text":"If we can answer that question, all of our other doubts about scripture can be addressed and affirmed. It starts with Jesus, and He is the key to unlocking all of eternity’s questions. He’s the key for finding the truth. He’s the key to having full knowledge of this Spirit of the Lord. He’s the standard that is lifted up against the enemy of sin."}]}]},{"start":20,"end":21,"title":"A Spirit Promise","entries":[{"start":20,"end":20,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Anyone who turns from their sin can be redeemed. That is why He is called the “Redeemer.” He will purchase us, and He will not return us to where we were before. He will purchase us if we would allow Him, and He will work on us for the intent of His purchase. He will make us better, sharper, and far more useful than anything we could ever dream of being by our own strength and religious deeds."},{"kind":"para","text":"If you want your religious practices to mean something and have actual value, you must get rid of them all, take Christ, and serve Him. He will give you the right practices and traditions. It won’t be based on your religion; it will only be based on your Redemption."}]},{"start":21,"end":21,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The promise of His Spirit is given to the “Redeemer” and kept through the redeemer’s lineage. Now, if you haven’t noticed, Jesus never had any children. He also never had any sort of temptation with women while He ministered on Earth, contrary to some religious beliefs. He never struggled with lustful temptation and even openly says that “looking” at a woman with lust is a sin. He never had thoughts of sin, nor actions of sin. He was always and entirely perfect. So how does His seed have the promise of God’s Spirit? Well, Jesus’ seed are His purchased or “redeemed” people. They belong to Him. We are adopted into the family of God and into the lineage of Jesus:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Having predestinated us unto the adoption of children by Jesus Christ to himself, according to the good pleasure of his will,","ref":"Ephesians 1:5"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"To redeem them that were under the law, that we might receive the adoption of sons.","ref":"Galatians 4:5"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"That is, They which are the children of the flesh, these are not the children of God: but the children of the promise are counted for the seed.","ref":"Romans 9:8"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But as many as received him, to them gave he power to become the sons of God, even to them that believe on his name:","ref":"John 1:12"},{"kind":"para","text":"The promise is given to all of us who believe in Jesus, and are following the Lord in faith and trust. Not the religious. Not the good. Not the hopeful. The believer."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":11},{"start":12,"end":12},{"start":13,"end":13},{"start":14,"end":15},{"start":16,"end":16},{"start":17,"end":17},{"start":18,"end":18},{"start":19,"end":19},{"start":20,"end":20},{"start":21,"end":21}],"verses":{"1":"Behold, the Lord's hand is not shortened, that it cannot save; neither his ear heavy, that it cannot hear:","2":"But your iniquities have separated between you and your God, and your sins have hid his face from you, that he will not hear.","3":"For your hands are defiled with blood, and your fingers with iniquity; your lips have spoken lies, your tongue hath muttered perverseness.","4":"None calleth for justice, nor any pleadeth for truth: they trust in vanity, and speak lies; they conceive mischief, and bring forth iniquity.","5":"They hatch cockatrice' eggs, and weave the spider's web: he that eateth of their eggs dieth, and that which is crushed breaketh out into a viper.","6":"Their webs shall not become garments, neither shall they cover themselves with their works: their works are works of iniquity, and the act of violence is in their hands.","7":"Their feet run to evil, and they make haste to shed innocent blood: their thoughts are thoughts of iniquity; wasting and destruction are in their paths.","8":"The way of peace they know not; and there is no judgment in their goings: they have made them crooked paths: whosoever goeth therein shall not know peace.","9":"Therefore is judgment far from us, neither doth justice overtake us: we wait for light, but behold obscurity; for brightness, but we walk in darkness.","10":"We grope for the wall like the blind, and we grope as if we had no eyes: we stumble at noon day as in the night; we are in desolate places as dead men.","11":"We roar all like bears, and mourn sore like doves: we look for judgment, but there is none; for salvation, but it is far off from us.","12":"For our transgressions are multiplied before thee, and our sins testify against us: for our transgressions are with us; and as for our iniquities, we know them;","13":"In transgressing and lying against the Lord, and departing away from our God, speaking oppression and revolt, conceiving and uttering from the heart words of falsehood.","14":"And judgment is turned away backward, and justice standeth afar off: for truth is fallen in the street, and equity cannot enter.","15":"Yea, truth faileth; and he that departeth from evil maketh himself a prey: and the Lord saw it, and it displeased him that there was no judgment.","16":"And he saw that there was no man, and wondered that there was no intercessor: therefore his arm brought salvation unto him; and his righteousness, it sustained him.","17":"For he put on righteousness as a breastplate, and an helmet of salvation upon his head; and he put on the garments of vengeance for clothing, and was clad with zeal as a cloak.","18":"According to their deeds, accordingly he will repay, fury to his adversaries, recompence to his enemies; to the islands he will repay recompence.","19":"So shall they fear the name of the Lord from the west, and his glory from the rising of the sun. When the enemy shall come in like a flood, the Spirit of the Lord shall lift up a standard against him.","20":"And the Redeemer shall come to Zion, and unto them that turn from transgression in Jacob, saith the Lord.","21":"As for me, this is my covenant with them, saith the Lord; My spirit that is upon thee, and my words which I have put in thy mouth, shall not depart out of thy mouth, nor out of the mouth of thy seed, nor out of the mouth of thy seed's seed, saith the Lord, from henceforth and for ever."}},
    "60": {"chapter":60,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: In our last chapter, we looked at God's viewpoint in regards to what we think is strong and reliable. God calls those things weak compared to what He can personally give to His people. He gives a very detailed look at what most modern day (and current time) religions look like. Honestly, I say \"most\" but this is the look of all religions in general. They all struggle with the same exact issues, and God doesn't like it. He has turned His way from religious groups and false worship. He wants genuine believers."},{"kind":"para","text":"In this chapter, God continues to give hope and encouragement to His people. There is a light coming, and it's not simply the one you see in the sky. No, it will be the Lord who produces everlasting light and that is something we must look forward to. The rest of the world will walk in darkness, but the city of the Lord will have a permanent fix of light given to it's people."}],"previously":["In our last chapter, we explored God’s perspective on what we perceive as strong and reliable. God considers these things weak compared to what He can personally offer His people. He provides a detailed examination of what most modern-day religions, and indeed all religions in general, look like. They all face the same issues, and God disapproves of this. He has turned away from religious groups and false worship, seeking genuine believers instead. In this chapter, God continues to offer hope and encouragement to His people. There is a light coming, and it is not merely the one we see in the sky. No, it will be the Lord who produces everlasting light, and that is something we must eagerly anticipate. While the rest of the world will walk in darkness, the city of the Lord will have a permanent source of light provided to its people."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":3,"title":"A True Light","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"When I was growing up, my mom used to wake me up with a song: “School day, school day, it’s a golden rule day!” It’s a small song, but after a while, it became an annoying song. She would sing it as she opened the blinds. She would also sing, “Let the sunshine in! Say it with a grin.” My eyes and brain hated it. I was comfy in my dark, comfortable bedroom. That is the awake state of an evil man. Every bit of light burns the sinner. That is why God came to us as light to the world, not as a cover for our sins. I think that is important to note."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Then spake Jesus again unto them, saying, I am the light of the world: he that followeth me shall not walk in darkness, but shall have the light of life.","ref":"John 8:12"},{"kind":"para","text":"This world needs the light, but just like me in my comfy bed, when the light shines, we are not ready for it. It tends to irritate us rather than wake us up and get us ready. That is what the light is supposed to do. It’s supposed to inform us that we should be awake and moving. God’s light has been displayed in this world, and the world has tried to snuff it out because they like the darkness. However, you can’t snuff the light of God out of this world. His light will always be shining."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is a perfect illustration of the Earth. We are walking in darkness. Everything here is dark. Every day, I wake up to the news about how one group or organization has killed, blown up, destroyed, or otherwise hurt another group or organization. There’s always someone angry at someone, and it’s usually for something very small and nonessential. Our world is full of people who like to spread more darkness rather than illuminate the truth and grace of God."},{"kind":"para","text":"But God has some light here. He reflects off of a small remnant of people today. Supposedly, in a 2020 study, there are 2.38 billion people in the world who identify as Christian. I wouldn’t have guessed it. Perhaps they identify as Christian, but I don’t think they are genuine in their faith. They are genuine in their hate. They are genuine in their groups. They are genuine in their politics and in their rituals. They are not genuine in Christ. They are Christians by name only, not by deed. False Christians, if you will. But there are some who are genuine, even if they are hard to spot. God’s glory still shines in this world, but you have to be willing to look for it."}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"If we look at Israel today, we would not see them as people of “light.” If we looked at them in the time of Israel, we wouldn’t see them as people of life. During the ministry of Christ, we wouldn’t see them as people of light. Has there been a time in Israel’s history where they were representatives of light? Very few and far between. The only light that the Israelites brought was the light of Christ through the Apostles and the start of the churches. The Gentiles got to see that light, but I find far more light by Gentile believers than I do by Jews today."},{"kind":"para","text":"You’d be pretty hard-pressed to find a real Israelite who believed in Christ and His sacrifice. There’s something about a follower of Christ that just gives an obvious light to everyone they are around. That light just HAS to radiate. I don’t know what it is. Perhaps the Holy Spirit shining through them? Either way, the only way for the Israelites to have any light is if they have the light of life."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But if we walk in the light, as he is in the light, we have fellowship one with another, and the blood of Jesus Christ his Son cleanseth us from all sin.","ref":"1 John 1:7"}]}]},{"start":4,"end":9,"title":"Gathering People","entries":[{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is something that a lot of people don’t really think about, I don’t think. The Israelites were not just taken from their land. They didn’t just lose everything. They were separated from their own families. Husbands were separated from wives, sometimes remarried later. Children were taken from parents. Brothers were separated from sisters. They have been scattered."},{"kind":"para","text":"I think that is what disobedience gets you. Rebellion doesn’t unify people; it scatters them. That is a life lesson for everyone who feels the need to revolt. Is the cause you are revolting for worth scattering your family for? That is likely the end result of your rebellion."}]},{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Everyone will join with God’s people in the end. God is going to unite every walk of life with His people because He desires that His love, salvation, and direction be available to all of His creation. That is another good reminder by the way. We are all God’s creation! There are many very staunch Christians, Catholics, Jews, and religionists who believe that God is only concerned about their group. They think God will not love anyone outside of their group and that He doesn’t care about anyone but those selected in that group. That is not the case. God loves the whole world!"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For God so loved the world, that he gave his only begotten Son, that whosoever believeth in him should not perish, but have everlasting life.","ref":"John 3:16"},{"kind":"para","text":"He has opened His salvation for every person everywhere. Even the most evil among us has the opportunity to have salvation. That’s not just some sort of feel-good message; that is the purpose and reason for the gospel. Even here, God makes it clear that He wants to reach everyone, not just His own children. He wants the whole world to come and see His light, and He wants them all to dwell in it."}]},{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"\"Dromedaries\" means \"young camels.” These camels and carriers will be bringing gold, and incense to them. We see this happen when Christ comes into the picture:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And when they were come into the house, they saw the young child with Mary his mother, and fell down, and worshipped him: and when they had opened their treasures, they presented unto him gifts; gold, and frankincense, and myrrh.","ref":"Matthew 2:11"},{"kind":"para","text":"We are not sure how many Magi showed up to offer gifts that day. We assume it’s three, only because there were three specifically mentioned gifts. I’m sure there were a lot more than that. This particular verse leaves out the Myrrh gift, though. This must be a different time of gift-bearing."},{"kind":"para","text":"Obviously, when Christ comes into this world, the Jews and the Gentiles have nothing to do with each other. So this has to be a different time of gifting. Perhaps at His second coming. Either way, it all belongs to Him, and the Lord is worthy of every good gift we can offer to Him and His people."}]},{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Flocks and rams are generally witnessed as sacrificial animals. Perhaps there will be sacrifices made when Christ returns to display what He has already done. I don’t really know. Maybe it’s more of a symbol of gift-giving to the Lord. What we do know for sure is that everything that is depicted here is about and for Jesus Christ the Redeemer."}]},{"start":8,"end":9,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Who are they? They will be God’s people. They will see the Lord’s glory fulfilled and will flock to His temple to worship and see Him. That is a mode that every Christian believer should be in, by the way. We should not just be visiting the Lord when something bad is happening. When we see something good happen, we should run straight to the Lord to thank Him as well. He deserves our praise and thanks just as much as our prayers of sorrow."}]}]},{"start":10,"end":14,"title":"Rebuilding","entries":[{"start":10,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"“Kings shall minister unto thee” is a very important statement. That is the look of a true leader. We spoke about what it looks like to be a boss in our last chapter, but this is what it looks like to be a genuine leader."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But he that is greatest among you shall be your servant. And whosoever shall exalt himself shall be abased; and he that shall humble himself shall be exalted.","ref":"Matthew 23:11-12"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But Jesus called them to him, and saith unto them, Ye know that they which are accounted to rule over the Gentiles exercise lordship over them; and their great ones exercise authority upon them. But so shall it not be among you: but whosoever will be great among you, shall be your minister: And whosoever of you will be the chiefest, shall be servant of all. For even the Son of man came not to be ministered unto, but to minister, and to give his life a ransom for many.","ref":"Mark 10:42-45"},{"kind":"para","text":"This doesn’t just apply to the disciples, by the way. Can we look at any leaders in our lives as servants? Maybe your church pastor is a great servant to his congregants, but I have not met a single one who has ever been a true servant. All the pastors I’ve ever met want to be served rather than be the server. They misquote scripture to make their point:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Then the twelve called the multitude of the disciples unto them, and said, It is not reason that we should leave the word of God, and serve tables.","ref":"Acts 6:2"},{"kind":"para","text":"They will say that the service work is beneath them based on this verse. That is not what the disciples were saying here. If you read the whole chapter in context, they are saying that they are stretched too thin to also go and take care of the widows. They didn’t just say, “Someone should do something.” Rather, they said, “We need to meet the needs of these poor neglected widows.” They took it seriously and found very specific men for the job so that they could be assured it is taken care of with grace and tact. Leaders are not to play the “that’s good for you, but not for me” card. Grace is needed for every ministry, and presence is the key to a growing ministry. If your leader is not present for your ministry, he is not a leader. He is a boss. We already talked about how that looks in the eyes of the Lord. Kings will come to minister with the children of God. By the way, just because the rulers are ministering doesn’t give you the right to stop ministering too. Co-laborers is the key word for ministry. If there is not unity in service, then you are doing the service for nothing."},{"kind":"para","text":"Furthermore, God says He is turning around His wrath. His wrath will be poured out, but when that time is over, mercy will be the theme. The wrath of God has been being stored up for a long time now, so I can’t imagine how that will look once it’s poured out. We have writings of it, but we can never know for sure until we physically see it. All I know is that it won’t be pretty for those who don’t turn to Him while they have the chance."}]},{"start":11,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God’s presence and people will be widely available for all the believers. All those who have turned to the Lord will have access to His greatness and prosperity. Those who have rejected it… well, we can study that better in Revelation. Here’s a small hint to what will happen:"}]},{"start":12,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"A nation that doesn’t turn to the Lord will not be a nation any longer. They will be completely destroyed and forsaken. There will be nothing left for anyone to go back to. Perhaps even the greatest nations in the world will be wastelands in those days."},{"kind":"para","text":"America is still a great nation (whether the people of this nation want to agree with it or not). But even this nation will be completely destroyed if we are not willing to turn our hearts to God and go after Him. We must turn. We must search for Him with everything we have. We must be saved. If we are not, there is no other end than destruction."}]},{"start":13,"end":14,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"It seems to me that the people and nations that have turned to the Lord will be bringing the materials to build God’s temple, where Christ will sit and judge for a thousand years. We can study this better in Revelation and other prophecies. We must keep in consideration that this is Isaiah writing this account. His main focus is bringing the good news of the Savior to the people. The reason that God is bringing this up here is not so that they can say they will become something special. Rather, God brings it up here to give them hope after all the trouble they are going to face. It’s also to provide the Gentiles with hope. It’s to provide you and me with hope today."},{"kind":"para","text":"We are going to face immense troubles in this world over small things, and we might lose valuable people because of it. In the end, God will have the final judgment, and if we are preparing ourselves for that, we will have the ability to let those small things go and build towards His kingdom and His power. We should want Christ to have the final say."}]}]},{"start":15,"end":18,"title":"A Fixed Economy","entries":[{"start":15,"end":15,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Again, I believe this is a further indication that God is not done with Israel yet. He is going to use this land in those days, and that will be where He reigns from for the time being. Jerusalem specifically will be a place of worship for the Lord, and that is where the world will have to go in order to be in His kingdom. He will rule from there. That is why ships and all sorts of life will be traveling to them. Right now, it’s a difficult place to visit and stay, but when Christ is there, it will be a joy for many generations."}]},{"start":16,"end":16,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This seems like a weird thing for God to say. Sucking milk from Gentiles? Breasts of kings? Why would we want to do that? It’s more of a symbol, I would assume. I don’t think the Israelites are going to literally be doing this. The Gentiles and kings that took everything from them are going to be giving everything back, and these actions are just to symbolize that they will have extra added to it. The nations will offer more than what they stole from them, so they will be blessed above and beyond measure. He clarifies a bit better in this next verse:"}]},{"start":17,"end":17,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"If brass was stolen, then the people who took the brass would bring gold. If iron was taken, they would bring silver. Wood would be brass, and stones would be iron. Everything would be increased in value, and there would be plenty of material—sturdy material at that—for them to build and trade with. The economy must have been booming in those days."}]},{"start":18,"end":18,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is such a great verse. It sounds like Heaven to me. No more violence. No more destruction. Instead, when we are living in the land of the Lord, the very walls will be a sign of salvation, and the gates of this city will bring you peace. I think everything outside of the city will look like chaos and loss. But this one central place will be salvation and peace. Nothing can touch you if you are within the borders of God’s city. There’s no safer place for a person to be than in God’s salvation and peace."}]}]},{"start":19,"end":22,"title":"His Presence and Hope","entries":[{"start":19,"end":20,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"My daughter and I were just talking about this the other day. I forget how it was brought up, but I told her about how it could be dark for a lot longer during the tribulation period. She asked, “Why does that matter?” I explained, “Because people do their work during the day. Sunlight is actually needed to energize a person.” She replied, “I think we’d be okay just working at night and sleeping all day.” I don’t think anyone else in the world would agree with that. In fact, I’ve been to Alaska during the time when the sun is up the longest, and we were very confused as to why we were still tired, even though it was still the same day. We found out it had been two days since we slept, and we never saw the sun go down."},{"kind":"para","text":"Thankfully, when God’s city is built, we will not need to worry about the sun. We won’t have to worry about the work either. God will give us energy, strength, and power through His presence, salvation, and peace. God will be our source of energy. He will be our source of work. He will be the reason we do anything at all in this world. That should be the case today, but we are blinded by the necessities. We need to rest. We need to eat. We need to work. When we are in the millennial reign, we won’t NEED to do any of that. We will simply GET to rest, GET to eat, and GET to work. And it will all be for and by the Lord."}]},{"start":21,"end":21,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is what God wants. He desires unity for His creation under the direction of His glory and presence. He wants us to be His people, and that requires us to be without sin. With the world as it is now, that will not be possible. However, if we have Christ, He will give us the power and ability to live in His righteousness. It will be God’s glory that grants us perfect access to His land. That is what this life is about."},{"kind":"para","text":"The ultimate goal while we are here is to know God. We must know Him and work towards seeing Him face to face. Once we accept Christ, that becomes our will. God’s will is for us to get to know Him face to face. His will for us is to prepare us for that day."}]},{"start":22,"end":22,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Again, this is prosperity. The weakest men will be the strongest in the world during the reign of Christ. God’s nation will be the perfect image of prosperity. I don’t understand these prosperity preachers. They talk about how you can have the best now. There is nothing actually good to achieve in this current life. The real life to achieve is the one that is mentioned in this chapter. That isn’t possible in our current standing and world."},{"kind":"para","text":"Whatever prosperity looks like to us today is a cheap substitute for what God is wanting us to prepare for. He wants us to look forward to this moment, rather than having everything we need now. The reason for that is because He wants us to rely on Him and depend on Him until that day when He has all His children from all walks rule and reign together with Him. He’s preparing for that day too. We must be patient for His timing."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":9},{"start":10,"end":10},{"start":11,"end":11},{"start":12,"end":12},{"start":13,"end":14},{"start":15,"end":15},{"start":16,"end":16},{"start":17,"end":17},{"start":18,"end":18},{"start":19,"end":20},{"start":21,"end":21},{"start":22,"end":22}],"verses":{"1":"Arise, shine; for thy light is come, and the glory of the Lord is risen upon thee.","2":"For, behold, the darkness shall cover the earth, and gross darkness the people: but the Lord shall arise upon thee, and his glory shall be seen upon thee.","3":"And the Gentiles shall come to thy light, and kings to the brightness of thy rising.","4":"Lift up thine eyes round about, and see: all they gather themselves together, they come to thee: thy sons shall come from far, and thy daughters shall be nursed at thy side.","5":"Then thou shalt see, and flow together, and thine heart shall fear, and be enlarged; because the abundance of the sea shall be converted unto thee, the forces of the Gentiles shall come unto thee.","6":"The multitude of camels shall cover thee, the dromedaries of Midian and Ephah; all they from Sheba shall come: they shall bring gold and incense; and they shall shew forth the praises of the Lord.","7":"All the flocks of Kedar shall be gathered together unto thee, the rams of Nebaioth shall minister unto thee: they shall come up with acceptance on mine altar, and I will glorify the house of my glory.","8":"Who are these that fly as a cloud, and as the doves to their windows?","9":"Surely the isles shall wait for me, and the ships of Tarshish first, to bring thy sons from far, their silver and their gold with them, unto the name of the Lord thy God, and to the Holy One of Israel, because he hath glorified thee.","10":"And the sons of strangers shall build up thy walls, and their kings shall minister unto thee: for in my wrath I smote thee, but in my favour have I had mercy on thee.","11":"Therefore thy gates shall be open continually; they shall not be shut day nor night; that men may bring unto thee the forces of the Gentiles, and that their kings may be brought.","12":"For the nation and kingdom that will not serve thee shall perish; yea, those nations shall be utterly wasted.","13":"The glory of Lebanon shall come unto thee, the fir tree, the pine tree, and the box together, to beautify the place of my sanctuary; and I will make the place of my feet glorious.","14":"The sons also of them that afflicted thee shall come bending unto thee; and all they that despised thee shall bow themselves down at the soles of thy feet; and they shall call thee; The city of the Lord, The Zion of the Holy One of Israel.","15":"Whereas thou has been forsaken and hated, so that no man went through thee, I will make thee an eternal excellency, a joy of many generations.","16":"Thou shalt also suck the milk of the Gentiles, and shalt suck the breast of kings: and thou shalt know that I the Lord am thy Saviour and thy Redeemer, the mighty One of Jacob.","17":"For brass I will bring gold, and for iron I will bring silver, and for wood brass, and for stones iron: I will also make thy officers peace, and thine exactors righteousness.","18":"Violence shall no more be heard in thy land, wasting nor destruction within thy borders; but thou shalt call thy walls Salvation, and thy gates Praise.","19":"The sun shall be no more thy light by day; neither for brightness shall the moon give light unto thee: but the Lord shall be unto thee an everlasting light, and thy God thy glory.","20":"Thy sun shall no more go down; neither shall thy moon withdraw itself: for the Lord shall be thine everlasting light, and the days of thy mourning shall be ended.","21":"Thy people also shall be all righteous: they shall inherit the land for ever, the branch of my planting, the work of my hands, that I may be glorified.","22":"A little one shall become a thousand, and a small one a strong nation: I the Lord will hasten it in his time."}},
    "61": {"chapter":61,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: In our last chapter, God gave us a picture of how the future promise is going to look. Things will start to be restored when the Lord returns, and everything will be in it's place. God will provide us with light (from His presence), and He will gather His people from all over the world to help rebuild His Earthly kingdom and fix the economy (that at the moment of this writing seems to be sinking further and further into a pit)."},{"kind":"para","text":"In this chapter, God will emphasize the importance of His Redeemer, and the necessity to preach with the right Spirit. While this is very specifically pointed to Christ, it is something that we should all learn to understand if we want to be faithful and useful ministers and preachers in our churches today. It will be displayed through the person of Christ, but it should be something we take special note of as we live in a world not too different from Isaiah."}],"previously":["In our last chapter, God gave us a picture of how the future promise is going to look. Things will start to be restored when the Lord returns, and everything will be in its place. God will provide us with light (from His presence), and He will gather His people from all over the world to help rebuild His Earthly kingdom and fix the economy (that at the moment of this writing seems to be sinking further and further into a pit). In this chapter, God will emphasize the importance of His Redeemer and the necessity to preach with the right Spirit. While this is very specifically pointed to Christ, it is something that we should all learn to understand if we want to be faithful and useful ministers and preachers in our churches today. It will be displayed through the person of Christ, but it should be something we take special note of as we live in a world not too different from Isaiah’s."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":3,"title":"Preaching Rules","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Now, these first three verses go very well together (that is why they don’t end in periods), but I think it’s sufficient to break them up into smaller, more manageable sections. I think this particular verse is a much-needed reminder to every reader today. Isaiah is not talking about himself here (though he might have somewhat of a right to). He is preaching a prophecy, let’s not forget. We know this is prophecy because this is what Jesus reads during His ministry."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And he came to Nazareth, where he had been brought up: and, as his custom was, he went into the synagogue on the sabbath day, and stood up for to read. And there was delivered unto him the book of the prophet Esaias. And when he had opened the book, he found the place where it was written, The Spirit of the Lord is upon me, because he hath anointed me to preach the gospel to the poor; he hath sent me to heal the brokenhearted, to preach deliverance to the captives, and recovering of sight to the blind, to set at liberty them that are bruised, To preach the acceptable year of the Lord.","ref":"Luke 4:16-19"},{"kind":"para","text":"But if we could pause for a moment, this should be the heart’s call for every preacher in the world today. Preaching has lost its touch in our era, I’m afraid. I think there are very good preachers who are being drowned out by very shallow preachers. I don’t think there are many today who have a true calling to preach. I think those who preach are those who are looking for a paycheck or simply looking to be heard."},{"kind":"para","text":"If you are preaching to simply be heard, do that in the streets. If you are preaching out of a heart of affliction and compassion for those who are hurting, do that behind the pulpit. We have it very backwards today. I see a lot of very hurt people preaching in the streets, and very calloused people preaching behind the pulpit. This is what Jesus provides, though. You can tell a person has the Spirit of God if their preaching is in this order."},{"kind":"para","text":"1) GOOD TIDINGS"},{"kind":"para","text":"This is what “Gospel” means. Far too many people are preaching a message of tidings, but I don’t know if I’d consider it good. They preach themselves, and Christ is somewhere in the background of it. I’ve heard more preaching on soulwinning in my short time of being a Christian than I have on any other sermon or lesson in the church. The gospel is not just reaching the lost. The gospel is equipping the saints."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And he gave some, apostles; and some, prophets; and some, evangelists; and some, pastors and teachers; For the perfecting of the saints, for the work of the ministry, for the edifying of the body of Christ: Till we all come in the unity of the faith, and of the knowledge of the Son of God, unto a perfect man, unto the measure of the stature of the fulness of Christ: That we henceforth be no more children, tossed to and fro, and carried about with every wind of doctrine, by the sleight of men, and cunning craftiness, whereby they lie in wait to deceive; But speaking the truth in love, may grow up into him in all things, which is the head, even Christ: From whom the whole body fitly joined together and compacted by that which every joint supplieth, according to the effectual working in the measure of every part, maketh increase of the body unto the edifying of itself in love.","ref":"Ephesians 4:11-16"},{"kind":"para","text":"Good news is only good because we don’t deserve it. That is why he specifically says, “good tidings unto the meek;” “The meek” specifically. The proud won’t hear the message of good news because they already think they are good enough without it."},{"kind":"para","text":"2) BIND UP THE BROKENHEARTED"},{"kind":"para","text":"“Brokenhearted” actually comes from two Hebrew words meaning “The inner part (even the soul)” and “in pieces.” He is not going to hold the hurt captive (that’s not the image here). He is going to gather the people that are neglected and hurt by our world. The world shuns people. That is an absolute fact. You won’t go to many places (especially today) where you will feel very welcome, especially if you are a certain race or ethnicity. The world seems to really care about what color your skin is. But, furthermore, it seems that everyone has something they desire from other people. You can’t just simply be a friend anymore. You must have something to give to those that you want to be friends with. That is not how this world should work, but here we are."},{"kind":"para","text":"The more interesting part is that it has seeped into the church. If your church shuns you because you don’t measure up to their standards, then your church is (I’m sorry to say) worldly. They are not spiritual. According to this verse, only the Spirit of the Lord will gather the brokenhearted and strive to heal them with their God-given abilities. If you don’t see that happening in your church, the Spirit of the Lord is not there."},{"kind":"para","text":"3) PROCLAIM LIBERTY TO THE CAPTIVES"},{"kind":"para","text":"When we preach the good news of Jesus Christ, it should leave people with the knowledge that they have a way to escape their sins. That is what Jesus’ cross gives to those who hear the message. It gives them access to forgiveness and grace. That’s what makes it “good” news."},{"kind":"para","text":"4) OPENING PRISON TO THOSE THAT ARE BOUND"},{"kind":"para","text":"When we are born again, we don’t just completely dis-attach ourselves from our old ways of living. Our old nature creeps up on us and tries to get us to do things that we know (at this point) we should no longer do. We have been given liberty, yet we still struggle with sin."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For, brethren, ye have been called unto liberty; only use not liberty for an occasion to the flesh, but by love serve one another.","ref":"Galatians 5:13"},{"kind":"para","text":"Christ gives us access to His grace anytime we need it, and it never runs dry. When we are tempted with sin, those who have been given liberty are able to unshackle themselves from that sin. Will it be a piece of cake just walking away? Probably not. But we have the ability to say no to sin whenever we want now."},{"kind":"para","text":"Before Christ, we just followed sin. We felt the need to say yes to sin and shun God. When we have Christ, He gives us the ability to say no to our old ways out of a heartfelt love for the Lord. This is the real preacher’s message. It doesn’t end there though:"}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Interestingly enough, Jesus ends His reading right here in this verse. If you notice, He doesn’t read the part about “the day of vengeance.” His mission when He first came was not to preach about His vengeance. That will be His message at His second coming. Whenever we see the Lord preach in the New Testament, it isn’t a message of judgment and fear. It’s a message of salvation and hope. If we have the Spirit of the Lord, that is the message we should be preaching too."},{"kind":"para","text":"The only times that Christ preaches a message of judgment is to His disciples behind the scenes because they were asking about the end days. These were more like common talks with them because they were curious about what Christ is going to do. They didn’t understand that He was going to die and that He would be coming again at a later date yet. But as a preacher with God’s Spirit, we should be encouraging the saints with this message."},{"kind":"para","text":"The second coming of Christ (to the Christian) is not one to shun away from because we don’t understand it fully. Rather, that is something we should be preaching to the saints to get them ready."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For the Lord himself shall descend from heaven with a shout, with the voice of the archangel, and with the trump of God: and the dead in Christ shall rise first: Then we which are alive and remain shall be caught up together with them in the clouds, to meet the Lord in the air: and so shall we ever be with the Lord. Wherefore comfort one another with these words.","ref":"1 Thessalonians 4:16-18"},{"kind":"para","text":"The second coming of Christ should be a comforting conversation with the saints. If you are not comforted by the thought of His second coming, you might have missed the message of the gospel. I’d go back and hear that message first. After that, this message of God’s vengeance should give you comfort. He continues:"}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Here is the state of a sinner, and I don’t think we even know it until we come to know Christ. We have:"},{"kind":"para","text":"1) Ashes as our end. 2) Mourning as our life. 3) A spirit of heaviness as our walk."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is not a good list to have said about your way of living. Imagine that list on your tombstone. The truth is, though, that this is the exact image of this world without Christ as their compass. It’s sad and pathetic, but God wants to turn that around with His Spirit preaching. He wants to give you:"},{"kind":"para","text":"1) Beauty as your end. 2) Joy as your life. 3) Praise as your walk."},{"kind":"para","text":"I think anyone who reads this (saved or not) would desire a lifestyle like this. To find beauty in this world, even in the death of people you love, is a very strange thing to think about. But it’s possible. We will get to see the world the way God sees it."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Thou art all fair, my love; there is no spot in thee.","ref":"Song of Solomon 4:7"},{"kind":"para","text":"He see's beauty in you. Furthermore, His Spirit produces joy even in the middle of trouble:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"My brethren, count it all joy when ye fall into divers temptations;","ref":"James 1:2"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Now the God of hope fill you with all joy and peace in believing, that ye may abound in hope, through the power of the Holy Ghost.","ref":"Romans 15:13"},{"kind":"para","text":"And it's all culminated by a Spirit of praise:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"I will greatly praise the LORD with my mouth; yea, I will praise him among the multitude.","ref":"Psalm 109:30"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"By him therefore let us offer the sacrifice of praise to God continually, that is, the fruit of our lips giving thanks to his name.","ref":"Hebrews 13:15"},{"kind":"para","text":"I'd venture to say, with these three attributes of the Spirit, you will live a full and fulfilling life. That's what real Godly prosperity looks like. Not in the possessions you hold, but in who possesses you."}]}]},{"start":4,"end":6,"title":"Ministering Needs","entries":[{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Everything all over the world is in disarray. Furthermore, we don’t see this kind of beauty and fixing in modern Israel. That means this is for a future promise, likely during the time of Christ’s second coming. Things will turn around, and Christ will call all His people to Himself, where there will be plenty of labor to fix and repair this ancient city."},{"kind":"para","text":"Truly, the Lord could fix it Himself, but He wants to use His people for the job, and we should have no problem being used by the Lord. To serve God is man’s greatest gift."}]},{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Perhaps this is what the world thinks of as prosperity: having people who serve you. The reason we can’t have this in our lives today is because we abuse that kind of power. We like people serving us, but we would never do that in return. During the reign of Christ, we will all be serving each other with the end goal of glorifying the return of the Lord."}]},{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"We should know that the Levites were the only tribe of the original twelve called “priests.” It seems that God is going to flip that to everyone in the land, however. That was the intention the entire time. The other tribes should have wanted to be more like the Levites, but instead, the Levites wanted to be more like the other tribes. Now we just have religious cults popping up and making themselves out to be something special."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Levitical priests were to be “ministers,” and instead, they wanted to be ministered to. That is how our modern church looks as well. The preacher, the priests, or the church leadership wants to be served. In fact, they seem to demand it behind the pulpit. If you are not willing to serve them, then you are not worth any of their time. What a shame, seeing as one of the greatest gifts a man can be given is the ability to minister. I think this verse is specifically about that."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"I have shewed you all things, how that so labouring ye ought to support the weak, and to remember the words of the Lord Jesus, how he said, It is more blessed to give than to receive.","ref":"Acts 20:35"},{"kind":"para","text":"This isn't just talking about money. This is talking about ministry. I know that's really confusing for most of this world to understand, but God cares far more about what you do with your ministry than what you do with your money."}]}]},{"start":7,"end":9,"title":"Service to God","entries":[{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The children of God will have everlasting joy as they minister to each other. This is another thing lacking in church leaders today. They might be ministers, but they are not joyous ministers. This is why we can come to believe that the modern church is dead. But when the Lord returns, it will all be how it’s supposed to be."}]},{"start":8,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Instead of doing what they do simply because they have to, they will do it because they love the Lord and want to please Him. He will give them a Spirit above their own flesh, and their enticements won’t come from themselves anymore, but rather from the Spirit given by the Lord. Honestly, that is how it should look even now with the Christian community."},{"kind":"para","text":"Our flesh is always getting in the way, though, and we just look like sad and unwilling ministers. We want to be involved, but we don’t want to put in any real work. Worse yet, the church leaders want to get us involved, and instead of playing on your strengths, they put you in a ministry you know nothing about and then look down on you when you fail. Thankfully, that is not how the Lord will work His people in His Kingdom."}]},{"start":9,"end":9,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"It will be an obvious display to this world who belongs to God. Now, I want to view this in light of how many scholars view it today. Perhaps all of this is primarily focused on Israel. Maybe that is who we are going to be serving with, and who will be leaders in the coming kingdom of God (at His return). Perhaps we will help them build the old Jerusalem back up. I could not know for sure."},{"kind":"para","text":"Whatever the case may be, I am serving the Lord in the endeavor, and to know that He will be sitting on His throne while we are working in His kingdom is a joyous thought to me. Perhaps it’s not to you if you have to serve Israel in doing it, but I don’t really care, as long as the Lord is being glorified. That is the end goal, whether you want to believe this is strictly about Israel or not. The end goal is to glorify God. Period. Nothing more, nothing less. We have plenty of examples of how we are to serve in the New Testament alone. We are not serving Israel; we are serving the Lord."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And whatsoever ye do, do it heartily, as to the Lord, and not unto men; Knowing that of the Lord ye shall receive the reward of the inheritance: for ye serve the Lord Christ.","ref":"Colossians 3:23-24"},{"kind":"para","text":"Again, we know that the Lord prophecies in threes, so I’m sticking to that logic as we read through these future promises. I could argue both sides. I could argue that this is primarily about Israel. But I can just as easily argue that this is about the church as well. Either way, those who are saved will be serving the Lord, and that is what we should be looking forward to."}]}]},{"start":10,"end":11,"title":"A Meaningful Work","entries":[{"start":10,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is the real thought of God’s people, no matter what work they are doing for His kingdom. We are not wasted servants. We all play a role, and the Lord has bestowed value in our efforts and work for His love and grace. That is key to understand."},{"kind":"para","text":"You might see your gifts as small in this world. Your family and friends might think that the little you can do will amount to nothing. Your pastor, your church leader, your work leader, your state leader… even the President of the United States might think very little about your efforts for the Lord, but God doesn’t see any gift (no matter the size) as invaluable. He gives more value to your gifts if you are using them for His work and will. Purpose is not based on how good you are with your gifts. Purpose is based on what you use your gifts for."}]},{"start":11,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Right now, righteousness and praise are a distant memory for nearly every nation. I don’t see the Spirit moving like He used to. There were whole kingdoms built by the Spirit of the Lord. The nation of the United States was built and established by God’s Spirit."},{"kind":"para","text":"Now we see people shunning the Spirit of God and callously preaching it behind their pulpits. They don’t want God’s Spirit; they want center stage. They don’t want to display God; they want to display themselves. We all clap and “amen” the preacher, and it doesn’t make them humble; it just lifts them with pride. We should amen the Word of God and His Spirit; the preacher has very little to do with it."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For though I preach the gospel, I have nothing to glory of: for necessity is laid upon me; yea, woe is unto me, if I preach not the gospel!","ref":"1 Corinthians 9:16"},{"kind":"para","text":"There’s nothing for a preacher to glory in. Yet, we see preachers glorify themselves all the time when they are up on stage. They preach their heart and forget their Bibles. Perhaps their Bibles are there, and they are reading from them in front of the congregation, but they twist them to showcase their own thoughts and feelings. That is not the Spirit of God; that is the spirit of man. It’s a dead spirit. If you preach from a dead spirit, you will preach to a dead church."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":9},{"start":10,"end":10},{"start":11,"end":11}],"verses":{"1":"The Spirit of the Lord God is upon me; because the Lord hath anointed me to preach good tidings unto the meek; he hath sent me to bind up the brokenhearted, to proclaim liberty to the captives, and the opening of the prison to them that are bound;","2":"To proclaim the acceptable year of the Lord, and the day of vengeance of our God; to comfort all that mourn;","3":"To appoint unto them that mourn in Zion, to give unto them beauty for ashes, the oil of joy for mourning, the garment of praise for the spirit of heaviness; that they might be called trees of righteousness, the planting of the Lord, that he might be glorified.","4":"And they shall build the old wastes, they shall raise up the former desolations, and they shall repair the waste cities, the desolations of many generations.","5":"And strangers shall stand and feed your flocks, and the sons of the alien shall be your plowmen and your vinedressers.","6":"But ye shall be named the Priests of the Lord: men shall call you the Ministers of our God: ye shall eat the riches of the Gentiles, and in their glory shall ye boast yourselves.","7":"For your shame ye shall have double; and for confusion they shall rejoice in their portion: therefore in their land they shall possess the double: everlasting joy shall be unto them.","8":"For I the Lord love judgment, I hate robbery for burnt offering; and I will direct their work in truth, and I will make an everlasting covenant with them.","9":"And their seed shall be known among the Gentiles, and their offspring among the people: all that see them shall acknowledge them, that they are the seed which the Lord hath blessed.","10":"I will greatly rejoice in the Lord, my soul shall be joyful in my God; for he hath clothed me with the garments of salvation, he hath covered me with the robe of righteousness, as a bridegroom decketh himself with ornaments, and as a bride adorneth herself with her jewels.","11":"For as the earth bringeth forth her bud, and as the garden causeth the things that are sown in it to spring forth; so the Lord God will cause righteousness and praise to spring forth before all the nations."}},
    "62": {"chapter":62,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: Our last chapter was filled with very important and practical tips about what the future church would look like. Perhaps in Acts we saw glimmers of this kind of functionality in the church, but in our modern church today we have completely strayed away from preaching with passion, ministering with compassion, serving with Godly action, and working with attraction. In fact, there are hardly any church leaders today (if any at all) who do anything for the Lord with the motive of simply loving people. They want something from their work. Usually something tangible (like money)."},{"kind":"para","text":"In this chapter, we get a closer look at the work of the Spirit (and particularly the viewpoint of Christ's working ministry on Earth). We will talk about building spiritual muscles (the most neglected muscle in the human body), and why it's important that we take the example of Christ as we serve our community for His glory and peace."}],"previously":["Our last chapter was filled with very important and practical tips about what the future church would look like. Perhaps in Acts, we saw glimmers of this kind of functionality in the church, but in our modern church today, we have completely strayed away from preaching with passion, ministering with compassion, serving with Godly action, and working with attraction. In fact, there are hardly any church leaders today (if any at all) who do anything for the Lord with the motive of simply loving people. They want something from their work, usually something tangible (like money). In this chapter, we get a closer look at the work of the Spirit (and particularly the viewpoint of Christ’s working ministry on Earth). We will talk about building spiritual muscles (the most neglected muscle in the human body) and why it’s important that we take the example of Christ as we serve our community for His glory and peace."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":3,"title":"Our Hope and Rest","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God has a mission. Actually, it is better to say that God has always had a mission. His mission is to reach the world with His salvation. This has been His mission since the first sin in the garden, through the cross of Calvary, and it will continue to be His mission into the Millennium. He wants people to know Him, and this verse states that God will not rest until it happens. I know there was one day of rest at the beginning of scripture for the Lord, but I don’t think He has ever rested since. Yet, without resting, He is our rest."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Rest in the LORD, and wait patiently for him: fret not thyself because of him who prospereth in his way, because of the man who bringeth wicked devices to pass.","ref":"Psalm 37:7"},{"kind":"para","text":"That’s why I don’t understand the argument behind a “Day of Rest.” I have some family members who are very strict about keeping a specific day to worship the Lord and rest. Yet, the Lord tells us to have a relationship with Him to enter into perpetual rest. He is a God of action, but in Him, we are a people of rest. His mission is to burn a fire for the lost so they have a direction to go. Our mission is to rest in Him. Once we have stood next to His fire, we have rest. What a beautiful gift given to humanity by the Lord."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"We have a couple of things to remember here. Firstly, the Lord is bringing up the Gentiles again. He talks about how the whole world will see this salvation, and they will be tasked with a choice. You, reading this today, have either had, will have, or are currently considering the choice of the Lord. Come to Him for salvation, or reject Him for self-gain. That has been the theme for a few chapters now as we have read Isaiah."},{"kind":"para","text":"Furthermore, God talks about a new name being given to His people. Again, this is why I don’t think this relates to Israel alone. This is a promise given to the church in the New Testament."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"He that hath an ear, let him hear what the Spirit saith unto the churches; To him that overcometh will I give to eat of the hidden manna, and will give him a white stone, and in the stone a new name written, which no man knoweth saving he that receiveth it.","ref":"Revelation 2:17"},{"kind":"para","text":"Only Christ can give us a new name. He gives us a perfect name. I might still be Jonathan, but I am not just Jonathan anymore. I am now what my name really means: “the gift of God.” I’ve been gifted salvation, a family, and a ministry. I’ve been given life and abilities that are all useful to proclaim the gospel and to worship and glorify the Lord with."},{"kind":"para","text":"Everyone else without Christ has a name, but it’s nothing new. It’s nothing special. It’s just a name that’s been given to them. That’s not how the Lord wants to keep you, though. He wants to give you a new name."}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Once again, a symbol attributed to the church."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And every man that striveth for the mastery is temperate in all things. Now they do it to obtain a corruptible crown; but we an incorruptible.","ref":"1 Corinthians 9:25"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Behold, I come quickly: hold that fast which thou hast, that no man take thy crown.","ref":"Revelation 3:11"},{"kind":"para","text":"We should recognize, and we will learn more about it in Revelation, that these symbols of glory—the Heavenly rewards spoken about here and throughout the rest of scripture—are all representative of Christ. He is our crown of glory. God might consider His children His crown of glory, but it’s only because of the faith and salvation of Jesus Christ that we have any chance of holding that title. Christ makes us His child, and when we are His child, we are bestowed with certain gifts from the Lord. That is what the Lord wants for His creation. He wants us to be gifted by Him with spiritual things. Glory is a spiritual thing; it’s not a mental or physical attribute. Rest is also a spiritual thing. It can be a mental or physical attribute, but true, genuine rest comes from knowing the Lord. Peace is also spiritually charged. Salvation is a spiritual attribute. God wants to give you a spiritual life."},{"kind":"para","text":"Let’s be honest for a second here. We can rightfully say we have spent a good portion of our lives exercising our mental and physical beings. School is literally filled with those two motivations to graduate. Yet, it’s the spiritual life that is neglected. There is no spiritual exercise in schools today. We need these three strands in order to function properly in society, and for some reason, our government and officials in this country have thought it appropriate to neglect spiritual maturity to focus on mental and physical maturity. I’ve noticed, however, that physical and mental growth doesn’t seem to be making for a reputable person in society. I’ve known people who were way smarter than me, even graduating with a 4.0 average, who end up wasting the rest of their lives away in prison, by suicide, or through drugs. They were not obese people either. In fact, three particular men I can think of had really high grades in school. Their grades were so good that they would actually help tutor me for certain subjects, possibly even give me answers to homework. Mentally, they were about as fit as they come. They had said and done some weird things in school, but they were growing and learning. Two of them were even on the track team. They were runners and were in good physical shape as well. Once these three graduated, they went a completely different direction. One got into drugs, another committed suicide, and the other seems to have completely disappeared off the face of the earth (I know they were experiencing some legal troubles about a girl). The school seems to have done a decent enough job training their physical and mental muscles, but without the spiritual exercise, these people lost everything. That should make you realize how important spiritual exercise really is."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For bodily exercise profiteth little: but godliness is profitable unto all things, having promise of the life that now is, and of that which is to come.","ref":"1 Timothy 4:8"},{"kind":"para","text":"Sadly, these students are fed a web of lies and indoctrination. That is why they end up like this. That is why the schools don’t want to build spiritual muscles for these students. If the students are more spiritually stable, they will start to think on their own, and the school can’t indoctrinate them quite as easily. The end objective is to sell a narrative, and as long as they dumb down the spiritual, the narrative is easier to sell."},{"kind":"para","text":"But Christ doesn’t work based on the school systems. He doesn’t have to depend upon what this world is trying to teach (or hold back for that matter). He will build your spiritual muscles one way or another, and you will either reject it and forget it, or you will accept it and grow into an ultimately mature human being. We have a child-like faith, perhaps, but we are not children in understanding."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Brethren, be not children in understanding: howbeit in malice be ye children, but in understanding be men.","ref":"1 Corinthians 14:20"}]}]},{"start":4,"end":5,"title":"A United Relationship","entries":[{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"“Hephzibah” means “my delight is in her.” “Beulah” means “to marry,” “possess,” or “own.” The Lord references His people as His bride over and over again throughout scripture. Even Isaiah has made mention of it if you don’t remember:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For thy Maker is thine husband; the LORD of hosts is his name; and thy Redeemer the Holy One of Israel; The God of the whole earth shall he be called.","ref":"Isaiah 54:5"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"He that hath the bride is the bridegroom: but the friend of the bridegroom, which standeth and heareth him, rejoiceth greatly because of the bridegroom's voice: this my joy therefore is fulfilled.","ref":"John 3:29"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"That he might present it to himself a glorious church, not having spot, or wrinkle, or any such thing; but that it should be holy and without blemish.","ref":"Ephesians 5:27"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And there came unto me one of the seven angels which had the seven vials full of the seven last plagues, and talked with me, saying, Come hither, I will shew thee the bride, the Lamb's wife.","ref":"Revelation 21:9"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And the Spirit and the bride say, Come. And let him that heareth say, Come. And let him that is athirst come. And whosoever will, let him take the water of life freely.","ref":"Revelation 22:17"},{"kind":"para","text":"The point is, God’s people will not be called “forsaken.” They will be called “possessed.” We are owned by the resurrection of Christ, married by the faith of Christ, and possessed by the Spirit of Christ. We have value, purpose, and security through the finished process of Christ’s death and resurrection. That’s the greatest gift a man can ever receive."}]},{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This further drives the nail into the bridal coffin. We are God’s bride. And as a man rejoices over his marriage to the woman of his dreams, the Lord is going to rejoice over His unity bond with you. That is what a marriage is, by the way. I know there are a lot of people who get married today because of this thing, that thing, or some sort of money-specific workaround, but that is not the way in which the Word of God relates marriage. He calls marriage holy. He calls marriage sacred. He calls it unity, trust, and spiritual. He calls it blessings, example, and perfection. Marriage, to the Lord, is the perfect example gifted to man about His desire to unite with mankind. It was not invented by Adam; it was invented by God specifically to make His creation one, in the same sense that He would make Himself one with us. He wants our relationship to Him to be so close that we are nearly the same person."},{"kind":"para","text":"Some people might see the marriage I have to my wife and think, “That looks too personal. It looks like they can’t be separated.” And you are right. I’ve had people ask me about a specific thing they want to do with me, and I say, “Let me check with my wife and I’ll let you know.” They have started just going straight to her to ask at this point. That might seem too restrictive to some people, but it has been so much easier to make decisions with my wife than to just make decisions without her. Obviously, there are some decisions that I can make without her, but the majority of my life is spent with her by my side because she completes me. That is the way in which the Lord wants to have a relationship with us. He should complete us."}]}]},{"start":6,"end":9,"title":"No Wasted Effort","entries":[{"start":6,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Is there peace in the Middle East? Nope. There are still wars and things happening over there. There will not be any peace in Jerusalem until the Lord returns. There will be no peace anywhere on this Earth until the Lord has ruled and reigned. We can try and fight for peace until the day we die, but we will never see it without the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"Schools teach you to fight. They teach you what to try and do to help create peace. But those visions and flickers of peace are fleeting. They don’t last. Why? Because they are human efforts for peace. As long as we are trying to obtain peace through our own power and strength, we will never have it. It must be through the Lord’s leading and spiritual maturity that provides peace. Again, peace is a spiritual matter. It’s not a physical or mental ability. Physical and mental peace might exist, but it doesn’t last long. Spiritual peace is eternal, but it’s (sadly) not found in this life. It’s found in the next. World peace will only happen if this world is destroyed of its sins and wickedness and replaced with righteousness and truth."}]},{"start":8,"end":9,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Often, it feels as if my work benefits others more than it benefits me. I put in the labor, the effort, the time, and the energy, yet someone else gets all the rewards. The Lord is not going to keep that trend going. That is an earthly trend. He wants us to benefit from our own hands and labor. He wants us to see the fruit of our own work. In His kingdom, that’s what it will be. Everyone will benefit from it, including those who worked hard for it. We will rejoice over every work that is done."},{"kind":"para","text":"Even in writing this commentary, it sometimes seems like a dismal feat. It feels as if I am wasting my time. I know I am doing it for the Lord. Really, the only ones benefiting from this are those who want to know about scripture better. But it’s also building my own spiritual muscles too. When the day comes where we are serving the Lord in His physical kingdom, we will get to use these talents and personally benefit from them. They won’t be wasted efforts, lost on wasted people, who will just waste the given benefits that they haven’t earned. That kind of freedom and rest only comes through Christ, though, let’s not forget."}]}]},{"start":10,"end":12,"title":"A Completed People","entries":[{"start":10,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The invitation, and the necessity are read and felt in this verse. He's calling everyone to walk through the gate."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"I am the door: by me if any man enter in, he shall be saved, and shall go in and out, and find pasture. The thief cometh not, but for to steal, and to kill, and to destroy: I am come that they might have life, and that they might have it more abundantly. I am the good shepherd: the good shepherd giveth his life for the sheep.","ref":"John 10:9-11"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Enter ye in at the strait gate: for wide is the gate, and broad is the way, that leadeth to destruction, and many there be which go in thereat: Because strait is the gate, and narrow is the way, which leadeth unto life, and few there be that find it.","ref":"Matthew 7:13-14"},{"kind":"para","text":"Christ has lifted the standard of the Lord. The only way to Heaven is through perfection, and none of us can reach it. However, Christ has opened the gate! He could reach the standard, and He is going to hold it up for you. Seeing as you can’t get to Heaven through your own vain attempts, you should probably trust the one that is offering you a free ride to it."},{"kind":"para","text":"He has given you the perfect ability to have a home with Him. He has given you every reason possible to trust in Him. Isaiah has written this whole book with this specific thought in mind. Christ wants to save you. That is the whole reason God has not given up on us yet. He has every right to give up on us. We have done everything in our own power to go against Him, yet He is determined to reach this world with His salvation. We would do well to take that seriously."}]},{"start":11,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Christ had His work set before Him, that is for sure. When we read the four “gospel” accounts, we don’t immediately think of them as “good” news. We think of the gospel accounts as news, but I don’t know if I can argue them to be “good” to the human eye. In our world vision, the gospel accounts are very sad historical records. They are four of the same stories about a man who lived to serve, gave His time, energy, and efforts to help heal and encourage people, didn’t make any money, was rejected by all of His peers (including the people who claimed to love Him the most), had no place to rest His head, didn’t have time for family and personal activities, and then was hung on a cross to be tortured and tormented until He died."},{"kind":"para","text":"The only part of the gospel accounts that could be considered “good” is the fact that He rose again three days later and showed Himself alive to over five hundred people. To the Christian, though, the work set before Christ was all for us. It was for you personally. It was for me and my sins. His work was before Him, but His reward was with Him. His reward was the gift of salvation to you! He did the work so you don’t have to live and die in your sins. You can live and die in His forgiveness. He didn’t just say, “Hey, I forgive you of your sins.” No, He displayed that forgiveness by dying a painfully cruel death on the cross. He showed that He forgives you. He proved it to you."},{"kind":"para","text":"If there is ever a moment (as a Christian) where you don’t feel forgiven by the Lord, don’t forget that He has proven His forgiveness for you on the cross. We don’t have to only trust His Word alone; we can trust His completed promises and actions. God is a God of action, mind you. He is a physical God as well. He doesn’t just care about the spiritual; He certainly cares about the physical and mental just as much. All three of these can work together if we are wise enough to think for ourselves. We just have to break the mold that has been placed over us from our youth so we can exercise our spirits as well."}]},{"start":12,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Again, this is easily referenced to the church today. Perhaps the people of Israel will be known as “the holy people,” “the redeemed,” or “Sought out.” But right now, as Israel stands, they are not these things. They are far from these things. Whatever the case may be, I know that the Lord has not forsaken the city of my heart. He has personally redeemed me and considered me to be one of His holy people. He has given me salvation, peace, and every spiritual tool to help me exercise that muscle."},{"kind":"para","text":"I’ve been exercising my physical and mental muscles my whole life, so I’m getting a late start to exercising my spiritual muscles, but He still gives me the ability and tools to do it. He has still reached me even though I’ve been trained to shun it. The kind of powerful minds and forces that this world could make and be if we honed in on building the spiritual muscles as well."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":9},{"start":10,"end":10},{"start":11,"end":11},{"start":12,"end":12}],"verses":{"1":"For Zion's sake will I not hold my peace, and for Jerusalem's sake I will not rest, until the righteousness thereof go forth as brightness, and the salvation thereof as a lamp that burneth.","2":"And the Gentiles shall see thy righteousness, and all kings thy glory: and thou shalt be called by a new name, which the mouth of the Lord shall name.","3":"Thou shalt also be a crown of glory in the hand of the Lord, and a royal diadem in the hand of thy God.","4":"Thou shalt no more be termed Forsaken; neither shall thy land any more be termed Desolate: but thou shalt be called Hephzibah, and thy land Beulah: for the Lord delighteth in thee, and thy land shall be married.","5":"For as a young man marrieth a virgin, so shall thy sons marry thee: and as the bridegroom rejoiceth over the bride, so shall thy God rejoice over thee.","6":"I have set watchmen upon thy walls, O Jerusalem, which shall never hold their peace day nor night: ye that make mention of the Lord, keep not silence,","7":"And give him no rest, till he establish, and till he make Jerusalem a praise in the earth.","8":"The Lord hath sworn by his right hand, and by the arm of his strength, Surely I will no more give thy corn to be meat for thine enemies; and the sons of the stranger shall not drink thy wine, for the which thou hast laboured:","9":"But they that have gathered it shall eat it, and praise the Lord; and they that have brought it together shall drink it in the courts of my holiness.","10":"Go through, go through the gates; prepare ye the way of the people; cast up, cast up the highway; gather out the stones; lift up a standard for the people.","11":"Behold, the Lord hath proclaimed unto the end of the world, Say ye to the daughter of Zion, Behold, thy salvation cometh; behold, his reward is with him, and his work before him.","12":"And they shall call them, The holy people, The redeemed of the Lord: and thou shalt be called, Sought out, A city not forsaken."}},
    "63": {"chapter":63,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: In our last few chapters, God has been talking about His goodness for His people. He has made it a point to hone in on His hope, rest, unity, effort, and fulfillment towards His people. He wants His people to know how much they are loved."},{"kind":"para","text":"In this chapter, things change quite a bit from talking about God's love, to talking about God's wrath. He has two sides, but the same goal for both, and that is something we have to not only wrap our heads around and affirm, but that we should be careful with and respectful of. God's wrath is something God stores out of our sin. God's love is something God stores out of His mercy. The choice is our sin, or His mercy."}],"previously":["In our last few chapters, God has been talking about His goodness for His people. He has made it a point to focus on His hope, rest, unity, effort, and fulfillment towards His people. He wants His people to know how much they are loved. In this chapter, things change quite a bit from talking about God’s love to talking about God’s wrath. He has two sides, but the same goal for both, and that is something we have to not only wrap our heads around and affirm but also be careful with and respectful of. God’s wrath is something He stores out of our sin. God’s love is something He stores out of His mercy. The choice is our sin or His mercy."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":6,"title":"God's Wrath","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"And who is Edom? Esau is Edom, representing the worldly lineage. It is interesting that Edom is specifically pointed out here. God is speaking about His ability to save, but this chapter (at least here at the beginning) is not going to be about that. The people of Edom are equal to the people of the world. They love the world and the things in it. They are willing to give life and limb for things that are present before them. They are willing to reject eternity and the gifts that come after this life to hold onto their gifts in this present life. That is why judgment must come on this Earth."},{"kind":"para","text":"It is not because there are too many evil people that God has to do away with (even if it hurts the saved people). No. God will protect His chosen. He will redeem His own. Those that are not under His redemption are the ones that will face His judgment. That will (sadly) be the entire Earth at that point. We see our worldly quickly spinning in that direction, so it’s not much of a surprise if the Earth is filled with nothing but evil that God must destroy."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"That is interesting, isn’t it? Perhaps I should have made this association sooner with Edom. “Edom” means “Red.” I believe that is to define (or reference) the color of their skin, at least it was for Esau. Either way, the Lord is changing the meaning of that color to symbolize His wrath. Edom will be the color of their clothes and the color of their future."}]},{"start":3,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"A lot of scholars don’t like to talk about these particular sections of scripture. I suppose I get it, but this is something that God points out because it’s something that HAS to happen. I don’t think the Lord enjoys this kind of punishment. I don’t believe that God WANTS to bring wrath on humankind. However, we have left Him with no choice, especially when we turn from Him daily."},{"kind":"para","text":"Just going on social media alone will help anyone see the depravity of man. Everyone seems to have a stick up their rear about every sort of issue in the world, and the only ones they can release their frustration on are those strangers online. Social media used to be a place you would go to update your family. Now it’s a market square and public speaking square where complete strangers can yell at each other over small problems."},{"kind":"para","text":"If that’s not enough, when you don’t agree with someone, they can post all your information online so that people can come (as they say) “dox” you and vandalize your house, your car, and harass your children and family. They even put your parents’ information in there to give them trouble too. On top of that, you can’t go to the grocery store without it being locked down in some way now."},{"kind":"para","text":"Things are progressively getting worse as the days go by because man is not getting better. We are becoming more evil. That’s just obviously a proven fact. Don’t tell me you see the world getting better; you know that this simply isn’t true. I wish it were. But it’s not. In fact, look at this next verse:"}]},{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God has an arm of salvation and an arm of fury. With His right hand, He provides salvation, while with His left hand, He brings down judgment. His right hand offers peace and promise, whereas His left hand allows destruction and turmoil. With His right hand, He tests His children and strengthens His people, while His left hand pours out His wrath. In His right hand lies mercy, and in His left hand, there is desolation. God is able to do both at once, something we cannot fathom because we cannot do it ourselves."},{"kind":"para","text":"We cannot be angry with someone and be loving to them at the same time. We seem to choose one or the other; we are either angry with them or we love them. We are either fearful or full of love, and these emotions do not mix together. However, God can do both. He can protect His own and be angry. Consider it like someone trying to break into your house. Honestly, I don’t care what people might steal from my house; I don’t have much anyway. However, I do care about my family, and I will protect them at all costs. I can certainly be angry with the trespasser and loving towards my family at the same time. However, I cannot be angry with the trespasser and love him too; I can only choose one or the other. God can be angry with the trespasser and still have an open hand of salvation towards them. That is power."}]},{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Again, there is a reason for this. I know many pastors and preachers who don’t want to talk about this. I also know some who talk about this too much. It seems you can only land on one side of the spectrum when it comes to the topic of God’s wrath. It’s either too much for you to handle, so you avoid it, or everyone who is not saved deserves God’s punishment for their cruel, evil lifestyles. God stands in the middle with this. I, perhaps, will get in trouble for saying this, but God is not going to choose sides in regards to His wrath. Wrath is given to sinful creation. We are all sinners, but we aren’t all evil. Some of us (who have turned to the Lord) are actually living the lives the best we know how. The Lord is simply pleased with our turning to Him. Those who have rejected Him will experience His wrath, not because they are indecisive. Those who face His wrath will face the full brunt of it because of the evil they lived in this life without the Lord. They don’t just turn away from God; their whole life’s purpose is to try and hurt and destroy God and His people. That is evil."},{"kind":"para","text":"I think that is the ultimate choice in life after high school. You have two choices: one is to follow the world in the same passions and pursuits that the school has taught you (body and mind exercise, remember?). Or, the better choice is to build your spiritual muscles and follow the Lord in a path of righteousness and change. To remain the same after being indoctrinated your entire life is not a wise decision. I know plenty of people who have stayed the same, and they are living very mundane, sad, and empty lives. They have nothing to show for it. With Christ, however, you have much more to live for and even more to gain in eternity. God doesn’t want to destroy His creation, but He is going to have to because of His creation’s willingness to reject, hurt, abuse, and even kill Him and His people. God has come back from the dead, however, and He will bring those who follow Him with Him."}]}]},{"start":7,"end":10,"title":"A Better Hope","entries":[{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is a sudden and dramatic change from the first part of this chapter. However, it is something we must understand about the coming wrath of God. In order to live in the new world and to put Him in ultimate authority, where sin will no longer run rampant, there must be a pouring out of wrath first. Once that has happened, world peace will actually exist. There is no peace today because there is too much evil. There is too much evil because there are too many people who reject the Lord and His ways. So God will bring peace, and the only way to do that is to get rid of evil. Those who do not want Him will simply not have Him. That was the choice they made, and the actions of that decision will be theirs to live with in eternity. Those who turn to Him know how good He is, and that is what we should honestly be dwelling on."},{"kind":"para","text":"I mentioned that there are some preachers I know who dwell on the wrath of God. That is true. That is not something they should be dwelling on. It is a fact, obviously, that God will be pouring out His wrath. That is something that should be warned about in ways. But that should not be the message we harp on. The message we should be focusing on is the message of God’s lovingkindness;"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Herein is love, not that we loved God, but that he loved us, and sent his Son to be the propitiation for our sins.","ref":"1 John 4:10"},{"kind":"para","text":"God's praise;"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Bless the LORD, O my soul, and forget not all his benefits:","ref":"Psalm 103:2"},{"kind":"para","text":"God's providence;"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But my God shall supply all your need according to his riches in glory by Christ Jesus.","ref":"Philippians 4:19"},{"kind":"para","text":"God's goodness;"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Surely goodness and mercy shall follow me all the days of my life: and I will dwell in the house of the LORD for ever.","ref":"Psalm 23:6"},{"kind":"para","text":"God's mercy;"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But God, who is rich in mercy, for his great love wherewith he loved us, Even when we were dead in sins, hath quickened us together with Christ, (by grace ye are saved;)","ref":"Ephesians 2:4-5"},{"kind":"para","text":"and God's forgiveness;"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"If we confess our sins, he is faithful and just to forgive us our sins, and to cleanse us from all unrighteousness.","ref":"1 John 1:9"},{"kind":"para","text":"That should be the theme of the Christian preacher. Times of preaching wrath should exist, but they shouldn't exist more than times of preaching God's salvation."}]},{"start":8,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This will be during the time of Christ’s reign. They will be the ones that will remain here on Earth and will likely be saved before Christ’s second coming. Again, that open hand of salvation is always present with the Lord, at least until He returns physically. It’s not by faith anymore if we see Him. That’s a conversation for Revelation."},{"kind":"para","text":"The part that I find interesting is the “children that will not lie” part. The whole world lies. The church has the most liars in it, if I can be honest. People lie about their salvation, their reason for serving, and their promises to meet, attend, or help those that are in the church all the time. I think the promises of a Christian are held to a higher standard than the rest of the world. Yet, it’s those people who break promises the most. That must be very disappointing to God according to this verse…"}]},{"start":9,"end":9,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There is only one Savior, and whenever scripture speaks about “The Angel of The Lord,” we can rightfully dedicate it to Christ (preincarnate, of course). Jesus is the saving angel. The Catholic Church has an angel for everything, but Christ fills all the roles of every angel they can muster up. We don’t need a legion of angels; we just need ONE Christ. That has been the picture since the beginning of scripture."},{"kind":"para","text":"You can either depend on God’s servants to help you or depend on God Himself. I think it only makes sense to depend upon the Lord for strength and salvation, seeing as He CREATED everything (including the angels), but I digress."}]},{"start":10,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"To fight against the Lord is one thing, but to have God fighting against you is a completely different problem. It’s a problem with no resolve except through mercy. To have God as your enemy is the worst decision we can make. You might say, “I’m good without God, and I don’t need Him. I will hurt and destroy anyone that calls on His name.” But God says, “How little you are… Your life and death are in my hands.”"},{"kind":"para","text":"It’s funny that the strongest and most prideful among us still have the same fate as the poorest and weakest in this world. You might not like God, but He’s the only one you’ve got, so I think it would be wise to get to know Him. Honestly, anyone that is willing to know Him has found that He is actually the perfect God for creation. Imagine if we had a God that was hellbent on chaos and disorder. A God that created humanity out of evil, and wanted to watch His creation kill itself. A God that didn’t care about us, but only wanted to play with us like the Bruce Almighty joke as if He were a “kid with a magnifying glass, and I’m the ant.”"},{"kind":"para","text":"Instead, He has given us access to goodness, to righteousness, to love and purpose, and WE have decided to make ourselves into gods deciding what we want to be good and evil. Furthermore, we simply choose evil all the time. I think we like to watch ants burn. God is not that way though."}]}]},{"start":11,"end":14,"title":"A Reason For Hope","entries":[{"start":11,"end":14,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God has made promises to His people for the future hope and goal of salvation, as well as the world impact of the church bringing that message to every walk of life. I find it odd that there are religions that are exclusive or that want to limit the salvation power of God. You have to become like them and hold their rituals and traditions in order to have God’s love and sacrifice. Yet, that has not been the purpose and plan of God in scripture. If they know their Bibles at all, they would know that God has been working hard since the beginning of time, with patience and endurance, to get the entire world to see His salvation. He has carefully and meticulously chosen very specific moments in history as turning points to lead to the Savior. He is still doing that today. That is why people are still being saved today, and it’s only because God is keeping His promises."},{"kind":"para","text":"He made promises to these people, like Moses depicted here, and proved His salvation and outreach through these moments in history because He wants to lead them all to a direct and purposeful Savior. If God chose to stay silent and avoided His people, they would have experienced their end rather quickly. They would have been ended right in the book of Genesis, likely with Cain and Abel. That would have been a quick story. Actually, it wouldn’t have been a story at all. Humanity would have never existed, and we wouldn’t be talking about this right now. But God had a plan, He had a purpose, and He has a reason to do these things in this way at these specific times. He wants His creation to enjoy His work. We miss that by living our lives sadly. That is His goal, however, and we should take that into consideration every morning we wake up. It’s a new day, and it’s a new chance to experience God’s gift of creation."},{"kind":"para","text":"Instead of enjoying God’s creation, we argue about the one who created it. Instead of enjoying God’s salvation, we argue about who gets to be the leader of His work. Instead of enjoying God’s goodness, we argue over the evil in this world. Instead of enjoying God’s love, we argue over who deserves it. Instead of enjoying God’s presence, we argue over politics and money. Do you see how small-minded we are? God has given us the opportunity to enjoy Him and enjoy His gift of creation, and we spend all of our time focused on arguing about it. That, I believe, is the very reason that God must do away with this old world."}]}]},{"start":15,"end":19,"title":"God Is Personal","entries":[{"start":15,"end":15,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I’m assuming this is a pleading of Israel. They are wondering where God is. After spending so much time away from the Lord, they are starting to feel what it’s like to not have God’s presence and mercy. Everything around them is falling apart, and it feels as if they have been forgotten."},{"kind":"para","text":"God has not forgotten them. They have forgotten Him, but He could never forget His creation. He doesn’t want to forget what He created. He wants to redeem and grow His creation. Honestly, this is probably why it feels this way."}]},{"start":16,"end":16,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Israel references God as “our” Father almost every time we read about it in the Old Testament. God is not personable to them; He is (collectively) their Father. With the church age, that name changes. It’s no longer “our Father”; it is now “My Father.” He is the Father of the individual believer. Israel doesn’t seem to ever associate that. Perhaps that was what led them to their downfall. They didn’t see God as a personal Father; they saw Him as a collective creator. They might have used the title “Father,” but they didn’t see Him as a direct Father to them. They were just simply part of the family. That is about as far as that relationship went. I believe that is what is depicted in Genesis with the twelve sons of Jacob. There was only one son that Jacob really poured into, and the other children felt neglected. They were his sons, but they were not the center of attention. Only Joseph was. In this same way, the Israelites relate to God as their Father, but nothing personal."},{"kind":"para","text":"Today, I am the center of God’s attention. You are the center of God’s attention. My wife is the center of God’s attention. Every person that turns to Him is in the center of God’s attention all at the same time. God’s attention span is not limited to time, effort, or pleading. His attention span is ever-reaching and always centered on you. Even right here in this verse, Israel is calling out to God as “OUR” God. God is in the business of saving one person at a time, yet with access to everyone at the same time. It’s not like a DMV waiting room, where you must wait for your number to be called. You can get salvation right away, but it’s only to you individually. It won’t be your whole household (unless they take Christ personally for themselves as well)."}]},{"start":17,"end":17,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"More clarification is needed to emphasize that this is Israel speaking to the Lord. They are the “tribes” of His inheritance and the foundation of the universe’s story. They are pleading to return to the Lord, which is precisely what God has desired. He wants His creation to turn back to Him and love Him. Despite His unwavering love, they have done everything in their power to reject it. Now, having been away from God’s love and guidance, they realize how miserable this world is without it. They have no other direction to turn than to the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"This realization is often where God reaches most people. Sometimes it comes through immense trials, burdens, or health problems. Other times, it occurs on their deathbeds. Regardless of the circumstances, most people turn towards the Lord when they truly have no other place to go. However, some still reject Him, which also happens quite frequently, and they die in their sins and stubbornness. Israel, however, needs God’s help. Those who know the power of God still need His assistance today as well."},{"kind":"para","text":"This is the same prayer we should be praying towards the Lord. It should be the first prayer we offer to God, instead of the Lord’s Prayer. We should pray for salvation before we pray for prosperity."}]},{"start":18,"end":18,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God, honestly, has allowed His people to face trials. Again, that’s to get them to turn in only one direction. They can’t turn back because they face defeat. So they must turn towards their Strength, which is Jesus Christ and His sacrifice for them. That is the only direction for any of us to turn. It doesn’t matter how strong you think yourself to be; you will always lose to God’s power."}]},{"start":19,"end":19,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is a really good verse. Again, obviously, this can be used for the Israelites, but it can be just as easily used for us. We belong to the Lord. I, personally, belong to the Lord. He rules over me. He has called me. He doesn’t call the lost to serve Him. He calls the saved. He calls His own."},{"kind":"para","text":"It might seem as if the lost in this world have a better or easier time in life, but they won’t have a better or easier time for eternity. God is personable, and that is key to salvation. Instead of asking for God to save us (plural), you have the right to ask God to save you (singular). He will answer the individual calls of people, and He will gather those people together for worship (the church). That won’t happen if we are too busy distancing ourselves from God’s personable relationship with us."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":9},{"start":10,"end":10},{"start":11,"end":14},{"start":15,"end":15},{"start":16,"end":16},{"start":17,"end":17},{"start":18,"end":18},{"start":19,"end":19}],"verses":{"1":"Who is this that cometh from Edom, with dyed garments from Bozrah? this that is glorious in his apparel, travelling in the greatness of his strength? I that speak in righteousness, mighty to save.","2":"Wherefore art thou red in thine apparel, and thy garments like him that treadeth in the winefat?","3":"I have trodden the winepress alone; and of the people there was none with me: for I will tread them in mine anger, and trample them in my fury; and their blood shall be sprinkled upon my garments, and I will stain all my raiment.","4":"For the day of vengeance is in mine heart, and the year of my redeemed is come.","5":"And I looked, and there was none to help; and I wondered that there was none to uphold: therefore mine own arm brought salvation unto me; and my fury, it upheld me.","6":"And I will tread down the people in mine anger, and make them drunk in my fury, and I will bring down their strength to the earth.","7":"I will mention the lovingkindnesses of the Lord, and the praises of the Lord, according to all that the Lord hath bestowed on us, and the great goodness toward the house of Israel, which he hath bestowed on them according to his mercies, and according to the multitude of his lovingkindnesses.","8":"For he said, Surely they are my people, children that will not lie: so he was their Saviour.","9":"In all their affliction he was afflicted, and the angel of his presence saved them: in his love and in his pity he redeemed them; and he bare them, and carried them all the days of old.","10":"But they rebelled, and vexed his holy Spirit: therefore he was turned to be their enemy, and he fought against them.","11":"Then he remembered the days of old, Moses, and his people, saying, Where is he that brought them up out of the sea with the shepherd of his flock? where is he that put his holy Spirit within him?","12":"That led them by the right hand of Moses with his glorious arm, dividing the water before them, to make himself an everlasting name?","13":"That led them through the deep, as an horse in the wilderness, that they should not stumble?","14":"As a beast goeth down into the valley, the Spirit of the Lord caused him to rest: so didst thou lead thy people, to make thyself a glorious name.","15":"Look down from heaven, and behold from the habitation of thy holiness and of thy glory: where is thy zeal and thy strength, the sounding of thy bowels and of thy mercies toward me? are they restrained?","16":"Doubtless thou art our father, though Abraham be ignorant of us, and Israel acknowledge us not: thou, O Lord, art our father, our redeemer; thy name is from everlasting.","17":"O Lord, why hast thou made us to err from thy ways, and hardened our heart from thy fear? Return for thy servants' sake, the tribes of thine inheritance.","18":"The people of thy holiness have possessed it but a little while: our adversaries have trodden down thy sanctuary.","19":"We are thine: thou never barest rule over them; they were not called by thy name."}},
    "64": {"chapter":64,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: In our last chapter the topic of this book became really heavy again as we talked about God's wrath, trusting in a better hope, giving us a reason to trust in God, and knowing that God is more personal to you than just an overlooking collective. You don't need to be a part of a religious group in order to have God personally. You just have to trust in His promises of scripture to know Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"In this chapter, we go back to God's presence and wrath, but we address it from a different angle. God's wrath will be poured out for a reason, and though we have talked about this topic before, we would do well to remember why He must do it, when He plans to do it, and where we stand before that time comes. This chapter should give us a zeal and compassion for God's people, and for those that have lived their lives openly rejecting the sacrifice and salvation of the Lord for them."}],"previously":["In our last chapter, the topic of this book became really heavy again as we talked about God’s wrath, trusting in a better hope, giving us a reason to trust in God, and knowing that God is more personal to you than just an overlooking collective. You don’t need to be a part of a religious group in order to have God personally. You just have to trust in His promises of scripture to know Him. In this chapter, we go back to God’s presence and wrath, but we address it from a different angle. God’s wrath will be poured out for a reason, and though we have talked about this topic before, we would do well to remember why He must do it, when He plans to do it, and where we stand before that time comes. This chapter should give us a zeal and compassion for God’s people, and for those that have lived their lives openly rejecting the sacrifice and salvation of the Lord for them."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":4,"title":"God's Presence","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"If God is who He says He is, then you would think this would be the case, and everything would melt because of His glory. Yet, all throughout scripture, that is not the image of God’s presence. Look at the burning bush:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And the angel of the LORD appeared unto him in a flame of fire out of the midst of a bush: and he looked, and, behold, the bush burned with fire, and the bush was not consumed.","ref":"Exodus 3:2"},{"kind":"para","text":"Look at the pillar of smoke and fire:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And the LORD went before them by day in a pillar of a cloud, to lead them the way; and by night in a pillar of fire, to give them light; to go by day and night: He took not away the pillar of the cloud by day, nor the pillar of fire by night, from before the people.","ref":"Exodus 13:21-22"},{"kind":"para","text":"Look at the birth of Christ:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Glory to God in the highest, and on earth peace, good will toward men.","ref":"Luke 2:14"},{"kind":"para","text":"Look at the ministry of Christ:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"A new commandment I give unto you, That ye love one another; as I have loved you, that ye also love one another.","ref":"John 13:34"},{"kind":"para","text":"Look at the death of Christ:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For in that he died, he died unto sin once: but in that he liveth, he liveth unto God. Likewise reckon ye also yourselves to be dead indeed unto sin, but alive unto God through Jesus Christ our Lord.","ref":"Romans 6:10-11"},{"kind":"para","text":"Look at the Spirits ministry:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But God hath revealed them unto us by his Spirit: for the Spirit searcheth all things, yea, the deep things of God.","ref":"1 Corinthians 2:10"},{"kind":"para","text":"And many more examples like these. Our God is certainly a consuming fire:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For our God is a consuming fire.","ref":"Hebrews 12:29"},{"kind":"para","text":"But our God’s presence has always lifted His creation up, not torn it down. At least not yet. There will be a day when God is going to destroy this old world and make all things new. That will have to happen; we’ve spoken about this before. God will have to get rid of evil. But when Jesus comes in His first incarnation, He is not here to melt things away. At His first coming, everything is lifted up. At His second coming, everything will be torn down, and the mountains will fall."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And said to the mountains and rocks, Fall on us, and hide us from the face of him that sitteth on the throne, and from the wrath of the Lamb:","ref":"Revelation 6:16"}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The crazy part is, in Revelation, we get the opposite picture of the nations:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And blasphemed the God of heaven because of their pains and their sores, and repented not of their deeds.","ref":"Revelation 16:11"},{"kind":"para","text":"They see all the power and might of God literally coming out of Heaven, and the spiritual decline of the world, and yet they still find reason to blaspheme their creator. They still don’t care about the love and salvation of God. And we wonder why God is storing up so much wrath."},{"kind":"para","text":"If there are things in this world that you can’t understand and fathom now, just imagine how it will be in those days of great tribulation. Imagine seeing God’s wrath coming from the sky, and being poured out on mankind, and still cursing God and rejecting Him. That is pretty crazy to me. But at that time, they will certainly be without excuse."}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"It’s only because of God’s wrath that the mountains and creation will melt. That we would even allow God’s anger to build up this far is beyond me. We are evil people. It’s funny because someone posted about how evil people are on social media, and he was made fun of for asking God to forgive him. They said things like, “Why would you want to spend your life begging for mercy because your God said you’re an evil sinner?” My response to that was, “You don’t hate evil enough is what you are saying.” Honestly, that is the truth. If you knew the purpose of Jesus, you would realize the overflowing evil that comes from all people. There’s no response to my comment that won’t lead into the gospel message. She did respond, and it was a great way to showcase God’s love. We choose evil, but God gives us every opportunity to choose love."},{"kind":"para","text":"The fact of the matter is, this world will always choose evil over righteousness, and that is proven by the simple fact that there are a mass number of people in this world who are not willing to repent of their sins and turn to the Lord. During the time of Isaiah’s writing, it might have seemed as if the entire world was a lost cause. Obviously, it wasn’t, but in time the world will be. In the days of Noah, almost everyone (except for Noah) was completely lost and evil. We have been building up God’s wrath against us ever since the floods ended, and we are leading God straight to releasing His anger upon us. We have chosen to do that. Not Him. He has been patient with our wayward generation for thousands of years. I think it’s about time that He gives this world what they deserve."},{"kind":"conversation","text":"### Conversation: *It's funny because someone posted about how evil people are on social media, and he was made fun of for asking God to forgive him. They said things like, \"Why would you want to spend your life begging for mercy because your God said you're an evil sinner?\" My response to that was, \"You don't hate evil enough is what you are saying.\" Honestly, that is the truth. If you knew the purpose of Jesus, you would realize the overflowing evil that comes from all people. There's no response to my comment that won't lead into the gospel message. She did respond, and it was a great way to showcase God's love. We choose evil, but God gives us every opportunity to choose love.*"}]},{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Paul actually quotes this (if that is why it sounds familiar to you):"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But as it is written, Eye hath not seen, nor ear heard, neither have entered into the heart of man, the things which God hath prepared for them that love him.","ref":"1 Corinthians 2:9"},{"kind":"para","text":"We have seen it and heard it. We have the completed works of God in our hands and phones. We can carry it with us wherever we go. It’s all about Jesus Christ and His sacrifice for you! The mystery of God is the ministry of Christ, and when we know Him, we are not left with a mystery to solve. We are given the answer right up front, plain and simple. If you are confused about the gospel message, it is likely because someone gave you the wrong answers. They might have left you with clues to pick up and track down the case for Christ, but the answer is as simple as accepting His sacrifice for you. That’s why I love 1 Corinthians 15 so much. Paul makes it very simple, and that is all the gospel needs to be. The Spirit is what reveals God’s mystery of salvation to us."},{"kind":"para","text":"To those who are hearing Isaiah’s words, they are completely lost and confused. Even still today, if you told someone to start reading their Bibles from the Book of Isaiah, they would be completely lost. That is why I point them to John. The gospel of John is the most personal and simple book of the four gospels. However, you can point them anywhere in scripture, and it all leads to Jesus Christ and His sacrifice. Every bit of scripture points to Him (including Revelation). If you walk away from scripture with the attitude of good works, you read it wrong. You don’t have the right context. Anytime you read scripture, it must be through the lens of “How does this point to Christ?” If you don’t read it that way, you will never get the truth out of it. That is why we have so many atheist “scholars” trying to downplay the power of the Bible. They don’t point any of it to a real man named Jesus, who is the Son of God that defeated death and the grave and is now seated at the right hand of the Father."}]}]},{"start":5,"end":7,"title":"No Good Works","entries":[{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Funny, in Christ's first coming these are the people He hung out with:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And when the Pharisees saw it, they said unto his disciples, Why eateth your Master with publicans and sinners? But when Jesus heard that, he said unto them, They that be whole need not a physician, but they that are sick. But go ye and learn what that meaneth, I will have mercy, and not sacrifice: for I am not come to call the righteous, but sinners to repentance.","ref":"Matthew 9:11-13"},{"kind":"para","text":"Why does that matter? Why does it matter if we know what it means to have mercy and not sacrifice? Well, it is not enough to just be a good religionist. We have spoken about this several times. In this verse of Isaiah, we see that when Christ returns, it will not be with the sinners that He is meeting and rejoicing with. It will be those that have turned to Him and have given mercy to their enemies."},{"kind":"para","text":"God’s anger is against us if we are just playing the part of religion. His presence is with us if we are giving mercy to others out of a love for God’s mercy to us. That is what salvation looks like. It looks like a just God, who has every right to be angry with us, forgiving us because we have turned to Him and held to the sacrifice of His Son. If we have to work for that love, we cannot take it as a “gift” but as a wage."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For the wages of sin is death; but the gift of God is eternal life through Jesus Christ our Lord.","ref":"Romans 6:23"},{"kind":"para","text":"Even still, if we wanted to work for it, this is what Isaiah says:"}]},{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I’ve heard people describe the “filthy rags” illustration as menstrual cloths. Perhaps that is what Isaiah is referring to here, but I don’t know. “Filthy” comes from a Hebrew word that means “menstruation.” Either way, the point of this passage is that we cannot do anything to earn favor with God. We are born enemies of God, and we will die enemies of God even if we are full of good works or “righteousness.” Compared to the Lord’s standards, our iniquities are far greater than our righteousnesses could ever be. We might do some good things here and there, but we are pulled by sin everywhere else, and we have to live with the fact that there is nothing we can do to pay off our sin debt. In fact, the further we get into our sin, the more we desire to reject God and refrain from His presence. Our sins are like the dark. God is light. So when our sins are revealed, the only thing we want to do is run away from the light and hide again. God won’t let that happen though, and that is why He sent His light into the world."},{"kind":"para","text":"When we do good things in our own strength, it doesn’t give us any points with God. When we hold our rituals and keep God’s commands, God is not moved with compassion for us. This is how God is moved with compassion:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But when he saw the multitudes, he was moved with compassion on them, because they fainted, and were scattered abroad, as sheep having no shepherd.","ref":"Matthew 9:36"},{"kind":"para","text":"He sees so many wandering people, and instead of making Him angry, it makes Him hurt. He has salvation right in the palm of His hand, and all these people (we) must do is take it. It’s there for them as a free gift if they are willing. Yet, they will try to climb into the sheepfold some other way, and the Lord is going to reject that:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Verily, verily, I say unto you, He that entereth not by the door into the sheepfold, but climbeth up some other way, the same is a thief and a robber.","ref":"John 10:1"}]},{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"All hope is lost for those who don’t have Christ. It’s such a plain and simple truth, yet there are still millions of people in this world who don’t understand and believe it. They think they will be fine until they are faced with a life-altering dilemma and have no place to turn but in prayer. At that point, it’s already too late. I’m thankful that the Lord has given me access to His throne of grace for any time and all the time. Even if it’s small, God’s grace is there."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And he said unto me, My grace is sufficient for thee: for my strength is made perfect in weakness. Most gladly therefore will I rather glory in my infirmities, that the power of Christ may rest upon me.","ref":"2 Corinthians 12:9"},{"kind":"para","text":"Our works are not enough, but God’s grace is more than enough. We should not be leaning on our good works or keeping of the law. We should only be leaning on the finished work of Christ. Honestly, I could argue that there is really no such thing as good works in our own flesh. Only good intentions, but nothing good comes from my fleshly hands. Everything I touch turns to iniquity. Everything the Lord touches, however, becomes new."}]}]},{"start":8,"end":12,"title":"Facing God's Wrath","entries":[{"start":8,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Again, Isaiah says (on behalf of Israel) “our” Father. Not just “my” Father, but “our” Father. He is the Father of the righteous, not of the lost. He is the Father of the repentant sinner, not of the unrighteous. We cannot call Him Father and yet live a completely separate life away from Him. He is either the leader and captain of our lives or He is not."},{"kind":"para","text":"When Adam said in the beginning with Eve that marriage required “leaving father and mother” and “cleaving” to his wife, he had no father or mother to leave but one. He left the directives of his Heavenly Father. That is not the way in which the Lord intended. We are to leave the spiritual and provisional authority of our Earthly fathers and mothers, but we are not to leave the spiritual and provisional authority of God the Father. We must keep Him in charge of our lives. Always."},{"kind":"para","text":"God is always our Father, whether we are married or not, and He will always need to be the one that leads and guides the individual, not just the group. God can lead a group too, but only if we are all of the same mind;"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Fulfil ye my joy, that ye be likeminded, having the same love, being of one accord, of one mind.","ref":"Philippians 2:2"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Be of the same mind one toward another. Mind not high things, but condescend to men of low estate. Be not wise in your own conceits.","ref":"Romans 12:16"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Now I beseech you, brethren, by the name of our Lord Jesus Christ, that ye all speak the same thing, and that there be no divisions among you; but that ye be perfectly joined together in the same mind and in the same judgment.","ref":"1 Corinthians 1:10"},{"kind":"para","text":"If we don't have the mind of Christ, we are not going to be led by our Heavenly Father. If we want to be \"potter\" in the hands of the Father, we must be like His Son who was always tender to God's leading, and never shunned His presence."}]},{"start":9,"end":9,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Isaiah couldn’t have had a very easy time saying this particular thing. There were, perhaps, many who were still calling on the name of the Lord (I’m sure Isaiah was one of them), but there were far more who had shunned God and caused all of this chaos to ensue."},{"kind":"para","text":"Isaiah is pleading on behalf of the saved. He’s pleading on behalf of those that are looking to serve the Lord and stay the course, even with the entire rest of the world against Him. He is pleading with God for those that have no other strength and know they can’t depend on their own strength. That is the pleading all of us should have with our Heavenly Father because He IS our strength and peace."}]},{"start":10,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Imagine how the entire world will look when Christ returns, considering these are just the cities in Isaiah’s time. Perhaps you take a look out of your window right now. You might see some trees, birds, grass, the sky is blue, maybe there’s rain on the horizon. Perhaps, you look out your window and see cars driving by, or a quiet road, or children playing, or cats meowing, or whatever the case may be. Perhaps all of this bugs you when you look out your window, but this is the creation of God!"},{"kind":"para","text":"Some day those sights will all be gone. Everything in this world will result in chaos once the Lord prepares His return. Those trees, birds, cats, cars, children, sky, grass, or even rain will all be gone and replaced with smoke, fear, murder, famine, and death. That’s the view that Israel is having because of their iniquity. They lost everything because they rejected the leading of the Lord for so long. They had everything, and they could have maintained what they had if they just stood firm on the presence and affirmations of the Lord. That’s a very important rule to make for yourself as well."}]},{"start":12,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Our chapter here ends on an open-ended question: Will God always be mad with this world? Will God’s wrath afflict and destroy even His own children’s way of living? I think the prophets felt the wrath of God in these moments. They felt God’s judgment as the people they loved were being taken captive and treated like animals. They felt the pains of their own people as they saw everything become destroyed and taken over. They felt what the wicked felt."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Much more then, being now justified by his blood, we shall be saved from wrath through him.","ref":"Romans 5:9"},{"kind":"para","text":"While God is not going to pour His wrath out on His own, His own should not feel calloused to the fact that others around you are feeling His wrath and judgment. It should do something to our hearts to know that people you love, people you know, and people you see will experience God’s judgment and destruction. Not just experience it, but feel the full brunt of it."},{"kind":"para","text":"It should make us uneasy to know that you have lost family members who are going to go through God’s vengeance because they have decided to reject His salvation. If it doesn’t bug you, and you can just shrug it off, I’d argue that you don’t have the love or Spirit of God. Your heart is hard, and that needs to be addressed and fixed as soon as possible. Otherwise, the Lord will work on your heart by making you face His wrath as well. God’s Spirit should make us feel the pains and hurts of our neighbors, whether they are saved or not."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":9},{"start":10,"end":11},{"start":12,"end":12}],"verses":{"1":"Oh that thou wouldest rend the heavens, that thou wouldest come down, that the mountains might flow down at thy presence,","2":"As when the melting fire burneth, the fire causeth the waters to boil, to make thy name known to thine adversaries, that the nations may tremble at thy presence!","3":"When thou didst terrible things which we looked not for, thou camest down, the mountains flowed down at thy presence.","4":"For since the beginning of the world men have not heard, nor perceived by the ear, neither hath the eye seen, O God, beside thee, what he hath prepared for him that waiteth for him.","5":"Thou meetest him that rejoiceth and worketh righteousness, those that remember thee in thy ways: behold, thou art wroth; for we have sinned: in those is continuance, and we shall be saved.","6":"But we are all as an unclean thing, and all our righteousnesses are as filthy rags; and we all do fade as a leaf; and our iniquities, like the wind, have taken us away.","7":"And there is none that calleth upon thy name, that stirreth up himself to take hold of thee: for thou hast hid thy face from us, and hast consumed us, because of our iniquities.","8":"But now, O Lord, thou art our father; we are the clay, and thou our potter; and we all are the work of thy hand.","9":"Be not wroth very sore, O Lord, neither remember iniquity for ever: behold, see, we beseech thee, we are all thy people.","10":"Thy holy cities are a wilderness, Zion is a wilderness, Jerusalem a desolation.","11":"Our holy and our beautiful house, where our fathers praised thee, is burned up with fire: and all our pleasant things are laid waste.","12":"Wilt thou refrain thyself for these things, O Lord? wilt thou hold thy peace, and afflict us very sore?"}},
    "65": {"chapter":65,"intro":[{"kind":"scripture","text":"Wilt thou refrain thyself for these things, O LORD? wilt thou hold thy peace, and afflict us very sore?","ref":"Isaiah 64:12"},{"kind":"para","text":"In this chapter, the Lord answers that question. He explains how He will take care of His own, and still give judgement to the wicked. He concludes this chapter will an amazing future promise of entirely new life, and the reward for sticking through to the end. Fighting the good fight of faith may not seem worth it right now, but the rewards of standing and holding the promises of God are going to be worth it."}],"previously":["In our last chapter, Isaiah spoke about the importance of God's presence in this world, and in our lives, as well as establishing how evil and undeserving we are as a creation to even have God's attention set on us. If you don't remember our last chapter ended with a question to the Lord pleading for His redemption and coming."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":7,"title":"A Reason For Judgement","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God has been calling His people in Israel for generations. He has been trying to get their attention since the beginning of time. They should have every reason possible to ask for God and to search for Him, yet they have chosen to reject the Lord, His goodness, His compassion, and His prosperity. If we are not facing prosperity in our country today, that is the reason we aren’t. Our nation’s leaders have rejected the Lord, and the people under that leadership have followed suit."},{"kind":"para","text":"So God calls to people who are not of that nation. He calls to the Gentiles. If you are saved today, you can really understand this. You weren’t asking for God. You were not trying to find Him. Yet, here you are, and you are a nation called by God’s name. This doesn’t mean that He has completely unhitched from His people Israel. This simply means that (as proof of His salvation, His compassion, and His ability to reach the lost), His arms are open to the whole world that is willing to come to Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"Instead of just one nation to follow in our scriptures (after the Old Testament), we will follow the world church. That would include all walks of life from nations that they have never even heard of. The book of Acts is a great resource for seeing how that came to be and this particular verse coming to fruition."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God has “exhausted” His resources on these people who couldn’t care less about what the Lord wanted to do in their lives. Honestly, I think there are still a lot of people like this in the church today. These church leaders have been saved so long, or they have simply gotten used to God’s providence so much that they no longer plead with the Lord. They just expect God to hold His end of the bargain at this point. That’s a perfect match for God’s turning away. He doesn’t want to give to a rebellious people that will only take His good gifts and walk a different path, and after their own thoughts."},{"kind":"para","text":"Really, that is the key part of this lifestyle “after their own thoughts.” This simply means that they did what THEY wanted to do rather than what God wanted them to do. Pastors will say, “The Lord is directing me into this or that,” but really it’s just their own personal agenda of what they want to see happen. Don’t get me wrong, I think the Lord can still lead a thought and idea that a man has, but He won’t do it if that man is not relying on Him for the outcome."},{"kind":"para","text":"Our current church is trying to build a home church on a property. They’ve been trying to do this for a few years now. There seems to always be something getting in the way (we live in California, and there’s a builder’s permit for literally everything, and they will charge you thousands of dollars to pull each permit (for instance, you need a permit to test the ground, and then there’s some sort of Native American permit to make sure that it’s not tribal property even though the property has already been purchased, and then there’s permits for water lines, electricity, building, etc.)). Really, the fact of the matter is if the Lord is not the one that our church is leaning on for this, we will never see this church built. I don’t blame the Lord for not building this church. We either wait for Him and respect His timing, or we try and take it into our own hands and see God reject it."},{"kind":"para","text":"Don’t chase your own thoughts trying to force God to accept it. Chase the moving of the Spirit, and wait for the Lord to move you. It’s really simple, yet leaders make this mistake all the time. They just think they have too much power, and that is what gets them into trouble."},{"kind":"conversation","text":"*Our current church is trying to build a home church on a property. They've been trying to do this for a few years now. There seems to always be something getting in the way (we live in California, and there's a builders permit for literally everything, and they will charge you thousands of dollars to pull each permit (for instance you need a permit to test the ground, and then there's some sort of native american permit to make sure that it's not tribal property even though the property has already been purchased, and then there's permits for water lines, electricity, building, etc.)) Really, the fact of the matter is if the Lord is not the one that our church is leaning on for this, we will never see this church built. I don't blame the Lord for not building this church. We either wait for Him, and respect His timing, or we try and take it into our own hands and see God reject it.*"}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Notice the way in which the Lord sees His people going against Him. They are seemingly not doing it in secret. They actually know that they are doing the wrong things, and they are doing it on purpose to try and make the Lord angry with them. I’m sure I’ve used this illustration before, but when I was younger, they were building a gas station in the town where I was growing up. They took quite some time to build it, but one of the things that caught my eye was this large open red button that read “Do Not Push” on top of it. Now, why would a place tempt teenage children like this? Why put an obviously pushable button right on the side of a building and then tell you not to push it? It must be pushed. Little did I know it was the pump shut-off switch, and when you push it, it makes all the gas pumps turn off so that there is no overflow. They had to fix it, and eventually, they put a little door over it so that people had to work a little harder to push that button."},{"kind":"para","text":"We like to do the opposite of what we are told. We seriously are a rebellious people, but we should not be towards the Lord. I think there are things we should be okay with rebelling against honestly. This might not be a popular message for many Christians today, but there are some things that our government, our leaders, even our church leaders do that are actually anti-biblical and would displease the Lord. You have the choice to trust your leaders and simply go with the flow, or you have the choice to ask questions, request answers, and make a better decision based on what God says in His Word. If you want to help lead your church into the grave, then don’t question your leadership. If you want to help people move forward, succeed, and grow, everything must be brought before the knowledge of scripture."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"God forbid: yea, let God be true, but every man a liar; as it is written, That thou mightest be justified in thy sayings, and mightest overcome when thou art judged.","ref":"Romans 3:4"},{"kind":"para","text":"In the end, we will make the better choice if we simply trust and obey the Lord rather than those who are over us. With that said, we should want to trust our leaders. God has placed them there on purpose, and we should want to see our leaders succeed."},{"kind":"para","text":"I don’t much care for our current governor of California, and I think he makes a lot of really dumb mistakes about policies that affect the entire state. He (in my eyes, as well as many of the public) is an evil human being who wants to do everything in his own power to go against what is good and right, to make things “fair and even.” If you have to waver on truth and righteousness to make things “fair,” then you will never have a righteous state. We will just grow in evil ways because that is what is being promoted. I have reason to dislike him. However, I do pray that he makes better decisions. I pray that he would succeed and focus on the right things, and that he would help the people who need it the most. That is a wishful prayer, but it’s a prayer nevertheless. I don’t want to see him fail, but it seems he fails on purpose. It probably just makes him more money is the only reason why."},{"kind":"para","text":"The success of leaders trickles down to the people who are under their authority, and the same is true with failures. However, when a leader fails, we have the right and God-given privilege to rebel against that leadership to stand on truth and conviction."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Then Peter and the other apostles answered and said, We ought to obey God rather than men.","ref":"Acts 5:29"},{"kind":"para","text":"Rebellion is okay if it's against the evil of this world. It is never okay if it's against the standards of the Lord. That's the rule of thumb."},{"kind":"conversation","text":"*I'm sure I've used this illustration before, but when I was younger they were building a gas station in the town where I was growing up. They took quite some time to build it, but one of the things that caught my eye was this large open red button that read \"Do Not Push\" on top of it. Now why would a place tempt teenage children like this? Why put an obviously pushable button right on the side of a building, and then tell you not to push it? It MUST be pushed. Little did I know it was the pump shut off switch, and when you push it, it makes all the gas pumps turn off so that where there is no overflow. They had to fix it, and eventually they put a little door over it so that people had to work a little harder to push that button.*"},{"kind":"conversation","text":"*I don't much care for our current governor of California, and I think he makes a lot of really dumb mistakes about policies that affect the entire state. He (in my eyes, as well as many of the public) is an evil human being that wants to do everything in his own power to go against what is good and right, to make things \"fair and even.\" If you have to waiver on truth and righteousness to make things \"fair\" then you will never have a righteous state. We will just grow in evil ways because that is what is being promoted. I have reason to dislike him. However, I do pray that he makes better decisions. I pray that he would succeed and focus on the right things, and that he would help the people that need it the most. That is a wishful prayer, but it's a prayer nevertheless. I don't want to see him fail, but it seems he fails on purpose. It probably just makes him more money is the only reason why.*"}]},{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"These are pagan rituals that God is talking about here. He told His people over and over again that they were not supposed to be a part of those kinds of traditions, and they didn’t listen. There were times when they listened, but then they went right back to everything they weren’t supposed to do again. Like some sort of magnet, sin has a way of pulling even the strongest Christians into it."},{"kind":"para","text":"The children of Israel didn’t have the sight of their Savior in their vision, and so they lost sight of the Lord in the process, which led them to do the exact opposite of what God wanted for them. Whenever we lose sight of the Savior, we are pulled into sin."}]},{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is a very big problem in the church today. It’s not just the leaders who are this way; many congregants leave a bad taste in people’s mouths when they come to church. Instead of welcoming them in, they segregate them and make them feel as if they don’t belong. I’ve seen in every single church I’ve visited that people form alliances and circles. If you didn’t help them form those circles, you have to form your own because there is no way they will let you into their club. This is especially true with very large churches. The bigger the church, the more standoffish they are. They act “holier than thou” and claim stake in their territory of the church, thinking they somehow belong there more than anyone else. They consider themselves far more used by God and a lot less prideful, yet the opposite is true."},{"kind":"para","text":"They perform their rituals, sacraments, prayers, talking, music, and sermons, but not because there’s a fire in them. They do it because they want eyes on them. They do it because they want people (not God) to think that they are the pinnacle of Christian examples. Those kinds of people always fall in time. They are graceless, and that is the end of their walks of faith. It’s faith without grace. When people treat others without grace, it doesn’t draw them closer to the church or to God; rather, it pushes them away from it altogether. I wish I would have known this when I was a younger Christian. I probably made a lot of new people in the church feel unwelcome. I tried to meet new people all the time. I’d write their names down, pray for them throughout the week, and then see them the next Sunday and let them know that I was praying for them that week. If I didn’t see them, however, I wouldn’t even try to follow up with them after that. I just thought they didn’t like the church and probably didn’t want to come to the Lord anyway. That was foolish of me to think. I should have gone out of my way for them when I had the chance. I don’t make this mistake now. I leave myself open to any possibility and give them the benefit of the doubt, thinking, “Maybe someone they love is in the hospital. I should go check up on them.”"},{"kind":"para","text":"We should have tender hearts as people of the faith. We should think the best in people, even though we know that everyone is a sinner. We shouldn’t just jump straight to conclusions. We should hope that they are okay and that they might need a little encouragement and help. I’ll let you in on a little secret for this particular case study. I haven’t been going back to my church for nearly eight months now. Not a single person in leadership has reached out to me or asked me what has been going on. That is a huge problem if this is happening in your church. The leaders are not “holier than thou.” If they were, they wouldn’t allow people to just disappear after serving them for three years. That’s a great method to make people feel used and thrown away. I’ve had to struggle with thoughts of uselessness, depression, bitterness, and pain because of it. I know that I’m not the only one either. There is a whole world out there that has felt this pain and feels like they have nowhere to turn and no one to trust. If they can’t even trust the church to do what’s right, then who can they trust?"},{"kind":"conversation","text":"*I tried to meet new people all the time. I'd write their names down, I'd pray for them throughout the week, and then I would see them the next Sunday and let them know that I was praying for them that week. If I didn't see them, however, I wouldn't even try to follow up with them after that. I just thought they didn't like the church, and they probably didn't want to come to the Lord anyway. That was foolish of me to think. I should have gone out of my way for them when I had the chance. I don't make this mistake now. I leave myself open to any possibility, and give them the benefit of the doubt thinking, \"Maybe someone they love is in the hospital. I should go check up on them.\"*"}]},{"start":6,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"You reap what you sow. This is a law for how we treat others here on Earth, but also for how we treat the Lord in our lives. If you spend your entire life mocking and rejecting the Lord, doing everything in your power to go against Him, there will be consequences from that action. You will eventually have to reap your harvest of disobedience and sin. The fruit of sin is bitter and cold. It’s not a welcoming fruit. It’s poisonous and doesn’t give you any real substance. It might taste sweet at the start, but it will just leave you feeling sick."},{"kind":"para","text":"In contrast, the fruit of the Spirit is eternal and everlasting. This fruit gifts you with fullness and substance. Better yet, it continues to provide for you even after you have taken a bite out of it. The fruit of sin robs you, while the fruit of the Spirit rewards you. Israel acted the part; they looked the part and made it seem as if they truly were the holiest of all people. When in reality, their God was not with them. Fake Christians are the worst kinds of Christians because they fool the innocent and lead them into a pit with them. This is why we should not follow man."},{"kind":"para","text":"Someone said recently that “the single greatest cause of Atheism today is Christians who acknowledge Jesus with their lips and deny him by their lifestyle.” It’s not entirely wrong, but we do not follow man to be saved. If your salvation is contingent upon the perfection of Christians, you will lose your faith almost instantly. It must solemnly be hung upon the cross of Christ if you want it to be genuine. Otherwise, your faith fails when the Christians fail (and they always do). Please don’t look to me to grow your faith. Look to God, and He will never fail you."}]}]},{"start":8,"end":12,"title":"Security For The Faithful","entries":[{"start":8,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is an interesting thought. Not everyone in that nation was completely lost. There were prophets and believers still living among them. The only reason that God would not completely wipe them out was because there were still believers living among them. I truly believe that the only reason that God has not completely demolished and destroyed California is because there are still believers in the midst of all the evil. There are still faithful people who believe."},{"kind":"para","text":"If this state finally achieves its goal of silencing and getting rid of all the faithful Christians it has left in it (though they may be few), I truly believe the Lord would sink this state quite quickly. It would turn over to chaos and destruction either by the hands of the evil people still remaining in the state, or by the hands of God. Either way, it wouldn’t last forever. We should be thankful for faithful Christians. They are the only reason that God is not done with us yet. That is why I lean more towards the rapture happening before the tribulation period. God needs to destroy this Earth, and if there are still faithful people living in it, He still has a reason to keep it going."}]},{"start":9,"end":9,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Obviously, this is speaking about Jesus. Again, as I’ve mentioned before, the elect is Jesus Christ. He is the only one who is “elected.” Anyone else who is saved is only because of the election of Christ. We get saved because we are under His elected umbrella."},{"kind":"para","text":"Either way, the promise of salvation, protection, and security is found only under the direct ruling and governing of the Lord alone. He will keep His promises to His people who turn to Him in faith and trust."}]},{"start":10,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"“Sharon” means “Level,” and “Achor” means “Trouble.” During the time of tribulation, I am assured there will be a small remnant that will survive, and they will turn to the Lord. This small remnant will live in the middle of “trouble” but will “lie down” with God’s protection. It won’t be a rocky, steep ground they will be lying on. It will be “level.” It will be a place of pasture in the midst of chaos."},{"kind":"para","text":"If you lean towards a post-tribulation rapture, this certainly can still apply. While the world is facing complete chaos and destruction, God has a place for His faithful people to rest. He will protect and take care of His own, even while serving justice to the wicked."}]},{"start":11,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The prophets were all taken care of because of their faithfulness to the Lord. However, the rest of the nation went into captivity and slavery. They returned to bondage because they rejected the Lord while they had the chance."},{"kind":"para","text":"We might think we have time to follow God. We have time to make things right. We can just serve ourselves for a little longer before we have to turn. But we really don’t know how much time we have left. God can change the tide in a second without us knowing what is happening."},{"kind":"para","text":"This is why we must be carefully considering our actions and motives while we walk this Earth. If we are not thinking about the Lord, He will simply give us over to our ways and thoughts. Again, we reap what we sow. It’s wise to sow God throughout our lives, so we reap His rewards when the season comes."}]}]},{"start":13,"end":16,"title":"God of Truth","entries":[{"start":13,"end":14,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"It should not be a surprise to us that God is able to do both. I am able to provide for my family and be angry with my enemy. That is a very simple characteristic engrained into every human being. God has the ultimate authority to do this. He can give His faithful people food, drink, joy, and song, and still give His enemies hunger, thirst, shame, and sorrow."},{"kind":"para","text":"I could probably argue that the enemies of the Lord will only feel these things out of jealousy for the provision God gives to His own people. They will see that they are being taken care of, and it will only increase their anger against God, rather than increase their faith in Him. That is why we will see them attacking the Christians in the end times. I am getting ahead of myself, though."}]},{"start":15,"end":16,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"He is not just the God of Creation. He is not just the God of Salvation. He is not just the God of Nations. He is the God of Truth! His Word is trusted. Honestly, His Word is the only thing that CAN be trusted in this Earth. I have heard people say that they can’t trust modern scriptures because they have been “tainted.” Yet, I have done nothing BUT trust this book with my life since my salvation, and it has never (not one time) steered me wrong."},{"kind":"para","text":"If it HAS been tainted, it wouldn’t be able to change my thoughts and restructure my life. If it HAS been tainted, I would have no problem simply twisting it and making myself feel better. If it HAS been tainted, I wouldn’t question any of my past decisions, mistakes, or sins. If this is a tainted book, I would not be influenced by it at all. Yet I’m a completely changed person. Not because someone shared the gospel with me, but because this book reflects my flaws and displays my Christ."},{"kind":"para","text":"The soulwinner that told me the gospel gave me the information of where to start, but it was SCRIPTURE that saved my life and changed it to His glory. If this book is tainted, then there’s no hope for eternity, and no hope for the truth. Yet, our God is a God of truth. You either believe He is true, or you simply taint your own version of truth. That is YOUR decision."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And if it seem evil unto you to serve the LORD, choose you this day whom ye will serve; whether the gods which your fathers served that were on the other side of the flood, or the gods of the Amorites, in whose land ye dwell: but as for me and my house, we will serve the LORD.","ref":"Joshua 24:15"}]}]},{"start":17,"end":25,"title":"The World's Change","entries":[{"start":17,"end":17,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God is going to create a new heaven and earth once His judgment has been settled. He will not do it while there is still evil on this Earth, otherwise, everything goes back to the way it was before. He will have to get rid of the evil first, as we’ve already discussed in previous chapters (and will discuss again, no doubt). This is quite an amazing promise given here, though. We don’t read much about a new heaven and earth until we get into the book of Revelation."},{"kind":"para","text":"One of the things that I have not mentioned about these Old Testament prophecies is that the timeline is a little more… uncertain. There are specificities about the times, but not for everything. We could argue about when this new heaven and earth will come (for instance) in this chapter of Isaiah, or we can get the appropriate timeline in the book of Revelation. Even in that, there is a lot of folding between events happening. John does a little better job of giving appropriate times (though I could argue that some of it is symbolic rather than literal, but we can research that in Revelation). Whatever the case may be, the Lord is making a grand promise to the future of this whole world right here."},{"kind":"para","text":"God’s promises don’t just affect the nation of Israel. God’s promises will (and always have) affected the entire Earth. We might only be honing in on Israel in this half of the Bible, but the impacts of God reach to everyone (even those nations not mentioned in scripture). God’s movement impacts history’s timeline. Even when evil people do evil things, it is God’s movement that creates the biggest events in history."},{"kind":"para","text":"You might say, “So God was in charge of Hitler’s slaughter of millions of Jews?” No. But He was in charge of keeping the Jews alive even though they were the underdogs of the world in the beginning of creation. If God didn’t choose that nation, there wouldn’t be any Jews left for Hitler to be so evil. It is supposed that Hitler eventually committed suicide later on when he saw that Germany was going to lose the battle of Berlin. Either way, God has made some major impacts before all of that, and while evil people might make major impacts as well, it will be God’s goodness, provision, and ability to make all things new that will always come out on top and have the greater impact over evil."}]},{"start":18,"end":18,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God says that there will be a \"new\" Jerusalem as well after the wrath and judgement of God is poured out;"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And I John saw the holy city, new Jerusalem, coming down from God out of heaven, prepared as a bride adorned for her husband.","ref":"Revelation 21:2"},{"kind":"para","text":"In this new Jerusalem, there will be nothing but rejoicing and people of joy. All evil will be gone, and sin will be cast into the lake of fire with Satan, his demons, and those who were evil, rejecting the Lord and His people. That is the picture God paints about these two very different places. The people of Hell are “wailing” and “gnashing teeth.”"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And shall cast them into the furnace of fire: there shall be wailing and gnashing of teeth.","ref":"Matthew 13:50"},{"kind":"para","text":"The people of Heaven are “rejoicing.\" Personally, I like joy more than wailing, but I suppose that's not for everyone."}]},{"start":19,"end":19,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"No, the voice of weeping and crying will only be found in the furnace. That might sound sad to you, but that is the truth. God wants nothing but to “rejoice” in His people and be face to face with us. That is something He is really looking forward to, and that is why all of this must take place."},{"kind":"para","text":"He wants us to be able to stand in His presence and speak to Him as closely as you would speak to your own earthly father. He wants to look you in the eyes when He speaks to you. That has been what His whole work of love has been since the beginning of scripture—to get you prepared to see Him face to face."}]},{"start":20,"end":20,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Age will not exist in this new heaven and Earth. We will all be young and agile. People place a lot of influence on your body today. They say, “That is God’s temple, and you only get one body, so you should take care of it.” I’m all for taking care of yourself and exercising, but this will not be the only body you have. You will have a Spiritual body, and it will be renewed to the best version of yourself. The same goes for babies. If you have a baby and they are raptured, or (God forbid) they die, their bodies will be young bodies, not baby bodies. They will grow up into the best version of themselves. I might be balding today, but I will not be in Heaven. We will stay forever young (as the secular song implies)."}]},{"start":21,"end":21,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God says there will still be work in this new Heaven and Earth. We will continue to “build,” “plant,” and “eat.” We will still put in effort. The only difference is that we won’t grow tired or weary when we do it."},{"kind":"para","text":"I can’t wait to build a house on this new Earth without having to worry about growing tired or running out of resources. That will be an amazing gift. We can dwell with the Lord and still get to live a gifted life."}]},{"start":22,"end":22,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"We won’t have to worry about even locking our doors. No one is going to try and rob you. There won’t be a single evil soul in anyone’s body, and there will be no more sin. I believe we will have absolute trust in man in those days. We cannot have that here today. Man is evil in our current world, and they are enticed by evil acts today. But when the new world comes, we have the freedom to trust our neighbors, help our neighbors, and build with our neighbors like never before."}]},{"start":23,"end":23,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"If we read through Ecclesiastes, Solomon says that everything in this world (including all the labor that he labored in) is vanity and vexation of spirit."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Then I looked on all the works that my hands had wrought, and on the labour that I had laboured to do: and, behold, all was vanity and vexation of spirit, and there was no profit under the sun.","ref":"Ecclesiastes 2:11"},{"kind":"para","text":"He goes on to say that because life is fleeting, we should just enjoy what we have right now because it will be gone when we die anyway:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Wherefore I perceive that there is nothing better, than that a man should rejoice in his own works; for that is his portion: for who shall bring him to see what shall be after him?","ref":"Ecclesiastes 3:22"},{"kind":"para","text":"Yet, in this new Earth, the thoughts will not be the same. We won’t die again, so the purposes of building and maintaining will be for the reason and purpose of eternal enjoyment. Also, nothing will corrode or wither away; everything will be upright and kept properly in this new Earth. I don’t know if you will even have to worry about dust ever again."}]},{"start":24,"end":24,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Obviously, the fact that we are going to rebuild life doesn’t mean that we are not going to have access to the Lord. I believe that is what the New Jerusalem is for. It’s God’s dwelling place. It’s God’s house. Before we even request anything, God is going to answer our prayer thoughts. Maybe even before we know what we need, God will answer our requests. He has done that from time to time even today, but when the Earth is completely new, He will do that for everyone forever without hesitation or worry about what problems can come down the line if He answers our prayers."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord might not answer our prayers right away today because it may mean something terrible happening in the future. But when sin is gone, and evil no longer exists, He has no problems with any future events. He will never have to worry about the consequences of giving us what we want again, because everything we will want will be directly in line with God’s goodness and glory. Even if it might seem selfish in this life, God will answer that prayer in the next."},{"kind":"para","text":"You might have heard the prosperity preachers talking about praying for that new car. Perhaps you really need a new car, but God usually doesn’t answer those prayers today because it’s selfish and ultimately will lead you to sin. However, in the new Earth, that prayer will be answered without a single thought to it because none of your thoughts will be selfish, and nothing can lead you to sin anymore."}]},{"start":25,"end":25,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This will be a strange thing to see honestly. It might take us some getting used to. There is no such thing in this new Earth called a “savage” animal. All animals will simply dwell together and will live in a way that doesn’t seem natural. Lions eating straw would be a very strange thing for us to witness. Wolves and lambs dwelling together is not even a possibility in our minds. Serpents being satisfied with dust to eat is such a strange reality. Yet that is how the Lord intends to make this Earth."},{"kind":"para","text":"There will be no more food chain. There’s no “circle” of life. It’s just God’s people, living, thriving, and exploring together with the Lord always by their side. To walk and explore this Earth with my family and Jesus is the most beautiful picture I can muster up in a world that is so lost and out of control today. I really look forward to when these things come to pass and we will forever dwell with God in eternity."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":9},{"start":10,"end":10},{"start":11,"end":12},{"start":13,"end":14},{"start":15,"end":16},{"start":17,"end":17},{"start":18,"end":18},{"start":19,"end":19},{"start":20,"end":20},{"start":21,"end":21},{"start":22,"end":22},{"start":23,"end":23},{"start":24,"end":24},{"start":25,"end":25}],"verses":{"1":"I am sought of them that asked not for me; I am found of them that sought me not: I said, Behold me, behold me, unto a nation that was not called by my name.","2":"I have spread out my hands all the day unto a rebellious people, which walketh in a way that was not good, after their own thoughts;","3":"A people that provoketh me to anger continually to my face; that sacrificeth in gardens, and burneth incense upon altars of brick;","4":"Which remain among the graves, and lodge in the monuments, which eat swine's flesh, and broth of abominable things is in their vessels;","5":"Which say, Stand by thyself, come not near to me; for I am holier than thou. These are a smoke in my nose, a fire that burneth all the day.","6":"Behold, it is written before me: I will not keep silence, but will recompense, even recompense into their bosom,","7":"Your iniquities, and the iniquities of your fathers together, saith the Lord, which have burned incense upon the mountains, and blasphemed me upon the hills: therefore will I measure their former work into their bosom.","8":"Thus saith the Lord, As the new wine is found in the cluster, and one saith, Destroy it not; for a blessing is in it: so will I do for my servants' sakes, that I may not destroy them all.","9":"And I will bring forth a seed out of Jacob, and out of Judah an inheritor of my mountains: and mine elect shall inherit it, and my servants shall dwell there.","10":"And Sharon shall be a fold of flocks, and the valley of Achor a place for the herds to lie down in, for my people that have sought me.","11":"But ye are they that forsake the Lord, that forget my holy mountain, that prepare a table for that troop, and that furnish the drink offering unto that number.","12":"Therefore will I number you to the sword, and ye shall all bow down to the slaughter: because when I called, ye did not answer; when I spake, ye did not hear; but did evil before mine eyes, and did choose that wherein I delighted not.","13":"Therefore thus saith the Lord God, Behold, my servants shall eat, but ye shall be hungry: behold, my servants shall drink, but ye shall be thirsty: behold, my servants shall rejoice, but ye shall be ashamed:","14":"Behold, my servants shall sing for joy of heart, but ye shall cry for sorrow of heart, and shall howl for vexation of spirit.","15":"And ye shall leave your name for a curse unto my chosen: for the Lord God shall slay thee, and call his servants by another name:","16":"That he who blesseth himself in the earth shall bless himself in the God of truth; and he that sweareth in the earth shall swear by the God of truth; because the former troubles are forgotten, and because they are hid from mine eyes.","17":"For, behold, I create new heavens and a new earth: and the former shall not be remembered, nor come into mind.","18":"But be ye glad and rejoice for ever in that which I create: for, behold, I create Jerusalem a rejoicing, and her people a joy.","19":"And I will rejoice in Jerusalem, and joy in my people: and the voice of weeping shall be no more heard in her, nor the voice of crying.","20":"There shall be no more thence an infant of days, nor an old man that hath not filled his days: for the child shall die an hundred years old; but the sinner being an hundred years old shall be accursed.","21":"And they shall build houses, and inhabit them; and they shall plant vineyards, and eat the fruit of them.","22":"They shall not build, and another inhabit; they shall not plant, and another eat: for as the days of a tree are the days of my people, and mine elect shall long enjoy the work of their hands.","23":"They shall not labour in vain, nor bring forth for trouble; for they are the seed of the blessed of the Lord, and their offspring with them.","24":"And it shall come to pass, that before they call, I will answer; and while they are yet speaking, I will hear.","25":"The wolf and the lamb shall feed together, and the lion shall eat straw like the bullock: and dust shall be the serpent's meat. They shall not hurt nor destroy in all my holy mountain, saith the Lord."}},
    "66": {"chapter":66,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: In our last chapter, God explains why He must do these things in the end. There's a reason for His judgement on this Earth, and it's not to just hurt people, or destroy people for no reason. He wants to provide this creation with security and closer, and He wants to give His own people a place of worship and rest. The things He has promised for His people are things that we should take seriously, and He promised a new Heaven and Earth when the time is right."},{"kind":"para","text":"So here we are. We are in our last chapter. It has been a journey. There have been ups and downs as we read through God's future plans for this nation, the world, the lost, and the saved. He has made promises, kept promises, and we anticipate the final promises being made. Isaiah finishes this book up with displaying the heart of God, and the desire for God to give salvation and pleading for this lost and wicked world. He doesn't want to see His creation fail here. He doesn't want them to go down the wrong path. He definitely doesn't want them to suffer for all eternity. But He will not force you to make the proper decision. He will just open both doors to you and allow you to choose for yourself."}],"previously":["In our last chapter, God explains why He must do these things in the end. There’s a reason for His judgment on this Earth, and it’s not just to hurt people or destroy them for no reason. He wants to provide this creation with security and closeness, and He wants to give His own people a place of worship and rest. The things He has promised for His people are things that we should take seriously, and He promised a new Heaven and Earth when the time is right. So here we are. We are in our last chapter. It has been a journey. There have been ups and downs as we read through God’s future plans for this nation, the world, the lost, and the saved. He has made promises, kept promises, and we anticipate the final promises being made. Isaiah finishes this book by displaying the heart of God and the desire for God to give salvation and pleading for this lost and wicked world. He doesn’t want to see His creation fail here. He doesn’t want them to go down the wrong path. He definitely doesn’t want them to suffer for all eternity. But He will not force you to make the proper decision. He will just open both doors to you and allow you to choose for yourself."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":4,"title":"God's Heart","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I know we have spoken about this before quite a bit, but there was a time when Israel was dedicated to God. The house that was built to Him was not just a storage closet for their idols. They had everything they needed when they had the Lord, but now that they have been disobedient, they lost it all. God’s house and place of rest aren’t about what is made here on Earth, though. I think that is important to note."},{"kind":"para","text":"There are many religions that are strict about when God should rest. We limit Him to one specific day, and if you don’t follow the rules for that matter, you will be treated like a heathen man. We also limit the Lord to one denomination, thinking that He belongs in our small box of tradition and ritual. We think God fits in the box of religion. That is what the Ark of God became. It was just a box of religion. It had nothing to do with the presence of God and everything to do with people trying to “use” God. The house of God should not contain these kinds of things to limit the Lord. His house and place of rest (thankfully) are in eternity."},{"kind":"para","text":"If you want to talk about Sabbaths and religions, then you must be eternally minded. If you are trying to achieve those things on Earth, you will never be great at it. The standards of God are set far too high on purpose. He wants us to depend on Him, not on our own strengths. I can’t stress that enough."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"We might think that our religious duties, acts, and service will get the attention of the Lord, but that isn’t what God is looking for. He’s looking for the downcast, the burdened. He looks for those who know they can’t do it on their own, those who are too far gone for anyone else to deal with, those who are troubled and lonely, and those who need the support and encouragement from their maker. So many people live in our world today who are going through burdens. People will say, “Just pick up your pants, put your belt on, and start getting after it. No one is going to help you.” That is the wrong attitude. The Lord wants His children to help and encourage these same kinds of people."},{"kind":"para","text":"We have (obviously) a lot of need to help those who are heavily laden in our churches and society today, and we either ignore it and try to snuff out hope for it, or we choose which one we want to spend our time on. Church leaders will focus on one or the other. They will either focus on those outside of the church who are burdened, or they will only focus on those inside the church who are burdened. I don’t understand why it can’t be both. I know that there are many in the church who need help, and those are the ones that take priority (they not only pay the bills, but they are of the same family and they deserve our attention the most)."},{"kind":"para","text":"I have two daughters and many people who request counsel from me. If my daughters came to me with a burden, and someone asked me to counsel them that same day, I would choose my daughters over the needy Christian. Not because I don’t want to talk and help meet the needs of other Christians, but because my family always comes first. I’ve learned that the hard way a few times. Taking that same theory into the pastorate, your congregation should come before the lost. This does not mean we just downright disrespect and forsake the lost, but it does mean that if you have the opportunity to soul win, or the opportunity to counsel a congregant, you should choose your congregant first."},{"kind":"para","text":"Again, this is something we have already talked about, but it needs to be repeated before this book ends. If we don’t get anything else from this book, we should at least get this. God does not want your extravagant services and vain preaching. He wants your heart. He wants you to come to those who are hurting. He wants you to be a good minister and example for Him. That’s all He seeks to do. He has a heart for the hurting. It’s interesting because God has given me that ability. I assumed this was an ability that everyone had. He has given me empathy. It’s a gift and a curse. It’s a gift because I can understand what people are going through without going through it myself. I understand it even better if I go through it, but I still can put myself in other people’s shoes and address their burdens based on what I would personally do in their situation. It’s a curse, however, because I am always feeling what other people feel. It burdens me. You tell me you have an addiction to alcohol that you just can’t break, and my heart breaks with you for weeks (sometimes months) at a time. I will sit and dwell, and pray, and hope that you can find freedom and comfort in Jesus Christ for that burden. I will call, and encourage, and try to equip you until there is even the slightest amount of alleviation."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Lord wants the same thing for His creation. He has empathy for us. Not only that, but He actually lived with the same trials and burdens as us when He came to this Earth. While we might see the majestic Jesus in His glory and healing ministry, we miss the burdened Jesus in His weeping and praying ministry. Jesus doesn’t want us to be like Him in His good-time ministry. He wants us to be like Him in His burden-carrier ministry. While we can certainly have times of both, the times of carrying burdens are usually far greater because that is what God cares about the most."},{"kind":"conversation","text":"### Conversation: *I have two daughters and many people that request counsel from me. If my daughters came to me with a burden, and someone asked me to counsel them that same day, I would choose my daughters over the needy Christian. Not because I don't want to talk and help meet the needs of other Christians, but because my family always comes first. I've learned that the hard way a few times.*"},{"kind":"conversation","text":"### Conversation: *It's interesting, because God has given me that ability. I assumed this was an ability that everyone had. He has given me empathy. It's a gift and a curse. It's a gift because I can understand what people are going through without going through it myself. I understand it even better if I go through it, but I still can put myself in other people's shoes and address their burdens based on what I would personally do in their situation. It's a curse, however, because I am always feeling what other people feel. It burdens me. You tell me you have an addiction to alcohol that you just can't break, and my heart breaks with you for weeks (sometimes months) at a time. I will sit and dwell, and pray, and hope that you can find freedom and comfort in Jesus Christ for that burden. I will call, and encourage, and try and equip you until there is even the slightest amount of alleviation.*"}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"If we look down this list here, these are all things that God had commanded to give as a sacrifice for Him. He talks about killing an ox:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Also a bullock and a ram for peace offerings, to sacrifice before the LORD; and a meat offering mingled with oil: for to day the LORD will appear unto you.","ref":"Leviticus 9:4"},{"kind":"para","text":"He requests offering oblations:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And every oblation of thy meat offering shalt thou season with salt; neither shalt thou suffer the salt of the covenant of thy God to be lacking from thy meat offering: with all thine offerings thou shalt offer salt. And if thou offer a meat offering of thy firstfruits unto the LORD, thou shalt offer for the meat offering of thy firstfruits green ears of corn dried by the fire, even corn beaten out of full ears.","ref":"Leviticus 2:13-15"},{"kind":"para","text":"He talks about burning incense:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And he shall put the incense upon the fire before the LORD, that the cloud of the incense may cover the mercy seat that is upon the testimony, that he die not:","ref":"Leviticus 16:13"},{"kind":"para","text":"These are things they have been doing, but they have been doing it for the wrong reasons. They did it (once again) as rituals, not as worship. God is not going to allow this in the new Earth. Killing will not be permitted at all. Not that we would want to at that point anyway, but the fact is that He is going to treat all killing (including sacrificial) as wicked."}]},{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Bringing it full circle, the Lord has been calling these people for generations. It’s not as if He was not loud enough for them to hear. Isaiah heard the calling of God right at the beginning of this and offered His will to the Lord."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Also I heard the voice of the Lord, saying, Whom shall I send, and who will go for us? Then said I, Here am I; send me.","ref":"Isaiah 6:8"},{"kind":"para","text":"That is the example the Israelites should have taken from the prophets of God. God’s prophets were willing, but God’s children were negligent. They were unmoved by the voice of God. I think that is the great dilemma for the atheist today. It is not that he has not heard the Lord, seen the Lord, or believed in the Lord. It is that he is unmoved by God’s love."},{"kind":"para","text":"They only see the God of judgment (and His children don’t do a good job at portraying anything better), but the God of love and salvation is in the same place. Yes, we will face His judgment if we are calloused to His love. This Bible we are holding, and even this book of Isaiah, is God’s love letter to the world. It’s His heart on paper."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For the word of God is quick, and powerful, and sharper than any twoedged sword, piercing even to the dividing asunder of soul and spirit, and of the joints and marrow, and is a discerner of the thoughts and intents of the heart.","ref":"Hebrews 4:12"},{"kind":"para","text":"This commentary reflects the thoughts and intents of my heart. Scripture, on the other hand, represents the thoughts and intents of God’s heart. While He may not have written His Word specifically about you, He certainly wrote it FOR you. There is a reason why this is the most stolen book in the world: there is power in His message of salvation to this world."},{"kind":"para","text":"Sin may draw us away from God, but God’s love draws us closer to His Word. In this life, we are pulled in these two directions. However, in the next life, we will only be pulled by the love of God."}]}]},{"start":5,"end":9,"title":"The Promise Keeper","entries":[{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God is not tricked by fake people; He knows the heart. While His Word displays God’s heart, it also cuts the readers’ hearts. If God’s Word doesn’t affect you, then you are not a true believer of God. He knows better than I do. There are people whom I look up to and believe are genuine Christians. However, some of these people have made major mistakes that I cannot follow. They’ve done things that make me question the impact that scripture really has on them."},{"kind":"para","text":"They are ministers without grace and are not taking care of the needy and hurting. In fact, it seems they are the ones inflicting the pain most times. They are not pleading for people when they preach; they are competing with people when they preach. They just want to be the one on stage and the center of attention. They want to change people into their ideas of Christians rather than just preaching God’s Word and allowing His Word to do the convicting."},{"kind":"para","text":"They try to force conviction down your throat. That is not how Godly conviction works. The Spirit will convict and guide; we just have to be mouths to speak the truth out of a love for people, like God has a love for people. Even in Christ’s sermon of woes, it was not with a spirit of hate for His hearers. Let’s look at one example."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! for ye shut up the kingdom of heaven against men: for ye neither go in yourselves, neither suffer ye them that are entering to go in.","ref":"Matthew 23:13"},{"kind":"para","text":"This is not a message of hate; it is a message of warning. Christ wants them to turn and do the right thing, not just engage in religious practices. The religious were merely doing their ministry and work for personal gain and profit. In Matthew 23, which is a great chapter and you should read it, Christ wants them to do their Godly work simply because they love Him. It’s a sermon of pleading, not a sermon of judgment and damnation. He is trying to get them to avoid God’s wrath, instead of pouring into it."},{"kind":"para","text":"Obviously, they don’t take His sermon very seriously because these are the same people who end up killing Jesus because of these kinds of words. If you feel like you don’t belong in the church today, you are in good company. Jesus certainly didn’t belong to His religious groups in His day, and He was the spearhead of starting the church. The church (the physical building) and its leadership are not very open and honest groups today. I don’t think you’ll find many genuine people in the church anymore. However, God knows, and He will sort them out when the time comes."}]},{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Mark of the beast! Chapter 66, verse 6! Obviously, those two things are not related here, but I just figured I would share. This is a good verse for Satan though. The Lord will deal with His enemies. He will give them what they deserve. It only has to be through His voice too. He doesn’t have to do much more but speak a word to completely destroy His enemies."},{"kind":"para","text":"We think about great battles of scripture, and we see angel armies helping and serving the Lord and His people. We might even think about the great battle of Armageddon, and the battle that will come with Gabriel and the demons. But really, the greatest battle will be fought with the Word of God."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And out of his mouth goeth a sharp sword, that with it he should smite the nations: and he shall rule them with a rod of iron: and he treadeth the winepress of the fierceness and wrath of Almighty God.","ref":"Revelation 19:15"},{"kind":"para","text":"That is how all great battles will be overcome. God’s Word is the final authority, and it’s the only logical conclusion to Heaven’s greatest battle against Satan. God won’t have to lift a single finger. He will just have to whisper one word to defeat Satan."},{"kind":"para","text":"Satan knows this. He knows that God is not going to have to attack Satan. He knows that God will not even have to leave His throne for this cause. Perhaps He will send Christ for the battle, but in the end, it will just be a simple Word from Christ that will put Satan where He belongs. How little and weak Satan looks comparatively."}]},{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"These are the same examples that John will give in Revelation. Israel is going to go through the Great Tribulation after Christ is born. She (Israel as we will see in Revelation) gave birth to a “man child” before there were “pains.” Usually, it’s the other way around. We experience pain before birth, not after. Yet, in the Great Tribulation, it will be backwards. The peace of God has already been born into this world, and now we are waiting for the pains to come (and they are already here). Since Christ has ascended, and the church has gained traction, nothing has gotten easier. Every day becomes more painful in our world. Eventually, the Lord will end all suffering and pain."}]},{"start":8,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"It will take time. Salvation was still yet to come. After that, though, there will be conflicts and a rising rebellion against the Lord. God knows this. He is prepared for it. He is warning about it. He is getting this world ready for it. He wants us to be prepared as well."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"These things I have spoken unto you, that in me ye might have peace. In the world ye shall have tribulation: but be of good cheer; I have overcome the world.","ref":"John 16:33"},{"kind":"para","text":"He never said that now that He has come to the world and defeated death, everything would become more peaceful. He never promised better days. He did, however, promise a better eternity. He promised a life after this that was worth going through our pains today for. That is the only reason that we are alive today. We have better promises in eternity. That should be the focus of our minds."}]},{"start":9,"end":9,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God will accomplish His promises. He promised a Savior, and He is going to give them a Savior. He is promising a remnant, and there will be a remnant. He promised safety, and He will give safety. He is not going to go back on any of His promises. He can’t. He is the only trusted source in our universe. Again, He is the God of truth. He is a God that cannot lie. He will only do what is right, good, and holy (thankfully). He will keep all of His promises."}]}]},{"start":10,"end":14,"title":"Perfect Peace","entries":[{"start":10,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Again, God is specifically focused on Jerusalem. He cares very much for this city and wants to redeem it. I believe that is where the majority of the saved during the Great Tribulation period will end up. I think that is the place He will revert to for safety to His children. God wants to transform this city back to its glory days before He completely wipes it away. There will be a “New Jerusalem” in the future, but for now, He is working to redeem that place. How that might look is debatable."},{"kind":"para","text":"I think the Lord has already provided salvation for this land, and they have openly rejected it. They will continue to reject it even into the Millennium. However, the Lord will still use it, and there will still be people who turn to Him and find safety in His city. He will always have a place of safety for His children."}]},{"start":12,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Again, we see the Gentiles mentioned here. This is why I don’t believe the one hundred and forty-four thousand will be specifically Jewish. I believe it’s a symbol of a small quantity. But we can talk about that in Revelation. The point is, there will be plenty of providence and safety in this city when the Lord rebuilds it in those days."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is why a lot of scholars and pastors pay close attention to Jerusalem today. It’s still a very sought-after land even in our current era. It’s up to the Lord to decide what to do with it, but there will be a place of safety, even for the Gentile believers."}]},{"start":13,"end":13,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Another promise is given by the Lord here. He promises to give you comfort."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But the Comforter, which is the Holy Ghost, whom the Father will send in my name, he shall teach you all things, and bring all things to your remembrance, whatsoever I have said unto you.","ref":"John 14:26"},{"kind":"para","text":"Today, we experience the comfort of God. If you have not experienced His comfort, it’s one of the most blessed gifts God can give. I have done things that I never thought I would do in a million years. I’ve played music in front of hundreds of people before, and I didn’t really have a problem with it. It was simple, and I knew exactly what I would sing and sound like, and I didn’t think twice about it. Speaking in front of people about the Bible, however, is a very different fear that I’ve overcome only by the comfort of the Spirit. Moving my family to Texas (and back again to California) was a fear that was overcome by God’s comfort. Teaching scripture to people, leading worship in an Egyptian church (while I’m not Egyptian), soulwinning, and counseling people with hard truths are all things that I could never do without the comfort of the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"God is going to provide comfort to His people, and if you don’t have that comfort, it is well worth searching for with everything you have to get it. There’s nothing like the assurance of God’s moving in your life. There’s great comfort when you know that this is what God wants, and we just have to simply accept it. Jonah is a great example of what it looks like to reject the comfort and calling of God. That is what Israel is doing at this time. They didn’t want God’s comfort. They were asking for God’s judgment without even realizing that it’s what they were asking for. It has come, and the scars of that judgment are still visible today. But the healing of God’s comfort is also evident in the lives of believers."},{"kind":"conversation","text":"### Conversation: *I've played music in front of hundreds of people before, and I didn't really have a problem with it. It was simple, and I knew exactly what I would sing and sound like, and I didn't think twice about it. Speaking in front of people about the Bible, however, is a very different fear that I've overcome only by the comfort of the Spirit. Moving my family to Texas (and back again to California) was a fear that was overcome by God's comfort. Teaching scripture to people, leading worship in an Egyptian church (while I'm not Egyptian), soulwinning, counselling people with hard truths are all things that I could never do without the comfort of the Lord.*"}]},{"start":14,"end":14,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"If you are experiencing God’s judgment, it is not because you are not a good person. It’s because you are not a saved person. You are not a born-again person. You are also not a good person, but none of us are. Even Christians are not “good.”"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And Jesus said unto him, Why callest thou me good? there is none good but one, that is, God.","ref":"Mark 10:18"},{"kind":"para","text":"We are only redeemed, and if there is anything good in us, it is only because God is displaying it through us, not because we have mustered it up ourselves. If it’s our own goodness that we are spreading, we are leading the viewers of our goodness into destruction. We are only making man followers of our acts, not the acts of God."},{"kind":"para","text":"If you are people’s savior, they will lose the moment you do. We must place our trust in someone who cannot lose, someone who has provenly overcome. That someone is God only, through Jesus Christ His Son."}]}]},{"start":15,"end":17,"title":"God's Pleading","entries":[{"start":15,"end":16,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God is not going to just destroy and kill everyone in this world. He is going to “plead with all flesh” first. He is going to draw the sword and ask them to turn rather than fight. That is how every situation should be treated. Instead of going straight to the defensive, God sets the example of pleading with His enemy first."},{"kind":"para","text":"It’s not too late for them to turn to Him and ally with the Lord. Instead, though, they will try and combat the Lord, thinking they have the ability to overcome Him. That will not be possible. They’ve already tried that with His Son, and His Son proved that to be impossible. Imagine fighting against the Creator of the universe. How silly that must look from the view of Heaven."}]},{"start":17,"end":17,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God will not let evil and wickedness go unchecked. Even if they do it in secret, God will judge it. He will plead for them and destroy them if they don’t ally with the Lord. If you have chosen (against all hope and sanity) to be an enemy of the Lord, the consequences are all on you. You have the choice and ability to follow Him. He’s not just opening the door and hoping you’ll see it and walk through. He’s calling out to you, pleading with you, and giving you chance after chance to join Him. Eventually, that will come to an end. Either you will die in your sins, or the Lord will return to wrath. Either way, you don’t know how long that door of salvation will remain open."}]}]},{"start":18,"end":21,"title":"Goal of Two","entries":[{"start":18,"end":18,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There will not be a single person in this entire world who will not face God before their eternity. They have the chance to face Him here through the Spirit. However, no matter what they might choose here on this Earth, they will face God eventually for judgment."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And as it is appointed unto men once to die, but after this the judgment:","ref":"Hebrews 9:27"},{"kind":"para","text":"Every single person in this world will face God in judgement. That includes the Christians:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For God shall bring every work into judgment, with every secret thing, whether it be good, or whether it be evil.","ref":"Ecclesiastes 12:14"},{"kind":"para","text":"I’ve heard many sermons and preachers speak about the day we will face the Lord in judgment. They say, “Once you die, you will have to give an account to the Lord.” When they said this, I always thought that I would have to try and explain myself before God. I would have to try and remember the things I did for Him and have to explain away my sins. I thought there would be no way for me to do that because even after being saved, I have still sinned. But I’ve been understanding it wrong (and preachers have not helped me to understand it). Perhaps I’m not the only one."},{"kind":"para","text":"We are going to give an account. But that simply means that God is going to bring the receipts. He will recount your life. You will not have to say a single thing for or against the account given. I think you will stand before the Lord in anticipation of all the sin that you have done (especially as a saved man) and you will think, “Oh, I don’t want to remember these things. I don’t want to talk to the Lord about these things. I am a very wicked person and deserve whatever treatment I get.” And God will say, “Well done, my good and faithful servant,” simply because of Jesus Christ alone."},{"kind":"para","text":"He will recount your story, but there will be no assessing your sin. That’s already been handled by Christ for you. Your debt will have been paid, and you will be secure in the Lord’s promise and gift of mercy and forgiveness. That has been what this whole book of Isaiah has been about. It’s been about receiving God’s mercy. That’s only through faith in His Son."},{"kind":"conversation","text":"### Conversation: *I've heard many sermons and preachers speak about the day we will face the Lord in judgement. They say, \"Once you die, you will have to give an account to the Lord.\" When they said this I always thought that I would have to try and explain myself before God. I would have to try and remember the things I did for Him, and have to explain away my sins. I thought there would be no way for me to do that, because even after being saved I have still sinned. But I've been understanding it wrong (and preachers have not helped me to understand it). Perhaps I'm not the only one.*"}]},{"start":19,"end":19,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The whole world will know of the Lord. Even if the whole world doesn’t know today, they will eventually all know in the future. Before the Lord comes, there will be no excuse for anyone on this planet to not have turned and trusted in Him. Yet, we will see almost the entire Earth has rejected the salvation of God in the Great Tribulation, and there will be nothing left for them but destruction and suffering."}]},{"start":20,"end":20,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Honestly, our labors and efforts in ministry, including reaching the lost, preaching the gospel, counseling the saved, and gathering God’s people, should be our offering to the Lord. That is our act of worship towards Him. It’s not about how much money we spend, how many sermons we preach, how many people are in your seats, how catchy your quotes are in the outlines, or how many structures we can build for our church. It’s about giving our all and sacrificing it to the Lord. If there was a man saved in your congregation last Sunday, sacrifice him to the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"Now, I should probably rephrase this because you might read this and think, “Wait… sacrifice? Are you telling me to kill the people that come to the Lord in our church house today?” No. I’m saying you must sacrifice your connection of “saving” that person to the Lord. I have seen far too many preachers take credit for the amount of hands raised at the altar call at the end of a service. They say, “Look at those hands. Count them and we can tally up the score at the end of the year!” No. Sacrifice your connection with that. You see a hand raised, sacrifice that connection to the Lord. Say, “God, this hand is my offering to you. Please accept my gift of worship and any other hands that might be raised today.” Sacrifice your own efforts to the Lord in worship to His glory and ability to save."},{"kind":"para","text":"If you don’t sacrifice these things, you will take the burden of salvation upon your own shoulders. If that is what you are willing to do, then you must be their Savior, not Jesus Christ. Stop pointing people to Christ if you are going to rob Christ of His work for them!"}]},{"start":21,"end":21,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God will take the sacrifices you make of these people and turn them into tools of ministry. He will make them love other people and reach more. If you’ve never seen the movie “Pay It Forward,” then you should probably watch it (I say hesitantly; I’m not exactly sure what’s in it, but I remember the plot pretty well, so I think it’s safe to watch). In that movie, a kid is tasked with trying to change the world for a school project. He has the idea to “pay it forward” by doing something nice for two people, and they each have to find two people to do something nice to, and so on and so forth until the entire world is reached. This is a biblical concept."},{"kind":"para","text":"God wants us to “pay it forward” in our faith, and once we are able to see a person’s life change, we give it to the Lord, who will then use those people to change others’ lives who will give those lives to the Lord and so on and so forth. If you just reach two people in this world with the gospel message and give that to the Lord, it doesn’t matter if you don’t reach any more, though you may try your hardest. That is a goal we should all set for ourselves. In our lifetimes on Earth, reach at least two people with the gospel message. Don’t stop trying to reach more, but be satisfied if you at least reach two."},{"kind":"conversation","text":"### Conversation: *If you've never seen the movie \"Pay It Forward\" than you should probably watch it (I say hesitantly, I'm not exactly sure what's in it, but I remember the plot pretty well so I think it's safe to watch). In that movie, this kid is tasked with trying to change the world for a school project. He has the idea to \"pay it forward\" by doing something nice for two people, and they each have to find two people to do something nice to, and so on and so forth until the entire world is reached. This is a biblical concept.*"}]}]},{"start":22,"end":24,"title":"Eternal Destinations","entries":[{"start":22,"end":22,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Here’s another promise for and about the new Heaven and Earth. He has already talked up quite a game for this promise, and now He sweetens the pot. He says that it will remain forever. It will never disappear. There will be no reason to ever destroy the Earth again. There will be no sin in it, so there will be no reason for God to store up any wrath against it. The Lord will be pleased with His creation, and everything will work the way it was supposed to since the beginning of time. There will also be no death anymore, but that is something better studied in the gospels or in Revelation."}]},{"start":23,"end":23,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I don’t know if there will be a need for a moon in those days. The point that God is trying to make is that no matter how long time might span, everyone will be worshipping the Lord and living in obedience to Him. Not in the sense of forceful submission (though we will be submissive to our Savior finally), but out of earnest compassion for our God. We will not just have to worship Him like our flesh seems to encourage on this Earth today. We will get to worship Him like our Spirit wants to encourage in the life to come. This is how we should be thinking about our worship now."},{"kind":"para","text":"We don’t have to go to church on Sunday. We don’t have to listen to the preacher. We don’t have to study our Bibles or pray every day. We get to. It’s a privilege, not a chore. If anyone feels burdened by worshipping God today, there is likely a schism in your Spirit that needs to be addressed. You need to be refreshed and renewed in order to have the right attitude about it."},{"kind":"para","text":"I can’t wait for the new Earth where we don’t feel burdened by the same things week in and week out. Everything will be a joy for us, remember? He is creating a people of rejoicing in this new Earth, and that is what I’m looking forward to experiencing for the rest of eternity."}]},{"start":24,"end":24,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This doesn’t end on a high note. It’s a high note for the believer, but it’s a very daunting and terrifying thing to the non-believer. Their end will be continual suffering without Christ. That is not what God wants, but it’s what He will give to those who really desire it. He will do whatever it takes to talk you out of that path, but He will not force you to love Him. He will only open the door for you to do it. You have the chance to walk through that door still. You have until He returns. Seeing as scripture is specific about NOT telling us when that time is, it would be wise to make your decision as quickly as possible."},{"kind":"para","text":"What a way to end this book of the Bible though. He ended it with a very important warning to the reader. Choose God today. Don’t wait. Don’t gamble with your soul. That has been the gospel call throughout this book. He has been pleading with the readers and hearers of this word to turn to God before it’s too late. God has wrath stored up for the evil in this world, and Isaiah (and God Himself) does not want you to be at the tail end of that. He wants you to be at the beginning of safety, not the end of wrath. All He will do, though, is plead with you to turn. You will not win the battle against the Lord. It is impossible if God is the author of all creation and all power. We would be foolish to even try and combat the Lord. We also don’t have a reason to fight against God. There’s every reason possible to trust Him and love Him, but that seems to be missed on the hearers today. Turn to the Lord before it’s too late. Take hold of God’s salvation and safety. This is not just for the Israelite. It’s for this lost world to receive."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":9},{"start":10,"end":11},{"start":12,"end":12},{"start":13,"end":13},{"start":14,"end":14},{"start":15,"end":16},{"start":17,"end":17},{"start":18,"end":18},{"start":19,"end":19},{"start":20,"end":20},{"start":21,"end":21},{"start":22,"end":22},{"start":23,"end":23},{"start":24,"end":24}],"verses":{"1":"Thus saith the Lord, The heaven is my throne, and the earth is my footstool: where is the house that ye build unto me? and where is the place of my rest?","2":"For all those things hath mine hand made, and all those things have been, saith the Lord: but to this man will I look, even to him that is poor and of a contrite spirit, and trembleth at my word.","3":"He that killeth an ox is as if he slew a man; he that sacrificeth a lamb, as if he cut off a dog's neck; he that offereth an oblation, as if he offered swine's blood; he that burneth incense, as if he blessed an idol. Yea, they have chosen their own ways, and their soul delighteth in their abominations.","4":"I also will choose their delusions, and will bring their fears upon them; because when I called, none did answer; when I spake, they did not hear: but they did evil before mine eyes, and chose that in which I delighted not.","5":"Hear the word of the Lord, ye that tremble at his word; Your brethren that hated you, that cast you out for my name's sake, said, Let the Lord be glorified: but he shall appear to your joy, and they shall be ashamed.","6":"A voice of noise from the city, a voice from the temple, a voice of the Lord that rendereth recompence to his enemies.","7":"Before she travailed, she brought forth; before her pain came, she was delivered of a man child.","8":"Who hath heard such a thing? who hath seen such things? Shall the earth be made to bring forth in one day? or shall a nation be born at once? for as soon as Zion travailed, she brought forth her children.","9":"Shall I bring to the birth, and not cause to bring forth? saith the Lord: shall I cause to bring forth, and shut the womb? saith thy God.","10":"Rejoice ye with Jerusalem, and be glad with her, all ye that love her: rejoice for joy with her, all ye that mourn for her:","11":"That ye may suck, and be satisfied with the breasts of her consolations; that ye may milk out, and be delighted with the abundance of her glory.","12":"For thus saith the Lord, Behold, I will extend peace to her like a river, and the glory of the Gentiles like a flowing stream: then shall ye suck, ye shall be borne upon her sides, and be dandled upon her knees.","13":"As one whom his mother comforteth, so will I comfort you; and ye shall be comforted in Jerusalem.","14":"And when ye see this, your heart shall rejoice, and your bones shall flourish like an herb: and the hand of the Lord shall be known toward his servants, and his indignation toward his enemies.","15":"For, behold, the Lord will come with fire, and with his chariots like a whirlwind, to render his anger with fury, and his rebuke with flames of fire.","16":"For by fire and by his sword will the Lord plead with all flesh: and the slain of the Lord shall be many.","17":"They that sanctify themselves, and purify themselves in the gardens behind one tree in the midst, eating swine's flesh, and the abomination, and the mouse, shall be consumed together, saith the Lord.","18":"For I know their works and their thoughts: it shall come, that I will gather all nations and tongues; and they shall come, and see my glory.","19":"And I will set a sign among them, and I will send those that escape of them unto the nations, to Tarshish, Pul, and Lud, that draw the bow, to Tubal, and Javan, to the isles afar off, that have not heard my fame, neither have seen my glory; and they shall declare my glory among the Gentiles.","20":"And they shall bring all your brethren for an offering unto the Lord out of all nations upon horses, and in chariots, and in litters, and upon mules, and upon swift beasts, to my holy mountain Jerusalem, saith the Lord, as the children of Israel bring an offering in a clean vessel into the house of the Lord.","21":"And I will also take of them for priests and for Levites, saith the Lord.","22":"For as the new heavens and the new earth, which I will make, shall remain before me, saith the Lord, so shall your seed and your name remain.","23":"And it shall come to pass, that from one new moon to another, and from one sabbath to another, shall all flesh come to worship before me, saith the Lord.","24":"And they shall go forth, and look upon the carcases of the men that have transgressed against me: for their worm shall not die, neither shall their fire be quenched; and they shall be an abhorring unto all flesh."}},
  },
};
